{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles","id":434590,"title":"Leviathan: The Cult Chronicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-09T14:43:35-07:00","id":434590,"title":"Leviathan: The Cult Chronicles","content":"So some people have expressed interest in working on this. Lets start a thread and see if it goes anywhere <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And lets start with the core, an expanded Cult system. The goals of Cults in Leviathan 2e is of course to create plots. A Leviathan's Cult is an extreemly dysfunctional and arguably evil organisation that's going to do stupid fanatical things like march down Broadway in black robes sacrificing bystanders and get the Leviathan killed unless she manages them. And the only tools Leviathans have to manage their cults are bronze age tyranny.<br /> <br /> Cults are also strongly tied to the X-Splat. Your Strain isn't really what kind of sea mosnter are you, sure giant turtles are kinda a Bahamutan thing and sharks are more Tanninim. Rather, your Strain is what kind of god are you - and naturally your cult follows suit. Your strain is essentially a path of least resistance to a certain kind of cult; and that kind of cult synergies with the Strain's typical psychology. Though the path of least resistance is universal to the strain, psychology varies.<br /> <br /> Bahamatuan's are gods you worship for safety and comfort. It's less about physical blessings and more about being told what to think. Consequently their cults are basically whiny needy babies. (Honestly, that's probably the least bad Leviathan cult)<br /> <br /> Dagonite's are typical bronze age gods. Rain for your crops, plagues for your enemies. Their cults tend to be bronze age in mindset, with strong focus on blood ties, brutal politics and theology.<br /> <br /> Lahamin are secret manipulator gods. Probably closer to Tzeentch than any real mythology, and their cults tend to be secret soceities with agents in positions of power.<br /> <br /> Nu are the kind of god you'd see in modern Christianity. If you see theologians saying &quot;it's a metaphor&quot; a lot you're close to Nu. Just add in some evil. Their cults tend to resemble legitimate religions, but with an undercurrent of alien mysticism.<br /> <br /> Oceaneads are the gods you worship because because being a beliver makes you better than not being a believer. Consiquently their cults are social circles fighting for the Leviathan's attention with lots of passive aggression and subtle sabotage.<br /> <br /> Tanninim aren't gods you worship. They're gods you fear, terrible judges who punish sin without mercy. Their cults are military organisations who exist to enforce the God's will.<br /> <br /> Thalassans are gods of luxury and wealth. The sort of god you'd follow when survival is assured and you can think of acquiring luxuries. Consiquently their cults resemble merchants guilds, corporations and remain stable so long as the cash is flowing in. Cultists and Leviathans aren't that good at commerce though - so you'll have to use Leviathan powers (which aren't that suited either)<br /> <br /> <br /> Mechanically I was planning to do something like Mummy's Reach and Grasp; but with a lot more options, including one kind of cult for every Strain instead of Mummy's three (you don't have to pick the one that matches your strain). And with Leviathan cults being much better at violence than non-violence.<br /> <br /> Cults are also going to be tied into the Rituals system. Leviathans get a full Blood Sorcery style system but they need a cult to use it; and cults can use a Leviathan's power without permission. If you abandon them, they typically will start using it (usually to summon you)<br /> <br /> So lets leave it there for now. Thoughts, suggestions or questions?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0B9DMG5y7ZdngflpNQzVQRDVrSTdDdnFOckNSemFzUjEyNjdWcXU5c0FDVGQwakRDX1BIMjQ&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">See this link for all current Leviathan documents.</span></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-15-2015, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T14:57:16-07:00","id":434616,"title":"","content":"Yes! This was an awesome idea when I first saw it, and I'm glad to see more love! I'm curious about how the Schools might change, in all honesty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:10:37-07:00","id":434638,"title":"","content":"I'd start with nailing down what the Cult types, actually are, given how it is now a part of Character Creation. Maybe the type can be called Dogma.<br /> <br /> I'd say none of the Mummy kinds are really Leviathan's forte-or rather, only one is, due to the effects of the Wake, and how it subconsciously modifies people into fundamentally Tribal groups.<br /> <br /> Other suggestions look great; I'd also add in the idea that getting minions from the Depths is something only the Cult can do, it adds to the Lovecraft aesthetic of Summoners of Alien Creatures.<br /> <br /> For my own offerings, I suggest we look at a soon-to-be-released game called Silent Legions for crunch inspiration involving Cults; it's a D&amp;D retroclone, but thanks to the writer loving the idea of dice-generated plots that make actual sense, he also made a &quot;cult-as-character&quot; system. Given how much Leviathans depend on their Cults and are involved in day-to-day running of it, I'd say we could do worse than yank the Asset and Goal system, along with Cult Turns.<br /> <br /> (In case you were wondering, I backed the Kickstarter and have access to the final draft-not posting it, but I can legally describe what's in there and how it might help once the general public has it).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, Tranquility-I think we can use Harmony as a good baseline for it, in that one can &quot;break upwards&quot;, gaining a point with a roll instead of an Experience. I would have it that 10 is good, 0 is unplayable, though; it keeps with the themes of trying desperately to keep above the Storm, you can actively find stabler ground and lose it just as easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 03-09-2015, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:13:35-07:00","id":434647,"title":"","content":"Maybe change their morality system to something that feels a bit more like 2E Werewolf? (so, for example Too high, and you have trouble accessing your bestial side, too low, and you have trouble maintaining your quasi-divine powers. Your sanity is best served by remaining in the middle)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh! Maybe a little focus on the whole Ego, Id, Superego thing going on in a Leviathan's head?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:44:01-07:00","id":434738,"title":"","content":"So Tranquility, yes it needs an update to a more 2e style morality system. I did think of a Werewolf style but there's a slight hitch that Leviathans have 3 sides to them not two.<br /> <br /> The current Tranquility concept is about building an identity you can live with despite being a monster, but I kinda prefer the old age metaphor to the puberty metaphor. So focusing more on how well you're coping with mad cults, hunters, and whatever else might work. Maybe base it more on Humanity than anything else, but with the ability to break upwards.<br /> <br /> The Ego, Id, Superego would be more Virtue/Vice than Tranquility under that system.<br /> <br /> BTW; it's Id (beast, fighting/feeding/fucking), Ego&amp;Superego (man), Id again (god, domination and authoirty).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=434616#post434616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes! This was an awesome idea when I first saw it, and I'm glad to see more love! I'm curious about how the Schools might change, in all honesty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't thought much about Schools; beyond the fact that there needs to be seven of them.<br /> <br /> I was thinking that the new Schools would be Moon (copy other supernatural societies) and Sand (use Technology to overcome the limits of the Tribe)<br /> <br /> <br /> Leliel, Silent Legions sounds interesting. I can't really say more than that without reading it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:54:42-07:00","id":434751,"title":"","content":"After reading your description I'm sold. Count me in if you are looking for co-writers.<br /> <br /> Also, I always saw it as Id (beast), Ego (man), Superego (God). With a Leviathan's superego encompassing not only their own mind, but that of their cult (and bystanders) as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Perhaps Leviathans could have two morality stats, one to measure their descent towards bestiality and one to measure their ascent towards Godhood. That way it's possible to be very bestial, but nor particularly divine, or extremely composed and absolutely domineering...or a savage hungry god of slaughter and chaos <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 03-09-2015, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T16:19:58-07:00","id":434800,"title":"","content":"PenDragon you know I'm always glad to have you onboard <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Linking the Superego to the god part of the Leviathan's mind is interesting; because the divine part is more like an anti-superego. If the superego is the &quot;internalization of cultural rules&quot;, a levithian's divine nature is about the &quot;externalisation&quot; of cultural rules. I don't like waking up early, therefore there will be a cultural rule against anyone else doing things that might wake me up (I didn't say they're good rules <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> If Leviathan could get away with two morality stats then it could work. So I guess the question is what's better. A morality stat based on how ethical you are, or a morality stat based on how well you're keeping your life in control.<br /> <br /> If we did go for the Beastal and Divine morality stats then Virtue and Vice should probably be around stress (and vice versa. Morality gets one, Virtue/Vice gets the other). In this system you can either get Willpower by solving a problem, or by hulking out and smashing stuff until the problem goes away - when you're cultists come to you and go &quot;when you said you don't want human sacrifice, obviously you meant unless they're virgins&quot; you can either come up with some elaborate scheme to distract them or start eating cultists until they finally get it through their thick skulls.<br /> <br /> Edit: It occurs to me that this system wouldn't have enough charachter customisation options to be the virtue/vice system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-09-2015, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T16:51:22-07:00","id":434857,"title":"","content":"I think, you could make a very interesting reward/temptation system out of this.<br /> <br /> Two Morality Stats, Beast and Divine (working names). Each tied to a vice/virtue equivalent: Id and Ego (again, working titles). Fulfilling your Id recovers willpower, but also risks descent on the Beast path. While indulging your ego also grants willpower, but can push you further up the Divinity track. <br /> <br /> Naturally there'd need to be other ways to recover Willpower (though not enough that these wouldn't remain enticing choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T17:45:32-07:00","id":434907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=434857#post434857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, you could make a very interesting reward/temptation system out of this.<br /> <br /> Two Morality Stats, Beast and Divine (working names). Each tied to a vice/virtue equivalent: Id and Ego (again, working titles). Fulfilling your Id recovers willpower, but also risks descent on the Beast path. While indulging your ego also grants willpower, but can push you further up the Divinity track.<br /> <br /> Naturally there'd need to be other ways to recover Willpower (though not enough that these wouldn't remain enticing choices.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If that's the case, I'd still make it you could move away from the Threshold of No Return without spending XP, though-maybe by betraying said Anchors.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, everything goes down the XP Sink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T17:47:58-07:00","id":434941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=434907#post434907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If that's the case, I'd still make it you could move away from the Threshold of No Return without spending XP, though-maybe by betraying said Anchors.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, everything goes down the XP Sink.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thoroughly agreed. Frankly I dislike the use of XP to recover morality. It's substituting brownie points for roleplaying and a really boring expense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T18:29:43-07:00","id":434996,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd be borrowing the rules for Packs in Werewolf 2ed with Reach, Grasp &amp; Benefits from Mummy. I'd say that the Strains begin with certain Benefits, much like the Deceived. The thing to remember is that the Leviathan functions as the Totem or the Relic in Mystery Cult Initiation terms. Or perhaps the Purpose, depending on how you want the Wake to work. Does the Leviathan ground the faith of the Cult, or if the Cult only needs the Wake and will exist as long as people are inside said Wake.<ul><li>Totems grant a 4th Aspiration, which seems to be a good start. Personally I'd let the ST pick which Aspiration the Cult picks up, barring silly choices...</li> </ul><br /> &quot;Why is everyone paving the streets in wood?&quot;<br /> &quot;...I wanted to build a veranda &amp; I haven't gotten around to it yet. So yeah, they've picked up my Wake. I've told them to stop, but I'm not a part of the Cult, so...&quot;<ul><li>Cult Benefits describe how the group functions and the basic mentality there of. Also there is a lot more variation than just Reach &amp; Grasp. Just a thought.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T19:20:07-07:00","id":435105,"title":"","content":"Will leviathans still be ocean based or can they finally leave the ocean and into land without penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 03-10-2015, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T19:36:01-07:00","id":435137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=435105#post435105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will leviathans still be ocean based or can they finally leave land without penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested in seeing the fabled &quot;Jormugandr&quot; Strain brought into the rules, even as a sidebar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T22:18:43-07:00","id":435273,"title":"","content":"Ooh, I wish I could do more than my support. Unfortunately, all I have is Vampire 2E to go off of. <br /> <br /> Split morality does add an extra layer to the Leviathans, in my opinion. Insofar, it could tie into the &quot;puberty&quot; aspect; maybe playing into the idea of having some sort of power fantasy to deal with the realization of the Leviathan's own nature (sorta like having the idea of &quot;bullying the bully&quot; work into the &quot;Beastly&quot; morality and have something like &quot;being the popular kid&quot; work into the &quot;Godhood&quot; morality, to use metaphors). To be entirely honest, I feel that &quot;Beastly&quot; and &quot;Godhood&quot; could be worked into one type of morality while the other is based around the Leviathan accepting its nature and taking responsibility, to continue the &quot;puberty&quot; idea. <br /> <br /> For example, the original system Tranquility works through being able to accept difficulties and coping in an acceptable manner (thereby remaining Tranquil); high Tranquility represents an individual that is capable of existing beyond the walls of their cult, acting as their own free agent, low Tranquility represents an individual who is stuck in a delusion and is incapable of moving on in their own life. The &quot;Beastly&quot; and &quot;Godhood&quot; aspects work with how the individual conducts themselves through their Tranquility and I just translated D&amp;D alignments into Leviathan, didn't I?<br /> <br /> Does this sound like it would fit in Leviathan or am I entirely off the mark?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T23:29:05-07:00","id":435362,"title":"","content":"Is the theme of stagnation still a major theme of the game? <br /> <br /> How would that work mechanically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T01:34:16-07:00","id":435464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=434857#post434857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, you could make a very interesting reward/temptation system out of this.<br /> <br /> Two Morality Stats, Beast and Divine (working names). Each tied to a vice/virtue equivalent: Id and Ego (again, working titles). Fulfilling your Id recovers willpower, but also risks descent on the Beast path. While indulging your ego also grants willpower, but can push you further up the Divinity track.<br /> <br /> Naturally there'd need to be other ways to recover Willpower (though not enough that these wouldn't remain enticing choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could definately work as a start. However Leviathans don't become Beasts because they were hungry and humans looked tasty, on some level they become Beasts because they could not cope with the pressure of Leviathan life - the lack of healthy relationships, being surounded by cultists, hunters.<br /> <br /> If Id/Ego could be written as using a Leviathan's tools: Claws &amp; psychic dominance to brute force your way past the problems of Leviathan life in a way that's easy and satisfying but self-destructive in the long term then it would be perfect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=435105#post435105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will leviathans still be ocean based or can they finally leave the ocean and into land without penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>They always could in every Depth but the final one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=435362#post435362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the theme of stagnation still a major theme of the game?<br /> <br /> How would that work mechanically?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about mechanically; but I'm leaning towards stagnation replacing puberty as the core theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=435137#post435137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be interested in seeing the fabled &quot;Jormugandr&quot; Strain brought into the rules, even as a sidebar.</div> </div> </div> </div> If I made rules for &quot;Jormugandr&quot; they'd probably be the result of a social fad rather than genetics. Perhaps an Evolution that became popular among Bahamatuans for a while. Perhaps actual rules for Legions - when enough Leviathans join togeather big things happen (though big things typically attract Hunters).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T02:18:00-07:00","id":435488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=435464#post435464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could definately work as a start. However Leviathans don't become Beasts because they were hungry and humans looked tasty, on some level they become Beasts because they could not cope with the pressure of Leviathan life - the lack of healthy relationships, being surounded by cultists, hunters.<br /> <br /> If Id/Ego could be written as using a Leviathan's tools: Claws &amp; psychic dominance to brute force your way past the problems of Leviathan life in a way that's easy and satisfying but self-destructive in the long term then it would be perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly, much like Mask and Dirge (Vampire), or Blood and Bone (Werewolf), I see Id and Ego as the character's go-to responses, those they find easy. Id describes the sort of beast the character <b>could</b> become: The Man Eater, The Hoarder, The Fury. While Ego marks the the sort of rule they ascend towards: The Mother, The Tyrant, The Judge. When a character descends/ascends, these are the Archetypes he tends towards. Even a very well balanced Leviathan, one who maintains his humanity in both fields, finds a refreshing freedom in indulging his Id and Ego. Not getting lost in the short term pleasures, that's the real trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T08:03:16-07:00","id":435707,"title":"","content":"I am all about this.<br /> <br /> The only suggestion I can really contribute is that I think Schools need a little something extra to tie them into the themes of the game. As is, they're just kind of there, feeling like some sort of design obligation. It seems like one's School is at least the start of a direction for a member of a directionless species, so maybe School modifies Tranquility in some way? It could function in a similar vein to Touchstones, as when you start to stagnate your School reminds you of what you're working toward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:48:17-07:00","id":436018,"title":"","content":"I'm liking both of those ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:55:07-07:00","id":436024,"title":"","content":"So, for the Integrity equivalent(s) (I still like the idea of two Integrity stats), I had a thought: Breaking Points that go either way.<br /> <br /> Say a Leviathan is placed in a position of authority, one that he could easily abuse, like being appointed a judge or something, and manages to keep himself from doing so. He rolls a &quot;Reverse Breaking Point&quot;, and if he succeeds, his Integrity equivalent rises instead of falling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:51:21-07:00","id":436179,"title":"","content":"Maybe reverse breaking points should be tied specifically too schools.<br /> <br /> If you're Abyss and you discover something that sheds light on your problem - how an ancient leviathan coped, a ritual that solves it - you get a reverse breaking point. If you're Reef and you solve a problem through violence, I mean legitimately, violence was an appropriate solution, then you get a reverse breaking point.<br /> <br /> Good idea? Should that be instead of or in addition to Touchstones? I do quite like the idea that School is active rather than passive, you have to keep moving just to stay still. It ties into the Stagnation metaphor well, no matter how fast you move you can't actually get anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T14:06:10-07:00","id":436213,"title":"","content":"So... when do we begin with the &quot;Things a Leviathan Doesn\u00b4t Want to Hear from his Cultists&quot; list? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T14:10:45-07:00","id":436219,"title":"","content":"You're late, you should have had the first ones in that post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T14:50:56-07:00","id":436294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=436179#post436179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe reverse breaking points should be tied specifically too schools.<br /> <br /> If you're Abyss and you discover something that sheds light on your problem - how an ancient leviathan coped, a ritual that solves it - you get a reverse breaking point. If you're Reef and you solve a problem through violence, I mean legitimately, violence was an appropriate solution, then you get a reverse breaking point.<br /> <br /> Good idea? Should that be instead of or in addition to Touchstones? I do quite like the idea that School is active rather than passive, you have to keep moving just to stay still. It ties into the Stagnation metaphor well, no matter how fast you move you can't actually get anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like tying it to Schools. If we still like having Touchstones, and we <i>do</i> go forward with double-Integrity, maybe we tie Reverse Breaking Points to one (I think the Bestial one, as Schools seem to be more about keeping your bestial self in check), and Touchstones to the other (probably the Divine, as Touchstones would probably represent a way of keeping in touch with humanity and keeping your tyrranical divine urges in check).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T14:57:55-07:00","id":436308,"title":"","content":"all leviathans have people who are influenced by their wake but not all can make use of them<br /> for those who can I would make a merit like<br /> cult *-*****<br /> which can get you goods and service of lesser availabilty than the dot rating<br /> you get say dot rating * 2 dots for free but after that you get consequences(authorities/unruly cults/monster spawn/ criminal rivalry)<br /> <br /> wake I would make 3 tiered and condition based<br /> first tier are the imposed who get a condition which makes it hard to speak up againts leviathans <br /> second tier are the enthralled who are obsesed with you and wil obey you but with out fine control over them<br /> third tier are beloved who get so infected by you mind that they get 1 of you virtue/vice replacements and some merits to influence and maybe a wake light + the entrhalled<br /> and every strain has a modification of the condition that the enthralledd and beloved get<br /> <br /> vice/virtue replacement <br /> as mask/dirge but threefold <br /> human/beast/divine<br /> how are you Human<br /> how are you a Beast<br /> how are you a God<br /> for instance mother(or parent) could be used for all three but would have very different expresions<br /> <br /> tranquility <br /> represent how at ease you are with you life as a leviathan how balanced you human/beast/divine natures are<br /> the image I have of tranqulity is of calm waters that are frequitly stirred and sometimes form a strom(tempest)<br /> the same way humanity is a downward spiral<br /> breaking points are things that disrupt you live (social interactons going wrong / cult cermony(read sacrifce) being disturbed by hunters/ thypon destroying you house)<br /> or disbalance of your natures losing your self in you instinct or you cult is bad but so is clinging to humanity and rejecting you self<br /> when tranqulity drop you get affliction based on dominant nature<br /> beastial afflictions<br /> you grow fang,scales and hungers<br /> divine afflictions<br /> you develop alien thought patterns and you wake and cult grow out of control<br /> human affliction<br /> you loos control over you powers and grow obsesssed with humans and humanity<br /> <br /> reqaining tranquility <br /> with tranquility xp<br /> which you get for solving problems wich got you a breaking point<br /> and balancing you natures<br /> \u200bactions based on school<br /> which slowly calms te waters of a leviathan soul<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3902-yao","name":"Yao","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T15:12:51-07:00","id":436324,"title":"","content":"I like the ideas behind your stuff here, Yao, but I think the Cult should be a bit more like Mummy's, with Reach and Grasp and Special Features (some of which are tied to Strain, either being exclusive or receiving a cost break).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T16:51:00-07:00","id":436415,"title":"","content":"I was rereading the rules in Second Sight recently, and I actually really like the angle on Cults taken there. It's more a shared pool of Social merits, like Retainer, Contacts, Allies, and Resources, that members of the Cult can access depending on their own Cult Status (equivalent) merit. It doesn't quite have the mechanics for Organisation scale conflict half-built into the Mummy system, and I'm not entirely sure how you'd go about building the mechanics into a Leviathan's character creation, but it seemed to me like an elegant way to represent the advantages of such a group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T12:31:29-07:00","id":437352,"title":"","content":"Azahul; the cult rules in second sight are designed for graduated stages of membership. Leviathan's are always the top dogs. Anyway, here's a first draft at the two morality Tracks. I'm not sure about the names though, thoughts?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sapience</b><br /> <br /> It is a cruel irony that divine beings should fear being reduced to mindless beasts, but The Tribe do fear. As the Tempest breaks against a Leviathan it drags him down with a terrible Undertow, a current that drags them down into the mindless depth. Swimming with a current is always easier than fighting it and a Leviathan who goes with the flow feels an instinctive satisfaction, but acting like a mindless beast has it's costs. Too much indulgence and a Leviathan may forget how to think like a man or a god, becoming a Typhon. A savage mindless monster.<br /> <br /> Sapience measures a Leviathan's descent. A leviathan with high Sapience can think as well as any human, perhaps even better. As Sapience falls a Leviathan becomes more minimalistic, at first they are easily overwhelmed by instincts and emotions but by the end thought and reason wash away.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Undertows</b><br /> <br /> Every Leviathan has an Undertow deep within their psyche. It is the path to beast they might become, a genetic legacy, the lizard brain of a species that was ancient when the first lizards crawled from the sea. Or perhaps it is the dying thoughts of Tiamat still alive within her descendants. Or the Tribe's psychic trauma at their Progenitor's death. In the Tribe these concepts are not mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> Whenever the Leviathan solves a problem in a primal monstrous manner befitting their Undertow they gain a Beat and a point of Willpower. However if they do so they must also roll to see if they loose Sapience.<br /> <br /> &lt;Humanity like guidelines for the dicepool go here&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Effects of Successes and Failures go here&gt;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sentience</b><br /> <br /> Mankind cherishes the ability to feel. They carve idols to gods of love and compassion, fear and anger. Their own passions reflected from the heavens. The Tribe are not those gods, any recognisable emotions a Leviathan feels comes from their human or beastal nature. A Leviathan's divine mind is profoundly alien, devoid of any emotions as we might recognise them. Perhaps underneath their inscrutable behaviour it's as mindless as any beast, perhaps any divine wisdom or godlike intellect the Tribe possessed died with the Progenitors, but perhaps it is our thoughts that are empty and meaningless. Alien as they might be they are the gods. What gives mere mortals the right to see difference and call it lesser?<br /> <br /> Within a Leviathan the divine nature is represented by an Upwelling. A spring that carries the Tribe's divine legacy up form the Rift and into the material world. A Leviathan who follows their Upwelling adopts the alien tyranny of their forbearer's becoming an Ophion, but power over mortals is intellectually satisfying.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Upwellings</b><br /> <br /> Every Leviathan has an Upwelling, it is the god they might one day be. It is a set of instincts and drives that push the Leviathan into becoming that god. It is a fragment of their Progenitor. It is a throne in the primordial waters that is theirs by birth. It is perhaps all of those, or maybe none of them.<br /> <br /> Whenever the Leviathan solves a problem by using people in a manner befitting their Upwelling, as is their divine birthright, they gain a Beat and a point of Willpower. However if they do so they must also roll to see if they loose Sentience.<br /> <br /> &lt;Humanity like guidelines for the dicepool go here&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Effects of Successes and Failures go here&gt;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:10:07-07:00","id":437519,"title":"","content":"Mechanics look about right, though the names could use some work. I do love the ring of Sapience and Sentience, but can't help but feel there are better words. <br /> <br /> To the thesaurus I go!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:37:10-07:00","id":437652,"title":"","content":"I feel that <b>Sapience </b>and <b>Sentience </b>work as counterparts and parallels, as well as the <b>Undertow </b>and the <b>Upwelling</b>. I find it lightly iffy that Upwellings would break downward, but that's all semantics. I do feel that the two work on two ideas: self-satisfaction and self-awareness.<br /> <br /> To me, <b>Sapience </b>feels like it's more about what a Leviathan can do and what it chooses not to do. It could go on a rampage and consume the flesh of the unaware for giggles, but it restrains itself from that, sort of like how the Superego corrects the behavior of the Id (to use the previous Freudian/Jungian concepts). Sapience is pleasure-seeking, staying within the basic needs without going for the bigger picture. The more the Leviathan consumes, the less Sapient it becomes until it is only concerned with the next great meal or pleasure. I feel like it is less about the monstrous, behemoth-destroyer-of-worlds aspect and more about how the Leviathan can retain its higher thought processes.<br /> <br /> With <b>Sentience</b>, it feels like &quot;I can go so far, but I limit myself&quot;; the Id bringing down the Superego before it becomes too big for its britches. It has direction, but no force behind it. It is control over the world around it, meticulously working every aspect in order to attain a sense of order within chaos. Sentience is reason-seeking, sticking too many fingers into one pie and purposefully placing importance on every little detail. The more the Leviathan restrains, the less Sentient it becomes until it becomes more concerned with results than actions. Sort of like Azathoth, the Blind Idiot God; responsible for everything, aware of nothing.<br /> <br /> To clarify, say that a Leviathan learns that a cultist has abandoned its god and is working against the Leviathan in some plot to otherwise decimate the Leviathan's strength. The Leviathan can take to its rage, finding vengeance in torturing the cultist. Likewise, the same action brings order by setting an example, culling the herd by demonstrating what happens to betrayers. That action may satisfy both the <b>Undertow </b>and the <b>Upwelling </b>by demonstrating the Leviathan's Beastly/Godly nature. Going into a murderous rage, destroying whatever even hints at a conspiracy would demonstrate a lack of higher thinking but satisfy the <b>Undertow </b>while taking a calculative, premeditated stance and sniffing out the offending conspiracy demonstrates a desire to restrain beastly behavior but satisfies the <b>Upwelling</b>. Allowing the betrayer to go free but preparing a counter restrains the Leviathan's beastly nature and denies the Leviathan's divine right, demonstrating <b>Sapience</b> through a lack of gut-reaction and <b>Sentience</b> by acknowledging the world around it.<br /> <br /> My thoughts only. Feel free to rip this apart and gut it like a fish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T23:53:01-07:00","id":438103,"title":"","content":"Concerning the change, how would you separate leviathans from werewolves in terms of how they come about?<br /> <br /> Like, what's the difference between a werewolf (whose born a werewolf) and a leviathan (whose also born as such)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T01:47:21-07:00","id":438178,"title":"","content":"So here's a question for everyone. I can kinda see how I want Ophions to be: Highly intelligent beings with sinister plots and a tendency to work through cults; creatures who have thoughts and intelligence, but no feelings as we can understand them. They can commit atrocities without feeling empathy, regret, or even satsifaction at the completion of their goals.<br /> <br /> In short; they're like Lovecraft's monsters. They don't kill you because it benifits them. They kill you because you're so insigificant they have no reason not to step on you.<br /> <br /> The question is; how do you describe that from the inside? Why do Ophions do anything at all if they have no feelings? I don't really want to make them another God Machine following their programming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=438103#post438103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concerning the change, how would you separate leviathans from werewolves in terms of how they come about?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't bother. It's not a big deal if both use generic inheritence. Family is a fundamental human theme, it doesn't need to be unique to one gameline, or two now Beast is coming.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T02:29:33-07:00","id":438215,"title":"","content":"As Ophions are antagonists I'd err on the side of uncertainty. Part of the elder god's monstrousness resides in how totally alien they are, even their desires are indetermineable. The real question is how to spin them into A) a different form of alien from the God-Machine and B) an alienness that seems approachable by players looking to walk the road less traveled (e.g. Divining into divine madness). That second one is a toughy, but I'd venture a good jumping point is unconscious impulse and an implicit desire to bend the world into a very specific, but extremely alien shape (this especially is a departure from the G-M). For players this process goes: &quot;take your most gonzo idea of how the world should work, now keep expanding and refining it for five millennia.&quot;<br /> <br /> To the point of becoming a Leviathan, I agree that there is little need to differentiate their inheritance from that of Uratha. Where the difference should be pronounced is in the handling of that inheritance, and the culture that rises around it (which are already very different from Forsaken). What Leviathan 2e could draw from WtF2 is having some alternatives to direct blood relation. Off the top of my head this could include:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Rosemary's baby style children who were born through occult ritual, channeling a specific strain.</li> <li>Victim's cursed/processed/devoured and shat out(literally or figuratively) by power Leviathans (similar to how Stigmatics &amp; Wolf-Blooded may arise from exposure).</li> <li>People who've come into possession of some terrible ancient artifact that begins to bend their very being into something new and alien.</li> </ol>I'm sure I can think of a few more with time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:19:25-07:00","id":438368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=438178#post438178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's a question for everyone. I can kinda see how I want Ophions to be: Highly intelligent beings with sinister plots and a tendency to work through cults; creatures who have thoughts and intelligence, but no feelings as we can understand them. They can commit atrocities without feeling empathy, regret, or even satsifaction at the completion of their goals.<br /> <br /> In short; they're like Lovecraft's monsters. They don't kill you because it benifits them. They kill you because you're so insigificant they have no reason not to step on you.<br /> <br /> The question is; how do you describe that from the inside? Why do Ophions do anything at all if they have no feelings? I don't really want to make them another God Machine following their programming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if they do something on a regular basis and show logical behavior, they aren't truly emotionless. Living beings need emotion to assign a priority of decisions and to internally judge their options. Psychological fact; truly emotionally-void people show an inability to come to decisions, even what they'll order for lunch, easily.<br /> <br /> I'd say an Ophion lacks any degree of empathy or even the abstract concept that other beings are real. To them, every other entity is simply a Thing I Use To Do Things or a Thing That Stops Me From Doing Things. Think a Real Time Strategy fan with his/her computer-generated army; on a conscious and subconscious level, the army does not actually exist to the player, they're just bits of code that look like people. Thus, the kind of human wave tactics that would be utterly horrifying in real life are interpreted by the player as having the moral context of shuffling army men or pieces on a chessboard around, and their deaths affect the player about as much as losing a piece to the unharmed and non-hostile opponent.<br /> <br /> I imagine an Ophion is the same way, but without the human opponent-and with no capacity to actually care for the cult except as resources. While an RTS can have a good story that makes the player care whether the individual characters in the army live or die, an Ophion never develops that, and never can. Any cultist conferring with them is, at best, just another mission briefing.<br /> <br /> That, and PenDragon's idea of an alien image of what the world should be. Becoming an Ophion should come off as losing your ability to care. By contrast, getting away from becoming an Ophion should come off as painful, as walled-off altruism comes crashing back, sort of like an eye in a dark room having a bright light suddenly switched on; the pain quickly vanishes, and you're probably better off by the end of it, but losing your detachment hurts.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, seems in-theme to have Calling events. Particularly because Leviathans are terrified of dying out, and giving out plot hooks to have a genuine chance of actually increasing the overall population of the Wicked Tribe and for a solitary Leviathan to create a friend out of loneliness doesn't seem life a net loss. You are Cthulhu, it makes sense to also be able to Call, even if it's hard and inexact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 03-12-2015, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T12:10:08-07:00","id":438758,"title":"","content":"Best of luck, folks!<br /> <br /> In terms of nomenclature, I'll note as an outside observer that a lot of the terms I saw floating around in the later iterations of the game came off as a little too... clinical? Especially some of the biology terms. To my mind, while it's true that the Tribe is very biological, it is in a very immediate, physical, and visceral sense; I think terms like &quot;Sentience&quot; and &quot;Sapience&quot; lack that immediacy - they may be accurate labels but they're very much &quot;cooked&quot; terms, while in my head I'd expect the line to feel much more &quot;raw.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T12:27:40-07:00","id":438777,"title":"","content":"Ok; lets go with that for Ophion. That means we can't use the word Sentience; so suggestions please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=438215#post438215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the point of becoming a Leviathan, I agree that there is little need to differentiate their inheritance from that of Uratha. Where the difference should be pronounced is in the handling of that inheritance, and the culture that rises around it (which are already very different from Forsaken). What Leviathan 2e could draw from WtF2 is having some alternatives to direct blood relation.</div> </div> </div> </div> One thing to keep in mind. Leviathans are gods of Fecundidty who were around since pre-history. Genghis Khan has nothing on the tribe - that DNA humans share with banannas, that's where you look for dormant Tribe DNA.<br /> <br /> With tribal DNA being so common environmental triggers are key - and any of those three could be a trigger. Plus each Strain works differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T16:38:42-07:00","id":439044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=438777#post438777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok; lets go with that for Ophion. That means we can't use the word Sentience; so suggestions please.<br /> <br /> One thing to keep in mind. Leviathans are gods of Fecundidty who were around since pre-history. Genghis Khan has nothing on the tribe - that DNA humans share with banannas, that's where you look for dormant Tribe DNA.<br /> <br /> With tribal DNA being so common environmental triggers are key - and any of those three could be a trigger. Plus each Strain works differently.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That gives me a thought for a new adversary/creature: Animals (or plants!) with Leviathan traits, maybe a merit to have one as a pet/attack shrubdog. We could call them Chimeras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T17:36:49-07:00","id":439131,"title":"","content":"I like the concept, though a better name might be <a href=\"http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/atavism\" target=\"_blank\">Atavisms</a>, things from before when the Elder Gods walked the world. Bizarre animals and plant life that just doesn't belong in modern reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T17:38:50-07:00","id":439134,"title":"","content":"Would <b>Judgment </b>and <b>Sentiment </b>work for <b>Sapience </b>and <b>Sentience</b>? <b>Judgment </b>plays into the idea of power and godhood, giving the Leviathan both divine right and the mental capacity to cast judgment. Being unable to clearly make decisions and only reverting to beastly behavior subverts Judgment. <b>Sentiment </b>relates to how the Leviathan cares for their cultists, placing importance in whatever it does. Treating others with obvious disdain, while a power trip and very cathartic, subverts Sentiment.<br /> <br /> Plus, they both end with -ment. Parallels, ahoy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T02:15:01-07:00","id":439637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=439134#post439134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would <b>Judgment </b>and <b>Sentiment </b>work for <b>Sapience </b>and <b>Sentience</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like Judgement I'm afraid; it implies that Leviathans are more competent at being gods than they should be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=439044#post439044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That gives me a thought for a new adversary/creature: Animals (or plants!) with Leviathan traits, maybe a merit to have one as a pet/attack shrubdog. We could call them Chimeras.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're already in there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Have a look at Cyptids.<br /> <br /> That said; I've long considered renaming Channels to Atavisms so there'll have to be a decision on where that word is used.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:27:47-07:00","id":439954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=434638#post434638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tranquility-I think we can use Harmony as a good baseline for it, in that one can &quot;break upwards&quot;, gaining a point with a roll instead of an Experience. I would have it that 10 is good, 0 is unplayable, though; it keeps with the themes of trying desperately to keep above the Storm, you can actively find stabler ground and lose it just as easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if Tranquility affects how badly you need your cult to access certain powers? I could see low Tranquility needing the stablising influence of a human presence to reach down into the storm of your power in a controlled way - though I could also see high Tranquility being a repressed enough state that you need your cult's yearning and drive to reach <i>far</i> down. Both of those could theoretically coexist (and parallel reach and grasp).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=434738#post434738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The current Tranquility concept is about building an identity you can live with despite being a monster, but I kinda prefer the old age metaphor to the puberty metaphor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm, I'd say Mummy has old age licked (and werewolf kinda has puberty linked. Perhaps Leviathan could be rooted in parenthood: you've acquired people who are dependent on you, and because of that very dependence exert an inescapable pull on your life; you have authority over them, but that authority marks you. It would also fit in with how Leviathans represent an older &quot;generation&quot; of life, which is in large part superseded by the very humans who now worship them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=437352#post437352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, here's a first draft at the two morality Tracks. I'm not sure about the names though, thoughts?<br /> <br /> &lt;snip&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>They both sound interesting (and I like the names FWIW). To prevent trait-crowding, what if they also divvy up the effects of the power stats between them? Say Sentience affects Skill Maxima, while Sapience affects Attribute maxima (but upside down compared to most charts, so 1 gives you 10, and 6-10 give you 5). They both contribute to fuel pool, but Sentience is the one that gives you spend rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:34:35-07:00","id":440118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=439637#post439637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like Judgement I'm afraid; it implies that Leviathans are more competent at being gods than they should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about <b>Rationality </b>and <b>Solidarity</b>? <b>Rationality</b> is the ability to make clear decisions and think beyond what is occurring now. <b>Solidarity</b> is how close to humanity Leviathans identify as. Irrational, unconcerned behavior demonstrates the animalistic, beastly nature while detachment and abandonment of humanity demonstrates the otherworldly nature.<br /> <br /> I feel like it's a bit of a stretch, this duo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T11:27:32-07:00","id":440188,"title":"","content":"I'd like to make another push for <b>Ego </b>as the divinity tracking stat. Sure it doesn't fit the Freudian definition of the word, but other more common uses of the word (as in <a href=\"http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/egotism\" target=\"_blank\">Egotistic</a>, <a href=\"http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/egoism\" target=\"_blank\">Egoism</a>, and <a href=\"http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/egocentric\" target=\"_blank\">Egocentric</a>) are an ideal fit. Other possible terms: <b>Humility</b>, <b>Hauteur</b>, or going a little foreign <b>Ahamkara.</b> (That last one requires <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahamkara\" target=\"_blank\">explanation</a>, but seems a good fit.)<br /> <br /> As for tracking how bestial a Leviathan has become I'm still quite fond of <b>Sapience</b>. It has a ring to it that evokes Homo sapiens, which, at low levels of Sapience, a Leviathan would be far from. Other possible terms: <b>Rationality, </b><b>Temperance, </b>and going into the Quaran <b>Nafs </b>(which again requires <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nafs\" target=\"_blank\">explanation</a>).<br /> <br /> We could also dip into Aristotle, notably his works on the concept of Ethos. Where he posited Ethos had three parts: Phronesis, Arete, and Eunoia. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phronesis\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Phronesis</b></a> could be a good term for a Leviathan's bestiality, as low Phronesis would dictate someone without prudence or practical wisdom. <b><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eunoia\" target=\"_blank\">Eunoia</a> </b>refers to a persons receptivity and good-will between himself and his audience, which is ideal for a Divinity track (though tragically it would also be a descending track).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:04:50-07:00","id":440513,"title":"","content":"I admit I'm hesitant to use Ego because that's what I'd use for a psychic morality trait if I ever did a Psychic splat. But lets bat that idea around a bit; if we used Ego how do you think the loss of Ego would manifest in gameplay?<br /> <br /> Right now I'm feeling really annoyed that Empathy is a skill; because it would have made a perfect one. Think we could get away with using it anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-13-2015, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T20:08:33-07:00","id":440814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=440513#post440513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now I'm feeling really annoyed that Empathy is a skill; because it would have made a perfect one. Think we could get away with using it anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say it would pass, but I'm the type of person who gets confused with The Shadow. How about <b>Compassion</b>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T23:27:49-07:00","id":440939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=440513#post440513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit I'm hesitant to use Ego because that's what I'd use for a psychic morality trait if I ever did a Psychic splat. But lets bat that idea around a bit; if we used Ego how do you think the loss of Ego would manifest in gameplay?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I think it sounds cooler, I'm going to use <b>Ahamkara </b>instead of Ego for this example, as Pendragon suggested.<br /> <br /> <b>Ahamkara</b><br /> <br /> Mankind loves their emotional material ties. He loves that brand new company car, that watch his wife gave him, that homemade card crafted by his daughter. Because, to this mortal mind, these objects have meaning outside their usage, He subscribes qualities to them they do not exist in reality. The Wicked Tribe have a clearer vision, any recognizable emotions a Leviathan feels comes from their human or beastial nature. A Leviathan's divine mind is profoundly alien, devoid of any emotions as we might recognize them, perceiving only that which is true. Ahamkara is the talent of drawing forth that mortal deception, so that a Leviathan might sympathize with their subjects. Otherwise their behaviour appears inscrutable or worse, mindless as any beast, leading to the assumption that perhaps any divine wisdom or godlike intellect the Tribe possessed died with the Progenitors. Alien as they might be they are the gods. What gives mere mortals the right to see difference and call it lesser?<br /> <br /> (Yes I borrowed liberally from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=437352#post437352\">here. </a>That's not a bad thing. It also allows us to keep Upwellings as presented in that post.)<br /> <br /> It's not quite Empathy, because no matter what that piece of yourself no longer exists. It's too far away, you've changed too much. But you can feel a higher calling, Upwelling within your blood. If you were ever truely human you have long since passed that point. But sometimes you can fool yourself, that you haven't changed, that all those small, petty, mortal things matter. That the new iphone is exciting, that your daughter's birthday is not another Tuesday and that faith is a matter of more than obedience to a greater power.<br /> But somewhere, deep down, you know that it's a lie. Nothing ever really changes.<br /> <br /> Edit: This fan-line deserves a skull. I recommend something like <a href=\"http://i873.photobucket.com/albums/ab292/wimhoppenbrouwers/Natuurhistorischmuseum%203D/DSC_0003s.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Out of curiosity, how much of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/LeviathanTheTempest\" target=\"_blank\">these</a> we will be keeping? Makes working the crunch easier if we know everything we're keeping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 03-14-2015, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T05:43:43-07:00","id":441236,"title":"","content":"You know what. I'm going to say <b>Ahamkara </b>for now. It can always change later and has a fundamental advantage in that unlike a zero <b>Sentience</b> charachter; a zero Ahamkara charachter is actually possible to describe without making them robots.<br /> <br /> Plus your write up is pretty sweet, I don't think I'll do more than tweak it, I don't want to say the Leviathan perspective is true. More that who is a mortal to question it, now Portunus (Roman god of keys among other thing) can argue with the tribe about a key's sentimental value.<br /> <br /> I think the Leviathan Skull should look like Cthulhu <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for TvTropes - you'll have to be more specific.<br /> <br /> <b>Sapience</b><br /> <br /> It is a cruel irony that divine beings should fear being reduced to mindless beasts, but The Tribe do fear. As the Tempest breaks against a Leviathan it drags him down with a terrible Undertow, a current that drags them down into the mindless depth. Swimming with a current is always easier than fighting it and a Leviathan who goes with the flow feels an instinctive satisfaction, but acting like a mindless beast has it's costs. Too much indulgence and a Leviathan may forget how to think like a man or a god, becoming a Typhon. A savage mindless monster.<br /> <br /> Sapience measures a Leviathan's descent. A leviathan with high Sapience can think as well as any human, perhaps even better. As Sapience falls a Leviathan becomes more minimalistic, at first they are easily overwhelmed by instincts and emotions but by the end thought and reason wash away.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Undertows</b><br /> <br /> Every Leviathan has an Undertow deep within their psyche. It is the path to beast they might become, a genetic legacy, the lizard brain of a species that was ancient when the first lizards crawled from the sea. Or perhaps it is the dying thoughts of Tiamat still alive within her descendants. Or the Tribe's psychic trauma at their Progenitor's death. In the Tribe these concepts are not mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> Whenever the Leviathan solves a problem in a primal monstrous manner befitting their Undertow they gain a Beat and a point of Willpower. However if they do so they must also roll to see if they loose Sapience.<br /> <br /> &lt;Humanity like guidelines for the dicepool go here&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Effects of Successes and Failures go here&gt;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ahamkara </b><br /> <br /> Mankind loves their emotional ties. He loves that brand new company car, that watch his wife gave him, that homemade card crafted by his daughter. He loves his wife and daughter. Because, to this mortal mind, these objects and people have meaning outside their usage, he subscribes qualities to them they do not exist in reality and sings praises to the goddess of love and the god of cars. The Wicked Tribe are not those gods, and they have a different way of perceiving the world. A Leviathan's divine mind is profoundly alien, devoid of any emotions as we might recognize them, perceiving only the practical utility in objects, and people. Ahamkara is the talent of drawing forth that mortal viewpoint, the domimence of the two mortal minds within the Leviathan's threefold nature, so that a Leviathan might sympathize with their subjects. Otherwise their behaviour appears inscrutable or worse, mindless as any beast, leading to the assumption that perhaps any divine wisdom or godlike intellect the Tribe possessed died with the Progenitors. But no matter how Alien they might be, the Tribe are gods. What gives mere mortals the right to see difference and call it lesser?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Upwellings</b><br /> <br /> Within a Leviathan the divine nature is represented by an Upwelling. A spring that carries the Tribe's divine legacy up form the Rift and into the material world. A Leviathan who follows their Upwelling adopts the alien tyranny of their forbearer's becoming an Ophion, but power over mortals is intellectually satisfying. Every Leviathan has their own Upwelling, it is the god they might one day be. It is a set of instincts and drives that push the Leviathan into becoming that god. It is a fragment of their Progenitor. It is a throne in the primordial waters that is theirs by birth. It is perhaps all of those, or maybe none of them.<br /> <br /> Whenever the Leviathan solves a problem by using people in a manner befitting their Upwelling, as is their divine birthright, they gain a Beat and a point of Willpower. However if they do so they must also roll to see if they loose Sentience.<br /> <br /> &lt;Humanity like guidelines for the dicepool go here&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Effects of Successes and Failures go here&gt;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Schools</b><br /> <br /> A Leviathan is a being of great and terrible power, surrounded by a cult of worrying zeal and questionable sanity. Consequently a Levithan's life is one of hardship, and no matter how instinctively satisfying it may be to use the tools given to them by their Birthright, enormous claws and psychic dominance, neither is appropriate in this complex and dangerous modern world of international politics and attack helicopters. And so The Tribe swim in Schools.<br /> <br /> A School is something that gives the Leviathan direction; a way of solving problems that does more than just buy time until the next crisis. It provides solutions that build upon each other, until at last the Leviathan finds a stable long term solution to their life's problems. Or at least, a School provides Leviathans with the illusion that they're moving towards a long term solution.<br /> <br /> Whenever the Leviathan solves a problem by using people in a manner befitting their School they gain an Evolutionary Beat. In addition they may roll to see if they regain Sapience or Ahamkara, if the solution involved the Leviathan's personal supernatural abilities they may regain Sapience. If it involved working through willing allies, pawns or Rituals they may gain Ahamkara. This can result in a situation where a Leviathan risks loosing or gaining a Dot in the same roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> &lt;Humanity like guidelines for the dicepool go here&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Effects of Successes and Failures go here&gt;<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> So this leads to an obvious question: Do the current schools fit the needs of this system, that is, do they provide a broad array of potential ways to regain Sapience or Ahamkara?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T07:15:13-07:00","id":441262,"title":"","content":"Yay! I sort of helped!<br /> <br /> Fair enough about the skull. A quick google shows potential. I liked this one the <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/8e/21/42/8e2142539d8e2c62385a192204f60028.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">best</a>.<br /> <br /> As for TVTropes...I was asking which ones we wanted to keep or lose, if any.<br /> <br /> Edit: In answer to your question, the existing schools seem to work in this regard, but given the nature of the Sun &amp; the Clay I'd say that it needs to be difficult to earn both that Beat &amp;that [Morality] dot. That said, someone has already had an idea that may suit the system better. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=436294#post436294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like tying it to Schools. If we still like having Touchstones, and we <i>do</i> go forward with double-Integrity, maybe we tie Reverse Breaking Points to one (I think the Bestial one, as Schools seem to be more about keeping your bestial self in check), and Touchstones to the other (probably the Divine, as Touchstones would probably represent a way of keeping in touch with humanity and keeping your tyrranical divine urges in check).</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Schools of the Sun &amp; the Clay already encourage a lot of interaction with mortals any Ahamkara 'reverse breaking points' would either be frequently triggered or significantly more difficult to trigger than the other Schools. Neither of which feels satisfactory to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 03-14-2015, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T07:15:34-07:00","id":441263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=441236#post441236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooo... Me likey!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=441236#post441236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Schools</b><br /> <br /> A Leviathan is a being of great and terrible power, surrounded by a cult of worrying zeal and questionable sanity. Consequently a Levithan's life is one of hardship, and no matter how instinctively satisfying it may be to use the tools given to them by their Birthright, enormous claws and psychic dominance, neither is appropriate in this complex and dangerous modern world of international politics and attack helicopters. And so The Tribe swim in Schools.<br /> <br /> A School is something that gives the Leviathan direction; a way of solving problems that does more than just buy time until the next crisis. It provides solutions that build upon each other, until at last the Leviathan finds a stable long term solution to their life's problems. Or at least, a School provides Leviathans with the illusion that they're moving towards a long term solution.<br /> <br /> Whenever the Leviathan solves a problem by using people in a manner befitting their School they gain an Evolutionary Beat. In addition they may roll to see if they regain Sapience or Ahamkara, if the solution involved the Leviathan's personal supernatural abilities they may regain Sapience. If it involved working through willing allies, pawns or Rituals they may gain Ahamkara. This can result in a situation where a Leviathan risks loosing or gaining a Dot in the same roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> &lt;Humanity like guidelines for the dicepool go here&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Effects of Successes and Failures go here&gt;<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> So this leads to an obvious question: Do the current schools fit the needs of this system, that is, do they provide a broad array of potential ways to regain Sapience or Ahamkara?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think they all should. Abyss (personal introspection), Clay (learning from humanity), and Fog (learning from history) all are definitely locks, since they all provide somewhere for the Levianthan to look for inspiration to adapt and change to the world and prevent themselves from stagnating. Fog's likely the most round about of those three, but there are still plenty of example of historical God-Kings, and well as learning from the successes and mistakes of other members of the Tribe. <br /> <br /> The Sun and Reef are a bit harder, since they seem to be giving into the Upwellings and Undertows respectively. <br /> <br /> The School of the Sun could definitely be adjusted a little bit. Instead of just focusing on The Tribe reclaiming its place as objects of human worship, it could now focus on the two way relationship between God and worshiper, and on how the the Leviathans should be the focus of faith for mankind... but they also need their cults and can't afford to neglect them. Its really already in the School's description, it just needs a slight shift in emphasis. <br /> <br /> The School of the Reef is a bit trickier for my brain right now, but the idea of defending one's friends and self, while vanquishing one's enemies should be workable on finding a way to ground oneself in the world and not degenerate into a monster or tyrant. Course, that also sounds like a really good way to get to both of those points... <br /> <br /> I'm also wondering if it may not be a bad idea to create a school that looks for answers in the Leviathan condition by exploring the Rift. Sounds like that could have an interesting spin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T07:34:27-07:00","id":441293,"title":"","content":"Never Mind; found a better skull.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/originals/98/62/86/986286357184c4f395c52c9689304507.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not to fond of the name <b>Sapience</b> either. But I don't have much in the way of better ideas and I am currently too tired to give <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nyaya#Etymology\" target=\"_blank\">Nyaya</a> the write up that would give it a chance. Maybe tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 03-14-2015, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:37:53-07:00","id":441484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=441236#post441236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Schools</b><br /> <br /> A Leviathan is a being of great and terrible power, surrounded by a cult of worrying zeal and questionable sanity. Consequently a Levithan's life is one of hardship, and no matter how instinctively satisfying it may be to use the tools given to them by their Birthright, enormous claws and psychic dominance, neither is appropriate in this complex and dangerous modern world of international politics and attack helicopters. And so The Tribe swim in Schools.<br /> <br /> A School is something that gives the Leviathan direction; a way of solving problems that does more than just buy time until the next crisis. It provides solutions that build upon each other, until at last the Leviathan finds a stable long term solution to their life's problems. Or at least, a School provides Leviathans with the illusion that they're moving towards a long term solution.<br /> <br /> Whenever the Leviathan solves a problem by using people in a manner befitting their School they gain an Evolutionary Beat. In addition they may roll to see if they regain Sapience or Ahamkara, if the solution involved the Leviathan's personal supernatural abilities they may regain Sapience. If it involved working through willing allies, pawns or Rituals they may gain Ahamkara. This can result in a situation where a Leviathan risks loosing or gaining a Dot in the same roll.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> So this leads to an obvious question: Do the current schools fit the needs of this system, that is, do they provide a broad array of potential ways to regain Sapience or Ahamkara?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Abyss:</b> Meditative and introspective, searching for purpose and meaning; perhaps they gain an Evolutionary Beat when the Leviathan finds a reason to exist in a world composed of humans or evolves as an individual. <i>(This School feels more like a means for personal development and watching the world around them)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sun: </b>Faithful and retrospective, becoming the moral keystone against uncertainty; maybe an Evolutionary Beat when the Leviathan gives hope to the hopeless or offers some sort of sanctuary for those who suffer. <i>(This School, as translated into the Cult Chronicles, seems the most-involved with their own cults, teaching their followers and attempting to emulate the progenitors)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Clay:</b> Adaptive and integrating, emulating humanity despite their nature; an Evolutionary Beat when the Leviathan accomplishes an important aspect of mortal life or identifies with humanity for personal reasons. <i>(To be entirely fair, I feel that a Leviathan allowing itself to get close enough to humanity to ask someone on a date and actually having a relatively normal experience is a big milestone for ANY Leviathan but the School of Clay would place more importance on it)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Reef:</b> Vigilant and defensive, tempering divine fury with a tight leash; gain an Evolutionary Beat when the Leviathan anticipates danger or controls the direction of a conflict. <i>(While the original School of the Reef focused on the &quot;soldier&quot; aspect, it also plays with the ideas of expecting dangers and how to react; deconstructing the &quot;war&quot; aspect allows this School to work with the Sapience/Ahamkara mechanics)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Fog:</b> Seeking and questioning, analyzing themselves and the world around them; receive an Evolutionary Beat when the Leviathan discovers new information about the Tribe or pulls underlying problems to situations. <i>(Actually, I have no idea how to summarize these guys; any takers?)</i><br /> <br /> The Schools themselves <i>(and their foundation) </i>works cohesively with Sapience and Ahamkata. I do think that they could be rewritten to add more depth into what they are and how they function in a Leviathan's life. Above, I was trying to see what my own thoughts about what the Schools focus on would shape their &quot;gain Beats&quot; action. Right now, it's all fuzzy but it's what I feel their direction would lead them.<br /> <br /> Also, I think platypus skulls would fit the nature of the Tribe.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/originals/64/c7/33/64c733dfb916488b49efbeedee808462.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T10:38:49-07:00","id":441561,"title":"","content":"If it's just about the Name for the Second Morality (Sapience) how about just Changing the Name too Cognizance, Sapiance is awareness of ones Self and The Effect you have in Effect right? (Not Massively Up on Leviathan so.. Sorry if i'm incorrect) Cognizance is the same in meaning but.. Sounds abit more.. Cerebral.<br /> <br /> Just a Thought?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T11:38:13-07:00","id":441663,"title":"","content":"As for Rituals, I always prefer splat rituals to be structured like Vampiric Blood Sorcery, rather than having a bunch of individual, pre-made rituals. Perhaps we could use that, but have the existing rituals as example rituals?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh! Maybe make each theme/arcana easier for each school to use! (The School of the Abyss, for example, would have talent for using rituals that call forth creatures from the Rift, while the School of Reef would be better with rituals of fortification).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 03-14-2015, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T13:15:35-07:00","id":441773,"title":"","content":"After doing a bit of research into Aristotle I must revise my original assessment of terms for Integrity stats. Phronesis and Eunoia are absolutely perfect.<br /> <br /> In Aristotle's (translated) words Phronesis is, <span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#191919\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">wisdom to take counsel, to judge the goods and evils and all the things in life that are desirable and to be avoided, to use all the available goods finely, to behave rightly in society, to observe due occasions, to employ both speech and action with sagacity, to have expert knowledge of all things that are useful.&quot;</span> </span></span></span>If that isn't an ideal term to measure how bestial/non-sapient the Leviathan has become I don't know what is.<br /> <br /> Eunoia on the other hand is semi-synonymous with benevolence or goodwill possessed between others (literally &quot;beautiful thinking&quot;). In reference to rhetoric Eunoia is, &quot;<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Goodwill </span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">towards an audience, either perceived or real; the perception that the speaker has the audience's interest at heart.&quot;</span> </span></span></span>In Leviathan terms this is a measure of the Leviathan's ability to perceive the interests of others, and put put them before himself. In this sense a character with high Eunoia would be, well, like a normal person. While one whose Eunoia has fallen low takes on sociopathic tendancies, finally becoming perfectly greedy, unable to recognize that others even possess interests, and quite incapable of caring.<br /> <br /> Relevant Synonyms:<ul><li>Phronesis: Sagacity, Wisdom, Foresight</li> <li>Eunoia: Benevolence, Goodwill, Selflessness</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T04:36:22-07:00","id":442420,"title":"","content":"For skulls; I like both of Fallen Echo's chuthulu skulls. But the keyhole would have to go.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>malonkey1</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=441663#post441663\">View Post</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">As for Rituals, I always prefer splat rituals to be structured like Vampiric Blood Sorcery, rather than having a bunch of individual, pre-made rituals. Perhaps we could use that, but have the existing rituals as example rituals?</span><br /> </span><br /> </i></span><br /> <br /> A Blood Sorcery style system is absolutely the intent. My current plan is to have the Arcana be the Vestiges. So if you want to perform a 4 dot Elements ritual you need to have 4 different Elements Channels; and 4 dots in the Rituals trait (probably Eldrich Lore).<br /> <br /> This is to create the idea that the power comes from the Leviathan itself. The cult is performing a ritual petittioning the god of the elements to send a storm at your enemies. They have to actually be a god of the elements to do that.<br /> <br /> PenDragon also had a very neat idea that for Sympathy, it's not how much the Leviathan knows about the target. It's how much the target knows about the Leviathan. So do be careful when reading those tomes of forbidden lore.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>PenDragon</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=441773#post441773\">View Post</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">After doing a bit of research into Aristotle I must revise my original assessment of terms for Integrity stats. Phronesis and Eunoia are absolutely perfect.</span><br /> </span><br /> </i></span><br /> <br /> Lets go with that. How much rewriting do you think Sapience / Ahamkara would need?<br /> <br /> <br /> Now onto Schools.<br /> <br /> I think ReaperVerse's summery highlights an issue. The old schools were, mostly, about where a Leviathan looks for meaning. The Abyss looks internally, Clay looks a humanity. I'm not sure that works with the new morality system being worked here.<br /> <br /> Lets use an example: A local fisherman has become an Ahab and wants to kill you. If you turn into a giant fish and eat him, you risk loosing Sapience/Phronesis. If you get your cult to lynch him you risk loosing Ahamkara/Eunoia.<br /> <br /> But if you do X you have a chance to regain either Sapience/Phronesis or Ahamkara/Eunoia. So what is X for each School?<ul><li>Abyss - no idea.</li> <li>Sun - Have your cult kill him, but do it in a way that increases their reverence for the Progenitors.</li> <li>Clay - Have the Ahab arrested or committed into a mental asylum.</li> <li>Reef - Turn into a giant fish and eat him.</li> <li>Fog - no idea.</li> </ul><br /> So that's 2 I'm not sure about. One where it's the same action you'd do anyway. Two with different actions.<br /> <br /> Actually; maybe those numbers aren't so bad. However the revised School write ups would have to talk a lot more about the kind of actions that fit the School's ethos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 03-15-2015, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T08:49:15-07:00","id":442598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=442420#post442420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For skulls; I like both of Fallen Echo's chuthulu skulls. But the keyhole would have to go.<ul><li>Abyss - no idea.</li> <li>Sun - Have your cult kill him, but do it in a way that increases their reverence for the Progenitors.</li> <li>Clay - Have the Ahab arrested or committed into a mental asylum.</li> <li>Reef - Turn into a giant fish and eat him.</li> <li>Fog - no idea.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Abyss: Use mystical methods to befuddle and lose the Ahab.<br /> Fog: Best the Ahab using investigation and trickery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T16:12:56-07:00","id":443220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheKingsRaven</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets go with that. How much rewriting do you think Sapience / Ahamkara would need?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than detailing the differences let me write up a draft and see what you think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now onto Schools.<br /> <br /> I think ReaperVerse's summery highlights an issue. The old schools were, mostly, about where a Leviathan looks for meaning. The Abyss looks internally, Clay looks a humanity. I'm not sure that works with the new morality system being worked here.<br /> <br /> Lets use an example: A local fisherman has become an Ahab and wants to kill you. If you turn into a giant fish and eat him, you risk loosing Sapience/Phronesis. If you get your cult to lynch him you risk loosing Ahamkara/Eunoia.<br /> <br /> But if you do X you have a chance to regain either Sapience/Phronesis or Ahamkara/Eunoia. So what is X for each School?<ul><li>Abyss - no idea.</li> <li>Sun - Have your cult kill him, but do it in a way that increases their reverence for the Progenitors.</li> <li>Clay - Have the Ahab arrested or committed into a mental asylum.</li> <li>Reef - Turn into a giant fish and eat him.</li> <li>Fog - no idea.</li> </ul>So that's 2 I'm not sure about. One where it's the same action you'd do anyway. Two with different actions. </div> </div> </div>Here's my take, off the top of my head:<ul><li><b>Abyss </b>- Take the &quot;Living Nightmare&quot; approach. Obfuscate yourself behind veils material and magical. Send the Ahab astray and leave no evidence of your existence. Let his paranoia annex him and his obsession kill him.</li> <li><b>Sun </b>- Take the &quot;God-King&quot; approach. Set your cult upon him, let him be an example to others. They will make an offering of his flesh and soul.</li> <li><b>Clay </b>- Take the &quot;Mob-Boss&quot; approach. Burn down his home, lock up his finances, take hostage his lovers and threaten his family. Put his name on a registry and his body in an asylum.</li> <li><b>Reef </b>- Take the &quot;Alpha Monster&quot; approach. Go yourself, in the most terrific form you possess. Fight him mano e mano and prove that none are greater. Bonus points if your cult is there to see.</li> <li><b>Fog </b>- Take the &quot;Dark Lord&quot; approach. Drag the Ahab into your wake, bend his interests to your whim, delve into his life and psyche. Make him yours or leave him mad.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 03-15-2015, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T01:15:02-07:00","id":443883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=443220#post443220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than detailing the differences let me write up a draft and see what you think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I look forward to seeing it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T13:40:45-07:00","id":451985,"title":"","content":"Any new thoughts or developments?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T10:42:28-07:00","id":452839,"title":"","content":"Been a busy time; quite a few things happening around Princess and there's the Hunter history fanbook in progress. However I do have this:<br /> The Mother<br /> The Mother exists for her children, she has given birth to heroes and monsters and will give birth to many more until the day she is dragged up from the depths. Her only wish is to see her children triumph. No matter if they wish to build empires, defeat champions or ruin nations, she will give them a world where they can flourish.<br /> <br /> The Judge<br /> The Judge does not wish to create a world without sin, no his motive is far more brutal. The Judge wishes to create a world where all sin is punished and all sinners face their judgement. So long as this is so, The Judge would be satisfied if the whole world turned against the gods and drowned,<br /> <br /> The Lawgiver<br /> In many ways the Judge's twin, the Lawgiver emerges from the depths with bronze tablets to create a world where all follow the laws within. He punishes harshly and rewards sparingly but when faced with the choice the Lawgiver would ignore one sinner to instil his commandments within two.<br /> <br /> The Patriarch<br /> Parisian without limits, The Patriarch will see his people thrive. He bestows his favor freely but never spares the teacher's rod when his people stray from their own best interests. To those who threaten the chosen people or just stand in their way The Patriarch sends his storms and his plagues.<br /> <br /> The Tyrant<br /> The Tyrant is involved with the day to day affairs of his kingdom or church, woe betide anyone who questions or disobeys his orders no matter how cruel. The Tyrant is a close cousin of The Patriarch, both are invested in the success of their chosen people or faith. They differ in the tools they use.<br /> <br /> The Weaver<br /> It is said Fate binds even the gods, but the Weaver believes she can play Fate at it's own games and master the future. But no Weaver plays for the love of the game, they have goals and plans which they enact through mortal pawns.<br /> <br /> The Devil<br /> Even the gods must acknowledge others, even if only other gods. The Devil defines herself by opposition, another church, another nation is her enemy. But she has no wish to destroy it for where would that leave her? The Devil instead spreads her corruption, turning her enemy against it's sacred values. Leaving it alive in name only as a testament to her victory.<br /> <br /> <br /> Feel free to speculate about the Progenitors, but that's just for fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:06:21-07:00","id":452859,"title":"","content":"So, with the Moon School you mentioned earlier in the thread, do you think we'll see a Vestige dedicated to supporting/dealing with other Splats? (E.G., giving a vampire Ichor-as-Vitae, replicating supernatural weaknesses, etc.) Or would that be more reserved for Evolutions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 03-22-2015, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:14:47-07:00","id":452874,"title":"","content":"With the new direction Leviathan 2E is going; I'm no longer sure Moon school is appropraite. In 1E there was room for niche schools, but in 2E a School has to be consistently relevant.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:18:03-07:00","id":452877,"title":"","content":"Though it might make a interesting Evolution, in all honesty.<br /> <br /> But yeah, we may need to just stick with the five we have, since they seem to cover a wide range of responses. <br /> <br /> Also, though this probably doesn't matter, Beast is using Atavism for one of it's powersets, so we might want to stick with Vestige and Channel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:18:19-07:00","id":452878,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I still wonder if inter-splat interaction is worth its own Vestige.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T12:41:19-07:00","id":454736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=452877#post452877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, though this probably doesn't matter, Beast is using Atavism for one of it's powersets, so we might want to stick with Vestige and Channel.</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh; if Humanity can appear twice so can Atavism.<br /> <br /> That said; I'm currently thinking that Atavisms are automatic Attribute boosts when you Transform and Channels remain as Channels. This will require another 8 Channels at least to replace the old Attribute boosters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=452877#post452877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, we may need to just stick with the five we have, since they seem to cover a wide range of responses.</div> </div> </div> </div> I do want to go up to seven, but other splats and monsters probably won't make the cut.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking instead Moon will be a School that seeks to find purpose in being a good god to their cult; but typicaly manifests as toxic codependency. They need their cult to need them, and will <i>make that happen</i>.<br /> <br /> (Actually which way round should Moon and Sun be? One is being a god, one is being high priests of the Progenitors)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=452877#post452877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I still wonder if inter-splat interaction is worth its own Vestige.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T22:12:07-07:00","id":457767,"title":"","content":"Just so you know, Silent Legions is out now, if you still want to check it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T14:10:19-07:00","id":461429,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think sun functions better as a priestly idea- religion and solar icons is a pretty common idea and it illustrates the concept better, plus people will probably grasp it easier. The moon functions better as the deity-needing-cult. The cult is like a star- glorious and full of purpose. The leviathan may inspire them, but it's really just a reflection of their light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>-Failure is always an option<br /> roseerifnosi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/115-dahqueendiva","name":"DahQueenDiva","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T15:39:46-07:00","id":461604,"title":"","content":"So, the type of cult you get is determined by your Strain, but how you run it is determined by school? So, for example, a Thalassan in the School of Clay would resemble a modern financial corporation, whereas one in the School of the Reef would be more like a paramilitary organization?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T16:23:47-07:00","id":461626,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Incidentally, Kings Raven, have you read China Mi<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u00e9ville's <i>Kraken</i>? If not, you might find it inspiring.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T16:50:47-07:00","id":461645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DahQueenDiva</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=461429#post461429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think sun functions better as a priestly idea- religion and solar icons is a pretty common idea and it illustrates the concept better, plus people will probably grasp it easier. The moon functions better as the deity-needing-cult. The cult is like a star- glorious and full of purpose. The leviathan may inspire them, but it's really just a reflection of their light.</div> </div> </div> </div> Another way to express the idea of the Moon school. From the Earth, the moon is something grand and glorious, a power that controls the tides, and with them, life. But with knowledge comes the understanding that the moon, while inspiring, is not independent; the Earth keeps the moon in its cycle, stopping it from flying off without purpose or power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T17:01:11-07:00","id":461653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=461645#post461645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Another way to express the idea of the Moon school. From the Earth, the moon is something grand and glorious, a power that controls the tides, and with them, life. But with knowledge comes the understanding that the moon, while inspiring, is not independent; the Earth keeps the moon in its cycle, stopping it from flying off without purpose or power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Admittedly, the Earth isn't doing a great job. <a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/news/science-environment-12311119\" target=\"_blank\">The Moon is slowly drifting away.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T17:08:36-07:00","id":461656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=461653#post461653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Admittedly, the Earth isn't doing a great job. <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.bbc.com/news/science-environment-12311119&amp;quot;]The</a> Moon is slowly drifting away.[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div> A metaphor for the all too often irreversible slide of the Tribe into monstrousness? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T03:13:42-07:00","id":462054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=461604#post461604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the type of cult you get is determined by your Strain, but how you run it is determined by school? So, for example, a Thalassan in the School of Clay would resemble a modern financial corporation, whereas one in the School of the Reef would be more like a paramilitary organization?</div> </div> </div> </div>That works remarkably well actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T09:55:48-07:00","id":462383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=461626#post461626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Incidentally, Kings Raven, have you read China Mi<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u00e9ville's <i>Kraken</i>? If not, you might find it inspiring.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Kraken is more Unkown Armies than Leviathan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=461604#post461604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the type of cult you get is determined by your Strain, but how you run it is determined by school? So, for example, a Thalassan in the School of Clay would resemble a modern financial corporation, whereas one in the School of the Reef would be more like a paramilitary organization?</div> </div> </div> </div>That wouldn't work IMO. you'd need 49 different types of cult. I'm thinking that 7 different kinds of cults will be sufficient.<br /> <br /> I was going to give each Strain a favoured cult - since Strain is &quot;what kind of god are you&quot;. But let them choose another if they like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-30-2015, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T12:39:55-07:00","id":462610,"title":"","content":"Well, the fact i didn't discovered <b>Leviathan: The Tempest</b> before is certainly unfortunate, but at least i arrive on time to this new expansion.<br /> <br /> I'm currently consuming all its information, so i won't be able to help properly until finished... and given the amounth of work i have, that will take some time still. But i didn't want to wait until finish it to compliment the developers of the game and the unique flavour it creates. Great game, well done (so far)!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As player of both WoD and Call of Cthulhu, i absolutely love the Leviathan's vibe. I've been reading through the <b>Introduction and Lexicon</b>, and also <b>The World that Is (and Was). </b>And i couldn't resist and jumped over the rules and stuff to go directly into <b>The Rift</b>. And here is the first thing i wanted to share with you all: definitely a concept so awesome as The Rift needs a lot more love than what i've read so far. The stuff i've read is great, but feels... incomplete, too schematic maybe. Needs much much more flesh in those titanic bones. (And i'd remove the conscient changing form pr\u00f2hibition). <br /> <br /> You see, i've fallen in love with the idea of the Rift. It seems to me the definitive identity point of the game. I see (and the Old God sectarian in myself cannot help but approve) the Cult direction this new edition is taking, but to me the Rift and its nature is the real core (and maybe even the real enemy!) of a Leviathan. (Yes, sorry, I'm total Rift fanboy). After all, we already have Mummy to focus on Cults, and all the splats have some in-built &quot;Cult&quot;. I get perfectly that Leviathan's Cults are totally different thanks to that beautiful Wake mechanic, and they add all the Cthulhu-esque flavour to the game... But the Rift? That's Leviathan stuff only. Have you thought about changing the Rift in any way? I'd love to help on that!!&lt;3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T12:49:34-07:00","id":462614,"title":"","content":"I have no plans or ideas to change the Rift. I love it, but like a lot of the stuff I worked on, it's reached the point where the Rift is written just as I imagined it and so I can't really imagine it any different.<br /> <br /> Did you have something in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T14:08:58-07:00","id":462667,"title":"","content":"Well, i was kind of thinking about the Rift as a fight.<br /> <br /> Not only a battle of minds though, but a fight of gods, a clash of worlds. I'll explain. As i was reading through The World that Is (and Was), Tiamat gradually rose from an incredibly powerful monster, an inmense and utterly titanic god, to a pillar of the creation, a reality itself, a terrifying Gaia, (or more accuratedly, Angrboda), an idea, a concept in fact: Tiamat as embodiment istelf of the Old World.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">(Or more accuratedly, the young world, a world still full of violence and the elements themselves coiling and fighting each other, a world where the reminiscences of its own birth were still present because it hadn't been so far away, with primeval oceans and volcanoes bleeding lava and spitting fire and smoke to the young skies; a world full of potential and furious energy)</span><br /> <br /> And i started thinking. Tiamat, as this, destroyed by a human hero? No way. No way even if all the warriors of all the Tribes would have lead a charge against her, against<b><i> it</i></b>. But what about the collective impulse of Humanity and Time itself? The mere presence of humanity, the rising numbers of it and the progressive domestication of the World (a world no longer as elemental and vigorous as was before), lead to a world in which Tiamat itself was left behind, a World in which her/it, the concept of the Old World, had no place. And so Tiamat fell in torpor, a dream so deep that sinked itself through reality... creating the Rift.<br /> <br /> And so Tiamat dissapeared, dragging down with herself not only, well, herself, but also the most powerful -and therefore purest- of her incarnations/sons: the titanic Progenitors.<br /> <br /> The blood of Tiamat flowed still through the world, of course, and so new Leviathans rose among humanity itself: a pirric victory -but a victory nonetheless-. And in their dreams, the Leviathans would hear the deep call of Tiamat and the Progenitors, and those who would follow it, swimming into the Depths, would arrive into the Lost Dream-Mind-World of their Goddess. The Rift. They quickly realized that the Rift was a physical place as much as the memories of the Whole Tribe. Even more so, the Rift was also their own minds. And so (like the first Leviathan goes) the First Depth is forged of their collective minds, while the most you sink, the nearer you are to Tiamat. Tiamat would be at the other side of The Tempest (or so the legend goes), and the Tempest would be its own Call: so powerful and alien it is to these newborn from Humanity Leviathans that the Voice of their Goddess reveals itslef as pain and obstacles (exemplified as is done in the first edition).<br /> <br /> That's why The Rift is a triple fight: of the mind (the more human mind of the first Depths against the more primeval mind of the darkest Depths), of Worlds (as is the fight of this world against the world that was) and of Gods (of the God that each Leviathan has in his core against the Older, more powerful Leviathan-Gods who lurks in the ever sinking depths of the Rift).<br /> <br /> Thougts? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> PS. Following this direction, maybe the Cults would be not only sources of power and adoration for the Leviathan, but also ways of bringing back a little bit of the Old World into the actual one, as each Leviathan thinks of the Call and the Old World in his/her own way. They fail again and again, as they are fighting not only against humanity and its warriors (the Ahabs and the Marduks) but against Time, always going forward. That could be the explanation of the major theme of the game, stagnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":1349,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","user":"Phersus","date":".  More and more ideas :) 03-30-2015, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T14:25:26-07:00","id":462670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=462667#post462667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And i started thinking. Tiamat, as this, destroyed by a human hero? No way. No way even if all the warriors of all the Tribes would have lead a charge against her, against<b><i> it</i></b>. But what about the collective impulse of Humanity itself? The mere presence of humanity, the rising numbers of it and the progressive domestication of the World (a world no longer as elemental and vigorous as was before), lead to a world in which Tiamat itself was left behind, a World in which her/it, the concept of the Old World, had no place. And so Tiamat fell in torpor, a dream so deep that sinked itself through reality... creating the Rift.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, that's one of the possible truth's behind Tiamat.<br /> <br /> My personal preference is that Marduk really was just a mortal who killed Tiamat. He actually did it by building the tower of Babel, a tower that stretched from the sea bed into the ocean above the sky, and out of the ocean into the post-primordial world. Since Tiamat was the whole pre-fall world that's basically a giant spear through her gut.<br /> <br /> To do so he had to invent civilisation, order, law, science, magic, and all sorts of other stuff. Which let him hold the Progenitors at bay.<br /> <br /> Then when humanity climed to the top he made some appropriately wise speech (I'm not a genius like Marduk, I won't try) about why mankind's gods shall come from the heavens and not the waters. When he finished a bolt of lightning struck the tower and conducted itself downwards, finally destroying the Primordial world; Tiamat and the progenitors. Everything but what mankind carried with them.<br /> <br /> Basically. In the primordial world, things work like they do in mythology. In mythology a mortal hero can overcome the gods, and a giant stone tower can survive a god who shapes islands with her claws/tenticles/tail (depictions of Thalassa vary) because it's righteous or some junk like that.<br /> <br /> Hey; it makes as much sense as a giant cow licking the ice to free a giant; then the gods killed the giant and made the world from his body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=462667#post462667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thougts? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>How would that be different on a practical level?<br /> <br /> I'm not going to add anything that will give a single canonical answer to what Tiamat was. She could have been a planet sized goddes that got punched in the face by Marduk with a god of lightning. She could be nothing more than a metaphor for the pond where the first single celled life was formed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T14:30:14-07:00","id":462673,"title":"","content":"I like to be inspired by old cosmology maps. <img src=\"http://www.webpages.uidaho.edu/ngier/308/OTcosmos.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> They're pretty crazy. For Leviathan's primordial world I always imagined something like that, except that there's no underworld or solid land. Instead the only continant is on Bahamut's back. The ocean is Nu. etc. Tiamat is the whole thing put togeather.<br /> <br /> Though obviously this isn't cannon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T14:44:44-07:00","id":462688,"title":"","content":"That map and the idea behinf it is pretty damm cool, i have to say it. Speaking about the practical differences between the Rift ideas... i'll have to think about them. I let myself speak of the whys and the feeling and forgot about actually expanding the lore about the Rift. I feel as i said that the Rift, being as important to the Leviathans as it is, has to be more fleshed out. I will think about it and post my ideas here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks for the quick answers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T17:47:56-07:00","id":462894,"title":"","content":"I kind of like the idea of the Rift being something that doesn't technically &quot;Exist&quot;, like a racial memory made manifest, of a past that was made false by Marduk's actions. Yeah, that's kind of ripping off Atlantis from Mage, but why do Mages get to be the only heirs to a past paradise (for them) that never was?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=462383#post462383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That wouldn't work IMO. you'd need 49 different types of cult. I'm thinking that 7 different kinds of cults will be sufficient.<br /> <br /> I was going to give each Strain a favoured cult - since Strain is &quot;what kind of god are you&quot;. But let them choose another if they like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't really mean for each Strain/School combination to have a totally different type of cult. I meant more like how different denominations of a religion might exist: The core ideas of the religion (determined by the Strain) remain consistent within that Strain, but how they go about it differs with the School of the Leviathan (Baptists and Catholics are both Christian, for example, but they have different practices related to that religion, as an example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:46:25-07:00","id":463901,"title":"","content":"So now for something a bit different. One of the minor templates tied to the tribe:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Primordial Theurgist</b></span><br /> <br /> To the gods, performing miracles is as natural as breathing. A goddess of love touches the world every time two young things lock eyes, even when the goddess herself is giving her full attention to elaborate plots of revenge against her stepsister.<br /> <br /> The Tribe are no different. Each Leviathan is, in some infinitesimal sense, a law of nature, and like any natural law they can be studied and manipulated, even against their own wishes.<br /> <br /> There are of course drawbacks and risks. You can call it Newton's laws, though that is an oversimplification. Nevertheless, if you touch the Leviathan's mind then the Leviathan's mind, in all it's sanity rending eldrich glory, is touching you. Primordial Theurgists, mortals who wield Rituals and claim the Tribe's power as their own, are Beloved of the gods they seek to control. If they are not, then they will be before they call their first miracle.<br /> <br /> Not all Theurgists wish to control their god of course. Plenty are priests and cult leaders who have been taught how to perform Rituals to enact their god's will while it's busy elsewhere. Others believe themselves to be loyal worshippers who've started experimenting in their deity's absence. Many Leviathans flee in horror when they first discover their presence creates Beloved, only to return years later when their abandoned cult's experimentation finally creates some horrific yet effective summoning ritual.<br /> <br /> But other Theurgists do want to control Leviathans, or at least their divine power. Why wouldn't they? Leviathans are a broken shattered people, mankind has already scattered them upon Earth and the gods cast them down from the heavens. The Tribe are still gods, but defeated gods with little ability to defend their drop of divinity from mortals eager to tamper in the gods' domain.<br /> <br /> For your sanity, a far cheaper price than a soul, a scholar can acquire power that's not merely occult or supernatural, but truly divine. It might not be more powerful than other forms of magic but it operates on a different level of reality. To an oculist who understands the difference, it can be the most important factor in which tradition they peruse.<br /> <br /> Priests and cultists, whether they're doing their god's work or just believe they are, typically use a mixture of trial and error, insight from their own madness, and whatever their deity has taught them.<br /> <br /> Occultists stealing the Tribe's power typically have a much more academic approach. They have their theories and maps of the heavens, charts of stars and tides, and tomes of research from their predecessors. Many draw on research that spreads beyond the Tribe to other gods, especially if they with to use the Tribe's power to influence other divine beings. (A risky prospect, Leviathans couldn't stand up to the gods when their powers weren't being controlled mortals, but if you're lucky the god will only lay his vengeance upon the Leviathan).<br /> <br /> This research isn't just for figuring out the correct Ritual. A cultist rarely thinks about which Leviathan to petition, he has at most one Cohort and knows them all quite well. But to occultists the choice is paramount. The wrong Leviathan might notice and eat you or attempt to control you, and of course you have to pick a Leviathan who's Vestiges can prower the desired ritauls.<br /> <br /> Occultists typically use Ophions to power their rituals, as an Ophion has no way of withholding his power save direct intervention; and trapped in the Rift many Ophions are unable to do so. The closest thing to coin among these Thurgists is lists of Ophions with their powers and the techniques they might use to influence their Beloved from wtihin the rift. No Thurgist wants to wake up one day and realise they're a cultist, or the guy who freed a monstrous god from the depths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:02:52-07:00","id":463917,"title":"","content":"So this isn't quite finished. I feel in tails of a bit, so I need to think of some way of wrapping it up; but the core is there. Though on re-reading, I might split the bits about priests/cultists and the bit about academic occultists into separate sections.<br /> <br /> When I think of Primordial Thurgists I always think of the occultist from Darkest Dungeon <img src=\"http://oyster.ignimgs.com/mediawiki/apis.ign.com/darkest-dungeon/thumb/7/7e/Occ.jpg/468px-Occ.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> I suspect that's because we're both thinking of Abdul Alhazred.<br /> <br /> <br /> The actual rules for these guys will have to wait for the Rituals rules of course. But it shouldn't be much; an alternative to the cult merit; probably apprentices and Allies with advantages or disadvantages for each. Rituals should work identically to Leviathans; which is a bit unusual for me. Normally I make my mortals far weaker than full splats at ritual magic \u2013 but in this case the weakness is you go mad. It fits the theme of humanity being triamphant over the tribe.<br /> <br /> One neat fact is that Leviathans are insanely good at Clashes of Will (Sheol + Depth; which means that an Occultist channelling an Opheon has a minimum dicepool of of 7). I quite like the fact that vampire sorcerers and Mages will have to admit that, no, these guys really are using divine power.<br /> <br /> (It's a shame we don't have Morality any more, giving Benedictions Morality for Clash of Wills would have had the same effect)<br /> <br /> <br /> Fun fact. Leviathans actually have no magical ability whatsoever. They have biological abilties and psychic abilities. Some of it is divine biology and divine psychic powers. But, in my WoD anyway, trying to draw a distinction between divine and not divine requires insanely advanced supernatural lore.<br /> <br /> Two random people falling in love is divine in the sense that it's a subconscious thing at least one Love God is doing, but it's also purely mundane consequence of brain chemistry. Trying to figure out what's what is ridiculously complex and there isn't always a distinction.<br /> <br /> So trying to say \u201cthat psychic power is divine\u201d and \u201cthat one wasn't\u201d isn't really productive. Same goes for a Mage's magic, plenty of gods of magic out there (Hectae, Isis...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T17:09:50-07:00","id":464034,"title":"","content":"I like them. Seems like they might make both good allies and enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T17:53:45-07:00","id":482981,"title":"","content":"Have there been any steps made on the Ritual rules? If not, I could take a swing at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T00:55:15-07:00","id":483331,"title":"","content":"Let me dig up the ol' notes.<br /> <br /> I was thinking that rituals will probably be based on the rules for Mage 2e. However I do have some concepts, mostly based on the Blood Sorcery book.<br /> <br /> So firstly Leviathan rituals require two things: Channels, Sacrafices and and a cult. The Themes/Arcana are: Awareness, Elements, Fecundity, Might, Predation, Sanctity and Vitality. You have three different Elements Channel, you have Arcana: Elements 3.<br /> <br /> For the cult, I'm thinking that Zeal will be moved to a purely Rituals thing. Zeal will work like Gnosis.<br /> <br /> One thing I am worrying about is that Channels go up to 7 (if you count the Birthright). Arcana obviously only goes up to 5 without Archmastery and I don't want to give Leviathans archmastery for a simple exp cost. So either Rituals will need to have more gradual progression from 1-7 or just break the Leviathan tradition of using the number 7 everywhere and make Rituals go up to 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> So next up: Sacrafices. Mage's get Yantra's to extend their Reach in a spell. Leviathans depend on moral evils, the more dots in the ritual the more evil the sacrifice must be. Maybe something like your Reach being equal to (1 + Zeal + Sacrifice - twice Rituals dots); and of course you need to have a Reach of at least one to make a Ritual work.<br /> <br /> You can also get bonus Reach for <i>The Stars Being Right</i>. But if the stars are wrong you get negative Reach. The nice thing here is that a Zeal 4 Cult can never perform a 5 dot Ritual unless the Stars are Right.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now some miscellaneous points:<br /> <br /> Rituals are really bad at helping people. Like lets say you want to give your followers superhuman toughness, they'll grow fish scales.<br /> <br /> Sympathy works in reverse. Instead of how much the Leviathan knows about you, it's how much you know about the Leviathan. (So don't read that tome of eldrich lore!). Fluff wise it's because gods are partly a concept. So Leviathans partly exist inside every mind or book that talks about them. Just like how Thor exists inside every thunderstorm.<br /> <br /> Rituals are technically a combination of divine and psychic phenomina. There's no actual magic involved. (This probably doesn't matter much.)<br /> <br /> When Mages get modifiers like area of effect; Rituals get more for the same success. Rituals focus on big things; a Leviathan can't throw a fireball at someone near him with a ritual (not that she needs too) but she can send a storm against an entire town.<br /> <br /> Aside from that it's probably going to look a lot like Mage 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> Best of luck, I look forward to seeing this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T02:04:54-07:00","id":483362,"title":"","content":"In order to cast level 7 ritual even with zeal 5 and sacrifice 5 you would need at least +4 from Stars Being Right. So, once in a few years the most powerful Leviathans with most zealous cults sacrficing dozens of virgins can cast one level 7 Ritual. So maybe that's not that bad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/120-daimon","name":"Daimon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T05:57:25-07:00","id":483439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daimon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=483362#post483362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order to cast level 7 ritual even with zeal 5 and sacrifice 5 you would need at least +4 from Stars Being Right. So, once in a few years the most powerful Leviathans with most zealous cults sacrficing dozens of virgins can cast one level 7 Ritual. So maybe that's not that bad?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that's the intent, and it's <i>very</i> in-theme. I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T10:00:09-07:00","id":483681,"title":"","content":"Yes, but it would require coming up with seven ranks of Rituals that fit the themes of Leviathan. Simply using Imperial Mysteries won't work; a power like &quot;you can't be hurt, ever&quot; fits Imperial Mystery's themes, but not Leviathan's.<br /> <br /> I'd be tempted to say that a level 6 ritual might be once every few years, but a rank 7 might be every few hundred years.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T10:11:39-07:00","id":483691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=483681#post483681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but it would require coming up with seven ranks of Rituals that fit the themes of Leviathan. Simply using Imperial Mysteries won't work; a power like &quot;you can't be hurt, ever&quot; fits Imperial Mystery's themes, but not Leviathan's.<br /> <br /> I'd be tempted to say that a level 6 ritual might be once every few years, but a rank 7 might be every few hundred years.</div> </div> </div> </div>So less warping reality, more biblical plagues. Floods and Eathquakes with top-tier Elements, Swarms of all-consuming vermin with Fecundity, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T10:45:26-07:00","id":483710,"title":"","content":"Well warping reality can be very lovecraftian. But the power levels and styles will have to be Leviathan appropraite.<br /> <br /> Twisting space to build a city of obscene geometries is fine. Twisting space so that attacks never hit you is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T15:16:45-07:00","id":483917,"title":"","content":"Glad to see this come for a new edition <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Question, I'm trying to explain to a friend of mine what Leviathan is and I'm having trouble explaining it to him. Any help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2295-coderr","name":"CodeRR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2295_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T16:04:21-07:00","id":483982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CodeRR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=483917#post483917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad to see this come for a new edition <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Question, I'm trying to explain to a friend of mine what Leviathan is and I'm having trouble explaining it to him. Any help?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your character goes through the most extreme puberty imaginable, and finds that he's part human, part mad god, part sea monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T23:10:13-07:00","id":484311,"title":"","content":"That's the old one. The new one is about old age. Worrying about your legacy (which as a Leviathan is doomed to be nothing) while the kids (you're cult) run around getting themselves and you intro trouble and expecting you to fix it for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T11:03:39-07:00","id":510028,"title":"","content":"This thread returns from the depths; it's been a while I know, but I return with something substantial - the entire chapter on Cults.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TY33912o7ngUtKEXT4ow-5uHNyOlmKWkmykWoNrCuQE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a><br /> <br /> Fourteen pages, heavily adapted from Mummy's cult rules. (Mummy had 4 if you're wondering. I have no word count limits. Mwahahah <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <hr /><br /> Next up I think I'll do the Strains. Here's my current concept for a Template:<br /> <br /> Opening - an in character section from the journals of The Mad Arab; in Leviathan he's a golden age Mu`tazila Islamic scholar and an Occultist (see earlier in the thread) who sought to use the Tribe's power to see Allah with his own eyes. We never hear if it worked or not. I know I won't be able to write these, so after the rest is done I'll see if someone around here can.<br /> <br /> Theology - the core of each Strain, what kind of god are they. It will be framed in a sort of cult centric way, the Strain isn't who are you as a god, it's who do your followers treat you as. Most Leviathans go with the flow, but either way the way your cult sees you is going to cause problems.<br /> <br /> Puberty - Unlikely to change.<br /> <br /> Morphology - Will be reworked to offer more clear guidance; the Evolution section will be merged in.<br /> <br /> Ecology - the subsections will likely be expanded. Progenitor will be moved into this section.<br /> <br /> Vestiges, Symbols and Associations, Concepts, unlikely to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-10-2015, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T11:34:14-07:00","id":510067,"title":"","content":"I can try with the Mad Arab.<br /> <br /> With Hunted, I'd have hard guidelines for what the Hunters are. For example: A governmental agency or community seeing the Cult for the abuser's paradise it is creates a group of 15-20 people who don't precisely know the supernatural aspects but do know the Cult is a a menace, or an in-the-know Hunter cell of 6-7 people with some off-battlefield support if they do figure it out (the majority of people freak out, leaving only the bravest/most foolish). An Ahab manifesting consists of them and possibly a cell of non-Ahab Hunters who believe them. Modify as appropriate, though skilled and knowledgeable people generally appear in less numbers (unless they're the Marduk Society, if you've <i>really </i>managed to cheese them off).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T11:42:43-07:00","id":510071,"title":"","content":"There's a reason that Hunted doesn't have Hard guidelines. It needs to scale enormously, far to enormously to fit into the condition. At the low end 15-20 mostly ordinary people is enough. At the high end you might get the USA sending an entire carrier battle group.<br /> <br /> Part of the premise of Leviathan is that you can just about play Cthulhu. That means if you're Hunted you have to be Hunted by people who can threaten Cthulhu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T13:17:34-07:00","id":510149,"title":"","content":"The first Strain is done, probably the only one I'll do tonight. There's quite a lot of reused material, but also plenty of new stuff. I'd definitely like feedback on this.<br /> <br /> Leliel, best of luck with The Mad Arab, my only request is that he's a stone cold badass, he survives by being patient, cautious, and balls to the walls crazy enough to look Chuthlu in the eye and go &quot;yes, clearly stealing that guy's power is the best way to understand Allah's creation&quot;. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Bahamutans</span><br /> <br /> [Picture: The Symbol of Bahamut: An oval, fish-like scale with iridescent rays. It is inlaid with intricate filigree-work in some precious metal. Over this has been crudely painted an open eye, with no iris but a wide black pupil. Fingerprints are still visible in the paint. ]<br /> <br /> [Picture: Central. A fisherman is standing under a streetlight. He is a young man, with a general Latino appearance. His legs are in oilskin pants but he is barefoot. He wears a wifebeater, under which bumpy, scaly ridges are visible that delineate his muscles. He has no hair and his scalp is glistening. His arms are tattooed, and one of his hands is holding the rostrum of a sawfish like a macahuitl. His jaw is gaping wide open, much larger than a human jaw could, and displays several rows of teeth along with a flat, wide tongue.]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Theology</span><br /> <br /> In a world of chaos they cry out to the depth for guidance. What is just, what is moral, what is right? Mankind has always turned to the gods for answers to life's unanswerable questions. At their best philosophers and sages debate the wisdom of their ancestors or craft parables out of mighty gods and heroic mortals to teach ordinary men extraordinary ideas. At their lowest the gods become a shield to escape responsibility or a chain that binds nations to traditions that, if they ever made sense, only did so in a world that no longer exists. At the very lowest, in the darkest, murkiest depths of the oceans, you can find the Bahamatains.<br /> <br /> The blood of Bahamut carries a strong protective instinct. It creates a strain driven to guard what it considers it's own, and even when it doesn't a Bahamatain can't help but be aware that they inhabit a world which is, to them, crushingly small and unbearably fragile. Bahamatains often seek to retreat from the world and dwell in solitude among their beloved, but in this the Strain's nature is at war with itself. The Leviathan's need for self restraint is a constant irritation, and when they decide to let go the results can be quite literally apocalyptic.<br /> <br /> The cults that surround Bahamatains reflect this. A Bahamatuns's Beloved bask in that reassuring power, they do not ask the Leviathan for help with their problems so much as they ask the Leviathan for permission, placing the burden of responsibility on titanic shoulders large enough to bear it. The Strain often sees it's Beloved as tiny helpless creatures, who's neediness is both irritating and self-affirming. The greatest danger arises when the Cult calls upon their deity to abandon his self-restraint, when that happens something is going to snap.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Morphology</span><br /> <br /> Even in a family of titans, Bahamutans are known for their size. Even when not expressing their Leviathan natures members of this Lineage tend towards broad shoulders and considerable height. When they Transform Bahamutans display characteristics of life famed for prodigious size or toughness. Among the strain one can find echoes the whale's titanic form, or the catfish dwarfing the other inhabitants of it's lake. Shells resembling a turtle or a crab are common, as are iron hard scales. The Strain's immense forms can seem to drift, untouchable and listless, through the Depths.<br /> <br /> Bahamutans who favour Awareness typically manifest it their proclivity for size, with enormous eyes or forests of antenna. Their titanic bodies can provide a place of safety and sustenance to whole ecologies of strange and sometimes voracious life created by the Tribe's legendary Fecundity. Of course, it need not be said how a being of immense size might manifest divine Might.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Progenitor</span><br /> <br /> The Bahamutans trace their descent back to a Progenitor labelled Bahamat. Reputedly a fish or whale of immense size, it was said that Bahamat was the spine of the world and supported whole cities on its back, his enormous size gave entire nations shelter from waves and storms unimaginable in today's post-antediluvian world, yet when roused his hanger would topple mountains and shake the very heart of the world.<br /> <br /> Modern Bahamutans see obvious parallels between their Progenitor, their restraint and their relationship to their cult. For spiritual and more human Leviathans Bahamat's role as a source of life and safety is a point of pride and comfort. Others say the power and fury their Progenitor would display when angered proves the Strain possesses a lost tradition as warrior judges who punish traitors and troublemakers.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Puberty</span><br /> <br /> It begins with distance. As master of the natural armours and Vitality of the tribe a Bahamatun's inheritance first manifests by a feelings of inner security. What once seemed like enormous problems seem small, easily solvable but also unimportant. In these early days the hardest and most important thing is for the Leviathan to maintain a sense of proportion. Some describe it as an almost dreamlike state where the world seems formed of mist, where force and reaction seem unrelated. What feels like a simple push topples trees, an attempt to rescue a drowning man churns the beach into muck. The first step taken by many Bahamatuans is to relearn their own strength.<br /> <br /> Bahamatun families, even those unaware of their own heritage, have a moderate tendency to be surprisingly calm when a new Bahamatuan emerges. Sometimes this is stoicism, sometimes shock, but it always gives a little breathing room that gives the family time to get to grips, or succumb to the wake, before making any rash decisions.<br /> <br /> A curious fact is that Bahamatuans usually emerge in a group and when they do, even if they had never met before, they lack the territorial instincts that most Leviathans feel against each other. They may also include any other Bahamatuan who was a family figure in their upbringing in their instinctual trust though this is unreliable. A Cohort formed of related Bahamatuans can be among the most stable and thus the most successful in the Tribe, however instincts to cooperate can repress disagreement leading to stagnation. Even worse, repressed feelings can escape in other self destructive ways or build up until they explode.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Genetics</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Family</span><br /> <br /> Bearing both the Vestiges of Fecundity and Vitality the Strain has the reputation for voracious breading but also having the ability to weather the rigours of reproduction. Bahamatain families are often impressively large, bearing more children than most strains and loosing far fewer to infighting or birth defects. This size and stability can make Bahamatain families a culture all onto themselves with outsiders marrying into the clan only after it's been determined that they will fit in without making waves. If no one can be found, the Strain is remarkably resistant to the dangers of incest.<br /> <br /> Don't be fooled, Bahamat's blood has problems all of it's own. The tight-kit and self-sustaining structure of a Bahamatan clan conceals a stifling tendency to self-replicate and an abhorrence of change and independence. Many Bahamatains have found their family unchanged since the Leviathan that founded the clan, and awash with heirlooms, advice and talents uniquely sorted to whatever problems faced their ancestor. In such cases it is a great challenge to reform the clan in his own image, many Leviathans simply flee and start their own family elsewhere. It has been noted that once a generation of Leviathans departs, two generations at the most, Behamut's mystical inheritance departs and the clan is assimilated into the modern world or destroyed by their own obsolescence.<br /> <br /> Bahamatain families can exist independent of an extended clan. Such families are marked by extreme internal loyalty and, while they are not shunned by outsiders it's obvious to all that their family comes first and they are treated accordingly. Leviathans from such families find that the hardest part is the irrevocable change in their relationship after claiming their Birthright, or the distance they must create to protect their family from the Wake.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Reproduction</span><br /> <br /> There seems to be some sort of mechanism at work in bloodlines touched by Bahamut. Some subconscious system that prevents a Leviathan being born until there is space for a new arrival. Of course this isn't to say it's polite enough to wait for parents who genuinely want a Leviathan, yet as a general rule Bahamatuns are rarely born to parents struggling to get by, and most commonly emerge in times of prosperity and expansion. This trait is amplified when there are living Bahamatuns present: A Bahamatun finding herself pressed for resources will rarely discover that a nephew is the latest addition to their worries.<br /> <br /> Bahamutans normally arrive in a group of between two and three at a time. These individuals often show some remarkable similarities even before coming into their Heritage: Appearance, mannerisms, an odd trait like shared allergies. This isn't that surprising in long running Bahamutan families but for Bahamatains with a culturally normal background it can be quite the shock meeting your nearly identical third cousin for the first time at a family reunion. Bahamatun families with a more Tribe oriented culture and no access to prophecies often look for odd similarities as portents of an future Leviathan. Identical twins (either actual identical twins or fraternal twins who happen to look identical, that happens a lot) are considered an especially auspicious sign. When born to a bloodline touched by Bahamut if one identical twin is a Leviathan the other certainly is too.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lahmasu</span><br /> <br /> The line of Lahmasu that Bahamut's lineage produces are the Gugal or &quot;great bulls.&quot; The strain is distinguished by characteristically large builds and often a distinctly aquatic appearance, especially later in life. Uniquely among Lahmasu the Gugal tend towards genetically stable populations - often taken to extremes, a Gugal community eventually ends up populated with genetically identical inhabitants. Many prefer the company of their own, where their distinctive appearances are accepted.<br /> <br /> There are entire underwater cities and nations populated exclusively by Gugal. Some have been a source of Leviathans for centuries, being remade each generation and producing Bahamutans who's ignorance of the surface and tales of underwater life both fascinate other Leviathans and leave them afraid of the damage that ignorance might cause. Other cities have long lost their share of Bahamat's mystical inheritance and retain only his genetic legacy, some of these cities worship ancestral Opheons or zealously worship long dead gods in hope that one day Bahamut's favoured children will return to them. Others, unshackled from the legacy of stifling self-replication, pursue strange sciences and magics unknown upon the surface and vow to defend their independence from any would be conqueror god, even their own children.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Vestiges</span><br /> <br /> Vitality, Awareness, Fecundity, Might<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Symbols and Associations</span><br /> <br /> The Sea of Salahit, the Caspian Sea, the vice of Sloth.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Concepts</span><br /> <br /> Awkward young linebacker, high-stakes fisherman, neighbourhood protector, surprisingly burly kindergarten teacher, professional wrestler, church camp counsellor<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Quote</span><br /> <br /> &quot;This is a good place. I like it here, and I spent years making sure it remains the sort of place I like. Usually this involves making sure punks like you don\u2019t bother the good people of this town. Then it becomes the sort of place they don\u2019t like. You still sure you want to set up shop here?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-11-2015, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T10:41:41-07:00","id":512121,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I like how the Cult chapter has turned out so far. Although, how exactly does a Leviathan Cult interact with a Mummy cult? Does it just map Piety=Reach, Grasp=Fervor? Or are we going to leave that out for now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T11:28:37-07:00","id":512158,"title":"","content":"Grasp=Fervor. Piety+1 = Reach.<br /> <br /> Fervor is roughly equal to Mummy Grasp until they get to high Sheol and unlock levels of violence that Mummies can't hope for. Typically a Leviathan Cult can't get past Reach 2! Yes, that limited. Organising specifically to get around their weaknesses can bump their maximum up to Reach 4, which is still inferior to Scorpion Cults.<br /> <br /> It's only when a Leviathan gets so powerful that their very existance warps reality and empowers their cultists that, combined with special organisation, they can eventually match or possibly exceed a Mummy's cult at Reach.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't look too closely at the Merits when comparing Leviathan and Mummy Cults. The fact that Home Turf is better than Mummy's +1 Reach/Grasp for being near their Tomb isn't because Leviathans are better with territory. It's a different game assumption, owning a creepy lovecraft town is far more central to Leviathan's themes than Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-12-2015, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T13:36:44-07:00","id":512280,"title":"","content":"How does this come up in the gameplay? Will players be using their cults a lot, or will they be a more background thing? In the old wiki, there's a style that revolves around the leviathan being the background entity and using the cult as the main play factor- is that kinda thing gonna be easier/ more interesting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T14:12:24-07:00","id":512329,"title":"","content":"People who have experience in playing Mummy games might be able to give a more detailed answer than me. However I imagine players will be using their cults a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T13:35:02-07:00","id":515407,"title":"","content":"The beginnings of my attempt at the Mad Arab.<br /> <br /> <i>Beneficent One.<br /> <br /> I have spent long and hard at the translations of the texts you bequeathed unto me. While I have spent all that was needed to fully clear the text of any errors, I plead your forgiveness; there is almost certainly problems in this English version. Not because of lack of competence on the efforts of my allies in academia, but because I am sure a significant portion of these books are not Medieval Arabic. The author seems to have either invented or miswrote several words, and both seem...problematic. The invented words don't generally follow Arabic conventions, but they seem awfully consistent for misprints.<br /> <br /> For example, his name. The name &quot;Abdul Alhazred&quot; is, quite simply, phonetically impossible. &quot;Al-&quot; is a morpheme that cannot be used twice in a row. Since his name only appears once throughout the texts, I have transposed it into a close Modern Arabic equivalent, one whose meaning seems fitting enough. And yet, &quot;Alhazred&quot; makes sense from an </i>English <i>perspective, on the term &quot;All has read&quot; or even &quot;Hazard&quot;, both of which make sense as pseudonyms.<br /> <br /> Also, there's something else; he mentions your name. </i><br /> <br /> <b>The Travels of Abd-al-Hazred </b><br /> <br /> ...It was at that point that I finally arrived at the final truth that had so long troubled me. The vision marked my form of humanity as small because it <i>was </i>small, a tiny part of the whole of Creation, A beauty eclipsed by grander beauty, a meaning lost in meaning. It was always a foolish thing to assume &quot;the image of god&quot; was two arms, two legs, and a mind to somehow confront the difficulties posed by such a form that has neither the strength of a beast or the magic of smokeless fire. No, Creation was far greater than me, the Earth, and even the stars in the Heavens themselves. And I knew from my vision, the beholding of the sea-jinn's soul, that even the fragment of the image that human's embodies was omniferrous and flexible, with even the capacity of becoming as a jinn itself.<br /> <br /> A rather foolish proposition. The jinn are mighty, but humans in all their forms are the perfected creations of God. As the myths and stories state, a human, a true human, is able to bend them to their will. While that art is beyond me, and I have little doubt the thrill of such power corrupts lesser men, I certainly know enough of it to thieve the smokeless fire, however briefly, and my goal is purer. Through examining humanity's predecessors, I will harden the clay that composes me, and so attain a form capable of beholding Allah and the angels as they truly are, without my insignificant perceptions blinding me to their true glory...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T14:16:27-07:00","id":515437,"title":"","content":"Thanks Leliel, now for my feedback. Sorry it's so critical.<br /> <br /> <br /> I looked it up and you're right, Abdul Alhazredisn't a real Arabic name. However in that case I think what I'd do is say that the Leviathan version of the Mad Arab, is simply called Abd-al-Hazred. As I said previously, I intend for him to be an actual medieval Arab. (BTW the word &quot;problematic&quot; is shibboleth for left wing academia/activism. It's an odd choice for a cultist to use)<br /> <br /> That said, I thought &quot;he mentions your name&quot; was a great touch. Definitely keep that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Moving on to the second part. The first paragraph was good, but I'd cut the jinn out entirely. They might exist in the WoD, but so does many things and they have little to do with Leviathan. Abd-al-Hazred certainly wouldn't refer to a Leviathan as a sea-jinn. One of the Progenitors, Bahamut, is from Arabian myth, he'd have a frame of reference. So, I'd just suggest removing the jinn entirely, it's only a few words and won't cause any damage.<br /> <br /> The second paragraph needs work though. It should be entirely about his plans to steal power from the Tribe and use it to study Allah's creation, rather than his dismissive views of different sorcery traditions. That will set up nicely for the future entries that detail his encounter with each Strain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-15-2015, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T17:11:27-07:00","id":515609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=515437#post515437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Leliel, now for my feedback. Sorry it's so critical.<br /> <br /> <br /> I looked it up and you're right, Abdul Alhazredisn't a real Arabic name. However in that case I think what I'd do is say that the Leviathan version of the Mad Arab, is simply called Abd-al-Hazred. As I said previously, I intend for him to be an actual medieval Arab. (BTW the word &quot;problematic&quot; is shibboleth for left wing academia/activism. It's an odd choice for a cultist to use)<br /> <br /> That said, I thought &quot;he mentions your name&quot; was a great touch. Definitely keep that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Moving on to the second part. The first paragraph was good, but I'd cut the jinn out entirely. They might exist in the WoD, but so does many things and they have little to do with Leviathan. Abd-al-Hazred certainly wouldn't refer to a Leviathan as a sea-jinn. One of the Progenitors, Bahamut, is from Arabian myth, he'd have a frame of reference. So, I'd just suggest removing the jinn entirely, it's only a few words and won't cause any damage.<br /> <br /> The second paragraph needs work though. It should be entirely about his plans to steal power from the Tribe and use it to study Allah's creation, rather than his dismissive views of different sorcery traditions. That will set up nicely for the future entries that detail his encounter with each Strain.</div> </div> </div> </div>....That's critical?<br /> <br /> I have little problem with that.<br /> <br /> The second paragraph is the result of my thinking along the lines that he's a bit narcisstic and megalomanical, but I don't need putting down other people for he to bring himself up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T23:29:42-07:00","id":515875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=515609#post515609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....That's critical?</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess it wasn't then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=515609#post515609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second paragraph is the result of my thinking along the lines that he's a bit narcisstic and megalomanical, but I don't need putting down other people for he to bring himself up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad assumption, normal people don't decide to get involved with sanity rending demigods so he'd have to have something. I'd say it's hubris rather than narcasism or megalomania though. Like the typical Awakened he doesn't go around putting other people down, but is quick to dismiss criticisms of himself or go beyond his limits. Of course, he's badass enough to get away with it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't try too hard to fit it in though. It's written from the first person and since hubris means you downplay or ignore criticisms, it would probably be something the viewer has to deduce from his actions. Also, while Abd-al-Hazred is the viewpoint charachter, the actual purpose of his journals is to provide flavour to illustrate each Strain - which also means after this introduction there's less room to focus on Abd-al-Hazred himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T19:39:11-07:00","id":516658,"title":"","content":"Okay, second draft.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Beneficent One.<br /> <br /> I have spent long and hard at the translations of the texts you bequeathed unto me. While I have spent all that was needed to fully clear the text of any errors, I plead your forgiveness; there is almost certainly problems in this English version. Not because of lack of competence on the efforts of my allies in academia, but because I am sure a significant portion of these books are not Medieval Arabic. The author seems to have either invented or miswrote several words, and both theories have large problems that cannot be accounted for. The invented words don't generally follow Arabic conventions, but they seem awfully consistent for misprints.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Also, there's something else; he mentions your name. </i><br /> <br /> <b>The Travels of Abd-al-Hazred </b><br /> <br /> ...It was at that point that I finally arrived at the final truth that had so long troubled me. The vision marked my form of humanity as small because it <i>was </i>small, a tiny part of the whole of Creation, A beauty eclipsed by grander beauty, a meaning lost in meaning. It was always a foolish thing to assume &quot;the image of god&quot; was two arms, two legs, and a mind to somehow confront the difficulties posed by such a form that has neither the strength of a beast or the magic of smokeless fire. No, Creation was far greater than me, the Earth, and even the stars in the Heavens themselves. And I knew from my vision, the beholding of the ocean daughter's soul, that even the fragment of the image that those humans embody was omniferrous and flexible, with even the capacity of becoming as Bahamut itself, a living foundation of the world.<br /> <br /> But the limitations posed by humanity, I realized, were still vexing my ultimate goal. I realized my initial scholarship was naive, in and of itself; it is not just the <i>hadith </i>that are flawed, a thousand canons written by a million different flawed humans, it was that humans are flawed to begin with. How was I supposed to truly behold the mind and image of Allah if there was no being on Earth in my learned experience that even begins to approach the complexity of even this minute, forgettable corner of the True World? No, I would have to approach the zenith of scholarship not as a philosopher alone, but an engineer and architect. I would have to understand the foundations of Creation to understand where to even begin in my explorations of its palace, and from there understand and behold the Builder of the palace.<br /> <br /> What better place to begin than by seeing the world as Bahamut does, from the foundations itself and eternally looking upwards? And what better way to become as Bahamut than through interrogation and mimicry of its descendants?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T07:45:12-07:00","id":517013,"title":"","content":"It's looking good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Reading this, what I'm thinking is that with a few minor modifications this would be the introduction to Abd-al-Hazred himself, it will go at the opening to the Strains section of the book. That way when we get to the individual splats readers already know who Adb-al-Hazred is and why he's commenting on the Strains. So onto the red lining.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=516658#post516658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ocean daughter's soul</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd change this to Ocean Mother's soul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=516658#post516658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;And I knew from my vision, the beholding of the ocean daughter's soul, that even the fragment of the image that those humans embody was omniferrous and flexible, with even the capacity of becoming as Bahamut itself, a living foundation of the world.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> this section talks about becoming more than human, thus I think it would fit best after the section about the limitations of humanity. I would put it imediately after &quot;engineer and architect&quot;.<br /> <br /> That also gives a replacement for Bahamut by name. Instead of &quot;with even the capacity of becoming as Bahamut itself, a living foundation of the world&quot; you could something like &quot;be distilled and studied given only the proper tools&quot;.<br /> <br /> The final paragprah can then be replaced with him explaining why The Tribe are the proper tools - because they have divine power but mortals can wrest that power from them.<br /> <br /> <br /> The stuff about Bahamut as a pillar of the world is good - so definitively keep that as the central theme for Bahamut's entry. Perhaps make the source of his understanding an encounter with a cult that would row to an &quot;island&quot; to prey every morning, then one day the Bahamutan swam off. A literal pillar of the world and a pillar of society. Hmmm, framing each Strain's entry as a personal encounter would probably work quite well.<br /> <br /> Anyway enough from me. Like I said, it's looking good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T13:30:17-07:00","id":517296,"title":"","content":"And I have something to contribute myself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Dagonites</span><br /> <br /> [Picture: The Symbol of Dagon: A wooden carved statue representing a bust of a man. His cheeks are hollow and his eyes are bulging like a fish\u2019s, but he has a full Sumerian-style beard. The bust has claw marks imprinted on it.]<br /> <br /> [Picture: Central. A young woman with shoulder-length black hair. She wears a light gray business suit with a white baby-tee underneath. Her shoes are stylish and heeled, but not ostentatious. She has an attractive full, rounded figure without being really fat. From the collar of her tee-shirt, you can see patterned patches of colour like the skin of an octopus reaching up to her ear. She is leaning against the edge of a desk, nearby a window. In her left hand is a pair of glasses, half-folded. In her extended right hand, she is holding a practical butcher\u2019s knife, blade first as if she was offering it to someone. ]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Theology</span><br /> <br /> The world is a raging tempest and man is a drop of water before the storm. Disease, famine or an invading army could crush anybody without even noticing, and so men tell themselves it is otherwise. If I pray tonight the crops will have rain tomorrow. If I burn these incenses my daughter will be healed. If I sacrifice my firstborn son the gods shall grant me victory in battle. The children of Dagon hear their prayers, and they shiver in pleasure.<br /> <br /> More than any other Strain, the Dagonites revel in their divine power. Their divine instincts whisper to them, telling them to open their eyes and see the naked truth of a world where the strong eats the weak. Telling them that nobody can depend upon morality or justice, that if such things even exist they it is only because someone had the power to back them up. Most of all it tells them that they are gods, they alone have true power. And yet their human mind looks out and sees differently, they see the need to hide from a mighty humanity, they see weak men thriving under the protection of the law. Every Dagonite resolves this contradiction in their own way, or is torn apart by it.<br /> <br /> Their cults reflect the same truths. The Wake imposes upon their Beloved, not a feeling of powerless, but an understanding of how powerlessness they always were. To a Dagonite's cultist submission to a Leviathan is, paradoxically, about seizing control. If they could only present their god with the correct offerings they could control the rains. If they could only become high priest then surely they would have the power to look any king in the eye and say no. A Dagonite's cult is a vicious cesspool of backstabbing, power-grabbing, and competition for the God's favour. Dagonites love every minute of it.<br /> <br /> Until the cult's turmoil attracts the wrong attention and the Dagonite realises that even a demigod is powerless before a true deity.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Morphology</span><br /> <br /> The line of Dagon is traditionally considered as the meeting point between primordial muck and higher life. As the heirs to the Progenitors\u2019 Fecundity no Dagonite is truly a single creature. The Strain is inhabited by or swims in symbiosis with lesser creatures which are, in fact, simply another part of the Leviathan's body. The most common Dagoinite traits are those of the simple fish, a clade which has multiplied beyond all others in the sea. Bulging eyes, gaping mouths and slimy scales, a fish's most unsettling traits, can be found in abundance. A Dagonites' symbiotes typically echo barnacles, coral or maritime plantlife but more mobile creates are far from unknown. At their extreme a Dagonite may be an entire school with no primary body and some of the most ancient Dagonites are entire ecosystems that travel the ocean assimilating everything in their path.<br /> <br /> The most common manifestations of Predation among Dagon's get are the most insidious. Paralytic toxins and incapacitating venoms. Needle thin barbed spines. Weapons to disable and control. Anemone cling to their bodies dripping with venom or a cloud of thin tentacles spreads around them laced with toxins. Those who favour the Vestige of Elements typically express it through their Fecundity, pushing it to greater extremes until the ocean around them is more microscopic life than water. Awareness touches Dagonites lightly, and typically manifests as an exaggeration of fish traits. To the Strain a Fish's bulging eyes are a icon of confidence and power, able to see the harsh truths of the world without blinking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Progenitor</span><br /> <br /> Dagonites claim their ancestry in the Progenitor Dagon. An endless wellspring of life, Dagon's womb contained the power of creation itself and his rule held dominion over the harvests, the rains, but also over rituals and religion. It was Dagon who taught mankind rituals and observances to control the a tempestuous world and so his get honour him as the Hierarch, as Dagon's rituals were free of the theology and covenants that bind mankind's gods Dagon is also honoured as the Arch-Heretic. Modern Dagonites boast that their ancestor was the last Progenitor to fall before Marduk and the rituals he bequeathed to the Tribe are the weapons that will one day reclaim the heavens.<br /> <br /> While Dagon is honoured by his descendants, compared to the other Strains relatively few Dagonites relate to Dagon as a deity. The typical Dagonite believes Dagon's death was final and honour their ancestor as a paragon and a culture hero. He is the example that shows how a god should relate to his flock and an inspiration for those Leviathans who still fight their ancestral war. As a consequence Dagon is the progenitor with the most consistent depiction among the Tribe's art. He is a man with bulging fish like eyes, a full Sumerian beard and a fish's tail; his belly swollen in pregnancy.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Metamorphosis</span><br /> <br /> Transition begins with the flesh. The first a Dagonite notices of his heritage is some physical affliction. These are impermanent and fluid markers, attempting to peal away a patch of scales will cause them to melt into flesh. Just as it seems like the fledgeling may come to terms with their condition the effects spread outwards. Attempting to remove an affliction causes it to burst in blood and small sea life. Small animals bearing outlandish mutations follow the Leviathan in slavish loyalty, the Wake begins during this time. Many Dagonites have to question where they end and other creatures begin. Who is an individual with their own thoughts and desires and who is merely a part of them to be used as one uses their own arm? The creatures in her blood? The loyal animals who follow her around? Her Beloved? Everyone?<br /> <br /> Due to the insular and cultic nature of many established Dagonite families, the arrival of a new Leviathan is typically responded too with well rehearsed rituals. This can provide a sense of stability both to the young Leviathan and her mortal family, however depending on the nature of these rituals some Dagonites honestly would have preferred naked panic. Away from cults Dagon's blood seems to lead towards no particular reaction.<br /> <br /> As his puberty progresses a Dagonite feels a growing instinct to emigrate, and for good reason. The stereotype says they tire of family and seek unclaimed lands to conquer, and while there is some truth in this they are in fact instinctively fleeing their own blood. Should the Dagonites remain, whether out of familial loyalty, a deliberate (and usually successful) attempt to breed more Leviathans or some other reason, then the touch of Dagon's blood continues to strengthen. Whether mystical effect of Dagon's blood or just the result of so many Leviathans possessing the powers of Fecundity in the gene pool, the family homeland is soon plagued with feral Lahmasu and mass graves filled with the young victims of horrible diseases.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ecology</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Family</span><br /> <br /> The Dagonite Strain is cited as the most fruitful but least nurturing of the Strains - the bloodline begets miscarriages, stillborn and birth defects, but also twins, triplets and even larger clutches. The social dynamics of a Dagonite\u2019s family are as unhealthy as the genetics and plagued with infighting, with members constantly disowning their blood and setting off into the wider world. It takes powerful social factors to keep a Dagonite family together, and that usually requires a cult.<br /> <br /> Thus Dagon\u2019s family tree takes shape. Scattered around the world are the primary bloodlines, cults where the Dagon\u2019s heritage is most concentrated, and most numerous for those cults don\u2019t have a social expectation that you\u2019d stop after a few kids. Surrounding those cults is a enormous but thin web of exiles, refugees and disowned relatives. Those distant cousins are typically assimilated into mortal culture, most are unaware of their heritage and aside from a tendency to large dysfunctional families and genetic disorders they are indistinguishable from regular anyone else. As the generations progress some cults fall, others are formed, and the distant cousins marry each other or get indoctrinated into cults just a little too often to be chance. When enough different Dagonite bloodlines meet new Leviathans are born.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the most fundamental question you can ask a Dagonite is \u201cwere you born into a cult\u201d? A Dagonite born into a cult is surrounded with knowledge of the Tribe and endlessly pliable followers, but the size of a Dagonite cult means they may face immediate competition from other young Leviathans. In addition they are unlikely to have had any positive role models. Due to the pyramid shape of most cults, the odds are that a Dagonite grew up on the bottom rungs, envying the elder's\u2019 power and possibly fearing them too. Upon their first metamorphosis power is thrust upon them without any of the experiences they might have gained through climbing the ladder.<br /> <br /> In contrast a Dagonite born outside a cult is probably born into a life of conflict, if only typical family drama, but this conflict is tempered by immersion in mortal society which while flawed is superior to the Tribes in every way. His family is unlikely to have much knowledge of the tribe. If he is lucky they might have a heirloom in the attic, or perhaps he overheard a few mentions of the bad old days before his mother walked out on the family, at best the family may have uncovered some genuine knowledge after investigating Hybrids or Lahamsu children.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Reproduction</span><br /> <br /> In it's way Dagon's blood is the one that makes the most sense to modern understandings of genetics. While Leviathans of any Strains are most commonly born to bloodlines that have given birth to Leviathans before this tendency is most pronounced in the Dagonites. The more Dagonites in your recent ancestry, the more Lahmasu in your immediate family, the more likely you are to be a Leviathan yourself.<br /> <br /> Because the blood of Dagon weighs genetics heavily, if one Leviathan begins his transition it's likely that others will soon follow. As many as five or six may appear, typically among siblings and first cousins over two or three generations. While this period can be extended even further it stereotypically ends when the young Leviathans yearn for control and power and leave their birthplace to forge their own petty kingdoms. The family splits, new converts are brought into the fold and the bloodline thins for a time.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lahmasu</span><br /> <br /> The Dagonites lay claim to the Lahmasu Abuu, or &quot;fathers&quot; (singular Abum, often read &quot;Patriarchs&quot;). The bloodline is distinguished by both grotesque fertility and the appearance of overlarge eyes, scales, and similar piscine features as the blood of Dagon becomes more pronounced - visual markers that betray the &quot;purity&quot; of a bloodline and signify, in the minds of the Lahmasu, greater connection to the revered Tribe.<br /> <br /> Abuu share much of the same instinctual understanding of power as their Leviathan cousins, though as Lahmasu their instincts are quieter and easier to ignore. When an Abbu listens his instincts tell the Dagonite philosophy from a different angle. While a Dagonite instinctively feels that morality and justice only exist at the sufferance of those with power, an Abuu instinctively feels that somebody, themselves, needs to enforce morality. However the Abuu share the Dagonite\u2019s instinctual belief that only divine beings possess power, and Lahmasu are barely divine. At their best they are vissers and priests who help Leviathans use their powers productively or pios priests in humanities churches. At their worst, and under the Wake Abuu are usually at their worst, they are scheming would be puppet masters. Either way Abuu are driven to size power and use it to create a society for their people.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Vestiges</span><br /> <br /> Fecundity, Elements, Predation, Sanctity<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Symbols and Associations</span><br /> <br /> The Sea of Harkand, the Cilician Sea, the vice of Pride.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Concepts</span><br /> <br /> Ubermensch, Contract lawyer, backwoods patriarch, small-town mayor, preacher, head cheerleader, militia leader<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Quote</span><br /> <br /> &quot;When you put your trust in me, that makes me responsible for what you do. I know you did it out of love, and I know you regret it now. But what happened is still inexcusable. And I\u2019m sorry, I really am, but I can\u2019t trust that it won\u2019t happen again. For what it\u2019s worth, I will miss you.&quot; <hr /><br /> And this is just me having a bit of fun, it probably won't go in the final product.<br /> <br /> Leviathan's like having Beasts around, both instinctively understand the importance of family and you cannot overestimate how useful it is to have someone you can tell to Honour Thy Father and take a middle management role in the cult without screwing it up. Beasts in turn appreciate how easily it is to hold a family dinner when all you need is a bathtub full of water, and hey, if you get powers through kinship who wouldn't want to be kin with gods?<br /> <br /> However Beasts are not quite immune to the Wake. The instinctitual fear and subservience affects them too, but the wakes effect is most pronounced upn the Primordial Dream. So long as a Beasts Lair is at least two dots lower than a Leviathan's Sheol then they add the traits &quot;ocean&quot; and &quot;stormy&quot; to their Lair. A Minatour standing next to a Leviathan may find his maze is knee deep in sea water and filled with heavy wind. If the Lair already had one of those traits it will not duplicate or get double power; however the Leviathans presence will always provide sufficient resonance to draw the Lair forth.<br /> <br /> One thing a Beast should <b>never</b> do is invite a Leviathan into his own Lair. The Primordial Dream is mankind's, not the Tribes. Leviathans have their own, the Rift, and a Beast who brings a Leviathan into their own Lair is trying to contain the entire Rift within a handful of chambers. A Beast who even attempts such a thing is instantly aware what is happening, if they don't change directions then the Rift will burst into the Lair like a tidal wave, destroying it utterly and then pouring forth into the primordial dream. If left unchecked the leak would eventially prove be catastrophic for mankind and worse for the Tribe - but powerful Conspiracies and even Gods would notice the collective mindscapes of two Tribes at war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-20-2015, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T12:36:02-07:00","id":528005,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Oceaneads</span><br /> <br /> Who am I? Am I more than a face in the crowd? A cog in the machine? What makes me special?<br /> <br /> Perhaps it is the god you follow. She named her chosen people, and you are one of them. You wear the icons, you sing the praises, and that's why you're more than the unwashed masses. Perhaps you even live up to her teachings.<br /> <br /> It's not that Oceaneads see themselves as teachers or leaders, the best of them do but this is their human self making the best of far more primordial instincts. Deep down Oceaneads just like control. There's something inside each one that sees how desperately mortals clinging to them for their identity and loves it. Some Oceaneads enjoy tormenting their beloved, teaching them contradictory beliefs and watching the fallout or asking them to them violate their sense of self, the parts of it that don't come from associating with her. Most enjoy the fact they don't have to, their instincts are for control, not sadism, and watching cultists desperately trying to please her provides satisfaction.<br /> <br /> The cultists that follow an Oceanead are inflicted with absolute knowledge of their own insignificance by her Wake. In response they heap praise upon their deity. They place her on a pedestal as a symbol of everything they are not and hope some of her glory will reflect upon them. Oceneads find themselves surrounded by fawning sycophants who constantly wage passive aggressive wars for the Leviathan's attention and favour, most Oceaneads are amused by how pathetic it is.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Morphology</span><br /> <br /> Oceaneads are renowned among the tribe for their grace and beauty. Their forms draw from the most vibrant and colourful of sealife, traits taken from dolphins and tropical fish can be found in abundance. Other Oceaneads reflect the majesty of whales or mythical creatures: Aquatic dragons and sea serpents with a regal continence and shining scales. Most strikingly the blood of Oceanus can retain human characteristics, some Oceaneads are essentially mermaids even in their most divine form. An Oceanead's body may extend beyond the biological with halos or aura's that display the Strain's revered Sanctity, but this is only a minority and such Leviathans are no greater than their unadorned cousins, no matter how much they boast otherwise.<br /> <br /> When Oceaneads inherit the Vestige of Predation they do so with elegance. Their claws are sharp and precise weapons in gleaming colours, more a rapier than broadsword. Their toxins and venoms are resplendent, as is the warning colours that sometimes manifest upon their forms. Their smile becomes even more alluring with a mouth full of elegant fangs. The vestigate of Might harkens to the Greek Gods of old with large yet tasteful muscles. In contrast the Vestiege of Elements rarely has visible manifestations, when it does it is a halo or aura that is either formed of the elements itself or visible only by disrupting the elements which pass through it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Progenitor</span><br /> <br /> The Oceanids reverar Oceanus as their ancestor. The king of the seas, the rivers, and the rightful ruler of the other Progenitors. That last one is hotly contested by the other Strains, but for all the churn and uncertainty within the Tribe\u2019s mythology the image of Oceanus as a ruler shows up with remarkable consistency - perhaps merely a commentary of his descendants\u2019 lust for power.<br /> <br /> In person Oceanus was said to be a terrible being, who demanded unwavering loyalty and would remake the minds of entire nations if denied his due or turn families against each other in a night of blood and madness to make examples. Modern Oceaneads see this as an lesson, a parable of how far the tribe has fallen, if only because the ones who see Oceanus as an aspirational figure rarely survive long<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Metamorphosis</span><br /> <br /> It starts with a feeling, one day a new Oceanid wakes up to the sound of her heart pounding in her chest. Her palms are sweaty, adrenaline is pumping and she feels like queen of the world. At this early stage her goals are unchanged, merely pursued with greater confidence and, with a small measure of her inheritance, fulfilled to satisfaction. If she is not scared by hints of the supernatural behind her successes she may even enjoy it for a while. This cannot last, a young Oceanid's powers grow to meet each challenge. As her abilities becomes increasingly uncontrolled, she must confront her greatest challenge: mastering her own abilities and the quest for Tranquillity.<br /> <br /> Oceanids are unique in that their transition affects not just them but their close (both genealogically and geographically) family as well. These changes are permanent and the results are among the most healthy, and often physically human, Pelopsids to be found. Unsurprisingly this can be a time of great expansion, metaphorically as members rise in wealth and status, but also literally with successful courtships and newborn babies.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ecology</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Family</span><br /> <br /> An Oceanead instinctively sees their family as a regal bloodline and between their instincts and their Progenitors inheritance they usually get one. Typically an Oceanead begins with a large family which is then paired down by internal conflict until few members remain. The Strain is not known for voracious breading, at least not by the tribe's standard, but even an Oceanead's relatives are blessed with easy access to relationships and physically healthy children, Oceanus' inheritance runs towards unhealthy minds within sound bodies. Then the joyous early years give way to times of strife and hardship as a family full of narcissistic and conflict prone personalities begin their inevitable infighting. As the casualties rise and factions emerge the Oceanead gets the aristocratic bloodline she desired, with all the worst traits that implies.<br /> <br /> Oceaneads tend to be involved with their families, and it is the Leviathan's intervention that keeps the family from falling apart. Her presence give the family something to fight over and keeps child services away. Typically the prize is simply the Oceanead's favour, made irresistible by her Wake, but a successful Leviathan has no shortage of more material rewards to bestow. By the time things get really bad, when patriarchs or matriarchs start culling relatives to keep their branch pure and pleasing to their deity, the family is often so far removed from mortal society that assimilation is unthinkable and the conflicts will last long past the Leviathan's departure or demise. Such families depend upon a new Leviathan's arrival to bolster their numbers otherwise the conflict will inevitably drive them to extinction.<br /> <br /> For all that a childhood in an dynastic family is awful, the experience can provide a Leviathan with a wealth of useful skills and resources just as it robs them of a healthy human childhood which they might use to remember morality and humanity. The infighting can teach an Oceanead much about politics and family conflicts that will prove useful in similar conflicts with her fellow Leviathans, while the family's aristocratic self image means that Oceanead families are among the most likely to preserve Hairlooms and information about their lineage which can provide a great boon to a Leviathan who delves into her history. Inevitably people will seek to escape unhealthy dynamics and a Leviathan born away from the conflict will often find that the topics older relatives won't talk about are just as telling. Oceanead families rarely truely escape their past, being apart from it will define generations as surely as being a part of it would have done, though less negatively, and the main dynasties are still there waiting for a Leviathan to come asking for the family tree.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Reproduction</span><br /> <br /> Chronologically the lasting Oceanid bloodlines are among the most reliable for the tribe. Within a family the number of generations between Leviathans remains constant to within a few generations. The Strain as a whole, however, does not have a set timetable and even within a family the period may slowly change over time, increasing or decreasing by a few generations every cycle.<br /> <br /> While the Oceanids can reliably tell when their inheritance will next be bestowed knowing where it will appear is a lot harder. A new Oceanid can be born to almost any direct descendent of a previous Oceanid. The only noticeable pattern is that all the Oceanids from a single cycle, typically just one or two, are roughly the same age. It's even possible for the inheritance to permanently move away from the family through the line of an illegitimate child or a single family member who cuts his ties; often this causes either celebration or a frenzy of family reunions as the family tries to find and reforge ties with the newborn Leviathan before their inheritance is forever lost.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lahmasu</span><br /> <br /> The Oceanids call their Lahmasu the Pelopsids. A Pelopsid tends to preserve the grace and beauty of their Leviathan ancestors but without any of the tact or social charm. Physically the Pelopsids are the most likely to wear their heritage lightly, the result is typically \u201cexotic beauty\u201d rather than \u201chideous mutant\u201d. When they don\u2019t look human a Pelopsid is still going to look good, colourful scales are in, slime and gaping mouths is out. Sometimes a Pelopsid is both at once, if a Leviathan meets an actual mermaid, it\u2019s probably a Pelopsid.<br /> <br /> This outer beauty is not reflected internally, or at least not by the Strain\u2019s instinctual nature. Oceaneads possess an instinctual sociopathy and a lust for control. Pelopsids just have the sociopathy. They lack the talent for manipulation and so many Pelopsids simply resort to base brutality or mental domination.<br /> <br /> In a Leviathan\u2019s Cults the Pelopsid\u2019s psychic abilities and the ability to walk among humanity make the Strain useful specialists for subtle work, while the Strain\u2019s tendency towards Might and Predation means no one should underestimate a Pelopsid\u2019s use as front line combatants. However Leviathan\u2019s often use Pelopsid\u2019s as trophies or ornamentation, a role most Pelopsids find innately unsatisfying and stressful.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Vestiges</span><br /> <br /> <b>Sanctity</b>, Elements, Might, Predation<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Symbols and Associations</span><br /> <br /> The Sea of Fars, the Ionian Sea, the vice of Lust.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Concepts</span><br /> Club diva, big man on campus, queen of the suburbs, reclusive CEO, bright young son of a political dynasty<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Quote</span><br /> &quot;People love beaches, perhaps now more than ever. You know why? Because there\u2019s no roof. You\u2019re totally exposed \u2013 the more you\u2019re naked, the more you\u2019re at ease. It\u2019s the place in the world where you\u2019re the most defenseless. Don\u2019t you think it\u2019s interesting that everyone rushes there?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-25-2015, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T13:45:09-07:00","id":528050,"title":"","content":"What made you add that bit about them having more 'human' final forms? Is it meant to reflect something that I missed, or is it just fluff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T14:23:21-07:00","id":528093,"title":"","content":"That entire section is just giving guidance for what they look like, so pure fluff. [edit - there's no particular reason for it. I just thought some players would like to play Posideon and Oceneads were the natural strain for that kind of thing.]<br /> <br /> If a visual helps - here's two examples of Oceaneads; one 'human', one not, both graceful and beautiful. (if I could find one the third example would be majestic rather than colourful)<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://th07.deviantart.net/fs71/PRE/f/2012/190/2/7/sea_goddess_by_james_face-d56lstq.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://fc08.deviantart.net/fs70/f/2011/135/6/b/6b34cb4b7c7f67b25361d677da46ed90-d3gezdo.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-25-2015, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:29:33-07:00","id":528447,"title":"","content":"Third times the charm?<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Beneficent One.<br /> <br /> I have spent long and hard at the translations of the texts you bequeathed unto me. While I have spent all that was needed to fully clear the text of any errors, I plead your forgiveness; there is almost certainly problems in this English version. Not because of lack of competence on the efforts of my allies in academia, but because I am sure a significant portion of these books are not Medieval Arabic. The author seems to have either invented or miswrote several words, and both theories have large problems that cannot be accounted for. The invented words don't generally follow Arabic conventions, but they seem awfully consistent for misprints.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Also, there's something else; he mentions your name. </i><br /> <br /> <b>The Travels of Abd-al-Hazred </b><br /> <br /> ...It was at that point that I finally arrived at the final truth that had so long troubled me. The vision marked my form of humanity as small because it <i>was </i>small, a tiny part of the whole of Creation, A beauty eclipsed by grander beauty, a meaning lost in meaning. It was always a foolish thing to assume &quot;the image of god&quot; was two arms, two legs, and a mind to somehow confront the difficulties posed by such a form that has neither the strength of a beast or the magic of smokeless fire. No, Creation was far greater than me, the Earth, and even the stars in the Heavens themselves.<br /> <br /> But the limitations posed by humanity, I realized, were still vexing my ultimate goal. I realized my initial scholarship was naive, in and of itself; it is not just the <i>hadith </i>that are flawed, a thousand canons written by a million different flawed humans, it was that humans are flawed to begin with. How was I supposed to truly behold the mind and image of Allah if there was no being on Earth in my learned experience that even begins to approach the complexity of even this minute, forgettable corner of the True World? No, I would have to approach the zenith of scholarship not as a philosopher alone, but an engineer and architect. I would have to understand the foundations of Creation to understand where to even begin in my explorations of its palace, and from there understand and behold the Builder of the palace. I must see as divinity does; an impossible task for a human without tools.<br /> <br /> The Ocean Mother's own kind, born of human flesh but of great Bahamut's blood. have that vision. They are ideal sources of that vision I need, born of the living foundations of the world. And in my travels, I have learned of many ways to tap that vaunted source...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T10:48:13-07:00","id":528955,"title":"","content":"Third time is the charm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T02:06:25-07:00","id":531802,"title":"","content":"Are the vestiges getting re-written, or are they reasonably gmc compatible? There was talk about leviathans getting 'transformed dots' a la princess- is that still a thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T05:06:05-07:00","id":531849,"title":"","content":"I plan to look at Vestiges again, some of them might remain unchanged. The Attribute boosters are going to go.<br /> <br /> Leviathans will get Transformed dots, but it won't be like Princess. Here's how <b>Atavisms</b> are going to work: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Depth</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Atavism</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Greater Atavism</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Ancient Atavism</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">-</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">-</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">-</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">-</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">-</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">-</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">-</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+3</td> </tr> </table></div> Leviathans begin play with one Atavaism, one Greater Atavism and one Ancient Atavism. They gain an additional Atavism at Sheol 3, an additional Greater Atavism at Sheol 6 and a final Ancient Atavism at Sheol 9<br /> <br /> You can stack multiple Atavisms on the same attribute, but you may never gain more than +7 to a single Attribute from Atavisms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T20:51:46-07:00","id":532727,"title":"","content":"When this is ready, I think it could do to have a Dark Eras-style historical setting. Any times and places stand out as particularly good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T10:05:23-07:00","id":534564,"title":"","content":"Sumer is a pretty obvious go to, and a lot of the stuff that's already around about it has themes on divinity etc- but all I can remember right now is that bit from the Deva write-up. The first civilisation of man gives a pretty good chance to leave a legacy behind and could help reinforce how stagnant leviathans are.<br /> This might be a bit tenuous, but I like the idea of a setting based on the Hindu/Zoroastrianism split- it's the kind of massive cult-based war that leviathans dream of. I can imagine them trying to capitalise on the newly forming religions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T10:23:35-07:00","id":545487,"title":"","content":"I have returned from vacation and now have internet access again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> expect the Tanninim soon.<br /> <br /> Good Dark Ears for Leviathan:<br /> <br /> Book of Judges Judea - the Judges were half priest and half warlord; basically humans acting like Leviathans. Or maybe the Judges actually were Leviathans (I don't think the Hunter era got funded).<br /> <br /> Early King Reign of Saul Judea - immediately after the Judges, a new king brings law and order, ending the time of warlords and fear.<br /> <br /> Golden age of Piracy - Leviathans are powerful and occult Davy Jones (Pirates of the Carribian - version) like pirates who rule through fear and sorcery. Opposing them are dashing Jack Sparrow esque swashbucklers. Two ideals of freedom battle - the freedom to do what you want to others; and the freedom from others doing onto you. Some justification would be required to keep Marduk activity to a minimal level.<br /> <br /> Pirates of Somalia - Lawlessness on the high seas in the modern era.<br /> <br /> Today - ISIS/ISIL could be portrayed as a very large Leviathan's cult. All you need is the inevitable ending when internal strife, Marduk or someone else destroys it. (Call me an optimist but I don't see ISIL lasting too long). Of course today isn't really a historical era <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - check your group is comfortable before running this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-08-2015, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T11:41:56-07:00","id":545587,"title":"","content":"I like idea of golden age of piracy, but where would you put cults? It seems like more mechanics would be needed to have them pilot ships. It'd be worth it to play as pirate-cthulhu though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:02:19-07:00","id":545601,"title":"","content":"Cults would naturally default to being your ships crew; and I imagine any piracy setting would need rules for ships <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T13:05:45-07:00","id":545699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=545601#post545601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cults would naturally default to being your ships crew; and I imagine any piracy setting would need rules for ships <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the actual piloting of a ship would be Drive, and coordinating the crew would use Cult mechanics for Leviathans, and be an Expression + Wits roll for non-Leviathans. Navigation based on Landmarks would be Wits + Survival, and navigation via astronomy would be Academics + Intelligence<br /> <br /> But that's just my rough thoughts right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T13:27:13-07:00","id":545721,"title":"","content":"How would stagnancy and the other themes carry over into piracy though? Would it be a Jack Sparrow-esque last of the pirates thing?<br /> If beast doesn't take Sumer, I still think it'd be cool to at least have a few story hooks and such related to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T15:07:44-07:00","id":545836,"title":"","content":"A Jack Sparrow-esque last of the pirates is exactly how it plays out. Law and order comes to the Caribbean. Human pirates are caught, become privateers, go legit or retire until eventually all that's left is the Leviathans who cannot adapt; they are all killed.<br /> <br /> Sumer is an hard one - since it would be drastically different depending on what the actual truth of the Leviathan's origins is. Is Marduk a literally a god or wizard who killed Tiamat? Is he just an ideal that led mankind to abandon the tribe's cults and build a civilised city instead? Arguably the best solution would be to do an ancient Sumer Era that says Marduk was just an ideal, or a distant god, and a completely contradictory Primordial era where Marduk walks around throwing lightning bolts and kills Tiamat by building the Tower of Babel.<br /> <br /> (Note that would probably be redundant with King Saul era)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T07:48:29-07:00","id":547046,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Tanninim</span><br /> <br /> [Picture: The Symbol of Tannin: A hanging piece of cloth, coarsely woven. The edges fray and resemble used fishing nets. The centre piece of the cloth depicts four snakes in a circle, each eating the body of the next one.]<br /> <br /> [Picture: Central. A young man in dress Navy uniform. He is currently pulling off his dress jacket, revealing a t-shirt on which several weapons have been strapped with medical sticking tape. All of the weapons are variations on harpoons and pointy metallic sticks, including a piece of sharpened rebar. The man is blonde, with a crew-cut and thin-rimmed glasses. His left hand has a crustacean-like look, with each knuckle articulated with the next like the segments on a lobster\u2019s body. He is smiling, looking down towards the ground.]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Theology</span><br /> <br /> Why don't you take what you want? Hurt whoever you want? The blood of Tannin remembers the Tribe's answer, a simple thing that predates mankind's moral philosophers. Fear.<br /> <br /> Now the Tanninim themselves are rarely afraid, their heritage brings the self confidence you'd expect when you know you're the most dangerous monster in the room; but they look upon others and something tells them the only reason she hasn't killed is fear of the punishment. These instincts, combined with the Strain's need for a controlled environment, at best drive the strain to impose their own brutal order and at worst create monsters who live and breath violence.<br /> <br /> Given all this you might expect a Tanninim's wake to inflict fear, but in truth the Tanninim create no more fear than their cousins. Their Wake is something far worse. A Tanninim's wake strips away morality and civilization, reducing their Beloved to a state of Primordial savagery. Not quite rabid beasts but something close: Brutal rapacious warlords and warriors. If a Tanninim starts to believe humanity is nothing more than a species of violent savages, it's because he spends his days surrounded by zealots kept from brutality only through fear of the Leviathan's displeasure. When the Tanninim forget why they shouldn't join in and start to take the results can be terrible indeed, Leviathan's have far less to fear from violence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Morphology</span><br /> <br /> The primordial form of a Tanninim betrays no weakness. Theirs is the greatest mastery of the Tribe's natural weapons; in this the Strain shows considerable diversity. All the sea's weapons can be found within the Tanninim. A shark's jaws with row upon row of razor teeth or a snapping turtle's beak, perhaps both. Wicked hooked claws, or strangling tentacles, maybe one upon the other. Venoms, barbs, spurs, the Tanninim have them all. The bodies they adorn with these weapons tend to be sleek and streamlined for pursuit, or squat and solid for the long fight. Bodies built like sharks, sea serpents, alligators, and other apex predators are common.<br /> <br /> Secondary Vestiges inherited by Tanninim are focused on the fight. Might works in conjunction with the Tanninim's natural weaponry, and the Leviathan who focuses on both will develop weapons that kill through simple kinetic energy. Claws to swing, horns to ram, or spines to impale during serpentine constriction. Vitality begets scales and shells, and combines with spikes or venomous tendrils to cover the body in protection. Only Awareness shows that the Strain are more than mere killers, with eyes that gaze into the soul or strange halos or symbonites bristling with odd sensory appendages. Nevertheless, a Tannaim's Awareness tends towards well defended sensory organs or multiple levels of redundancy.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Progenitor</span><br /> <br /> The Tanninim claim a beast called Tannin as their Progenitor, a figure who they claim is echoed in the Leviathan of the bible and in medieval images of the mouth of Hell. A monster who's glowing eyes would see through all deception, and who would stop at nothing to punish sinners.<br /> <br /> Hailed as the feircest and most terrible of Tiamet's brood, his descendants are quick to venerate Tanninim for his judgement and sense of duty, traits the Progenitor allegedly displayed in his role as the devourer of sinners and the executioner of the Tribe's enemies. Modern Tanninim hope these ideas will endear them to cousins weary of a Strain reputed for violent denmours and combat prowess or provide a cultural ideal fit for people who's very bodies are designed to fight and to kill.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Metamorphosis</span><br /> <br /> One moment he's fine, the next he feels his skin begin to itch. Within moments he's on fire and he knows he needs water. The first time even a drink can restore him and for a few days normality returns. From this point the attacks become more frequent and the cures more demanding until nothing short of immersion in natural running water will do. With time or tutoring he will learn that to prevent these attacks with control, both over his surroundings and over himself. Some favour rigid rules and routines that they enforce on all around them, or at least try to; the Wake helps. Others choose to seek authority but refrain from using it, and some find control in isolation. Regardless, the young Tanninim eventually applies this doctrine to him or herself, mastering the body through iron self discipline and beginning the quest for tranquillity.<br /> <br /> The ascension of a Tanninim can be a disaster for his human family. No one likes to suddenly find another claiming dominion over them. Among families unaware of the Tribe, some feign acceptance, they play along simply because they see it as a medical necessity. In most other cases the sheer desperation the fledgeling can feel around preventing their painful episodes can escalate to violence. While the Strain is usually late to their physical powers, nothing accelerates a Tanninim's development like combat. The family either has to call the police and hope their clawed son won't be shot on sight (plenty do make the call) or surrender to a more dangerous foe. When the family knows what's coming the usual response is the frenzied clean ups seen in organisations awaiting an important inspection, or for the entire family to run for the hills.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ecology</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Family</span><br /> <br /> A Tanninim's family is often their greatest victim. The Strain's innate need for order begins at home, as does their Wake and the brutal response lurking within their blood. A Tanninim's family, and for that matter their Beloved's descendants, are often traumatised for generations. Such families remember traditions and taboos which strike outsiders as backwards or puritanical, and most do keep a heavy rein on their members - for their protection, they might claim, though not all the touched families recall what it is they are truly protecting themselves against; given time the traditions become their own purpose, divorced from theology or worship.<br /> <br /> Most of these families are small, a product of frequent excommunications (or worse), traditions or just Tannim's mystical bloodline, but they are often physically healthy and with few mutations. Darwinian necessity purges Gibborim genes from the bloodline, or at least isolates it from more human descendants. Growing up in an isolated and traditional environment does little to aid many Tanninim in avoiding the stereotype of inquisitorial zeal that they are painted with.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Reproduction</span><br /> <br /> The heritage of Tannin favours direct descent. Father to son, mother to daughter. The Tanninim do not favour the sometimes bizarre leaps through cousins or nephews sometimes seen in other Strains. Age seems to play a part, with the first-born being the most likely to inherit, the second-born being second most likely and continuing down the chain. Sex also plays a part, with the current carrier more likely to pass the birthright to a child of his or her own (human) sex. Even parental favouritism plays a part. Since who exactly is carrying the heritage in the many generations without a Leviathan is essentially unknowable the Tanninim are only rarely aware of their tendency towards direct descent.<br /> <br /> When a Tanninim claims his birthright he usually does so alone. In the rare case that two or more Tanninim are born they will be immediate relatives: Two brothers, a mother and daughter or something along those lines. What's more, there will be a clear chain of authority between the two. It might be that one was older, or that one one was the parental favourite and the other was the least liked, or just that one is more popular in school. Even when it doesn\u2019t make sense they both know instinctively who is in charge and why. Whether they accept these instincts is another question, but in these early days when genetics and not choice govern which aspects of the Tribe's powers they hold, the lesser of the two would be strongly advised to avoid direct confrontation. Tanninim have one other unique trait, up to several months before they begin to develop their powers a Tanninim develops one minor trait such as eye colour or a small verbal tic that is identical to their most recent Leviathan ancestor. Any who knew that ancestor personally might recognise this trait as an early warning of a new Leviathan to be, other Tanninim, Gibborim \u2013 or the ancestor himself if he still lives \u2013 find this especially easy. To them it's instinct.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lahmasu</span><br /> <br /> The Tanninim proudly call their Lahmasu brethren the Gibborim, or &quot;mighty&quot; for the Strain shares the Tanninim's natural mastery of combat. Gibborim tend to born almost human, but most develop a frighting array of mutations as they age. Those that claim their inheritance in the womb are almost invariably fatal for a human mother and this means that as a family line grows further from the Leviathan that created it, the human descendants will eventually purge themselves of the potential to birth Gibborim. Often social ties fall just a quickly, for Gibborim are dangerous and frequently animalistic. Most Tanninim who wish to learn about their Lahmasu relatives find wild creatures living in an isolated lagoon, not mutated humans hidden away in some uncle's isolated farmhouse.<br /> <br /> In a cult the Gibborim's role is simple: Aarmed to - or with - the teeth, Gibborim are trained like soldiers, or like dogs, to serve as elite shock troops. A tendency towards Awareness means that they also make good trackers and guards, so long as subtly is not required. Tanninim often like to have Gibborim wonder around the cult's temples and strongholds giving people the evil eye to keep their Beloved afraid and in line. Outside of cults Gibborim are often too mutated to live among humanity, or to realize they shouldn't, and rarely survive. Those who retain enough intelligence to do so can find acceptance with or sell their services as mercenaries to appropriate clientele inside and outside the Tribe. Most independent Gibborim simply live like animals in the wilderness where their natural abilities make them apex predators. Others haunt forgotten temples and dwellings of the Tribe, happily remaining after all others leave and the wilderness returns; and often remaining loyal to a long dead god's orders that the temple must be guarded.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Vestiges</span><br /> <br /> Predation, Awareness, Might, Vitality<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Symbols and Associations</span><br /> <br /> The Sea of Kalah, the Red Sea, the vice of Wrath.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Concepts</span><br /> <br /> Internal affairs officer, editor, televangelist, deep-woods survivalist, professional fisherman<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Quote</span><br /> <br /> &quot;You think you\u2019ve been pretty much invisible, don\u2019t you? Well I\u2019ve been keeping tabs on you since you showed up, and guess what: I am not amused. Now I\u2019m not an unreasonable man. We can find a suitable arrangement, and we\u2019ll stay here until we do. No, don\u2019t get up. You\u2019ll be more comfortable here on the floor.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T12:36:07-07:00","id":557215,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Lahamin </span><br /> <br /> [The Symbol of Lahamu: Half a Nautilus shell. There have been holes cut out inside the separation between each chamber, and a dark liquid is flowing from one chamber to the next, until it leaks out of the shell in a small pool below.]<br /> <br /> [Picture: Central. A woman is entering a wooden cabin. She is young, around 16 and pretty. She wears a brown waterproof coat over torn jeans with sturdy rubber boots. All her clothes are muddy and show the signs of an outdoor life. She carries two large fish over her shoulder, the fish are dripping water down her back. The woman is blond with roughly cut short hair and has unnaturally large brown eyes that are too far apart. You can see patches of mud coloured skin on her arms, they are irregular and look smooth.]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Theology</span><br /> <br /> Everyone assumes that gods are distant beings content to answer the occasional prayer but never challenging the status quo, after all, if a divinity really did want to destroy America for sodomy wouldn't he have already done so with a snap of his omnipotent fingers. The cults that follow the Lahamin know better. The worlds of gods and mortals are alike, full of complex systems and competing power blocks; but their god is cunning, she has a plan, victory is inevitable and it will be glorious.<br /> <br /> The Lahamin claim their lineage is the best adapted for the mortal world, for their instincts are fearful and secretive. The Strain considers direct action to be crude or unrefined, instead the Lahamin favour networks of Cultists placed within centres of wealth and power and vast hordes of stolen secrets. Rarely seen, the eyes and influence of the Lahamin can be felt everywhere. This does serve to prejudice the Tribe with assumptions that the Lahamin avoid personal involvement or are outright cowards. While there is some truth to this, the Tribe's natural weaponry comes easily to the Lahmin; when backed into a corner, their enemies fall to hidden venoms.<br /> <br /> Cults that follow the Lahamin believe in the cause, they are agents of a god sent forth to change the world for the better. Sometimes it's even true, Leviathan's are partly human and may try to use their wicked powers for good intentions. More often the cause is evil or just petty. The Beloved's themselves become secretive and isolated, for a Lahamin's Wake creates disgust or fear for, or of, mortal society. Consumed with thoughts of humanity's decay A Lahamin's beloved are easily convinced to take immoral actions or trust in vague plans that promise a solution.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Morphology</span><br /> <br /> From the sea floor came the Lahamin and to the sea floor they return. Their bodies resemble the soft and squirming creatures that dwell within the seabed. Flatworms, snails, seaslugs, and other alien creatures that dwell within the deepest depths. The Strain is marked with all manner of strange sensory organs upon their alien forms, their eyes peer from the deepest depths and nothing may hide from their gaze.<br /> <br /> When the Lahamin manifest Vitality they mostly do so through exoskeletons. Their soft bodies are wrapped in a snails or trilobite\u2019s armour. Predation manifests with subtle and cruel weapons, venoms, toxins, stingers, a Lahamin's seemingly vulnerable form hides a deadly heart. Though it is one of the more Subtle Vestiges, the Lahamin tend manifest Sanctity visibly. They reach into people's minds through hypnotic eyes or entrancing colours that flow across their antenni.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Progenitor</span><br /> <br /> With so little family in their own lives, the Lahmin often turn to their ancestor Lahamu as a substitute. This idea is not entirely without merit, for Lahamu was said to see across all of space and time. Many Lahamin believe that their foremother knew of her descendents plight and does her part to help her children from the Primordial world.<br /> <br /> No one ever saw Lahamu, she hid herself at the bottom of the sea. Only her many eyes, the sun, the moon, and the stars, shone out from the depths and reminded the people that no matter where they hid, the gods were always watching.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Metamorphosis</span><br /> <br /> The first two steps are constant. The Wake comes first, then the eyes open to see into the hearts of men. This is a disastrous combination because what she will see in the hearts of men are echoes of the Wake. Unaware of any supernatural explanation a young Lahamin can quickly be led to believe that all her past friendships were a lie. Some fight back with logic, especially when they have reason to believe that their friends changed their opinions recently or doubt their new senses. Others retreat into solitude, only those with guidance from an early point are likely to escape with their faith in humanity intact. This faith can provide a solid anchor in the search for Tranquillity. Lahamin typically become Leviathans alone, they are alone because only one from any immediate family tends to become a Leviathan at a time, and because they tend to be born far from the influence of the Tribe. However while the situation of the Tribe tends to be unremarkable \u2013 because there usually is no Tribal presence to remark upon \u2013 the situation with humanity tends to become remarkable quite fast. One is still in school when she starts changing and she spots that one of the teachers is a child molester even though he always kept his depravities to another country. In the panic and media frenzy chaos reigns. Another was responsible for negotiating an important contract, when the changes begin he takes sick leave. Without him negotiations fail, hundreds loose their jobs and a community spirals into poverty.<br /> <br /> The Lahamin often talk about being part of a infinitely complex plan their precognitive Progenitor set in motion in prehistory. It's a point of pride and some even use the presence of Lahamu's long dead hand (or equivalent) as a surrogate parental figure. The other Strains rarely agree with these beliefs. If they believe there even is a mystical effect behind the chaos, they tend to assume it's impersonal and random. Those who believe each event was designed chosen by Lahamu tend to assign the Progenitor similar motives that they see in it's descendent. Rather than an ancient world changing plan it's simply one final act of spite against the species that slew the Progenitors, a Fuck You of truly biblical proportions echoing down the ages.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ecology</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Family</span><br /> <br /> Not many Lahamin know thier families, and those that do tend to be small. A nuclear family at the most with little contact and sometimes no knowledge of other relatives. Bloodlines touched by Lahamu are full of stillbirths, miscarriages, but also orphans, latchkey kids, absent or distant parents and abandoned or adopted children. Whether they were raised by aloof relatives or passed through a string of adoption homes. Whether they were born to a Leviathan or many generations removed, most Lahamin grow up alone. Worst of all they somehow bring the bloodline\u2019s touch to any family they join, blood ties or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Consequently most Lahamin who look to their own bloodline to understand their divine nature must first find out exactly who their relatives are. Many Lahamin live in isolation, surrounded by a horde of memorabilia from family they never knew.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Reproduction</span><br /> <br /> The Lahamin are the most dependent on the mystical facet of the mystical, environmental and genetic trinity that governs the birth of a new Leviathan, which does rather annoy them since as it means the Lahamin are behind the other Strains in knowing how to predict the birth of a new cousin. What can be known, the genetic side of the equation, is unusual by the standards of the tribe. The Lahamin can appear from any direct child of another Lahamin but usually only appear as direct descendants of several different Lahamin. Certainly it's not that rare for several Leviathans to exist within a closed gene pool, and if you go far back enough everyone is related to everyone, but neither of those are particularly relevant to the Lahamin. Rather a Lahamin is actually likely to have more than one unrelated Leviathan in the near family tree. The odds of this are staggering and the Tribe generally agrees it's a mystical function of their bloodline, a far more subtle but perhaps a more powerful effect than those seen in the other Strains.<br /> <br /> Off all the Strains the Lahamin are the least likely to have established families. Lahamin Bloodlines still exist but they rarely remain as a cohesive unit, nor do they remain distinct from other families. This makes it hard to determine the pattern in which Lahamin might emerge; when three Lahamin appear is this evidence that the Lahamin appear in large numbers? Is it actually that three different Lahamin families have recently intermarried and only have one Leviathan each? Has anyone double checked that none of them were adopted? None of this has prevented the masters of Awareness from learning that there dosn't seem to be any limit to the number of Leviathans who can be born in a given time or place, yet the mystical requirements are often personalised and so it's rare that more than one Leviathan will appear at the same time and place. When many Lahamin begin their transition at once be warned, something big is about to happen.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lahmasu</span><br /> <br /> The Lahamin consider their Lahmasu an embarrassment, and seek followers or breeding stock from their cousins more than any other Strain. The reason is simple: The Mahhu, with their secretive nature and their gift for prophecy, are essentially redundant next to the Lahamin herself; though often invaluable in a different Strain's cult. What's more, the Mahhu are quick minded and can see through a enough of the Lahamin's secrecy to realize they're better off away from the cult, or maybe they're just familiar with their more powerful relatives.<br /> <br /> Away from the Tribe, and wearing their mutations openly, the Mahhu seek acceptance but possess the awareness to know why they must say hidden. Most live on the outskirts of civilization or among society's invisible, surviving off the land and petitioners seeking prophecy or sorcery, talents the Stain cultivate through instinct and individual genius. The lucky find open minded patrons, and dispute the Strains rarity Mahhu can find acceptance and gainful work for mortal corporations, governments and even Hunters.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Vestiges</span><br /> Awareness, Vitality, Predation, Sanctity<br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Symbols and Associations</span><br /> The sea of Larwi, the Persian Gulf, the vice of Envy<br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Concepts</span><br /> Shadowy information broker, deep sea treasure hunter, neighbourhood gossip, determined reporter, deep cover agent, internet addict, sewer-dwelling alligator.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Quote</span><br /> <i>&quot;You heard that I pay well for juicy gossip. So you've decided to come here, find out what you can take from me. But as it turns out, there is nothing you know I'm interested in, because I've been watching you, honey, and everything you know, I already know. So the question now becomes, what are you willing to pay to get out of here in one piece?&quot;</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-22-2015, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T21:33:34-07:00","id":584163,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, is work still going on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T00:21:01-07:00","id":584357,"title":"","content":"It should start again soon. I've been distracted by Hunter work and work work recently. I almost have the Nu ready though. Then after them an the Thalassans it should be on to Antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:24:59-07:00","id":584826,"title":"","content":"Sweet. I look forward to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T13:44:53-07:00","id":585105,"title":"","content":"Me too. I have some great ideas for Antagonists. Take Ahabs. They're basically Heroes before Beast did Heroes (and without the weirdly hostile authorial voice). Not a problem for a minor antagonist but they can be so much more. As a little teaser - Ahabs can stab a Leviathan in the cracks within a damaged mind and pry the cracks open, or in more practical terms they can go Shadow of the Colossus on a Leviathan. How they learn new Damnations is just as neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:07:46-07:00","id":585179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=585105#post585105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me too. I have some great ideas for Antagonists. Take Ahabs. They're basically Heroes before Beast did Heroes (and without the weirdly hostile authorial voice). Not a problem for a minor antagonist but they can be so much more. As a little teaser - Ahabs can stab a Leviathan in the cracks within a damaged mind and pry the cracks open, or in more practical terms they can go Shadow of the Colossus on a Leviathan. How they learn new Damnations is just as neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>This! All this, in my face, bbbbbbbbbl!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:12:44-07:00","id":585183,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\">Nu</span><br /> <br /> [Picture: The Symbol of Nu: An Egyptian-style stone cartouche, lying left-to-right horizontally. The following Gardiner hieroglyphs are carved on the cartouche: a leaping fish (K4), then a heart (F34), bleeding into a bowl (V31), and finally a stalk of grain (M23). Above them, a line of five stars (N14). All around them, the inner border is made of sinuous wave-carvings. ]<br /> <br /> [Picture: Central. A man or woman, entirely covered in clothes. This includes a baggy hoodie, sweater pants and sports shoes. The figure is misshapen, with one shoulder higher than the other and a folded knee. The posture is jumpy, as if he/she was ready to bolt at any time. All the clothes are soaked and dripping. The hood is pulled over his/her head, and you only see steam rising from the location of the mouth. The figure is wearing a golden, heavy medallion on a chain over his jumper. Three small tentacles with sucker cups are sliding out from each of the sleeves.]<br /> <br /> He comes before the elders with a question: Why does it rain? Why did my son take ill and die? Mankind has always spun tales of the divine to explain the world around them. These stories don\u2019t tell the truth, sometimes they contradict the evidence of your own eyes, for the village elders have life experiences not scientific education, but they don\u2019t need to be true. They merely need to make sense.<br /> <br /> The Nu consider it their curse. Their cousins enjoy slavish devotion but the Nu often feel their Beloved don\u2019t care about them at all. Their cults worship elabourate occult ideologies to which the Nu is merely a figurehead and a source of ideas. Their followers will obey orders of course, but when you can send a zealot out to buy your lunch only to find out later that your shopping list has been reinterpreted into elabourate criteria for virgin brides there\u2019s a temptation to withdraw from even your own cult. The Nu feel that they cannot lead cults, merely set some direction and ruthlessly prune their followers whenever they go in the wrong. As a result the Strain has a reputation for flexibility and a tendency to fold under pressure, but this stereotype comes from taking the Nu\u2019s armour at face value, and also from judging them by their bodies.<br /> <br /> As for their Wake. The Nu\u2019s wake have a simple effect on their Beloved. It drives them mad. Not mad like a screaming madman, but hallucinations and nightmarish yet euphoric religious visions follow the Nu wherever they go. Their cultists are not blessed with insight into the cosmos or the Primordial world, but they think they are and a Nu\u2019s cult is a rich source of theology which, if not exactly true, is great for helping a Leviathan make sense of the world.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Morphology</span><br /> <br /> The Nu are believed to be the lineage with the most direct connection to water \u2013 not as a place to live, but as an essential component of life. Their Tribal forms tend towards the gelatinous and sinuous, with traits taken from spinless ocean life. Jellyfish, tadpoles. More solid traits may come from squid or octopi but a Nu is equally likely to draw from microorganisms such as the ancient amoeba. Their large and awkward-seeming forms bely surprising grace, and many Nu are nearly invisible in deep water - their bodies are akin to natural extensions of the depths.<br /> <br /> Nu manifest their Vestiges in strange ways, even by the standards of a strange Tribe. Awareness draws upon the strangest and oldest senses in the ocean, from light sensitive crystals embedded in their skin to detecting magnetism. A Nu often seems designed to see things beyond mortal ken. Fecundity touches Nu lightly, but those who bear it reflect water as a component of life, there is a fluidity to their acts of creation and at the extreme they may ooze life bearing liquid wherever they travel. Sanctity has the oddest effect of all, for Nu who bear it transcend the physical to reflect the viewer's concept of the leviathan or give the impression of being no more than the fingertip of a far greater being.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Progenitor</span><br /> <br /> The Nu claim descent from a Progenitor called Nu, Naunet, or simply by the honourific \u201cthe Elder\u201d. Both male and female, depending on the context, Nu controlled the sea and skies and in some tales was the elements themselves.<br /> <br /> Among the Strain it is common to talk about Nu\u2019s life giving nature. Water is both the origin of all life, and a vital component of all living beings. Always distant, Nu remains revered by the Strain as a being whose existence gave great gifts to the world around him.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Family</span><br /> <br /> A Nu's family resembles small nuclear groups, but with strong links between them. In this they are the most normal seeming to a modern perspective, the individual units are mostly normal families and they are united in an endless series of reunions, barbecues and similar events. At any given time one family is the focal point for Nu's mystical inheritance. Which family is equally split between how much of the Leviathan's dna they retain, environmental factors, and how close to the Leviathan they are. If the Leviathan is still alive then closeness is easily measured, but if they are not it falls to things like who lives in the Leviathan's old house or who owns the most heirlooms. The closer any family is to the focal family the more mutations and Lahmasu will be found in their family tree, but the next Leviathan is always found furthest away. Nu are like, or are, primordial ooze. They emerge in lifeless places far from the Tribe but the Eldest have a touch that lasts for generations.<br /> <br /> Even though the spawn of Nu cannot emerge within an established Tribe family they can, and many do, seek out their distant relatives. Once they find a leed they need only following Nu's touch to it's source. Typically a Nu's descendants, if kept apart from living Leviathans or cults, adapt well to the modern world. The strain's families have a reputation for adapting their old cult's theology to fit the modern world, which is a useful skill for any Leviathan. A Nu can learn much and leave with a collection of Heirlooms. Most do leave before long, if a second Nu stays long enough to impart social influences the mystical effects of Nu's bloodline compound. The effect is strongest when the family are direct relatives but a Nu living among an unrelated family can still create outlandish mutations and powerful Lahmasu. As with more conventional forms of inbreeding evolution has imparted instincts to avoid damaging the bloodline, but it must be said that the Tribe has done worse for longer odds to create powerful servants.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Genetics</span><br /> <br /> They say if a Nu wants to trace his ancestry he should start by looking at his great uncle's second cousins. Like ripples spreading, the touch of the divine bloodline moves outwards from a Nu to his surrounding family. Their families are large, but often suffer from stillbirths, infertility or just fail to find romance creating many dead ends on the family tree. Yet a few branches will be spared. Like runner shoots these often are, or soon will be, the most distant to the original Leviathan, genetically, culturally, or even geographically. It is these distant and healthy relations which are most likely to give birth to the next full blooded Leviathan while the more direct descendants are often destined to die out or leave their heritage behind entirely.<br /> <br /> Nu are most commonly born out the blue, as it were. The healthy branches tend to be free of Lemashu and other markers of the Tribe. Even culturally, most tend to be distant from the unusual side of their heritage. It is rare for the same branch of the family tree to produce more than one Leviathan before the cycle repeats itself but several escaping branches may exist in parallel. As far as anyone can tell in regards to when and if they produce another Leviathan, each branch is entirely independent of the others.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lahamin</span><br /> <br /> The Nu claim as their own the Heqen, a Lahmasu lineage marked with amphibious features. Most Heqen are frog-like in appearance, but as the bloodline becomes rarified their skin becomes transparent and liquid, like that of a jellyfish. The Heqen are said to belong everywhere and nowhere. Among humanity or the Tribe they live on the edges, neither accepted or attacked, the Heqen are happiest amongst their own company.<br /> <br /> That a family that probably looks like bipedal frogs is a testament to the intelligence and practicality of the Heqen and many Leviathan prize them as diplomats or middle managers who can keep the Cult protected from it\u2019s own stupidity. Away from the Tribe Heqen once found employment as shamen, mediums, or wondering professions. While their innate abilities rarely let them see the invisible realms relevant to mortals, they can learn mortal magic and had the right mindset. As such roles are harder to find in the modern world most Hequen keep to their own kind on the edges of humanity, their subtle existence masks a life rich in theology, symbolism and worship of the tribe. Or other gods.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Vestiges</span><br /> <br /> <b>Elements</b>, Awareness, Sanctity, Vitality<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Symbols and Associations</span><br /> <br /> The Sea of Kardanj, the Mediterranean, the vice of Gluttony.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Concepts</span><br /> <br /> Martial arts instructor, inscrutable guru, conspiracy theorist icon, underground artist<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Quote</span><br /> <br /> &quot;You\u2019re so beautiful. I saw you yesterday night, but I didn\u2019t dare approach you. No, you didn\u2019t see me. I was in the rain, outside. I saw you cry, in the dark. And I saw what you did to that poor man. Don\u2019t cry! I wouldn\u2019t do anything to hurt you. But would you please, just\u2026 look at me?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T02:16:40-07:00","id":595491,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Thalassans</span><br /> <br /> They beseech the gods, grant me wealth, grant me fame, grant me glory. For the children of Thalassa religion is a contract. You sing praises and perform sacrifices and return you get, well that\u2019s negotiable. For most of history people asked for miracles, a drought ended or a sickness healed now they are more likely to ask for money or status. To the Thalassans it doesn\u2019t matter, every Leviathan seeks some way to control their Beloved before mad zealotry gets everyone in trouble. A miracle or a paycheck, either way\u2019s better than crushing their skulls between your claws.<br /> <br /> Thalassans boast about being the best adjusted to the modern world. They sit in the hearts of cities, living in the penthouse above corporation-cults and doing business with mortals unaware of their true nature. In truth the Strain sits on a razor\u2019s edge. The Leviathan instincts to dominate and destroy, and the Strains own instinctual greed, conflict with good business sense and cultists, no matter how competent at running the shop, rarely tell the boss anything but what they think he wants to hear. A Thalassan\u2019s corporation is often only one setback from disaster, because every setback tempts a Leviathan to crush an employee or a rival CEO and that makes paper trails.<br /> <br /> Cults surrounding a Thalassan tend towards paranoia and fixation on the past, echoing the early days when mankind had to be ever vigilant for plague or storm and vengeful least they become known as easy prey. When times are good these traits are, not absent, but muted. In a good year there is less to worry about and nothing to take vengeance for, but when the Leviathan can no longer provide good times their cult becomes ineffective as paranoia and anger take root.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Morphology</span><br /> <br /> A Thalassans' body is the place where the ocean meets the land. Their forms take after creatures found in shallow waters, within tidepools, or tree covered swamps. In this they exhibit enormous diversity: From the strong legged frogs to the mighty clawed crabs. A starfish's symmetry to an octopus' shifting form. The colours of a tropical fish or the camouflage of an alligator. The Thalassans are a diverse lot, but if their is a constant it is the Strain's clear Might. Their claws, tentacles, tales or flippers radiate strength and grace.<br /> <br /> When Thalassans master the Elements they often do so physically. Strange limbs that are half flesh, half sea and storm. With mighty arms and tentacles they grip the sky, bending the heavens to their will. Crabs are considered holy to Thalassa, and when her children manifest Vitality exoskeletons and shells are common.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Progenitor</span><br /> <br /> The Thalassans claim descent from 'mighty armed' Thalassa. With a single stroke she could shatter cliffs or raise up islands from the depth. Hailed as the patron of sailors and merchants, Thalassa demanded tribute from all who traveled upon her domain but would bestow wealth and fortune upon her favourites, and her favourites alone.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Metamorphosis</span><br /> <br /> It begins with dreams of the Rift. In his dreams the Thalassan stands at the forefront of the Tempest. Call it the weight of history, the expectations of the ancestors or just the weight of billions of tons of water. It pushes him ever onwards with no regards to his wishes or direction. As his powers begin to grow dreams become hallucinations. He sees the Shallows in every drop of water. A glass teems with bizarre life, a tap flows with the fury of the Tempest. If it wasn't for milk and fruit juices dehydration would be a big, and rather ironic, threat. Finally the weight escapes from his dreams. This effect is entirely unsubtle, he simply feels as though he weighs several times more, it requires mental fortitude and physical strength to do anything but collapse onto the floor. To free himself a Thalassan must fight back. With each step against the tide his body begins to adapt, claiming the Vestige of Might. In time he will have the strength to swim against the tide, to find his own path, he must do this for the currents of the Rift lead nowhere you'd want to go.<br /> <br /> What separate the Thalassans from the other Strains is that one can actually fail to become a Leviathan. To stop the processes of changing permanently. It's not perfect, you might end up as a Hemitheos rather than a human and you're certain to have some sever mental damage, yet the option to deny goodhood and instead live a full and fulfilled mortal life exists. If you swim against the tides and have the strength you'll become a Leviathan. If you get swept away by the tides you'll probably become a Ophion. But if you cling to a rock until you're raw and bloody \u2013 that is cling to another person or some other source of direction external to yourself \u2013 the waters will eventually recede. Unsurprisingly many Thalassans teach their children to be strong and self reliant encase they get the chance to become a Leviathan, equally unsurprisingly many Thalassans try to encourage their children to be dependent on others so they won't become a Leviathan.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Reproduction</span><br /> <br /> Unlike the other Strains Thalassan genetics are pretty simple. Everyone who has more than a trace of Thalassan genetics is a potential Leviathan. Genes simply aren't relevant past a certain minimum. While it's not the only factor, the most important prerequisite to becoming a Thalassan is, in fact, the opinion of your fellows. When a someone with Thalassan heritage is thought off highly \u2013 the definition of \u201chighly\u201d depends on the Beholder; one might respect power, another might pass his mark of confidence through love \u2013 by her peers her blood takes notice, the tribe grows within her DNA. Not all Thalassans are measured equally. The stronger the Tribe is within you, the more your \u201cvote\u201d counts. This leads to Thalassa's heritage growing stronger over the generations. Once critical mass is reached, and other environmental and mystical factors are in place a new Leviathan is born.<br /> <br /> Sometimes only one Thalassan appears at a time, sometimes it's two, or even three. The biggest factor is how many with Thalassan heritage are present. When a Thalassan begins Transforming she drains the mystical potency from everyone nearby with dormant Thalassan genetics to fuel her transformation. It simply takes more people to fuel two new Leviathans than one new Leviathan. The birth of a Lahmasu has a similar effect, but several orders of magnitude smaller. It can be safely ignored.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lahamin</span><br /> <br /> The Thalassans give birth to Hemitheos a Strain famed for herculean strength and ambition, but also for madness. Rising from their Tribal biology, a Hemitheos\u2019 madness is, not beyond the reach of medical science, but poorly researched at present. Most Hemitheos remain functional, aware of their own flaws, willing to make accommodations but endlessly frustrated that they need too. Typically the strain does poorly in a structured environment, but free to act as they wish they are larger than life powerful, but also dangerous figures.<br /> <br /> In Cults a Hemitheos makes a good champion or squad leader. They make poor organizers or managers, but they can possess blazing charisma and mighty strength that can lead by example. Too many Hemitheos in a Cult can quickly become a tangle of rivalries and one-oneupmanship so smart Leviathans use them as the spice rather than the main dish. Hemitheos also work well as lone wolves. They make poor spies and diplomats, but excellent scouts, explorers and tomb raiders.<br /> <br /> Away from the Tribe Hemitheos look for roles where they can excel all by themselves. They are athletes and actors, but also independent craftsmen, hired guns, and rugged survivalists. Not all Hemitheos rise to the top of course, many crash and burn spectacularly, but if a Hemitheos understands her nature she will seek a place outside of society's rules; either through self isolation or simply rising above the rules.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Family</span><br /> <br /> Thalassan dynasties are torn between meritocracies and favouritism. Children are pushed hard to excel but a Thalassan\u2019s favour is often arbitrary. Unsurprisingly a Thalassan family produces just as many burnouts and relatives walking away as it does overachievers and spoilt brats. Due to the workings of Thalassa\u2019s bloodline, Leviathans are almost always born in the center of the family from among the most favoured of their generation and many are raised with experience at managing others even before their Wake sets in.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Vestiges</span><br /> <br /> <b>Might</b>, Elements, Fecundity, Vitality<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Symbols and Associations</span><br /> <br /> The sea of Sanji, the Aegean Sea, the Vice of Greed.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Character Concepts</span><br /> <br /> Fishing or shipping magnate, legbreaker, profiteering televangelist, merchant captain, star athlete, get-rich-quick enthusiast.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Quote</span><br /> <br /> &quot;Can I put a value on godhood? Can I estimate the worship of men and the adoration of children? Can I put a price on the heritage of the heavens? Hell yes I can. Everything I have, everything my heritage gives me, has been taken from another. I am a tick, sucking at the blood of society. The only redeeming feature, the only one, is that all of it was given freely.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T04:43:41-07:00","id":603737,"title":"","content":"And now for something different. Ahabs.<br /> <br /> In 1E Ahabs were written as a special kind of Slasher; their reasoning was mostly &quot;you're whales, gotta have Ahab in there&quot;; and they weren't much of a threat unless you're just starting out or they caught you unaware and unTransformed.<br /> <br /> In short, they were basically like Beast's Heroes - except without the write up making sneering political allusions. Ahabs were crazy and broken, but it was always the Leviathans fault for breaking them.<br /> <br /> <br /> In 2E they now have a real thematic role. They're the physical embodiment of a Leviathan's broken mind and the harm damaged gods cause to all around them. They're created when Levaithans do harm and draw power from the things a Leviathan loathes about itself. They're also able to climb a Leviathan's back and do catastrophic psychic damage with every strike of the Harpoon.<br /> <br /> <br /> The write up is six pages long, a lot of that being powers. So instead of posting it here I direct you to this <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ISiYxINVYvbHsFDcXKopDS8Lxwa0RzNIVgIWQcjg5Qw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">link</a><br /> <br /> In addition I put all the strains in one page <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JPb2CioodnfracCT4Zb6H-P2ieuYQ7WyBPQeVePBX9k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. I didn't do much with formatting since I'd just have to redo it when it comes to creating the PDF.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T10:07:24-07:00","id":603913,"title":"","content":"Glad I'm not the only one who saw Heroes and thought &quot;Wow, these are just worse Ahabs!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T09:24:53-07:00","id":604764,"title":"","content":"Forgive my stupidity, but what are Phronesis and Eunoia? Are they mentioned in this thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T09:37:12-07:00","id":604769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=604764#post604764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive my stupidity, but what are Phronesis and Eunoia? Are they mentioned in this thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are the twin Integrity replacements. One represents your control over your monster self, and the other control over your divine self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T01:07:15-07:00","id":606424,"title":"","content":"Almost.<br /> <br /> Phronesis is your ability to tell right from wrong, good ideas from bad. A Leviathan with low Phronesis isn't loosing control to their beastal self, their human self is dying and the beastal self isn't taking control; it's the only one left.<br /> <br /> Eunoia is benevolence, the ability to tell that other people are people and care for their wants and needs. A Leviathan with low Eunoia is loosing the ability to recognise mortals and non-divine supernaturals as anything but their own fingertips or some other god's fingertips.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T00:39:38-07:00","id":620965,"title":"","content":"So the next thing I'm working on is Leviathan's arch enemy. The Marduk Society.<br /> <br /> The major difference between 1E and 2E is that now, the Marduk civil war is over. The good guys have won, decisively. This completes Marduk's parallel of the Tribe:<ul><li>Both founded in the adventdalen world</li> <li>Both fell from grace with the death of their founder</li> <li>But the tribe never improved after their fall. Marduk steadily improved throughout history and now practically saints.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Another difference is that I'm taking more time to explain just where Marduk (who're actually not that big) get access to more advanced tech than VALKYRIE - so a preview for you all. (And yes, there will be player advice for how to survive Marduk - it's about avoiding or killing their scouts before they pin your location down)<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Superscience</span><br /> <br /> Marduk is famed as the builder of the first city, a bringer of civilization. Upon Marduk's death his treacherous disciples stole back the knowledge of civilisation in a brutal campaign of censorship, they kept the best for themselves and shared lesser knowledge with their servants.<br /> <br /> These secrets were not blueprints for weapons or scrolls of magic spells, they were something far greater. They were techniques and methodologies for research and education. The scientific method itself was once the propitiatory knowledge of the Marduk Society, who's campaigns of censorship against Helenistic philosophers and the courts of China finally failed against the Islamic golden age.<br /> <br /> The society never had the resources to forge ahead alone, or maybe it might have if it wasn't riddled with infighting and led by paranoid sorcerers watching their underlings for signs of brilliance or independence, but every new technology (and occult-science, before most of humanity turned away from that path) mankind developed could be quickly refined and improved upon using Marduk's techniques.<br /> <br /> When ancient man developed copper working, the society refined their technique into metallurgy to develop iron and occult electrically charged alloys. By the time the Ancient Greeks were using clockwork to display the movement of the heavens the society were using clockwork logic engines to unearth hidden cults. In 1783 the French launched the first manned flight in a hot air balloon, by the end of the decade floating fortresses were keeping vigil over the world's oceans.<br /> <br /> Today the Marduk society can only begin to scratch the surface of new technological developments, but that scratch alone is approaching the Clarke limit. Marduk has artificial intelligences as smart as a dog, aircraft that fly and fortresses that float on folded spacetime, and directed energy weapons orbiting Earth waiting for a Leviathan to emerge from hiding.<br /> <br /> Leviathans say the Tribe has been at war with the society for most of history, in truth it hasn't been a war for a very long time. It's been pest control.<br /> <br /> &lt;list of equipment handheld equipment goes here - this might end up the same or similar to the 1E Superscience Endowment.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T04:58:27-07:00","id":621087,"title":"","content":"Is there still going to be room for the &quot;occultists seeking Leviathan flesh to maintain their immortally (or other exploitive goals)&quot;? Maybe split off as a separate group?<br /> <br /> And if the Marduk Society is both Good and Advanced, why haven't they been sharing these developments with the rest of the world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T08:13:41-07:00","id":621277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=621087#post621087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there still going to be room for the &quot;occultists seeking Leviathan flesh to maintain their immortally (or other exploitive goals)&quot;? Maybe split off as a separate group?<br /> <br /> And if the Marduk Society is both Good and Advanced, why haven't they been sharing these developments with the rest of the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the moment the average person gets directed energy weapons and advanced AI, all hell breaks loose? Most people simply aren't ready for many of these advancements.<br /> <br /> Plus, it's quite possible a little hubris is involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T08:38:36-07:00","id":621345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=621087#post621087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there still going to be room for the &quot;occultists seeking Leviathan flesh to maintain their immortally (or other exploitive goals)&quot;? Maybe split off as a separate group?</div> </div> </div> </div> Most of those guys are dead but it will be mentioned that nobody actually knows how many, if any, of those guys are left.<br /> <br /> Also remember that there's now an Antagonist splat called Occultists who're unrelated to the Marduk society but can fill most of those niches.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=621087#post621087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if the Marduk Society is both Good and Advanced, why haven't they been sharing these developments with the rest of the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cultural inertia - they're still going &quot;what now&quot; in the aftermath of victory, and unless they want to be public enemy number one it's not a good idea to point out they have kill-sats in orbit. However they're going to start creating a spin off organisations with clean hands and sharing technology sooner or later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=621277#post621277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the moment the average person gets directed energy weapons and advanced AI, all hell breaks loose? Most people simply aren't ready for many of these advancements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always felt that trope didn't make sense. Mankind already has enough nukes to end all life on Earth. You don't need directed energy weapons to build killsats, just dropping a piece of metal from orbit would do it.<br /> <br /> New and more advanced weapons isn't going to be any more dangerous than nukes; on the other hand personal flight technology and clean energy sources could revolutionise society in a good way.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T09:17:53-07:00","id":621394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=621277#post621277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the moment the average person gets directed energy weapons and advanced AI, all hell breaks loose? Most people simply aren't ready for many of these advancements.<br /> <br /> Plus, it's quite possible a little hubris is involved.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=621345#post621345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...<br /> <br /> Cultural inertia - they're still going &quot;what now&quot; in the aftermath of victory, and unless they want to be public enemy number one it's not a good idea to point out they have kill-sats in orbit. However they're going to start creating a spin off organisations with clean hands and sharing technology sooner or later.<br /> <br /> I always felt that trope didn't make sense. Mankind already has enough nukes to end all life on Earth. You don't need directed energy weapons to build killsats, just dropping a piece of metal from orbit would do it.<br /> <br /> New and more advanced weapons isn't going to be any more dangerous than nukes; on the other hand personal flight technology and clean energy sources could revolutionise society in a good way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. A little &quot;they aren't ready&quot; arrogance could add a little human-understandable grey to their character.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=621345#post621345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Most of those guys are dead but it will be mentioned that nobody actually knows how many, if any, of those guys are left.<br /> <br /> Also remember that there's now an Antagonist splat called Occultists who're unrelated to the Marduk society but can fill most of those niches.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, Leviathans still have to worry about at least someone/some group hunting them merely to cut them up? Cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T13:23:24-07:00","id":624568,"title":"","content":"So the previews for the Edo Jidai Hunter Compacts and Conspiracies are out, andI can't help but think that think that the <i>ama-san</i> would probably have been antagonistic to Leviathans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T13:27:37-07:00","id":624571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=624568#post624568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the previews for the Edo Jidai Hunter Compacts and Conspiracies are out, andI can't help but think that think that the <i>ama-san</i> would probably have been antagonistic to Leviathans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> His Majesty is currently trying to figure out how to give the Conspiracy an edge, so an open fight against a Levi doesn\u00b4t end always with the Hunters themselves turned into sushi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 08-12-2015, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T13:32:04-07:00","id":624573,"title":"","content":"You mean me?<br /> <br /> I said they'd need more power if they want to avoid becoming fish food, but I have no particular plans to homebrew them an edge against Leviathans. Here's what I wrote about the ama-san in my read through of the edo period.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/622428-where-i-read-hunters-of-the-edo-jidai#post622428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how would the Ami San tie in to Leviathan? Thematically they'd actually do great. Practically, a Transformed Leviathan with 2E mechanics (once they're written) has nothing to fear from them.<br /> <br /> Thematically they're draw power (namely Small Unit Tactics) from being an insular and close knit community. That makes a nice foil to Leviathans who's insular and small knit communities are unhealthy cults.<br /> <br /> But as I said. Even a starting Leviathan (if they chose combat powers) would probably wipe the floor with dozens of Ami San and depending on how the sea whistle works \u2013 Leviathans are going to be all but immune to mental influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T16:25:37-07:00","id":627096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=624573#post624573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean me?<br /> <br /> I said they'd need more power if they want to avoid becoming fish food, but I have no particular plans to homebrew them an edge against Leviathans. Here's what I wrote about the ama-san in my read through of the edo period.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would think that they wouldn't be doing much of the direct fighting v. Leviathans. Perhaps an Ahab might enlist their services in tracking and drawing out a member of the Tribe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T06:48:08-07:00","id":627513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Leviathans are going to be all but immune to mental influence.</span></i></span></span> </div> </div> </div>With that as my intro, may I ask how many of the new leviathan mechanics we've seen and how many are still to be written?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T11:37:08-07:00","id":627738,"title":"","content":"Not that much so far. You've seen the rules for Ahabs, for Cults and Atavisms (if you missed it. Leviathans get a number of free Atavisms based on Sheol which which give +X to the chosen attribute at Depth Y; this will replace the Attribute boosting Channels).<br /> <br /> The immunity to mental influence is simply that instead of rolling Attribute + Sheol they roll Attribute and get an extra Sheol + Depth automatic successes to resist mental influences. The only exception is when their own Beloved are using mental influence. Which is why when you leave cults alone and they start attempting to summon their god back to them, it might work.<br /> <br /> Warning Ahabs are technically a form of Beloved, which is why they can destroy a Leviathan's mind with a few well placed harpoons. Occultists are also Beloved, regular Beloved but they take precautions to avoid falling under a Leviathans control (avoiding all contact is the big one) which is why a Leviathans mental defenses don't let them stop an Occultist using their power for rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T12:27:30-07:00","id":627772,"title":"","content":"So, when this is all homebrewed up, where's this all going to be consolidated and organized? I'm assuming the RPG.net wiki.<br /> <br /> <br /> In any case, let me just say I like your work and would enjoy a nice 2e update, though I'm unsure about the Marduk Society. I like the idea of tech and such, but I worry if it's overstepping or not as unique as it should be.<br /> Also, the &quot;Saintly&quot; bit. I'll definitely get it if the higher ups are the ones who are the &quot;good guys&quot; narrative speaking, but I'm unconvinced if the <i>whole </i>organization should be like that. Maybe some grey like they're perhaps a little &quot;too good&quot; maybe? I don't know, I'll probably like them more once I see a full write up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 08-15-2015, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T13:20:13-07:00","id":627819,"title":"","content":"Regarding sorcery, do you have some guidelines about what can or not be accomplished by them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T13:37:33-07:00","id":627868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=627772#post627772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, when this is all homebrewed up, where's this all going to be consolidated and organized? I'm assuming the RPG.net wiki.</div> </div> </div> </div> Probably a PDF this time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=627772#post627772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, let me just say I like your work and would enjoy a nice 2e update, though I'm unsure about the Marduk Society. I like the idea of tech and such, but I worry if it's overstepping or not as unique as it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div> Marduk has to be tech. Marduk's power has to be a metaphor for how human civilisation has progressed and improved since the bronze age.<br /> <br /> Unless someone can think of a way Marduk can kill a leviathan by blasting it with Freedom of Religion, or The Right to Liberty, the only weaponasiable improvements in human civilisation is technological.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=627772#post627772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the &quot;Saintly&quot; bit. I'll definitely get it if the higher ups are the ones who are the &quot;good guys&quot; narrative speaking, but I'm unconvinced if the <i>whole </i>organization should be like that. Maybe some grey like they're perhaps a little &quot;too good&quot; maybe? I don't know, I'll probably like them more once I see a full write up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at this way. The Marduk Society as an organisation brings out the best in it's members, that has to be the case because the Society has to be the opposite of the way a Leviathan cults brings out the worst in it's members. A supportative internal culture, technology that's powered by virtue, possible sponsorship by a god (no one knows what really happened in the deep past). It all adds up into something that brings out the best in it's members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-15-2015, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T14:41:42-07:00","id":627956,"title":"","content":"Oh, I am not advocating dropping tech all together, I just mean that technology at Marduk's disposal might need to feel less generic. Which I suppose is a tall order now that I think about it since you'd have to define what generic is. <br /> <br /> You could probably design a way to use Right to Liberty to break a Leviathan's Cult up, but that's only if you use outright magic to suppress the Wake.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Marduk's culture, I'm just thinking it's a little extreme for them to be <i>all good</i>. I suppose that's the point since playing a Leviathan is meant to be <i>all bad </i>though. Just feel it needs some stains to make them not perfect. <br /> <br /> <br /> Thinking on it, I realize how foolish I must sound to you, especially since my problems likely step from a difference in taste rather something more objective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T15:19:25-07:00","id":628024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=627956#post627956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I am not advocating dropping tech all together, I just mean that technology at Marduk's disposal might need to feel less generic.</div> </div> </div> </div> It has a theme. 1930s science fiction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=627956#post627956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could probably design a way to use Right to Liberty to break a Leviathan's Cult up, but that's only if you use outright magic to suppress the Wake.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe someone could, but I've got nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=627956#post627956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking on it, I realize how foolish I must sound to you, especially since my problems likely step from a difference in taste rather something more objective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Opinions are never foolish.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T16:20:12-07:00","id":628102,"title":"","content":"Regarding Marduk, what if the culture encourages healthy and good things, but you can still have the rare rotten higher ups (just like it is <i>possible</i> to have non-jerkass Leviathans)? I mean, Marduk's generally benevolent culture would mitigate any harm they could cause (just like the nature of the Wake would handicap even well meaning Leviathans).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-15-2015, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T17:12:56-07:00","id":628142,"title":"","content":"I have to admit, seeing a conversation like this isn't really selling me on this splat. I liked the initial concept of Leviathan because it had some really &quot;monstrous&quot; feel. Now it's starting to sound like playing on the losing side of a &quot;Humanity, F*** Yeah!&quot; saga. If I wanted HFY! theme, I'd play Hunter.<br /> <br /> \u200bSeriously, it sounds like Leviathan is going to play up the &quot;being a monster absolutely sucks&quot; angle harder than Promethean and Mummy combined. At least Promethean had a hopeful end-game and Mummy has other themes to distract it. Maybe some folks here like that, but it's not for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T00:17:22-07:00","id":628282,"title":"","content":"&quot;Starting too?&quot; Leviathan has been about playing the loosing side of a &quot;Humanity, F*** Yeah!&quot; saga since 1E. Look at Chapter One, it out right says there was open warfare between humanity and the Tribe in the bronze age; and the Tribe lost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=628102#post628102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Marduk, what if the culture encourages healthy and good things, but you can still have the rare rotten higher ups</div> </div> </div> </div>Afraid not. It used to have rotten higher ups; but their removal from the Society is the key difference between the Society's history and the Tribe's history. Both groups fell from grace in prehistory (Tiamat's Death by Marduk / Marduk being overthrown by his evil disciples) but the Marduk Soceity recovered from their fall; hence the bad guys were kicked out.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T07:51:41-07:00","id":628632,"title":"","content":"Ah. As I understood it, the ancient &quot;keep humanity depressed to fuel our secret power&quot; higher ups got the can. Even overly ambitious, zealous, and just bureaucratically malevolent/petty higher ups got fired too? (In which case, is superior-hiring-and-HR going to be one of the goodies eventually released to the rest of humanity?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Marduk's power has to be a metaphor for how human civilisation has progressed and improved since the bronze age. </div> </div> </div>And we've still got a fair amount of room for improvement, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-16-2015, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T08:47:35-07:00","id":628702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=628632#post628632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even overly ambitious, zealous, and just bureaucratically malevolent/petty higher ups got fired too?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=628632#post628632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(In which case, is superior-hiring-and-HR going to be one of the goodies eventually released to the rest of humanity?)</div> </div> </div> </div> I see no reason why not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=628632#post628632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we've still got a fair amount of room for improvement, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. That bit you quoted was about their technology though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T10:03:36-07:00","id":628769,"title":"","content":"I suppose on thinking on it, perhaps my problem can be best phrased as that they feel a bit too perfect. Atleast in the context of the information provided thus far.<br /> <br /> While the presentation and the idea of playing the losing side of some ancient war people have forgotten is fine in of itself, Marduk as written makes things rather problematic. If they're all pure good, even the most well meaning leviathans would not have much of any moral ground to stand up against them. Maybe it's intentional, but that kind of bothers me. All organizations should have flaws of some sort.<br /> <br /> Perhaps their flaw should not be that they have secret evils, but perhaps the idea that they are all idealistic. Not misguided idealistic, but rather more that they have different ideas on how to improve the world. Such as maybe a faction that tries to do things like &quot;fix&quot; leviathans while another that goes for killing them all. Or another that tries to go form amnesty.<br /> <br /> But if you feel I'll drop this topic, I shall.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> More important and relevant to me, how much change is going to be done to the structure of Channels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T10:23:57-07:00","id":628776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=628769#post628769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> even the most well meaning leviathans would not have much of any moral ground to stand up against them. Maybe it's intentional, but that kind of bothers me.</div> </div> </div> </div> It is intentional, and it's also a key point that even the most well meaning leviathan is hurting everyone around them. The Wake creates beloved, which is basically driving people insane.<br /> <br /> There are some schools of thought that say that a Leviathan cannot be blamed for what it can't control and that fighting Marduk is justifiable self defence. So they do have some moral ground to defend themselves. But in my opinion the ethical thing for a Leviathan to do is to swim out to sea and only communicate with mankind through the internet - yes Leviathans can connect to the internet with their powers.<br /> <br /> Marduk doesn't go trawling through the sea for Leviathans to kill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=628769#post628769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> More important and relevant to me, how much change is going to be done to the structure of Channels?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably nothing. Some powers will change, and the attribute boosters will be replaced (so I'll need at least 8 new ones) but the structure will probably be unchanged.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T12:00:57-07:00","id":628923,"title":"","content":"Does the Marduk Society really <i>need</i> to exist in the present day?<br /> <br /> Consider the backstory. The Society broke the power of Leviathans three thousand years ago, with technology that was, perhaps, highly advanced by Bronze Age standards - but whatever they had must have become wholly mundane, or been superseded by mundane technology, long before the present. That surely implies that any Leviathans who made themselves obnoxious would be defeated and destroyed by, well, an ordinary modern military unit, with no access to supernatural techniques at all - never mind what hunter conspiracies like Task Force Valkyrie could put into the field. It would be a much stronger statement of the idea that the Tribe were broken by humanity at its best if, in fact, ordinary technology as wielded by ordinary people is what the Tribe are most scared of.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, the Leviathan-eating sub-sect of the Marduk Society is the only thing that really justified its existence in the game. Everything else the Society does would be done just as well or better by hunters and mortals. In your position I would turn it into an interesting historical footnote: an odd secret society of philosophers and engineers that dissolved during the early Roman Empire, leaving only notes on the demons from the sea to molder in libraries where modern power-seeking occultists sometimes discover them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T12:29:31-07:00","id":628960,"title":"","content":"There's a flawed premise in your post. You argue that Marduk could be better handled by Hunters, but Marduk is a Hunter Conspiracy. There's a sidebar in 1E that flat out states they are, and if you look at the 1E write up it uses the template for a Hunter Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> And yes. A modern military unit is more than a match for the Tribe. Leviathans, like most WoD critters, have a large weakness for anything that can remain in the air out of reach and pelt them with missiles until they go down.<br /> <br /> <br /> What Marduk has is two fold:<br /> <br /> 1) Thematic focus. A modern military unit represents society as it is, or perhaps society at it's worse. War is horrible, and the political left is often opposed to the military-industrial complex which means if I use the military as society's best I alienate half the readers (more really, WoD demographics skew). TF:V represents fears of government conspiracies and other sinister things. In contrast, Marduk, with their technology that's more effective if you behave virtueously and their larger than life heroic personalities are laser focused on representing what's good about society.<br /> <br /> You can't make the modern military into a metaphor for what's good about society because they're a real organisation and real organisations are complex. You can't do it with TF:V because it contradicts the established cannon. A new organisation is the only way.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) Battle strategy designed to be fun for players over effective. Look at Al-Qaeda or Isis. The USA army (and thus TF:V) has no qualms bombing brainwashed fanatics. Marduk does. That's why they try to lure the Leviathan into the open before unleashing the big guns. A player could not hope to fight VALKARIE, they'd just bomb Innsmouth flat. Seriously, the very first line of their write up &quot;Fact: in December 1927, the US Army raided a number of coastal towns in Massachusetts. The towns no longer exist.&quot;. Marduk wouldn't do that. Marduk are nice, they try and minimise casualties. That gives players an oppotunity to misdirect, to evacuate, to role play rather than just dying in a rain of missiles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-16-2015, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T14:35:41-07:00","id":629090,"title":"","content":"How does Marduk play into the larger World of Darkness? I don't even mean crossover, I mean the more general mysterious and cynical horror that goes on. Baseline has miscellaneous other things that go bump in the night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T00:06:38-07:00","id":629613,"title":"","content":"I'd say they don't go looking for it, but are pretty good at dealing with it or just getting out it's way when they stumble across it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T09:35:26-07:00","id":629988,"title":"","content":"OK, here's the problem. You want to turn the Marduk Society into a hunter conspiracy that has no awful secrets and doesn't force moral compromises on its members, and give it access to hyperpowerful technology better than anything any other World of Darkness faction has (other than high-end supernatural beings.) That is, you're proposing to make Marduk a band of Big Damn Heroes, with the moral authority to persuade most NPCs in the setting to back them up and the power to defeat the few who would object. And you've had them around for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> With that combination of traits, Marduk breaks the nWoD setting. It's a bedrock assumption of the new World of Darkness that the real powers are all, in one way or another, alien to the human mindset. Marduk as you want it to be would be a real power that is <i>not</i> alien in any way.<br /> <br /> So I ask you again. Does Leviathan really need the Marduk Society to continue to the present day?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T10:23:02-07:00","id":630022,"title":"","content":"Once again you're post is based on a misconception.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=629988#post629988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you've had them around for thousands of years.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not true.<br /> <br /> The Marduk Society. An organisation of evil sorcerers and their minions was around for thousands of years.<br /> The Marduk Society. An organisation of heroic adventurers and profiteering conspirators manipulated from the shadows by evil sorcerers was around for thousands of years<br /> The Marduk Society. A heroic organisation has been around for about one to five years. And they still haven't quite come to grips with their history and what it means for their future.<br /> <br /> Give them time and yes, they'll break the setting but their existence doesn't break the established cannon.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yes. Breaking the setting, (barring them getting into some big fight with the God Machine or the Exarchs - neither of whom exist in Leviathan unless you're playing crossover) is intentional. The Tribe's greatest dream is to return to their lost golden age, so naturally the grand ending of their long conflict with humanity is their arch enemies getting to return to their golden age.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=629988#post629988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a bedrock assumption of the new World of Darkness that the real powers are all, in one way or another, alien to the human mindset. Marduk as you want it to be would be a real power that is <i>not</i> alien in any way.</div> </div> </div> </div> Welcome to the second edition Michael. Where we break all the assumptions set by the first edition.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T12:24:06-07:00","id":630146,"title":"","content":"Perhaps war fatigue is what's holding back the new Marduk, or perhaps maybe they're still trying to clean up their closet. Essentially, they'd be like the Loyalists, but well, bigger and better funded.<br /> <br /> Also, for fun, how do you envision them in an &quot;everything is true&quot; scenario, where everything, atleast on the global scale, noncosmic scale, is canon?<br /> <br /> <br /> Moving away from Marduk, do since Leviathans have their own cults, how are rules for combined or conjoined cults so far? Or maybe Cult vs Cult warfare (because &quot;holy war&quot; is kinda inevitable when you play a godling)<br /> <br /> Are Occultists going to have their own cults?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T13:09:10-07:00","id":630171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=630146#post630146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps war fatigue is what's holding back the new Marduk</div> </div> </div> </div> Didn't I say exactly that just one post ago <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Marduk's currently in a state of institutional shock. They just discovered they've been controlled by evil immortal wizards, they had a civil war, and now they're running on autopilot while they try to figure out which parts of their strategy is a good idea and which parts were part of the conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Fatigue won't last forever though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=630146#post630146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving away from Marduk, do since Leviathans have their own cults, how are rules for combined or conjoined cults so far? Or maybe Cult vs Cult warfare (because &quot;holy war&quot; is kinda inevitable when you play a godling)</div> </div> </div> </div> The Cult rules have been written up already. They're linked somewhere on the thread... <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TY33912o7ngUtKEXT4ow-5uHNyOlmKWkmykWoNrCuQE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">or right here</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There's no &quot;conjoined&quot; cult rules. It's just treated as one cult. As for warfare, click the link <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=630146#post630146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Occultists going to have their own cults?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes, they're more likely to use a combination of Allies and Retainers for their rituals and if they rule an organisation it could be either a sane organised crime group instead of a cult (it still uses the cult rules though) since sane people are easier to manage.<br /> <br /> When they have cults they're usually small. Mad cultists are harder to control when they can take you in a fight (Occultist magic is stolen Leviathan rituals: to slow to use against a gun)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T15:36:25-07:00","id":630305,"title":"","content":"Why does having an exceptional Success give you negative conditions when using the drawback of the Secret Society, but not a normal success?<br /> <br /> Legitimate Organization doesn't say that it increases Piety cap by 2.<br /> <br /> Lahmasu returns as part of the cult, I see. Very nice. Are they going to get a treatment or update similar to Wolf Blooded?<br /> <br /> Hm, so apparently according to the rules, it's theoretically possible for a cult to actually win another war with the Marduk Society. Has to be one epicly big cult, but it's possible.... in much the same way epic adventurers can beat D&amp;D gods. You probably need to hijack an IBCM to do so and be like the focus of the Chronicle to actually, you know, happen. Wonder what happens in such a scenario?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T00:33:14-07:00","id":630785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=630305#post630305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does having an exceptional Success give you negative conditions when using the drawback of the Secret Society, but not a normal success?</div> </div> </div> </div> Whenever a Cult gets an Exceptional Success the cultists get &quot;excited&quot;. Normally a Leviathan can reign them back in, but in a Secret Society they don't have the nessacary oversight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=630305#post630305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legitimate Organization doesn't say that it increases Piety cap by 2.</div> </div> </div> </div> Does now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=630305#post630305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lahmasu returns as part of the cult, I see. Very nice. Are they going to get a treatment or update similar to Wolf Blooded?</div> </div> </div> </div> Mutations will get stronger, but the core framework was already a 2E minor template rather than 1E<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=630305#post630305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, so apparently according to the rules, it's theoretically possible for a cult to actually win another war with the Marduk Society. Has to be one epicly big cult, but it's possible.... in much the same way epic adventurers can beat D&amp;D gods. You probably need to hijack an IBCM to do so and be like the focus of the Chronicle to actually, you know, happen. Wonder what happens in such a scenario?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the Tribe saying &quot;whooo.... now what?&quot; in charachter.<br /> <br /> Though if you can beat Marduk, chances are you can come up with a good now what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T11:24:14-07:00","id":631332,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's a good idea to give the Marduk Society definite institutional limits, since we run into the If It Has Stats, We Can Kill It issue. Note that it's possible for a sufficiently powerful and well-funded Leviathan to destroy their ancient foes, but don't describe a definite power level at which the Leviathan can fundamentally change the setting -- that's up to the ST, and how they use Marduk from game to game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T10:36:37-07:00","id":632506,"title":"","content":"Here's something I just realized. Are Leviathans going to have innate: &quot;resistances&quot; to make certain attacks less damaging? Asking because vampires downgrade everything lethal to bashing except magic and werewolves downgrade nonmagical or bane based aggravated damage to lethal, allowing to be quick healed. Monster splats seem to be heading in the direction of being innately tougher to kill than more humanoid ones it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T10:48:05-07:00","id":632517,"title":"","content":"Not innately; though they'll get extra health from Size once they transform.<br /> <br /> The right Channel will catch them up to other supernaturals though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T20:19:50-07:00","id":642439,"title":"","content":"Had a thought regarding Tranquility today. I know it is currently planned for it to be replaced by 2 Morality/Integrity meters, to track the 2 failure modes Leviathans can undergo (Typhon and Ophion). But what about this for salvaging it: Tranquility measures how much control one of the Tribe has over themselves (keeping them above their bestial heritage), and when it bottoms out, they become little more than a very cunning, <i>very</i> powerful animal/monster (much like Kindred descending to become Draugr). But there is a way to circumvent this: by granting oneself an <i>exemption</i> (similar to how Vampire 2ed get personal Banes, and Hunters modified their Code) to the sins/disruptions of Tranquility, one doesn't need to worry about that. After all, one is <i>different</i> from others. <i>Godly</i> even. Basically, 0 Tranquility = Typhon, Replacing 10 or so Tranquility sins = Ophion. The more subtle insanity/corruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T09:05:52-07:00","id":646839,"title":"","content":"Had some thoughts on the Wake, Leviathan brainwashing, etc.<br /> <br /> The Wake represents the Leviathan's psychic presence: part shadow, part manifestation of their Tempest. Much like a Vampire or Werewolf Predatory Aura, but in the Leviathan's case, <i>they can't turn it off</i>. When it intersects with another psychic presence (such as, say, people's minds), it has a number of effects: For those &quot;lucky&quot; enough to be Atolls (Touchstone-equivalents?), their minds ground out the Tempest and calm the Leviathan's Wake. Most other people whose minds and ideologies conflict with the Leviathan's get their minds worn down by the swirling Tempest, manifesting increasing severities of mental Conditions. They either modify their worldview to match the Leviathans (swimming with the current, and joining the Leviathan's cult), or learn to live with their misery. Some unfortunates, though, <i>break</i> under the strain and become hollowed out (Soul Loss?), only to be filled with the Leviathan's psychic presence - the Beloved. Of course, there is breaking, and then there is <u><i>breaking</i></u> - some minds get so warped by the trauma, they come to hate and revile the very mental presence that now fills them, drawing power from it to turn against its source (Ahab's having a Power-Stat mirroring the Leviathan they are obsessed with, like a Changeling's Fetch?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=627868#post627868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">Unless someone can think of a way Marduk can kill a leviathan by blasting it with Freedom of Religion, or The Right to Liberty, ...</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">For close-knit, supportive communities that conflict with the Leviathan's worldview, their mind reinforce each other and act not as debris to toss, or rocks to wear down, but a shoreline that checks the Leviathan's presence. (&quot;Good&quot; communities inflicting a penalty on Leviathans due to psychic conflict. May necessitate Leviathans working to &quot;break up&quot; a community, solely so they have mental &quot;breathing room&quot;)</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-31-2015, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T09:56:00-07:00","id":646908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=646839#post646839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For those &quot;lucky&quot; enough to be Atolls (Touchstone-equivalents?)</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope. Atolls aren't touchstones. They invert the Wake, making Leviathans obsessed with them and easily manipulatable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=646839#post646839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They either modify their worldview to match the Leviathans (swimming with the current, and joining the Leviathan's cult), or learn to live with their misery. Some unfortunates, though, <i>break</i> under the strain and become hollowed out (Soul Loss?), only to be filled with the Leviathan's psychic presence - the Beloved.</div> </div> </div> </div> modifying your worldview and joining the cult is Beloved. It's rare to find even a single non-Beloved as part of a Leviathan's Cult.<br /> <br /> The Wake will have odd effects on Soul Loss (and Leviathans will gain the ability to rip souls out of people or eat them) - esentially being Beloved can act as a poor quality substitute soul and soulless people tend to become Beloved in seconds.<br /> <br /> (Leviathans can also rip the Geist (+ soul, they can't disentangle them) out of a Sin-Eater and the Horror out of a Beast. But storytellers will be told that doing so is &quot;as hard as killing them&quot;)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=646839#post646839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">For close-knit, supportive communities that conflict with the Leviathan's worldview, their mind reinforce each other and act not as debris to toss, or rocks to wear down, but a shoreline that checks the Leviathan's presence. (&quot;Good&quot; communities inflicting a penalty on Leviathans due to psychic conflict. May necessitate Leviathans working to &quot;break up&quot; a community, solely so they have mental &quot;breathing room&quot;)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>That wouldn't let Marduk win in a straight up fight - in fact since it's easier to destroy than toe create it would put Leviathans at a massive disadvantage; and Marduk is supposed to have the advantage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T18:13:54-07:00","id":647493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=646908#post646908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nope. Atolls aren't touchstones. They invert the Wake, making Leviathans obsessed with them and easily manipulatable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking from a mechanical perspective, such as benefits to Integrity-equivalent rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=646908#post646908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> modifying your worldview and joining the cult is Beloved. It's rare to find even a single non-Beloved as part of a Leviathan's Cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;shrug&gt; I was just thinking of degrees between: joining for the secret handshake/relief from nightmares vs &quot;brainwashed and crazy&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=646908#post646908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Wake will have odd effects on Soul Loss (and Leviathans will gain the ability to rip souls out of people or eat them) - esentially being Beloved can act as a poor quality substitute soul and soulless people tend to become Beloved in seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just though of integrating the Soul Loss rules in there. Beloved = Soul Lost as an inherent function (making what Leviathan's do, sometimes incidentally, potentially even more horrific). Also means that even eliminating the Leviathan still leaves its hollowed out cult in tatters, desperately looking for meaning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=646908#post646908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That wouldn't let Marduk win in a straight up fight - in fact since it's easier to destroy than toe create it would put Leviathans at a massive disadvantage; and Marduk is supposed to have the advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I didn't mean instead of technology, or even restricting it solely to Marduk. Just one more thing that makes a Leviathan trying to get by incidentally causing harm to those around them. Also means that fostering healthy communities is yet another thing for Marduk to focus on (other than ray guns).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T11:53:40-07:00","id":659630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=629988#post629988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, here's the problem. You want to turn the Marduk Society into a hunter conspiracy that has no awful secrets and doesn't force moral compromises on its members, and give it access to hyperpowerful technology better than anything any other World of Darkness faction has (other than high-end supernatural beings.) That is, you're proposing to make Marduk a band of Big Damn Heroes, with the moral authority to persuade most NPCs in the setting to back them up and the power to defeat the few who would object. And you've had them around for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> With that combination of traits, Marduk breaks the nWoD setting. It's a bedrock assumption of the new World of Darkness that the real powers are all, in one way or another, alien to the human mindset. Marduk as you want it to be would be a real power that is <i>not</i> alien in any way.<br /> <br /> So I ask you again. Does Leviathan really need the Marduk Society to continue to the present day?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the real problem is the all-powerful role the above Raven write-up grants them, basically a scientific version of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> But the idea that a small cult of people with their limited resources can soar ahead of the whole world's scientific progress is just unfitting and unrealistic. How?<br /> <br /> The new WoD has been a lot more sober on this subject, thankfully - secret societies aren't secret world governments that control everything, like a conspiracy nut's wet dream. They are mostly busy dealing with their own internal affairs and focusing on simpler, local goals; world events catch them as powerless as everybody else, and they have no choice but to follow the times and hunt for scraps along the way usually either.<br /> <br /> I always enjoyed the MS as a concept, and I liked that they are kinda steampunk-y - if Ahabs are a tribute to &quot;Moby Dick&quot; then Marduk seemed like a salute to &quot;Captain Nemo&quot; and similar Verne-ish adventures. But it has to be kept at that level.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> I'm totally a nobody here, but let me picture a Marduk Society -I- wouldn't mind putting in a campaign -I- was running, chop it up and take from it what you want:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>What the Marduk society has are certain mystical teachings about the supernatural nature of lightning and electricity. </b><br /> - the secrets about Marduk's identity and his powers. (Whether Marduk used a device, godly powers, some kind of magic, some special trick, etc. to defeat Tiamat, that's what the MS got hold of.) Whenever society developed a new use for electricity, they could use this knowledge to improve those technologies. An improved way to bake pottery in 2000 BC, ultra-effective Tesla Coils around 1900. Their scope is narrow, and their researchers must still follow &amp; lag behind the world's scientific progress.<br /> This is especially true in the modern age where technological advancement has become so rapid that Marduk is decades behind -there certainly isn't a Marduk Cell Phone (though there are quite probably low-tech subtitutes, like ammonite-shaped personal radio transmitter the size of a hand to be placed on one ear that'd have seemed amazingly small and powerful to a person 50 years ago, not so much today.)<br /> Other Marduk tech is more advanced, but the real draw of these toys is not that they are sci-fi, but that they are avaliable cheaper and more easily than modern top-notch tech, and their effectiveness in Leviathan-hunting.<br /> <br /> The means by these crafting methods become possible is borderline supernatural. It is not simply a new scientific fact that allows them to be built; it's an occult understanding about the supernatural associations of lighting.<br /> Sharing this method (while it would also be against the Society's goals) would also most likely be flat out impossible unless the world is &quot;awakened&quot; to the existence of the supernatural first; without that, these theories would simply look like strange occultism. A Marduk Society blueprint for a stun-gun would more closely resemble a page from Agrippa's &quot;Occult Philosophy&quot; than a page from modern engineering text.<br /> <br /> This is also why a Marduk agent has to buy them with merits.<br /> Only the initiated of the inner circle of MS have access to the rituals and creation and re-supply is only possible through these channels.<br /> <br /> While these methods are supernatural though, they do not require a supernatural advantage like Vitae, Ichor, etc. (the advantage of a minor template). If that question ever comes up, rituals would consume Willpower (similar to other minor templates) instead.<br /> <br /> <b>History: </b>(again, pulling this off the top of my head - pick whatever you like from it and discard the rest):<br /> <br /> Marduk was a legendary hero. He may have been a metaphorical figure, a god, a demigod, a spirit-being, a Mage or a Genius (maybe the first or one of the first) or evensomething in-between or something even stranger than these. His battle with Tiamat may have been taken place before the the beginning of the world as we know it, or may have been quite recent and taken place in the real world.<br /> The truth has been obscured by the (first) Marduk Society who stole and suppressed all accounts they could about him after his death.<br /> <br /> What is known that Marduk faced Tiamat, the embodiment of the sea and the mother of all the monsters in it, and he could &quot;draw forth lightning from the earth&quot; to strike down his hated enemy. Victorious, he then reigned over the city of Babel until his death. Following his death, knowledge about his personal history and his power was seized by the cult that arose around him in his lifetime.<br /> Yet Marduk was smart enough to foresee this, and real power, real scientific knowledge made its way back to the hands of the common people; what the cult was left with were a small number of select secrets.<br /> Foremost among these was the secret that the flesh of Leviathans could grant a man immortality. The cult existed for centuries around this one goal, extending their own lifespan beyond its natural capacity. Their other secret they could stole, Marduk's power over lightning became their tool in this, used to seek out the descendants of Tiamat which they then hunted down and devoured.<br /> <br /> Only some time after the 10th century would some leaders of the Society become interested in technological advancments, and sarted harnessing the lightning for other purposes, gaining a technological edge that would make the sciety the stuff of legend and gained them unimaginable power.<br /> <br /> (They have NOT been, however, a contributor to technological development for the rest of the world. Their discoveries haven't been that numberous in comparison, and were kept strictily for themselves.)<br /> <br /> In fact, the 1st industrial revolution left the society completely unaffacted.<br /> It was during the 2nd revolution in the 19th century that the society would start to develop the devices they are now known for.<br /> <br /> In the meantime however, however, another big change happened. Fate has finally caught up with the society. The Age of Discovery made some Leviathans realise that mankind's advance was unstoppable and they would eventually not be able to hide themselves even in places previously safe. Word of mouth and records about the men secretly hunting them has piled up over the centuries conspired and came down on them hard. A group of Leviathans later to be known as the 7-Sea Alliance have grouped together to end the threat once and for all.<br /> The followers of Marduk may have had immortal lifespans, but they were not invulnerable, nor were they expecting the enemy to find them in their own homes. Previous Leviathan retaliations have always been solo efforts and settled at sea.<br /> After a relatively short but intense campaign, the Society as it previously existed - the traditionalists, the priest-wizard, the robed ntediluvians - were wiped out. If any remained, they hid themselves completely from Leviathans and mortals alike.<br /> <br /> Yet this was not the end of the Society, and ironically, this act contributed to the birth of a more radical and violent incarnation.<br /> <br /> Some submarines left behind by the society were discovered by British sailors. These men were primarily motivated by profit and the spreading of British (and Western) imperialism. They cared little for traditions around Marduk's secrets and more about how these could be used for their present-day goals.<br /> <br /> A man named Jacob Arronax, who became their new founder and leader, laid down the new tenets that would guide them (and still do):<br /> <br /> 1. Earth belonged to man (and particuarly, the Western man and Western civilization); the monsters that would step in their way would have to be destroyed.<br /> <br /> 2. Marduk's secrets and technology should be kept within the group and used to achieve real-world political and financial benefits.<br /> <br /> 3. immortality through Leviathan flesh became a secret kept from the common foot soldiers. Only the captains would parttake in immortality should the opportunity arise. (Even like this, the few leaders who achieved immortality would rarely live beyond 200 years - done in by Leviathans or, more often, by their own crew members.<br /> <br /> Unlike the 1st society which viewed the Tribe merely as monsters, the new Society realized that they could be at least partially human if they wanted and more importantly, they could be keepers of important secrets. Maybe a few Leviathans did try to negotiate their way out of captivity by offering maps to treasures or occult secrets, but the Marduk Society now believes that all Leviathans have such know a secret. They are more likely to capture and interrigate Leviathans than outright kill them.<br /> <br /> Let's not mince the world, the new Marduks were little more than a band of pirates. Only at the end of the 20th century did a more intellectual element begin to arise within a society. By and large, the group still follows Arronax's ground rules, but a select few now have started to rediscover their roots (which the annihilation of the 1st society left them largely ignorant of), and re-examine their place in the modern world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T21:01:07-07:00","id":660284,"title":"","content":"Nice. More World of <i>Darkness</i> compliant, I'd think. One element from your version that's nice is the concept of conspiracy replacing conspiracy, yet the faction more or less remains intact, functionally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T00:15:12-07:00","id":660453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=659630#post659630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the idea that a small cult of people with their limited resources can soar ahead of the whole world's scientific progress is just unfitting and unrealistic. How?</div> </div> </div> </div> They don't soar ahead. See post #139 - it's actually rather similar to what you have here, but not limited to electricity.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for your proposed Marduk. It's simply not going to happen. The theme of the Marduk Society is that they are precisely the opposite of Leviathan's core theme - stagnation. Leviathans fell from grace in pre-history with the death of their founder and stayed there. Marduk fell from grace in pre-history with the death of their founder and slowly rose back up to greatness.<br /> <br /> Having Marduk destroyed by an alliance of Leviathans after they've been improving themselves for thousands of years and Leviathans have not completely goes against the theme.<br /> <br /> <br /> I did actually consider having a pirate themed antagonist but I couldn't make it work. I couldn't find any thematic way to make a meaningful conflict with Leviathans; and while Pirate Somalia would make a great Dark Age for Leviathan - it's already a Dark Age and the pirates would be mortal antagonists (or a Leviathan's Beloved) not a separate group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-11-2015, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:39:39-07:00","id":660802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=660453#post660453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They don't soar ahead. See post #139 - it's actually rather similar to what you have here, but not limited to electricity.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have levitating fortresses that float on top of &quot;folded space&quot; and AI as intelligent as a two-year-old human -- you explicitly describe them as scratching the Clarke limit. I'd call that &quot;soaring ahead.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for your proposed Marduk. It's simply not going to happen. The theme of the Marduk Society is that they are precisely the opposite of Leviathan's core theme - stagnation. Leviathans fell from grace in pre-history with the death of their founder and stayed there. Marduk fell from grace in pre-history with the death of their founder and slowly rose back up to greatness.<br /> <br /> Having Marduk destroyed by an alliance of Leviathans after they've been improving themselves for thousands of years and Leviathans have not completely goes against the theme. </div> </div> </div>Think of it as a &quot;pruning&quot; -- at the time, Marduk was still, on some level, a cabal of immortal &quot;magi&quot; who consumed Leviathan flesh to live. In terms of theme, consuming Leviathan flesh for immortality would definitely carry a cost on a symbolic level -- why not assuming the curse of stagnation? Sure, Marduk's tech advanced, but until the deaths of the Wise Old Men who ran the whole show at the hands of Leviathans, they were using the same pseudo-ritualistic, hyper-secretive occult conspiracy methodology that served them faithfully in the early days of civilization. The extermination of those who consumed Leviathan flesh allowed them to grow as an organization; they haven't conquered the world yet because their leaders still eat mermaids to survive, which gives us a good reason for there to be a status quo as opposed to &quot;Marduk will rule the world in fifty years and their Golden Age is only a matter of time.&quot;<br /> <br /> In other words, it's in theme -- Leviathans can do big showy shit and utterly wreck the day of the conspirators, because they're good at waging war and they've got cults everywhere, but their success is ultimately Pyrrhic and marks a mere blip on their path to eventual extinction; only their corruption in Marduk's ranks keeps them from being chum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T10:12:12-07:00","id":660843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=660802#post660802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have levitating fortresses that float on top of &quot;folded space&quot; and AI as intelligent as a two-year-old human -- you explicitly describe them as scratching the Clarke limit. I'd call that &quot;soaring ahead.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> In real life we have AIs and teleportation right now. Just really early days stuff. Marduk couldn't develop either until they had regular tech to piggy back off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=660802#post660802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they haven't conquered the world yet because their leaders still eat mermaids to survive, which gives us a good reason for there to be a status quo as opposed to &quot;Marduk will rule the world in fifty years and their Golden Age is only a matter of time.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is exactly why this version is never going to happen. Leviathans are defined by being unable to escape their status qou. Marduk's entire purpose is to be the Leviathans antithesis. The people who don't have a status qou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-11-2015, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T12:55:59-07:00","id":660985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=660843#post660843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In real life we have AIs and teleportation right now. Just really early days stuff. Marduk couldn't develop either until they had regular tech to piggy back off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even so, you've still got them inherently ahead -- Marduk technology is always fundamentally better. (Not quite sure how that works, actually -- Marduk is capable of building AI leagues ahead of what we've got today... but they can't build AI that's as good as what we have today? Why is it that a Marduk scientist can build an AI as smart as a dog, but can't build an AI that isn't as smart as a dog until a normal scientist does?)<br /> <br /> Also, I feel like I'm missing something -- Leviathans attack the Marduk Society and kill off their traditionalist, antediluvian faction, but Marduk adapts and comes out stronger for it... and you feel that this <i>muddles</i> the theme of &quot;stagnation versus adaptation.&quot; Marduk's immortal Wise Old Men were mystics who governed humanity from the shadows and consumed the flesh of monsters to gain immortality -- they weren't changing, they were preserving the status quo, and do you think they ever planned on exterminating Leviathans when that meant they'd die right along with them? That puts Marduk-as-it-was on an even keel with Leviathans, in your thematic terms -- why shouldn't the Leviathans win with their big old Eld God powers, in that case? And, likewise, a Marduk that relies on the ancient secrets -- eating mermaid, the power of lightning, the Sigil of Marduk -- is still reliant, on some level, on the inheritance of Babylon rather than innovation -- and that's <i>interesting</i> and makes them a little more morally ambiguous, which is sort of the nWoD's Thing.<br /> <br /> Jut-jawed Science Heroes don't actually exist; people are people everywhere and always susceptible to moral turpitude, although they don't always fail -- but organizations are people multiplied, and someone can always be tempted with a sufficient sample size; opposing evil doesn't make you a good person, and opposing static monsters doesn't make you a perfectly dynamic demigod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","user":"CalvaryKeter","date":". 09-11-2015, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T13:43:55-07:00","id":661048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=660985#post660985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (Not quite sure how that works, actually -- Marduk is capable of building AI leagues ahead of what we've got today... but they can't build AI that's as good as what we have today? Why is it that a Marduk scientist can build an AI as smart as a dog, but can't build an AI that isn't as smart as a dog until a normal scientist does?)</div> </div> </div> </div> There is no sensible Watsonian explanation for this and I won't pretend there is one. But the Doylist explanation is that it ties Marduk's progress to that of regular society rather than to &quot;book of secrets&quot; written in ancient Babylon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=660985#post660985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I feel like I'm missing something -- Leviathans attack the Marduk Society and kill off their traditionalist, antediluvian faction, but Marduk adapts and comes out stronger for it... and you feel that this <i>muddles</i> the theme of &quot;stagnation versus adaptation.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Abso freaking lutely.<br /> <br /> Marduk's theme (which btw is &quot;improvement&quot;, not &quot;adaptation&quot;) is an enormous metaphor for how civilisation, law and order, reason, etc, allowed humanity to overcome our primordial instincts which are savage and cruel. (More or less anyway - I'm leaving it open if any Old Men survived)<br /> <br /> In this metaphor the Society is civilisation. The Old Men are the primordial instincts. Marduk himself is that one in a million stroke of blind luck that meant some apes evolved super intelligence. Thus to make the metaphor work it is absolutely imperative that the Marduk Society (and regular civilisation) are the ones who defeated the Old Men.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=660985#post660985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That puts Marduk-as-it-was on an even keel with Leviathans, in your thematic terms</div> </div> </div> </div> There's no even keel. Marduk won, period.<br /> <br /> This is the <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.co.uk/2013/12/red-sky-at-morning.html\" target=\"_blank\">Chaoskampf</a>. One of the oldest and most widespread pieces of mythology. Marduk vs Tiamat. Zeus vs Typhon. Odin vs Ymir (to use a non-typical example) Even Abrahamic religion gets in on it with Leviathan himself.<br /> <br /> There's an ancient battle between a sky god and a water dragon. The sky god wins, and this represents the fundamental triumph of order over chaos. I am making full use of this cultural legacy, I'd be mad not too. And that means the whole reason we have cities, laws, etc, is because Marduk beat Tiamat. War's over, humanity won.<br /> <br /> The core idea, and the core horror of Leviathan, is what do you do after you've lost and your whole species lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-11-2015, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T14:42:20-07:00","id":661116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661048#post661048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There is no sensible Watsonian explanation for this and I won't pretend there is one. But the Doylist explanation is that it ties Marduk's progress to that of regular society rather than to &quot;book of secrets&quot; written in ancient Babylon.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, if there's no sensible Watsonian explanation for something, you can't put it in your narrative. There's got to be some kind of explanation that doesn't ruin suspension of disbelief -- at least, if you're working with a semi-real setting like the WoD, instead of a pulpy, character-comes-second setting, which Leviathan isn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Marduk's theme (which btw is &quot;improvement&quot;, not &quot;adaptation&quot;) is an enormous metaphor for how civilisation, law and order, reason, etc, allowed humanity to overcome our primordial instincts which are savage and cruel. (More or less anyway - I'm leaving it open if any Old Men survived) </div> </div> </div>Semantics -- Marduk &quot;improved&quot; when the Old Men were killed and came out stronger for it, yadda yadda exact same thing. As for your metaphor -- humanity hasn't overcome its primordial instincts. Like, it's developed mechanisms to deal with them, but we have the word &quot;atrocity&quot; for a reason -- people still murder, steal and make war on each other, like, all the time! Society is a mechanism for distracting and lulling our ids -- and, rather neatly, that's why we still have Leviathans. They're in the blood -- to wipe out Tiamat's entire legacy, you'd need to kill or replace the entire human race, since the ichor flows eternal in some bloodline somewhere...<br /> <br /> You can't kill the id. You can direct it constructively or control it medically or physically or psychologically or socially, but you can't kill it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In this metaphor the Society is civilisation. The Old Men are the primordial instincts. Marduk himself is that one in a million stroke of blind luck that meant some apes evolved super intelligence. Thus to make the metaphor work it is absolutely imperative that the Marduk Society (and regular civilization) are the ones who defeated the Old Men. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.co.uk/2013/12/red-sky-at-morning.html\" target=\"_blank\">Chaoskampf</a>... The core idea, and the core horror of Leviathan, is what do you do after you've lost and your whole species lost. </div> </div> </div>I know what the Chaoskampf is -- but the thing is, <i>there are still Leviathans</i>. You can't claim to have won when the other side is still kicking and occasionally turning your coastal towns into cult communes. And if the metaphor breaks down because of it, that's actually totally fine with me; the game benefits if the metaphor isn't perfectly coherent, because Marduk has to be able to lose once in a while, or else players will feel like they can't affect the setting at all. If Leviathan were directly parallel to the Chaoskampf, it wouldn't be a game, because our protagonists would be electrocuted corpses -- Leviathan's got Lovecraft in it, too, not just Babylon, and part of Lovecraft is that the descendants of Dagon have to be a legitimate threat on some level.<br /> <br /> You can't just translate a myth one-to-one and expect it to make a good narrative -- you've got to allow for deviation from the central themes, for the plot changing according to what the characters do or how the ST wants to tell the story.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Vree's Marduk Society isn't a perfect one-to-one with the forces of civilization -- it's an organization of people, with all that that implies. They're sometimes selfish and imperialistic. They're still &quot;the good guys,&quot; but they're not perfectly ethical and their motives aren't universally good. (That's one of the issues I have with the Society, by the way -- you can't just purge all the Bad members and wind up with only paragons who want to do right by all of humanity; typically, the dude who suggests guillotining all the nobles isn't the one you want in charge in peacetime, because the guillotine's probably gonna come out again.) It's the same with the Pentacle, for example -- the Silver Ladder is idealistic but has the ethical lure of temporal power and an excuse to ignore Wisdom. It's not the good Silver Ladder members who do good things and the bad ones manipulating them from the shadows -- it's all just people, some of whom can (build lightning guns/fire lightning from their hands), trying to get by.<br /> <br /> I mean, Vampire's big metaphor is &quot;drug addiction.&quot; Where does the Ordo Dracul fit into the latter? &quot;I was on crack, so I joined the crack transhumanists who want to develop a new variant that will give them immunity to sunlight&quot;? The WoD clearly doesn't require absolute conformity to the themes set out in canon game lines; why should we do that when the alternative is a) interesting and b) justified in a Watsonian sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","user":"CalvaryKeter","date":". 09-11-2015, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T15:15:40-07:00","id":661141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661116#post661116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, if there's no sensible Watsonian explanation for something, you can't put it in your narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure you can. Loads of stories have things work for not-sensiable reasons. Why on Earth did Gordon Freeman climb into a cage inside the bad guy's fortress in Half Life 2? There's no sensible reason for him to do that, but most people are fine with it.<br /> <br /> Marduk's themes work best when they're only a few steps ahead of society's technology. So they have some secret scrolls that let them improve technology but aren't helpful for creating brand new technology. Not a particularly sensible reason, but it does the job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661116#post661116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for your metaphor -- humanity hasn't overcome its primordial instincts. Like, it's developed mechanisms to deal with them</div> </div> </div> </div> Developing mechanisms to deal with primordial instincts is how we overcame them. It's not like metaphors need to be perfect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661116#post661116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't claim to have won when the other side is still kicking and occasionally turning your coastal towns into cult communes.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's nonsense. Humans control the planet, they won.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661116#post661116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because Marduk has to be able to lose once in a while, or else players will feel like they can't affect the setting at all.</div> </div> </div> </div> You can't hurt the God Machine or the Exarchs. At best you can kill a few of their minions or derail one of their plans. You can't drive the True Fae to extinction either.<br /> <br /> Same with Marduk. You can destroy some of their safehouses, once they finish cleaning up and start making plans I'm sure you could derail those. But knocking their space stations out of the sky is like exterminating the entire True Fae. If you're trying to do that you've gone well outside the intended game. You're welcome to do so, but I'm not going to focus on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661116#post661116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't just translate a myth one-to-one and expect it to make a good narrative -- you've got to allow for deviation from the central themes,</div> </div> </div> </div> I didn't and I do.<br /> <br /> But Marduk's history isn't the place to put deviation from the central themes. Marduk's history <b>is</b> the central theme. Marduk's actions in the present day can deviate from the central theme. The other antagonists like Ahabs or Occultists don't have anything to do with the central theme at all because Marduk's got it covered.<br /> <br /> But Marduk's history and their big picture. That is the central theme and it's not going to change. If you want to make constructive criticism suggest ways to make Marduk an even better expression of the central theme because the only way they'll be changed into something other than the central theme is if somebody else writes their own version of Leviathan (which they're welcome to do. All my work here is available for forking)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T15:40:52-07:00","id":661174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661141#post661141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't hurt the God Machine or the Exarchs. At best you can kill a few of their minions or derail one of their plans. You can't drive the True Fae to extinction either.<br /> <br /> Same with Marduk. You can destroy some of their safehouses, once they finish cleaning up and start making plans I'm sure you could derail those. But knocking their space stations out of the sky is like exterminating the entire True Fae. If you're trying to do that you've gone well outside the intended game. You're welcome to do so, but I'm not going to focus on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you notice that all of the entities you described there are a) nonhuman and b) prevented in some way from directly acting on the world? (The True Fae and Arcadian politics / the Courts, the God-Machine is too big to directly affect humanity in the way it wants without agents, the Exarchs are opposed by the Oracles, Archmasters, Pax Arcana et al). That's my issue, here -- Marduk is inevitably going to radically alter the setting because they're humans with no enemies capable of stopping them from attaining their goals; the G-M, True Fae and Exarchs aren't. At the very least, you can get to a place where the G-M can't affect you because it's decided to just set everything up again after you die; it's not causing any paradigm shifts in human culture. Likewise with the True Fae; likewise with the Exarchs, who love the status quo. And I know that you want a big bad that changes things for the sake of your favorite themes, but... an enemy who's inevitably going to conquer the world, whose plans to eliminate you and everyone like you will ultimately succeed on a macro-scale no matter what you do, is frustrating to the point of being pointless to fight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't and I do.<br /> <br /> But Marduk's history isn't the place to put deviation from the central themes. Marduk's history <b>is</b> the central theme. Marduk's actions in the present day can deviate from the central theme. The other antagonists like Ahabs or Occultists don't have anything to do with the central theme at all because Marduk's got it covered. </div> </div> </div>If you replaced Vree's &quot;7-Sea Alliance&quot; with &quot;other members of Marduk, who disbanded in disgrace after realizing that they were glorified butchers,&quot; would that be satisfying to you? It resolves the problem of Leviathans being able to affect the setting. Ultimately, all I want is a Marduk that isn't poised to conquer the world, because the World of Darkness isn't run by conspiracies but by people; multiple other people have expressed this preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","user":"CalvaryKeter","date":". 09-11-2015, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T15:54:48-07:00","id":661179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661174#post661174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you notice that all of the entities you described there are a) nonhuman and b) prevented in some way from directly acting on the world?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, that is obvious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661174#post661174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marduk is inevitably going to radically alter the setting because they're humans with no enemies capable of stopping them from attaining their goals</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, that is intentional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661174#post661174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, all I want is a Marduk that isn't poised to conquer the world, because the World of Darkness isn't run by conspiracies but by people; multiple other people have expressed this preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said they're poised to conquer the world? I certianly didn't. I intentionally haven't said what Marduk is going to do once they finish figuring it out.<br /> <br /> But why would Marduk want to conquer anything? They want to help people. They'd do a better job of that by dismantling all their weapons and reinventing themselves as a legal and very publicly visible technology company than they would by conquering the world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T16:47:24-07:00","id":661228,"title":"","content":"Good to see there's a Leviathan project ongoing again. I never participated in the previous threads but I did run a few successful games of it.<br /> <br /> The current conversation seems to be stagnating. Here are a few points that I don't think have been adressed in detail concerning Marduk.<br /> <br /> - Where do they recruit from these days? Are all their members people who have had run-ins with Leviathans? If not, how does the initiation process go? Are promising candidates picked out from their Police Precinct or Anthropology Lecture and forcefully exposed to footage of the Ancient Tribe? Does the soceity have strong material rewards for its employees? What is the real motivation of those who drop everything to become sea monster Hunters?<br /> <br /> - What is the Societys policy towards Ahabs? They seem to have changed since the last version so that they are now only connected to a single Leviathan. Will the soceity recruit Ahabs they encounter? Use them to track down the local threat? Try to dissuade them and offer psychiatric therapy? Detain them if they're liable to cause harm to themselves or others?<br /> <br /> - Are the internal divisions of Marduk remaining the same with the three Comittees? Or does that no longer fit with the new Society?<br /> <br /> - What is their position on other Supernaturals? Almost all of the main splats prey on or threaten humanity in some way. I'm not sure of this was actually ever adressed.<br /> <br /> - With this incarnation of a virtually Omnipotent and flawless Society, what place do you see them occupying in the average Leviathan session? Are they a constant threat on par with the God Machine in Demon tD, with informants and surveillance everywhere and likely to notice even minor ripples in a small fishing town or are they more deterrants for players that can't control their Outbursts, with more quotidien antagonists being Typhons/ rival Leviathans and the Theurgists?<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Have the ritual mechanics been updated yet? I have plenty of ideas for some new rituals. The 1st edition grimoire was severely lacking.<br /> <br /> I also have a small piece of fiction from the viewpoint of a Beloved in the works if you're interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","user":"Opprobrium","date":". 09-11-2015, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","name":"Opprobrium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T03:19:33-07:00","id":661728,"title":"","content":"Now that's a productive post. Welcome to the thread Opprobrium.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661228#post661228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Where do they recruit from these days?</div> </div> </div> </div> This is a very good question, I never thought about that and it's something that should be covered.<br /> <br /> Personality is definitely key to Marduk recruitment. They go for people who genuinely believe in making a positive difference. Beyond that I'll have to think on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661228#post661228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the Societys policy towards Ahabs?</div> </div> </div> </div> The society sees Ahabs as victims of Leviathans and tries to help them.<br /> <br /> Whether help means isolating them from Leviathans and giving them therapy, helping them slay the Leviathan, or just leaving them be and assuming it will work out once they zap the Leviathan will depend upon the individual Marduk member and the current situation.<br /> <br /> Marduk's become less willing to work with Ahabs over time, because the difference in power between Marduk technology and an Ahab's Damnations has grown over time. But if a Marduk hunter is in a bad spot and sees an Ahab they'd team up without hesitation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661228#post661228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the internal divisions of Marduk remaining the same with the three Comittees? Or does that no longer fit with the new Society?</div> </div> </div> </div> Things won't be changing up too much, mostly they'll just be expanded upon. However that said you won't see the names of three committees and might not see the word comitee in the new edition.<br /> <br /> Take the Cross Disciplinary Committee. There's still Marduk member's who's job is to aquire the money Marduk needs to function and there is going to be actual details on how Marduk gets it's money however now I'm not trying to squeeze everything into three Committees I won't be lumping them in with the guys who design the tech.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661228#post661228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is their position on other Supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div> Canonically undefined. As is typical in the WoD for the Leviathan book I'm mostly pretending that Leviathans and related things are the only supernatural beings that exist.<br /> <br /> You might see some mention of Ghosts and Spirits when the powers are written, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> -<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661228#post661228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what place do you see them occupying in the average Leviathan session? Are they a constant threat on par with the God Machine in Demon tD</div> </div> </div> </div> About time someone asked this question.<br /> <br /> However I can't really answer it. In Demon there's basically two antagonists: The God Machine and other Demons. Leviathan is going to have more than two antagonists - which means the Storyteller will have to pick which ones they're interested in at this moment. Maybe it's a game with Ahabs and rogue cults and Marduk isn't even mentioned; or maybe Marduk's the primary antagonist.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd put it this way. Marduk show up when the storyteller want them too. They could notice a slight ripple in a small fishing town or miss several Leviathans fighting to control Chicago's mobster underworld (part of the reason for the civil war is that it Marduk's current state justifices this kind of lopsided behavior if you suspend some disbelief). If the Storyteller wants to play a game about the mob Demi-Godfathers at war with each other, they shouldn't feel obliged to include Marduk.<br /> <br /> Once Marduk is in play they represent the way Leviathans can't fit in to human society or the modern world. Their modus operandi is to push Leviathans into a point where they can't control their Outbursts because once a Leviathan looses control they'll probably reveal themselves in the open and that allows Marduk to take them down without collatoral damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661228#post661228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have the ritual mechanics been updated yet? I have plenty of ideas for some new rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not yet. I won't seriously work on rituals until Mage 2E rules are out to build upon but my general idea is:<br /> <br /> All rituals fall under one of the Vestiges; the more Channels you have in a Vestige the more advanced rituals you can perform. Want to perform a 4 dot Fecundity Ritual? You simply can't do it without having three Fecundity Channels (+ the Birthright).<br /> <br /> Leviathans have something similar to Mage's 2ED's Reach. They automatically start each Ritual with 1 Reach per dot of Zeal, and a Ritual costs 1 Reach per Dot. Note that Zeal only goes up to five, not seven. However Leviathans can also get Reach from Omens. Pulling of a seven dot Ritual can be done but it requires both high Zeal 5 and good Omens.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure on the exact pricing but my goal is that performing a six dot ritual is worth an Aspiration, while a seven dot ritual is more of a plot device than an actual power players might use. You might spend the entire game trying to stop (or perform) one seven dot ritual.<br /> <br /> Ideally I'd also have room for fairly easy uses of Omens to bump you from, say, Zeal 2 to 4 dots, and to spend Omen points on other things like bonus effects or less evil sacrileges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661228#post661228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have plenty of ideas for some new rituals. The 1st edition grimoire was severely lacking.</div> </div> </div> </div> You could probably start on the grimoir now. A quick look at the Mage spoilers to see how they set up sample spells should be enough for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661228#post661228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have a small piece of fiction from the viewpoint of a Beloved in the works if you're interested.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course I am <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-12-2015, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T04:29:46-07:00","id":661779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not yet. I won't seriously work on rituals until Mage 2E rules are out to build upon </div> </div> </div>But..but Mage 2ed won't come out until next year <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 09-12-2015, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T07:27:55-07:00","id":661869,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T18:33:26-07:00","id":663671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661141#post661141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Marduk's history and their big picture. That is the central theme and it's not going to change. If you want to make constructive criticism suggest ways to make Marduk an even better expression of the central theme because the only way they'll be changed into something other than the central theme is if somebody else writes their own version of Leviathan (which they're welcome to do. All my work here is available for forking)</div> </div> </div> </div>I might just take you up on that challenge <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But I think you're overstating the importance of your newest write-up.<br /> Nowhere in the version that is currently on the Wiki is this huge importance and influence of the Society ever indicated or mentioned.<br /> (Even Marduk himself is kept deliberately vague and possibly untrue.)<br /> The first chapter (The World As it Was) does a perfectly good explanation of what the Tribe are, why they are so rare, etc. without bringing up the Society even once.<br /> Even the Marduk Society's own section on the Wiki paints a more modest picture (sans space stations or kill-sats).<br /> <br /> If the idea existed prior, it certainly did not seem vital for the setting.<br /> Saying that altering it would change &quot;themes&quot; is simply not true.<br /> <br /> On the contrary, I feel like adding them like this seems to destroy this otherwise awesome game and settings.<br /> I completely agree with CalvaryKeter (and judging from the votes, others do too) that you can't put in something like this and NOT alter the setting and completely shift focus. This is done at the expense of the existing relevant themes, contrary to your claim.<br /> <br /> I see no reason why they even need to be more than what you repeatedly described them as: a Hunter conspiracy.<br /> What you've written here is a 6+ power stat ascended template.<br /> <br /> The first problem is that you're forcing an element (a Technocracy) in a game it doesn't fit and draws attention away from the actual themes.<br /> The second is that you've written them above in a Mary Sue fashion (stupid powerful, perfectly good, perfectly devoid of any interesting human traits). (Why, I don't know.)<br /> <br /> It's like you forgot that these guys are NOT going to be the actual PCs, so glorifying them in fact steals opportunities from the PCs.<br /> <br /> I definitely wouldn't put them into a Leviathan game I run because,<br /> a. I'm not the kind of GM who bullies the players with an invincible antagonist,<br /> b. nor am I the kind of GM who has the NPCs get the glory other than the players (that should be like, &quot;how NOT to run a GMPC no 1.)<br /> c. since you did not write them as people but as some 10-year old's idea of a hero, I literally can't come up with an interesting character to represent them.<br /> d. I simply don't want to play &quot;Leviathans in Future City&quot; or &quot;Leviathans on Space Station Alpha&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, players who don't want it can just ignore them&quot; isn't good justification;<br /> They could've put robots into Vampite:tR on the basis that <i>some</i> players might like them and it'd still have been an awful idea. But you aren't just adding a throwaway antagonist, you're ALTERING THE WHOLE SETTING just so that you can include this one.<br /> <br /> This was supposed to be a setting about adventures at sea, sea monsters, with a side dish of Chtulhu.<br /> Wizards who point laser satelites at the Earth from space is comparable to Doctor Who showing up in your D&amp;D dungeon.<br /> <br /> You talked a lot about themes and messages, but the problem is none of them are actually reflected in your Marduk write-up.<br /> We only know of the supposed themes because of you're informing us.<br /> eg. you say they say they are meant to embody dynamic change as opposed to Leviathan stagnation, yet this group following the same goal for millenia and even having the same leaders is anything but dynamic.<br /> Or if they are meant to represent humanity, yet there is nothing in these idealised supermen that is even remotely human.<br /> <br /> I read though the comments and wondered if you maybe inflated Marduk Soc to justify Leviathan rarity.<br /> If that was the intent, it seemed superfluous. The opening chapter already explains why Leviathans are comparatively rare.<br /> <br /> Now my example write-up, shoddy as it may be, achieves actual relevant goals better, not because it is so good but because this other is so bad.<br /> <br /> The Marduk I proposed is deeply human, with all of the destructive/selfish tendencies.<br /> <br /> Your Marduk has nothing human about it. Immortal, infinitely good, leaving in ametaphorical mountain somewhere separated from humanity.<br /> <br /> &quot;Pirate Marduk&quot; I would have no problem including in a campaign, I throw into them everything that'd would be useful to rope characters into quests. They are more dynamic characters with a variety of goals, wants, and weaknesses. Their purpose is to allow characters do more.<br /> <br /> Yours actually PREVENT player characters from doing sh&amp;t.<br /> <br /> It's like you're even proud of it:<br /> <br /> &quot;Marduk's won, period.<br /> You can't destroy Marduk.&quot;<br /> <br /> So why have them at all?<br /> <br /> The only way I can imagine putting them in the game is either not doing anything, or curb stomping everything.<br /> <br /> I'm not doing either.<br /> <br /> I don't think an idealized view of human-centrism and human progress is called for even under normal circumstances, but since this is the WoD, cynism is 2x appropriate.<br /> Hunters aren't clear &quot;good guys&quot; even in Vigil since they are also killing creatures with clear human conscience.<br /> What excuses it is that they are acting out of self-defense, fear, and a desire to protect their friends &amp; families.<br /> <br /> MardukSoc is even closer to committing systematic genocide as they'd attack/kidnap ANY Leviathan they can find.<br /> What makes them the &quot;good guys&quot; from a human pov is that the Tribe ARE actually the most ancient horrors embodied.<br /> <br /> I don't think there's a need to whitewash them further than that.<br /> They're doing what humankind is best at: attacking a potential rival/threat and calling it self-protection.<br /> THAT is what makes them actually represent humans.<br /> <br /> I don't want to dictate what sort of Marduk you should dream up other than that this is not it;<br /> I only know that the &quot;Leviathan flesh hunters for immortality&quot; and &quot;steampunk electro-raygun Nemo&quot; angles were the ones that were appealing to me.<br /> (By contrast, I have no f-ing idea what a &quot;sky wizard&quot; even is (and the images it evokes in my mind are utterly ridiculous).)<br /> <br /> Flesh-eating I think is great both because it is a nod to the &quot;mermaid flesh&quot; myths of Eastern lore, and makes them even more morally gray.<br /> <br /> Also: do you have rules yet for an &quot;ascended&quot; Leviathan?<br /> If you want to fill this niche,<br /> I feel that place should be occupied by Leviathans themselves, probably the horrific slumbering monstrosities waiting for the stars to align from Lovecraftian lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T19:21:38-07:00","id":663717,"title":"","content":"I think that with me and a few others voicing dislike for the new direction of Marduk, I think it's quite clear there's likely some sort of dissonance between the the Kings Raven and his audience.<br /> <br /> I mean, we've all pretty much voiced the same problems and concerns over Marduk as it stands in the current draft.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't mind them having access to space travel, as every Conspiracy would need its own cool gimmicks and that's a neat way to say &quot;We rule the heavens&quot;. Individual agents may or may not have kill sats, but as a whole letting the whole faction possess both absolute moral purity and better technology than everyone in the setting feels a little ham-fisted.<br /> <br /> My proposal (outside of morality) to make them more plausible/more unique would be to emphasize their reliance on orbital assets even on a cell level for delivery and supply versus other &quot;advanced technology&quot;, their tech isn't <i>that</i> much better than other groups in the setting. Maybe they had access to outer space since ancient times and today are the absolute masters of catapulting things to and from orbit, which they do so regularly and expediently to the point that weekly ammunition drops from space are the norm.. This I feel, makes it more obvious that they are the inheritors of the sky at least on a thematic level.<br /> <br /> All you'd need to do is say their drop pods are near impossible to detect on traditional means, radar, and other astronomic things and I don't think anyone would have much problem with that.<br /> <br /> I mean, they shouldn't be so technologically advanced that F-22's possess no threat to their own craft whatsoever (unless that part was hyperbole).<br /> <br /> Oh, and technically, I think we just have to write a different version of Marduk Society instead of writing a whole new Leviathan gameline.<br /> <br /> <br /> Moving away from that, is there going to be a segment discussing deep ocean settings? Speciffically, a setting that's way underwater but is like other settings, in that there's people there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 09-13-2015, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T05:05:35-07:00","id":664109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=663717#post663717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving away from that, is there going to be a segment discussing deep ocean settings? Speciffically, a setting that's way underwater but is like other settings, in that there's people there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, I was hashing out an advanced Leviathan's plan as something just like that: creating a kingdom/civilization for themselves &quot;under the sea&quot; (using specialized Hybrids, largely). If it were to ever be expanded out, complications would have, of course, arisen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T10:11:35-07:00","id":664523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=663717#post663717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving away from that, is there going to be a segment discussing deep ocean settings? Speciffically, a setting that's way underwater but is like other settings, in that there's people there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I'm bored with repeating this discussion.<br /> <br /> The answer is probably not. There's more than enough work here to keep me busy for a very long time so I don't want to add a whole extra setting. I'd love to do a sample city that's an underwater city populated by Gugal that's collapsed into warring Opheon cults until most of the city is rubble and any survivors are either fanatical cultists or desperate civilians (whom the fanatics hunt for canbalism and sacrafaices)<br /> <br /> But that would be a ton of work, and Leviathan's already a ton of work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T12:07:47-07:00","id":664610,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd like to do it too, but yeah, so much work to write out a sample city. But you'd gotta admit, it might be a great thing to do once all of the other things are taken care of?<br /> <br /> I always thought it'd be interesting for Levithan Chronicles to be both undersea...while interacting with humans at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T13:27:30-07:00","id":664693,"title":"","content":"Sadly, I can't think of many excuses to put regular humans underwater. Gugal can fill that niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T15:15:32-07:00","id":664868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=661728#post661728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could probably start on the grimoir now. A quick look at the Mage spoilers to see how they set up sample spells should be enough for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bCould you provide a link? I haven't been following 2ed Mage development.<br /> <br /> Do you want the cosmetic parts of the ritual format to remain the same? With the Portents and the Sacrifice/Effigy setup?<br /> <br /> --------<br /> <br /> The problem with permenant underwater settings is that it's very hard to keep them interesting. To really experience the deep ocean requires senses that humans don't have, to move in directions that we find disorientating and what about communication? Are all inhabitants of the underwater city psychic? Do they have a unique method of sign language? How do you express the intricacies of communication to players in an immersive way if this is the case? It's great to have a character who is able to adapt to marine life in order to explore a sea-floor ruin - and then return- and they occasional Sea Monster vs Submarine combat will make a refreshing change to the story but if the characters don't return to land semi-frequently then there's little way to frame their experiences. Atlantis as a primary setting has little to do in between travelling to a different ruin and fighting other sea monsters and it can be hard to keep the descriptions interesting too - there are only so many ways to describe coral and vast blue expanses. In addition, it negates one of the core aspects of Leviathan in that they will almost entirely be in monstrous forms.<br /> <br /> --------<br /> <br /> Semi-relevant reading material from the SCP foundation :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2662\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/nav:side/social-facebook.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2662\" target=\"_blank\"> SCP-2662 - SCP Foundation </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2662\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2662 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The SCP Foundation's 'top-secret' archives, declassified for your enjoyment. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","user":"Opprobrium","date":". 09-14-2015, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","name":"Opprobrium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T16:13:44-07:00","id":664996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=664868#post664868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bCould you provide a link? I haven't been following 2ed Mage development.</div> </div> </div> </div> Here you go<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/paradoxical/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/paradoxical/\" target=\"_blank\"> Paradoxical &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/paradoxical/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/paradoxical/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=664868#post664868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you want the cosmetic parts of the ritual format to remain the same? With the Portents and the Sacrifice/Effigy setup?</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope. Portents and sacrafices will probably be generic and applicable to all rituals.<br /> <br /> That said - a ritual still needs example of what a cult might be doing when they perform it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=664868#post664868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To really experience the deep ocean requires senses that humans don't have, to move in directions that we find disorientating and what about communication? Are all inhabitants of the underwater city psychic? Do they have a unique method of sign language? How do you express the intricacies of communication to players in an immersive way if this is the case?</div> </div> </div> </div> Leviathans can talk underwater just fine.<br /> <br /> Honestly an all underwater Leviathan game would probably be an above water game in all but name. Except that with no humans or Marduk around Leviathans and their cults would have little reason to hide. Which is great if you want a justification for a game where Leviathans and their Cults are in total war with each other, and massive storms or Gozilla like rampages are common weapons.<br /> <br /> You're right that by removing the need for Transformation it removes a key part of a Leviathan game. But sometimes that's the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=664868#post664868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Semi-relevant reading material from the SCP foundation :<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2662\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2662</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I have no interest in reading SCP foundation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally one last point before I close the discussion on Marduk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=663671#post663671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was supposed to be a setting about adventures at sea, sea monsters, with a side dish of Chtulhu.</div> </div> </div> </div> Leviathan is not and has never been about adventures at sea. It's about being a remnant of an aborted stage of creation, and trying to figure out what to do with your life when you have no place in the world - morally, physically or even spiritually.<br /> <br /> That's been there since 1E - I'm enhancing the focus on those aspects. It's not for everyone but it's the only Leviathan I'm interested in writing. Constructive criticism is attempts to help me achieve that goal. Attempts to change that goal are a waste of everyone's time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leviathan 1E</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Together, the Leviathans form the Tribe. United in blood and by circumstance, they are, for good or ill, the remnant of an aborted stage of creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leviathan 1E</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Members of the Tribe do not have the luxury of dismissing this negative portrayal of their lineage. Their existence is unequivocally something horrific, something wrong - the world distorts around them. Their instincts guide them inevitably towards the pursuit of sin and excess, towards the abuse of others, the destruction and perversion of minds. The blood of the Progenitors cries out for the destruction of this new, diluted creation cast in the image of mankind and not their own. A Leviathan cannot plead necessity or make excuses for themselves - they <i>should not be.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=663671#post663671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (sans space stations or kill-sats).</div> </div> </div> </div>And for goodness sake. Kill Sats are in the wiki right now. 5 dot weaponry.<br /> <br /> [edit] Missed this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=663671#post663671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also: do you have rules yet for an &quot;ascended&quot; Leviathan?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm still deciding if I want them. If I have them they'll just be Leviathans who buy more than 10 dots of Sheol.<br /> <br /> However I can't imagine a Sheol 11+ Leviathan suriviving. They'll attract so much attention that something will kill them (Marduk, The God Machine, an Archmage. Nobody wants ascended Leviathans rampaging through the cosmos). If they hid in the Rift they might survive and grow.<br /> <br /> It really comes down to a simple question. Would it be more fun to have plots about summoning a sheol 10 Leviathan that will go on a Godzilla rampage and damage New York or plots about summoning a Sheol 20 Leviathan that will attack Mother Luna (or something) and damage the very fabric of reality?<br /> <br /> But I definitely have no plans for playable ascended Leviathans. What would players even do? (That isn't done better by Imperial Mysteries)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-14-2015, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T01:38:18-07:00","id":665465,"title":"","content":"Speaking as someone who has been following Leviathan only sporadically and who doesn't have any personal investment...<br /> <br /> I have to side with Vree and CalvaryKeter and the others expressing dissent with TKR's stance on Marduk.<br /> <br /> I'm happy to play as a &quot;cosmic abortion&quot; of a PC.<br /> <br /> But I don't see why that means there has to be some Mary Sue Technocracy rip-off running around in the setting.<br /> <br /> Yes, humanity won, the Leviathan's lost, the Chaoskampf and all that.<br /> <br /> But Marduk as it is? Bores the hell out of me. It feels far too much like some OWoD fanboyism mixed with the &quot;Humanity, F**K YEAH&quot; attitude of Hunter fanboys.<br /> <br /> I would happily play in a game with Vree's take on Marduk, but I wouldn't want anything to do with a game that uses TKR's version. It is that freaking overblown and overhyped and generally offputting.<br /> <br /> Lightning-manipulating science heroes makes a great Hunter Conspiracy. But they should NOT be &quot;The Good Guys&quot;. NOBODY in the World of Darkness is &quot;The Good Guys&quot;. That's the whole damn POINT of the setting.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest here: I love the idea of &quot;okay, so I'm a monster: what do I make of myself?&quot; as a game concept. I love the idea of trying to define myself when I don't have a &quot;place&quot; other than that which I make for myself. It's one of the reasons I loved draft!Beast so much.<br /> <br /> And contrasting Leviathan stagnation to humanity progression is great and all... but, still, it's far too limiting, the way it's being portrayed.<br /> <br /> As was commented a page or two back, humanity is STILL, at heart, little more than an animal. We wear our clothes and use our tools and perform our rituals and tell ourselves that this makes us better than the beast. We shun the dark and foul impulses from our primeval self. But the Leviathans? They are US, stripped of all our trinkets and talismans. They are the beast within brought to hideous life, the living reminder of the bloody seas from which we dragged ourselves. They are our darkest impulses and most primeval natures garbed in hideous, ever-shifting flesh. We might try to deny them, we do so with great success... but we cannot eradicate them. And, perhaps, we never will.<br /> <br /> Leviathans are scary because they represent the darkness humanity was born in, and that it still hasn't finished clawing its way out of. Worse, they represent the possibility that we may - or even that we <i>will</i> - lose our grip and be swallowed by it once again.<br /> <br /> Their time has passed... and yet, their time may come again. That is not dead which can eternal lie. And with strange aeons, even death may die. What was once mundane is now unthinkable, and may yet, in time, become mundane again. The light may burn so brightly, but darkness is eternal; in the end, darkness will always swallow the light.<br /> <br /> THAT, to me, is far more interesting a thematic backdrop than &quot;you're just pale shadows, hiding from the Mighty Men of Marduk before they inevitably scour you from existence&quot;. It gives Leviathans an &quot;anchor&quot;, and a source of hope. Promethean has attracted so much backlash for its bleakness, and yet, to me, Leviathan seems to make Promethean look downright super-happy-funtime. Prometheans at least have the hope of reaching the New Dawn. Leviathans have nothing to look forward to but death.<br /> <br /> Humanity and Marduk have the strength of reason and their advanced technology. Good. But let Leviathans have their own strength, the old strength; muscle and blood and bone. Technology is always progressing, and so to is nature evolving. The stars are wrong, the blood thins, Leviathans have faded from relevance in the modern era. But that is the core of nature: Adapt or Die.<br /> <br /> In my games, I want the options for Leviathans to Adapt. I want the option to tell of Leviathans winning shoals in which to wait for their time to come again. I want the option to let the stars tumble into the seas and the drowned cities to rise and for mankind to shudder as the veil of civilisation is torn away to reveal the screaming, bloody animal that has always been behind it all.<br /> <br /> So why am I not getting those options!? That's Lovecraftian as hell, right there - the very essence of Cosmic Horror is how utterly <b>insignificant</b> humanity ultimately is, for all its culture and science and technology and civilization.<br /> <br /> So why is the impression I am constantly getting from this project that I'm supposed to be signing up to play the &quot;Super Cool and Ultra Righteous Marduk Organization, who hunts down the Things From Out of Time with the power of Science!&quot;, instead of the game's <i>titular</i> antediluvian horrors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T09:50:25-07:00","id":665822,"title":"","content":"Seriously. It's a waste of time saying I should remove the idea of Marduk representing human progress; it's not going to change.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665465#post665465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NOBODY in the World of Darkness is &quot;The Good Guys&quot;. That's the whole damn POINT of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're talking to one of the Princess developers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> that argument won't work on me.<br /> <br /> As far as I'm concerned there is not such thing as &quot;the point&quot; of the World of Darkness. Each gameline has it's own point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665465#post665465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest here: I love the idea of &quot;okay, so I'm a monster: what do I make of myself?&quot; as a game concept. I love the idea of trying to define myself when I don't have a &quot;place&quot; other than that which I make for myself. It's one of the reasons I loved draft!Beast so much.<br /> <br /> Leviathans are scary because they represent the darkness humanity was born in, and that it still hasn't finished clawing its way out of. Worse, they represent the possibility that we may - or even that we will - lose our grip and be swallowed by it once again.<br /> <br /> &lt;And more stuff along these lines&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now unlike arguing against Marduk's thematics, this is actually a productive line of discussion. It starts from the core idea of Leviathan as the remnants of a bygone age - but it explores it in different ways to the ones I've been thinking of of. That's invaluable feedback to have.<br /> <br /> Now while I disagree with some core things you're saying, for example: &quot;The light may burn so brightly, but darkness is eternal; in the end, darkness will always swallow the light.&quot; and &quot;humanity is STILL, at heart, little more than an animal.&quot; But lets carefully avoid the second one, because bringing real world politics into this thread would be an awful idea. Instead I want to focus on the positives.<br /> <br /> <br /> Firstly. I like the idea of Leviathans representing humanity's primordial darkness. Secondly I think it's compatible with the current themes. Yes, even your bit about &quot;I want the option to let the stars tumble into the seas and the drowned cities to rise and for mankind to shudder as the veil of civilisation is torn away to reveal the screaming, bloody animal that has always been behind it all.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because while I genuinely do believe that compared to the Bronze age - reason and compassion have won. Humanity is genuinely a long way away from those blood soaked lizards in the deepest recesses of our brain. But that dozen't mean it can't go backwards. A nuclear war, a zombie apocalypse (by which I mean the standard zombie idea that other survivors are the real danger), and we're back to square one.<br /> <br /> Remember I said that Marduk had won. I did not say that Marduk will eradicate the tribe. They can't, new Leviathans will always be born. Nor did I say that the Tribe cannot start a rematch. I just said that Marduk had an enormous advantage, &quot;no even keel&quot;. A Leviathan is more powerful than an Unchained, and Marduk is far less powerful than the God Machine. And unlike the G-M, I'm actually giving details that tell players where to attack if you want to hurt Marduk. The G-M is everywhere and nowhere, Marduk is in orbiting satilights. One of those two is a physical object you can attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> So basically. Leviathan is about being a monster with no place in the modern world trying to get by. Humanity's oldest and worst instincts are a kind of monster. Fits nicely.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now onto where we disagree. That word &quot;adaptation&quot;.<br /> <br /> Firstly nature adapts, but the Tribe are not &quot;nature&quot;. Even in your metaphor they represent part of the human mind, not nature, and IMO if human's adapt for the modern world we'd do so by loosing those outdated instincts.<br /> <br /> I actually think Stagnation works better with your ideas than adaptation. The evil instincts in the lizard brain causing trouble today are the exact same evil instincts we had back in the bronze age. In short, they've stagnated. IMO, that works just fine for your metaphor. Leviathans are stuck in a bronze age mindset ruling over small fishing villages - hence stagnation. But if an opportunity arises (lets say a zombie apocalypse) they will still be there, ready to rise up and tear the world apart with their conflicts.<br /> <br /> In short - I have no intention of getting rid of stagnation as a core theme. The idea of Leviathan's representing humanity's primordial instincts will have to work with Stagnation or not at all; fortunately I think they'd work just fine with stagnation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though this still leaves the question of what practical effects Leviathans=Mankind's worst instincts will have on the write up. An essay explaining the themes would just be ugly and I'm not sure how to represent it through a Leviathan's powers. The Strains can carry a far amount of the weight; since they're all written as different reasons people worship gods there's already some support for the idea in the strains.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which brings us too:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665465#post665465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why am I not getting those options!?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are. Did you somehow miss the post imediately before you when I talked about the possibility of summoning a Sheol 20 Leviathan who'd get into a fight with the Moon and damage the very fabric of reality by doing so; that sounds rather similar to the stars falling from the sky to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665465#post665465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the very essence of Cosmic Horror is how utterly insignificant humanity ultimately is, for all its culture and science and technology and civilisation.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Leviathan the cosmic horror is how utterly insignificant Leviathans are, for all their innate divine power.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:24:05-07:00","id":665924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665822#post665822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though this still leaves the question of what practical effects Leviathans=Mankind's worst instincts will have on the write up. An essay explaining the themes would just be ugly and I'm not sure how to represent it through a Leviathan's powers. The Strains can carry a far amount of the weight; since they're all written as different reasons people worship gods there's already some support for the idea in the strains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's a couple of methods I can think of for conveying this.<br /> <br /> Firstly; a noted part of the Wake could be the stripping of &quot;humanity&quot; from humans exposed to it. Unless a Leviathan explicitly forbids it, those who succumb to her mental presence will mentally devolve back to a more primal state. This then gives Leviathans a choice; do they try and preserve their minions by taking the responsibilities of godhood to reinforce Thou Shalt Not Steal, Murder, Covet Another's Wife, etc? Or do they simply let it happen, because it's easier, it makes the worship stronger and purer, and it makes the cult more useful - a cult that no longer suffers Integrity loss for murder or torture or theft will more viciously and effectively defend their god. Especially if, as I hinted at earlier, a &quot;devolved&quot; Cult grants increased benefits for worship.<br /> <br /> Secondly, part of the Leviathan's powers might include options for mental and even physical devolution in humans. A Leviathan, by its very nature, can tear through the veil of humanity and flick on that primordial lizard-brain, bringing out all the darkness humanity tries to deny resides in it. When a Leviathan focuses its psyche, madness, barbarity, degeneracy and decadence soon bloom. And once a mind has been torn down, perhaps a Leviathan can proceed to do the same to the body, allowing them to transform and warp humans in their own image once that &quot;veil of lies&quot; is stripped from them.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, I would add anti-tech powers to the Leviathan's arsenal. Technology is the physical manifestation of how humanity has managed to suppress its instincts, an embodiment of logic. As the living avatar of the primeval darkness of instinct, a Leviathan can subvert the very ideology that technology is symbolically presenting, making a lie of its existence. This also has the advantage of making Leviathans feel less &quot;one wrong step from total extermination&quot; against Marduk. Yes, Marduk tech is superior to anything humans have, and so it's more resistant to these powers, but the same ideological clash is still there. Leviathans can't build it better... but they CAN tear it down.<br /> <br /> In fact, a deleterious effect on higher technology might be an inherent aspect of higher Sheol. The most powerful Leviathans are Walking Techbanes, capable of destroying technology with their very presence. They can possibly suppress it, but it adds to that primeval god feel when electronics die (bad news for you if you have a pacemaker) and gunpowder just stops functioning.<br /> <br /> Fourthly, making virtues of &quot;politically incorrect, yet primevally justifiable&quot; actions helps enforce that &quot;A Leviathan is the bloody beast of the past made manifest&quot; feel. A Leviathan sees someone disabled and is immediately goaded to prey upon them; society calls that ableist, incompassionate, but to a Leviathan, the Weak Are Prey, The Sick Must Be Culled From The Tribe. It feels <i>good</i>, it feels [/b]right[/b] to slay them. This is the trickiest idea to convey without getting it wrong, so I'm hesitant to suggest it myself.<br /> <br /> Finally, Leviathans at higher Sheol could be &quot;walking rifts&quot; in the Gauntlet; their presence makes it easier for spirits to slip through, and those spirits that flock to them and join their Cults are always of the most primal natures - you cannot see Knowledge or Electronic Spirits in a Leviathan's wake, but Blood, Death, Birth, Murder, Joy, Hate, these all flock to them. Again, this references and reinforces the idea of &quot;Leviathans are gods&quot; (they summon and maybe can even control spirits, the most primeval form of worship-figures, as their &quot;angels&quot;), the idea of &quot;Leviathans are inherently primordial, evil&quot; (they drive away &quot;higher&quot; spirits and allow only the most basic and elemental of spirits to thrive in their presence), and the idea of &quot;Leviathans are living manifestations humanity's darkness&quot; (the spirits that flock to them are things of murder, sex, blood, violence, hatred, death).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:57:15-07:00","id":665949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665924#post665924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstly; a noted part of the Wake could be the stripping of &quot;humanity&quot; from humans exposed to it. Unless a Leviathan explicitly forbids it, those who succumb to her mental presence will mentally devolve back to a more primal state.</div> </div> </div> </div> Have a look at the<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JPb2CioodnfracCT4Zb6H-P2ieuYQ7WyBPQeVePBX9k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> Strain write ups</a>. Each Strain already has detailed effects of what that Strain's wake does.<br /> <br /> You're more or less describing a Tanninim's wake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665924#post665924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, part of the Leviathan's powers might include options for mental and even physical devolution in humans. A Leviathan, by its very nature, can tear through the veil of humanity and flick on that primordial lizard-brain, bringing out all the darkness humanity tries to deny resides in it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, we'll need new Scantity powers at some point. All the attriubte boosters are going to be replaced with the new Atavism mechanic.<br /> <br /> That said. This power might fit in better as part of Call of the Depths. While Leviathans need to have a siren power; an entire channel that's nothing but siren song is a bit much. Letting it be mass scale mind control (in contrast to Besieging the Tower of Will for targeted one person mind control and telepathy) that can do any number of simple effects including everyone go mad and start slaughtering would be more appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665924#post665924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thirdly, I would add anti-tech powers to the Leviathan's arsenal.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm thinking Adaptations not Channels. However anti-tech would have to be limited in scope and functionality.<br /> <br /> While Leviathans are weak against &quot;lightning&quot; not &quot;science&quot; there's a thematic link which prevents too much anti-tech powers. Still Fecundity to clog tech with spores or vitality to clog them with dead flesh could work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665924#post665924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Fourthly, making virtues of &quot;politically incorrect, yet primevally justifiable&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds more like petty bullying than primordial instinct. Besides we already have Virtue/Vice for Leviathans planned out. It's &quot;What kind of God are you&quot; and &quot;What king of monster are you&quot;. I can think of a few gods that would cull the week, but the key is that they have reasons for doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665924#post665924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, Leviathans at higher Sheol could be &quot;walking rifts&quot; in the Gauntlet</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather not create strong ties between Leviathans and Spirits. They're two different cosmologies on a thematic level.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:58:00-07:00","id":665950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665822#post665822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're talking to one of the Princess developers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> that argument won't work on me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as another Princess developer - Princess is like a World of Darkness game because, while the Hopeful are unambiguously Good Guys, they have little power compared to the other supernatural factions and tend to get locked into conflict with most of them. As I said before, the Marduk Society as you conceive it is both good and powerful, and it has no real reason to oppose any splat but Leviathans; thus it just isn't compatible with the World of Darkness in general.<br /> <br /> Besides, look back through the thread. There's several people telling you that your Marduk makes for a poor antagonist. Is there <i>anyone</i> who thinks your Marduk is a good idea, other than you?<br /> <br /> I even question whether Leviathan needs a representative of human progress for thematic purposes. It seems to me that the implicit history of the Leviathans represents that theme adequately already. Back in the Bronze Age it took supernatural backing and self-sacrificing heroism for mortals to challenge a Leviathan and his cult; today, a unit of the National Guard can break a Leviathan's cult in a week and drive him to the ocean's depths to lick his wounds. There is human progress in a nutshell: you don't need a Tier 3 conspiracy with a fancy Endowment to ruin a Leviathan's day anymore. <hr />As it happens I think there <i>is</i> a more interesting take on Marduk that keeps a lot of their original flavor, without turning them into plaster saints. Make them into Randian heroes.<br /> <br /> Vree's mention of Captain Nemo is my starting point here. Nemo, you see, is a genius engineer (his submarine is his own design), an aristocrat and a scholar, and a generous man (he gives salvaged treasure to the poor and oppressed), but he's an enemy to the social order of his time (the European empires) and has removed himself from it, living in exile by sheer intellect, and controls his technology and subordinates with an iron hand. He is, thus, a precursor to John Galt - though Verne was more dubious about his character than Rand was about hers.<br /> <br /> Now let's suppose that the Marduk Society shares the general capabilities and outlook of Nemo or Galt. They retain the technology beyond the edge of what public science can do (superscience is central to the trope these characters embody) but they also withhold that technology from the world at large, because they want to control what is done with it. They firmly believe that their purposes are pure and righteous, so they can use these tools without fear, but the rest of humanity has not caught up to them, and therefore doesn't deserve to have them. And while they protect humanity from supernatural threats (especially Leviathans) they refuse to submit themselves to humanity's judgement, so they conceal themselves from the public. In short, they are Man in his pride: triumphant exemplars of Reason applied to master Nature ... and swollen in an unreflective hubris.<br /> <br /> You can even keep the part about eating Leviathan flesh with this mindset - not as an ancient practice, but as an example of their hubris. The Marduk Society are so much masters of themselves that they can steal immortality from their ancient enemies in the Tribe without being corrupted ... or so they think. Mermaid meat isn't the secret of a cabal of hidden masters, it's a perennial temptation that any Society member might succumb to.<br /> <br /> Now, that would make for a more interesting antagonist - and a thematic contrast with the Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:00:57-07:00","id":665952,"title":"","content":"You're late MB. I already said I've finished with the Marduk debate.<br /> <br /> (Though thanks for agreeing with me that you can have unambiguous good guys in a WoD game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-15-2015, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:32:34-07:00","id":665969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=664996#post664996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Here you go</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I'll have a few of my ritual ideas adapted soon, at least to see if the theme is in line with what others here are envisaging.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thirdly, I would add anti-tech powers to the Leviathan's arsenal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Modern technology and science as it stands essentially *is* a Leviathans bane as much as electricity is. It seems strange to give them anti-tech powers. I'd rather support the theme to the point where Leviathan channels and rituals always receive a penalty when opposed by high technology. Amongst other things it supports the motive for Leviathans to remain in backwater / rundown areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","name":"Opprobrium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:33:09-07:00","id":665970,"title":"","content":"Sigh... TKR? It does. <i>Not</i>. <b>Matter</b>. If you say &quot;I'm done with the Marduk debate&quot;. <b>No one</b> is going to shut up about it until and unless you manage to address their concerns convincingly, which so far you have <i>failed</i> to do.<br /> <br /> Listen to what Michael Brazier is saying! If absolutely <i>nobody</i> is willing to step in and speak up in defence of your depiction of Marduk, and in fact most everyone is ripping it a new one, then... <i>you may just have a problem with it</i>. It may just be that the complainers have a point, and that it is a <b>bad idea</b>.<br /> <br /> This is exactly why I made my complaint earlier about &quot;Technocracy/Humanity F**k Yeah Fanboyism&quot;. It really comes off more like the designer - which, at this stage, is TKR - is saying &quot;you should be playing Marduk and slaughtering Leviathans&quot; instead of &quot;you should be playing Leviathans&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:44:35-07:00","id":665992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665969#post665969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. I'll have a few of my ritual ideas adapted soon, at least to see if the theme is in line with what others here are envisaging.</div> </div> </div> </div> Looking forward to them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665970#post665970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>No one</b> is going to shut up about it until and unless you manage to address their concerns convincingly, which so far you have <i>failed</i> to do.</div> </div> </div> </div> That would just waste everyone's time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:48:02-07:00","id":665996,"title":"","content":"I'm new here but I just want to throw in that I do support the notion of idealistic 'unambiguous' good guys.<br /> <br /> I think something to keep in mind is that the concept of Perfection can be disturbing in its own right. Think about how you would react if you met one of these ultra-moral, holier-that-though superheros who have fought monsters, had incredible adventures and are a part of a secret soceity with access to futuristic technology. What would your opinion be of these people who are essentially Mary-Sues incarnate in a grimdark world? Would you like them? I wouldn't - I'd hate their guts in envy. I certainly wouldn't be interested in playing such a character.<br /> If the Leviathans primary enemy is of dubious morality (egotistic goals, hunting beasts to eat their flesh and gain immortality) then it sows seeds of doubt upon the concept that Leviathans are undebatedly the bad guys. There shouldn't be this doubt. 'Earths Most Wicked Tribe' is an absolute, and absolutes come in twos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","name":"Opprobrium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:53:06-07:00","id":666000,"title":"","content":"I'm into all of that, MB; the Randian angle to Reason vs. Brute Nature hadn't occurred to me, but it definitely seems properly explanatory for an imperfect-but-powerful Marduk; likewise, it retains the whole Leviathan flesh angle, which is definitely one of my favorite parts of the Marduk Society. Plus, it allows for more characters than the current crop of dudes whom I would universally have to describe as &quot;jut-jawed&quot; -- everything from a faction of capitalist magi who want to build &quot;Leviathan farms&quot; from Typhons and mass-produce eternal life (reliant, of course, on the continued existence of the Tribe in constant torment -- think Omelas) to traumatized former Beloved who want to prove their strength by freeing cultists and building tasers into their own teeth. Ditto on the human progress aspect.<br /> <br /> @TKR:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, look back through the thread. There's several people telling you that your Marduk makes for a poor antagonist. Is there <i>anyone</i> who thinks your Marduk is a good idea, other than you? </div> </div> </div>I know you really like this write-up -- but you shouldn't just shut off all criticism. (&quot;I'm okay with constructive criticism, which means not criticizing any of the parts I like because they're not changing at all&quot; is not remaining open to criticism.) Sometimes you have to kill your darlings; people criticizing the stuff you like is not &quot;pointless&quot; or &quot;nonconstructive.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you've decided not to engage with criticism over Marduk at all, then I can't actually stop you from doing that; nevertheless, this isn't <i>just your </i>project. Keep in mind that this game will be designed and played, to some extent, by people with different tastes than you, whose tastes may resemble ours more than yours, and then think about whether you feel the debate is &quot;pointless&quot; to game design.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665996#post665996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm new here but I just want to throw in that I do support the notion of idealistic 'unambiguous' good guys.<br /> <br /> I think something to keep in mind is that the concept of Perfection can be disturbing in its own right. Think about how you would react if you met one of these ultra-moral, holier-that-though superheros who have fought monsters, had incredible adventures and are a part of a secret soceity with access to futuristic technology. What would your opinion be of these people who are essentially Mary-Sues incarnate in a grimdark world? Would you like them? I wouldn't - I'd hate their guts in envy. I certainly wouldn't be interested in playing such a character.<br /> If the Leviathans primary enemy is of dubious morality (egotistic goals, hunting beasts to eat their flesh and gain immortality) then it sows seeds of doubt upon the concept that Leviathans are undebatedly the bad guys. There shouldn't be this doubt. 'Earths Most Wicked Tribe' is an absolute, and absolutes come in twos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leviathans as a class are undebatably the losing side, and descendants of Eld Beasts whose reign on Earth was a time of unparalleled horror. Individual Leviathans are of variable morality. They're &quot;Earth's Most Wicked&quot; because they've got predispositions in that direction and obstacles to behaving well, but there's no reason they can't make an effort to be good people. Likewise, Marduk is the winning side and, as a whole, superior; individual members of Marduk are likewise of variable morality, but they fight the Wicked Tribe, so they're the Good Guys. Individually, and as a class, they may be less than perfect, but they're not Paragons any more than Leviathans are, as a class, of zero ethical value and always worth executing without a twinge of guilt.<br /> <br /> I'm willing to admit that one side is better than the other; I'm not willing to accept Perfectly Ethical Guys and Vile Universally Amoral Guys, because that's flat and contradicts what I know about the real world (i.e. not everyone who buys into a bad idea is a Perfect Monster, not everyone who guys into good ideas is a Glorious Idealist). If I met a perfect superhero in real life, I might hate them or envy them; in writing, it just seems shoddy. (Also, remember we're supposed to be playing as Leviathans, with not-quite-human mindsets but who still have a sense of right and wrong. How do you reconcile being Earth's Most Wicked Tribe with playing a Leviathan, who is not constantly committing atrocities, who does, in fact, have an Integrity-equivalent that gets dinged by certain transgressions?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","user":"CalvaryKeter","date":". 09-15-2015, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:55:00-07:00","id":666002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665996#post665996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm new here but I just want to throw in that I do support the notion of idealistic 'unambiguous' good guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=665996#post665996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you like them? I wouldn't - I'd hate their guts in envy.<br /> <br /> If the Leviathans primary enemy is of dubious morality (egotistic goals, hunting beasts to eat their flesh and gain immortality) then it sows seeds of doubt upon the concept that Leviathans are undebatedly the bad guys. There shouldn't be this doubt. 'Earths Most Wicked Tribe' is an absolute, and absolutes come in twos.</div> </div> </div> </div>You get it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-15-2015, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:11:11-07:00","id":666022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666002#post666002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't people (rightfully, I think) criticize Beast for doing this exact same thing?<br /> <br /> (&quot;If we make Heroes anything less than disgusting sad prideful douchebag monsters with zero moral worth, it'll dilute the fact that Beasts are the good guys.&quot; Find/replace: Heroes -&gt; Marduk, disgusting sad etc. -&gt; gorgeous flawless idealistic heroes with no ethical lapses, Beasts -&gt; Leviathans, good guys -&gt; bad guys.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","user":"CalvaryKeter","date":". 09-15-2015, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:13:37-07:00","id":666025,"title":"","content":"By the way, if the linked Leviathan in your sig and homebrew index only contains the 1e content, you might want to update either your homebrew index or your signature to link to the new Leviathan docs. Other than that Strains doc you linked on page 14, I have no idea where to find any of the 2e stuff.<br /> <br /> In fact, setting up a &quot;compendium doc&quot;, a doc that exists only to link all of the sub-docs, and linking back to that compendium doc in each individual doc, is something I cannot recommend enough. It makes it drastically easier to follow the links between docs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","user":"VoidDrifter","date":". 09-15-2015, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:24:53-07:00","id":666033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666000#post666000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How do you reconcile being Earth's Most Wicked Tribe with playing a Leviathan, who is not constantly committing atrocities, who does, in fact, have an Integrity-equivalent that gets dinged by certain transgressions?)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no need to 'constantly commit atrocities' ... you only realy need a few good atrocities to stain your soul forever. I think it's more a case of constantly committing minor offences, the effects of the wake ensure that Leviathans passively engage in intimidation and bullying ... it's not even as though they're pushed to do so and can overcome their impulses, it's essentially a reflex for them. Constant minor acts of crime, selfishness and ill-will combined with the utter inability to actually help humanity in any way make the Leviathans fully evil. They don't nessecarily need to be murdering entire families, violating their corpses and eating them for breakfast every Sunday.<br /> In any case, depending on just how much Lovecraftian influence you want I think a Leviathans lifespan should more-or-less be a slow but steady decline into Insanity/ Monstrosity (Ophionism?) or death. Hope is after all a gift that is only avaliable to Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","name":"Opprobrium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:34:16-07:00","id":666037,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666025#post666025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, if the linked Leviathan in your sig and homebrew index only contains the 1e content, you might want to update either your homebrew index or your signature to link to the new Leviathan docs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point.<br /> <br /> Here's the master link: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0B9DMG5y7ZdngflpNQzVQRDVrSTdDdnFOckNSemFzUjEyNjdWcXU5c0FDVGQwakRDX1BIMjQ&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/folderview?...jQ&amp;usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> I'll edit it into the first post too and my sig.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666000#post666000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I'm okay with constructive criticism, which means not criticizing any of the parts I like because they're not changing at all</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not about the parts I like vs the parts I don't like. It's that the criticism is opposed to the core ideas of the Marduk Society, or Leviathan as a whole.<br /> <br /> The Marduk Society will be a metaphor for how reason, civilisation, science, etc helps mankind overcome their base urges and becomes better people. That will not change and trying to argue against it will just waste everyone's time.<br /> <br /> Criticism that tries to make the Marduk Society a better and more fun metaphor for reason, civilisation, science, etc helping mankind... will still be eagerly considered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666000#post666000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but there's no reason they can't be good people.</div> </div> </div> </div> There absolutely is! Leviathans have an uncontrollable sanity destroying psychic aura. Leviathans cannot ethically be in the physical presence of normal humans for an extended period of time, not in 1E nor in 2E.<br /> <br /> What's more a Leviathan who avoids all human contact will slowly loose their mind to lonelyness and becomes an evil monster - regular humans can go mad from lonlynes and Leviathans have two other minds fighting their human one for dominance.<br /> <br /> <br /> The whole point is that there's no way a Leviathan can survive that's remotely ethical. Their very existance harms others, and then exploring how you build a life and a self identity in that situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666022#post666022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't you criticize Beast for doing this exact same thing?<br /> <br /> (&quot;If we make Heroes anything less than disgusting sad prideful douchebag monsters with zero moral worth, it'll dilute the fact that Beasts are the good guys.&quot; Find/replace: Heroes -&gt; Marduk, disgusting sad etc. -&gt; gorgeous flawless idealistic heroes with no ethical lapses, Beasts -&gt; Leviathans, good guys -&gt; bad guys.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure I didn't.<br /> <br /> I criticised Beast for the whole concept of &quot;teaching through fear&quot; which I think is both impractical and morally wrong. But my response to that was to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571205-compact-llannerch-athrawon-the-wizard-behind-the-hero\">write a rebuttal</a>. If Matt wants to write a game about teaching through fear I'd either suggest ways to make it a better game about teaching through fear, or politely disagree and go elsewhere. Which I did, I politely went off to Hunter and wrote a Beast Hunting Compacts that presented my views. <hr /><br /> Secondly, I don't actually have a problem with the bit you quoted. Giving your PCs vile antagonists to make them look good is a standard tool in any writer's arsenal.<br /> <br /> The problem with <u><b>pre-revision</b></u> Heroes wasn't that Matt was douchebags to make Beasts look bad. It's that book was a huge thematic muddle with Heroes being portrayed as the ultimate douches for doing the exact same things as Beasts (who're portrayed as cool and awesome) - and then it mixed in real world groups and... long story short: the entire thing was just a huge thematic muddle.<br /> <br /> The idea of creating antagonists to make your protagonist look good or evil by contrast is perfectly fine; however you can screw up the implementation. If I have any criticisms of Heroes - it's that Matt screwed up the implementation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-15-2015, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:46:55-07:00","id":666046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666037#post666037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point.<br /> <br /> Here's the master link: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0B9DMG5y7ZdngflpNQzVQRDVrSTdDdnFOckNSemFzUjEyNjdWcXU5c0FDVGQwakRDX1BIMjQ&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/folderview?...jQ&amp;usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. I looks like I just leaked the 3/4 written Marduk draft. Oh well, leaked is leaked. Feel free to have a read.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:57:08-07:00","id":666053,"title":"","content":"Here's an interesting question I just realized: because Marduk is on top of the world and enjoying a victory high, its primary antagonist has long been a minor threat... wouldn't that make them... NOT a Hunter conspiracy since they lack the same desperation that characterizes the other groups in the Vigil?<br /> <br /> Perhaps it might be best if we they weren't defined as Hunters, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:03:50-07:00","id":666057,"title":"","content":"That depends on how core you think desperation is to Vigil. Personally I think that the entire reason that Tier 3 is different from Tier 1 is that they're not nearly as desperate. I actually like my Hunter Conspiracies to be, generally, the biggest dogs in the setting.<br /> <br /> Of course, arrogance gets a lot of big dogs killed. And if a Marduk agent is cornered by a Leviathan while on foot then I'm sure they'll feel very very desperate.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said. I wasn't planning to have the big &quot;they're hunters&quot; sidebar. In retrospect it's unnecessary and if a storyteller doesn't think they should count as hunters for whatever reason I'm fine with leaving that call to them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:16:32-07:00","id":666063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666033#post666033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no need to 'constantly commit atrocities' ... you only realy need a few good atrocities to stain your soul forever. I think it's more a case of constantly committing minor offences, the effects of the wake ensure that Leviathans passively engage in intimidation and bullying ... it's not even as though they're pushed to do so and can overcome their impulses, it's essentially a reflex for them. Constant minor acts of crime, selfishness and ill-will combined with the utter inability to actually help humanity in any way make the Leviathans fully evil. They don't nessecarily need to be murdering entire families, violating their corpses and eating them for breakfast every Sunday.<br /> In any case, depending on just how much Lovecraftian influence you want I think a Leviathans lifespan should more-or-less be a slow but steady decline into Insanity/ Monstrosity (Ophionism?) or death. Hope is after all a gift that is only avaliable to Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case, why do we need Marduk to be absolutely moral?<br /> <br /> If any given Leviathan is self-evidently a bad person, then do we actually need Perfect Paragon Marduk? After all, they're just eating Leviathan flesh and concealing their tech from humanity because the general populace isn't ready to confront the supernatural; it doesn't seem like people will forget that we're dealing with the Earth's Most Wicked Tribe just because Marduk occasionally acts badly. (Also, &quot;absolutes come in twos&quot; isn't true. The Strix are amoral horrors and nemeses to vampires, but vampires aren't good people.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Marduk Society will be a metaphor for how reason, civilisation, science, etc helps mankind overcome their base urges and becomes better people. That will not change and trying to argue against it will just waste everyone's time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You really aren't getting this. Rephrasing it doesn't change that you have a favorite thematic use for Marduk, and that you don't want to hear criticism about that use or your specific implementation of said; criticism of your implementation is pointless only if you've decided that all criticism of your interpretation is illegitimate.<br /> <br /> (Also, if you're gonna play it like this: Marduk can be altered without ruining Leviathan's core themes, because Leviathan's core theme is Stagnation, not By Reason Do We Become Perfect. Marduk isn't the core theme; Marduk as plaster saint scientists with no ethical lapses as a direct counterpoint to Leviathans' unchanging culture is your favorite interpretation of the core theme, and removing it will not make Leviathans dynamic or give them a chance of reviving their culture, because, y'know, there's still the thing where what used to take an army of trained soldiers and the loss of many lives now takes the National Guard.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: I could also say that because so many people have this hang-up, it's you who's &quot;wasting time&quot; by refusing categorically to change anything or compromise anywhere; anyone can say &quot;the conflict would be resolved if you just agreed with me,&quot; but as a conflict resolution method, it sort of works on the &quot;I don't want to compromise or do anything I don't want to do, and it's your fault for wanting different things from me&quot; level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","user":"CalvaryKeter","date":". 09-15-2015, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:26:12-07:00","id":666069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666063#post666063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any given Leviathan is self-evidently a bad person, then do we actually need Perfect Paragon Marduk?</div> </div> </div> </div> As metaphors for how reason, etc, make humanity better people. Marduk needs to be those better people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666063#post666063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">criticism of your implementation is pointless only if you've decided that all criticism of your interpretation is illegitimate.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree, and clearly we'll have to leave it as an irresolable difference.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:37:10-07:00","id":666074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666063#post666063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this case, why do we need Marduk to be absolutely moral?<br /> <br /> If any given Leviathan is self-evidently a bad person, then do we actually need Perfect Paragon Marduk? After all, they're just eating Leviathan flesh and concealing their tech from humanity because the general populace isn't ready to confront the supernatural; it doesn't seem like people will forget that we're dealing with the Earth's Most Wicked Tribe just because Marduk occasionally acts badly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has it got to the point when the primary dispute here is based on Marduk eating Leviathan flesh? Surely that can be adressed by having the flesh inflict severe side-effects on the eaters mind and soul - it seems self-evident in any case that devouring the meat of a lovecraftian God-Monster will not be a healthy thing to do - it contains traces of Ichor after all. Regular consumers will see their mentality warped, develop minor physical afflictions and gain an affinity for Leviathanesque rituals. In short they're on the path to being theurgists.<br /> I'm not sure there's anything wrong with the -occasional- Marduk agent going rogue and hunting Leviathan flesh, but when they begin to do so they're essentially proclaiming that they see value in the Leviathans nature over Humanity to some extent, thus are no longer the most virtuous and no longer a truly functioning element of the Marduk Soceity. The important point is that the entire organisation shouldn't be seeking the power of the eldritch beasts they hunt on a regular basis or really they're little more than a cult that have overthrown their masters.<br /> <br /> ---------------------<br /> <br /> To return to the subject of rituals, I'm seeing potential issue with the Vestige = Arcana parralel. The themes don't seem to fit quite as clearly with a few : Awareness, Elements, Fecundity and Sanctity seem well disposed to ritual use but what of the others? What kind of rituals fall under Predation? What about Vitality given that bestowing genuine benefits on Cultists should be off the table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","name":"Opprobrium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:40:24-07:00","id":666075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666069#post666069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As metaphors for how reason, etc, make humanity better people. Marduk needs to be those better people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reason, etc. haven't made humanity perfectly ethical people, and can be leveraged towards ill ends (i.e. nukes in most situations, electroshock torture, enabling refinement of sweatshops, building an unfriendly AI that kills us all to make paperclips). Whether it's the symbol of progress or not, Marduk shouldn't be perfect, because people definitely aren't; sometimes science is made to serve our ids, but it's still better than nothing. In fact, I'd argue that making Marduk imperfect serves your metaphor -- science doesn't make us perfect (hence Marduk, which consumes mermaid flesh and assumes some of its corruption and is composed of humans with human flaws), but it's definitely better than brute unreason and prehistoric wildness (Leviathans), so we prefer it.<br /> <br /> In any case, Big Perfect Marduk is something which -- multiple people feel -- breaks the setting in an unfun way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666069#post666069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree, and clearly we'll have to leave it as an irresolable difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>You disagree about what? Thatcriticism of your implementation is pointless only if you've decided that all criticism of your interpretation is illegitimate? Or something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:43:43-07:00","id":666078,"title":"","content":"I just have to say this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Marduk Society will be a metaphor for how reason, civilisation, science, etc helps mankind overcome their base urges and becomes better people. </div> </div> </div>This is indeed a powerful metaphor. The only problem is... does this metaphor <b>fit</b> the World of Darkness?<br /> <br /> There's other &quot;spots of hope/light&quot; in the setting. Hunters in canon, Princess: The Hopeful in fanon. However, <b>both</b> of those are subject to limitations that keeps them in line with the crapsack nature of the game as a whole. Hunters are inherently morally tarnished; they are, as a whole, no better than any of the supernatural races. Gray Hats rather than White. Princesses, as Michael Brazier pointed out on page 14, are inherently inefficient: they try their hardest, but they just can't build the critical levels to effect grand, sweeping change.<br /> <br /> <b>That</b> is the fundamental problem people are having with the Marduk Society. Namely, if they are what you say they are, then <b>why</b> is this still the World of Darkness? The Leviathans <b>cannot</b> be both a blip on the radar <b>and</b> singlehandledly responsible for the WoD being the utter shithole it is - by your own words, the setting is based on the assumption that the Leviathans are the only &quot;supernaturals&quot; in its canon. If that's the case, then if this is the World of Darkness... where's all the darkness coming from, if we have the Marduk Society around to light the darkness?<br /> <br /> As it is, the Marduk Society is falling <b>exactly</b> into the same pitfalls that most people presume Princess: The Hopeful does based on the concept.<br /> <br /> Hell, as it is, the Marduk Society actually does have gray in it - it's been stagnating itself under the leadership of the Old Men, it's nearly torn itself apart with its revolution - it's just not admitting that it has clay feet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:50:02-07:00","id":666085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666074#post666074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure there's anything wrong with the -occasional- Marduk agent going rogue and hunting Leviathan flesh</div> </div> </div> </div> Rogue Marduk agents can do whatever evil things the storyteller desires - and are stated to exist in the write up. Since Marduk also has the theme of improvement they were naturally worse the further back in history you go. And the recent civil war that flushed out the bad guys also means that all the rogues hiding in the organisation are now busy doing stuff rather than working in the shadows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marduk write up</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the new commanders of the Marduk Society are busy re establishing lines of communication and figuring out which dark sites were looted and destroyed by fleeing conspirators, which are active rogue enclaves and which simply don't have the latest encryption codes.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666074#post666074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To return to the subject of rituals, I'm seeing potential issue with the Vestige = Arcana parralel. The themes don't seem to fit quite as clearly with a few : Awareness, Elements, Fecundity and Sanctity seem well disposed to ritual use but what of the others? What kind of rituals fall under Predation? What about Vitality given that bestowing genuine benefits on Cultists should be off the table?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know that's an issue. There was a half written 1E ritual rewrite that should have some ideas. Let me dig them out<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> Awareness<br /> <br /> Rituals that incorporate the Vestige of Awareness can pear across time and space to answer questions. A Leviathan can predict the future, unearth the past, or just watch that Atoll from afar. The curse of Awareness is that it can only uncover facts, not answers. The Tribe can gain any knowledge they wish, but they cannot answer the questions that truly matter.<br /> <br /> Elements<br /> <br /> Rituals that incorporate the Vestige of Elements can warp the world itself. The sea and sky, the Earth end even the sun's light all bend before a master of Elements. Rituals can raise terrible storms, or quell them and even twist the fabric of space and time. The curse of Elements is that every place touched by it's power is unnatural and tinged with the nature of the Tempest. Even when the Ritual ends a storm the result is not calm but an oppressive silence that can cause madness to those within.<br /> <br /> Fecundity<br /> <br /> Rituals that incorporate the Vestige of Fecundity can bestow the Tribe's life giving elements upon others. They can gift, or curse, other's with strange biological mutations. Reproduction, both physically and as a concept, fall under the purview of Fecundity. The curse of Fecundity is that no life but the Tribe can safely hold divine Ichor. The Tribe's gifts are cancerous corrupting things.<br /> <br /> Might<br /> <br /> Rituals that incorporate the Vestige of might can control physical forces. They can bestow strength and move mountains, sending crushing forces at the Leviathan's enemies. The curse of might is that the Tribe's power is to large for this world, it cannot be restrained to delicate tasks or distinguish between friend or foe.<br /> <br /> Predation<br /> <br /> Predation is the most vicious of the Vestiges. Poisons, toxins and diseases - the fruits of life turned toxic - are the tools of a master of Predation. The curse of Predation is that it is an imprecise weapon at best, a Leviathan can pick his targets one by one but she cannot blanket the land with toxins tailored to her enemies.<br /> <br /> Sanctity<br /> <br /> Rituals that incorporate the Vestige of Sanctity cover the very concepts of religion and godhood. With Sanctity a Leviathan can force others to recognise his divinity or bind people's social identities to religious faith. The curse of Sanctity forever links the Tribe to ancient ideas, the god who demands worship and punishes heresy. The Tribe can only force others to kneel, they cannot ask.<br /> <br /> Vitality<br /> <br /> Rituals that incorporate the Vestige of Vitality can protect. A Leviathan can bestow strange armours upon their subjects, bar intruders from their domains and protect against even stranger threats. The curse of Vitality is that it forms barrier between the world and the &quot;blessed&quot;. People touched by Vitality become lethargic and unmotivated, and ever more dependent upon the Leviathan's protection.</div><br /> I hope this helps. Don't take it as an iron hard rule - especially the bit about the specific draw backs. This was just rough notes. Ultiamtely Sanctity and Elements will always be inherently better than Vitality or Might at powering rituals. I'm ok with that so long as we get at least a few good ones under all the Vestiges.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-15-2015, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:53:12-07:00","id":666089,"title":"","content":"Guys, guys, I support your direction for Marduk, but I think Kings has had enough of Marduk for one week. Perhaps we should give him some breathing room and argue about this after he completes another section over material that we as a group would more unanimously support. At this point, I think regardless of whether or not your arguments are valid, Tilting on both sides will prevent a more amicable resolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T14:55:43-07:00","id":666091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666074#post666074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it got to the point when the primary dispute here is based on Marduk eating Leviathan flesh? Surely that can be adressed by having the flesh inflict severe side-effects on the eaters mind and soul - it seems self-evident in any case that devouring the meat of a lovecraftian God-Monster will not be a healthy thing to do - it contains traces of Ichor after all. Regular consumers will see their mentality warped, develop minor physical afflictions and gain an affinity for Leviathanesque rituals. In short they're on the path to being theurgists.<br /> I'm not sure there's anything wrong with the -occasional- Marduk agent going rogue and hunting Leviathan flesh, but when they begin to do so they're essentially proclaiming that they see value in the Leviathans nature over Humanity to some extent, thus are no longer the most virtuous and no longer a truly functioning element of the Marduk Soceity. The important point is that the entire organization shouldn't be seeking the power of the eldritch beasts they hunt on a regular basis or really they're little more than a cult that have overthrown their masters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a false binary; the entire organization isn't hunting for mermaid meat, but it represents a constant temptation to individual agents, since, y'know, immortality usually is. Remember, Marduk's members don't perceive the whole affair as a metaphor or call themselves the Virtuous Tribe -- they see a means towards immortality. And isn't that what science is all about? Making use of available resources? It's just another step in human progress, innovation and evolution! Not only that, it involves destroying the monsters who rule the world and claiming dominion over what was originally theirs -- and isn't that just what Prometheus did? Why, any self-respecting agent of Marduk would be nearly <i>obligated </i>to consume Leviathans for power! And the mental instability and physical changes can, of course, be countered with science...<br /> <br /> ...is a rationalization I could see more than a few rogue agents of Marduk using, because they're <i>people </i>and make special exceptions for themselves, like pretty much all humans do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T15:10:41-07:00","id":666101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666091#post666091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...is a rationalization I could see more than a few rogue agents of Marduk using, because they're <i>people </i>and make special exceptions for themselves, like pretty much all humans do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Change 'more than a few' to 'a few' and I think we're coming to a consensus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope this helps. Don't take it as an iron hard rule - especially the bit about the specific draw backs. This was just rough notes. Ultiamtely Sanctity and Elements will always be inherently better than Vitality or Might at powering rituals. I'm ok with that so long as we get at least a few good ones under all the Vestiges.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is in line with what I had in mind although I feel it needs more abstract potential in some cases - a ritual that disables a witness from directly speaking about the Leviathan or his cult for example could perhaps be placed under Might. It is not subtle, attempts to force the target of this ritual to divulge his information results in him speaking in tongues or attempting to maim his vocal apparatus - it's a brutal (although metaphysical) imposition of the Gods will over a mortal.<br /> Fecundity rituals that grant physical mutation seem dangerous to me as it overlaps with Everflowing Fetid Growth. We need to ensure a minimum of overlap with channels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","name":"Opprobrium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T15:13:27-07:00","id":666104,"title":"","content":"I over looked this post, and there's some stuff worth replying too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666078#post666078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is indeed a powerful metaphor.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now I'm a bit confused by where you're coming form when you say this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666078#post666078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>That</b> is the fundamental problem people are having with the Marduk Society. Namely, if they are what you say they are, then <b>why</b> is this still the World of Darkness? The Leviathans <b>cannot</b> be both a blip on the radar <b>and</b> singlehandledly responsible for the WoD being the utter shithole it is - by your own words, the setting is based on the assumption that the Leviathans are the only &quot;supernaturals&quot; in its canon. If that's the case, then if this is the World of Darkness... where's all the darkness coming from, if we have the Marduk Society around to light the darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you also say this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666078#post666078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hell, as it is, the Marduk Society actually does have gray in it - it's been stagnating itself under the leadership of the Old Men, it's nearly torn itself apart with its revolution - it's just not admitting that it has clay feet.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which I would have thought answers your question.<br /> <br /> As I have said - one of Marduk's key themes is improvement. The further back in time you go the worse the Society is. If you want to blame a &quot;supernatural&quot; faction for Leviathan's itteration of the WoD being so grimdark - you could blame the Society for spending it's early history causing damage and it's mid history being a self-counterbalancing force.<br /> <br /> That said I wouldn't blame the society. I'd blame WoD mortals for being worse than real life mortals.<br /> <hr /><br /> When I said the Society is unambigiously good, I'm exclusively talking about the post civil war Soceity (was that unclear?). The society being the good guys is a very recent development. So recent that they still haven't finished repairing the physical damage from the civil war. You ask how can the WoD be such a bad place with super powerful good guys like the Marduk Society running around.<br /> <br /> The answer is that they haven't had time to fix anything. Becoming unambigiously good is so recent in their history that they're still repairing the physical damage from the civil war.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666089#post666089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, guys, I support your direction for Marduk, but I think Kings has had enough of Marduk for one week.</div> </div> </div> </div> Very wise of you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (But VoidDrifter should feel free to reply anyway. I genuinely want to know if there's some misunderstanding somewhere).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666101#post666101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is in line with what I had in mind although I feel it needs more abstract potential in some cases - a ritual that disables a witness from directly speaking about the Leviathan or his cult for example could perhaps be placed under Might. It is not subtle, attempts to force the target of this ritual to divulge his information results in him speaking in tongues or attempting to maim his vocal apparatus - it's a brutal (although metaphysical) imposition of the Gods will over a mortal.<br /> Fecundity rituals that grant physical mutation seem dangerous to me as it overlaps with Everflowing Fetid Growth. We need to ensure a minimum of overlap with channels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right now Rituals are so early on that I'd say there's no such thing as a bad idea or a wrong answer. Explore and experiment, and we can decide what works later <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T15:17:11-07:00","id":666107,"title":"","content":"I think many people, myself included are more peeveed about the &quot;Post War&quot; Marduk being perfect rather than prewar.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the best way to resolve this conflict on every side might be to emphasize the vulnerability of &quot;New Marduk&quot;. It's for all intents and purposes a new born organization that sprung up from the ashes of an old one, one that shows great promise, but at the same time possesses a great danger. While it is true that the metaphor of Marduk is that is constantly improving itself, perhaps a great fear that holds back New Marduk is that potential that things don't go as planned. What if in the future they could become worse than their predecessors ever were? Not to say that is what they should be, but rather it is a possible future that Marduk itself dreads from happening.<br /> <br /> But dropping Marduk. I'm interested in looking at Leviathans right now, specifically, the &quot;Antagonist&quot; versions and the Rift. Are there changes to them as of late?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 09-15-2015, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T15:34:01-07:00","id":666114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666107#post666107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But dropping Marduk. I'm interested in looking at Leviathans right now, specifically, the &quot;Antagonist&quot; versions and the Rift. Are there changes to them as of late?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not yet. Ophions and Typhons will have different behaviours though. Leviathan Virtue/Vice is what kind of God/Monster are you. When you become an Ophion and Typhon that becomes your entire personality.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T15:58:44-07:00","id":666117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666037#post666037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Marduk Society will be a metaphor for how reason, civilisation, science, etc helps mankind overcome their base urges and becomes better people. That will not change and trying to argue against it will just waste everyone's time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are running a risk by insisting on this concept: that 1) almost nobody will actually use your Marduk Society in play and 2) many people reading Leviathan 2e who aren't sold on it yet will hit the section on Marduk, think &quot;what ridiculous Mary Sues&quot;, and throw the game away. You're lucky that the Society isn't woven into the setting and mechanics of Leviathan; people can play the game without using them, and I expect most people will. But then any work you put into them will be wasted effort.<br /> <br /> By the way, I have known you for a few years now, and ... you have a pattern of falling in love with an idea and categorically refusing to reconsider it or change it in any way. I don't know whether that helps you on your personal projects, but it's a serious problem when you're collaborating with others. You're doing it now with Marduk. Try to remember that you may be mistaken, and listen to the critiques you're getting, or you may find that at the end nobody else is interested in your work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T16:55:02-07:00","id":666176,"title":"","content":"Is the Rift another part of the Astral, like the Primordial Dream? Or is it yet another plane in the complicated WoD cosmology?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T20:16:24-07:00","id":666357,"title":"","content":"To clarify things on my end, since TKR actually risked asking...<br /> <br /> One big problem is that, until just now, I had no idea that the Old Men of Marduk were still a thing. I remembered them, vaguely, from 1e, but I had no idea from what I saw presented of Marduk that they weren't retconned out and that Marduk hadn't been Squeaky Clean Perfection since the beginning.<br /> <br /> The other big problem is that, even with them still being present, there's the problem of &quot;if they chucked the Old Men centuries/decades ago, why haven't they fixed the world? If they only just got rid of them, why are they a significant threat at all - why aren't they too busy with cleaning house and reorganizing themselves?&quot;<br /> <br /> The biggest issue here is that it felt like the Old Men were being handwaved away - hypocritically, that Marduk is claiming to be perfection now when the truth is that they have their own dirty laundry, which means they're stained by gray from the beginning. They might be the lightest of grays NOW, but at least it should be acknowledged, instead of insisting that they're totally white and pure and incorruptible and perfect, which is a feeling I got from the talk about them there.<br /> <br /> Let's not beat around the bush here: I hate the idea of Post War Marduk being &quot;perfect&quot;. Like Almarak had said, I'd be a whole hell of a lot less bothered if emphasis had been placed on the post war Marduk's vulnerability, and even less so if, like Princesses, they had been presented as having flaws that reasonably explained WHY the World of Darkness is still the way it is - hampered by their idealism, inherently restricted, just in some way not able to peel away the shadows completely.<br /> <br /> I actually agree with the comment earlier that the whole &quot;Leviathans used to need a self-sacrificing, probably die in the attempt hero bolstered by magic to be stopped; now a simple unit of SWAT can probably scatter one non-epic tier Leviathan or even mortally wound it&quot; thing quite accurately conveys how humanity is progressed beyond the Leviathans, but I admit that the idea of lightning wielding science-heroes is too tempting an idea for a Hunter conspiracy to pass up, so I'll just pass that by.<br /> <br /> Even so, I think that the whole idea of &quot;The Light of Reason&quot; being used to justify Marduk's perfection is an inherently flawed one, simply because of the world that this game is set in. Humanity <b>still</b> is in the grip of the primordial darkness that Leviathans represent in the real world, but in the WoD, that grip is even <b>stronger</b>. The whole idea of WoD is a darker, grimmer take on our world; it makes too much sense that any group based on that symbolism would not be as strong as they'd be in a NobleBright or a GrimBright setting. Hell! TKR even <b>says</b> that you should &quot;blame mortals for making the world so crapsack&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is a world where even spirits of Love and Joy can ruin people's lives or kill them. As commented by CalvaryKeter on page 15:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reason, etc. haven't made humanity perfectly ethical people, and can be leveraged towards ill ends (i.e. nukes in most situations, electroshock torture, enabling refinement of sweatshops, building an unfriendly AI that kills us all to make paperclips). </div> </div> </div>Even beyond this, in the World of Darkness, the Light of Reason is by definition a pale and flickering thing. It cannot chase all of the darkness away, and it probably never will. That's what defines this world. I would not expect a group like Marduk to feel the way that TKR is adamant that they should feel, and the insistence only puts me off of it.<br /> <br /> ...I'm tired and not thinking straight. But that's my problem in a nutshell: Marduk is far too squeaky clean, even though they shouldn't be seen that way, and far more powerful than they have a right to be in the World of Darkness. It can be one, or the other. <b>NEVER</b> both.<br /> <br /> There's lots of interesting ways to handle Marduk. I've seen several versions of the Society drafted up in the last couple of pages that I'd happily pit my Leviathans against. But the only use I'd have for the current, canon version would be to watch it wiped out by a charge of angry Prometheans who have found peace through acceptance into a Leviathan's cult. See how much good your fancy occult science does against monster-kin who heal from lightning!<br /> <br /> Also, really iffy on the idea of the Wake being a permanently-on soul-scouring effect. There's black and gray morality, and then there's forcefeeding the &quot;you are a total monster and if you had any decency you'd kill yourself&quot;. Seriously, even Prometheans, who have &quot;Thing That Should Not Be&quot; written all over their concept sheet (hence Disquiet/Wasteland) and Beasts (who are blatant Villain protagonists) don't get that message shoved down their throat so hard. Hell, Prometheans are even getting ways to dampen their aura of unnaturalness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T21:15:31-07:00","id":666434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666357#post666357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, really iffy on the idea of the Wake being a permanently-on soul-scouring effect. There's black and gray morality, and then there's forcefeeding the &quot;you are a total monster and if you had any decency you'd kill yourself&quot;. Seriously, even Prometheans, who have &quot;Thing That Should Not Be&quot; written all over their concept sheet (hence Disquiet/Wasteland) and Beasts (who are blatant Villain protagonists) don't get that message shoved down their throat so hard. Hell, Prometheans are even getting ways to dampen their aura of unnaturalness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I just like integrating mechanics when possible. The concept of becoming Beloved (i.e. Brainwashed worshipper of a Elder Horror) and having your &quot;you&quot; replaced with the creatures will seemed to resonate with the Soul Loss mechanics (and paradoxically, gives the Leviathan's wake a potential <i>beneficial</i> use: they can prop up someone who has already lost their soul as a Beloved until said soul gets recovered... or replaced). And I was operating under the model that becoming Beloved isn't cult wide or too common (akin to Ghouls for Vampires - there, but hardly the only assets, or flooding the scene).<br /> <br /> (Personally, I have a homebrew system for holding the Wake in. Costs Willpower and can't be maintained forever, but it can get a Leviathan through some non-brainwashy interaction, if everyone keeps their distance.)<br /> <br /> And as to the &quot;you are a monster who should commit suicide&quot;: if wanting to continue existence, and <i>minimize</i> what harm you cause is good enough for Vampires, why should Leviathan's be held to a higher standard?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-16-2015, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T21:57:40-07:00","id":666463,"title":"","content":"True, but vampires <i>can</i> minimize the harm they do. I may just not be caught up on the crunch, but it looks like leviathan's <i>can't</i>. Even a nosferatu doesn't drive people insane just by sitting in a bar at night quietly listening to the karaoke stand, even if he does plan on drinking blood from some barfly or other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T22:29:09-07:00","id":666477,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, people don't go insane immediately. That take prolonged exposure (so don't be a regular). Yeah, you rain on everyone else nearby's mood, but poor hygiene can do that too.<br /> <br /> And don't Atolls neutralize the Wake? At least in their immediate proximity? Fluff seems to indicate something in that direction, what with wording that they act as sinkholes.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Stepping into &quot;The Marduk Problem&quot; again)<br /> <br /> So, the write-up currently mentions the civil war that left the &quot;good guys&quot; in charge of Marduk proper. What about the &quot;loyalist&quot; faction? Couldn't they <i>also</i> be active now? Lacking much of the resources of TMS at large, yes, but they may make up for it in ruthlessness no longer curbed by having to play nice for their idealistic collegues. Basically, mirror the SHIELD/Hydra civil war, except in this case the &quot;good guys&quot; emerged with more/better infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-16-2015, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T00:01:57-07:00","id":666536,"title":"","content":"Actually, if you check back around page 10, Atolls neutralizing the Wake was brought up - as I recall, they don't. Rather, they &quot;invert it&quot;, causing the Leviathan to become infatuated with them, but without actually stemming the Wake's influence on anyone around the Leviathan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T00:12:36-07:00","id":666540,"title":"","content":"Odd. I remember seeing that effect mentioned, but I also remember seeing that it &quot;calms&quot; the Leviathan which is at odds with the Wake being turned upon them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T00:50:31-07:00","id":666571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666176#post666176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Rift another part of the Astral, like the Primordial Dream? Or is it yet another plane in the complicated WoD cosmology?</div> </div> </div> </div> It's a completely isolated second astral world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666357#post666357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One big problem is that, until just now, I had no idea that the Old Men of Marduk were still a thing. I remembered them, vaguely, from 1e, but I had no idea from what I saw presented of Marduk that they weren't retconned out and that Marduk hadn't been Squeaky Clean Perfection since the beginning.<br /> <br /> The other big problem is that, even with them still being present, there's the problem of &quot;if they chucked the Old Men centuries/decades ago, why haven't they fixed the world? If they only just got rid of them, why are they a significant threat at all - why aren't they too busy with cleaning house and reorganizing themselves?&quot;<br /> <br /> The biggest issue here is that it felt like the Old Men were being handwaved away - hypocritically, that Marduk is claiming to be perfection now when the truth is that they have their own dirty laundry, which means they're stained by gray from the beginning. They might be the lightest of grays NOW, but at least it should be acknowledged, instead of insisting that they're totally white and pure and incorruptible and perfect, which is a feeling I got from the talk about them there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ok something clearly went wrong in the conversation somewhere. I did mention the Old Men were still around. In Post #139 - the first mention of Marduk has this in it: &quot;if it wasn't riddled with infighting and led by <b>paranoid sorcerers</b> watching their underlings for signs of brilliance or independence&quot;.<br /> <br /> But no use crying over spilt milk. To clarify fully for anyone still confused. 2E Marduk is the exact same organisation as 1E Marduk a few years later in it's history. The civil war was implied to be in 1E Marduk's near future, now it's in their near past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666357#post666357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not beat around the bush here: I hate the idea of Post War Marduk being &quot;perfect&quot;. Like Almarak had said, I'd be a whole hell of a lot less bothered if emphasis had been placed on the post war Marduk's vulnerability,</div> </div> </div> </div> That's another thing I never actually said. I said they're &quot;saints&quot; and have a big power advantage over Leviathans but even saints aren't perfect and while it's hard for Leviathans to attack aircraft or space stations it's not impossible. There's also fair amount of text in the write up mentioning that they're in a bit of a disorganised mess following the civil war.<br /> <br /> In retrospect useing the word &quot;saint&quot; may have been a bad idea and led to the idea of &quot;perfect marduk&quot;. Perhaps I should have said something along the lines of &quot;like Captain America in his first MCU film&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666357#post666357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even so, I think that the whole idea of &quot;The Light of Reason&quot; being used to justify Marduk's perfection is an inherently flawed one</div> </div> </div> </div> On this we'll simply have to disagree.<br /> <br /> While humanity is currently flawed and WoD huamnity is worse; Reason is, IMO, a good thing. And Marduk aren't a metaphor for humanity. They're a metaphor for &quot;the way reason makes humanity better than their base natures&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also again - perfect is your word not mine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666357#post666357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, really iffy on the idea of the Wake being a permanently-on soul-scouring effect. There's black and gray morality, and then there's forcefeeding the &quot;you are a total monster and if you had any decency you'd kill yourself&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> The wake was a permanently-on soul-scouring effect back in 1E.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666434#post666434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">gives the Leviathan's wake a potential <i>beneficial</i> use: they can prop up someone who has already lost their soul as a Beloved until said soul gets recovered...</div> </div> </div> </div> Did that come up in the thread before? That's going to be a mechanic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666434#post666434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as to the &quot;you are a monster who should commit suicide&quot;: if wanting to continue existence, and <i>minimize</i> what harm you cause is good enough for Vampires, why should Leviathan's be held to a higher standard?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there are ways to get blood ethically.<br /> <br /> But the core question of Leviathan is &quot;you are a monster who should commit suicide. You don't kill yourself, explore why you don't and how you justify that decision&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666540#post666540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odd. I remember seeing that effect mentioned, but I also remember seeing that it &quot;calms&quot; the Leviathan which is at odds with the Wake being turned upon them.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit of both. An Atoll gains similar mechanical bonuses against Leviathans as Leviathans go against their Beloved; but the underlying fluff is different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666477#post666477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, people don't go insane immediately. That take prolonged exposure (so don't be a regular). Yeah, you rain on everyone else nearby's mood, but poor hygiene can do that too.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'll probably say that most people require prolonged exposure but in some cases an Exceptional Success and/or a Dramatic Failure allows it to happen very quickly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666477#post666477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And don't Atolls neutralize the Wake? At least in their immediate proximity? Fluff seems to indicate something in that direction, what with wording that they act as sinkholes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope. One thing I very much want is the possibility for an Atoll to be the &quot;man behind the man&quot; and the real villian of the story. So they aren't going to take away a Leviathans powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666477#post666477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the write-up currently mentions the civil war that left the &quot;good guys&quot; in charge of Marduk proper. What about the &quot;loyalist&quot; faction? Couldn't they <i>also</i> be active now? Lacking much of the resources of TMS at large, yes, but they may make up for it in ruthlessness no longer curbed by having to play nice for their idealistic collegues. Basically, mirror the SHIELD/Hydra civil war, except in this case the &quot;good guys&quot; emerged with more/better infrastructure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sheild/Hydra is a good way to think about it. And the write up covers this already. For example:<br /> <br /> &quot;the new commanders of the Marduk Society are busy re establishing lines of communication and figuring out which dark sites were looted and destroyed by fleeing conspirators, <b>which are active rogue enclaves</b> and which simply don't have the latest encryption codes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Early second season Agents of Shield Shield would be a good model for a rogue enclave, while Avengers/Captain Amercia II would be the idealists current situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-16-2015, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T01:22:16-07:00","id":666612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666571#post666571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While humanity is currently flawed and WoD huamnity is worse; Reason is, IMO, a good thing. And Marduk aren't a metaphor for humanity. They're a metaphor for &quot;the way reason makes humanity better than their base natures&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might Original Marduk (henceforth referred to as oMarduk or oTMS) serve as a metaphor for Reason unconstrained by ethics/compassion/methods? To serve as a dark mirror to New Marduk's virtue and optimism?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666571#post666571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wake was a permanently-on soul-scouring effect back in 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Missed that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666571#post666571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did that come up in the thread before? That's going to be a mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666571#post666571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there are ways to get blood ethically.</div> </div> </div> </div>And a Leviathan <i>might</i> be able to get away with only socializing with Atolls. And people online, as the Wake doesn't (likely) extend there. (though I've got an idea for an Evolution...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666571#post666571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. One thing I very much want is the possibility for an Atoll to be the &quot;man behind the man&quot; and the real villian of the story. So they aren't going to take away a Leviathans powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might such an effect be an optional Merit? Potentially not even limited to Atolls (such as a misbegotten Hybrid who naturally acts as a scarmbler, screwing up your cult when it wanders nearby).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666571#post666571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sheild/Hydra is a good way to think about it. And the write up covers this already. For example:<br /> <br /> &quot;the new commanders of the Marduk Society are busy re establishing lines of communication and figuring out which dark sites were looted and destroyed by fleeing conspirators, <b>which are active rogue enclaves</b> and which simply don't have the latest encryption codes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Early second season Agents of Shield Shield would be a good model for a rogue enclave, while Avengers/Captain Amercia II would be the idealists current situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even though they almost certainly won't be referred to as such in the materials, it would be great if they both <i>called</i> themselves The Marduk Society. Spreads confusion, and adds complications for nMarduk cleaning up oMarduk's PR messes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T03:10:03-07:00","id":666665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666612#post666612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might Original Marduk (henceforth referred to as oMarduk or oTMS) serve as a metaphor for Reason unconstrained by ethics/compassion/methods? To serve as a dark mirror to New Marduk's virtue and optimism?</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps closer to Reason uesd to justify base instincts.<br /> <br /> A domiment ape: I get to enslave you because my muscles are bigger than yours. Now go fetch me fruit.<br /> <br /> An age of sail slaver / old Marduk: I have &quot;scentifically proven&quot; that enslaving you is the natural order. Now grow my sugar.<br /> <br /> New Marduk: I disprove your racist nonsense.<br /> <br /> <br /> The key differene is that I would say an age of sail slaver actually is constrained by compassion - but it's compassion for his rich buddies who'll loose their income if slavery is abolished and their self respect if they had to admit what they do is evil. Someone truely unconstrained by compassion and morality would probably be too much of a loner fit the civilisation themes of Marduk.<br /> <br /> Basically. Old Marduk are closer to the scientific racists than Rick (of Rick and Morty). Rick's from Genius: the Transgression, not the Marduk Society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666612#post666612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Missed that.</div> </div> </div> </div> No reason you would spot it. 1E leviathan didn't really use the word &quot;soul&quot;, because what's a soul really? It seems logical to me that if a divine being drives you mad - they'll be affecting your soul as well as your mind because divine and soul are very close concepts. But in 1E souls were a pretty Mage specific concept that Leviathan left to the Awakened.<br /> <br /> Now that souls are part of the WoD corebook and 2E Leviathan is going to do more with the concept of godhood souls will be mentioned and some powers will affect them directly. In practice though the 2E wake will be mechanically pretty similar. The Strain specific madness is the biggest change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666612#post666612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a Leviathan <i>might</i> be able to get away with only socializing with Atolls. And people online, as the Wake doesn't (likely) extend there. (though I've got an idea for an Evolution...)</div> </div> </div> </div> IMO online only socalising would give you a bonus dice but not prevent you from having to roll against the Erosion of your mind.<br /> <br /> A Leviathan who lives in a remote lake with an Atoll is living a perfectly acceptable ethical lifestyle. Good luck finding a willing Atoll though, and Atolls aren't immortal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666612#post666612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might such an effect be an optional Merit? Potentially not even limited to Atolls (such as a misbegotten Hybrid who naturally acts as a scarmbler, screwing up your cult when it wanders nearby).</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd say a Wake scrambler is too powerful for a Merit. You'd need a Mage, Genius, or perhaps someone like the Sons of Phobos but with reason or religion based magic to pull it off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666612#post666612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even though they almost certainly won't be referred to as such in the materials, it would be great if they both <i>called</i> themselves The Marduk Society. Spreads confusion, and adds complications for nMarduk cleaning up oMarduk's PR messes.</div> </div> </div> </div>OOC they're refered to by the word rogue. IC they can call themselves whatever you want <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T03:54:02-07:00","id":666683,"title":"","content":"Just responding in brief...<br /> <br /> Saintly was indeed an <b>awful</b> choice of words. In a place like the World of Darkness, that has &quot;crapsack&quot; written into the very fabric of reality, people with that level of idealism and incorruptibility would be incredibly rare, if not unheard of. That was a huge reason why people were throwing around the &quot;Mary Sue&quot; label.<br /> <br /> Nobody is disagreeing with the idea that Reason is a Good Thing. What is disagreeable is that Reason would be an especially potent force in the World of Darkness. There's an excellent quote in one of the Mummy books, can't recall which one, about the fact that the Cursed laugh bitterly when someone talks about humanity's progress; having lived since the Bronze Age, they can blend into society almost perfectly, because even though they have seen humanity's transition through thousands of years, witnessing the rise and fall of empires, <b>nothing. Has. CHANGED</b>. Not where it matters. <b>THAT</b> is how awful the World of Darkness is, where slaves from the early Bronze Age claim there's nothing different after all those thousands of years.<br /> <br /> I can support the idea of a group dedicated to the Power of Reason... with their Flame as a fragile, vulnerable thing that must be carefully guarded and tended, watched over for thousands of years and slowly fueled in hopes of one day chasing away the stormy darkness.<br /> <br /> What I cannot support is the idea of a group where the Flame of Reason burns so strongly that it's inevitable that it will overturn everything that makes the World of Darkness the world that it is. It's just too unthematic. It's the difference between Princesses, who do mesh so well with the World of Darkness, and Sailor Moon, which doesn't.<br /> <br /> The statements you are making are making Marduk seem less annoying, but still not really selling me on it at all.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think that moving the &quot;revolution of the idealists against the old men&quot; from &quot;near future&quot; to &quot;recent past&quot; was probably not a good move. Or an outright mistake. In large part because I cannot see that working out well for the idealists at all. Seriously, you mean to tell me that the Old Men never once decided to add in all sorts of boobytraps and backdoors to <b>keep</b> this sort of thing from happening? If I was one of the Old Men, I would make it that being able to use any of the Mardukian technology requires a special implant - which pulls double-duty as a brain-incinerating self-destruct device, just in case I need to protect myself from my own pawns.<br /> <br /> Seriously, this is something all of the long-living supernatural splats repeat: you do not <b>get</b> old <b>unless</b> you are a paranoid sneaky bastard.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that the Idealists couldn't have won, just that it <b>should</b> have cost them a hell of a lot of lives, technology, stockpiles, resources, knowledge and... well, everything. The Marduk Society should be a conspiracy on the brink, in no better shape than the Leviathans in terms of &quot;presence&quot;. <b>They</b> just have the confidence that they &quot;are destined&quot; to rise from the ashes like a phoenix. both because of their idealism and their ideology.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, I know the Wake was always on in 1e. I thought it was a pretty stupid mechanic back then too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T05:15:49-07:00","id":666771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666683#post666683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What is disagreeable is that Reason would be an especially potent force in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div> And here I think lies the problem.<br /> <br /> Wheather reason is a potent force in the WoD simply isn't relevant. The actual question is wheather reason is a potent force in Leviathan: the Tempest. And the answer is that the entire game is designed on this conflict between modern reason and primordial savagry; so of course reason is going to be a very potent force.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666683#post666683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's an excellent quote in one of the Mummy books</div> </div> </div> </div> I remember people talking about that quote, and I thought it was extreemly silly. Things have changed. Have a look at <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_Before_Civilization\" target=\"_blank\">War Before Civilisation</a> (and bare in mind that chart is for the 20th century so it includes both world wars). Or <a href=\"http://www.ted.com/talks/hans_rosling_shows_the_best_stats_you_ve_ever_seen?language=en\" target=\"_blank\">Hans Rosling's TED talk</a> TED talk about looking at world development. Things do change - not as fast as we'd like but it's nonsense to pretend they haven't changed since the bronze age.<br /> <br /> The WoD Bronze age is worse than the real bronze age. The WoD modern day is worse than the real modern day. But the WoD modern day is much nicer than the WoD bronze age. It's simply impossible to make the WoD a dark mirror or our world without that being true.<br /> <br /> Anyway I don't want to get too deeply into real world politics, that can derail any conversation. So I'll leave with this. Leviathan is not Mummy. They have different themes and different settings. Reason is much more powerful in Leviathan than it is in Mummy. And it has been ever since 1E where the Banes of the Tribe is called &quot;Electricity, Man's Power of Reason&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666683#post666683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, yes, I know the Wake was always on in 1e. I thought it was a pretty stupid mechanic back then too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some things are just too fundamental to the premise to change. Like vampire's drinking blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-16-2015, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T08:04:19-07:00","id":666986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666771#post666771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And here I think lies the problem.<br /> <br /> Wheather reason is a potent force in the WoD simply isn't relevant. The actual question is wheather reason is a potent force in Leviathan: the Tempest. And the answer is that the entire game is designed on this conflict between modern reason and primordial savagry; so of course reason is going to be a very potent force.<br /> <br /> I remember people talking about that quote, and I thought it was extreemly silly. Things have changed. Have a look at <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_Before_Civilization\" target=\"_blank\">War Before Civilisation</a> (and bare in mind that chart is for the 20th century so it includes both world wars). Or <a href=\"http://www.ted.com/talks/hans_rosling_shows_the_best_stats_you_ve_ever_seen?language=en\" target=\"_blank\">Hans Rosling's TED talk</a> TED talk about looking at world development. Things do change - not as fast as we'd like but it's nonsense to pretend they haven't changed since the bronze age.<br /> <br /> The WoD Bronze age is worse than the real bronze age. The WoD modern day is worse than the real modern day. But the WoD modern day is much nicer than the WoD bronze age. It's simply impossible to make the WoD a dark mirror or our world without that being true.<br /> <br /> Anyway I don't want to get too deeply into real world politics, that can derail any conversation. So I'll leave with this. Leviathan is not Mummy. They have different themes and different settings. Reason is much more powerful in Leviathan than it is in Mummy. And it has been ever since 1E where the Banes of the Tribe is called &quot;Electricity, Man's Power of Reason&quot;<br /> <br /> Some things are just too fundamental to the premise to change. Like vampire's drinking blood.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you're missing the point that bothers the rest of us. Some of us can accept them being potent, certainly.<br /> <br /> I mean, really, it's hard to call Marduk overpowered compared to the likes of the Exarchs and the God Machine and the masses of god beings in WoD.<br /> <br /> It's just that the way that they are handled, the description as being morally perfect, that really tends to strike us as being for lack of a better term &quot;Sueish&quot;. Which is why I want more emphasis placed on vulnerability or why other people want their power drastically nerfed. The many of us are unwilling to accept them as they are because they are seemingly completely without weaknesses.<br /> <br /> Regardless of their power, the fact of the matter is that we perceive them as out of place due to their seeming lack of flaws as an organization and the fact that you describe them as always improving across the board.<br /> <br /> Also, I am fairly sure reason isn't perfect either. I mean, really, in the World of Darkness, the fact of the matter is sometimes the rational thing to do is to murder a bunch of kids to summon murder demons.<br /> Moral dilemnas kinda put a damper on acting moral all the time and can reasonably inflict chronic jadedness into new Marduk if enough of them happen all at once.<br /> <br /> Here's a thought. If Marduk is entirely reason, would it make sense then to undergo processes to strip their base impulses and emotions. I mean, if you really want to emphasize that they are reason, perhaps removing all the things that make them &quot;unreasonable&quot;, emotion, impulses, love, hate... and replacing them entirely with &quot;reason&quot;. Marduk would be cold and devoid of feeling. They would still want to improve society, but they'd come off to the players as alien. I think people would be more willing to accept Marduk if they were Vulcans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 09-16-2015, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T08:52:51-07:00","id":667073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666986#post666986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're missing the point that bothers the rest of us.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it looks like different people are bothered by different things. Or at least putting emphasis on different things.<br /> <br /> Which is what you'd expect really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666986#post666986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of their power, the fact of the matter is that we perceive them as out of place due to their seeming lack of flaws as an organization and the fact that you describe them as always improving across the board.</div> </div> </div> </div> And while I can't change the way you feel; I disagree with the underlying logic.<br /> <br /> Leviathan is not Mummy, Mummy is not Mage, and Mage is not Vampire. Each game has different themes and different settings. To say something is out of place in the WoD is a statement that doesn't really make sense to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666986#post666986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a thought. If Marduk is entirely reason</div> </div> </div> </div>Marduk is not entirely reason. They're &quot;the way reason, civilisation, science, philosophy etc, allows humanity to rise above our base instincts&quot;.<br /> <br /> Unsprisingly people started using a short word instead that rather long sentence; but no, Marduk are not pure reason.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T09:13:51-07:00","id":667096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, I think that moving the &quot;revolution of the idealists against the old men&quot; from &quot;near future&quot; to &quot;recent past&quot; was probably not a good move. Or an outright mistake. In large part because I cannot see that working out well for the idealists at all. Seriously, you mean to tell me that the Old Men never once decided to add in all sorts of boobytraps and backdoors to <b>keep</b> this sort of thing from happening? If I was one of the Old Men, I would make it that being able to use any of the Mardukian technology requires a special implant - which pulls double-duty as a brain-incinerating self-destruct device, just in case I need to protect myself from my own pawns.<br /> <br /> Seriously, this is something all of the long-living supernatural splats repeat: you do not <b>get</b> old <b>unless</b> you are a paranoid sneaky bastard.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that the Idealists couldn't have won, just that it <b>should</b> have cost them a hell of a lot of lives, technology, stockpiles, resources, knowledge and... well, everything. The Marduk Society should be a conspiracy on the brink, in no better shape than the Leviathans in terms of &quot;presence&quot;. <b>They</b> just have the confidence that they &quot;are destined&quot; to rise from the ashes like a phoenix. both because of their idealism and their ideology. </div> </div> </div>This too. If Marduk is a power player, it should be jaded; if it's idealistic and ethically sound, it shouldn't be too effective, because the setting is one where you can't make an omelette without breaking a few spines. If reason and technology alone were sufficient to be powerful, the world would be ruled by scientists; as we clearly don't live in that world, and the WoD isn't that world, Marduk's Pure Reason isn't sufficient for it to become overwhelmingly powerful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reason is much more powerful in Leviathan than it is in Mummy. And it has been ever since 1E where the Banes of the Tribe is called &quot;Electricity, Man's Power of Reason&quot; </div> </div> </div>The fact that electricity is symbolically potent against Leviathans doesn't, as a matter of fact, make reason in and of itself more powerful. Vampires are burnt by sunlight and fire, and thematic reference is made to fire and sunlight as the Curse of Purity (something along those lines) in Vampire 2e, but humanity isn't any purer than usual, and mortal hunters don't wield the Powers of Purity against vampires -- despite the fact that &quot;defilement vs. humanity&quot; is a deeply embedded Vampire theme. Likewise, the vampires' Nemeses aren't Pure-Hearted Mortals, but demon owls who want them to sacrifice their humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wheather reason is a potent force in the WoD simply isn't relevant. The actual question is wheather reason is a potent force in Leviathan: the Tempest. And the answer is that the entire game is designed on this conflict between modern reason and primordial savagry; so of course reason is going to be a very potent force. </div> </div> </div>We appear to be getting into personal politics. Personally, I do believe that science et al are, in general, a force for good in a overwhelmingly apathetic universe -- but the thing is that you've built your understanding of the setting on your own personal assumptions, i.e., that humanity's better nature will inevitably overcome its baser urges and that the id has been squashed by modern society. Hell, I could argue for a mighty Leviathan power in the setting, mostly constrained by violence and Marduk spies -- reason doesn't rule the world; it forms a complicated infrastructure not too far from collapse and regression, and it fails frequently, presumably more so in the WoD.<br /> <br /> You've positioned Marduk as a representative of that better nature, and because you really love science, reason and all that jazz, you feel that giving Marduk any flaws that weren't imposed on it by external circumstances dilutes the theme of Reason vs. Savagery. Ultimately, I feel that this reduces Marduk to non-humans -- that is, you've decided that Leviathans, who aren't complicit in their own transformations, represent Absolute Evil, and that to oppose them, Marduk has to be Absolute Good, which... people generally aren't. By reducing Marduk to a pure metaphor, you dilute its value to players -- a grayer organization, one willing to take moral risks, offers more options.<br /> <br /> Reason, science, civilization et al. sometimes allow us to rise above our base instincts. They're also often used to supplement and aid our base instincts -- nuclear weapons, electroshock torture, rationalization, chemical weapons... a comprehensive Marduk should address the fact that humans haven't gotten less terrible, they've just worked out reward systems that reward terribleness less frequently -- but, too often, create new and inventive reasons and methods by which terribleness can be achieved.<br /> <br /> Personally, at this point, I'd go back to 1e's &quot;a civil war is on the horizon&quot; -- it gives players more freedom, acknowledges that science is imperfect and that people don't stop rationalizing the choices their ids make just because they own cars and computers (while still allowing for a degree of idealism), and lets us keep the mermaid flesh thing around, which -- let's be honest -- is just cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","user":"CalvaryKeter","date":". 09-16-2015, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:27:48-07:00","id":667285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667096#post667096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This too. If Marduk is a power player, it should be jaded; if it's idealistic and ethically sound, it shouldn't be too effective, because the setting is one where you can't make an omelette without breaking a few spines. If reason and technology alone were sufficient to be powerful, the world would be ruled by scientists; as we clearly don't live in that world, and the WoD isn't that world, Marduk's Pure Reason isn't sufficient for it to become overwhelmingly powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another option would be for Marduk to be fractured. Not just organizationally, as it is now, but ideologically. Part of progress is that it opens up new paths, and not everyone is going to agree on what is the right one. That is actually very thematically important, because once everyone in a group starts to agree you get groupthink, which leads to stagnation.<br /> That groupthink could actually be the reason they can only improve existing tech, but it clashes with the Progress theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667096#post667096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've positioned Marduk as a representative of that better nature, and because you really love science, reason and all that jazz, you feel that giving Marduk any flaws that weren't imposed on it by external circumstances dilutes the theme of Reason vs. Savagery. Ultimately, I feel that this reduces Marduk to non-humans -- that is, you've decided that Leviathans, who aren't complicit in their own transformations, represent Absolute Evil, and that to oppose them, Marduk has to be Absolute Good, which... people generally aren't. By reducing Marduk to a pure metaphor, you dilute its value to players -- a grayer organization, one willing to take moral risks, offers more options.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point about diluting the value to the player is particularly important. Marduk as it stands is basically a beat-stick. A whole lot of story potential from 1e has been lost.<br /> Basically, you're taking the themes too far, to the point where they cease to be interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667096#post667096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, at this point, I'd go back to 1e's &quot;a civil war is on the horizon&quot; -- it gives players more freedom, acknowledges that science is imperfect and that people don't stop rationalizing the choices their ids make just because they own cars and computers (while still allowing for a degree of idealism), and lets us keep the mermaid flesh thing around, which -- let's be honest -- is just cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd propose having Marduk caught up in a new conflict, based around the &quot;and then what?&quot; question.<br /> Off the top of my head, I'd see two major questions resulting in four major factions.<br /> <br /> <b>Questions</b><br /> What to do about the Leviathans<br /> -Kill 'em. They are inherintly monstrous, with no redeeming value.<br /> -Save 'em: Leviathans are victims of their own nature, and through the power of progress, we can find a way to redeem them.<br /> --Wake disrupting tech might not exist now, but that is not to say it could never exist.<br /> What to do with their advanced tech.<br /> -Keep it to ourselves. The world isn't ready.<br /> -Give it to the world. The world will never be ready if we don't.<br /> <br /> <b>Factions</b><br /> -Helping Hand: Give the tech, and the techniques by which the tech was developed, to the world. Use our moral high ground to save the Leviathans from themselves.<br /> -Surgeons: Give the tech to the world, mandkind will ultimately better themselves. Eliminate the Leviathans. They are offer no redeeming value, and are a cancer that holds us back.<br /> -Shepherds: Keep the tech, save the Leviathans. The world lacks the judgement to use our secrets without hurting themselves. We should use the tech to uplift them to the point where we are ready, and that includes the Leviathans.<br /> -Guardians: Keep the tech, eliminate the Leviathans. Mankind isn't ready for our secrets, but we can help them along by eliminating at least one of the things preying on them and holding them back.<br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, someone suggested Leviathans having access to anti-tech powers. I think there is potential there, but instead of having advanced tools break, I think having the Leviathan attack the human aspect would be more appropriate. Instead of having the Leviathan make a gun jam, instead they make the user forget everything they know about gun safety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:53:05-07:00","id":667314,"title":"","content":"Personally, my backup plan is (if Marduk's current treatment makes it to final release):<br /> Let nMarduk have control of all their fancy virtuous toys. Let everything seem bright and hopeful, that they can finally, really, improve the world now. And then let the reality of being in the World of Darkness smack them in the face. Complications, oMarduk false-flag operations, undiscovered Old Man back-doors and booby-traps, the crushing reality of their campaign of genocide against beings that include people who never asked for what happened to them, and just Murphy's Law. Basically, never let nMarduk catch their breath, and force them to make momentary compromises (such as the calculus of &quot;side with oMarkduk/Leviathans/something else to stop X&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T13:24:45-07:00","id":667384,"title":"","content":"I cannot understate just how accurate Almarak and CavalryKeter are in their posts. Metaphors are powerful and all, and the WoD does use them, but even so, there's such a thing as going too far - and Marduk Society, as it is, <i>goes too <b>far</b></i>.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness goes by several core assumptions that one HAS to maintain, or else you don't have a World of Darkness game anymore. You have something else using the Story Teller System.<br /> <br /> The first: mortals control their own fate on the grand scheme, there's no &quot;grand conspiracies&quot; running everything major in history like some conspiracy buff's take on the Illuminati. This is an assumption Marduk is dangerously close to overthrowing.<br /> <br /> The second: power at a price. You <b>never</b> get something for nothing in the World of Darkness. Supernatural powers <b>always</b> come at a drastic price, whether that's in the form of actual banes, as in PC splats, or in moral or thematic corruption, as in the case of every Hunter conspiracy ever - from Cheiron Group's mutilation of body, mind and soul with its thaumatechnology to the Malleus Malleficarium being built on a lie by an ambitious ghoul to the Lucifuge being the children of demons. This is an assumption Marduk has forfeited, unless one counts the whole &quot;Godtech is strengthened by Virtuosity&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> The third: innocence is the first casualty. The more idealistic you are, the <b>less powerful</b> you are. If you would hold yourself back from the shadows, you inherently weaken yourself. This assumption is the primary thing that Marduk is breaking.<br /> <br /> The author of Princess: The Hopeful actually said this a couple of pages back - around page 14. Princess: The Hopeful is an idealistic, hopeful game, but it's undercut by several notions of gritty realism and cynicism, mostly that the fundamental assumption of Princess is that Princesses have the deck stacked against them and it's very uncertain if they will ever succeed. This is good, this keeps them both in line with their core focus - Hope Springs Eternal, Hope Is Strength - but at the same time it recognizes and respects the three core assumptions of the World of Darkness. It's why the game has earned respect for being a Magical Girl Game that actually <b>fits</b> the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> The Marduk Society does <b>none</b> of that. It would be a terrible excuse for a game if the Marduk Society was actually supposed to be the player faction - and they're <b>not</b>! This is supposed to be <b>Leviathan: The Tempest</b>, the game of playing as primeval aquatic Lovecraftian monster. The Marduk Society are supposed to be the game's <i>antagonists</i>... and when your antagonists are portrayed as being all around better and cooler and more interesting than your protagonists, <i>something has gone <b>wrong</b> somewhere</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","user":"VoidDrifter","date":". 03-10-2016, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T14:01:52-07:00","id":667410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667073#post667073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it looks like different people are bothered by different things. Or at least putting emphasis on different things.<br /> <br /> Which is what you'd expect really.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's more accurate to say that we're all bothered by most of the same things and are attempting to resolve it by throwing out proposed solutions until one sticks.<br /> <br /> We all would want Marduk to be revised to make more sense: in general, they don't have enough flaws or limitations.<br /> <br /> I'm currently running on the idea Marduk <i>should </i>be reason and progress. specifically, <i>untrestrained reason and progress.</i> All of those things should have a price, because quite honestly, nothing is ever free. In the real world, progress comes at the cost of bloodshed, suffering, and political instability. Jobs are lost with every invention and not everyone is able to adapt to the new market. Voting gave people freedom to choose their leaders, but at the same time made them vulnerable to being guided like sheep. With security came gun control laws, with medicine came stronger diseases. With cameras came the invasion of privacy. We deposed Monarchies for elected officials... and often those leaders don't have enough practice at it to be what people consider competent.<br /> <br /> Reason and progress are good, don't get me wrong, but... maybe you're limiting Marduk's potential as a story antagonist by not letting them take reason and progress... to unreasonable levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 09-16-2015, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T16:01:44-07:00","id":667535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667410#post667410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more accurate to say that we're all bothered by most of the same things and are attempting to resolve it by throwing out proposed solutions until one sticks.<br /> <br /> We all would want Marduk to be revised to make more sense: in general, they don't have enough flaws or limitations.<br /> <br /> I'm currently running on the idea Marduk <i>should </i>be reason and progress. specifically, <i>untrestrained reason and progress.</i> All of those things should have a price, because quite honestly, nothing is ever free. In the real world, progress comes at the cost of bloodshed, suffering, and political instability. Jobs are lost with every invention and not everyone is able to adapt to the new market. Voting gave people freedom to choose their leaders, but at the same time made them vulnerable to being guided like sheep. With security came gun control laws, with medicine came stronger diseases. With cameras came the invasion of privacy. We deposed Monarchies for elected officials... and often those leaders don't have enough practice at it to be what people consider competent.<br /> <br /> Reason and progress are good, don't get me wrong, but... maybe you're limiting Marduk's potential as a story antagonist by not letting them take reason and progress... to unreasonable levels.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that goes too far in the opposite direction, and runs into the same problems. You're still rendering Marduk down to a singular thesis, which limits story ideas. Not to say that Marduk shouldn't incorporate unrestrained progress, but there should be more to it than that.<br /> I think borrowing from Genius makes sense, with the idea that there is no one at the wheel any more. That allows a lot of very different ideas about what constitutes Reason and Progress to emerge, opening up storytelling possibilities. Oversimplification is the enemy here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T16:11:52-07:00","id":667538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667535#post667535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think that goes too far in the opposite direction, and runs into the same problems. You're still rendering Marduk down to a singular thesis, which limits story ideas. Not to say that Marduk shouldn't incorporate unrestrained progress, but there should be more to it than that.<br /> I think borrowing from Genius makes sense, with the idea that there is no one at the wheel any more. That allows a lot of very different ideas about what constitutes Reason and Progress to emerge, opening up storytelling possibilities. Oversimplification is the enemy here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Obviously reducing them to a cariciture is probably disrespectful, but the idea to make the faction more morally grey by taking its premise as Progress and Reason and show casing the negative aspects of it is a valid portrayal that fits in within World of Darkness. I do not know where a good stopping point is to make them &quot;balanced&quot; though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T18:00:26-07:00","id":667650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667538#post667538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Obviously reducing them to a cariciture is probably disrespectful, but the idea to make the faction more morally grey by taking its premise as Progress and Reason and show casing the negative aspects of it is a valid portrayal that fits in within World of Darkness. I do not know where a good stopping point is to make them &quot;balanced&quot; though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they share some traits with both Task Force: Valkyrie, Null Mysteriis, Loyalists of Thule, and Utopia Now, so maybe looking there can give some ideas to make them grayer without compromising their core idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T19:21:33-07:00","id":667725,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say it is a question of disrespect, rather, what stories the treatment enables. For example, the unrestrained progress angle could lead to a Leviathan preying on people rendered redundant by Marduk inovations.<br /> <br /> Differentiation from TFV is actually pretty easy. They are not sanctioned. Whenever they fire an orbital weapon, they're going to have pretty much every government in the world out for their blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","user":"Thamuzz","date":". 09-16-2015, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T00:19:35-07:00","id":667942,"title":"","content":"You go to sleep and wake up to a whole new discussion and an entirely new poster (how did you here of the thread? I'm curious). I'll read it at some point when I've woken up, but for now I think the question of how much misunderstanding there was has been answered.<br /> <br /> Feel free to continue discussing among yourselves; but ideas that don't fit with Marduk representing &quot;the way science, reason, civilisation, etc help make humanity into better people&quot; aren't going to go in. In the mean while I'm thinking about ways to port the Philantophy Committee to 2E - creativity works at it's own pace, but if it takes too long I'll get started on Chapter 3. Most of that could be a straight port from the 1E rules or simple new rules; so good to get it over with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T01:49:17-07:00","id":667995,"title":"","content":"Just something I've been wondering: has any thought been given as to crossovers between Leviathan and the canon game splats?<br /> <br /> I mean, yes, all NWoD books are written as stand-alones, allowing the player race to be the only (or only significant) thing going bump in the night... but, at the same time, the NWoD has always been better than the OWoD in that it actually puts thought into what will happen if the other races of the meta-setting actually are running around and bumping into your PCs.<br /> <br /> So, it makes sense, to me at least, to put some thought into canonical interactions between Leviathans and other monsters. What do they think of Werewolves, who have similar shapeshifting powers and &quot;divine lineage&quot;? Or Mummies, who are literally relics of the old world that the Tribe once dominated? Or Mages, whose powers are such that they can claim to be the new gods of humanity, or Demons, who are literally technology beyond even human understanding come to life?<br /> <br /> Hell, no matter what ultimately happens to the Marduk Society, some thought should be put into what happens should they cross paths with the other horrors lurking in the dark. How do they think of Werewolves, who are so much like terrestrial-focused Leviathans, but which have adapted far better to the changing world around them, even being capable of subverting technology to their whim (thanks to &quot;ins&quot; with Technology spirits)? What happens when they come into contact with a being that seems to pollute the minds around it, and even the very earth underfoot, but which actually <b>feeds</b> on the lightning that they try to destroy it with? Mages can reasonably claim a divine status, being capable of commanding life, death, space, time, the matter around them, the fundamental forces of the universe itself - how does Marduk reconcile all that unimaginable power existing in the hands of &quot;superstitious primitives&quot;? Demons are many-angled transdimensional quantum data singularities who tore themselves free of a machine so vast that the <i>laws of physics</i> are either a side-effect of its operating system, part of its hardware, or both - and they use that technological nature to indulge in the most base and human of natures; how does the Marduk Society reconcile that with their reverence for technological progress as the physical expression of reason's triumph over primeval nature?<br /> <br /> There's just so many interesting aspects to think about when it comes into crossing over Leviathans or Marduk with the canon splats, it seems a shame not to try and address them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T02:29:30-07:00","id":668021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667995#post667995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just something I've been wondering: has any thought been given as to crossovers between Leviathan and the canon game splats?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. It's something my mind ocasionally drifts too, and I will be writing Steryotypes at some point, probably, it's not my strongest area. I don't plan to write a big crossover chapter, but a forum post - sure why not.<br /> <br /> The only ones I've really thought out so far are Vampires and Beasts. Vampires because I wondered how a Leviathan's cult might compare to a vampire's web of influence. Beast just because they're topical at the moment.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires hate Leviathans because they're harbringers of chaos, and nothing ruins a good subtle web of influence and control like chaos.<br /> <br /> Beasts of course think that Leviathans are Family; Leviathans are immune to Beast's first impression aura (Leviathan's are going to have really really strong psychic defences in 2E) but usually ok with having sane non-Leviathans who want to be around them. Beasts would make good middle management in a Cult. But in the tradition of WoD haughty and dismissive WoD steryotypes the Steryotype for Beasts will probably be something like:<br /> <br /> &quot;This girl walked into my temple and said her soul was a kraken too, and could she watch while I bathed. So I ate the creepy fucker's soul. It's funny, her soul actually was a kraken.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667995#post667995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;divine lineage&quot;? claim to be the new gods of humanity</div> </div> </div> </div> In Leviathan &quot;divine&quot; is a technical term that describes certain types of Supernatural entities. Mother Luna, Father Wolf, and their children are not divine even though Mother Luna is probably significantly stronger than most actual gods. Same with Mages, powerful but not technically divine.<br /> <br /> In my personal WoD the following things are Divine: Leviathans themselves, The Divine Fire, WoD Inferno, and it's mentioned but unpublished opposite WoD Empyerian. If Marduk, Zeus and the other gods of the Chaoskampf exist they're from WoD Empyerian. (The furies of Greek Myth are mentioned to have once been Empyerian so why not Zeus too?).<br /> <br /> Certain Hunters also weild divine power. I play Benidictions as being genuinely from Abraham's God and his Saints (WoD Empyerian). Shemot are either Empyerian or Divine Fire depending on how much of Promethian's setting is in play. And the Mantle of Bastet is also Empyerian.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667995#post667995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or Demons, who are literally technology beyond even human understanding come to life?</div> </div> </div> </div> Ignore the technology side of demons. Demons are spies, not tech, and the Demon-Leviathan relationship should be built on that.<br /> <br /> Sadly most of the cool spy themes would hinge on Demons working for a higher power that might have an <i>interest</i> in a Leviathan and their cult. Demons don't, so I'm not sure what to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667995#post667995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Mummies, who are literally relics of the old world that the Tribe once dominated?</div> </div> </div> </div> Mummy is an interesting one. While Leviathan uses ancient bronze age themes at. It's really more about the darker instincts in the human brain that predates the bronze age.<br /> <br /> And The Tribe's bronze age themes are closer to Abraham sacraficing Issac than to Babylonian or Egyptian cities and civilisation. So Mummies don't come from the same old world as the Tribe, but it's richer and more advanced and more advanced neighbours. There's a reason why the Bible is full of other nations (including Babylon!) invading ancient Israel.<br /> <br /> Also that's thinking about it from a themes perspective. From an in setting perspective Leviathans' Primordial World is far older than Irem, or at least, they think it is.<br /> <br /> From an IC Leviathan's perspective it's probably something like &quot;Ha Ha! Your civilisaition collapsed and the Primordial Waters wash over the remains. Just as the modern world and Marduk will one day fall&quot;. While true (more or less, what exactly are the Primordial Waters) in that Irem collapsed. In Leviathan's setting it's not proof that the modern world will fall.<br /> <br /> In Mummy's setting it is; so in crossover who knows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667995#post667995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, no matter what ultimately happens to the Marduk Society, some thought should be put into what happens should they cross paths with the other horrors lurking in the dark.</div> </div> </div> </div> Any thought put into the Marduk Society's relation to other splats would be just for fun. But it is fun, so think away <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This far though, my crossover thoughts have all been about the Tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-17-2015, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T03:19:19-07:00","id":668042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668021#post668021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While Leviathan uses ancient bronze age themes at. It's really more about the darker instincts in the human brain that predates the bronze age.<br /> <br /> And The Tribe's bronze age themes are closer to Abraham sacraficing Issac than to Babylonian or Egyptian cities and civilisation. So Mummies don't come from the same old world as the Tribe, but it's richer and more advanced and more advanced neighbours. There's a reason why the Bible is full of other nations (including Babylon!) invading ancient Israel.<br /> <br /> Also that's thinking about it from a themes perspective. From an in setting perspective Leviathans' Primordial World is far older than Irem, or at least, they think it is.<br /> <br /> From an IC Leviathan's perspective it's probably something like &quot;Ha Ha! Your civilisaition collapsed and the Primordial Waters wash over the remains. Just as the modern world and Marduk will one day fall&quot;. While true (more or less, what exactly are the Primordial Waters) in that Irem collapsed. In Leviathan's setting it's not proof that the modern world will fall.<br /> <br /> In Mummy's setting it is; so in crossover who knows.<br /> <br /> Any thought put into the Marduk Society's relation to other splats would be just for fun. But it is fun, so think away <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This far though, my crossover thoughts have all been about the Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u00b4m thinking in Stephen King\u00b4s <i>The Myst, </i>where the true horror weren\u00b4t the monsters, but how easily and quickly a town of modern, rational fellas turned themselves into a bunch of supersticious primitives ready to perform human sacrifices to appease the &quot;dark gods&quot;. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T03:30:35-07:00","id":668046,"title":"","content":"Quick question. Which part of that large quoted block are you replying too?<br /> <br /> <br /> Leviathans will absolutely have the ability to pull of an encore of The Myst. Actually 1E already has a ritual to do summon the mist (should it be a Ritual, an Elements Channel or both?). Fun fact though - it was actually inspired by Digimon and not The Mist.<br /> <br /> Devolving modern people into a bunch of superstitious primitives would probably be best represnted by the Leviathan's Wake turning them all into Beloved - but I plan to rework Call of the Depths and I think I can squeeze the The Myst into a couple of Adaptations quite easily. One that inflicts Conditions (combined with a Condition like Superstitious) and one that lets you ignore Breaking Points until the Condition is over to remove the disincentives to human sacrifice. EDIT: Actually one Adaptation and two conditions makes more sense.<br /> <br /> Tearing down a major city will be hard of course. To quote Watchmen &quot;I'm not locked in here with you, you're locked in here with me!&quot;. Going The Mist on all human civilisation is along the lines of defeating the Exarchs, but a typical seaside town. Fairly easy for a Leviathan with a bit of exp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-17-2015, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T04:03:03-07:00","id":668057,"title":"","content":"And here it is:<br /> <br /> If this doesn't satisfy people's desire to strip away civilisation, reason and morality then I don't know what will. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Call of the Depths (Descendant Channel)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The voice of the Leviathan is what inspired legends of sirens. Speaking, crying, bellowing, or whispering: all vocalizations of the Leviathan creep into the minds of listeners, robbing them of their will and self determination.</i></span></span><ul><li><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: Presence + Expression + Sheol</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action Type: Standard</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan's can create an unearthly song or other, stranger, vocalisation that interacts with the deepest and most primitive parts of the mind. Those that hear the voice, are vulnerable to the Wake, and have less (Resolve + Power Trait) than the Leviathan's successes are affected. However player characters and important NPCs should be aloud to roll Resolve + Power Trait independently. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 0\u201d: Birthright of Sanctity</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 1\u201d: Those who hear the Leviathan\u2019s voice are lulled into a hypnotic state and take the Insensate Tilt. They retain enough awareness to slow down gently and so a Leviathan can only cause the occasional accident and not mass carnage. The range is 100 yards per dot of Sheol. Physical barriers that block the Leviathan\u2019s voice can lower the range but water will not. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 2\u201d: As above, but the Leviathan may voluntarily exclude his Beloved from the effect and may speak normally without interrupting his song. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 3\u201d: As above, and the Leviathan gains an alternative ability. By expending 2 Ichor she may give a command that can be expressed in five or so words such as \u201ccome to the waterfront\u201d, \u201cbring me your jewelry\u201d or \u201ckill everyone you see\u201d. Everyone affected will obey the command to the best of their ability, if they complete the task they gain the Insensate Tilt.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 4\u201d: As above, and the range extends to 500 yards per dot of Sheol.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 5\u201d: As above, and the Leviathan may target his song\u2019s to a certain group. This group must have a shared biological trait, linguistic trait, or they can be the Beloved of a particular Leviathan. At the storyteller\u2019s discretion supernatural traits unrelated to the Tribe may be used. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 6\u201d: By expending 4 Ichor the Leviathan may make their song echo against the background fabric of the universe. The Depth 1 or Depth 3 iteration of this Channel become an Environmental Tilt that lasts for the remainder of the scene. Interrupting or otherwise silencing the Leviathan can no longer end the effects. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Adaptations</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unholy Disharmonies (O) - In Depth 2 or lower the Leviathan is able to use Call of the Depths to counter another Leviathan\u2019s song. Roll as normal and reduce the target Leviathan\u2019s successes by your successes. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Song of Madness (OO) - In Depth 3 and lower, when using the Depth 3 version of this Channel the Leviathan may trade in Successes to inflict Mental Conditions upon affected individuals at a ratio of 1 Success per Condition. If the Leviathan\u2019s only goal is to inflict Conditions she may forgo giving orders. Conditions last until they\u2019re Resolved, the Leviathan\u2019s song ends, or the affected individual moves out of range. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Echo\u2019s of Madness (OOOO, requires Song of Madness) - In Depth 6 the Leviathan may choose to have their song Echo for up to Sheol days. This cannot extend the duration of any given orders but it can extend the duration of Conditions inflicted through Song of Madness. </span></span></li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T05:35:39-07:00","id":668101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667942#post667942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You go to sleep and wake up to a whole new discussion and an entirely new poster (how did you here of the thread? I'm curious). I'll read it at some point when I've woken up, but for now I think the question of how much misunderstanding there was has been answered.<br /> <br /> Feel free to continue discussing among yourselves; but ideas that don't fit with Marduk representing &quot;the way science, reason, civilisation, etc help make humanity into better people&quot; aren't going to go in. In the mean while I'm thinking about ways to port the Philantophy Committee to 2E - creativity works at it's own pace, but if it takes too long I'll get started on Chapter 3. Most of that could be a straight port from the 1E rules or simple new rules; so good to get it over with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hi there! Found the thread through Tvtropes.<br /> I've got to implore you to take a closer look at the problems people are having with the current treatment of Marduk. I do think the themes of Progress and Reason can work, but well:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667942#post667942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of creating antagonists to make your protagonist look good or evil by contrast is perfectly fine; however you can screw up the implementation. If I have any criticisms of Heroes - it's that Matt screwed up the implementation.</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand:<br /> <br /> <b>From a game design perspective, what is the purpose of Marduk:</b> At the root level, you are trying to provide storytellers with tools that they can use to create stories that their players will enjoy. In the Leviathan toolbox, Marduk is supposed to highlight the Tribe's stagnation. As it exists, <i>it does this job terribly</i>.<br /> Consider the story options that the current treatment makes possible:<br /> 1. Beatstick. The players done pissed the ST off, time to die.<br /> 2. Cat and mouse: Players must deal with Marduk scouts. &lt;== There could be some potential there, depending on how the game goes. Characters will need to be put in situations where they can socialize with/observe the agents with an open mind. Requires a very skilled ST, but the will not have to reinterpret/change Marduk all that much to get it to work.<br /> 3. I wanna punch them in their stupid perfect faces. &lt;== This is the first one that has really has the potential to display the themes out of the box, but it requires the players to have a reason to be resentful of Marduk <i>because of how they are not stagnant.</i> Just wanting to punch them because they are stronger than you isn't going to convey Marduk's themes. It just makes them feel like bullies.<br /> 4. Rogue Cell: The players go up against a Marduk cell that has been cut off. Added wrinkle is that this cell has gone astray, and Marduk proper is also after them. &lt;== Here we have a chance to illustrate Marduk's themes by contrast. Thing is, this only really allows the players to see what Marduk is <i>not, </i>rather than what it is. Unless the rogue cell is cartoonishly evil, you run the risk of showing Marduk as close minded or bullies or something else not in keeping with Marduk's desired themes.<br /> 5. Greater Threat: The players have to team up with agents of Marduk to stop something bad enough that they would be willing to consider this. &lt;== Here we have a chance for the players to see Marduk as the good people that they are. It allows the players/storyteller to explore the differences in their approach to problem solving than those a Leviathan's abilities naturally predispose them towards. Unfortunately, it is next to impossible to do while staying true to the current treatment. In order to pull it off, you need:<br /> - An isolated cell, one that does not have the resources to resolve the problem on its own.<br /> - A problem that the cell and the players need to resolve, that neither party can actually resolve without the aid of the other.<br /> <br /> Here are a few stories that it prohibits (the storyteller will have to alter Marduk from the current presentation in order for these to work):<br /> 1. The players are approached by a Marduk faction who genuinely wants to find a way to help them. They believe that the characters are the victims of circumstance, and deserve a chance at a full and happy life. &lt;== Shows that Marduk are good people, but could also be used to foster resentment in the players, leading to a &quot;I wanna punch them in the face&quot; scenario.<br /> 1.1. The players are simultaneously attacked by a faction that believes that Leviathans are fundamentally unsalvageable, and should be excised for the good of the world. &lt;== Highlights the dynamic nature of progress, helps lead into an enemy mine situation. I think this is the greatest loss in the transition from 1e to the current incarnation. There, you could have a story about a relatively innocent Leviathan being pursued by a corrupt Marduk agent, bring in a good-guy Marduk agent, have the Leviathans reveal corruption, team up with good guy to stop the corrupt agent. Then, at the end, you can slap the players in the face by having the good agent say that, while the corrupt agent was evil, <i>that doesn't make them good</i>.<br /> 2. Have the Leviathans deal with people who have been in some way harmed with Marduk, such as people who were made redundant by a Marduk invention. &lt;== This breeds contrast, and allows the storyteller/players to more fully explore the themes of Progress vs their own stagnation.<br /> <br /> I'm not claiming that each list is exhaustive.<br /> Marduk as it currently is does not lend itself well to the stories that will best explore its themes. Remember, both players and storytellers need to be interested for it to work.<br /> <br /> <b>What does &quot;the way science, reason, civilisation, etc help make humanity into better people&quot; actually <i>mean</i>:</b> This is a biggie, and why I think it would make sense for you to make &quot;Reason and Progress&quot; the core or Marduk, and allow the &quot;better people&quot; part to emerge more organically. First however, a quick rant on the nature of Progress:<br /> Progress is not neat, it is not even, it is not inevitable, <i>it has no end goal</i>. Progress proceeds in fits and starts along a myriad different paths, and those paths do <u><i>not</i></u> all go in the same direction. One man's Utopia is another's hell. Progress is dynamic, and it arises from conflict and disagreement. When everyone agrees, that is <i>stagnation</i>, just as it is when no-one can agree.<br /> I actually have a lot more thoughts on that particular subject, but those are the points that lead to the question &quot;what does better actually <i>mean?</i>&quot;. If you want Marduk to be anything other than a beatstick, then that question has to be addressed. If you want Marduk to be an interesting beastick, then give a single answer, and be aware that you a diluting the theme of Progress. If you want Marduk to be a tool that is well suited, out of the box, to allow the players to explore Progress vs Stagnation in a meaningful way, then make that question the heart of what Marduk is. My proposal to give Marduk a variety of factions is a way to convey that question, but it isn't the only way. Marduk as it is is poorly designed to convey that question.<br /> At the moment, Marduk's only nod to the chaos and dynamism of Progress is that they are currently disorganized. This feels anemic for something so full of potential.<br /> <br /> <b>How does Marduk fit into the world, and the players expectations:</b> Like it or not, the WoD has certain expectations associated with it, things that a player wants when they play a WoD game. I don't agree with everything that has been said on that point, here is how I view it:<br /> 1. Cynicism: At its core, the WoD is cynical. Marduk as written clashes with that. Thing is, I regard this expectation as a flawed attempt to express the WoD's true draw, which I feel to be:<br /> 2. Mature Storytelling: As in emotionally mature. WoD is a place where players/storytellers can explore complex emotions, questions about morality, ect. A simple Good vs Evil divide is anathema to that. Marduk, as described and from the incomplete draft I've read, fails at this, and I feel that the reason is worth its own bold header.<br /> <br /> <b>Do not dictate value judgments:</b> You, as a designer, have opinions about what the game is and how it should be played. You design the mechanics and the lore to suggest that. However, it is up to the players, not you, not even the storyteller, to decide what they take away from that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=667942#post667942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the core question of Leviathan is &quot;you are a monster who should commit suicide. You don't kill yourself, explore why you don't and how you justify that decision&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't get to dictate that. Not in a system designed to promote mature storytelling. You can design the rules to suggest it, and I think that Leviathan's mechanics do a pretty good job at that. The treatment of Marduk does not. It presents a foregone value judgement <i>on the part of the game designer</i> rather than a question to be asked and explored.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd say in summary that what we want from Marduk is something more mature and nuanced, something that can be used out of the box to tell interesting stories and acknowledges the complexity of the human condition. I'd suggest drawing on a mix of Princess and Genius. Let them be good people who can't decide or agree which way forward (or even what constitutes &quot;forward&quot;) is best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","user":"Thamuzz","date":". 09-17-2015, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T05:35:52-07:00","id":668102,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> E..even a low-level Leviathan can turn a whole town, <b>any </b>town, into Innsmouth?!<br /> OK, these guys scare the daylight out of me. Congratulations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T05:48:32-07:00","id":668113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668102#post668102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> E..even a low-level Leviathan can turn a whole town, <b>any </b>town, into Innsmouth?!<br /> OK, these guys scare the daylight out of me. Congratulations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not so much <i>can</i>, more eventually <i>will</i>. Whether they want to or not.<br /> <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=664868#post664868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Semi-relevant reading material from the SCP foundation :<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2662\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2662</a></div> </div> </div> </div>So, I'd basically describe 2662 as a mixture of Nu/Oceanid with waaaaay too many purchases of Deep Wake* with a sadistic ST who keeps throwing Rogue Cults his way.<br /> <br /> *yes yes yes, you can only take that once, but its a good way to represent how in over his head the poor bastard is. Actually... a condition that inflicted a wider wake without the power to utilize it might be interesting, possibly connected to Euphronia degredation. Probably be too easy to abuse, particularly with Sanctity channels and the number of things that rely on the Wake to define their range. Perhaps a secondary Wake that has all the drawbacks, none of the benefits, and a larger radius? <hr /><br /> Looking at the cult rules (I can't access google docs from where I am, otherwise I would put this there), I think there is a conflict between mechanics and theme when it comes to piety. As it stands, at Piety 1, your cultists are explicitly described as being able to function more or less normally when they are away from you/not doing your biding. I think that undercuts the harmful effect the Wake/being a Beloved is supposed to have. Maybe bump the &quot;they can function in society&quot; up to a Piety 2 perk? Piety 3 if you are feeling sadistic, and want to emphasis how damaged your cultists are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","user":"Thamuzz","date":". 09-17-2015, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T06:28:21-07:00","id":668163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668057#post668057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this doesn't satisfy people's desire to strip away civilisation, reason and morality then I don't know what will. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Call of the Depths (Descendant Channel)</span></span></b><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Finally some updated channels - Call of the Depths always seemed a little lackluster in it's former incarnation. The only potential problem is that it seems to be encroaching somewhat on Besieging the Tower of Will with it's Depth 3 ability to issue direct commands. It's also pretty damn powerful, the ability to exert such control over a potentially large group to that degree seems lower than Depth 3 to me. Perhaps replace it with the ability the ability to implant more vague ideas rather than direct commands? 'The waterfront is safe' rather than 'Come to the watefront'. 'All outsiders are enemies' rather than just 'kill them all' - it remains a very powerful tool but a little less predictable and fine-tuned, with individuals reacting to threats/ concepts in different ways. Works well with the chaotic 'stripping away reason' aspect. All this assuming that BtToW is still extant as a channel.<br /> <br /> Actually, this channel seems fairly powerful in general. 100 yards per Sheol in Depth 1, where the 1ed Channel was only within standard voice range. Are lower depth powers receiving a general boost?<br /> <br /> EDIT : You also haven't specified whether targets can spend a willpower point to avoid its effects for a turn as in the pervious version.<br /> <br /> This is probably a good time to express my dislike of the birthrights. I know this will probably be an unpopular opinion but I don't like them, I don't think a Depth 0 Leviathan should have access to any supernatural powers save the wake (and rituals) without transforming. The Birthright powers seem sort of ... clumsy, as though they were implemented to appease some people who had difficulty with the Transformation based abilities and would be better merged with some low depth channel abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","user":"Opprobrium","date":". 09-19-2015, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","name":"Opprobrium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T07:22:23-07:00","id":668226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668101#post668101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Cat and mouse: Players must deal with Marduk scouts. &lt;== There could be some potential there, depending on how the game goes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Marduk is designed around cat and mouse - as was made clear in the Aventurer and the Army section. You seem to have overlooked how that section ties into the themes of progress.<br /> <br /> Namely that Marduk use social influence to &quot;stress a Leviathan out of hiding&quot;. This emphasises how a Leviathan has been made obsolete by progress. The problems their powers can solve mostly don't exist any more, and the modern problems Marduk create for them are things their powers aren't suited for. If Marduk shuts down your bank account, turning into Godzilla won't help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668101#post668101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. I wanna punch them in their stupid perfect faces. &lt;== This is the first one that has really has the potential to display the themes out of the box, but it requires the players to have a reason to be resentful of Marduk</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is why I made Marduk's core tactics give players a reason to be resentful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668101#post668101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;what does better actually <i>mean?</i>&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was thinking of longer life expectency, better medicine. Combat with court cases and words instead of swords. You know, the basic stuff that most people agree is good. Though other people might have different ideas and that's fine by me. You could change what Marduk and the old Marduk conspiracy actually believed quite easily (it's mostly left undefined anyway) and it should still work.<br /> <br /> Mostly. Princess is the game where you debate what &quot;better&quot; actually means. In Leviathan the details of progress is are less important. You're not exploring progress itself but the effect progress has on people. Specifically on Leviathans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668101#post668101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want Marduk to be an interesting beastick, then give a single answer, and be aware that you a diluting the theme of Progress.</div> </div> </div> </div> Since Marduk and the Leviathans are fighting, a single answer would be how conflict has changed to be less harmful, more managed, and often with lawyers not swords. Reflected by Marduk's use of soft weapons to stress the Leviathan and their unwillingness to kill cultists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668102#post668102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> E..even a low-level Leviathan can turn a whole town, <b>any </b>town, into Innsmouth?!<br /> OK, these guys scare the daylight out of me. Congratulations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> BTW do you think the ranges on the updated Wake and on Call of the Depths are good? Since I don't have playtesters I just picked some numbers out of thin air.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668113#post668113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much <i>can</i>, more eventually <i>will</i>. Whether they want to or not.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes indeed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Same question too you. What do you think of the new range numbers for Wake and Call of the Depths.<br /> <br /> So, I'd basically describe 2662 as a mixture of Nu/Oceanid with waaaaay too many purchases of Deep Wake* with a sadistic ST who keeps throwing Rogue Cults his way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668113#post668113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Perhaps a secondary Wake that has all the drawbacks, none of the benefits, and a larger radius?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not too keen on this. Just from an in setting POV I don't see how you could seperate out the good and the bad parts of the Wake. That said Conditions that make bad things happen in your Wake and cause you trouble could be great fun.<br /> <br /> For example, a paranoid Leviathan might start causing Rift Creatures to emerge into Earth and start attacking him - he believes he has enemies everywhere, and so he creates those enemies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668113#post668113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the cult rules (I can't access google docs from where I am, otherwise I would put this there), I think there is a conflict between mechanics and theme when it comes to piety. As it stands, at Piety 1, your cultists are explicitly described as being able to function more or less normally when they are away from you/not doing your biding.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason for that. Which was to allow players to not have to constantly worry about boring stuff like finding food and shelter for their cultists too sleep in.<br /> <br /> It's not like this is a core part of the game. If anything it's the opposite, the themes imply a Leviathan will have to worry about feeding and housing cultists (and be very frustrated by it). It just struck me as a good time to bend the rules a bit. Imagine a Vampire ST who insisted on roleplaying out every single feeding rather than just the <i>interesting</i> ones.<br /> <br /> What does the floor think? If people feel differently I'll change that one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668163#post668163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally some updated channels - Call of the Depths always seemed a little lackluster in it's former incarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah. You're not wrong there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668163#post668163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only potential problem is that it seems to be uncroaching somewhat on Besieging the Tower of Will with it's Depth 3 ability to issue direct commands.</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't worry, I've got this covered. 2E Tower of Will will allow you to do very complex commands with extended durations.<br /> <br /> Want to tell the security guard to unlock the door next Tuesday at 2AM, that's Tower of Will. Probably 1 Ichor = a complex command that is obeyed for the remainder of the scene. 2 Ichor = a complex command that is triggered at a later point. 4 Ichor = completely repalce somebody's personality as desired.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668163#post668163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's also pretty damn powerful, the ability to exert such control over a potentially large group to that degree seems lower than Depth 3 to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> No to vague ideas<br /> <br /> But I could swap the Depth 3 and 6 versions around; but it just seems a bit too inflexible to have an entire Channel that only freezes people until Apotheosis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668163#post668163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT : You also haven't specified whether targets can spend a willpower point to avoid its effects for a turn as in the pervious version.</div> </div> </div> </div> They can't. That's why that bit's been removed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668163#post668163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably a good time to express my dislike of the birthrights.</div> </div> </div> </div> I have no idea if your theory about the origins of Birthrights is correct; but I don't dislike them myself. But perhaps, my dislike is less strong as you think <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Removing Birthrights is easy, so right now I'd try to think of better and more thematic ones first and remove them later if we can. I mean, I completely agree that the current powers are clumsy. But I still have hope better ones can exist<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668163#post668163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, this channel seems fairly powerful in general. 100 yards per Sheol in Depth 1, where the 1ed Channel was only within standard voice range. Are lower depth powers receiving a general boost?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. 2E is generally a higher power level than 1E.<br /> <br /> The weather stuff is powerful enough already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-17-2015, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:19:02-07:00","id":668345,"title":"","content":"Mmmmm... By the rules, how much can a Levi reduce his impact on the population, keeping them funcional enough to not attract too much unwanted attention?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:28:32-07:00","id":668355,"title":"","content":"Best solution, apart from limiting your contact to humanity, is to build a cult that limits your Beloved's self-destructive tendencies. In other words buy up Piety.<br /> <br /> Not everyone can be turned Beloved, at least not without intentional effort, so a Leviathan can live in a city without destroying it. But he will attract conflict and attention. In a small town that's probably going to quickly divide the town into cultists and everyone else, but in a city there's room for street gangs and other misfits without becoming the talk of the town. You just need to have a structure, some way to justify the cult's existence (preferably without calling it a cult) before you get too big.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not using your powers to incite the masses into a frenzy of destruction is always a good plan for the Leviathan on the down low.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:36:53-07:00","id":668364,"title":"","content":"A few ways of looking at it:<br /> 100 yards ~= 90 meters, which is roughly about 1 city block (quick lookup gave ~= 80 meters for a city block). If we situate a Leviathan in an apartment complex surrounded by other apartment complexes, each complex taking up 1 block. By in this setup, at Sheol 1, the Leviathan will have significant influence over 1 building, partial influence over 4 buildings and tangential influence over 4 more. At Sheol 2, near complete control over 1 building, significant control over eight buildings and tangential control over 16 buildings. At Sheol 5, pretty much complete influence over something like 80 or 90 buildings.<br /> <br /> Alternately, go by square km and population density:<br /> 100 yards <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Sheol</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Tijuana</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Random Small Town</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">~1200-1300 people (0.09%)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">~40 - 100 people</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">~2500-2600 people (0.19%)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">~60 - 120 people</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">~6000-7000 people (0.45%)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">~200 people.</td> </tr> </table></div> 500 yards <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Sheol</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Tijuana</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Random Small Town</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">~6000-7000 people (0.45%)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">~200 people.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">~12500-12600 people (0.96%)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">~340 people</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">~31700-31800 people (2.43%)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">~900 people.</td> </tr> </table></div> Command &quot;Riot&quot;:<br /> A quick look at wikipedia says that the 1992 LA riots led to about 11000 arrests, while the 2001 Cincinnati riots had a little under 1000 arrests.<br /> So a Sheol 1 Leviathan could definitely make the national news in the US with this in the US, or bog down an assailant in a smaller area.<br /> Command &quot;Give me five bucks&quot;:<br /> Sheol 1 Leviathan in a big city will walk away with ~$6000, ~$200-500 in a small town.<br /> Command &quot;Protest X&quot;:<br /> National news, although protest probably won't be as well organized as you might like. The omnipresent eldritch song might also detract from the effectiveness.<br /> Command &quot;Flush your toilet&quot;:<br /> Serious problems for a major city's water infrastructure. Small town, probably nothing.<br /> Command &quot;Kill X&quot;<br /> In a big city, for most X, X is dead, assuming they can't hide from the mob. Small town, serious inconvenience.<br /> Command &quot;Gather at X&quot;<br /> In a city, X is swamped like Time Square at new years. Small town, small crowd.<br /> <br /> How would using this in a noisy environment, like say, at a concert, work? That is to ask, could a clever player hide their hand by disguising their song as something else?<br /> I think it is overpowered as a standard action. At Sheol 1, Depth 1, a Leviathan could paralyze most of an Aircraft Carrier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","user":"Thamuzz","date":". 09-17-2015, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T09:57:37-07:00","id":668388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668021#post668021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires hate Leviathans because they're harbringers of chaos, and nothing ruins a good subtle web of influence and control like chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but how do Leviathans <i>taste</i>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668021#post668021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignore the technology side of demons. Demons are spies, not tech, and the Demon-Leviathan relationship should be built on that.<br /> <br /> Sadly most of the cool spy themes would hinge on Demons working for a higher power that might have an <i>interest</i> in a Leviathan and their cult. Demons don't, so I'm not sure what to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple: Leviathan cults may or may not be G-M influenced, and that bares investigation. Or the Demon in question is hired by another power. They can be subcontracted (and/or blackmailed). And they can infiltrate (and potentially subvert) a cult nicely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668021#post668021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any thought put into the Marduk Society's relation to other splats would be just for fun. But it is fun, so think away <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This far though, my crossover thoughts have all been about the Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it depends how well Marduk handles Prometheans the heal from their lightning guns, Vampires and Mages that can suborn their agents, and Demon's hacking their systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:24:58-07:00","id":668619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668021#post668021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignore the technology side of demons. Demons are spies, not tech, and the Demon-Leviathan relationship should be built on that.<br /> <br /> Sadly most of the cool spy themes would hinge on Demons working for a higher power that might have an <i>interest</i> in a Leviathan and their cult. Demons don't, so I'm not sure what to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if this is or isn't a wasted opportunity - when I look at Demon/Leviathan interactions, I see the possibility for something glorious, something wonderful, something terrifying.<br /> <br /> If Leviathans represent the bloody past that progress has pulled us out of, then Demons represent the potential evils of progress unchecked. They are literally the principle of the soulless, coldly logical destructive machine made manifest in flesh and steel and data and bone. And, through this twisted yin-yang resemblance, they have uses for each other.<br /> <br /> <u>Inquisitors</u> have the hope that Tribe has secrets from before the God-Machine was born hidden away in their racial lore, in their cult's practices and their very blood. Such secrets could be useful to finding Hell.<br /> <br /> <u>Temptors</u> want something simple from humanity: it's most basic, simple of pleasures. They crave the pleasures of the flesh, the satisfaction of the lizard-brain in all its many forms. A Leviathan's cult could easily be a Temptor's private Hell.<br /> <br /> <u>Saboteurs</u> are the simplest and most direct. In a Saboteur's eyes, a Leviathan represents a perfect ally - or at least a perfect weapon - against the God Machine. With the combination of the Demon's Brain and the Leviathan's Brawn, all things can be rent asunder.<br /> <br /> Leviathans, meanwhile, have something more simple to gain from Demonic alliances: Hope. Demons, with their flat immunity to all psychic effects, offer the possibility for real companionship. Demons offer comfort, the ability to better reassure Leviathans that they aren't wrong to survive and that they have their place. They offer a target for Leviathan frustration and hate with the world - the God-Machine is so easy to demonize as being worse for this world than the Tribe ever was, and it's so feasible that if they could smash it all, then all this awful, awkward civilization would just GO AWAY. Moreover, Demons are strong in ways that Leviathans are weak. The &quot;soft combat&quot; that the Marduk Society likes to use to soften up the Tribe can be negated and turned against them by entities who can literally hack society in their sleep.<br /> <br /> Demon/Leviathan convergence is a Match made in Hell. So what if it often ends with the Demon secretly manipulating or controlling the Leviathan, turning them to its own ends? That's just the way it is. Some Leviathans may know that they are the subordinates in the relationship... and be perfectly happy with it. A place as a well-treated pet is better than no place at all, after all.<br /> <br /> Picture it. <br /> <br /> A Marduk cell begins its standard operating procedure against a Leviathan... but everything goes wrong. Their credit manipulation fails and gets them traced as hackers. Attempts to manipulate the system turn against them. And then, one night, the door to their hideout is torn open as a half-man half-monster backed by red-eyed cultists swarms in, catching them off-guard. And their guns stop working right, misfiring, aiming wrong. They are torn apart. And the last thing they see is the amused smile of a man whose empty eyes are filled with streams of whirling, neon-green 0s and 1s.<br /> <br /> A Hunter-Angel tears through the doors guarding its quarry, intent on slaying another Demon that would defy the God-Machine. And then the curvaceous whore at its target side roars and tears apart, a squamous, piscine horror of muscle and maw erupting into being. Teeth of razored bone close down on the Angel, devouring it effortlessly as an old goddess protects her new consort.<br /> <br /> It's very easy for Demons to manipulate Leviathans, simply by doing what they do best: covert infiltration. Assume a mortal form, work its way into a Cult, stand out by knowing how to tell a Leviathan what it truly wants to hear, win its grace as a Beloved who <i>isn't</i> a brainwashed (censored) idiot, and then play the Leviathan for the Demon's own ends. Perhaps even a mutual respect can be earned.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but I see a lot of possibility for Demon/Leviathan crossover. They're just too much yin-yang when I look at them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668021#post668021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any thought put into the Marduk Society's relation to other splats would be just for fun. But it is fun, so think away <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Offer accepted. For this exercise, I will be going under the presumption that Marduk Society may be more <i>virtuous</i> than the norm for the WoD, but that does <b>not</b> make them more <i>powerful</i>. You cannot be all about &quot;the way reason makes us better human beings&quot; <b>and</b> still be the ultimate fighters. A truly &quot;good man&quot; will not use weapons or tactics that bad men will. Marduk Society cares about collateral damage, cares about civil rights, cares about law and justice in a way even other Hunters don't (or reluctantly accept that they can't, not and be effective). In a cynical, grimdark setting like The World of Darkness, being The White Hat WILL hurt. If it was easy, it wouldn't BE so rare to be a White Hat in this game.<br /> <br /> <u>Vampires</u> tend to roll their eyes at the Marduk Society. Their hopelessly optimistic outlook and idealism scream &quot;weakness&quot; in a vampire's eyes anyway, but when they bring that into the socio-political arena, where vampires are masters? ...The phrase &quot;lambs to the slaughter&quot; comes to mind. Vampires do have a tendency to stagnate with age, but fresh embraces and Torpor allow them to regularly &quot;shake things up&quot; and keep them up to the curve, so the tactics that work so well against Leviathans are easily countered and deflected. In actual combat, Marduk tends to be at a disadvantage; they <i>have</i> flamethrower tech, but it's rarely deployed in the field since, y'know, Leviathans are mostly indifferent to fire and flame weaponry is considered a War Crime by civilised people and so Marduk is squeamish about using it. Which is bad news for the agent trying to fight a super-fast, super-strong bloodsucking monster who shrugs off bullets and lightning bolts alike as if they were spitballs. Fortunately for both sides, vampires rarely make the kind of waves that the Marduk Society is trained to look for, meaning they are usually ignored and so are content to ignore Marduk right back. No sense in picking a fight unnecessarily.<br /> <br /> \u200b<u>Werewolves</u> give the Marduk Society a feeling of unease. There's so many similarities there to Leviathans... but at the same time, the differences are critical, and have led to disaster for more than one hunting group. The idea that werewolves might be a branch of the Tribe that has managed to shake off some of its stagnation and evolve - symbolically represented by their land-animal nature rather than their sea-animal nature - is a nightmarish one. They rage like Leviathans, but they can strike through the same angles that the Marduk Society normally uses to prosecute them. And whereas Leviathans tend to be solitary, werewolves are <b>always</b> found together. The Iron Masters tribe, in particular, has a love-hate relationship with the Marduk Society; they envy the progress of Marduk's technology and strive to be more like them, but at the same time, Marduk keeps trying to kill them. Standard operating procedure for Marduk is to pull out and back away if the &quot;Leviathans&quot; they are after display the ability to effectively counter their social and technological warfare. This keeps them from being the subject of too many Iron Master-led hunts... because those often don't end well for the Society. It's not <i>fair</i> when the enemy can make your computers, your vehicles, every city utility and even the terrain itself want to kill you... or when they can get around any barrier you can create by sliding into some other dimension and out again....<br /> <br /> \u200b<u>Mages</u> puzzle the Marduk Society greatly. On the one hand, their powers are demonstrably real - there's a difference between skepticism and stupidity, and insisting that the man who just <i>caught your lightning gun's shot in one hand and threw it back at you</i> did it with smoke and mirrors leans towards the latter. On the other hand, their ideology sounds like primitive, backwards superstitions, running completely contrary to the Society's philosophy of reason and logic. Fortunately, they rarely cross paths, as mages tend to avoid the wide-scale and obvious disruptions of the Leviathans, and the Society has nothing mages generally want. That said, the Free League <b>adores</b> the Society, who seem to be living proof of their own ideology about humanity's inner nature being inherently magical, and it's not unheard of for them to secretly protect or support Marduk cells.<br /> <br /> \u200b<u>Prometheans</u> elicit a potent cocktail of guilt, shame, and fear amongst the Marduk Society. Like Leviathans, prometheans disrupt the fabric of the world around them, socially and physically, with their very presence. Even Marduk, who tries to live up to the ideals of humanity's better nature, can't resist this &quot;Disquiet&quot;, and that fills them with shame and guilt, especially since they have studied prometheans from a distance and seen they generally don't want anything but the simple courtesies and rights every human takes for granted. Of course, since prometheans feed on lightning and live off of the grid anyway, Marduk's efforts to fight them almost never go the Society's way. It's fortunate indeed that prometheans are rare as a general rule and especially that they aren't allied with leviathans, as they excel as anti-Marduk shock troopers.<br /> <br /> \u200b<u>Changelings</u> and Marduk are pretty much oblivious to each other. With Marduk being focused on the big, splashy presence of Leviathans, Changelings just sort of slip by unnoticed. Things almost never go well for the Society if it does get involved: although their idealism means they hate the idea of breaking their word, allowing them some protection against breaking pledges, their tendency to politely disdain &quot;superstitious nonsense&quot; means they get whammied <b>hard</b> when they unthinkingly cross a line that shouldn't be crossed.<br /> <br /> \u200b<u>Sineaters</u> scorn the Marduk Society as absolutely everything they hate about hunters in general; that self-righteous confidence, that idealistic overenthusiasm, that persistence in meddling in affairs where they don't belong because they trust SCIENCE! can solve everything. A typical sineater attitude is that Marduk is like a great, big, untrained, overenthusiastic puppy - comes barging in knocking things over and pissing everywhere and is too dim to understand why you get mad at them for messing things up.<br /> <br /> \u200b<u>Mummies</u> might almost be Enemy #2 in the eyes of the Marduk Society. Like the Leviathans, mummies can cause tremendous destruction wherever they go, and are living relics of the bloody past that Marduk embodies moving away from... worse, they are often surprisingly adaptable to modern society. It infuriates the Society when they hear the cynical commentary from mummies that, for all its fancy new gadgets and baubles, human nature hasn't changed in the slightest, and that the core of the world now is no different than the Bronze Age they originally lived in.<br /> <br /> \u200b<u>Demons</u> horrify the Marduk Society, distorting everything they believe about the purity of reason and the power of technology. Worse, they're almost impossible for the Society to effectively counter. Demons can hide in plain sight, being almost impossible to winkle out of hiding, and effortlessly hide again. Worse still, they can manipulate technology on a level even the Society doesn't understand, making the &quot;social warfare&quot; of the Society pretty much useless. A demon can outhack and outcode any human technology - hell, a Dataform demon sufficiently provoked could probably ride a communication signal up to one of Marduk's satellite bases and proceed to destroy everything on that station's network, if not manifesting in its true form and destroying the whole base.<br /> <br /> If this makes it sound like the Marduk Society is pretty out of its depth in the World of Darkness... that's because, realistically, they <b>ARE</b>. <br /> <br /> White Hatting in a world <b>built</b> on a basis of Black and Gray Morality is inherently costly. Being good is <b>HARD</b> - it wouldn't be the World of Darkness if that weren't the case.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Marduk Society is a very &quot;niche&quot; hunter group. They excel at taking down Leviathans - no other Conspiracy can hope to match them on that front. But it means their tactics, their arsenal, everything they have, is specifically geared towards fighting Leviathans. Entirely different beasts present entirely different problems, and whilst Marduk <b>could</b> adapt, the trick is surviving long enough to do so. The difference between trolling a Leviathan by erasing its bank account and doing the same to a Werewolf is that the latter can talk to spirits and find out <b>exactly</b> who did it, gather her buddies, jump into the Shadow, then pop out of it in the middle of your safehouse primed and ready to rip you into little pieces. Combine that unprecedented assault, with the fact you aren't going to have the specialized weapons you need to kill werewolves effectively, and... well, it's not pretty.<br /> <br /> This is a problem all niche conspiracies have in Hunter as it is. The corebook conspiracies are broadly natured for a reason, because they go after everything. Groups like Les Mysteres or The Cainite Heresy go after specific quarry, so they're less effective when out of their field. It's nothing against Marduk, it's just what happens - the inherent problem with specialization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:48:08-07:00","id":668673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668226#post668226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why I made Marduk's core tactics give players a reason to be resentful.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've previously established that Leviathans don't deserve to be alive, and Marduk is an organization whose flaws are encapsulated by &quot;hasn't won yet,&quot; right? As-is, I'd imagine that players would find it difficult to resent Marduk because, well, they're being constantly reminded that their characters are Atrocious Monsters who should've died out ages ago and their enemies are the Good People whose moral duty is to conquer the world.<br /> <br /> Remember, &quot;progress&quot; doesn't have just one meaning. Your &quot;ethically run corporation&quot; Marduk is still a participant in capitalism; for that reason, there is a not inconsiderable swathe of the human population which feels that that Marduk doesn't deserve to exist. Some would say that no singular organization can be trusted with killsats, especially one that hides its activities and doesn't submit to government regulations -- and progress enabled Marduk to do exactly that. The progress of science gave us nuclear weapons, the capacity to annihilate human society, and dissimilar rates of progress allowed for scientific racism and unethical experimentation, as well as imperialism powered by uneven technology levels. Scientific progress isn't just a bunch of benefits that go up all the time -- Marduk as an unalloyed good, and one that has, apparently, peaked in the year 2015/&quot;the present day,&quot; is both a poor tool for generating gameplay and a poor representation of progress and reason, both of which are ethically neutral. Progress is only a good thing when it is used to support good values, and reason is only a good thing when one has good premises; if Marduk is going to be a representative of Progress and Reason and Growth instead of a Principle of Goodness with very little depth, then it needs more ambiguity, or, at the very least, shouldn't be a perfectly noble organization with all its negative influences purged and nowhere to go but up.<br /> <br /> (Research also shows that nomadic hunter/gatherers were, by and large, much happier than agriculturalists; in that situation, better lifespans and more control -- progress -- reduced net lifestyle happiness. How's that for progress?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was thinking of longer life expectency, better medicine. Combat with court cases and words instead of swords. You know, the basic stuff that most people agree is good. Though other people might have different ideas and that's fine by me. You could change what Marduk and the old Marduk conspiracy actually believed quite easily (it's mostly left undefined anyway) and it should still work. </div> </div> </div>That's not quite the complaint, I think; Marduk's beliefs don't quite matter if they're in the current framework, whose tactics and actions are very carefully delineated according to your personal morals and understanding of progress.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since Marduk and the Leviathans are fighting, a single answer would be how conflict has changed to be less harmful, more managed, and often with lawyers not swords. Reflected by Marduk's use of soft weapons to stress the Leviathan and their unwillingness to kill cultists. </div> </div> </div>I think you've misunderstood Thamuzz's comment. Being an &quot;interesting beatstick&quot; is, in fact, a bad thing; players don't want a single answer, because it restricts the use of the game to tell stories. <br /> <br /> Vampire doesn't give a definitive answer as to whether Golconda is a real thing, even though &quot;redemption&quot; doesn't seem to fit with the &quot;decaying humanity&quot; theme; that's because &quot;Golconda is definitely a myth that vampires tell themselves because they miss humanity&quot; is a boring answer, whether or not it's thematic. Likewise here: if Marduk's character is carefully and clearly delineated (should the WoD really use the phrase &quot;good guys&quot; or the concept of evil? &quot;Idealist faction&quot; might be better -- it doesn't imply the impossibility of their erring, morally), then you really narrow the stories you can tell with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mostly. Princess is the game where you debate what &quot;better&quot; actually means. In Leviathan the details of progress is are less important. You're not exploring progress itself but the effect progress has on people. Specifically on Leviathans. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Asking complex questions about the themes&quot; isn't limited to a single game line. Promethean asks about the worth and the meaning of &quot;humanity&quot; and the nature of condemnation; Vampire asks us to consider the plight of the monster and what happens to morality in the face of overwhelming need; Mage wants to talk about hubris, whether lofty goals justify compromises of one's own soul, and whether &quot;hubris&quot; is a meaningful term in a Fallen World that people are intentionally grinding into the dirt. None of these supplies definite answers. This is why they are interesting, thematically. As is, Marduk is asking and answering Leviathan's core question, and it's using only one answer: &quot;What is the nature of progress?&quot; &quot;It is an unalloyed good that will save humanity.&quot; &quot;How does progress affect people who can't adjust?&quot; &quot;They can't win or achieve any meaningful victories with their outdated methods, and will ultimately be stamped out.&quot;<br /> <br /> Games don't answer questions; they just ask them, and the players and ST answer.<br /> <br /> (Also, remember: Leviathan is a game. As in, a game which will be played by people who aren't you. If a bunch of people object to your current portrayal of the setting on the grounds that they don't want to play with it or feel that it makes play less interesting/fun for them, defending and refusing to alter that portrayal in any way isn't constructive. Listen to MB -- I've been following your homebrewing projects, and you do, in fact, tend to fall in love with ideas and then refuse to change them for any reason. It's important to listen to your players and other people who comment on and develop the game, and to compromise with them -- that's how good games get made.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:19:55-07:00","id":668737,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on integrating the GMC Supernatural merits as Hybrid Mutations? Basically, allowing mutations with the same name, but (optionally) use Ichor instead. This pads out the Mutations, confers topical abilities and options, and lets you &quot;spend&quot; points on them as mutations instead of merits (for when enforcing Vestiges affinities is important).<ul><li>Awareness:<ul><li>Cursed* \u2022\u2022: As the merit [in GMC 172].</li> <li>Aura Reading* \u2022\u2022\u2022: As the merit [in GMC 172], but the Hybrid spends Ichor instead.</li> <li>Clairvoyance* \u2022\u2022\u2022: As the merit [in GMC 172], but the Hybrid spends Ichor instead.</li> </ul></li> <li>Elements:<ul><li>Hydrokinesis* \u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: As the merit Psychokinesis [in GMC 173], but the Hybrid spends Ichor instead. (though a medium dependent Telekinesis makes more sense...)</li> </ul></li> <li>Might:<ul><li>Telekinesis* \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: As the merit [in GMC 174], but the Hybrid spends Ichor instead.</li> </ul></li> <li>Sanctity:<ul><li>Telepathy* \u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: As the merit [in GMC 175], but the Hybrid spends Ichor instead.</li> </ul></li> <li>Vitality:<ul><li>Biokinesis* \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: As the merit [in GMC 172], but the Hybrid spends Ichor instead.</li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-17-2015, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:36:20-07:00","id":668757,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, Marduk is supposed to be resented by the Leviathans for the same reasons Homer Simpson resents Ned Flanders. Flanders is pious, devoted, kindly, and physically fit <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(stupid sexy Flanders...)<span style=\"font-size:12px\">, all things Homer can't or won't achieve. Leviathans are jealous of these little apes because they grow.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:44:17-07:00","id":668762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668757#post668757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it, Marduk is supposed to be resented by the Leviathans for the same reasons Homer Simpson resents Ned Flanders. Flanders is pious, devoted, kindly, and physically fit <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(stupid sexy Flanders...)<span style=\"font-size:12px\">, all things Homer can't or won't achieve. Leviathans are jealous of these little apes because they grow.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm sure the attempted genocide is just a minor annoyance, right? I mean, either it's the group that wants to dine on your sweet meats, or the one that merely decided &quot;oh, you were born with the wrong genetics, and now you need to die&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T14:10:41-07:00","id":668784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668364#post668364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few ways of looking at it:</div> </div> </div> </div> Oooh. Numbers, they're pretty.<br /> <br /> Going by this. I'm tempted to just go through and halve the range of Call of the Depths. I should probably add in an the ability to intentionally hold back. At a few dots of Sheol though you'll still rappidly get into the range of - you're power is only limited by the consiquences. And I'm ok with that. Freshly awoken Mummies don't have similar epic abilities from charachter creation, so Leviathans get them too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668364#post668364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Command &quot;Kill X&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As a quick note. This won't work unless X is famous. &quot;Kill the vampire prince&quot; would just leave people wondering around in confusion. Kill the Queen of England would work though; but again it would have consiquences. And who knows, maybe the British Government has some really nasty defences against Leviathans up and running just waiting for a player to stumble into them. It is St Geroge's patron nation after all<br /> <br /> Still. Some really creative and devious uses there. I approve of your wicked mind and don't envy the Storyteller who<br /> <br /> In a big city, for most X, X is dead, assuming they can't hide from the mob. Small town, serious inconvenience.<br /> Command &quot;Gather at X&quot;<br /> In a city, X is swamped like Time Square at new years. Small town, small crowd.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668364#post668364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would using this in a noisy environment, like say, at a concert, work? That is to ask, could a clever player hide their hand by disguising their song as something else?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd say no. If you can't hear it you're immune, it still requires sound, it's just that singing really really loudly is part of the power. And it's obviously inhuman and unnatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668364#post668364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is overpowered as a standard action. At Sheol 1, Depth 1, a Leviathan could paralyze most of an Aircraft Carrier.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here we run smack into one of the big problems with WoD balancing. Mortals have practically no defence against psychic attacks of any kind. No matter how much guns and armour you give them, 1 dot of Obsucificate or Call of the Depths and they're powerless.<br /> <br /> I don't like it. I want regular mortals to be a danger supernaturals must avoid along the lines of Unkown Armies' Sleeping Tiger. But they're not and without a major change to the WoD's core mechanics there's nothing you can really do about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668388#post668388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but how do Leviathans <i>taste</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div> For all their wickedness Leviathans are gods of Fecundity. They inherit the power that gave birth to all creations, the power of Life itself.<br /> <br /> In other words. Drinking Leviathan blood will, temporally, make Vampires essentially alive again. Able to grow, to change.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately these are still Leviathans we're talking about. So quite often &quot;grow&quot; actually means &quot;grow out of control&quot;, in other words Leviathan blood gives Vampire's cancer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But there's probably at least one Bloodline that formed spontaniously from a sip of Leviathan blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668388#post668388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple: Leviathan cults may or may not be G-M influenced, and that bares investigation. Or the Demon in question is hired by another power. They can be subcontracted (and/or blackmailed). And they can infiltrate (and potentially subvert) a cult nicely.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, but why would they stay after they figure out that it's not G-M influenced?<br /> <br /> As for the other powers that might hire a Demon - now the question becomes who's that power and what do <i>they</i> think of Leviathans?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668619#post668619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this is or isn't a wasted opportunity - when I look at Demon/Leviathan interactions, I see the possibility for something glorious, something wonderful, something terrifying.<br /> <br /> If Leviathans represent the bloody past that progress has pulled us out of, then Demons represent the potential evils of progress unchecked.</div> </div> </div> </div> No.<br /> <br /> No no no no.<br /> <br /> <br /> The evils of Progress Unchecked has nothing to do with Demon and it's spy stories.<br /> <br /> Progress unchecked is Genius: the Transgression <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Specifically it's the International Union of Artifice. Read their splat section, they're explicitly the fear of progress unchecked. Sometimes fears are unfounded, but given that this is Genius most of the time they're probably quite realistic fears.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand your team up metaphor looks nice. Leviathans as terrorists fits neatly as a metaphor with demons as spies. Your intelligent agents going rogue and helping the terrorists is every chief intelligence officer's worst nightmare after all.<br /> <br /> BTW. Did you ever read my homebrew Demon Agenda: Trators? It's linked in my sig.<br /> <hr /><br /> It looks like you had a lot of fun writing Marduk vs others. I won't respond to every point, but as a general thing, you're forgetting that just because Marduk fight <u>nice</u> doesn't mean they fight <u>fair</u>. Marduk's favourite fighting strategy is to remain too far above their opponents for them to shoot back. Wheather that means in jets, in orbit or just using jetpacks and hovering 15 foot up (ok, most supernaturals need more than 15 feet, but Marduk can fly higher).<br /> <br /> Take vampires. Vampires won't have a big advantage because they're superfast and bullet proof. They'll have an advantage because they'll send wave after wave of brainwashed pawns at Marduk, possibly in large suicide vests, and basically force Marduk to choose between killing civilians or abandoning their safehouses.<br /> <br /> Unlike Leviathans, who have the unique disadvantage of being 30 stories tall and psychically broadcast NOTICE ME! vampires are very very good at hiding. If Marduk wants to wait for the vampire to expose himself - they might be waiting a very long time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668619#post668619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<u>Mummies</u> might almost be Enemy #2</div> </div> </div> </div>They sure are. <br /> <br /> Fun fact: I had plans to write a group of Hunters who oppose Mummies and serve as their foils. They were a group of politicians in the European Union and (mostly) highly committeed to further European integration.<br /> <br /> The core idea was an &quot;empire&quot; built by diplomacy to be a foil to Irem's empire of conquest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668619#post668619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, the Marduk Society is a very &quot;niche&quot; hunter group. They excel at taking down Leviathans - no other Conspiracy can hope to match them on that front. But it means their tactics, their arsenal, everything they have, is specifically geared towards fighting Leviathans.</div> </div> </div> </div> No argument from me here.<br /> <br /> Orbital weapons sound nice, but lets face it. You're unlikely to even hit anything smaller than an aircraft carrier or a Leviathan. Unless the Marduk Society is willing to open up their orbitals guns and make them fire area effect shots most of their best guns are useless against most monsters.<br /> <br /> They are designed as a specalist group and specalising, as you say, has it's disadvantages.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ultimately though it's hard to really say how Marduk would do against different monsters because in the end anyone can just make up new devices for them on the spot. Orbital mirrors or sunlight bulbs against vampires? Bombs that only affect Spirits or part spirit beings against Werewolves? I'm going too obviously, but that's because vampires and werewolves sort of don't exist in Leviathan's setting. In a crossover setting where they do, Storyteller's choice.<br /> <br /> But it looks like you had some fun. That's the important part <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668737#post668737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts on integrating the GMC Supernatural merits as Hybrid Mutations?</div> </div> </div> </div> Haven't gottent around to thinking of Hybrid Mutations, but *thinks quicky* good idea.<br /> <br /> I might give them a full write up or I might not. I will not repeat GMC core's mistake of making Telekinesis use Occult. If you want to be a better telekenetic you don't read some Crowley, you go into the gym and start practicing with your powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668757#post668757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it, Marduk is supposed to be resented by the Leviathans for the same reasons Homer Simpson resents Ned Flanders. Flanders is pious, devoted, kindly, and physically fit <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(stupid sexy Flanders...)<span style=\"font-size:12px\">, all things Homer can't or won't achieve. Leviathans are jealous of these little apes because they grow.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Correct <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Two tribes were thrown into the gutter when the Primordial world ended. One of them reached the stars, the other is jealous of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668762#post668762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm sure the attempted genocide is just a minor annoyance, right? I mean, either it's the group that wants to dine on your sweet meats, or the one that merely decided &quot;oh, you were born with the wrong genetics, and now you need to die&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Naturally Leviathans also resent Marduk for trying to kill them. But the only people who say it's because of the wrong genetics are Leviathans who're really really good at lieing to themselves. It's pretty rare for a Leviathan to honestly say they've never intentionally hurt everyone, it's all the Wake (lets pick a number out a hat and say it's as rare as Vampires who only drink animal blood).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T14:55:22-07:00","id":668849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668784#post668784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ultimately though it's hard to really say how Marduk would do against different monsters because in the end anyone can just make up new devices for them on the spot. Orbital mirrors or sunlight bulbs against vampires? Bombs that only affect Spirits or part spirit beings against Werewolves? I'm going too obviously, but that's because vampires and werewolves sort of don't exist in Leviathan's setting. In a crossover setting where they do, Storyteller's choice.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>... last I heard, the anti spirit bombs was something TF:V was experimenting with in terms of a city scale nuke. They also have anti spirit rounds, too.<br /> <br /> Also, is that permission Marduk should come around with mechanized battlesuits?<br /> <br /> Also, Void, can you do one for fansplats too? Like your work as that sums up how I also feel things would play out in a crossover setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 09-17-2015, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T14:58:10-07:00","id":668852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668849#post668849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... last I heard, the anti spirit bombs was something TF:V was experimenting with in terms of a city scale nuke. They also have anti spirit rounds, too.</div> </div> </div> </div> They are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668849#post668849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is that permission Marduk should come around with mechanized battlesuits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pacific Rim style?<br /> <br /> You don't need my permission for that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> though I tend to think of Marduk as fighting from the Sky. giant battlesuits is more of a Genius thing IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T15:08:37-07:00","id":668861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668852#post668852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pacific Rim style?<br /> <br /> You don't need my permission for that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> though I tend to think of Marduk as fighting from the Sky. giant battlesuits is more of a Genius thing IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>... You know, I would actually have rebuttaled with a more appropriate robot type to power level 1-5 play, since Pacific Rim robots are the kinda thing that uses Power Stat +6 level play, but then I kept trying to figure out a source you'd know... Uh Metal Gear's GEKKO units? ATAT's? Robocop's ED209? Mass Effect's Atlas units?<br /> <br /> But it's not like you can't attach rockets to robots, ya?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 09-17-2015, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T16:23:44-07:00","id":668956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668784#post668784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here we run smack into one of the big problems with WoD balancing. Mortals have practically no defence against psychic attacks of any kind. No matter how much guns and armour you give them, 1 dot of Obsucificate or Call of the Depths and they're powerless.<br /> <br /> I don't like it. I want regular mortals to be a danger supernaturals must avoid along the lines of Unkown Armies' Sleeping Tiger. But they're not and without a major change to the WoD's core mechanics there's nothing you can really do about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's always been understood that mortals are, individually, weak. It's <i>humanity</i> that you have to fear. Obsfucate is great to hide from one person, but may not work against all systems of monitoring (does it deceive laser tripwires, for instance?). And it doesn't shield against setting fire to the room someone vanished in. Call of the Deeps is powerful against all mortals in it's area, but artillery out ranges it, as do bombers. A human is weak in the way a red blood cell is weak. The immune system as a whole though, is nothing to treat lightly. As I understand it, <i>that</i> is where mortals are dangerous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668784#post668784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but why would they stay after they figure out that it's not G-M influenced?</div> </div> </div> </div>To make Pacts with the deranged and desperate. To manipulate them towards the Demon's goals. To use them as camouflage against the G-M agents. They're <i>Demons</i>, they'll find a use for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668784#post668784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the other powers that might hire a Demon - now the question becomes who's that power and what do <i>they</i> think of Leviathans?</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;shrug&gt; I was just pointing out more &quot;Demon's get involved&quot; hooks. And when combo'd with the Leviathan/Demon team-up assessment...<br /> What fun it would be if a Marduk cell hired Demons (likely, unknowingly) to investigate a Leviathan cult, only for the Ring to turn double agent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668784#post668784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might give them a full write up or I might not. I will not repeat GMC core's mistake of making Telekinesis use Occult. If you want to be a better telekenetic you don't read some Crowley, you go into the gym and start practicing with your powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say science (understanding physics would help, I'd think), but Occult was likely just a catch-all. Not many skills directly relate moving things with your brain. (And adding Psychic-only skills is a bit much)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668784#post668784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Naturally Leviathans also resent Marduk for trying to kill them. But the only people who say it's because of the wrong genetics are Leviathans who're really really good at lieing to themselves. It's pretty rare for a Leviathan to honestly say they've never intentionally hurt everyone, it's all the Wake (lets pick a number out a hat and say it's as rare as Vampires who only drink animal blood).</div> </div> </div> </div>As presented, a fair number of neonates start that way. Time is lengthened by possessing Animalism. And Leviathans aren't supernaturally addicted to delibrately burning out someone's mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668861#post668861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... You know, I would actually have rebuttaled with a more appropriate robot type to power level 1-5 play, since Pacific Rim robots are the kinda thing that uses Power Stat +6 level play, but then I kept trying to figure out a source you'd know... Uh Metal Gear's GEKKO units? ATAT's? Robocop's ED209? Mass Effect's Atlas units?<br /> <br /> But it's not like you can't attach rockets to robots, ya?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fallout's Tesla Armor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-17-2015, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T16:31:45-07:00","id":668961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668849#post668849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Void, can you do one for fansplats too? Like your work as that sums up how I also feel things would play out in a crossover setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean a Marduk Society vs. Fansplats section? You really like my work that much? Well, I am flattered, but I don't really know that much about fansplats. I can give commentary on Geniuses and Princesses, from what little I know about them via overhearing, and also on Beasts now that I am forced to remember they exist, but beyond that...<br /> <br /> <u>Beasts</u> annoy the hell out of Marduk, for being an obvious branch of The Wicked Tribe who has the indecency to not &quot;play fair&quot; by staying in human-form all the time and having better control over their tempers, but still being obviously disruptive to the world around them and having the audacity to claim that their depredations are &quot;good for humanity&quot; somehow, even as they create an incredibly destructive form of Ahabs that seemingly can't be cured. What's worse is that, even though they are so obviously part of the Tribe, they somehow don't display any of the usual weaknesses.<br /> <br /> \u200b<u>Geniuses</u> <b><i>HATE</i></b> the Marduk Society. Hate it madly, with a blinding passion. Hate it with an intensity that sees A.M being quoted. The reasoning is so very simple. Take the seething resentment of the socially awkward nerd for the popular, beloved school-jock. Mix with the frustrated fury of a scientist who has been laboring in obscurity and sees others claiming accolades and fame that should <b>rightfully</b> be his, succeeding at <b>his</b> experiments. Spice with all-consuming, sanity-blinding intensity of the archetypical mad scientist. And you have some understanding of why Geniuses hate the Marduk Society, for taking the role that <b>should</b> be theirs, for having devices that work. The Peerage struggles to keep that resentment under control, and does its best to avoid the Society. But those who won't be part of the Peerage, like the Lemurians, and sometimes even members of the Peerage who just <i>snap</i> and can't take it anymore, go after the Society. And then <b>everybody</b> in the vicinity loses. The Marduk Society doesn't understand Geniuses - indeed, by virtue of their own mentality, they <b>cannot</b> understand what drives the Geniuses, and especially what drives their sheer, unadulterated, pure hatred of the Society. Standing orders for the Society is to vacate, to not give Geniuses the attention or the confrontation they crave. If needs must, Marduk is willing to abandon technology in order to distract a rogue Genius, and has standing orders about committing suicide rather than being captured. They have far too many cases of Marduk agents being violated in the most obscene ways, minds and bodies flayed, distorted and torn asunder as Geniuses tried to find out what makes them <b>capable</b> of doing what Geniuses aren't.<br /> <br /> Fortunately for the Marduk Society, Geniuses and Leviathans don't get on, generally. Beyond the fact that, outside of the (Mad Biologists) and (Exploration Faction), few Geniuses have interests in such &quot;primitive throwbacks&quot;, it's the standard &quot;mad scientist casually dismisses and unthinkingly mistreats the monster until it turns on him&quot; archetype. Of course, sometimes it doesn't happen that way - sometimes, a Genius/Leviathan pairing manages to get along despite their temperamental clashes. That's when the Marduk Society starts to sweat.<br /> <br /> But that's <b>nothing</b> in comparison to those nightmarish occasions when Clockbreakers(?) and Leviathans cross paths. An alliance between an entity that is a throwback to the primordial era of humanity, and a twisted anti-technologist capable of <b>warping reality to nullify humanity's progress</b> is perhaps the one thing that can force the Society and the Peerage to actively cooperate. The idea that, if you brought enough Clockbreakers together with enough Leviathans, or just one powerful enough Leviathan, you could <b>undo</b> everything humanity has accomplished and evolved into since the Stone Age... nobody wants to even think about the possibility, sane or otherwise.<br /> <br /> \u200b<u>Princesses</u> and Marduk are best friends forever! Well... sort of. They share the unique trait of being genuine White Hats in a world of Black and Gray Morality, and that gives them cause to cling together. But they have different focuses, different rationales, and though Marduk never fights with Princesses, it tends to be rather condescending towards them. Talking about &quot;feelings&quot; is too much like clinging to arguments about &quot;nature&quot;, which are all too often brought up to allow humanity to shirk progressing out of the primordial mire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T16:45:30-07:00","id":668967,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Some ritual stuff. Nothing close to usable mechanics yet.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sample Ritual</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Heed not the Blasphemer (Predation oo)</span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mankinds ability to cooperate and share ideas is perhaps the greatest threat to the Wicked Tribe. It is this ability that l</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">ed to civilisation and scientific progress, that builds nations and soceities, that allows </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">mobs of mere mortals to rout a would-be God from their </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">town. Communication exposes a Leviathans nature for all to perceive and births hope in the hearts of men. This ritual seeks to </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">disable opposition by removing their ability to share what they know about the horror that lurks in their town.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Suggested S</i><i>acrifice</i>: A living human (willing or unwilling) is subject to lingual mutilation, their </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">tongue is pulled out and devoured or incinerated.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><i>Sample acts </i>: The entire ritual is performed in silence or in incomprehensible gibberish. The assembly acts out a scene where the unfaithful try and fail to oppose the Leviathan in some way and are punished for it. A cultist reads a set of commandments including a law <span style=\"color:#000000\">invol</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">ving secrecy or blasphemy.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Base Effect : A single wake-vunerable target with knowledge of the Leviathan or his cult is rendered unable to relay this information to others in any meaningful way. Exactly how this manifests depends on the degree of knowledge the target has : if the target has only limited experience of the Leviathan or his cult (saw a group of robed men lingering around the docks on Saturday) then they will simply avoid talking about the issue or feign ignorance ; if the target has intimate knowledge of the Leviathan and his designs (has perceived the most Wicked in Apotheosis) then they go as far as biting off their own tongue to avoid revealing what they know. Despite the vocal themes of this ritual it applies to all forms of communication. In no way does the target actually forget his experiences.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">+1 Potency : The target instead is forced to express false information about the Leviathan. Again the effect depends on the intimacy of his knowledge \u2013 a survivor of a direct confrontation with a God-Monster can be made to tell any lies the Leviathan wishes, whereas those with only minor information will simply make mistakes.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">+1 Potency : The ritual can be used to target a group of people. The group must have some sort of relation (the entire Kramer family, appartment block 12b, all witnesses to the robbery at the natural history museum) to a maximum number of Sheol x 10.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">+2 Potency : The targets silence is contagious and self containing. Anyone who attempts to extract information from them will be subject to similar effects.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">---------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> In the end I went with Predation for this one because of that Vestiges ties to remaining unseen but I'm still not sure that the Vestiges as Arcana is going to work so smoothly. As an alternative how about a ritual will have various requisite channels, some would require only one kind of vestige but the above for example could require at least 1 channel from awareness and 1 from Predation. It might even be preferable to avoid mimicing the Mage system too closely.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sacrifices</span></b><br /> <br /> <i>Consecrate to me every first-born that opens the womb among Israelites, both man and beast, for it belongs to me. Exodus 13:2</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The hideous rites of the Wicked Tribe are no simple parlor tricks or magicians illusions. They are manifestations of divine power, surging through the primordial waters with reckless abandon and tempered with the captive willpower of a Leviathans cult. They are eldritch miracles and demand sacrifice. They are miracles born in sweat and blood.<br /> <br /> Each ritual by default requires a sacrifice of a value equal to its rating. A more powerful sacrifice will increase a rituals Potency - allowing the Leviathan to create more powerful effects on those rituals they have mastered and to cast formidable rituals that thir cult is otherwise incapable of. Likewise if they already have higher Potency than needed due to a Zealous cult or the Stars Being Right they may opt to use a less severe sacrifice instead of increasing the rites power.<br /> <br /> The sacrifices below are rough suggestions of what is to be expected for each ritual rank. Sacrifices must always be appropriate to the theme. The subject of the sacrifice can vary between cultists, captives or victims or the Leviathan themself.<br /> <br /> <b>-neg- Token Sacrifice </b>(only used if a rank 1 ritual has its sacrifice lowered due to potency)</span></span><ul><li>\u200bTrivial harm. 1 point of bashing damage at most.</li> <li>Destruction of an items of limited worth. Avaliability \u2022</li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>o Petty Sacrifice</b></span></span><ul><li>Minor physical harm . Several points of bashing damage or a single point of lethal damage is inflicted.</li> <li>Minor mental torment. Subject receives a temporary derrangement or is placed under heavy stress for the duration.</li> <li>A non-sapient animal is slaughtered.</li> <li>Destruction of items of some value. Avaliability \u2022\u2022</li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>oo Minor Sacrifice</b></span></span><ul><li>Severe physical harm. Dangerous ammounts of lethal damage, Subject is maimed or disfigured.</li> <li>Severe mental torment. Subject receives a lasting derrangement that will prove hard to treat.</li> <li>Destruction of items of considerable value. Avaliability \u2022\u2022\u2022</li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>ooo Mortal Sacrifice</b></span></span><ul><li>Fatal sacrifice. A humans life is sacrificed.</li> <li>Horrific physical or mental harm. The victim will be unable to function in soceity. (Driven to utter insanity. All limbs removed)</li> <li>Destruction of items of major value. Avaliability \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>oooo Monstrous Sacrifice</b></span></span><ul><li>Heinous Murder (sacrificed is a child or particularly virtuous person)</li> <li>Fatal sacrifice on a supernatural creature (enemy Leviathan?)</li> <li>Destruction of items of incredible value. Avaliability \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>ooooo Abominable Sacrifice</b></span></span><ul><li>Mass human sacrifice.</li> <li>Destruction of an entire settlement.</li> <li>Willing sacrifice of an abstract concept (love, innocence)</li> </ul>A sacrifice counts as a dot less if it is an inherent part of the rituals goal or otherwise advances the goals of the Leviathan in itself.<br /> I'm not sure about the material sacrifices, it might not be in theme.<br /> Another ideas:<br /> Sacrificing merits of dot value equal to the ritual - sanctity of merits applies but only at the end of the story and the same merit can't be bought with that experience (ex. A cult may burn down their magnificent temple to power a 4th rank ritual but they're doomed to be without refuge for some time.<br /> <br /> Criticism please.<br /> <br /> EDIT : I forgot to mention - 'Potency' is the equivalent to 2ed Mages 'Reach' hastily renamed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","user":"Opprobrium","date":". 09-18-2015, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","name":"Opprobrium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T16:46:08-07:00","id":668969,"title":"","content":"Bravo, VoidDrifter. More excellent assessment.<br /> <br /> Re: Genius, the Biologists are the Progenitors (for short), and the explorers are the Navigators (likewise). The Luddists are Clockstoppers. And yeah, an alliance of Leviathans and Clockstoppers is a match made in the Inferno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T18:06:08-07:00","id":669052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668961#post668961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<u>Princesses</u> and Marduk are best friends forever! Well... sort of. They share the unique trait of being genuine White Hats in a world of Black and Gray Morality, and that gives them cause to cling together. But they have different focuses, different rationales, and though Marduk never fights with Princesses, it tends to be rather condescending towards them. Talking about &amp;quot;feelings&amp;quot; is too much like clinging to arguments about &amp;quot;nature&amp;quot;, which are all too often brought up to allow humanity to shirk progressing out of the primordial mire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought princess hated them judgeing by their stereotype quotes of they are evil and we must run or kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T18:50:42-07:00","id":669125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669052#post669052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought princess hated them judgeing by their stereotype quotes of they are evil and we must run or kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doubtful. Cross-splat impressions are for the primary members, which would be Leviathans, not Marduk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T18:57:36-07:00","id":669129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669125#post669125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doubtful. Cross-splat impressions are for the primary members, which would be Leviathans, not Marduk.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was what I was talking about if you look at nearly every princess quote about leviathans in princess they all talk about killing or being disgusted by leviathans check the princess the hopeful wiki for each princess and look at their quote on leviathans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T19:27:37-07:00","id":669141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668784#post668784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a quick note. This won't work unless X is famous. &quot;Kill the vampire prince&quot; would just leave people wondering around in confusion. Kill the Queen of England would work though; but again it would have consiquences. And who knows, maybe the British Government has some really nasty defences against Leviathans up and running just waiting for a player to stumble into them. It is St Geroge's patron nation after all<br /> <br /> Still. Some really creative and devious uses there. I approve of your wicked mind and don't envy the Storyteller who</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the idea I had for an Oceanid goes as follows: Exclusive Club style cult, models itself after a band+roadies (allowing for a neat cover for their debauchery and an way to explain away the wake. A rock star is expected to have presence). Have a Beloved body double for the stage.<br /> Step 1: using a truck with a pool big enough for the Depth 6 Leviathan, set up a promotion, give the order &quot;buy tickets to this show&quot;, (or, if that isn't how the depth 6 version works, instead inflict an obsession regarding the show on passersby). Then, at the show, have a pool set up somewhere with good coverage (incidentally, near a speaker). Give the order &quot;Buy our merchandise&quot;.<br /> <br /> Question: how much do those hit with the Insensate tilt remember afterwords? How hard would it be for a Leviathan to play Dark City with, say, a small town?<br /> <br /> <br /> Question regarding Genius: how should the Wake effect Beholden? How should it effect Clockstoppers?<br /> On the one hand, Beholden are basically a Genus's Beloved. On another, they have been burned out by the Light, a force that is thematically the opposite of the Primal Waters.<br /> As for Clockstoppers, the phrase &quot;I tried to eat his soul, but all I found was a hungry void&quot; won't get out of my head. I'm imagining Clockstoppers as really, really disturbing Atolls, inspiring horrified fascination instead of addictive serenity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T21:52:39-07:00","id":669215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668961#post668961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean a Marduk Society vs. Fansplats section? You really like my work that much? Well, I am flattered, but I don't really know that much about fansplats. I can give commentary on Geniuses and Princesses, from what little I know about them via overhearing, and also on Beasts now that I am forced to remember they exist, but beyond that...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's pretty good.<br /> Sadly, I doubt I could do the same from the fansplats I am currently involved in since I lack the ability to think things ahead or do so tactfully. I also doubt I'd be objective about it especially since I'm writing one right now.<br /> <br /> I would honestly love to see their reactions to Inheritance Dragons (not to be confused with Embers Dragons) as well as some others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669141#post669141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question regarding Genius: how should the Wake effect Beholden? How should it effect Clockstoppers?<br /> On the one hand, Beholden are basically a Genus's Beloved. On another, they have been burned out by the Light, a force that is thematically the opposite of the Primal Waters.<br /> As for Clockstoppers, the phrase &quot;I tried to eat his soul, but all I found was a hungry void&quot; won't get out of my head. I'm imagining Clockstoppers as really, really disturbing Atolls, inspiring horrified fascination instead of addictive serenity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clockstoppers as though they were other supernaturals, which is to say, not at all affected. Unless I am misremembering things. Last I recall, being subject to the wake was more of a passive thing that gave you debuffs and acted more like a D&amp;D dragon's terrifying prescence for a supernatural rather than what it is for mortals<br /> <br /> Beholden should be treated as Beloved for simplicty. The effect of losing your independance is close enough to the point that it's really just different flavors of soul lose.... mechanically speaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 09-18-2015, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T22:27:34-07:00","id":669256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669215#post669215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's pretty good.<br /> Sadly, I doubt I could do the same from the fansplats I am currently involved in since I lack the ability to think things ahead or do so tactfully. I also doubt I'd be objective about it especially since I'm writing one right now.<br /> <br /> I would honestly love to see their reactions to Inheritance Dragons (not to be confused with Embers Dragons) as well as some others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Clockstoppers as though they were other supernaturals, which is to say, not at all affected. Unless I am misremembering things. Last I recall, being subject to the wake was more of a passive thing that gave you debuffs and acted more like a D&amp;D dragon's terrifying prescence for a supernatural rather than what it is for mortals<br /> <br /> Beholden should be treated as Beloved for simplicty. The effect of losing your independance is close enough to the point that it's really just different flavors of soul lose.... mechanically speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think Supernaturals are immune, but only if their Power stat is at a certain level compared to the Leviathan's Sheol.<br /> <br /> And I agree that Beholden should be treated like Beloved mechanically. Although, I would say that being Beholden or Beloved shouldn't be soul <i>loss</i> (at least, not until the most <i>extreme</i> Wake sets in), but more soul <i>suppression</i>. That is, they present some or all the symptoms of soul loss, but if the cause is removed (or they Catalyze, in the Beholden's case), then the soul quickly reasserts itself without need for replacement.<br /> <br /> And I wonder, what happens to a Leviathan who loses its soul? Does it have multiple souls due to its triple nature, or just one, incredibly large and fractious soul?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T23:40:18-07:00","id":669301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669129#post669129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was what I was talking about if you look at nearly every princess quote about leviathans in princess they all talk about killing or being disgusted by leviathans check the princess the hopeful wiki for each princess and look at their quote on leviathans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, the dissonance would probably be because the post was talking about interactions between &amp; respective opinions of Princesses and <b>The Marduk Society</b>, not Princesses and Leviathans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T23:42:57-07:00","id":669302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669301#post669301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, the dissonance would probably be because the post was talking about interactions between &amp; respective opinions of Princesses and <b>The Marduk Society</b>, not Princesses and Leviathans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Specifically, Pure and Idealistic Marduk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T01:57:18-07:00","id":669347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668956#post668956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say science (understanding physics would help, I'd think), but Occult was likely just a catch-all. Not many skills directly relate moving things with your brain. (And adding Psychic-only skills is a bit much)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm leaning towards Wits (for Dexterity) or Resolve (for Strength) + Depth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668967#post668967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[ SIZE=12px]<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sample Ritual</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Heed not the Blasphemer (Predation oo)</span></b></span>[/SIZE]</div> </div> </div> </div> Sweet!<br /> <br /> This Ritual's should name should refer to the tower of Babel... unless a later more fitting ritual claims that name instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668967#post668967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end I went with Predation for this one because of that Vestiges ties to remaining unseen but I'm still not sure that the Vestiges as Arcana is going to work so smoothly. As an alternative how about a ritual will have various requisite channels, some would require only one kind of vestige but the above for example could require at least 1 channel from awareness and 1 from Predation. It might even be preferable to avoid mimicing the Mage system too closely.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think Predation works fine; but I don't object to the idea of multi Vestige rituals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668967#post668967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Consecrate to me every first-born that opens the womb among Israelites, both man and beast, for it belongs to me. Exodus 13:2</i></div> </div> </div> </div> Given that he's saying send your first-born to work at the temple, perhaps Abraham and Issac instead?<br /> <br /> Then God said, &quot;Take your son, your only son, whom you love--Isaac--and go to the region of Moriah. Sacrifice him there as a burnt offering on a mountain I will show you. (Genesis 22:2)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668967#post668967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each ritual by default requires a sacrifice of a value equal to its rating. A more powerful sacrifice will increase a rituals Potency - allowing the Leviathan to create more powerful effects on those rituals they have mastered and to cast formidable rituals that thir cult is otherwise incapable of. Likewise if they already have higher Potency than needed due to a Zealous cult or the Stars Being Right they may opt to use a less severe sacrifice instead of increasing the rites power.</div> </div> </div> </div> Solid, with one point - Zeal and Potency won't be 1:1 because using a ritual higher than your zeal needs to be especially hard - thus limiting seven dot rituals to being plot points rather than powers.<br /> <br /> Maybe something like you get free (Zeal - Ritual Dots) potency, but it costs lots of potency to use a ritual higher than your Zeal. If you have Zeal 1 and want a three dot Ritual you need to spend 8 Potency: 2 for not having Zeal 2; 3 for not having Zeal 3, 3 for the default dot sacrafice.<br /> <br /> But there's no hurry. This works fine as a draft until Mage 2E lands<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668967#post668967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sacrifices below are rough suggestions of what is to be expected for each ritual rank. Sacrifices must always be appropriate to the theme. The subject of the sacrifice can vary between cultists, captives or victims or the Leviathan themself.</div> </div> </div> </div> Looks good, the big list is solid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=668967#post668967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT : I forgot to mention - 'Potency' is the equivalent to 2ed Mages 'Reach' hastily renamed.</div> </div> </div> </div>BTW. Potency is also a technical term in Mage, but I don't have any better ideas for the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669141#post669141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the idea I had for an Oceanid goes as follows: Exclusive Club style cult, models itself after a band+roadies (allowing for a neat cover for their debauchery and an way to explain away the wake. A rock star is expected to have presence). Have a Beloved body double for the stage.<br /> Step 1: using a truck with a pool big enough for the Depth 6 Leviathan, set up a promotion, give the order &quot;buy tickets to this show&quot;, (or, if that isn't how the depth 6 version works, instead inflict an obsession regarding the show on passersby). Then, at the show, have a pool set up somewhere with good coverage (incidentally, near a speaker). Give the order &quot;Buy our merchandise&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> That works fine, with a slight problem. Depth 6 Leviathans are much bigger than trucks at all but the lowest Sheol.<br /> <br /> Use Depth 5 instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669141#post669141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question regarding Genius: how should the Wake effect Beholden? How should it effect Clockstoppers?</div> </div> </div> </div> Beholden like normal, Clockstoppers like any full Supernatural.<br /> <br /> The Wake is significantly stronger than the Beholden effect, and Beholden don't have any Inspiration of their own. A Genius sending his Beloved against a Leviathan is strongly advised to use Prostasia to protect their Beholden.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669256#post669256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Supernaturals are immune, but only if their Power stat is at a certain level compared to the Leviathan's Sheol.</div> </div> </div> </div> Correct. But even when the Wake can affect a supernatural, it can't turn them Beloved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669256#post669256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, I would say that being Beholden or Beloved shouldn't be soul <i>loss</i> (at least, not until the most <i>extreme</i> Wake sets in)</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm pretty sure being Beholden affects your mind but has no direct effect upon your soul. Being Beloved is more like an infection in your soul, it won't ever actually remove your soul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669256#post669256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I wonder, what happens to a Leviathan who loses its soul? Does it have multiple souls due to its triple nature, or just one, incredibly large and fractious soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>One increadibly large and factious soul; I'd say Leviathans can't survive without it. Being divine they have a closer relationship between their mind, body, and soul than humans do.<br /> <br /> I doubt anything short of a Rank 6 Spirit could seriously remove a Leviathans soul though; well apart from the obvious method of killing the body first.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T03:06:31-07:00","id":669366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669347#post669347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Predation works fine; but I don't object to the idea of multi Vestige rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm ... we'll see. I think there's something missing here but at the same time I don't want to complicate the ritual rules excessively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669347#post669347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that he's saying send your first-born to work at the temple, perhaps Abraham and Issac instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either works, although they're both sacrifices. Frankly I think the verse I quoted is ambiguous given other situations where Jehovah demands first-borns and I just liked the feel of the sentence - seemed appropriate. I feel there's room for a little more Old Testament flavor in Leviathan, although not too much to avoid ressemblance to Mummy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669347#post669347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Solid, with one point - Zeal and Potency won't be 1:1 because using a ritual higher than your zeal needs to be especially hard - thus limiting seven dot rituals to being plot points rather than powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware - I've taken into account everything that was previously said on the subject in this thread, I have a better draft in works for ritual mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669347#post669347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> BTW. Potency is also a technical term in Mage, but I don't have any better ideas for the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eugh .. so it is.<br /> Ardor? It has a similar meaning to Zeal but the word is different enough to avoid confusion.<br /> <br /> --------------------------<br /> <br /> In other news I think we will need actual mechanics for when the Stars are Right in this version as they're going to be an important part of even using higher level rituals as opposed to just a bonus/malus. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669347#post669347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That works fine, with a slight problem. Depth 6 Leviathans are much bigger than trucks at all but the lowest Sheol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Size gain for basic transformation is Sheol dependant now? And Depth 6 are generally truck sized as opposed to bear sized? Good.<br /> Do you have a new depth progression chart to post for us?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","user":"Opprobrium","date":". 09-18-2015, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7755-opprobrium","name":"Opprobrium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T03:32:18-07:00","id":669426,"title":"","content":"a) If the power comes from the Leviathan himself, why does he need a sacrifice?<br /> b) What about incorporate symbols like in Werewolf 2ed rituals? To help channeling the power into the desire pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T04:08:45-07:00","id":669451,"title":"","content":"For a Leviathan, the sacrifices are the symbol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T11:50:10-07:00","id":671166,"title":"","content":"Some people worried that Call of the Depths might infringe upon Besieging the Tower of Will. Have a look at the 2E version and let me know if you're still worried <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Besieging the Tower of Will (Descendant Channel)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Leviathan's innate ability to casually dominate the herd is refined into a cold psychic sword that drives humans mad even as it enslaves them.</i></span></span><ul><li><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: Presence + Intimidate + Sheol vs. Target's Resolve + Power Trait</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action Type: Instant</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan may telepathically communicate to speak unseen. The target is aware that the Leviathan is the one communicating with them. As the Leviathan sinks Deeper they move beyond communication to shape the minds, and souls, of their victims. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 0&quot;: Birthright of Sanctity</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 1&quot;: At the cost of 1 Ichor, the Leviathan may create a psychic link to anyone within Sheol times 50 feet that they can perceive through natural means or Channels. The link remains for the remainder of the scene and allows the Leviathan to communicate telepathically at will. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 2&quot;: As above, and the Leviathan gains an alternative ability. Instead of forming a psychic link they may implant an order into the target\u2019s mind. The order may be as complicated or as vague as the Leviathan wishes and the target will obey to the best of their ability. They are unable to creatively misinterpret orders, however they may quite easily genuinely misinterpret orders because: </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> From the moment the command is implanted to the end of the scene, the target takes the Madness Condition. A Leviathan\u2019s psychic dominance is neither subtle nor kind to the minds of their victims. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 3&quot;: As above, and the Leviathan may spend an additional 1 Ichor to use the Depth 2 Iteration of this Channel with a delay. The Leviathan specifies a trigger and when the target experiences that trigger they immediately attempt to carry out their orders. The target is aware that they were the victim of some manner of psychic attack but without supernatural abilities they have no way of knowing the details of what happened to them.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The target suffers Madness in both the scene where the madness is implanted and the scene where the trigger is activated. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 4&quot;: As above, and the range extends to Sheol miles. The Leviathan still requires some way to perceive their targets without technological aid. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 5&quot;: As above, and the Leviathan may use the Depth 2 iteration of this Channel on up to Sheol + Wits targets in a single turn. All targets must be given the same command, but it only costs 2 Ichor to affect both of them. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 6&quot;: As above, and the Leviathan may spend an additional 3 Ichor to completely replace the personality of a single Wake vulnerable individual with a new personality of the Leviathan\u2019s own design. The Leviathan needs to accumulate Willpower successes, but may roll as an Extended action making one roll per turn. This effect is permanent but it can be undone. Either the target\u2019s on mental defences can purge the foreign elements given time and extreme psychological stimulus. Alternatively supernatural powers can reverse the effect. As a Leviathan is divine, their psychic powers can reach through the connection between mind and soul. Thus undoing the Leviathan\u2019s influence properly requires purging both.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The implanted personality will suffer from Madness and cannot be cured, only restoring the original personality can end the Condition. If the target is a mortal, they will be Beloved; as being Beloved is in of itself a form of Madness there is no need to take the Condition. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind Blast (OO or OOOO): In Depth 3 or lower, the Leviathan may unleash a psychic attack as an instant action. It costs 1 Ichor per Sheol + Resolve shots. The Leviathan rolls Presence + Intimidation + Sheol, subtracting the target's Resolve + Power Trait. The effects of success depend on the number of dots in this Merit the Leviathan possesses. With the two-dot version of this Merit, the Leviathan inflicts Bashing damage with the Stun property. With the four-dot version of this Merit, the Leviathan gains the option to inflict Lethal damage with the Stun property. The Leviathan may choose to split successes among multiple opponents, subtract only the highest Resolve + Power Trait amongst the targets.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Assimilation (OOOO+): Purchasing this Merit creates a Memory Slot. In Depth 3 or lower, the Leviathan may devour the mind of a recently deceased Wake Vulnerable character. This requires a (Resolve + Stamina - Target's Intelligence) check on the part of the Leviathan. On a failure, the mind is destroyed. On a success, the Leviathan fills one Memory Slot and benefits from one of the following:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A one-dot increase in one social or mental Attribute the devoured had at a higher rank than the Leviathan.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The devoured's rank in one skill.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once per session the Leviathan may roll Intelligence + Sheol and ask the storyteller (or the devoured\u2019s former player) one question per success. The Storyteller answers truthfully, from the devoured\u2019s perspective. </span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669366#post669366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ardor? It has a similar meaning to Zeal but the word is different enough to avoid confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ardor is fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669366#post669366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other news I think we will need actual mechanics for when the Stars are Right in this version as they're going to be an important part of even using higher level rituals as opposed to just a bonus/malus. Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Opprobrium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=669366#post669366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Size gain for basic transformation is Sheol dependant now? And Depth 6 are generally truck sized as opposed to bear sized?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in Apotheosis. I linked the entire folder in the origonal post. Under systems and advantages it's there. Sheol 1 gives you size 10; goes up by 5.<br /> <br /> Since WoD sizes make absolutely no sense, so I'm using a nice 5 increment and making up what the numbers mean myself.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T12:18:15-07:00","id":672275,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this has been answered or not, but...<br /> <br /> 2e has really boosted the power scale of monster races as a whole*, with two of our best examples being vampires degrading damage by one level towards Bashing (and personally I would have made it that vampires don't <b>take</b> bashing damage from weapons at all, it just makes no sense you can punch out someone who shrugs off having his shoulderblade blown into chunks) except from Bane damage, and Werewolves having both a damage protection (no Agg except from Banes and Lethal rollover) and suped up healing (to the tune of instantly regenerating all non-Agg damage each turn).<br /> <br /> So, I was curious: how are Leviathans going to compare? Their whole &quot;thing&quot; is their horrifically half-divine nature and their freakish fecundity, so, to me at least, that suggests that they should have some pretty major league innate armor and/or healing, and I'm not just talking the extra health-blocks gained from their Size boost by shifting forms.<br /> <br /> Also, does it make sense to anyone else that the Channels should include some options for acid and/or poison? Since bio-electricity is out due to the thematic association of lightning with Sky and thus The Enemy, acid and venom are the major &quot;biological&quot; options for nastiness.<br /> <br /> Is the &quot;spawn minions&quot; mechanic still going to be in effect for Leviathans? There's a lot of primeval monsters that could produce monsters in turn to aid themselves - I'm sure I remember some mythological creature producing scorpions from its open wound instead of blood - so being able to spawn mooks or swarms in mid-combat, which'd be lower power but instantly available in comparison to the &quot;seeding produced heirs&quot;, would b e kind of fitting for Leviathans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T13:13:31-07:00","id":672326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=672275#post672275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was curious: how are Leviathans going to compare?</div> </div> </div> </div> Given that Leviathan has basic rules for combat at large size, and basically says if you're big enough you're going to win no matter what (I mean, Dracula vs Godzilla in a fist fight. What exactly is Dracula going to do? Throw a truck at Godzilla's toe?) and the ability for a starting charachter to summon hurricanes, Leviathan's are plenty powerful already.<br /> <br /> But I'm going to bump them up anyway - not because 2E is more powerful, but because there's Channels who's effects are pretty meh and I want to fix that. Take Call of the Depths. I wasn't thinking that it needs to be stronger, I was just thinking I want to make it a useful power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=672275#post672275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">innate armor and/or healing</div> </div> </div> </div> Innate, no. One of Leviathan's few weaknesses is that they're pretty dependant on Channels and Transformation. However once they get a collection of powers they'll be terrifying, even without the inherent advantages of being many times larger than your foe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=672275#post672275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, does it make sense to anyone else that the Channels should include some options for acid and/or poison? Since bio-electricity is out due to the thematic association of lightning with Sky and thus The Enemy, acid and venom are the major &quot;biological&quot; options for nastiness.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's two already. The Toad's Curse and the Hunter's Blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=672275#post672275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the &quot;spawn minions&quot; mechanic still going to be in effect for Leviathans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. I have no plan to remove Womb of Terrors.<br /> <br /> I might make Incubation of the Second Self into an Adaptation though. It's a very niche power. I'm not sure what to replace it with though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-20-2015, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T13:16:00-07:00","id":672327,"title":"","content":"And about that. Any thought about giving Womb of Terrors a &quot;Swarm&quot; option? As much as I like the ability to spawn small creatures, I think it'd be a good thing if Womb of Terrors allowed spawning small swarms of flesh eating goop and bacteria with the only distinction being how large the swarm is when it procs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T13:33:25-07:00","id":672339,"title":"","content":"Sure. Swarms are cool.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-cate