 /> I might start thinking about Hybrids next.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://asset-e.soupcdn.com/asset/12297/2110_ef64.jpeg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-06-2015, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T04:10:51-07:00","id":692227,"title":"","content":"Souping them up (some of the mutations were kinda weak)? How about some abilities that Leviathans don't have direct access to (similarly to how Tells and Ghoul merits don't map <i>exactly</i> to their greater template's powers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T04:19:53-07:00","id":692237,"title":"","content":"An idea for an Atoll merit: Engender the Savior. Allows the Atoll to create Ahabs aimed at imprinted leviathans. Gives such Ahabs an obsession with &quot;saving&quot; the Atoll. Maybe let the Atoll treat Ahabs as Beloved. Probably mechanically linked to eroding Phronesis or Eunoia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","user":"Thamuzz","date":". 10-07-2015, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T11:45:08-07:00","id":692770,"title":"","content":"I'd rather keep Atolls and Ahabs completely seperate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=692227#post692227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Souping them up (some of the mutations were kinda weak)?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's the plan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=692227#post692227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How about some abilities that Leviathans don't have direct access to (similarly to how Tells and Ghoul merits don't map <i>exactly</i> to their greater template's powers).</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't the plan but it's almost certain to end up that way in the end.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T13:21:34-07:00","id":692869,"title":"","content":"I dig what you've done with Atolls, and I especially like the idea you've mentioned before of a villainous Atoll being the mastermind behind a Leviathan antagonist. In the case of a normal Leviathan game, do you expect such a scenario to always be a downer ending for everyone involved? I get the impression that no matter what the outcome, someone is going to end up Eroding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T13:56:11-07:00","id":692899,"title":"","content":"In a typical long form Leviathan game I'd expect the Atoll to be one session or one chapter. A nasty bump on the road rather than a downer ending.<br /> <br /> But yes, they did turn out to be a very dangerous threat to any Leviathan's sanity. I think that works well, and there's no shortage of other antagonists that players will have an easier time scoring an unambigious victory over if that's what the group is after. A Primordial Theurgist for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-07-2015, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T14:52:55-07:00","id":692928,"title":"","content":"So wait, atolls aren't a minor template?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T14:59:41-07:00","id":692954,"title":"","content":"They are, what's the confusion?<br /> <br /> Is it the stacking? IMO minor templates can be stacked in some circumstances. A Ghoul Thamaturge for example","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T15:42:10-07:00","id":693035,"title":"","content":"There we go, got it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T16:28:34-07:00","id":693120,"title":"","content":"Question, how to do you imagine Leviathans and Marduk in the Crossover Infinite Macabre setting?<br /> <br /> I've always thought that atleast one group of Leviathans would band together and colonize their own planet. Marduk feels itself at home, but their successfulness in such a setting would arguably be dependant on whether or not the setup is &quot;balanced&quot; between the various factions. I don't see them doing what TF:V did either.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, if you were given a Dark Era of your choice, what would it be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T18:05:53-07:00","id":693207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=693120#post693120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, how to do you imagine Leviathans and Marduk in the Crossover Infinite Macabre setting?<br /> <br /> I've always thought that atleast one group of Leviathans would band together and colonize their own planet. Marduk feels itself at home, but their successfulness in such a setting would arguably be dependant on whether or not the setup is &quot;balanced&quot; between the various factions. I don't see them doing what TF:V did either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, 1E had an Evolution of Leviathans that chose to drift across space, so it's very much possible that that Evolution and more like it would become very popular among space-faring Leviathans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T18:19:44-07:00","id":693223,"title":"","content":"Some other ideas for Atoll merits:<ul><li>One that lets them add/replace one of the Leviathan's Aspirations with one of the Atoll's choosing.</li> <li>One that easily lets them impose emotional Conditions. Due to their nature, this might even be done accidently.</li> <li>One that allows an Atoll to &quot;haunt&quot; a Leviathan's dreams: even seperated, the Atoll is treated as nearby, can influence the sleeping Leviathan, and (optionally) count their proximity as &quot;close&quot; for the purposes of remote ritual targeting (the Atoll may be immune, but this lets a manipulative Atoll &quot;request&quot; intervention on their behalf via the cult's rituals).</li> <li>One that negates any ongoing effect by a Leviathan (ex. An Atoll finds an ongoing Call of the Depths, or summoned hurricane, and uses their odd connection to the Wake/Tempest to &quot;dispel&quot; it).</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T19:06:54-07:00","id":693305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=693207#post693207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, 1E had an Evolution of Leviathans that chose to drift across space, so it's very much possible that that Evolution and more like it would become very popular among space-faring Leviathans.</div> </div> </div> </div> To be honest, such an ability would probably be best served as a Vestige in such a setting. Vitality or Elements, possibly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T19:35:33-07:00","id":693316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=693305#post693305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To be honest, such an ability would probably be best served as a Vestige in such a setting. Vitality or Elements, possibly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vitality, I say. Because Vitality needs more stuff in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T12:54:45-07:00","id":694153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=693223#post693223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some other ideas for Atoll merits</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of those should be done with just regualr old social rolls IMO. I'm ok with Atolls haunting a Leviathan's dreams but I'd make that a psychic ability - Atolls just have an easy time of using it on Leviathans where as most poeple would consider entering a Leviathan's dreams to be practically suicide. The last one I considered but felt that it strayed to far from the dynamic between Atoll and Leviathan being social rather than magical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=693120#post693120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, how to do you imagine Leviathans and Marduk in the Crossover Infinite Macabre setting?</div> </div> </div> </div> No idea for Marduk but Leviathans: Think of them as the Zerg (Heart of the Swarm is going to be a big inspiration for Channels).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=693120#post693120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought that atleast one group of Leviathans would band together and colonize their own planet.</div> </div> </div> </div> Of course, but that's like the Leviathans on Earth who try to colonise the sea bed. It ends badly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=693120#post693120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you were given a Dark Era of your choice, what would it be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pirate Somalia!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=693316#post693316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vitality, I say. Because Vitality needs more stuff in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elements I'm afraid. And yes; in an Infinite Macabare game space travel is just a Channel; in a regular game it requires an Evolution.<br /> <br /> Good progress on Hybrids today. Just the Mutations list to go. There's few changes mechanically so far - that's going to be the Mutations - but the whole intelligence cap thing is going. Instead that's going to be a Genetic Condition. However there's more text and setting. You can read it in the usual spot.<br /> <br /> Flyboy did the story, all credit should go where it's due.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T08:00:32-07:00","id":694918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not all mutations are cool powers. Hybrids must take Genetic Conditions to represent harmful side effects of their Mutations. A Hybrid takes one per depth, a Lahmasu takes one at Depth 1, 3 and 5.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This was pretty much just the house-rule I made regarding defective mutations.<br /> <br /> Regarding mutations, there should be at least a few that are more oddball or circumstantial, for story/scene purposes. Maybe one that allows the Hybrid to secrete addictive chemicals (like the &quot;heroin pissing dinosaurs&quot; I've heard about in Exalted). Gives the referenced corporations an obvious non-combat motive for using/hunting Hybrids.<br /> <br /> Other ideas:<ul><li>Hypnosis-based mental manipulation. Possibly using a combination of psychic, audio, and scent inputs. For implanting commands. Possibly illusions. &quot;No, I don't look at all like a fish-man, sir.&quot;</li> <li>Pheromone-based emotional manipulation. More subtle, but less controlled. Mostly social bonuses (but including Intimidation).</li> <li>Would something that essentially grants a scaling Influence Water be appropriate for Elements? Using Ichor instead of Essence? (The spending cap on Ichor limits it's combat applicability, but allows for the reclusive frog-shaman to do freaky things with water)</li> <li>Some kind of minion spawning? Based on Womb of Terrors (but obviously greatly reduced in power), or corrupting other wildlife? Allows for a minion master, or brood queen hybrid.</li> <li>Some psychic powers requiring the Hybrid to be dreaming, to mirror those that Leviathans possess. (Though that could just be flavor or a drawback applied to other psychic abilities)</li> <li>More like Leech's Hunger that allow for alternate Ichor gain. Destruction based (inferring that <i>this</i> Hybrid possesses more of the Bestial nature of their forebearers than their peers), or &quot;purpose&quot; based (same, but for the Divine part of their heritage)?</li> </ul><br /> <hr /><br /> Thinking more on the proposed temporary mutation ability, it could easily be used as a combined buffing/debuffing/healing ability if it grants (or modifies) the Hybrid template and selected Mutations. Buff? Give the target combat powers. Debuff? Give them bad Genetic Conditions. Healing? Give the target a healing/regen mutation and have them heal their own self.<br /> <br /> Mechanics: Successes - add/change/subtract 1 dot of Mutations (positive or negative), extend duration 1 interval/step? Aggravated damage per Depth when it wears off, with Lethal damage dependent on a resistance roll (or the number of rolls made for the initial transformation)?<br /> <br /> (need to work on mechanical balance...)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:58:33-07:00","id":695333,"title":"","content":"Start writing up Mutations <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> BTW when I get round to them the sample Hybrids will be a classical mermaid (because there has to be one) and an Atlantian secret agent. I'd estimate that 1 in 3 of the Gugal's underwater nations / city states / stone age villages calls itself Atlantis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T03:01:39-07:00","id":695913,"title":"","content":"I felt like doing Womb of Horrors - it's now in the updated Channels document and it's a doozy. Aside from being extreemly long. With the obvious shout out Adaptation &quot;Heart of the Swarm&quot; a Sheol 10 Leviathan can create 1000 minions per 4 Ichor, and if those minions eat 4 people it regains 4 Ichor.<br /> <br /> Powerful, but surprisingly counterable. A swarm of minions can't stop mortals from bombing the Leviathan to smithereens and they're not very powerful - to the point that a regular military grade chaingun will probably kill dozens of them every turn.<br /> <br /> And that's against regular humans. A Genius with Katastrofi 5 can build a device that blows up every Leviathan minion in 10 miles without hurting anyone else or a 10 mile wide force field that requires minions to roll at a maximum of -2 dice (-7 to -10 dice would be easy) if they want to break through. A Dramatic Failure just fries them and I'd rule that you get auto dramatic failures at -5 dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> So basically it's the usual. A Leviathan against an unprepared city could wipe it from the map without trouble. A Leviathan against a prepared foe with the power of Science! is doomed and the only question is how much damage it inflicts before it's inevitable end. A prepared military base might even withstand the assault. A Marduk base will just ward off the entire swarm with the Sigil. Well, unless mortal Cultists can clear a way in. <hr /><br /> Incubation of the Second Self is there now. It's just a few Adaptations though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-10-2015, 06:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T07:11:46-07:00","id":696034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=695913#post695913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I felt like doing Womb of Horrors - it's now in the updated Channels document and it's a doozy. Aside from being extreemly long. With the obvious shout out Adaptation &quot;Heart of the Swarm&quot; a Sheol 10 Leviathan can create 1000 minions per 4 Ichor, and if those minions eat 4 people it regains 4 Ichor.<br /> <br /> Powerful, but surprisingly counterable. A swarm of minions can't stop mortals from bombing the Leviathan to smithereens and they're not very powerful - to the point that a regular military grade chaingun will probably kill dozens of them every turn.<br /> <br /> And that's against regular humans. A Genius with Katastrofi 5 can build a device that blows up every Leviathan minion in 10 miles without hurting anyone else or a 10 mile wide force field that requires minions to roll at a maximum of -2 dice (-7 to -10 dice would be easy) if they want to break through. A Dramatic Failure just fries them and I'd rule that you get auto dramatic failures at -5 dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> So basically it's the usual. A Leviathan against an unprepared city could wipe it from the map without trouble. A Leviathan against a prepared foe with the power of Science! is doomed and the only question is how much damage it inflicts before it's inevitable end. A prepared military base might even withstand the assault. A Marduk base will just ward off the entire swarm with the Sigil. Well, unless mortal Cultists can clear a way in. <hr /><br /> Incubation of the Second Self is there now. It's just a few Adaptations though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This channel is particularly awesome! The zerg have always been my favorite faction in Starcraft, and this does a great job of capturing them. <br /> <br /> Would a high level adaptation that grants a few more points for either the first/second/third level monster design be too overpowered? Basically representing growing mastery of life manipulation. <br /> <br /> Also, how many points would a baneling style explosion be for monster creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","name":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T03:16:51-07:00","id":696906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tribute of a Dark Heart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=696034#post696034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a high level adaptation that grants a few more points for either the first/second/third level monster design be too overpowered?</div> </div> </div> </div> It might be. Though there's Adaptations that grant more verities of Horrors to represent mastery over life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tribute of a Dark Heart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=696034#post696034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, how many points would a baneling style explosion be for monster creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably two points.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T14:23:37-07:00","id":700123,"title":"","content":"Was reading through the Dagonite write-up, and thinking about Magnanimous Host to All. Would a Familiar-like companion be appropriate as a Merit? Representing a Symbiont either material, or ephmeral/Rift-based?<br /> <br /> (working on write-ups for the mutations...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T18:40:38-07:00","id":700376,"title":"","content":"Wow, after taking the time to read through the leviathan 2E docs I have to say I'm impressed, really stellar job, can't wait for the new mutations. Also are you going to update all the channels ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/530-bloodspeaker","name":"Bloodspeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar530_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T00:48:56-07:00","id":700533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=700123#post700123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was reading through the Dagonite write-up, and thinking about Magnanimous Host to All. Would a Familiar-like companion be appropriate as a Merit? Representing a Symbiont either material, or ephmeral/Rift-based?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the Dagonites I think such symbionites would be closer to a part of their own body/mind even if it's technically walking around next to the Dagonite. Though a Merit that actually lets a part of your own body act like a companion could work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=700123#post700123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(working on write-ups for the mutations...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking forward to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bloodspeaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=700376#post700376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, after taking the time to read through the leviathan 2E docs I have to say I'm impressed, really stellar job, can't wait for the new mutations. Also are you going to update all the channels ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Attribute boosting Channels are being replaced entirely with the new Atavism mechanic. The others I'll decide on a case by case basis - but most of them will probably get at least some tocuh ups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T15:41:28-07:00","id":701346,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how this turned out but the first sample character. Well half charachter, half hints for how to play those Gugal underwater cities that have been mentioned a couple of times.<br /> <br /> One thing I'm determined is that 2E will actually have reasons to go underwater - and putting cities full of people there means that what happens matters rather than underwater just being a place you go to look for that one specific thing then go back to the &quot;real world&quot;.<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Maxwell Clarke, Agent of Atlantis</b></span><br /> <br /> The oceans cover 70% of the planet, in this boundless hidden space dwell countless hidden communities of Hybrid. Most are villages or nomadic tribes with bronze age technology and their Mutations. Others are thriving city states or nations inhabited by the Gugal, the only Lahmasu Strain able to create genetically stable populations.<br /> <br /> Maxwell Clarke hails from one of these thriving city states. One of many underwater nations named Atlantis after the mythical sunken city. Maxwell's Atlantis was formed by the children of Geoffrey Clarke; a Leviathan born in the hight of the British Empire who's plans to travel to the colonies and live like the worst sort of imperial oppressor were cut short; but not so short that he didn't have time to sire dozens of children.<br /> <br /> After Geoffrey died and his children climbed free of his Wake they quickly concluded that Geoffrey was: Firstly, an evil tyrant who had made enemies of both his fellow British and the local population. Secondly, the product of a deeply racist society which incidentally he had frequently introduced his to obviously inhuman children. Thirdly, too dead to protect his children. Fourthly, in possession of a well stocked library detailing how to found a colony. With these facts in mind Geoffrey's children wasted no time in vanishing beneath the waves and founding their own colony. After a few centuries of all the usual drama of national politics and avoiding Bahamut's hereditary curse of stagnation, Atlantis still stands, still embroiled in all the usual drama of national politics.<br /> <br /> And this is where Maxwell comes in.<br /> <br /> A nation state needs it's spies, and Maxwell is one of Atlantis' best. A drop of Hemitheos blood, not enough to make him a Hybrid, set a lust for exploration and adventure within the young Gugal. After being caught trying to leave city limits without a permit Maxwell's parents were encouraged to find an outlet and after trying various options Maxwell chose the intelligence corps for the opportunity to see the surface first hand.<br /> <br /> He did not distinguish himself in a single bold heroic action, nor did he save his mentor's life or dramatically upstage him. Maxwell simply displayed a natural comfort with both surface culture and two dimensional life before steadily rising through the ranks on the back of consistent solid performances. Today he is a highly respected secret agent of Atlantis.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b><br /> <br /> Maxwell doesn't look even remotely human. He is a greyish green colour, save for a white belly, with slippery and slimy fish like skin except for a scaly back. His head is that of a fish with bulging, unblinking eyes, and palpating gills at the side of his neck. His hands and feet are webbed. A discription that applies to hust about everyone in his home city.<br /> <br /> When travelling on the surface Maxwell wears a glamour to conceal his identity and may take any appearance with roughly his size or shape \u2013 from a regular human to curling up and disguising himself as a rock. This disguise would not stand up to a Leviathan's Channels.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints</b><br /> <br /> Atlantis has definitely avoided all contact with Leviathans and if Maxwell identifies one he is unlikely to seek confrontation \u2013 however if he believes this Leviathan is a threat to Atlantis he will go to great lengths to destroy or distract it by provoking a conflict between the Leviathan and human society.<br /> <br /> Maxwell is also a proactive character who is always at work promoting Atlantis' interests and these may conflict with the players. Players might seeking to keep the Tribe hidden might discover that Maxwell has been trading Tribal sorcery for favours or players seeking to recruit Lahmasu into their cult might find they've disappeared beneath the waves to make a new life among \u201ctheir own kind\u201d. Like many Gugal cities Atlantis' population become closer to outright genetic clones each generation and the city has implemented a breeding program to introduce new abilities and remove defects into the population before the genetic template is finalised. Thus one of Maxwell's primary duties is to attract immigrants or acquire sperm and egg samples. Maxwell is particularly known for recruiting from &quot;care homes&quot; for Hybrids and isn't above a little revenge if he thinks the residents have been mistreated; especially if they're fellow Gugal.<br /> <br /> In terms of Resources Maxwell is limited. Atlantis is a magic society first and foremost. Technologically they resemble the western Roman Empire at it's peak but with drastic exceptions, for example their cloning and genetic technology is world class because they brought it from another underwater city who in turn adapted surface technology for underwater (and came up with some nifty discoveries when a few of their scientists went mad at the right moment).<br /> <br /> Magically Atlantis can do most things that WW1 era technology can do, often in a smaller and more convenient package. This is just a generalisation in some areas such as Maxwell's glamour they exceed modern technology. In other areas they lag far behind, most notable in the ability to mass produce anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T13:40:47-08:00","id":757188,"title":"","content":"Is this going on? It has been awfully quite for some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/530-bloodspeaker","name":"Bloodspeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar530_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T18:37:33-08:00","id":757643,"title":"","content":"Presuming so? I'm working on writing up some mutations, but I haven't had time to fine tune any mechanics. I think the lack of dialog slowed down the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T00:57:50-08:00","id":758168,"title":"","content":"Princess hit a busy patch but things have been happening. There's a new Channel, started the introduction, Empyrean Theurgists (I wasn't originally planning them, but I gave in to temptation), started a second pass on Marduk.<br /> <br /> Can you see the recent edits pane if you open the Leviathan folder?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T09:24:19-08:00","id":760705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=758168#post758168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Princess hit a busy patch but things have been happening. There's a new Channel, started the introduction, Empyrean Theurgists (I wasn't originally planning them, but I gave in to temptation), started a second pass on Marduk.<br /> <br /> Can you see the recent edits pane if you open the Leviathan folder?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice, good to know. I'm assuming you mean the google docs folder, no I don't see anything different when I open it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/530-bloodspeaker","name":"Bloodspeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar530_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T17:45:23-08:00","id":761075,"title":"","content":"Recent edits are generally only available to individuals with edit rights, since they can revert docs back to older edits. It's why I encourage the use of &quot;to do&quot; and &quot;continue here&quot; markers in my own Gdocs, since it makes it easier to track progress for myself and readers alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T09:19:21-08:00","id":761547,"title":"","content":"Ah, good to know that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T05:55:38-08:00","id":767009,"title":"","content":"Had another evil thought regarding Call of the Depth: go to the headquarters of say, Credit-Suisse, or any major broker-dealer and give the command &quot;sell everything&quot;. Give the Irrational Economic Actors Task Force something to do.<br /> A Sheol 1 Leviathan doing this a few times could probably bring about a global recession veeeeeery easily.<br /> Actually, an interesting idea would be to mix that with Fight Club to create an antagonist. Pretty much a perfect opponent for a clay school Thalassan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","user":"Thamuzz","date":". 11-16-2015, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T10:50:15-08:00","id":767152,"title":"","content":"I approve of this evil plan!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T12:29:47-08:00","id":767211,"title":"","content":"Now I'm envisioning a scene of WoD &quot;villains&quot; all sitting around a table boasting of their achievements.<br /> <br /> &quot;You've brutally murdered a small town, and think that is some achievement? I've brought woe to <i>nations</i>. My victory is counted in the millions of broken dreams. All those starving mouthes, all those souls ending in the gutter, because of what <i>I</i> brought about. And all it took me was a few afternoons.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T05:34:26-08:00","id":767763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=767211#post767211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm envisioning a scene of WoD &quot;villains&quot; all sitting around a table boasting of their achievements.<br /> <br /> &quot;You've brutally murdered a small town, and think that is some achievement? I've brought woe to <i>nations</i>. My victory is counted in the millions of broken dreams. All those starving mouthes, all those souls ending in the gutter, because of what <i>I</i> brought about. And all it took me was a few afternoons.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Then a Beast, a Namtaru Ravager, raises his hand and quietly says, &quot;Um, yes, well, uh, I invented reality TV.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T11:37:29-08:00","id":767973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=767763#post767763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then a Beast, a Namtaru Ravager, raises his hand and quietly says, &quot;Um, yes, well, uh, I invented reality TV.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good way to get murdered by the rest of the table...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T21:28:13-08:00","id":768277,"title":"","content":"So, I was reading the Leviathans and Beasts thread over in the Beasts forum, and it made me curious about something. I don't know if this has been spelled out in the docs so far or not, so I'm asking here.<br /> <br /> In general, WoD games tend to follow a principle of scaling powers, where the higher your Power Stat, the mightier you are. How strongly does Leviathan follow this principle?<br /> <br /> I ask not because I think Leviathan wouldn't follow that general principle, but because, in the wake of the Marduk Society debacle/underground fire, I was curious just how powerful elder Leviathans are planned on being.<br /> <br /> The reason why? In my opinion, high Sheol Leviathans should be, pardon the language, <b>fucking <i>terrifying</i></b>.<br /> <br /> Leviathans are supposed to be Old Gods still lingering in the mortal world, to the point that TKR said in one post that Leviathans are one of the few things he envisions in his headcanon to legitimately claim the position of Divine. And while we may have outgrown our need to worship them for comfort, that should <b>not</b>, in my opinion, negate the fact that humans should be <i>terrified</i> of them.<br /> <br /> Look at it like this; we know all about hurricanes, earthquakes and tidal waves now. We know what causes them, we understand where they come from, we no longer believe we need to sacrifice people to keep them from happening. That does <i>not</i> stop us from being scared of them. We take desperate precautions against them, we avidly watch for them, and even then, when they hit, all we can do is huddle in safety and pray that we'll make it through alive.<br /> <br /> And that, to me, is what an Elder Leviathan should be. A living disaster. Sure, they may not want to be - part of the tragedy of being a leviathan is to be alienated from humans at every step; like Mages, their powers only emphasize how different they are, how they can't be with humans no matter how much they want to. But that doesn't change the fact that when a God speaks. the world <b>trembles</b>.<br /> <br /> Sheol 1-2 Leviathans being fairly weak and easy prey, comparatively speaking, is fine. But when the Sheol 10 monsters crawl from the deep, that should be an &quot;oh, fuck me...&quot; moment for hunters. To stand before such an abomination is to forsake the right to laugh at your primitive ancestors and to understand intimately why they crawled on their bellies along the beach beneath the gibbous moon, offering tokens of blood and gold to the Masters from the Sea. You may stand defiant, you may use your arsenal to drive it back into the sea, but you know in your heart that you only slowed it for a time.<br /> <br /> Leviathan: The Cult Chronicles are, at their heart, a horror game. And whilst some of that horror comes to the Leviathans themselves - the horror of being outcast by what you are, the horror of seeing how your elders and future selves are as alien to you as you are to humans - more of that horror should be the impact on humanity from a Leviathan's presence.<br /> <br /> I have never read Delta Green, myself. But this description of one piece of fluff, describing how a retired operative has to be killed after a backed-up septic tank causes him to experience PTSD flashbacks of an anti-Deep Ones mission and butcher his family, haunts me.<br /> <br /> This, to me, is essential to the &quot;feel&quot; of Leviathan. The horror from humans is living it. The horror from <i>Leviathans</i> is know that you did this to them - even if you didn't want to.<br /> <br /> Many pages back, there was an intense argument about the proposed nature of the Marduk Society. In passing, I feel now that, whilst I wasn't happy with their portrayal before, I could be happy with it now... <b>if</b> it takes these motifs into account.<br /> <br /> The price of being a hero is the terrible, soul-crushing toil of battling Leviathans. It is murdering cultists whose minds have been shattered beyond repair, staining yourself with innocent blood so that greater numbers of innocents may never face this fate themselves. It is standing toe to toe with creatures who would rend your body and soul asunder with ease and knowing that even if you succeed this day, the scars will linger with you forever. It is knowing the injustice of it all, that you could do so much more, but you can do nothing to help; for you are the thin line that keeps back the wrath of monstrosities that could destroy all that humanity has built.<br /> <br /> And, on the other side of the battlefield, the Leviathan weeps; it did not want this, it did not want to hurt these people, but hurt them it did, for such is its nature. It cared for them as best it could, trying to be as kind as a being born of cruelty can. And now it must watch them die, cut down whilst screaming prayers to a god who cannot save them, their confusion and loss bubbling like blood between their dying lips. And it knows that, even if it survives today, it will all happen again in the future. But it cannot let it end in death. The beast that is their flesh will not let their life just slip away. The god that is their soul will not tolerate such insolence from mortals. And so it rises, to continue the age-old bloody dance, as it will tomorrow and tomorrow and tomorrow...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T10:58:19-08:00","id":768605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=768277#post768277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, WoD games tend to follow a principle of scaling powers, where the higher your Power Stat, the mightier you are. How strongly does Leviathan follow this principle?</div> </div> </div> </div> I never thought that was a strong principle.<br /> <br /> Take vampires for example. Vigor, Resilliance and Clerity have a far bigger impact on a vampire's combat power than Blood Potency. Majesty has a bigger impact on your social power. etc.<br /> <br /> But in answer to your actual question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=768277#post768277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I was curious just how powerful elder Leviathans are planned on being.<br /> <br /> The reason why? In my opinion, high Sheol Leviathans should be, pardon the language, <b>fucking <i>terrifying</i></b>.</div> </div> </div> </div> While some powers are locked behind Sheol requirements even a starting Leviathan is &quot;fucking terrifying&quot;. Call of the Depths alone can create carnage on a mass scale. The psychological impact on a nation of a Leviathan using Call of the Depth to make everyone start killing should easily rival 9/11.<br /> <br /> The general idea is that a powerful Leviathan can single handedly level a city (but is unlikely to survive the amount of enemies they make doing so), and a powerful Leviathan's cult is roughly equal to ISIS at the hight of it's power.<br /> <br /> Terrifying enough for you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-18-2015, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T10:32:38-08:00","id":777227,"title":"","content":"Inspiration comes and goes in waves, things have been a little slow recently but I did just create a Channel inspired by Yog Sothos. This replaces Orberos' Kin (and probably Memories Before Time as well)<br /> <br /> The idea of being able to obliterate your past without consequence came from Genius' Manes. It seemed fitting that as creatures of primordial chaos Leviathans aren't bound by orderly things like action -&gt; consequences. That said, unlike Archmages who also have a similar trick I think the most fitting use is to investigate your family history and make small changes to the very recent past. Tearing up all of reality, while awesome, is more a (arch)Mage thing than a Leviathan.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Key and the Gate (Descendent Channel)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Leviathan is not merely a thing of one Space-Time continuum, but allied to the ultimate animating essence of existence's whole unbounded sweep.</i></span></span><ul><li><ul><li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: Intelligence + Composure + Sheol</span></span></b></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action Type: Instant (no matter how long is spent in the past)</span></span></b></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Key and the Gate allows the Leviathan to stretch his perceptions across Time itself, at first they may only perceive but at deeper Depths a Leviathan may change the past. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As multidimensional beings of primordial chaos Leviathans frequently create temporal paradoxes and rarely care that they do. Damage to the fabric of spacetime is never predictable, but most commonly a Leviathan just ignores paradox. One who goes back in time and kills her grandmother returns to a timeline where her parents were never born and changes have spread forth like wind from a butterfly\u2019s wings; but she appeared ex nihilo at the point of her emergence and followed a similar life path from that point. The same usually happens if you go back and kill your rivals grandmother. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Killing the Leviathan themself is more likely to work, the closer to the present you do the deed the more likely it is. However if the Leviathan survives they\u2019re instantly aware of the attempt, if the Leviathan has this Channel they\u2019re also aware of exactly when the event took place and might pop back to see who did it. However there are risks, while a Leviathan is travelling back they are as vulnerable as they would be in the present. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Even in extreme situations - if a Leviathan went back and turned her home nation into an atomic wasteland - she will likely populate the new timeline with enough fragments of the original to preserve her life path. However such stupidity will fray spacetime to the breaking point and likely draw furious protectors of reality from all corners of the World of Darkness and beyond. That\u2019s if the Leviathan doesn\u2019t return to the present to find she\u2019s torn a huge hole in the spacetime continuum and is now floating outside reality (Leviathans can survive outside reality, but they generally don\u2019t like it there and it\u2019s hard to get back). Intelligent Leviathans stick to making small changes to the recent past.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fortunately this Channel endows the Tribe with an instinctive understanding of spacetime. It\u2019s far from perfect, but a Leviathan gets a bad feeling about any action which would cause too much damage.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 0\u201d: Birthright of Awareness</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 1\u201d: By spending one Ichor the Leviathan may inhabit the body of his past self. She has no control over his actions but complete control of his senses. She may focus on things her past self does did not and may spend Ichor in the present to activate Channels in the past so long as they are only used for observation. If the Leviathan has changed their past they see their past in the present time line, this is useful for filling in any blanks left by changes to the past. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 1\u201d: The Leviathan can perceive disruptions to spacetime. Depending on the disruption\u2019s nature this may be automatic or require a Wits + Composure + Sheol roll. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 2\u201d: If the Leviathan stands in a location that exists in more than one timeline they may choose to peer into any timeline they wish, and may use other Channels to enhance their perception. In addition the Leviathan is instantly aware if another version of themselves exists in any of the other timelines. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sidebar: Thy Greatest Enemy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It\u2019s rare to find temporal duplicates of the same Leviathan. Even when the timeline is split before the Leviathan is born, it is more common for all but one iteration to slide between timelines and become part of a merged being with personality and memories from every iteration. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Which is not to say it never happens. When temporal duplicates of a Leviathan exist they are all part of the same organism. Not in the way your hands are both part of you, there is no \u201chead\u201d containing a core brain above both Leviathans, instead think of conjoined twins. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Because they\u2019re technically the same individual both Leviathans are vulnerable to the other\u2019s psychic Channels and easy targets for Rituals. Naturally Leviathans dislike anyone having this power and it is not unknown for Leviathans to lead their Cults into war to destroy or assimilate their alternates.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 3\u201d: By spending two Ichor the Leviathan may see out of the perception of their Ancestors, they may not see through other Leviathans or go past a Leviathan on their family tree unless they can find a detour through human or Hybrid branches. The roll is automatically Contested by Composure + Supernatural Advantage, and this means that seeing through the eyes of another Leviathan is extremely hard though if a Leviathan achieves it she may use any Channels they have in common to enhance their perception. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 4\u201d: The Leviathan may now use the Depth 1 iteration on their future self and the Depth 3 iteration on their discendents. As the future is in constant flux Leviathans may create any paradox they want without consequence; usually. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 5\u201d: In the World of Darkness there is a past, a constantly moving present, and infinite possible futures. At this Depth the Leviathan can perceive not just their future self and future descendants but all their future selves and descendants and peer into possible futures other than the most probable one. For example the Leviathan may peer into the future where they decided to sacrifice their entire cult to acquire some guarded information (simply deciding to do that then changing your mind later isn\u2019t enough, since it was always more probable that you\u2019d rescind the order before acquiring the information).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cDepth 6\u201d: By spending four Ichor the Leviathan may not only inhabit the senses but take full control and act to change the past (or the future, though there is rarely any point in doing so). </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T04:38:17-08:00","id":777674,"title":"","content":"Have you played Achron? I think that is probably the best representation of what a Leviathan with this would play like.<br /> Giving players the ability to mash the reset button on a story practically out of the gates is kinda worrying from a ST perspective.<br /> <br /> Some thoughts on strains that favor awareness:<br /> Bahamutan: As the past was, so shall be the future. I shall permit no surprises to disrupt my peace.<br /> Bahamutan alt: When I turn into an (extra) giant monster, I know when to turn into a giant amoeba to avoid getting hit by the killsat.<br /> Lahamin: It is as I have forseen. As usual.<br /> Lahamin alt: I'm in yer past, killing yer dudes.<br /> Nu: I know when to call the storms.<br /> Tanninim: What do you mean, its wrong to punish you for your future transgressions?<br /> <br /> Not favoring awareness, but wanting this one<br /> Thalassans: Why the hell aren't my stocks going the way they should? What the hell do you mean, my actions affect the market?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T10:03:50-08:00","id":777806,"title":"","content":"I plan to revisit it once Mage is out to see what limitations are needed - but on the whole I don't think out the gate is much worse than requiring a little exp. Storytellers face the same issues either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T11:09:47-08:00","id":777829,"title":"","content":"What about limiting the time spent temporally projecting? Maybe higher Sheol Leviathans can play in the past or future longer? That forces newly transformed Leviathans to get crap done quick (encouraging them screwing things up, thus acting as a natural &quot;filter&quot; for potential Chrononauts), while mightier Leviathans can take their &quot;time&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T12:45:25-08:00","id":777860,"title":"","content":"Ask me again after Mage is published or has time travel mechanics spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T05:32:53-08:00","id":780519,"title":"","content":"Small suggestion for that time-travelling Channel of yours. Did you ever consider reading up on the Aing-Tii Monks' flow walking technique on Wookieepedia? Maybe it might inspire some ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T12:59:41-08:00","id":781810,"title":"","content":"I had a look but nothing comes from it. There doesn't seem to be much on Wookieepedia that's relevant to mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T17:03:21-08:00","id":798481,"title":"","content":"So, just wondering how this project is coming along?<br /> <br /> Also, I was curious; has it ever been discussed that maybe the Leviathans have kindred? In Judaic myths, Leviathan was the beast of the sea, but it was countered/contrasted by Behemoth of the land and Ziz of the sky. Perhaps these could be mythical - or even optionally canonical? - branches of the family tree who follow the same basic rules as Leviathans, but who owe their nature to land or aerial creatures instead, which slightly alters their perspective on things, even though they are still members of the same Wicked Tribe?<br /> <br /> Just so I'm not mistaken, Hybrids will be taking the equivalent role as Ghouls and Wolf-blooded, yes? With Beloved being the equivalent of Mummy Witnesses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T23:56:54-08:00","id":799107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=798481#post798481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, just wondering how this project is coming along?</div> </div> </div> </div> Slowly. Inspiration comes and goes in cycles. I did start on the School of Sand recently though if you want to check out the google docs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=798481#post798481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I was curious; has it ever been discussed that maybe the Leviathans have kindred? In Judaic myths, Leviathan was the beast of the sea, but it was countered/contrasted by Behemoth of the land and Ziz of the sky.</div> </div> </div> </div> They're already in 1E if you want to look at them. I'm not sure if they'll go in 2E though, I was never that satisifed with them.<br /> <br /> I might save them for a suppliment...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=798481#post798481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just so I'm not mistaken, Hybrids will be taking the equivalent role as Ghouls and Wolf-blooded, yes? With Beloved being the equivalent of Mummy Witnesses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Leviathan is doing things slightly differently.<br /> <br /> For all intents and purposes Hybrids share the same thematic roles as humans, they have powers, but they don't really <i>relate</i> to the tribe differently.<br /> <br /> Being beloved closer to a blood bond than anything else in Vampire. Both humans and Hybrids can be affected equally. The average Beloved will be the faceless masses that make up the Leviathan's cult, but you'd get the occasional high priest and other important NPC.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T15:40:03-07:00","id":846754,"title":"","content":"I have no idea if this project is still on-going, but I had some thoughts bubbling around in my head and I just had to get them out.<br /> <br /> Way, way back in this thread, back on page 14, I made a post about how the Leviathans represent the primordial darkness, the &quot;bestial nature&quot; of humanity that we try to tell ourselves we have conquered, but which may in turn conquer us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As was commented a page or two back, humanity is STILL, at heart, little more than an animal. We wear our clothes and use our tools and perform our rituals and tell ourselves that this makes us better than the beast. We shun the dark and foul impulses from our primeval self. But the Leviathans? They are US, stripped of all our trinkets and talismans. They are the beast within brought to hideous life, the living reminder of the bloody seas from which we dragged ourselves. They are our darkest impulses and most primeval natures garbed in hideous, ever-shifting flesh. We might try to deny them, we do so with great success... but we cannot eradicate them. And, perhaps, we never will.<br /> <br /> Leviathans are scary because they represent the darkness humanity was born in, and that it still hasn't finished clawing its way out of. Worse, they represent the possibility that we may - or even that we <i>will</i> - lose our grip and be swallowed by it once again.<br /> <br /> Their time has passed... and yet, their time may come again. That is not dead which can eternal lie. And with strange aeons, even death may die. What was once mundane is now unthinkable, and may yet, in time, become mundane again. The light may burn so brightly, but darkness is eternal; in the end, darkness will always swallow the light. </div> </div> </div>The more I've thought about it, the more I've realised; this is actually very close to Lovecraft's own writings on the Mythos. See, the Mythos has never been about Good vs. Evil - August Derleth's interjections aside. Indeed, Lovecraft all but calls them out as purely human inventions. But Order vs. Chaos - the attempts by sentients to impose order on an ultimately chaotic and indifferent universe, that's another story.<br /> <br /> Moreover, Lovecraft's writings are significantly embedded in his own cultural zeitgeist, of which he was admittedly on the extreme side even for his time. The defining attributes of what makes many of his stories scary is a compound.<br /> <br /> The first element, is Xenophobia - Fear of the Other, fear of that which is different, alien, new, that's a huge part of what made Lovecraft's works scary at the time. Indeed, this is what Lovecraft himself had to say on it, proving the importance of xenophobia to his works:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>&quot;The oldest and strongest emotion of mankind is fear, and the oldest and strongest kind of fear is fear of the unknown.&quot;</i> </div> </div> </div>The other element is... I'm not sure if I'm using the right terminology, but this feels right: Cultural Imperialism. Lovecraft grew up in a time in which WASP supremacy, the dominance of the world by WASP culture and its superiority to all other cultures were taken as given by its given. They were considered &quot;natural laws&quot;, as inherent and as obvious as the sun rising in the morning. That's why Lovecraft's heroes tend to go mad; they are forcibly confronted with proof that this deeply held belief is wrong, and they can't take it that they aren't the pinnacle of life.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, this is also why some of Lovecraft's works... haven't aged terribly well. I can easily name &quot;Facts Concerning the Late Arthur Jermyn and His Family&quot; and &quot;Medusa's Coils&quot; as two that just don't hold up today, as we've progressed beyond the mentality to see them in as terrible a light as their author intended.<br /> <br /> So, what I'm getting at is this: Stagnation vs. Progress is good as a secondary element. The Cthulhu Mythos itself is built on the great cycle of birth, growth, stagnation, decay, death and rebirth; the Elder Things had their time, and now it's humanity's time, but humanity is also going to fall in time. But I think a stronger element to build this revamp on is the conflict between Order and Chaos. It's something that can be done both internally - the Leviathans' need to control versus their powerful, primeval instincts and urges - and externally. It gives a more ambiguous nature to the Leviathans, and also gives them a hope spot.<br /> <br /> As I touched upon in that earlier post I commented, a big problem with Leviathan is that currently, it has overtones that are <b>too</b> dark. There's a trope called &quot;Audience Alienating Premise&quot;, and several of the canon World of Darkness games have fallen into it. If Leviathan is too bleak, it risks running into the exact same problems as Promethean and, closer still, Wraith before it; it becomes so dark a setting that nobody wants to play in it. And that's a certain death for a game. Prometheans at least have the New Dawn to look forward to, and we've received some hints that Promethean 2e is going to be tuning down some of the Hate Plague effect, for this simple reason. Leviathan needs some silver linings, or nobody's going to want anything to do with it.<br /> <br /> Also, while Marduk representing Order and Progress is fine, one needs to remember that the Chronicles of Darkness depict a Black and Gray Morality sort of world. Progress always comes with a cost, and that needs to be respected if Marduk and the other anti-Leviathan groups are going to actually enjoy respect. I mean, the cost/fearsomeness of progress was actually a part of Lovecraft's inspiration behind writing the Mythos in the first place:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While most people of his time were entranced by the technological innovation produced by the Industrial Revolution, Lovecraft was deeply suspicious of modern technology and the poorly-understood powers it vested in mankind. All of his work resonates with the terror of the newly-discovered magnitude of the universe, which in the early period of his life was believed to consist entirely of the Milky Way. Einstein's theory of relativity opened a door into teleportation, time travel, and alien geometry, and radically altered peoples' notion of space-time itself, while the discovery of pre-Cambrian fossils and Wegener's then-new-and-controversial hypothesis of continental drift brought the notion that the Earth was far older than previously believed, and that even the shape of the continents was not set in stone. All of this was subtly addressed in Lovecraft's stories of alien horror, and of the remains of ancient civilizations lost to the abyss of geological deep time.<br /> <br /> The dizzying speed of progress of his time was compounded by an expansion of the unknown. Each new development, instead of reducing the number of questions as had been expected by pre-modern philosophers, instead compounded them exponentially. Leibniz had hoped that the entire world could be described by reason, and that this is the best of all possible worlds \u2014 a possibility utterly abolished during Lovecraft's writing period. Each new discovery only increased humanity's knowledge of its own ignorance and insignificance, encouraging a nihilistic atmosphere, and this is perhaps the central theme of Lovecraft's incisive fiction </div> </div> </div>Finally... this is something I'm going to get a lot of hate for, but I think it needs to be said. Changes in culture aren't always a good thing. We've made a lot of progress in some ways since the Bronze Age, but in others, we've honestly gone backwards.<br /> <br /> Let us examine the case of Alan Turing. The man who saved Britain during WW2 with his codebreaking skills, the man who invented the Turing Test... the man who injected an apple with strychnine and ate it, committing suicide, after the same government he saved realised he was a homosexual, publicly prosecuted him as a criminal on crimes of immorality and indecency, and blacklisted him, until he couldn't live with a shame. Which culture would he consider superior? Britain of the 1950s? Or the Pagan Roman Empire, where his sexuality and his relationship with a younger man would have been seen as natural as the sun and moon?<br /> <br /> Much of the fearfulness in Lovecraft's work is born of the breaking of &quot;irrefutable laws&quot;, of conventionally held wisdom as to what constitutes morality and decency. But, as the example shows, aren't some laws better off <i>being</i> broken? This adds some gray to the Leviathans; they are chaos, yes, but they also hold in them freedom from order's bonds, from the society that stifles and strangles people for being &quot;different&quot;.<br /> <br /> I am not advocating that Leviathans should be some blatant GLBTIA metaphor. That's hamfisted, crude, and just generally offensive to everyone<br /> <br /> But Leviathans are the Outsiders, they are the Other. They are the shadow that terrifies those inside the circle, but which offers sanctuary, comfort and shelter to those who are similarly outcast. Leviathans do not merely force people into slavery, they actively draw other outsiders to them. It doesn't matter who you are; there may be no place for you in the System, but the Leviathans will take you. That, I think, could be an interesting angle to explore and exploit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","user":"VoidDrifter","date":". 03-13-2016, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T07:42:56-07:00","id":847059,"title":"","content":"So, the Wake attracts the more broken (low Integrity), rather than <i>making</i> people insane, at least passively?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:24:37-07:00","id":847175,"title":"","content":"The Wake is never going to not make people insane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=846754#post846754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, Lovecraft all but calls them out as purely human inventions. But Order vs. Chaos - the attempts by sentiments to impose order on an ultimately chaotic and indifferent universe, that's another story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember though, that while Leviathan is unashamedly influenced by Lovecraft. Lovecraft is not the only influence, and it is not even the primary influence. The primary influence is the Chaosmkampf.<br /> <br /> Leviathan's ideas of Good/Evil and Order/Chaos are taken from the Chaosmkampf and not Lovecraft. The Leviathan universe is not ultimately chaotic. It is ultimately ordered, and has been since<br /> <br /> 1) Marduk killed Tiamat and destroyed the Antediluvian world as the Tribe claims.<br /> <br /> 2) God divided the sea and land as book of Genesis claims.<br /> <br /> 3) Zeus, Marduk, Yehovah, etc killed their respective opponent - Typhon/Tiamat/Leviathan and reforged the universe in their imagage as Indo-European mythology claims<br /> <br /> 4) Human culture evolved, step by step, through completely mundane means until things became fairly orderly.<br /> <br /> Pick one of them, or all of them. It's not like any charachter in a WoD game will know the ultimate truth.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course the universe was remade once (maybe), who's to say it can't be remade a second time? Leviathan is at heart a game about a single question &quot;what do the Gods of primordial chaos do <i>after</i> they've been defeated in the Chaosmkampf?&quot; Regroup your forces and come back for a rematch is one possible answer.<br /> <br /> Of course it's not going to be easy. But just like destoriyng the God Machine is possible for Demons, and dethroning the Exarchs for Mages (DaveB's game did it) so to is destroying the Marduk Society, mankind's governments, etc and creating a world of chaos where the Tribe rule supreme (arguably it's a lot easier than defeating the God Machine).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=846754#post846754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Leviathan is too bleak, it risks running into the exact same problems as Promethean and, closer still, Wraith before it</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone who loves Promethean 1E I'm not seeing any reasons for concern here. While I've never played Wrath, it was considered to be a masterpiece so again it's not a cause for concern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=846754#post846754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which culture would he consider superior? Britain of the 1950s? Or the Pagan Roman Empire, where his sexuality and his relationship with a younger man would have been seen as natural as the sun and moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is cherry picking of the highest order. I could just as easily ask which culture is considered better, Britain of the 1950s? Or the Pagan Roman Empire where <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pater_familias#Children\" target=\"_blank\">deformed children were legally required to be put to death</a>?<br /> <br /> Different areas have progressed at different rates, and it's fairly common for something to improve and something else to get worse at the same time. However overall the trend of history has been positive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=846754#post846754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This adds some gray to the Leviathans; they are chaos, yes, but they also hold in them freedom from order's bonds, from the society that stifles and strangles people for being &quot;different&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Have you read the Strains document? Stifling and strangling people for being &quot;different&quot; is the core theme of the Bahamatan's Wake.<br /> <br /> Or stepping back from the individual Strains. If you want to find belonging in a group that embraces freedom and individuality, you do not want to join a <u><i>Cult</i></u>.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but this suggestion just doens't make any sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=846754#post846754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Leviathans are the Outsiders, they are the Other.</div> </div> </div> </div>The exact opposite. Leviathans are metaphors for mankind's most savage and primal emotions. Bahamatans are conformity. Thalassans are greed. Nu are superstition. All of which are taken to an unhealthy extreme; and nobody in Leviathan others people as much as an Oceanead's Beloved.<br /> <br /> Thus you cannot point to two different groups and say that this group is Dominant and that group is the Other - and thus Leviathans will be found in the Other group. Leviathans are metaphors for things that are part of every human and so no matter how you divide humanity in groups, Leviathans will be part of every single group.<br /> <br /> And the same goes for the Marduk society (and Empyrean Thurgists; who are basically the exact same idea but with mechanics that make them suitable antagonists when the Marduk society would be too powerful).<br /> <br /> The battle between humanity and Leviathans is not a metaphor for the struggles between the dominant group and the outgroup. It's a metaphor for the struggle between the civilisation and savage that's within each individual human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=846754#post846754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there may be no place for you in the System, but the Leviathans will take you. That, I think, could be an interesting angle to explore and exploit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Beast. There's no need to write Beast a second time.<br /> <br /> At least I think that's what the writers were going for (at least in the first draft - who knows what the intent was with Beast). It would probably go as badly as the first Beast draft though. With the amount of destruction Leviathans cause it would too easily sound like if you don't fit into the System join the terrorists, and Leviathan is already full of religious themes... yeah. I can't see that working too well.<br /> <br /> [Edit] I should add that, Bahamatans will usually take you in and offer protection if you're willing to give up your independence and individuality in return - it's certainly not freedom from the System but it's something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-14-2016, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T23:04:10-07:00","id":850432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=847175#post847175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember though, that while Leviathan is unashamedly influenced by Lovecraft. Lovecraft is not the only influence, and it is not even the primary influence. The primary influence is the Chaosmkampf.<br /> <br /> Leviathan's ideas of Good/Evil and Order/Chaos are taken from the Chaosmkampf and not Lovecraft. The Leviathan universe is not ultimately chaotic. It is ultimately ordered, and has been since<br /> <br /> 1) Marduk killed Tiamat and destroyed the Antediluvian world as the Tribe claims.<br /> <br /> 2) God divided the sea and land as book of Genesis claims.<br /> <br /> 3) Zeus, Marduk, Yehovah, etc killed their respective opponent - Typhon/Tiamat/Leviathan and reforged the universe in their imagage as Indo-European mythology claims<br /> <br /> 4) Human culture evolved, step by step, through completely mundane means until things became fairly orderly.<br /> <br /> Pick one of them, or all of them. It's not like any charachter in a WoD game will know the ultimate truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, one has to ask if the Chaosmkampf is really that good of a choice of an influence for this game's settings - or at least if your application of it isn't undercutting the viability of this game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666117#post666117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, I have known you for a few years now, and ... you have a pattern of falling in love with an idea and categorically refusing to reconsider it or change it in any way. I don't know whether that helps you on your personal projects, but it's a serious problem when you're collaborating with others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I bring this comment up because it's relevant here. Although it was initially brought up in regards the debate about Marduk, I'm seriously worrying about the general mood of Leviathans as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=847175#post847175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as someone who loves Promethean 1E I'm not seeing any reasons for concern here. While I've never played Wraith, it was considered to be a masterpiece so again it's not a cause for concern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a masterpiece does not necessarily mean &quot;being playable&quot;, and that's what I was commenting on. The bleaker a setting is, the harder it is to sell players on; I get that you love the Chaosmkampf motif, but as someone who hopes to either play this or run this, I genuinely worry that it's either going to be too awful to get into, or else that describing it will just put off any potential players.<br /> <br /> Like I said, Promethean is bleak, but at least it has a ray of hope in it. The New Dawn and everything related to it ultimately adds an optimistic aspect to the game. It's not perfect, there wouldn't be so many topics arguing about the fundamental theme of Promethean if it wasn't contentious, but still, at the end of the day, Prometheans as hate sinks is explicitly something they can overcome. It's a long, winding road full of struggle, strife and toil, but they can overcome their limitations, and that adds some poignancy to their struggle, some meaning to their existence.<br /> <br /> Leviathans... don't have that, as far as I'm aware. Maybe you've undertaken a lot of updating on the gdocs and just never spoken about them, so I've no idea what you've done. But, when all I have to fall back on is quotes like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=666037#post666037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There absolutely is! Leviathans have an uncontrollable sanity destroying psychic aura. Leviathans cannot ethically be in the physical presence of normal humans for an extended period of time, not in 1E nor in 2E.<br /> <br /> What's more a Leviathan who avoids all human contact will slowly loose their mind to loneliness and becomes an evil monster - regular humans can go mad from lonlines and Leviathans have two other minds fighting their human one for dominance.<br /> <br /> The whole point is that there's no way a Leviathan can survive that's remotely ethical. Their very existance harms others, and then exploring how you build a life and a self identity in that situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That indicates what I have to think on when I contemplate the setting. This is, in all honesty, even bleaker than anything that the Prometheans have to put up with, and I can't speak for anyone else here, but it robs me of a lot of investiture in the setting. This is not engaging. This is the equivalent of the stereotypical &quot;wangfesting&quot; stigma associated with the Old World of Darkness in the 90s. It doesn't make me want to pick up the game. It makes me want to ignore the game's very existence and go do something more productive. Like shooting myself in the head.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=847175#post847175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The battle between humanity and Leviathans is a metaphor for the struggle between the civilisation and savage that's within each individual human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this, this is something I can sink my teeth into... IF it's done well. It's a nice metaphor, but if Leviathan is to be a successful game, it cannot forget that, as much as it represents this metaphor, you're still supposed to be playing the Leviathans.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, then Leviathan needs to do either - or, better still, both - of two things.<br /> <br /> Firstly, it's got to keep things in a proper perspective.<br /> <br /> Yes, we're the &quot;Most Wicked Tribe&quot;, but if that's the case, then the theme of the game should involve embracing that. Let us run rampant with our wickedness, let us accept who we are... without devolving into mere caricatures. We should be the Sabbat, the Pure, the Seers of the Throne, the Centimani, never Belial's Brood, the Bale Hounds, the Sclesti. <br /> <br /> We cannot ever be the White Hats... but, at least we can be the Lighter Shade of Gray. Let Leviathan, at its core, be a tale of Evil vs. Evil, and it can stand more readily on its own fins as a game that one can enjoy. It's amazing how easily one can accept being &quot;the bad guy&quot; if at least we can take aim at &quot;the worse guy&quot;.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the metaphor needs both sides to be equally valid.<br /> <br /> What you seem to be doing is weighing things too heavily towards Civilization/Order = Good, Savage/Chaos = Evil.<br /> <br /> I can guarantee you that playing the overwhelmed underdog is a very niche appeal when the setting keeps harping on about your powerlessness.<br /> <br /> Look at Werewolf, both Apocalypse and Forsaken. You're doomed going in, you know that. But still, every victory you carve out is that much more meaningful. It stops mattering so much that the ultimate end is pointless, so long as, until the end comes, you can enjoy your personal victories. <br /> <br /> Apocalypse in particular has a theme of doomed epics and glorious destruction that I feel is perfectly mineable for Leviathan. If we are the dwindling eras of a bygone age, then let us go out not with a whimper, but with a roar. If we must die, then let us leave scars upon the world humanity has taken from us, so that our legacy will never be undone. Let us go down fighting, if we must go down.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=847175#post847175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Of course the universe was remade once (maybe), who's to say it can't be remade a second time? Leviathan is at heart a game about a single question &quot;what do the Gods of primordial chaos do <i>after</i> they've been defeated in the Chaosmkampf?&quot; Regroup your forces and come back for a rematch is one possible answer.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Of course it's not going to be easy. But just like destroying the God Machine is possible for Demons, and dethroning the Exarchs for Mages (DaveB's game did it) so to is destroying the Marduk Society, mankind's governments, etc and creating a world of chaos where the Tribe rule supreme (arguably it's a lot easier than defeating the God Machine).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>If this is truly the case, then the game needs to support it more. If I didn't feel that the game was presenting the exact opposite of this, that it was robbing the Leviathans of all agency and making them a game devoted to being the punchline in a &quot;Shoot the Shaggy Dog&quot; Story, I wouldn't complain as much as I do.<br /> <br /> That, more than anything, is what I want of Leviathan. If we're to be the underdog, then give us teeth. Victory must be an option, or there is no point to playing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=847175#post847175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to find belonging in a group that embraces freedom and individuality, you do not want to join a <u><i>Cult</i></u>.<br /> <br /> [Edit] I should add that, Bahamatans will usually take you in and offer protection if you're willing to give up your independence and individuality in return - it's certainly not freedom from the System but it's something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. But do you know why people do join a cult? Because it offers a place to fit in. No brainwashing aura or madness required. People will do awful, unspeakable things to find and hold a place &quot;in the group&quot;. That's how cults are born, that's how they grow - and, if a cult can become mainstream enough, become accepted enough, that's when &quot;cult&quot; makes the progression to &quot;culture&quot; (or, if we want to be cynical here, &quot;religion&quot;, but they're about the same thing).<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that Leviathans should lose the Wake, it's too intrinsic to their Cosmic Horror motif, but it adds bite to their &quot;we are the Savage that lurks within humanity's breast&quot; motif if there are genuine reasons why mortals would fall into a Leviathan's cult without needing to be mind raped first.<br /> <br /> As I said above, if Leviathan is to stand on the &quot;War between Civilisation and Savage&quot; metaphor, then both sides need to have equal punch to them. Both sides must have their good points and their bad points, or the game loses its hook for players.<br /> <br /> <br /> In summary, I want to say this: Leviathan should be the game of being a monster, with all of the horror and all of the glory that entails. Let us embrace our monstrosity, let us accept ourselves, like ourselves, and feel justified spitting in the eye of humanity for saying we should not exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T06:31:41-07:00","id":850527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, one has to ask if the Chaosmkampf is really that good of a choice of an influence for this game's settings - or at least if your application of it isn't undercutting the viability of this game.</div> </div> </div> </div> A fair question.<br /> <br /> The answer is that it works fine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bring this comment up because it's relevant here.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think you'll find any successful (defining successful as actually finishing at least one large project) fanwriter who dozen't show shades of this. Without that streak of stubbornness we'd get board half way though. MB and myself are just as bad as each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, Promethean is bleak, but at least it has a ray of hope in it.</div> </div> </div> </div> IMO Promethian is the most hopeful WoD game there is. Vampire is much worse. Promethian is about becoming more human and more moral over time, Vampire is the opposite.<br /> <br /> Leviathan is closer to Vampire. But even as far back as 1E we had an example charachter who found a way out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leviathans... don't have that, as far as I'm aware. Maybe you've undertaken a lot of updating on the gdocs and just never spoken about them</div> </div> </div> </div> They've had ways out since 1E. Look for Davy Jones in the Evolutions appendix. He's made a bargain with a death god, if he works as a psychopomp he gets paid with time as mortal human.<br /> <br /> Earlier in the thread I mentioned that isolating yourself with an Atoll is another way out; and since I said that Atolls were given a new power that can let them turn a Leviathan's Wake off.<br /> <br /> If you're going to make sweeping criticisms of Leviathan you really should at least make sure you're criticising what I've actually said and written first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, we're the &quot;Most Wicked Tribe&quot;, but if that's the case, then the theme of the game should involve embracing that. Let us run rampant with our wickedness, let us accept who we are...</div> </div> </div> </div> That's the School of the Sun; there's a rough draft Schools document already. Have a read, let me know if that's what you were hoping for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">without devolving into mere caricatures.</div> </div> </div> </div> School of the Sun's core philosophy: Religion is a covenant, write down the damn contract with your Beloved and stick to your side of the deal. If you're promised rain for the crops in exchange for vi grin sacrifices - deliver the rain before the blood dries on the altar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let Leviathan, at its core, be a tale of Evil vs. Evil</div> </div> </div> </div> If you want Evil vs Evil there's no shortage of Opheons, Typhons, Primordial Thurgists, Rogue Cults, or just other Leviathans you can set your players up against. Go for the Titanomachy. Have a School of the Sun Leviathan that broke their Covenant as your PC's father, and make the game about overthrowing their tyrannic rule and instituting your less tyrannic rule.<br /> <br /> If a rich selection of evil antagonists isn't enough and you want all the Antagonists to be evil; then you're going to be disappointed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you seem to be doing is weighing things too heavily towards Civilization/Order = Good, Savage/Chaos = Evil.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's Chaosmkampf 101. It's not going to change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can guarantee you that playing the overwhelmed underdog is a very niche appeal when the setting keeps harping on about your powerlessness.</div> </div> </div> </div> Um. Mage. Demon. The Exarchs and G-M are far more overwhelming than any Leviathan antagonist. I have also said to you before in this thread that Marduk can be defeated by Leviathans; this is not new information.<br /> <br /> And I challenge you to find anything in the google docs that &quot;harps on about Leviathan's powerlessness&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are the dwindling eras of a bygone age, then let us go out not with a whimper, but with a roar.</div> </div> </div> </div> There is another 1E character with this philosophy, and it's something that's easy for any player character to pursue with the raw destructive powers that Channels are getting in 2E.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this is truly the case, then the game needs to support it more.</div> </div> </div> </div> How is it not supported? I made your primary enemies a bunch of mortals with fancy guns and a space station rather than nigh unkillable gods. What more could you possibly need than that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I didn't feel that the game was presenting the exact opposite of this, that it was robbing the Leviathans of all agency and making them a game devoted to being the punchline in a &quot;Shoot the Shaggy Dog&quot; Story, I wouldn't complain as much as I do.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think your feelings here are in contradiction of the facts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true. But do you know why people do join a cult? Because it offers a place to fit in. No brainwashing aura or madness required.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't object to the idea that people will do awful and/or stupid things in order to fit in.<br /> <br /> I object to the idea that this is a good way to make Leviathans more morally grey. Willing volunteers or not, it's still a Cult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if there are genuine reasons why mortals would fall into a Leviathan's cult without needing to be mind raped first.</div> </div> </div> </div> Of course they are. Humans join cults in the real world, so naturally they'd join Leviathan cults for similar reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850432#post850432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In summary, I want to say this: Leviathan should be the game of being a monster, with all of the horror and all of the glory that entails. Let us embrace our monstrosity, let us accept ourselves, like ourselves, and feel justified spitting in the eye of humanity for saying we should not exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must say, it's rather nice when your criticism boil down to wanting stuff that's already in the google docs or 1E. Though if you want to make constructive criticism, you really have to read them first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-21-2016, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T07:37:50-07:00","id":850539,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a><br /> Question: How do you imagine the relationship of Marduk and Leviathans in future settings?<br /> Particularly depressing futures where things get... hopeless such as the famous Warhammer 40k. Now, I know that goes against your themes set forth, of moving past the fall and all, but I am kinda curious as to how you'd adapt the game for alternate futures went terribly wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-21-2016, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:22:52-07:00","id":850610,"title":"","content":"Interesting question. I actually think that you could get something that looks a LOT like 40K and works perfectly.<br /> <br /> The Emperor of Man trapped on his throne. Simultaneously the single most critical piece of infrastructure and utterly impotent: Able to watch but not intervene as his empire decays and abandons his teachings. (He wanted an atheist empire and ended up with a repressive theocracy).<br /> <br /> This makes a great model for the Marduk Society; or at least the Society as it is in the time of the typical Leviathan setting - In the grimdark future anyone could be using the name. Marduk technology is the underpinnings of the human empire, but no one remembers how it works. Text books on critical thinking have been put to music and become holy chants, but no one understands the old languages of Earth.<br /> <br /> The Imperium of Man itself could be functionally similar, but with a different aesthetic. Instead of Gothic/catholic influences, bronze age Mesopotamian. Instead of corrupt bureaucratic governess, go for passionate warlords who think with their muscles. They build massive pleasure palaces or start pointless wars for glory even as the empire collapses.<br /> <br /> As mankind falls Leviathans fill in the gaps nicely. Every century mankind becomes less able to build spaceships and more reliant on Leviathans swimming through the Rift to other planets and defending them from Typhons. Freed from the limitations of a single world - ancient Typhons have grown to enormous size, along the lines of entire Tyrannid hive fleets.<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically. In a setting like 40K the idea of man as a being of reason is (practically) dead, and the Imperium is built upon it's corpse. So the Marduk Society would be long gone and it's embers slowly fading. As Mankind reverts to a more primordial way of thinking like the Imperium of Man's Leviathans become integrated into every day society - causing enormous damage through the Wake and their behaviour even as they prove vital to keep the Imperium running. Just like how the actual 40K Imperium's fanaticism proves vital to protecting it from Chaos even as it causes enormous damage that will probably destroy mankind in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:44:11-07:00","id":850625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850610#post850610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting question. I actually think that you could get something that looks a LOT like 40K and works perfectly.<br /> <br /> The Emperor of Man trapped on his throne. Simultaneously the single most critical piece of infrastructure and utterly impotent: Able to watch but not intervene as his empire decays and abandons his teachings. (He wanted an atheist empire and ended up with a repressive theocracy).<br /> <br /> This makes a great model for the Marduk Society; or at least the Society as it is in the time of the typical Leviathan setting - In the grimdark future anyone could be using the name. Marduk technology is the underpinnings of the human empire, but no one remembers how it works. Text books on critical thinking have been put to music and become holy chants, but no one understands the old languages of Earth.<br /> <br /> The Imperium of Man itself could be functionally similar, but with a different aesthetic. Instead of Gothic/catholic influences, bronze age Mesopotamian. Instead of corrupt bureaucratic governess, go for passionate warlords who think with their muscles. They build massive pleasure palaces or start pointless wars for glory even as the empire collapses.<br /> <br /> As mankind falls Leviathans fill in the gaps nicely. Every century mankind becomes less able to build spaceships and more reliant on Leviathans swimming through the Rift to other planets and defending them from Typhons. Freed from the limitations of a single world - ancient Typhons have grown to enormous size, along the lines of entire Tyrannid hive fleets.<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically. In a setting like 40K the idea of man as a being of reason is (practically) dead, and the Imperium is built upon it's corpse. So the Marduk Society would be long gone and it's embers slowly fading. As Mankind reverts to a more primordial way of thinking like the Imperium of Man's Leviathans become integrated into every day society - causing enormous damage through the Wake and their behaviour even as they prove vital to keep the Imperium running. Just like how the actual 40K Imperium's fanaticism proves vital to protecting it from Chaos even as it causes enormous damage that will probably destroy mankind in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus it works well with the whole 'cyclic Chaoskampf' thing. Each time either side - leviathan or Marduk - thinks its won, it's only a matter of time before the cracks start to appear. Marduk 'killed' the Progenitors in prehistory and built this world upon their corpses. They build their towers of reason ever higher upon the bodies until they crack under their own weight and come tumbling down into the Primordial sea. The Progenitors rise again and eventually are slain again.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Leviathan itself, the themes rather remind me of a yin-yang symbol. The leviathans are by nature monstrous beings - evil as we understand it -, but they have the potential to do good, even if it's far more difficult for them than it is for humans. Marduk represents reason, progress, humanity. But also the problems with those things. Reason is cold, lifeless. Progress tears down that which came before, often indiscriminately. Humanity can create art, music and wondrous technology, but is capable of horrible cruelty. Perhaps this is too grey for your vision but for me the grey-and-grey morality is part of what makes both oWoD and CoD so interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:46:33-07:00","id":850630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850610#post850610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting question. I actually think that you could get something that looks a LOT like 40K and works perfectly.<br /> <br /> The Emperor of Man trapped on his throne. Simultaneously the single most critical piece of infrastructure and utterly impotent: Able to watch but not intervene as his empire decays and abandons his teachings. (He wanted an atheist empire and ended up with a repressive theocracy).<br /> <br /> This makes a great model for the Marduk Society; or at least the Society as it is in the time of the typical Leviathan setting - In the grimdark future anyone could be using the name. Marduk technology is the underpinnings of the human empire, but no one remembers how it works. Text books on critical thinking have been put to music and become holy chants, but no one understands the old languages of Earth.<br /> <br /> The Imperium of Man itself could be functionally similar, but with a different aesthetic. Instead of Gothic/catholic influences, bronze age Mesopotamian. Instead of corrupt bureaucratic governess, go for passionate warlords who think with their muscles. They build massive pleasure palaces or start pointless wars for glory even as the empire collapses.<br /> <br /> As mankind falls Leviathans fill in the gaps nicely. Every century mankind becomes less able to build spaceships and more reliant on Leviathans swimming through the Rift to other planets and defending them from Typhons. Freed from the limitations of a single world - ancient Typhons have grown to enormous size, along the lines of entire Tyrannid hive fleets.<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically. In a setting like 40K the idea of man as a being of reason is (practically) dead, and the Imperium is built upon it's corpse. So the Marduk Society would be long gone and it's embers slowly fading. As Mankind reverts to a more primordial way of thinking like the Imperium of Man's Leviathans become integrated into every day society - causing enormous damage through the Wake and their behaviour even as they prove vital to keep the Imperium running. Just like how the actual 40K Imperium's fanaticism proves vital to protecting it from Chaos even as it causes enormous damage that will probably destroy mankind in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That almost makes me wonder of running a crossover involving them. Like, actually Warhammer 40k with Levithans... I imagine a depressing number are Chaos worshippers with a few ascending to Daemon Princehood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How about for a much ... smaller, somewhat less ridiculous setting like Warframe (maybe even more so on the small scale stuff)? I'm considering adding fan projects to the list of &quot;splats&quot; covered in my setting hack, Leviathan being my first I was wondering about your opinion about that over how it would go. It's... weird compared to a number of other scifi settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:58:36-07:00","id":850638,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I can't help there. I don't know anything about Warframe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:20:38-07:00","id":850656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850638#post850638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I can't help there. I don't know anything about Warframe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually expecting that.<br /> <br /> Short summary.<br /> <br /> <br /> Advanced Empire that was several star systems big fell due to a combination of an AI rebellion and the super soldiers they made to fight the Rebel ais deciding to destroy the Empire after the war. And by all reckoning, the the Orokin deserved it to the point no one is sympathetic about them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Their feats involve among other things making humans live for centuries, dimensional travel, and massive production bonuses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> After they died off and the Empire became nothing but a memory with its artifacts and lost technology fought over, the setting of Warframe is a single star system in perpetual war.<br /> <br /> <br /> This war is between Cyborg clone soldiers that are too genetically damaged to survive without augmentation and have extreme racism issues, a greedy merchant cult backed up by energy shields and robotics and considers wealth and profit the greatest ideal of all, and a nanomachine zombie plague bioweapon that can eat starships and that everyone hates so much that they put asside their differences to push it back. And all of these are a small remnant of the greater empire.<br /> <br /> So my question is this. How do Leviathans fit in in such a setting where despite being so high tech, it's all most like the bronze age all over again","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-21-2016, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T11:59:08-07:00","id":850728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850656#post850656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This war is between Cyborg clone soldiers that are too genetically damaged to survive without augmentation and have extreme racism issues</div> </div> </div> </div> From this alone: An Oceanead Cult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850656#post850656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a greedy merchant cult backed up by energy shields and robotics and considers wealth and profit the greatest ideal of all</div> </div> </div> </div> A Thalassan Cult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850656#post850656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and a nanomachine zombie plague bioweapon that can eat starships and that everyone hates so much that they put asside their differences to push it back. And all of these are a small remnant of the greater empire.</div> </div> </div> </div> A single Typhon. Possibly Dagonite - but in 2E the purpose of Strain is focused heavily on Cults so for a Typhon it's not that big a deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850656#post850656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my question is this. How do Leviathans fit in in such a setting where despite being so high tech, it's all most like the bronze age all over again</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd be everywhere, out in the open building cults and doing whatever they want.<br /> <br /> The high tech part doesn't really matter much. Leviathans represent a part of human nature, so ignore the technology and look at how the humans behave in the setting you're interested in. Match the humans' behaviour to the descriptions of different cults in the Strains document - if they match or if they feel like they could match some sort of 8th Strain - that's where you'll find Leviathans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T13:00:31-07:00","id":850756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850728#post850728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> From this alone: An Oceanead Cult.<br /> <br /> A Thalassan Cult.<br /> <br /> A single Typhon. Possibly Dagonite - but in 2E the purpose of Strain is focused heavily on Cults so for a Typhon it's not that big a deal.<br /> <br /> They'd be everywhere, out in the open building cults and doing whatever they want.<br /> <br /> The high tech part doesn't really matter much. Leviathans represent a part of human nature, so ignore the technology and look at how the humans behave in the setting you're interested in. Match the humans' behaviour to the descriptions of different cults in the Strains document - if they match or if they feel like they could match some sort of 8th Strain - that's where you'll find Leviathans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Never looked at it that way. I suppose it's possible there's secret cults everywhere that are hidden in plain sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T13:15:11-07:00","id":850768,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. The WoD is full of cults, and not all of them are Leviathan Cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T13:18:35-07:00","id":850769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850768#post850768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely. The WoD is full of cults, and not all of them are Leviathan Cults.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I've already included that a small portion of the Corpus have Mummy worshipers and that there's a sect of insane Grineer scientists who keep trying to make Prometheans to repair their genetics (not I say try).<br /> <br /> So adding more shouldn't be too big of a deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T11:30:51-07:00","id":851252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850527#post850527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A fair question.<br /> <br /> The answer is that it works fine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Citation, please? It seems that a large number of people ITT, myself included, feel that it does not work fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850527#post850527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you'll find any successful (defining successful as actually finishing at least one large project) fanwriter who dozen't show shades of this. Without that streak of stubbornness we'd get board half way though. MB and myself are just as bad as each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you've pre-committed to not being convinced by argument. That seems like the exact opposite of Progress and Reason -- science only works because it specifically provides for updating our beliefs and practices as information comes in! What you've stated here is, essentially, &quot;my system works fine, and I feel comfortable dismissing anyone who tells me that it doesn't; my ideas are fixed and unchanging because they're already as good as they could be.&quot; That stubbornness is <i>stagnation</i>.<br /> <br /> Your Chaoskampf morality is something you personally prefer to a more ambiguous or at-all-gray Marduk. Many of us feel that, as a theme, it renders the conflict lacking in depth, and leaves Marduk itself somewhat uninteresting as an antagonist. You have failed to address these concerns meaningfully; your response has largely become either &quot;disagreeing with me is unproductive&quot; or &quot;it's not changing, so stop talking about it.&quot;<br /> <br /> At this point, I feel like it's mostly fruitless to engage you on &quot;the validity of the themes you want to implement,&quot; as you've made it clear that you feel all criticism of your specific implementation is illegitimate. So consider this: a lot of people don't want to use this Marduk! The thread -- your &quot;sample&quot; for testing your work -- has objected on the grounds that they don't want to use Marduk as it is. The playability of a game has nothing to do with the correctness of its themes -- if you make a game, and a lot of people are put off by an element of the game, then that element has <i>failed</i>. Game design is at least in part about building a setting that players want to use.<br /> <br /> So I guess what I'm asking is, <u>do you have an answer for players who are dissatisfied with the Chaoskampf morality scheme that isn't &quot;tough&quot;?</u>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T11:43:03-07:00","id":851258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=851252#post851252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">science only works because it specifically provides for updating our beliefs and practices as information comes in</div> </div> </div> </div> Science also does not apply to questions of personal taste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=851252#post851252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point</div> </div> </div> </div> At this point? You mean not when I explicitly said it's a fuitless discussion way back?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvaryKeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=851252#post851252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess what I'm asking is, <u>do you have an answer for players who are dissatisfied with the Chaoskampf morality scheme that isn't &quot;tough&quot;?</u></div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, unless &quot;use of the many other Antagonist splats in Leviathan&quot; is a satisfactory answer. I could link to Matthew McFarland's blog post about <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/its-about-the-buy-in/\" target=\"_blank\">buy in</a> but that's just a longer fancier way of saying &quot;tough&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T16:31:21-07:00","id":851436,"title":"","content":"To clear things up, CalvaryKeter, I wasn't actually referring to Marduk specifically in my last post, but to the general &quot;feel&quot; of Leviathan as a whole. Marduk or no Marduk, I don't want this game to be basically a combination of the worst aspects, in my eyes, of Vampire and Hunter.<br /> <br /> Yes, I'll admit, Corvus Rex's comments here, particularly when defending Marduk, made it sound worse to me than perhaps it is. It doesn't help that he's been very quiet on the update front, so I've had no idea when or even if he's been working on this project. When my connection will allow it, I hope to actually read what he has written so I can give a more concise review, rather than basing my concerns on the impressions he's left of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T23:51:13-07:00","id":851607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=851436#post851436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't help that he's been very quiet on the update front, so I've had no idea when or even if he's been working on this project</div> </div> </div> </div>It's quiet because there just hasn't been much in the way of substantial updates. A bit of tinkering with wording, and some work on the Schools - which aren't finished yet. I think there's a new Channel since you last looked but I might be getting my dates wrong.<br /> <br /> (A forum debate/argument rarely gives the best or most accurate impression of anything)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-23-2016, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T11:06:19-07:00","id":851875,"title":"","content":"Continuing on about my question earlier, what would happen to Marduk in these future settings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T11:10:39-07:00","id":851879,"title":"","content":"As I said, in 40K they're definitely long gone, with maybe at most virtuous individuals who seem to have a knack for using their technology. But the idea of reason and progress as a powerful force in the setting, long gone in 40K.<br /> <br /> Warframe, maybe the same maybe not. I didn't see anything in the short blurb. You look for institutions that are helping humanity to behave in a civilised way and improve as a species. That's where you'd find Marduk agents turning up and seeking help, but you'd know better than me if there's any of those in Warframe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T13:36:49-07:00","id":851977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=851879#post851879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, in 40K they're definitely long gone, with maybe at most virtuous individuals who seem to have a knack for using their technology. But the idea of reason and progress as a powerful force in the setting, long gone in 40K.<br /> <br /> Warframe, maybe the same maybe not. I didn't see anything in the short blurb. You look for institutions that are helping humanity to behave in a civilised way and improve as a species. That's where you'd find Marduk agents turning up and seeking help, but you'd know better than me if there's any of those in Warframe.</div> </div> </div> </div>While we're on the topic of futuristic settings, I can't help but draw parallels with these Leviathans and the (spoiler rendered in white for your convenience) <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Leviathans that created the </span>Reapers in Mass Effect, at least visually. Not to mention the Reaper's Indoctrination resembling the Wake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T13:40:50-07:00","id":851981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=851977#post851977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're on the topic of futuristic settings, I can't help but draw parallels with these Leviathans and the (spoiler rendered in white for your convenience) Reapers in Mass Effect, at least visually. Not to mention the Reaper's Indoctrination resembling the Wake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree with this. i actually designed a Leviathan character once which was based on the ones from Mass Effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-23-2016, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T13:42:34-07:00","id":851983,"title":"","content":"Yes, but Leviathan: the Tempest did it first <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Visually the thing you have spoiled would probably be a low Sheol high Tranquillity Lahamin BTW.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. your quote block reveals the spoiler. You might want to edit that out, hopefully no one who didn't already know that has read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T14:03:28-07:00","id":852001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=851983#post851983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> P.S. your quote block reveals the spoiler. You might want to edit that out, hopefully no one who didn't already know that has read it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry.... *smacks forehead*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T12:56:40-07:00","id":857253,"title":"","content":"Forgive me if this question has already been answered in an earlier post and I just missed it, but what exactly are the mechanics for the (3?) integrity systems for leviathan 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11554-fate-inker","name":"Fate Inker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T13:11:49-07:00","id":857260,"title":"","content":"You want to check the Systems and Advantages doc for that: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11Cr2Af1VIZfvOOOJtCwAWTbhd4c-gO5R-pVbLn-atQY/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...VbLn-atQY/edit</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:51:25-07:00","id":857298,"title":"","content":"Sadly they're not up yet. There might be something in the early pages of the thread but I don't think there's more than discussion and outline and my thinkings evolved a bit since then. BTW it's 2 systems (even I'm not crazy enough to do 3 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> They're called Phronesis &amp; Eunoia. You risk Eroding Pheroneis when you indulge the Beastal Nature. Acts of violence, crimes of passion, etc. You risk Eroding Eunoia when you indulge the Divine Nature. Treating people like things, emotional abuse; wickedness you order your Cult to do defaults to Eunoia.<br /> <br /> There is also a third Trait, Tranquillity. However Tranquillity literally means &quot;lower of Phronesis &amp; Eunoia&quot; and only exists so I can make mechanics that are affected by Tranquillity without having to constantly say &quot;lower of Phronesis &amp; Eunoia&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Each School also has a favoured way of solving problems. If you solve a problem in the appropriate method you gain some benefit related to Phronesis &amp; Eunoia<br /> <br /> That much is locked down.<br /> <br /> <br /> Currently the Schools doc says that the Benefit is a chance to regain Phronesis &amp; Eunoia and that will probably stay. Originally I was thinking that if a Leviathan was going to do something evil they should do it in their School's way to reduce the risks of Erosion or turn it into more of a gamble where it could go up or down.<br /> <br /> But now I'm thinking that maybe I should nudge the mechanics away from that, rather than letting Schools help prevent Erosion they become exclusively a way to gain additional dots with the idea being that when a Leviathan is free to pursue their School they can rise in Phronesis &amp; Eunoia but when a crisis hits they're likely to go down. This fits the themes of Stagnation with a Leviathan going through cycles of building up only to loose it all. (It could be worse, at least they're not Vampires who generally just go down and stay there)<br /> <br /> Maybe what I'll do is split the difference. School lets you roll to increase Phronesis &amp; Eunoia when you solve a problem in the appropriate way. If you also did something worthy of Erosion you'd combine the two rolls with a success adding a dot and a failure removing a dot; but you'd use dicepool appropriate dicepool in the Erosion Chart - which is lower than the base dicepool for increasing Phronesis &amp; Eunoia through your school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T04:53:22-07:00","id":858891,"title":"","content":"Good news. Barring the odd picture or stereotype the Schools are now complete! <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Lhdf_lN5TBF0FnpBe8HfVj6an-YRMxIOVfEg2rSiQ-8\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a link.</a><br /> <br /> The Schools are probably the single most important section in Leviathan as they answer the two questions that every single RPG must give clear answers to: What do players do and why do players form a team?<br /> <br /> The seven schools and what they do are<ul><li>Abyss - Explore the oceans, rift, or something else.</li> <li>Clay - Try to fit into human society and study humanity.</li> <li>Fog - Try to unify the Tribe.</li> <li>Moon - Recreate the Tribe's lost way of life.</li> <li>Sand - Try to solve the Tribe's problems through technology.</li> <li>Sun - Acquire more power, wealth and influence.</li> <li>Reef - Enhance their powers, fight monsters even worse then themselves.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> So if you've asked earlier for Leviathans to get embrace who they are (Sun) or fight evil (Reef) now is the time to see how that works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T05:38:19-07:00","id":858910,"title":"","content":"Nice. I'm still reading through, and likely to edit with additional comments.<br /> <br /> School of Clay: the line &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mankind has made thousands of different societies, and unlike the Tribe\u2019s societies, they\u2019re healthy and functional.</span></span>&quot; really should have a &quot;mostly&quot; caveat - not all human societies have been healthy and/or functional. Though the School of Clay is likely interested in studying those as well, to find out <i>why</i> they didn't work.<br /> <br /> School of Fog: this line is copied from Clay in Direction &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mankind overcame their primordial instincts, and the School seeks Tranquility through copying man\u2019s successes.</span></span>&quot;.<br /> <br /> School of the Moon: Missing a stereotype for another gameline. Not sure what would work best, though. Promethean, due to Changing natures? Mummy, for similar Past/Cult/Religious focus?<br /> <br /> School of Sand: Considering that engineering is based on the understanding uncovered by science, this line just doesn't sit right with me &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">if the Tribe's curses cannot be understood by science they can still be measured, quantified, and compensated for by engineering</span></span>&quot;.<br /> <br /> They are also missing a -3 Erosion condition under Development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-04-2016, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T05:42:10-07:00","id":858915,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. I'll stick a qualifier in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T09:16:19-07:00","id":859056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=858910#post858910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">School of Sand: Considering that engineering is based on the understanding uncovered by science, this line just doesn't sit right with me &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">if the Tribe's curses cannot be understood by science they can still be measured, quantified, and compensated for by engineering</span></span>&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, right.<br /> <br /> That line is referring to tricks like using a telephone to communicate with people outside the Wake's area of effect. Science might not be able to figure out why a Leviathan takes Aggravated Damage from electricity, but an engineer doesn't need to know why to build some sort of insulated suit of armour.<br /> <br /> Would it scan better if I replaced &quot;by engineering&quot; with &quot;with technology&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=858910#post858910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are also missing a -3 Erosion condition under Development.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. I didn't come up with any ideas for that, put it aside to think on and forgot about it.<br /> <br /> I'll have to keep thinking about it. Destroying technology is unfair when your prime enemies are a technology based group, and using your natural powers is too broad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=858910#post858910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">School of the Moon: Missing a stereotype for another gameline. Not sure what would work best, though. Promethean, due to Changing natures? Mummy, for similar Past/Cult/Religious focus?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Checks notes</i>. It was supposed to be Mummies. This one's fixed now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-04-2016, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T14:56:45-07:00","id":859271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859056#post859056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ah, right.<br /> <br /> That line is referring to tricks like using a telephone to communicate with people outside the Wake's area of effect. Science might not be able to figure out why a Leviathan takes Aggravated Damage from electricity, but an engineer doesn't need to know why to build some sort of insulated suit of armour.<br /> <br /> Would it scan better if I replaced &quot;by engineering&quot; with &quot;with technology&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess. Basically you are saying &quot;A Leviathan doesn't need to understand why something works the way it does (their banes, for example), to be able to counter-act them with technology&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859056#post859056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah. I didn't come up with any ideas for that, put it aside to think on and forgot about it.<br /> <br /> I'll have to keep thinking about it. Destroying technology is unfair when your prime enemies are a technology based group, and using your natural powers is too broad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe when your technological terrors prove insufficient? Like, that Grounding-Harness you wore still wasn't enough to stand against Marduk's weaponry (for example). Drives home the pain of &quot;why do I even bother&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859056#post859056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Checks notes</i>. It was supposed to be Mummies. This one's fixed now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Still reading through.<br /> <hr /><br /> School of the Sun: Missing a cross-gameline stereotype. Since Mages and Mummies are already taken, Vampires would probably make the next logical parallel, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-04-2016, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T23:47:38-07:00","id":859497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859271#post859271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess. Basically you are saying &quot;A Leviathan doesn't need to understand why something works the way it does (their banes, for example), to be able to counter-act them with technology&quot;, right?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859271#post859271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe when your technological terrors prove insufficient? Like, that Grounding-Harness you wore still wasn't enough to stand against Marduk's weaponry (for example). Drives home the pain of &quot;why do I even bother&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm, probably not because that adds a risk to using technology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859271#post859271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">School of the Sun: Missing a cross-gameline stereotype. Since Mages and Mummies are already taken, Vampires would probably make the next logical parallel, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Checks notes again. I have Promethian down with<br /> <br /> Prometheans: Corpses Stitched together with science and stolen divinity. I spit upon the rotten fruit of this world\u2019s impotent gods.<br /> <br /> Vampires would be something like<br /> <br /> Vampires: Jesus offers love. I offer strength. But what can a leach offer?<br /> <br /> I could also do it from the perspective of a Leviathan worshipped by a branch of the Circle.<br /> <br /> Choices... choices... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-05-2016, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T03:43:24-07:00","id":859540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859497#post859497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmm, probably not because that adds a risk to using technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like that is going to stop a trans-humanist (well, trans-Leviathanist) from using technology?<br /> <br /> If you need a non-tech option, what about a mirror of Reef's +Tranquility? Penalize the for only using Channels and Adaptations (since it gices lie to their &quot;technology helps&quot; creed)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-05-2016, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T06:59:29-07:00","id":859607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859497#post859497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could also do it from the perspective of a Leviathan worshipped by a branch of the Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be a hook for a really cool bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:07:13-07:00","id":859679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859540#post859540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like that is going to stop a trans-humanist (well, trans-Leviathanist) from using technology?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm a <u>huge</u> believer that one of the primary reasons for mechanics is to be a guideline for role playing; the mechanically optimal way to play is acting in charachter for the splat and the themes of the gameline. Obviously mechanics are complex and context matters, but Schools are the area where this connection is at it's strongest. So a penalty to technology here would be me saying to the players &quot;don't use techonlogy if you're playing Sand&quot;.<br /> <br /> Just a little peak behind the curtain at how I design games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859540#post859540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you need a non-tech option, what about a mirror of Reef's +Tranquility? Penalize the for only using Channels and Adaptations (since it gices lie to their &quot;technology helps&quot; creed)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, you might be onto something. A penalty based on a Leviathan's supernatural nature could work, Channels &amp; Adaptations would lock players out of too much of the fun but as a secondary powers Rituals would work here - and since Rituals are thematically (and literally) religious they're thematically opposite technology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859607#post859607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could be a hook for a really cool bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Why do you think I decided on that mechanic* where a Vampire with Leviathan blood in their system is practically alive, capable of growth and change, and have a very high chance of developing mutations and/or cancer. The obvious consiquence is a Bloodline. (Well that and the Ordo doing lots of plot hook worthy stuff with it)<br /> <br /> * It will go in if I write a crossover chapter; but the odds of that are very low.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:50:31-07:00","id":859708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859679#post859679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm a <u>huge</u> believer that one of the primary reasons for mechanics is to be a guideline for role playing; the mechanically optimal way to play is acting in charachter for the splat and the themes of the gameline. Obviously mechanics are complex and context matters, but Schools are the area where this connection is at it's strongest. So a penalty to technology here would be me saying to the players &quot;don't use techonlogy if you're playing Sand&quot;.<br /> <br /> Just a little peak behind the curtain at how I design games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I meant it as &quot;over-reliance on technology <i>can</i> bite you in the tail&quot;. If you are going to use your toys, make them count. More Risk than Penalty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859679#post859679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, you might be onto something. A penalty based on a Leviathan's supernatural nature could work, Channels &amp; Adaptations would lock players out of too much of the fun but as a secondary powers Rituals would work here - and since Rituals are thematically (and literally) religious they're thematically opposite technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was saying &quot;only&quot;, in that the Leviathan is relying on their supernatural heritage, not leveraging the technology at their disposal (which would seem to imply that the tech isn't even necessary). But Rituals is a good option too (though it limits Sand-based Rituals targeting people through networks, and other Techno-Occult shenanigans).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T10:08:55-07:00","id":859717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859708#post859708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I meant it as &quot;over-reliance on technology <i>can</i> bite you in the tail&quot;. If you are going to use your toys, make them count. More Risk than Penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, penalty was the wrong word to use; but I think my point still holds when you call it a risk.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:01:21-07:00","id":859854,"title":"","content":"What are the thoughts on Heirlooms? How they work, where they integrate, how to make them (for STs, if not characters), <i>what</i> are they, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:45:40-07:00","id":859893,"title":"","content":"Funny you asked that, I came up with the answer a just two days ago.<br /> <br /> Heirlooms are basically ordinary objects once owned by a Leviathan. If you take one into the Rift you can find any memory where said object is contained. For example a Heirloom pen might lead you to memories of it's origonal owner having a conversation in his office with his pen on the desk. The pen isn't important, but it's in the memory.<br /> <br /> Mechanically Heirlooms will probably let you trade in a dot of Heirloom for the Informed Condition (and your exp back of course) - you gain advantages to current problems by watching a Leviathan who solved a similar problem. In short, they play to the mood of stagnation. Same problems, same solutions. They'd also be a good way to learn Rituals.<br /> <br /> The dots being traded in don't represent the Heirloom loosing power, but like a book you've already read twice there's not much more to learn from it. <hr /><br /> <br /> From a Mummy Perspective a Heirlooms actually is a Vestige. Not just similar, they're the exact same thing. But being part-god of fecundity Leviathans produce enormous amount of life energy. If a Vestige is a Sekhem alkaline battery, a Heirloom is like a lump of plutonium. Dangerous, unstable, and ridiculously powerful. The wise Arisen sends it to the Judges quickly because they can easily and safely handle it. The Arisen who likes to take risks might try and use it themself. It helps that a Heirloom can't match a Mummy's Virtue/Vice as Leviathans obviously have no Virtue/Vice trait.<br /> <br /> The Mummy angle was me noticing that 1E Heirlooms looked very similar to Vestiges and then going from there to obvious questions like &quot;given the established lore, can I guess how much Sekhem would a Leviathan produce&quot;. The fact this provides a big incentive for Mummies to try and steal a Leviathan's Heirloom (or the reverse) is just the icing on the cake.<br /> <br /> (Hmmm. What to Vestiges actually do for the Arisen? I never figured that out)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-05-2016, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T18:27:05-07:00","id":860021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=859893#post859893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Hmmm. What to Vestiges actually do for the Arisen? I never figured that out)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, not a lot. Spread the Arisen's Virtue/Vice around the area around their tomb if they have enough of them of the right types. Can be drained for pillars in an emergency. That's... kinda it. It always felt like a really important paragraph or three was cut from their section in the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T19:46:36-07:00","id":860060,"title":"","content":"Oh. I was hoping for more unique, rules-bendy properties (like 2E Fetishes, but more). Or is there room for that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T00:07:53-07:00","id":860154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860021#post860021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, not a lot. Spread the Arisen's Virtue/Vice around the area around their tomb if they have enough of them of the right types. Can be drained for pillars in an emergency. That's... kinda it. It always felt like a really important paragraph or three was cut from their section in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>And lifewebs are something I think had a few important paragraphs cut from the core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860060#post860060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh. I was hoping for more unique, rules-bendy properties (like 2E Fetishes, but more). Or is there room for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Look at the descriptions of underwater cities around the docs or search this thread for Maxwell Clarke. Those cities have occult technology* and strange sciences. I wasn't planning to do that much with the concept though. It's there, but I don't think it's that important to Leviathan. I was just going to stick a sidebar somewhere (probably next to Maxwell Clark) saying that you should look at WoD Reliquary and Mummy: the Curse for occult tech rules.<br /> <br /> *IMO that's not too suprising, huamnity used to have it back in Irem and some Conspiracies still do like the Ascending Ones with their mass producable elixirs. In my WoD it's entirely possible that if history had gone differently mankind would be using occult tech as our main tech; so an isolated underwater city could easily go either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T02:38:26-07:00","id":860198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860154#post860154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And lifewebs are something I think had a few important paragraphs cut from the core.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure. Look at the descriptions of underwater cities around the docs or search this thread for Maxwell Clarke. Those cities have occult technology* and strange sciences. I wasn't planning to do that much with the concept though. It's there, but I don't think it's that important to Leviathan. I was just going to stick a sidebar somewhere (probably next to Maxwell Clark) saying that you should look at WoD Reliquary and Mummy: the Curse for occult tech rules.<br /> <br /> *IMO that's not too suprising, huamnity used to have it back in Irem and some Conspiracies still do like the Ascending Ones with their mass producable elixirs. In my WoD it's entirely possible that if history had gone differently mankind would be using occult tech as our main tech; so an isolated underwater city could easily go either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anyone here has read Cthulhutech, that's the kind of technology I'm imagining here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T08:16:19-07:00","id":860318,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I was thinking things like &quot;when [Malkut's Lantern] is used in the Hidden Divinity Ritual, said Ritual works as normal, except the Leviathan can opt to employ their true Wake upon select targets at will&quot;, or &quot;When using The Key And The Gate Channel, the Leviathan can enter the past or future of the being on the altar instead&quot;. Stuff that leverages existing Leviathan powers and abilities, but bends or breaks a rule or two to enable new options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T09:23:51-07:00","id":860363,"title":"","content":"I can see both those niches being filled by occult tech and/or the &quot;strange sciences&quot; practiced beneath the waves. Neither of them are going to be parts of the corebook but the sea is a vast place. There's going to be lots of things down there that aren't touched upon in the corebook.<br /> <br /> Chuthulutech is a mecha game isn't it? Just crib the Wonder rules from Genius and drop the actual template, or just do Genius crossover. As far as I'm concerned if there's one non-Leviathan WoD game that's cannon to the Leviathan setting it's Genius, because Hurbert West is obviously a Genius. So's Captain Nemo for that matter (seriously, looking at Wikipedia he's way more Genius than someone like Nikola Tesla), hence the School of Sand stereotype. Between Inspired Lahmasu (Mahhu probably) in underwater cities, human geniuses with research projects underwater, non-Inspired weird science, there's lots of ways to do Chuthulutech in Leviathan.<br /> <br /> As for rule bending stuff. Take Werewolf's fetish rules, then look at Lovecraft's occultist or mad scientist characters for flavor. Instead of exploring an old temple for relics, swim through a sunken research submarine with escaped experiments and malfunctioning security systems. <br /> <br /> <br /> Rules for mecha and fetesh like items won't go in Leviathan core; but it should be easy to grab them from another gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T10:06:18-07:00","id":860395,"title":"","content":"Cthulhu tech though it covers mecha it isn't always about them, similar to how mecha aren't the point of Warhammer 40k despite it having them. It's a setting that can be basically described as scifi Lovecraft in the most literally way possible with actual Lovecraft aliens.... and humans with advanced technology of many types including Mech suits and powered armor and spaceships fight against monsters that also have these things....coupled with occult nagic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, if you specifically need Mech rules, I've got you covered already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T10:22:57-07:00","id":860407,"title":"","content":"What I meant by Cthulhutech was that kind of not-quite-technology,-not-quite-magic schtick as well as the if-you're-not-careful-this-tech-can-drive-you-mad. Not so much the mecha stuff. Things like the D-Engine or the way that arcanotech draws power from some kind of alternate, hellish, Great-Old-Ones dimension (that's the primordial Waters right there).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T10:37:23-07:00","id":860420,"title":"","content":"Ah, well I'm sure you could do that quite well with mummy's rules and a careful choice of curses. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860395#post860395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, if you specifically need Mech rules, I've got you covered already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, but I think one superscience themed antagonist in the corebook is plenty; and Marduk are all about the aircraft.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T10:41:09-07:00","id":860423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860420#post860420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, well I'm sure you could do that quite well with mummy's rules and a careful choice of curses. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks, but I think one superscience themed antagonist in the corebook is plenty; and Marduk are all about the aircraft.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, I was just clarifying. <br /> <br /> I have to admit, when I run a Leviathan chronicle, my Marduk will be using arcanotech. Just because I happen to like my antagonists served up with a hefty slice of hypocrite (and no, I'm not trying to reopen the Marduk debate That particular horse has been beaten to a bloody pulp and its remains dumped in the Rift (at least)).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T11:38:54-07:00","id":860459,"title":"","content":"Alright, I promised I'd try and get a review of what's actually been written in the docs at some point, so I finally found the time and connection to do so.<br /> <br /> Very first thought... what order am I supposed to read these in? Seriously, I have no idea. The doc titles are clear enough about the content, but it'd be a lot easier to put things into proper perspective if everything after the Introduction was given some sort of Chapter Number.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Introduction </div> </div> </div>Theme: Biblical Tragedy<br /> I've noted before that I'm cautious about this theme. The thing is, we've already <b>got</b> Vampire &amp; Promethean for wangstfesting. Still, the description here makes me cautiously optimistic; the emphasis on the &quot;biblical&quot; scale of the tragedy, on the idea of personal failings being more a metaphor for the eternal battle between Order and Chaos, makes the &quot;wallow in your misery&quot; aspect feel downplayed. The tragedy is in your effect on the world around you, not on you personally.<br /> <br /> Mood: Stagnation<br /> First of all, I'm not sure if I'd call &quot;Stagnation&quot; a mood. The text conveys the feel of the Mood quite well, but to me, I just don't know if &quot;stagnation&quot; is an accurate summary of it. I think Predestination is probably more accurate. <br /> <br /> Anyway, the important part here is that this description is a lot more... I guess optimistic than the impression I had of it from the descriptions of the game's mood in the forum. Yes, it talks about how the Wicked Tribe are trapped in their cycle of events, but it places equal emphasis on how there is always the hope that, this time, things will be different, and that with their divine power, Leviathans have both hope and a real chance.<br /> <br /> This is important to me. I don't care how much an author goes on about &quot;True Art is Angsty&quot;, if I utter those Eight Deadly Words about a game, I'm not going to touch it. Fortunately, this intro alone gives me hope that there is more to this game than doom and gloom. In fact, so far, I feel I could portray this akin to Lovecraft's &quot;The Stars Are Not Right - But Will Be&quot;. The predestination mood actually mixes well with the idea touched upon earlier that the world goes through cycles of ascent and descent... how was it put?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=850625#post850625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus it works well with the whole 'cyclic Chaoskampf' thing. Each time either side - leviathan or Marduk - thinks its won, it's only a matter of time before the cracks start to appear. Marduk 'killed' the Progenitors in prehistory and built this world upon their corpses. They build their towers of reason ever higher upon the bodies until they crack under their own weight and come tumbling down into the Primordial sea. The Progenitors rise again and eventually are slain again.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Leviathan itself, the themes rather remind me of a yin-yang symbol. The leviathans are by nature monstrous beings - evil as we understand it -, but they have the potential to do good, even if it's far more difficult for them than it is for humans. Marduk represents reason, progress, humanity. But also the problems with those things. Reason is cold, lifeless. Progress tears down that which came before, often indiscriminately. Humanity can create art, music and wondrous technology, but is capable of horrible cruelty. Perhaps this is too grey for your vision but for me the grey-and-grey morality is part of what makes both oWoD and CoD so interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's it. Yes, this is what I'd like out of Leviathan, and from the Introduction, I may get what I want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mad Arab </div> </div> </div>Not really a lot to say here. Just a fun little bit of fluff notes, though kind of incomplete. It makes me wonder if Corvus Rex is a native English speaker, because there's quite a few subtle errors and almost-but-not-quite word choices scattered here. &quot;Blaspheme&quot;, for example, is the verb-form of the term he's intending to use in the Dagon notes; blaspheme means &quot;to <i>commit</i> blasphem<b>y</b>&quot;. In other docs, I've made suggestions where I could to fix these, but I can't do that here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Systems and Advantages </div> </div> </div>I figured I should look at the crunch block before I went to the more fluff-related stuff, so this was my next stop along my reviewing list.<br /> <br /> Surprisingly, no spelling errors popping out here that I saw, maybe because Corvus Rex has been spending so much time and focus on this particular chapter?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm not much of a crunch guy. Mechanics don't usually have a lot of meaning to me, so I can't give the most elaborate and painstaking of reviews here. Some things that did catch my attention:<br /> * The Ocean Minds sidebar really encapsulates the Leviathan's mind and its nightmarish blending of eldritch abomination and primordial beast well; the difficulty in controlling its own mind nicely offset by the way that a leviathan's mind is &quot;reader: beware&quot; for any other race.<br /> * I remembered that &quot;Tranquility&quot; is supposed to be a shorthand for &quot;the lower of either Phronesis or Eunoia&quot;, or at least I think that's what it's supposed to be, but the doc could stand to make that distinction a little more obvious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Strains </div> </div> </div>Here we reach the first big &quot;draw&quot; of the gameline, the &quot;species&quot; sub-lines. <br /> <br /> <b>Bahamutans:</b> My first impression of these guys was, honestly, really positive. If these are setting the standard for the Strains, I'm going to be quite impressed with this section. Villain protagonists are very hard to do right, but these guys manage it pretty well. Attention is paid to their negative traits, but also to their positive ones; their need to protect, their attempts to focus their natural urges and influences towards the benevolence of their Beloved. The Bahamutan strain, at a reading, seems to embody not merely a Vice, but an Anti-Virtue, the ideal of Piety or Zeal embraced and taken to that warped point where a person will shamelessly do the most atrocious things because someone else provides the assurance that to do so is right. The Tribe may be The Most Wicked, but at a glance, even with their Slothful natures and their synonymy with conformity and tradition, the Bahamutans feels very, very sympathetic. Very well done.<br /> <br /> <b>Dagonites:</b> Although certainly not as inherently sympathetic as the Bahamutans, there's still an all-too-human and recognizable aspect to the children of Dagon. Being torn between their divine power and their awareness of the even worse things out there, they're really not so different to the humans who worship them, and even as they can come across as bullies and frauds, they are ultimately based in urges man felt since he capable of recognizing shapes in the darkness beyond the nest and which still remains a prominent aspect in people's mind today. They are the Oldest Law and its struggle against the Young Laws, a reflection in miniature of the great struggle symbolized by Leviathans as a whole. The section on their private ecology is filled with fridge brilliance, calling to mind the traditionally fecund yet irresponsibly cantankerous and fractious dynasties of pagan gods, homaging their Lovecraftian counterpart's roots in the fear of miscegenation and birth defects, all wrapped in the horrible tragedy that a Dagonite can either be alone, or see its progeny fall into madness and mutation. So far, two for two.<br /> <br /> <b>Lahamin:</b> This is the strain I have the least to say about, thus far. Nothing really sticks out about them, good or bad. The creepy crawly with eerie prophetic powers is an interesting idea, but their portrayal just... doesn't make them really catch my attention. They feel kind of gridholed as &quot;the stealthy/scouty ones&quot;... just, really, really bland. The most I can say about these Leviathans is that they sound the most lonely and sorrowful of their kind, alienated even from their own kind, and as much as it's at least partially self-induced, it kind of makes me want to comfort one.<br /> <br /> <b>Nu:</b> This strain, more than any other, seems to emphasize the idea that the Leviathans are as much victims of their natures as they are victimizers. Reading the description of these guys just brings to mind the idea of being the only sane man surrounded by insane idiots, and that makes me shudder in fellow feeling. I feel sympathetic towards these guys just because I can contemplate and understand the kind of hell they have to live in because of their very nature. Alongside the Bahamutans, the Nu strain are the first to jump to mind when I consider the words &quot;good/sympathetic Leviathan&quot;. Another well-written strain.<br /> <br /> <b>Oceaneads:</b> This strain feels like a counterpoint to the Dagonites, the opposite side of their coin. I can easily see the connections linking the Oceaneads to pagan deities, to the gods as beings whose glory is matched by their pettiness. They are the Beautiful Elite of the Tribe, the embodiment of man's willingness to subliminate itself to that which it finds beautiful, even as the source of their worship laughs at how pathetic man is. Sympathetic? No, not really, but then, the Pretty Ones of the various splats rarely are. Understandable, and relatable? Oh, most definitely.<br /> <br /> <b>Tanninim:</b> Alpha predators. Beautifully contrasting the Oceaneads, who are the strain that represents The Evil of God, the Tanninim are The Evil of Beasts, the most savage aspects of nature given vehement life. Worship and fear are so very much intertwined, after all. And yet, they're not entirely unsympathetic. When one's mind and body are driven by urges from beyond the mortal era, it's only natural to seek some element of control over yourself, and your surroundings. The need for control, the need to submit, these have a huge impact on humanity's collective psyche. Our entire culture has arguably evolved out of these feelings. So, as alien and as monstrous as the Tanninim are at first glance, at the core, there's still something awfully recognizable, and understandable, behind them.<br /> <br /> <b>Thalassans:</b> Greedy and avaricious, and yet with a certain sense of self-awareness shown by their quote. Like the Tanninim, the Thalassans are amongst the basest and more &quot;biological&quot; of the Tribe, rooted in the deepest and most primordial instincts of man and beast. They are horrors, but more than anything because we can see ourselves in them so readily, and admit that there are times when we were worse. They may not be very sympathetic, but they are understandable, and that's the important thing.<br /> <br /> Overall, a fairly positive chapter in my opinion. Two strains that I can personally sympathise with effortlessly, and four that are, while darker, still not painted so utterly black that I think it's impossible to empathise with them. The only flaw that really stands out to me is the Lahamin, who just don't leave any sort of impression on me. They're just... there. That's all I can say about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Schools </div> </div> </div>I was going to do this School by School like I did for the Strains above, but eventually I just gave it up; it'd be too repetitive. Spelling/grammatical errors aside (I'm sure that [Name's] Devoted reads far more smoothly than [Name's] Devotion for the members of the School, it looks so much like Corvus Rex getting his English fouled up again), these are all excellently written. They're believable, they're sensible, they're rational - and none of them are portrayed as inherently evil, or &quot;the bad guys&quot;. They're all different answers to the same question, but none of them feels forced or inherently flawed. Each takes pains to explain how it works out as part of a Cohort and what it can offer to Leviathans, individually and as a greater whole.<br /> <br /> And, best of all, they all counter the perception of &quot;forced grimdark&quot;. They all have a very strong, hopeful feeling, an essential contrast to the dark tones presented in the Introduction. There's a vibrancy in the Schools that makes the hardest part deciding which one I like best of all - there's never even the slightest feeling that I would be better served going with a School-less Leviathan PC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cults </div> </div> </div>Again, mostly crunch focused, so I can't really offer a lot of brilliant insights here. I can recognize some resemblance to Mummy's 1e Cult rules, but the Leviathan version feels unique and seems to quite effectively cover the unique hassles Leviathans have to put up with. Mummies &quot;only&quot; use their own mystical might to impress or intimidate mortals into service, and in fact may often find themselves being treated as just toys of their own cults (generally to the cult's eternal chagrin once the Mummy is properly awake, though). Leviathans have the added blessing - and curse - of mindraping people into fanatical zealots who will give their lives for their master without a second's thought. The Fervor and Piety mechanics cover this quite nicely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Atolls </div> </div> </div>A good, solid chapter, a nice blending of mechanics and fluff that adequately conveys the delicate balance between the Leviathan's raw <i>need</i> for meaningful human contact and the fact that toying with the emotions of a primordial monster-god are a good way to get hurt.<br /> <br /> Only thing I really have to comment on here is that, while I'm not a fan of the default assumption that &quot;Atolls are only as such whilst human&quot;, it least the sidebar admits it is possible. I'll be ignoring that assumption in my own games, as it feels... well, kind of pointless to me.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure why Wake Muting went from an inherent part of the Atoll's powers to something that requires merit points. But I guess it makes more sense for balancing mechanically this way, so I have no real problem with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lahmasu and Hybrids </div> </div> </div>I just... don't have a lot to say about this chapter. Seems solid enough, but it's more crunch than anything, and it fails to really explains why Hybrids are somehow human despite their monstrous shells. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> School of Thunder </div> </div> </div>The chapter itself... I'll be honest, it needs a lot of polish. Feels so sparse and barebones at the moment, it's hard to take a lot of interest. That said, what's there elicited a surprising reaction from me - a negative reaction. My first thought when I read the description of the school was... well, it was too profane to directly post here. Despite the fact that there's practically no detail here explaining <b>why</b> a Leviathan would join the School of Thunder, they still elicited a strong, hostile response. These are guys that just immediately stand out as bastards - the other Leviathans are struggling with finding their own path, and these lazy slime-suckers just betray their kin and beg like sniveling worms. A lot of potential here for antagonists, it just needs to get expanded to make more sense as to the how and the why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ahabs </div> </div> </div>I went into this chapter not really expecting a lot. I can see the fundamental point behind the creation of Ahabs, but, rather like Ghouls in Vampire: The Requiem, they just feel sort of an obligational inclusion. &quot;They're here because you got to have them&quot;, essentially.<br /> <br /> Ahabs honestly kind of remind me of Beast's Heroes. Only with more mechanical weight and a lot better fluff. There's a genuine connection, almost intimacy, between Leviathan and Ahab that I honestly feel makes them superior to their &quot;official&quot; analogues. They're antagonists, but there's a real feeling of tragedy and pity to them, making me feel sorry for them even as I plot their deaths in my own games.<br /> <br /> So, congratulations on taking what I thought would be a dull, &quot;by the numbers&quot; enemy and turning it into something that I can readily see as the primary source for non-mortal antagonists in my own Leviathan games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Empyrean Theurgists </div> </div> </div>Mortals who have become the proxies of the Young Gods, standing in opposition to those Old Gods who linger on Earth (aka The Tribe). It's a simple, yet awesome idea, and yet... the actual interpretation of them feels, honestly, &quot;blah&quot;.<br /> <br /> They're not Mary Sues or soul-crushingly overpowering. Far from it. They just feel... flat. Boring.<br /> <br /> Maybe if the inherent hypocrisy of the Theurgists was focused on more. Yes, the Young Gods gave mankind civilization, they created law and order, but they were often terrible, <b>terrible</b> people themselves. Blood sacrifices and petty cruelty, hedonism and arrogance; Virtue became an excuse and a shield for the Young Gods, leading to much the same tyranny as the Old Gods.<br /> <br /> The Chaoskampf is the story of Order vs. Chaos. It is <b>not</b> the story of Good vs. Evil, and treating it that way is doing it a serious disservice.<br /> <br /> At the least the document admits that Theurgists aren't always progressive reformers, and that their Virtues can lead them to behaviors that are, in many ways, no better than those of the Leviathans. It's the best part in an otherwise bland chapter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Primordial Theurgists </div> </div> </div>Now, these guys, they impressed me. There's not even any mechanical stuff here, it's just pure fluff, and that fluff was awesome. Scholar-mystics who, from desperation or arrogance or other understandable, human failings, seek to mystically leech power from the Leviathans to work their own occult rituals.<br /> <br /> It's great stuff, and especially because there's no clumsy attempt to make them &quot;in the right&quot; for it. They're insane and they're dangerous, to themselves and those around them. They're not guaranteed to succeed, and they walk the knife-edge between success and oblivion each time they power their rituals - at least, that's what I hope will be the case, because I can't think of many things more risky or more likely to blow up in your face than rummaging through a Leviathan's mind to try and siphon off some of her power.<br /> <br /> And that's good. Meddling with any sort of higher being, even a fallen primordial god, should not be something undertaken lightly. At least, not by anyone who values their life or is recognizably sane.<br /> <br /> If dramatic failures for Primordial Theurgists don't carry at least some chance of the Leviathan they were scanning immediately becoming aware of who they are and how to find them, I will be disappointed indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Marduk Society </div> </div> </div>I left this one for last on purpose, just because I was worried about what I'd find after all of the bitter arguing and worrying commentary spouted at various points in the thread.<br /> <br /> I had a glimmering of hope when the Cults document mentions that, by comparison, Marduk as a whole could be treated as Cult with Piety 5 and Fervor 7. Still, I was cautious going in.<br /> <br /> The opening parts of the fluff further fuelled that hope. Marduk is described as corrupt almost from the beginning; Marduk's followers murdering their founder and turning against mankind in order to feed on its despair, all to preserve their own power.<br /> <br /> This is great stuff, as it actually meshes well with the cyclical nature of Order vs. Chaos and the &quot;Tribe and Marduk aren't so different&quot; thing I quoted so far above.<br /> <br /> The description of the Chaoskampf further fuels that hope. Yes, Leviathans aren't really suited for fighting quick, high-altitude fliers. But the Marduk Society will not just indiscriminately carpetbomb if they can avoid it. So there's more of a balance between the two than Marduk is honestly comfortable with.<br /> <br /> ...In all honesty, the more of this I read, the more I wonder where the fears about Marduk Society being overpowered and Mary Sue came from in the first place. Because I really can't see where the impression of Marduk being All Powerful came from, not if this is what was on the table to begin with.<br /> <br /> Maybe Corvus Rex was just that bad at portraying his vision for his pet group. Maybe he actually took peoples' complaints into account and retailored them. Whatever the reason, this isn't what I feared at all.<br /> <br /> Actually, reading this doc kind of makes me feel a little sorry for the Society. Between all the damage they took to their infrastructure during their civil war, the fact they were stretched to the limit to keep everything both running AND secret even before that, their issues in providing funding in a steady flow when they need so much of it just to keep all of their stuff working right (especially when it's a hairline's thinness between even a basic plane working and it being a worthless pile of junk)... Not to mention the entire subchapter of &quot;the naked truth&quot; which opens outright with &quot;As an organization, Marduk is highly ineffiecient&quot;...<br /> <br /> Well, I've stopped wondering &quot;how the hell are the Leviathans supposed to survive with these guys running around?&quot; and started wondering &quot;how are these guys still clinging to existence as a coherent group?&quot; I went in dreading a Technocracy-homaging Mary Sue group. I found a half-dead, confused, bleeding technocratic cult that, from the fluff text, wasn't actually that powerful and deadly even before it fought a civil war. Still enough teeth to have some bite, Space Station Babylon is still operating and it's still got its arsenal trained on the world below, but it's not &quot;you get a single failed Ripple roll, your entire Cohort will be obliterated&quot;, which was the impression early comments on the Society gave.<br /> <br /> Really, about the only complaint I have left is that the doc talks about the Marduk Society having a civil war, but doesn't address any details about it. We don't know who fought, or why, and even just how much damage was done to it in the process is left a little vague.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I think it is warranted to cover Marduk's opinions of/interactions with the world around them. Yes, Marduk itself embodies Idealised Progress, but this is the World of Darkness; the contrast between what Marduk does with Super-Science and what the rest of the world does with or in the name of Progress should be given some attention. At the very least, I think it warrants mentioning as to <i>why</i> Marduk doesn't sell off &quot;old, not-quite-so-super-science&quot; gear instead of just the fact that it doesn't. Does Marduk fear the possibility that mankind may use their scientific advances to the world's detriment? Do they fear being made just a tool of the corrupt politics of the modern world, forced to wage war against the Government's definition of &quot;the enemy&quot; rather than the real dangers?<br /> <br /> These are very real fears and motifs brought up in &quot;super scientist&quot; characters and stories already written. It feels like it's doing Marduk discredit not to make use of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T11:48:39-07:00","id":860462,"title":"","content":"[edit] Not ignoring you VoidDrifter, you ninjaed me. Expect a thorough read and reply forthcoming.<br /> <br /> And speaking of conversations that are done, I don't think there's much more to say about Heirlooms so moving on.<br /> <br /> The Elements Channels. IMO these were the worst designs in Leviathan 1E. The Descendent Channels are all large scale obvious effects, which would be Masqurade risking in a game like Vampire where a masqurade breach is a plot hook. Leviathan is the game where a Masqurade serves the equivalent role of a Strix or Idigam coming to town. Meanwhile the Ancestral Channels were rather boring. An entire Channel just for dicepool bonuses to swimming?<br /> <br /> (I blame myself, since I wrote most of them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <br /> So I came up with the following for how 2E will handle Elements<br /> <br /> 1) Obviously wheather control will build off the existing Tilts mechanics<br /> 2) Descending channels of Elements will each have multiple abilities, allowing both massive environmental control and smaller more practical tricks to coexist<br /> 3) Maybe merging Uncrowned Fisher King and Being of Primordial Waters wasn't the best idea. I can't think of any other Ancestral Channels; and I need two, and swimming really should be an Ancestral ability.<br /> <br /> From that I present the first Elements Channel for 2E. Uncrowned Fisher King, as 6 different unique abilities.<br /> <br /> Oh, and wait till you see what I've got planned for Swallowing the Sun. Lets just say that since I wrote 1E I now know a bit about what Apep symbolised to the Egyptians<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Uncrowned Fisher King (Ancestral Channel)</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Leviathan at sea is a creature within its element. Its every movement is in perfect harmony with the depths.</i></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 1: Birthright of Elements</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 2: The Leviathan adds his Sheol to athletics and Survival rolls while in water. In addition the Leviathan becomes entirely immune to damage from water. Ice won\u2019t chil, steam won\u2019t scald, and a tidal wave throwing a building onto her won\u2019t even knock her off her feat. If the water is being manipulated supernaturally a Clash of Wills ensues, but the Leviathan gains extra protection equal to that provided by the Ocean Minds rule. The exception is when the water is being manipulated by a divine power with strong ties to water, such as a rival Leviathan or an Empyrean Theurgist invoking Poseidon. In such cases the Leviathan rolls a normal Clash of Wills. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 3: The Leviathan gains the ability to produce a form of \u201cwhale song\u201d. He can communicate for Strength + Sheol x 10 miles but the sound will not break the surface of the water. This song cannot be used to enhance Channels that depend upon the Leviathan\u2019s voice. Anyone who hears the Leviathan's call is instantly aware that it came from an unnatural creature. Any Leviathan in Depth 2 or lower who hears the song is instantly able to decode it even without this Channel. A Leviathan\u2019s song consists of their usual language modified to travel further underwater, they gain no automatic ability to communicate with Leviathans who don't share a language and with effort it can be electronically decoded.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 4: At this level the boundary between the Leviathan and the sea becomes fluid. The Leviathan becomes as much a living extension of the sea in a manner more true than the base material reality of solid shell contrasted with fluid liquid. So long as the Leviathan swims with the currents they become nigh indistinguishable from the water automatically apply one third Sheol (round up) as successes to Stealth rolls. If they match the water\u2019s speed the bonus rises to Sheol. Be warned, a injured Leviathan may still leave a trail to follow and most in the Tribe are aware of this trick. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 5: As the boundary between sea and skin blurs further the Leviathan\u2019s sense of self expands outwards into the water. Large artificial structures disrupt the sea\u2019s harmony and are as unmissable as another\u2019s arm resting upon your shoulder. The Leviathan is instantly aware of any ships, oil platforms, underwater cities, submarines, sunken temples, or any other large artificial structure within Sheol * 100 miles. No roll is required, but deliberate concealment may provoke a Clash of Wills.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 6: The Leviathan can cross oceans and circumvent the globe. Her maximum speed becomes 75 miles per hour per Sheol and her acceleration is equal to her Speed. Note: To convert from Speed to miles per hour divide by 1.46, to convert from miles per hour to Speed multiply by 1.46</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 7: The Leviathan is the sea, and the sea is the Leviathan. Where the Leviathan goes, the sea follows. If a Leviathan swims upstream and starts their journey from the sea, they no longer need to worry about finding rivers large enough for their forms. If the river is too small the Leviathan will water from the ocean with them, flooding the land and widening the river. They may travel up to Sheol * 10 miles this way. This is obviously unnatural and usually results in a river without any banks, and unless the Leviathan swims back the way they came this can result in a very large amount of water suddenly falling back into the grip of gravity when the Channel\u2019s effects end. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T14:47:53-07:00","id":860564,"title":"","content":"Well I must say reading your review made you very happy.<br /> <br /> I'm going to write a lot of responses to your review in a quote &amp; response format; but on the whole I agree with and like what you're saying. Quite a lot of responses will probably be me explaining why things are the way they are, just because, well I hope people will find it interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very first thought... what order am I supposed to read these in? Seriously, I have no idea.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah sorry about that. Obviously I plan to do something about this, but I'm planning to sort that out at the end when I compile the final book. The final version will be in a single large file.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've noted before that I'm cautious about this theme. The thing is, we've already <b>got</b> Vampire &amp; Promethean for wangstfesting.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the important part here is that this description is a lot more... I guess optimistic than the impression I had of it from the descriptions of the game's mood in the forum.<br /> <br /> This is important to me. I don't care how much an author goes on about &quot;True Art is Angsty&quot;, if I utter those Eight Deadly Words about a game</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm glad this is coming across; in your recent posts I got the impression that once you read the material you'd like it and I'm glad you did.<br /> <br /> Like you I'm really really not a fan of wangstfesting (though I consider Promethian the opposite of wangstfesting). That spark of hope you saw is completely intentional, and it's extreemly important because without hope why try in the first place. And if a Leviathan fails, I want them to fail in a way that's both feels fair to the players and the characters - hence the importance of their own flaws - and glorious so that players end on an emotional high not an emotional low.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mood: Stagnation<br /> First of all, I'm not sure if I'd call &quot;Stagnation&quot; a mood. The text conveys the feel of the Mood quite well, but to me, I just don't know if &quot;stagnation&quot; is an accurate summary of it. I think Predestination is probably more accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have a think about this. I know I'm pretty attached to the word stagnation, but the text is the important part<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really a lot to say here. Just a fun little bit of fluff notes, though kind of incomplete.</div> </div> </div> </div> They are indeed incomplete. What you're looking there is quite literally my workspace. When I write for Leviathan, it goes straight into that publicly viewable folder. Catch it at the right time and you can even watch me work in real time.<br /> <br /> So basically, there's a things in there that are quite literally unfinished. Like this section, when it's done it's actually going to be merged into the Strains with each Strain opening with a section from the Mad Arab; the idea is also to tell a coherent story where he goes from being the Islamic Golden Age version of a Null Mysteriis Hunter (the Nu section mentions he is/was <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wCHlfqPxlvyTQGroTmmwBDicVk6Sai9tegs2itjMqtU/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Mu'tazilite</a>) planning to use Leviathan power to uncover the truths of existence to his ambiguous ending where he's either an Archmage level Primordial Thurgist who actually knows the fundamental truths of reality; or just completely lost all grasp of reality and sanity.<br /> <br /> (It's also hard for me to to write them)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It makes me wonder if Corvus Rex is a native English speaker</div> </div> </div> </div> Embarrassingly yes, but in my defence I have dyslexia and other leaning difficulties. They don't hinder me too much but they do affect my spelling and grammar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I've made suggestions where I could to fix these, but I can't do that here.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks for that. Annoyingly there's no way to allow comments folder wide; so I have to go through an enable them manually for each doc. Annoyingly I only just found that out, and still need to go through and enable them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> * I remembered that &quot;Tranquility&quot; is supposed to be a shorthand for &quot;the lower of either Phronesis or Eunoia&quot;, or at least I think that's what it's supposed to be, but the doc could stand to make that distinction a little more obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div> Like I said about a lot of these docs being unfinished. The Phronesis/Eunoia/Tranquillity section is currently just an empty section with a heading. Once it's written it will be nice and clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Here we reach the first big &quot;draw&quot; of the gameline, the &quot;species&quot; sub-lines.</div> </div> </div> </div> Now this section of your review was very interesting to read, because you approached these from a Leviathan first perspective. Who is the Leviathan, what are they like.<br /> <br /> I actually wrote these from a cult first perspective. Note that the first paragraph of each Strain talks about cults. Each Strain starts with one aspect of why people join religions, twists it as appropriate for mad lovecraftian cultists, and creates a cult based primarally around that aspect. Then the Leviathans themselves were updated to 2E in the context of their cults.<br /> <br /> Obviously I'm not saying your reading is wrong, there is no right or wrong here, but it is something that jumped out at me and made me eager to look at the Strains from a new point of vie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first impression of these guys was, honestly, really positive. If these are setting the standard for the Strains, I'm going to be quite impressed with this section. Villain protagonists are very hard to do right, but these guys manage it pretty well.</div> </div> </div> </div> I just need to say I'm really flattered <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Bahamutans are my favourite too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they are ultimately based in urges man felt since he capable of recognizing shapes in the darkness beyond the nest and which still remains a prominent aspect in people's mind today.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes!<br /> <br /> All the Strains are (at least I hope) like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the strain I have the least to say about, thus far. Nothing really sticks out about them, good or bad.</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps there's a reason for the Lahamin being the one you found the weakest.<br /> <br /> Like I said, when I updated the Strains from 2E I took made cults the centre piece. For Lahamin I knowingly used a style of cult which I don't really think exists in the real world, and that's the &quot;religious illuminati&quot;. The cult that controls things behind the scenes, and anyone could secretly be a member. You'll see them all over the place in fantasy and horror. There's one in Charles Stross' Eschaton series for example. Heck, Mummy's Conspiracy cult Foundation is an example. But in real life I don't think you'll find that many of them.<br /> <br /> I don't want to change that cult design, it's such a popular fictional concept that I think it simply has to go in. But there's always room for improvement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Oceaneads:</b> This strain feels like a counterpoint to the Dagonites</div> </div> </div> </div> They definitely are. Dagonites are cults for people who feel physically powerless, Oceaneads are cults for people who feel socially powerless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as alien and as monstrous as the Tanninim are at first glance, at the core, there's still something awfully recognizable, and understandable, behind them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Tanninim are indeed alien to the way I imagine most people on this board think, you're not wrong there. But take a peak behind the curtain and discover that I did in fact base them on modern people.<br /> <br /> A while back there was a hurricane that hit America, I forget which one, and some preacher was in the papers saying that the hurricane was god's punishment for homosexuality. Tanninim were based on me trying to get inside his head. His homophobia wasn't actually relevant. Rather, I tried to imagine what humanity must look like to him so that a god who sent hurricanes was justified.<br /> <br /> I imagined that he saw humans as a thin veneer of civility over a savage brutal heart, with that veneer held in place by law and fear of punishment. Thus Tanninim's cults were built to resemble what I imagined he thought all humans were, and the Tanninim were created in what I imagined he saw God as. Someone trying to impose civilizaion and law upon savages who only understood the fear of punishment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall, a fairly positive chapter in my opinion. Two strains that I can personally sympathise with effortlessly, and four that are, while darker, still not painted so utterly black that I think it's impossible to empathise with them. The only flaw that really stands out to me is the Lahamin, who just don't leave any sort of impression on me. They're just... there. That's all I can say about them.</div> </div> </div> </div> I consider this a great result. When I'm writing splats I try and make different splats appeal to different people. It's clear that what you look for in a splat is the ability to emphasise with them. It's my hope that, if I did them right, other people who look for different things will find themselves drawn to different splats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">these are all excellently written. They're believable, they're sensible, they're rational - and none of them are portrayed as inherently evil, or &quot;the bad guys&quot;. They're all different answers to the same question, but none of them feels forced or inherently flawed.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yay! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks again for the complements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, best of all, they all counter the perception of &quot;forced grimdark&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yay again!<br /> <br /> From an in charachter perspective, Leviathans created Schools to counter &quot;grimdark&quot; and create hope so I'm glad that works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be ignoring that assumption in my own games, as it feels... well, kind of pointless to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> The origin of that rule is because in the WoD nobody can have a minor template like Atoll and a major template at the same time. The sidebar is me twisting that rule as far as I dared because, like you, I see potential in full Template Atolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also not sure why Wake Muting went from an inherent part of the Atoll's powers to something that requires merit points. But I guess it makes more sense for balancing mechanically this way, so I have no real problem with it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think it was ever part of their inherent powers; have I misremembered? But the actual reason is to give more flexibility.<br /> <br /> Want an Atoll struggling with the Wake on top of everything else? Don't give them the ability. Want to focus on the Atoll &amp; Leviathan's relationship without crazy cultists interrupting, take the Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just... don't have a lot to say about this chapter. Seems solid enough, but it's more crunch than anything, and it fails to really explains why Hybrids are somehow human despite their monstrous shells.</div> </div> </div> </div> Um, do I need a reason for that? Mentally they fall within human norms, Pelopsids tend to be socieopathic but they think and act like human socieopaths. Do I need a reason for that beyond &quot;as the author I declare this is how Lahmasu brains work&quot;? (Serious question)<br /> <br /> One thing that's worth pointing out. Lahmasu and Hybrid's purpose in the setting is not to be a source of servants or contacts for Leviathans like Ghouls are. But rather they're a setting element, designed to create a richer less knowable world.<br /> <br /> Heqen and Mahhu for example; challenge the assumption that supernatural magic is something the tribe has and humanity doesn't. With Heqen and Mahhu around anybody, the prim and proper house wife, the construction worker, the mayor, might have access to magic simply by hiring a Lahmasu.<br /> <br /> Gibborim are the storyteller's go to source for combat encounters while exploring a lost temple. They show that even a bloodthursty savage has a place in mankind's civilised modern world, and a Leviathan fighting some third world warlord might suddenly discover that the warlord's the one with Gibborim in his army; for that less knowable world.<br /> <br /> Gugal - well there's got to be something to do in the ocean <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> underwater cities to explore, trade with, conqueror, ect and that means there needs to be somebody who builds and lives in them.<br /> <br /> Hence why Hybrids are mostly human. They blur lines and challenge assumptions about where humanity ends and the tribe begins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The chapter itself... I'll be honest, it needs a lot of polish.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not surprising, it's not finished. In fact it's barely started. I had a burst of inspiration, started, then finished that bit and couldn't think of anything else so I put it aside for the time being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-06-2016, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T14:48:41-07:00","id":860565,"title":"","content":"I split this in two because it wouldn't let me post otherwise, weird.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, what's there elicited a surprising reaction from me - a negative reaction.</div> </div> </div> </div> Excellent! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alot of potential here for antagonists, it just needs to get expanded to make more sense as to the how and the why.</div> </div> </div> </div> Just to clarify encase there's any ambiguity at all. The School of Thunder are going in the antagonist section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahabs honestly kind of remind me of Beast's Heroes. Only with more mechanical weight and a lot better fluff. There's a genuine connection, almost intimacy, between Leviathan and Ahab that I honestly feel makes them superior to their &quot;official&quot; analogues. They're antagonists, but there's a real feeling of tragedy and pity to them, making me feel sorry for them even as I plot their deaths in my own games.<br /> <br /> So, congratulations on taking what I thought would be a dull, &quot;by the numbers&quot; enemy and turning it into something that I can readily see as the primary source for non-mortal antagonists in my own Leviathan games.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you yet again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And you're right about the resemblance to Heroes. Even post update I looked at Heroes and felt, where is the. Actually, you had the perfect word for it &quot;intimacy&quot;. Where's the intimacy between Beasts and Heroes?<br /> <br /> If I rewrote Heroes the relationship between a Beast and Hero would be very different to an Ahab and Leviathan and centred on the monomyth; but I do in fact have a design based on the relationship between Darth Vader and Luke Skywalker (with Palpatine as Vader's Horror) that I think would have just as much of that intimacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not Mary Sues or soul-crushingly overpowering. Far from it. They just feel... flat. Boring.</div> </div> </div> </div> I do keep tinkering with them, trying to find the magic.<br /> <br /> A religious themed antagonist to be a foil to the tribe's cults is a niche that needs to be filled; but I struggle between making something generic enough to fit whichever new god the storyteller wants and something that has real depth and flavour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not guaranteed to succeed, and they walk the knife-edge between success and oblivion each time they power their rituals - at least, that's what I hope will be the case</div> </div> </div> </div> I'll try to keep that in mind. Any mechanics for Rituals, and thus these guys, will not appear before Mage 2E is out and I've mined it for ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If dramatic failures for Primordial Theurgists don't carry at least some chance of the Leviathan they were scanning immediately becoming aware of who they are and how to find them, I will be disappointed indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div> That will definitely be a risk to the Primordial Theurgists, no doubt there. Whether it's a result of the ritual roll, a research roll, or something else remains to be scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...In all honesty, the more of this I read, the more I wonder where the fears about Marduk Society being overpowered and Mary Sue came from in the first place. Because I really can't see where the impression of Marduk being All Powerful came from, not if this is what was on the table to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div> And this is the biggest yay of all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This is actually a big relief.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Corvus Rex was just that bad at portraying his vision for his pet group. Maybe he actually took peoples' complaints into account and retailored them. Whatever the reason, this isn't what I feared at all.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure where the concept of Mary Sues came from either. What you're seeing here has been my vision from the start, however I did make use of the complaints as guides for what needed to be clarified and what questions had to be explicitly addressed in the text. So maybe the reason is all of the above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, about the only complaint I have left is that the doc talks about the Marduk Society having a civil war, but doesn't address any details about it. We don't know who fought, or why, and even just how much damage was done to it in the process is left a little vague.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'll see if inspiration strikes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860459#post860459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least, I think it warrants mentioning as to <i>why</i> Marduk doesn't sell off &quot;old, not-quite-so-super-science&quot; gear instead of just the fact that it doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div> I thought that was answered.<br /> <br /> It's not that Marduk don't make money off old, not-quite-so-super-science. It's that they go about it differently.<br /> <br /> Marduk won't sell, lets say smartphones just as an example. Anyway, they won't sell smartphones directly to a consumer.<br /> <br /> Instead they'll create a startup company that &quot;invents&quot; smartphones and sell the startup company to investors.<br /> <br /> The idea is that instead of creating a long term steady supply of money which in turn creates a long term paper trail. They go for a one off deal which creates a smaller paper trail. <hr /><br /> Finally, thanks for taking the time to review everything. I'm glad you liked so much of it, and it's a relief to know that even the Marduk Society came across well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-06-2016, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T16:54:13-07:00","id":860641,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing that the first line in your first post was supposed to be &quot;Well I must say reading your review made <b>me</b> very happy&quot;, but I'm glad that you liked it so much. ;p To make my own reply...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860564#post860564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now this section of your review was very interesting to read, because you approached these from a Leviathan first perspective. Who is the Leviathan, what are they like.<br /> <br /> I actually wrote these from a cult first perspective. Note that the first paragraph of each Strain talks about cults. Each Strain starts with one aspect of why people join religions, twists it as appropriate for mad lovecraftian cultists, and creates a cult based primarally around that aspect. Then the Leviathans themselves were updated to 2E in the context of their cults.<br /> <br /> Obviously I'm not saying your reading is wrong, there is no right or wrong here, but it is something that jumped out at me and made me eager to look at the Strains from a new point of viem.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll probably find most players approach Leviathans from that &quot;Leviathan-first&quot; viewpoint. Yes, all Leviathans gather cults, but as with Mummies, the players are still interested in their PC first and foremost. Approaching Strains with the idea of &quot;how does this Strain shape its cults?&quot; is an important thing, but my presumption would be that generally, players will consider their cults a secondary element in character design, as is generally the case in M:tC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860564#post860564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tanninim are indeed alien to the way I imagine most people on this board think, you're not wrong there. But take a peak behind the curtain and discover that I did in fact base them on modern people.<br /> <br /> A while back there was a hurricane that hit America, I forget which one, and some preacher was in the papers saying that the hurricane was god's punishment for homosexuality. Tanninim were based on me trying to get inside his head. His homophobia wasn't actually relevant. Rather, I tried to imagine what humanity must look like to him so that a god who sent hurricanes was justified.<br /> <br /> I imagined that he saw humans as a thin veneer of civility over a savage brutal heart, with that veneer held in place by law and fear of punishment. Thus Tanninim's cults were built to resemble what I imagined he thought all humans were, and the Tanninim were created in what I imagined he saw God as. Someone trying to impose civilizaion and law upon savages who only understood the fear of punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting note on the Tanninim. I think the best part of this game is that both of us are right; the Tanninim, as I said in my review, give of the feeling of being &quot;The Evil of the Beast&quot; - the most savage and primordial of all Leviathan archetypes. That their cult is based around The Rule of Fear and Might Makes Right makes sense, as these are the bloody origins of all social structures, even in animals today.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860564#post860564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it was ever part of their inherent powers; have I misremembered?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not exactly hugely familiar with the 1e rules for Atolls. I haven't looked at the 1e stuff for a long time. I think they used to just calm the Wake and that was their power; they were people who <b>didn't</b> descend into babbling idiocy and animal-level intelligence from the Leviathan's presence, and also made it so that the Leviathan could be around people without hurting them. I may just be misinformed, and really, they work fine as they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860564#post860564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, do I need a reason for that? Mentally they fall within human norms, Pelopsids tend to be socieopathic but they think and act like human socieopaths. Do I need a reason for that beyond &quot;as the author I declare this is how Lahmasu brains work&quot;? (Serious question)</div> </div> </div> </div>For Hybrids, yeah, it would be helpful. Just saying &quot;author's fiat&quot; feels lazy and it's dissatisfying. It feels too arbitrary if this catfishgator-man is somehow fully human, mentally/spiritually, whilst the other is a walking abomination that drives people insane with its mere presence. Especially since, if I recall correctly, you actually make it mechanically possible for Leviathans to have started as Hybrids before &quot;waking&quot; to their true power.<br /> <br /> It just doesn't really feel right to me, considering both the Lovecraftian origins of the game and the Leviathans' nature as &quot;The Most Wicked Tribe&quot;, both of which suggest that to allow their ichor into your bloodstream is to damn your heirs, condemning all future generations of your seed to spring into life tainted and abhored, shunned by all &quot;pure&quot; humans.<br /> <br /> That Hybrids can come from such thematic stock, and be physically mutated, but somehow have a grace beyond their ancestors, feels... wrong, to me.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the idea of the Marduk Society, Ahabs and Empyreal Theurgists striving to wipe out Hybrids because they may represent a real option for the Leviathans - to pollute humanity's genepool so thoroughly that humanity is squeezed out and replaced by their miscegenated bastard spawn, creating a world &quot;better suited&quot; for the Tribe by literally outbreeding and absorbing their competitors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860565#post860565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I split this in two because it wouldn't let me post otherwise, weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably sheer volume of text; there are character limits in most forums, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860565#post860565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify encase there's any ambiguity at all. The School of Thunder are going in the antagonist section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know they're antagonists, that was clear. I was saying that these guys will make good antagonists once they're given believable rationale for their existence. Even as they are, they got me with a gut reaction of &quot;spineless, gutless, traitors&quot; that made me want to kill them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860565#post860565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that was answered.<br /> <br /> It's not that Marduk don't make money off old, not-quite-so-super-science. It's that they go about it differently.<br /> <br /> Marduk won't sell, lets say smartphones just as an example. Anyway, they won't sell smartphones directly to a consumer.<br /> <br /> Instead they'll create a startup company that &quot;invents&quot; smartphones and sell the startup company to investors.<br /> <br /> The idea is that instead of creating a long term steady supply of money which in turn creates a long term paper trail. They go for a one off deal which creates a smaller paper trail.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, that's not really how I read it, so that explains part of the problem.<br /> <br /> Plus, as I concluded in my last post, it really feels like the Marduk Society's chapter should at least make some acknowledgement of how the Society handles the clash between their warm idealism and cold reality. Hand-wringing over the fact mankind's own brutality and self-absorbtion hinders their efforts to provide the wave of the future just meshes well with their characteristics/lore, and likewise there really needs to be some examination of how they handle the historical fact that Progess does not necessarily equate to Unilterally Good. Even if it is the hypocrisy of refusing to acknowlege it, that just makes them more believable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T23:53:53-07:00","id":860832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860641#post860641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll probably find most players approach Leviathans from that &quot;Leviathan-first&quot; viewpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div> So long as they read well from both viewpoints I guess all's well that ends well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860641#post860641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Hybrids, yeah, it would be helpful. Just saying &quot;author's fiat&quot; feels lazy and it's dissatisfying. It feels too arbitrary if this catfishgator-man is somehow fully human, mentally/spiritually, whilst the other is a walking abomination that drives people insane with its mere presence.</div> </div> </div> </div> But isn't that the way actual the Lovecraft setting worked? The Deep Ones were for the most part normal people and at the end of the story the charachter is looking forward to becoming one. At The Mountains of Madness ends with the protagonist feeling respect for the elder things. Meanwhile Cthulhu drove psychics mad just by existing. Hybrids/Lahmasu are the Leviathan equivalent of Deep Ones and Elder Things.<br /> <br /> It never felt arbitrary to me that Deep Ones were basically another species that humans could relate too, like aliens form Star Trek, while Cthulhu wasn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860641#post860641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just doesn't really feel right to me, considering both the Lovecraftian origins of the game and the Leviathans' nature as &quot;The Most Wicked Tribe&quot;, both of which suggest that to allow their ichor into your bloodstream is to damn your heirs, condemning all future generations of your seed to spring into life tainted and abhored, shunned by all &quot;pure&quot; humans.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's plenty of that, but it's independent of mutations. Lahamin's bloodlines for example. That said, Mutations themselves - there's that line a fine line between a superpower and a disability and the template requires you to take nasty persistent Conditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860641#post860641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably sheer volume of text; there are character limits in most forums, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div> It said I had too many images...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-07-2016, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T00:20:37-07:00","id":860840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860832#post860832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But isn't that the way actual the Lovecraft setting worked? The Deep Ones were for the most part normal people and at the end of the story the charachter is looking forward to becoming one. At The Mountains of Madness ends with the protagonist feeling respect for the elder things. Meanwhile Cthulhu drove psychics mad just by existing. Hybrids/Lahmasu are the Leviathan equivalent of Deep Ones and Elder Things.<br /> <br /> It never felt arbitrary to me that Deep Ones were basically another species that humans could relate too, like aliens form Star Trek, while Cthulhu wasn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly.<br /> <br /> The Mountains of Madness, you're right about. They're an incredibly rare exception to the Non Humans, who Lovecraft almost universally portrays as evil monsters.<br /> <br /> Deeps Ones, though... no. The Shadow Over Innsmouth is one of Lovecraft's direct &quot;miscegenation-fuelled&quot; horror stories, being in the exact same &quot;category&quot; as Facts Concerning the Late Arthur Jermyn and His Family and Medusa's Coils - it's just survived the passing of the zeitgeist better than those other two. The reveal that the protagonist is so fouled is played for all the horror of the hybridization with Yog-Sothoth in the Dunwich Horror, and the ending is intended to be a Downer Ender, showing resignation, madness, and a Gothic-style inescapable descent into evil.<br /> <br /> <br /> It said you had too many images? ...Well, frankly, my opinion is simply that this forum was put together in a shambles. I'd have to try in order to come up with a worse coding interaction than this. It doesn't surprise me it gave you that sort of gibberish answer, given the crap it's pulled on me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T02:29:11-07:00","id":860888,"title":"","content":"Ok, that does make more sense than <i>Lovecraft</i> writing a positive portrayal of turning into a fishman.<br /> <br /> Anyway, back to the topic at hand. There is definitely support in Leviathan for a &quot;miscegenation-fuelled&quot; horror story. The most obvious would be a story that starts with the PC getting their first dot of Mutations and starting an investigation, ending with the discovery that they're turning into a Leviathan. The Mahhu would also do great, Lahamin's bloodline curse of isolation creates an appropriate mood and scatters the clues far and wide for a nicely challenging investigation.<br /> <br /> But the thing about miscegenation horror, at least in my opinion, is that it works when the protagonist is investigating their own past and by default Hybrids are NPCs. Especially with Leviathan, I could just see the PC Leviathan looking at a Lovecraft deep one and going &quot;is that it, my cursed genetics are far worse than yours&quot;. There's definately room for Hybrid/Lahmasu to support miscegenation-horror. But I don't think miscegenation-horror could work as the core of Hybrids.<br /> <br /> And if nothing else. I do think that the setting really does needs thematic equivalents of Elder Things (and Deep Ones, I never said Lahmasu were good); I think that the way Lahmasu can blur the boundaries of mankind and the tribe makes a more interesting setting.<br /> <br /> I want Lahamsu to be able to do miscegenation horror; but I also want them to be able to do more than just miscegenation horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T03:17:22-07:00","id":860906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860888#post860888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, that does make more sense than <i>Lovecraft</i> writing a positive portrayal of turning into a fishman.<br /> <br /> Anyway, back to the topic at hand. There is definitely support in Leviathan for a &quot;miscegenation-fuelled&quot; horror story. The most obvious would be a story that starts with the PC getting their first dot of Mutations and starting an investigation, ending with the discovery that they're turning into a Leviathan. The Mahhu would also do great, Lahamin's bloodline curse of isolation creates an appropriate mood and scatters the clues far and wide for a nicely challenging investigation.<br /> <br /> But the thing about miscegenation horror, at least in my opinion, is that it works when the protagonist is investigating their own past and by default Hybrids are NPCs. Especially with Leviathan, I could just see the PC Leviathan looking at a Lovecraft deep one and going &quot;is that it, my cursed genetics are far worse than yours&quot;. There's definately room for Hybrid/Lahmasu to support miscegenation-horror. But I don't think miscegenation-horror could work as the core of Hybrids.<br /> <br /> And if nothing else. I do think that the setting really does needs thematic equivalents of Elder Things (and Deep Ones, I never said Lahmasu were good); I think that the way Lahmasu can blur the boundaries of mankind and the tribe makes a more interesting setting.<br /> <br /> I want Lahamsu to be able to do miscegenation horror; but I also want them to be able to do more than just miscegenation horror.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Huh. I had half-baked ideas about there being a classification of Hybrids that was between Hybrid (using their general template for construction, and sourced similarly) and full Leviathans (they might possess the Wake or Channels). Except their mental state broke down to the degree that they didn't even <i>have</i> Integrity (or Tranquility), and likely not Virtue or Vice either. Complete &quot;inhuman monster&quot;. Tentative name was Abomination.<br /> <br /> Might there be room for such a concept to fill this niche?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T03:24:23-07:00","id":860909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860906#post860906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Huh. I had half-baked ideas about there being a classification of Hybrids that was between Hybrid (using their general template for construction, and sourced similarly) and full Leviathans (they might possess the Wake or Channels). Except their mental state broke down to the degree that they didn't even <i>have</i> Integrity (or Tranquility), and likely not Virtue or Vice either. Complete &quot;inhuman monster&quot;. Tentative name was Abomination.<br /> <br /> Might there be room for such a concept to fill this niche?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that there might be Hybrids that have such animalistic minds as to not have Integrity or the like already. I'm not sure if that's from 1e though. If not, this certainly bears thinking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T03:27:08-07:00","id":860911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860909#post860909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think that there might be Hybrids that have such animalistic minds as to not have Integrity or the like already. I'm not sure if that's from 1e though. If not, this certainly bears thinking about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1E Hybrids had caps on their maximum Intelligence inversely related to their &quot;Depth&quot;, which could reduce them to animalistic intelligence. Not sure if that made them drop Morality, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T03:45:31-07:00","id":860920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860911#post860911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1E Hybrids had caps on their maximum Intelligence inversely related to their &quot;Depth&quot;, which could reduce them to animalistic intelligence. Not sure if that made them drop Morality, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the Depth ones were described as 'sub-sentient'. If a creature isn't sentient, I don't see how it can possess morality (at least more than 'programmed' morality).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T04:29:44-07:00","id":860936,"title":"","content":"So 1E Hybrids. Back in 1E there was hard rules about how intelligence and Depth interacted. I consider that to have been a mistake on my part, hence why it's not in 2E.<br /> <br /> To expand upon that. I don't think the idea of mutations reducing a Hybrids intelligence was a bad idea. I just think giving it hard rules was a bad idea. Firstly those rules didn't allow for exceptions, and secondly it didn't take into account the different themes and concepts of each Hybrid strain.<br /> <br /> So in 2E Hybrid mutations can still have reduced intelligence, there's just not rules about it. Just create the character with however many dots of Intelligence you think are appropriate.<br /> <br /> As for the Hybrids with &quot;animistic intelligence&quot; (they were a bit smarter than that actually. On the level of a human feral child) - they're not in 2E yet but they will be. I'm going to represent them with a Genetic Condition. Whether they have Integrity... no idea really. I'll leave that unstated and let the storyteller decide.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a><br /> Your Abomination niche sounds easy to fill with either a Typhon or a Hybrid who has the aforementioned genetic condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-07-2016, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T10:06:24-07:00","id":861119,"title":"","content":"Sans the fluff text, here's the next Elements Channel.<br /> <br /> <b>Swallowing the Sun</b><br /> <br /> Depth 1: Birthright of Elements<br /> Depth 2: The Leviathan may spend one Ichor and make a roll Contested by Resolve + Supernatural advantage to inflict the Blinded Tilt on a single target.<br /> <br /> Alternatively the Leviathan may spend an Ichor and roll to create the Low Light Environmental Tilt in an area with a diameter of Sheol * 10 yards. Each Success increases the severity of the Tilt by one and the effect lasts for a scene. At this Depth the Leviathan may not darken natural sunlight or any supernatural light source. If a character has fulfilled their virtue in this scene (including the Virtue Merit available to Marduk and Empyerian Thurgists) then they may immunise technology from this Channel with a touch. A torch they hold or any lights they switch on will cut through the Leviathan's darkness.<br /> <br /> Depth 3: The Leviathan's darkness conceals the hearts of men. If the Leviathan has created or enhanced the Low Light tilt, the penalty also applies to mundane uses of the Empathy Skill. At the Storyteller's discretion supernatural abilities that reveal the hearts of men may also be affected.<br /> <br /> Depth 4: The Leviathan may spend two Ichor and make a contested roll vs Resolve + Supernatural against a Wake vulnerable target to try and trap them in a pocket realm of pure darkness for a scene. Though physically unharmed they may be emotionally damaged. Roll Resolve + Composure<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The victim comes out their ordeal strengthened. Take the Steadfast Condition; alternatively if it is dramatically appropriate they may emerge as a Hunter, an Ahab, or something else entirely.<br /> Success: Take the Shaken Condition, also roll for a Breaking Point with a +2 bonus. Characters who do not have Integrity take the Condition but ignore the Breaking Point.<br /> Failure: Take the Broken, Madness or Phobia (of darkness) Condition. Alternatively become Beloved. Also roll for a Breaking Point.<br /> Dramatic Failure: As per a Failure, but automatically loose a dot of Integrity if you have it.<br /> <br /> Alternatively the Leviathan may spend two Ichor to summon a cloud of pure darkness. It covers an area with a radius of three feet per success, less if the Leviathan desires, and no natural sense or technological scan may penetrate into the cloud. Supernatural attempts trigger a Clash of Wills against the Leviathan.<br /> <br /> Depth 5: The Leviathan may now create darkness even in the presence of natural sunlight or supernatural light sources. The latter may require a Clash of Wills. Like technology, supernatural light sources can also be immunised through virtuous action, but only if the virtuous person is able to operate the light source. In addition the Leviathan's immunity to their own use of this Channel now extends to their Beloved.<br /> <br /> Depth 6: The Leviathan's ability to create darkness expands to truly prodigious levels. When using the Depth 2 iteration of this Channel to create the Low Light Tilt the affected area becomes that of the Leviathan's Wake.<br /> <br /> Depth 7: The Leviathan may spend four Ichor to create the Primordial Darkness tilt in an area with a diameter of Sheol * 3 miles. The Leviathan swallows the sun and returns the world to a purer chaotic state that existed before the gods created the world, if the myths of many different cultures are to be believed.<br /> <br /> Primordial Darkness requires regular darkness to exist, but any source of darkness will suffice. The Tilt lasts one scene.<br /> <br /> Low Light (Environmental Tilt)<br /> <br /> Within the affected humans take a penalty of -1 to -5 to all sight based perception. Ranged combat takes an equal penalty which increases by one at medium range and two at long range. Other creatures take a greater or lesser penalty depending on their natural or supernatural abilities for low light.<br /> <br /> Primordial Darkness (Environmental Tilt)<br /> <br /> Within the affected area all technology reduces it's equipment bonus by the penalty of the Low Light Tilt. Occult technology is also affected, if the dot rating is equal or lower than the penalty of the Low Light Tilt it ceases to function. Finally all mundane uses of Social Skills other than Intimidation take a penalty equal to the penalty of the Low Light Tilt.<br /> <br /> Anyone who fulfils their Virtue (including the Virtue merit available to Marduk and Emparian Thurgists) is becomes immune to the Tilt for the reminder of it's duration, and any technology they use also becomes immunised. They must be able to operate occult technology to immunise it.<br /> <br /> <br /> (All that stuff about virtue immunising is mostly there because it would be <i>so much</i> fun to play a Cloverfield like disaster movie story set after a Leviathan unleashes Primordial Darkness and the Virtue rule makes a good reason thematic reason for PCs to be immune. While I won't put crossover mechanics into the corebook. Princess Invocations also immunise. Judge Vestments don't immunise, but it would fit for Judges to get a Verdict that makes them uber effective inside Primordial Darkness. They're god's personal hard man for hard times.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-07-2016, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T10:23:07-07:00","id":861129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=861119#post861119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sans the fluff text, here's the next Elements Channel.<br /> <br /> <b>Swallowing the Sun</b><br /> <br /> Depth 1: Birthright of Elements<br /> Depth 2: The Leviathan may spend one Ichor and make a roll Contested by Resolve + Supernatural advantage to inflict the Blinded Tilt on a single target.<br /> <br /> Alternatively the Leviathan may spend an Ichor and roll to create the Low Light Environmental Tilt in an area with a diameter of Sheol * 10 feet. Each Success increases the severity of the Tilt by one and the effect lasts for a scene. At this Depth the Leviathan may not darken natural sunlight or any supernatural light source. If a character has fulfilled their virtue in this scene (including the Virtue Merit available to Marduk and Empyerian Thurgists) then they may immunise technology from this Channel with a touch. A torch they hold or any lights they switch on will cut through the Leviathan's darkness.<br /> <br /> Depth 3: The Leviathan's darkness conceals the hearts of men. If the Leviathan has created or enhanced the Low Light tilt, the penalty also applies to mundane uses of the Empathy Skill. At the Storyteller's discretion supernatural abilities that reveal the hearts of men may also be affected.<br /> <br /> Depth 4: The Leviathan may spend two Ichor and make a contested roll vs Resolve + Supernatural against a Wake vulnerable target to try and trap them in a pocket realm of pure darkness for a scene. Though physically unharmed they may be emotionally damaged. Roll Resolve + Composure<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The victim comes out their ordeal strengthened. Take the Steadfast Condition; alternatively if it is dramatically appropriate they may emerge as a Hunter, an Ahab, or something else entirely.<br /> Success: Take the Shaken Condition, also roll for a Breaking Point with a +2 bonus. Characters who do not have Integrity take the Condition but ignore the Breaking Point.<br /> Failure: Take the Broken, Madness or Phobia (of darkness) Condition. Alternatively become Beloved. Also roll for a Breaking Point.<br /> Dramatic Failure: As per a Failure, but automatically loose a dot of Integrity if you have it.<br /> <br /> Alternatively the Leviathan may spend two Ichor to summon a cloud of pure darkness. It covers an area with a radius of three feet per success, less if the Leviathan desires, and no natural sense or technological scan may penetrate into the cloud. Supernatural attempts trigger a Clash of Wills against the Leviathan.<br /> <br /> Depth 5: The Leviathan may now create darkness even in the presence of natural sunlight or supernatural light sources. The latter may require a Clash of Wills. Like technology, supernatural light sources can also be immunised through virtuous action, but only if the virtuous person is able to operate the light source. In addition the Leviathan's immunity to their own use of this Channel now extends to their Beloved.<br /> <br /> Depth 6: The Leviathan's ability to create darkness expands to truly prodigious levels. When using the Depth 2 iteration of this Channel to create the Low Light Tilt the affected area becomes that of the Leviathan's Wake.<br /> <br /> Depth 7: The Leviathan may spend four Ichor to create the Primordial Darkness tilt in an area with a diameter of Sheol * 3 miles. The Leviathan swallows the sun and returns the world to a purer chaotic state that existed before the gods created the world, if the myths of many different cultures are to be believed.<br /> <br /> Primordial Darkness requires regular darkness to exist, but any source of darkness will suffice. The Tilt lasts one scene.<br /> <br /> Primordial Darkness (Environmental Tilt)<br /> <br /> Within the affected area all technology reduces it's equipment bonus by the severity of the Low Light Tilt. Occult technology is also affected, if the dot rating is equal or lower than the severity of the Low Light Tilt it ceases to function. Finally all mundane uses of Social Skills other than Intimidation take a penalty equal to the severity of the Low Light Tilt.<br /> <br /> Anyone who fulfils their Virtue (including the Virtue merit available to Marduk and Emparian Thurgists) is becomes immune to the Tilt for the reminder of it's duration, and any technology they use also becomes immunised. They must be able to operate occult technology to immunise it.<br /> <br /> <br /> (All that stuff about virtue immunising is mostly there because it would be <i>so much</i> fun to play a Cloverfield like disaster movie story set after a Leviathan unleashes Primordial Darkness and the Virtue rule makes a good reason thematic reason for PCs to be immune. While I won't put crossover mechanics into the corebook. Princess Invocations also immunise. Judge Vestments don't immunise, but it would fit for Judges to get a Verdict that makes them uber effective inside Primordial Darkness. They're god's personal hard man for hard times.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> two words: love it.<br /> <br /> It's so much better than the original Swallowing the Sun which, frankly, was a bit underwhelming. I look forward to seeing more.<br /> <br /> BTW, what happened to the stuff for Rituals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T10:24:55-07:00","id":861132,"title":"","content":"Rituals are waiting for Mage 2E to be released so I can use it as a mechanical base.<br /> <br /> Also, did I use feet for Depth 1? Depth 4 uses feet, Depth 1 uses yards.<br /> <br /> Fixed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-07-2016, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T10:51:24-07:00","id":861150,"title":"","content":"If you are large enough,can you use your own shadow to create the darkness for Primordial Darkness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T12:42:38-07:00","id":861215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860936#post860936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a><br /> Your Abomination niche sounds easy to fill with either a Typhon or a Hybrid who has the aforementioned genetic condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it was also for weird interactions and odd cases. A Typhon is a Beastial Leviathan - they have Leviathan powers. Hybrids have Mutations. Abominations might have Wake distorting abilities (such as disrupting it so you can't &quot;manage&quot; your cult, or even turning them against you) without possessing the Wake (and thus, Ripples) themselves. Less &quot;direct danger&quot;, more outside-context. Definitely Antagonist-only material. But hey, if Typhons or Hybrids can get similar abilities, great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T13:48:18-07:00","id":861264,"title":"","content":"Love the new elemental channels! I may be going crazy, but i could have sworn maximum depth used to be 6? Did that change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","name":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T14:19:43-07:00","id":861291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tribute of a Dark Heart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=861264#post861264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love the new elemental channels! I may be going crazy, but i could have sworn maximum depth used to be 6? Did that change?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He changed Depth 0 to Depth 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T15:11:45-07:00","id":861361,"title":"","content":"Yep. The 0-6 numbering predated my involvement with 1E. At long last the all important number '7' is where it belongs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=861150#post861150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are large enough,can you use your own shadow to create the darkness for Primordial Darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. You'd have to position your body right to create enough darkness to inflict perception penalties, but you could do it.<br /> <br /> And I just noticed there is no Low Light Tilt in the GMC corebook. I guess I'd better write my own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-07-2016, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T04:21:02-07:00","id":861735,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=860641#post860641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I know they're antagonists, that was clear. I was saying that these guys will make good antagonists once they're given believable rationale for their existence. Even as they are, they got me with a gut reaction of &quot;spineless, gutless, traitors&quot; that made me want to kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it doesn't seem that difficult to justify their existance. All Levithans (I believe) started life as humans. Except for those born into a cult, many would have been raised in a human religion or adopted one later in life. Maybe a large percentage would be willing to abandon those beliefs when it turns out that they are gods of a sort in their own right, but the more devoted would be willing to hold on through even more severe challenges to their worldviews.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who are the real traitors:&quot; they might ask, &quot;the ones who side with their religion over &quot;kin&quot; they may never have met, or those who are willing to let mere genetics turn them against the institutions which nutured them and the God(s) who shepherded them?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T05:43:45-07:00","id":861764,"title":"","content":"I <b>cannot </b>believe I didn't think of that. I was thinking that Leviathans joined the School because if anyone can, E.G, turn a Leviathan back into human it would be God. That said, VoidDrifer is right, no matter how easy or hard it is to justify their existence the justifications need to be in the writeup; both justifications are now on my mental todo list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T18:59:19-07:00","id":863426,"title":"","content":"So, I was wondering; I've been doing some thinking about crossovers in a Leviathan context. I know the default assumption is that &quot;Leviathan is all there is&quot;, but that doesn't mean we can't consider an &quot;expansion book&quot; for those who like crossovers, does it?<br /> <br /> I was curious if my thoughts/ideas on the subject would be okay, or not until later, or just not welcome at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T21:02:56-07:00","id":863469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=863426#post863426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was wondering; I've been doing some thinking about crossovers in a Leviathan context. I know the default assumption is that &quot;Leviathan is all there is&quot;, but that doesn't mean we can't consider an &quot;expansion book&quot; for those who like crossovers, does it?<br /> <br /> I was curious if my thoughts/ideas on the subject would be okay, or not until later, or just not welcome at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know it there's anything to preclude it, and Leviathan could certainly cross over with other lines in interesting ways, especially Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T00:20:46-07:00","id":863510,"title":"","content":"There's already the stereotypes under Schools to give you some ideas.<br /> <br /> I imagine that Leviathans won't be popular with any supernatural group. Even if this particular Leviathan is keeping to itself and not causing trouble, a lot of people are going to feel nervous having something caperable of the kind of destruction Leviathans can cause nearby. Mages and the Circle of the Crone are probably the biggest exception, since Leviathans can be a great mystery to study, but even then - why not poke the sleeping dragon who doesn't live near you? Meanwhile the Circle may actually want the Leviathan to start causing mass destruction and chaos since, you know, they're the Circle. Someone really should write a Bloodline built for Circle-Leviathan crossover. (not me though, I don't know enough Vampire)<br /> <br /> For Beast? I wouldn't say that Beast is the closest game to Leviathan (that would definitely be Genius); but they both use themes of family and lizard brain instincts; and they use both in incompatible ways which makes crossover harder. I think the most interesting crossover you could do is to make Leviathan's into the Beasts' Beast. Beasts go around telling humans to learn lessons from their primordial instincts and encourage other supernaturals to embrace their monstrous nature. Leviathans tell Beasts &quot;I'm what you get when you take that too far&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:31:16-07:00","id":863628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=863510#post863510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's already the stereotypes under Schools to give you some ideas.<br /> <br /> I imagine that Leviathans won't be popular with any supernatural group. Even if this particular Leviathan is keeping to itself and not causing trouble, a lot of people are going to feel nervous having something caperable of the kind of destruction Leviathans can cause nearby. Mages and the Circle of the Crone are probably the biggest exception, since Leviathans can be a great mystery to study, but even then - why not poke the sleeping dragon who doesn't live near you? Meanwhile the Circle may actually want the Leviathan to start causing mass destruction and chaos since, you know, they're the Circle. Someone really should write a Bloodline built for Circle-Leviathan crossover. (not me though, I don't know enough Vampire)<br /> <br /> For Beast? I wouldn't say that Beast is the closest game to Leviathan (that would definitely be Genius); but they both use themes of family and lizard brain instincts; and they use both in incompatible ways which makes crossover harder. I think the most interesting crossover you could do is to make Leviathan's into the Beasts' Beast. Beasts go around telling humans to learn lessons from their primordial instincts and encourage other supernaturals to embrace their monstrous nature. Leviathans tell Beasts &quot;I'm what you get when you take that too far&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I didn't mean an easy crossover, so much as an interesting one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:53:55-07:00","id":863645,"title":"","content":"On the topic of other fansplats, I might have inadvertently created a fansplat the has a unique... clash with Leviathan on a thematic level.<br /> <br /> The idea for Monarch was that they were created as a result of experimentation from an alien race to act as rulers for a colonization attempt, or atleast, what seems like it.<br /> -They are relatively new having only showed up in the past 70 years, contrasting against the timeless and ancient existance of Leviathans<br /> -They are the beacons of civilization, order and authority imposed against wild evolution, contrasted against the Levithans being anticiviliation.<br /> -They possess great psychic powers able to command nests or small cities of creatures, but not men without first developing these powers and even then it's limited. Leviathans just passively brainwash bystanders.<br /> -Monarchs congregate into a massive feudal system or rules and regulations. Leviathans are more solitary.<br /> -The creators of the Monarchs still exist, creating only new Monarchs, sending them down to Earth, but otherwise, not being involved. Leviathans have their Progenitors long gone.<br /> <br /> <br /> They both possess psychic powers, reality warping abilities, the idea of being monsters that birth new horrors, and even rulership, but they're so different otherwise.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:39:13-07:00","id":863715,"title":"","content":"Asking out of curiosity, ignorance and because i just saw the two threads in this forum, but how do Leviathans relate or connect to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat\">demigods/empyreans</a>?<br /> <br /> And do the themes and vicissitudes of either - or both - touch on elements and concepts of either Immortals, Mirrors' Dark Heroes or Beasts (and their antagonists)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T10:02:39-07:00","id":863735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=863715#post863715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asking out of curiosity, ignorance and because i just saw the two threads in this forum, but how do Leviathans relate or connect to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat\">demigods/empyreans</a>?<br /> <br /> And do the themes and vicissitudes of either - or both - touch on elements and concepts of either Immortals, Mirrors' Dark Heroes or Beasts (and their antagonists)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They don't directly relate but I'm going to quote something I wrote about their relations:<br /> <br /> Leviathan: I would imagine that Demigods see leviathans as a twisted mockery of what they are while leviathans are fascinated by the way that Halysis doesn't directly drive people mad like the Wake. That would be a point of extreme interest for them I think. On the other hand, demigods are easily associated with the 'new gods' who oppose the Leviathans, a point which would most likely lead to some particularly destructive and impressive conflict.<br /> <br /> As for the others, I'm not so sure about the themes of Leviathan but demigod doesn't so much. I'd say to have a look at the concept work under 'Other Splats' for information on Beasts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T05:22:40-07:00","id":864220,"title":"","content":"I haven't read Monarch or Demigod, so I can't really comment. The Empyerian and gods such as Zeus are a part of the Leviathan setting, if a small part being the source of a couple of antagonist splats: Empyerian Thurgists and The School of Thunder. So the idea that that younger gods don't have a Wake would be pretty familiar to the Tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T05:31:50-07:00","id":864228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864220#post864220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read Monarch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They're kinda new so it's not unexpected. I only really started major work on them in the past 2 months, though the thread has been existant for longer due to Haitus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T06:19:06-07:00","id":864254,"title":"","content":"I had some ideas for channels/adaptations based on the Endbringers from Worm (for those who haven't read, think 2 Typhons and an Opheon all at the Sheol 20+ range)<br /> <br /> Behemoth: Behemoth's lightning attacks and pyrokinesis don't really fit thematically with the themes of Leviathan. Other than that, there are a few things that could be adapted. For these purposes, the most interesting thing from the Behemoth fight was the description of how the fires in the area were even worse than they should have been due to his power.<br /> <br /> - Sun Poisoned Bile: Probably a high Sheol adaptation to Swallowing the Sun. Enhance the darkness created with the depth 4 of Swallowing the Sun to do damage to those inside it (Benny's kill aura), cause the Primal Darkness of depth 7 to make existing environmental hazards worse (force people to check more often, increase severity, things like that)<br /> - Call The Earth's Fire: High Sheol adaptation to the channel that lets you create earthquakes. Lets you create persistent environmental hazards involving magma.<br /> <br /> Leviathan: Arc 8 (Extermination) of Worm should be required reading for anyone wanting to run/play a high Sheol Leviathan focusing on Elements. In fact, here is a link: <a href=\"https://parahumans.wordpress.com/category/stories-arcs-1-10/arc-8-extermination/8-1/\" target=\"_blank\">https://parahumans.wordpress.com/cat...rmination/8-1/</a> . Of Worm!Leviathan's abilities, the only one that probably isn't already being planned is his water clone, which totally needs to be an adaptation to whichever channel ends up letting the Leviathan control water.<br /> <br /> - The Levies Shall Break: Adaptation for the channel that lets you create storms/waves (I suspect the 2 1e channels that do that will be combined, maybe also incorporating the earthquake one), allows you to summon waves on land so long as your wake touches a body of water.<br /> - The Sea Shall Know Its Master's Face: Adaptation to the channel that lets you control water. Lets you duplicate your attacks/soak extra damage so long as there is water around.<br /> <br /> The Simurgh: An example of an Awareness/Sanctity focused Opheon. Most of her schtick could be accomplished by combining Lambent Eyes of Judgement, The Key and the Gate, Call of the Depths and Besieging the Tower of Will.<br /> <br /> - Herald of the Worst of all Worlds: Very high Sheol adaptation for Call of the Depths, requires Lambent Eyes of Judgement, The Key and the Gate and Besieging the Tower of Will. Allows you to declare a long term agenda when you use the depth 7 version of Call of the Depths. People affected by your Call of the Depths will be altered, a la Besieging the Tower of Will, to support that agenda. The Leviathan gains a number of points based on the roll and the number of people affected that can later be traded in to add bonuses to rolls supporting that agenda (mainly thinking cult rolls) or penalties to rolls opposing that agenda. These point can also be spent to retroactively introduce elements like hidden or unwitting collaborators as appropriate.<br /> <br /> All: The Endbringers keep most of their physical form in other realities.<br /> <br /> - Shielding the Source: Adaptation to whichever channel lets you trade size for durability. Places a cap on the damage you take from a single attack (maybe in a round at depth 7?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","user":"Thamuzz","date":". 04-12-2016, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T06:54:02-07:00","id":864267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864254#post864254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Behemoth: Behemoth's lightning attacks and pyrokinesis don't really fit thematically with the themes of Leviathan.</div> </div> </div> </div> Indeed they don't. If you dig up some of the old John's Scion's Resources blogs about redesigning Boons they talk about how in myths you never see Posideon &quot;waterbending&quot;, I'm trying to follow what I remember of their guidelines (and using the published list of powers) to make Elements appropriately mythic. Blasting people with a magic firehose is out, spontanious floods or drowning people on dry land is in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864254#post864254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Other than that, there are a few things that could be adapted. For these purposes, the most interesting thing from the Behemoth fight was the description of how the fires in the area were even worse than they should have been due to his power.</div> </div> </div> </div> A very simple Adaptation to write. This can go in as an effect on Storms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864254#post864254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sun Poisoned Bile: Probably a high Sheol adaptation to Swallowing the Sun. Enhance the darkness created with the depth 4 of Swallowing the Sun to do damage to those inside it (Benny's kill aura), cause the Primal Darkness of depth 7 to make existing environmental hazards worse (force people to check more often, increase severity, things like that)</div> </div> </div> </div> It could be done, the trick would be to avoid it clashing too much or being uesless next to other environmental hazard powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864254#post864254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Call The Earth's Fire: High Sheol adaptation to the channel that lets you create earthquakes. Lets you create persistent environmental hazards involving magma.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm going to say the policy is that Leviathns can't do anything with fire, and can only unleash lava by aiming an earthquake at a conviniently located volcano.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864254#post864254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worm!Leviathan's abilities, the only one that probably isn't already being planned is his water clone, which totally needs to be an adaptation to whichever channel ends up letting the Leviathan control water.</div> </div> </div> </div> Water clones would work better as something you use with Mother of a Thousand Young for the cloning and a Vitality or Fecundity ability to turn into water; rather than a specific water clone ability.<br /> <br /> It could also work as a feature so your Mother of a Thousand Young minions could be made of water.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864254#post864254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The Levies Shall Break: Adaptation for the channel that lets you create storms/waves (I suspect the 2 1e channels that do that will be combined, maybe also incorporating the earthquake one), allows you to summon waves on land so long as your wake touches a body of water.</div> </div> </div> </div> The power to make waves also lets you apply the Flooded tilt by summoning water from nowhere. Just summon water first, then make them go all wavy.<br /> <br /> Storms/waves will still be seperate in 2E; since I don't have any ideas to fill the gap that would be left by merging them. Instead I just made sure that the water element Channel can be used on dry land.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864254#post864254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The Sea Shall Know Its Master's Face: Adaptation to the channel that lets you control water. Lets you duplicate your attacks/soak extra damage so long as there is water around.</div> </div> </div> </div> Duplicating attacks would be OP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864254#post864254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Herald of the Worst of all Worlds: Very high Sheol adaptation for Call of the Depths, requires Lambent Eyes of Judgement, The Key and the Gate and Besieging the Tower of Will. Allows you to declare a long term agenda when you use the depth 7 version of Call of the Depths. People affected by your Call of the Depths will be altered, a la Besieging the Tower of Will, to support that agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to keep this simple. It simply creates a new Cult who're mechanically Beloved, but psychologically linked to the agenda rather than any particular Leviathan.<br /> <br /> I'll probably create a sidebar for The Key and the Gate giving guidelines on how to do Bill and Ted style time Shinanigans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864254#post864254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Shielding the Source: Adaptation to whichever channel lets you trade size for durability.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not going to happen in 2E. My policy: Anything that makes Leviathan's smaller is fundamnetally missing the point.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:36:23-07:00","id":864318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864267#post864267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storms/waves will still be seperate in 2E; since I don't have any ideas to fill the gap that would be left by merging them. Instead I just made sure that the water element Channel can be used on dry land.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible replacement: Charybdis. Creates an environmental hazard that draws stuff towards a particular spot. Even fits with the Elements &lt;=&gt; Nu &lt;=&gt; Gluttony thing. Maybe broaden from just being a vortex to encompass currents/undertow, allowing the Leviathan to herd enemies into other hazards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864267#post864267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Duplicating attacks would be OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and the more I think about it, the more his ability suggests Overpowering Strength of the Titans from 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864267#post864267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to keep this simple. It simply creates a new Cult who're mechanically Beloved, but psychologically linked to the agenda rather than any particular Leviathan.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually pretty much perfectly encompasses what I was going for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864267#post864267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not going to happen in 2E. My policy: Anything that makes Leviathan's smaller is fundamnetally missing the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking about making a human sized Leviathan smaller, I agree wholeheartedly. If we're talking about reducing (but definitely not eliminating) the amount a Leviathan grows via transformation/channels, I'll offer an uncertain disagreement.<br /> I'd suggest taking the depth 5/6 (1e/2e) power of No Mysteries of the Flesh and turning it into an adaptation that requires Lifeblood of the Titans, and allows the Leviathan to reduce the size increase they would get from it or transformation in exchange for extra durability (health levels and armor). The number of size levels they could sacrifice this way would be limited by a both a roll and a cap (say, they could use at most 1/3 of the size increase, min 1, no matter how many successes they accumulate). Shielding the source would depend on that adaptation, increasing the amount that could be sacrificed (lets say, to 1/2 for sake of argument) and allow them to store up healing that they could use in the future, or some other mechanic to represent the multiple dimensional aspect of their biology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","user":"Thamuzz","date":". 04-12-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:41:52-07:00","id":864323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864318#post864318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we're talking about making a human sized Leviathan smaller, I agree wholeheartedly. If we're talking about reducing (but definitely not eliminating) the amount a Leviathan grows via transformation/channels, I'll offer an uncertain disagreement.<br /> I'd suggest taking the depth 5/6 (1e/2e) power of No Mysteries of the Flesh and turning it into an adaptation that requires Lifeblood of the Titans, and allows the Leviathan to reduce the size increase they would get from it or Apotheosis form in exchange for extra durability (health levels and armor). The number of size levels they could sacrifice this way would be limited by a both a roll and a cap (say, they could use at most 1/3 of the size increase, min 1, no matter how many successes they accumulate). Shielding the source would depend on that adaptation, increasing the amount that could be sacrificed (lets say, to 1/2 for sake of argument) and allow them to store up healing that they could use in the future, or some other mechanic to represent the multiple dimensional aspect of their biology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that Lifeblood of Titans isn't in leviathan any more, given that Sheol basically covers the stuff that it did. I might be wrong mind you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:59:52-07:00","id":864327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864323#post864323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure that Lifeblood of Titans isn't in leviathan any more, given that Sheol basically covers the stuff that it did. I might be wrong mind you.</div> </div> </div> </div>And The Mountain Walked is probably out. LotT still might have a place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7874-thamuzz","name":"Thamuzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:08:17-07:00","id":864368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thamuzz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864327#post864327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And The Mountain Walked is probably out. LotT still might have a place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is though that the base leviathan's Size in the various Depths has been upped from 1e to the point that LotT would have only nominal effect. It might be changed a little but I honestly doubt that it'll still be in here. Is that right <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:13:56-07:00","id":864374,"title":"","content":"That is right. LotT is gone; with the boosts to size built into Sheol and Transformation there's no longer any place for a Size related Channel.<br /> <br /> And I am going to stick with no powers that reduce a Leviathan's size, in Apotheosis or otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:50:17-07:00","id":864391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864267#post864267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to say the policy is that Leviathns can't do anything with fire, and can only unleash lava by aiming an earthquake at a conviniently located volcano.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't there an Adaptation that let Hunter's Blood do Fire damage? Something related to Tiamat's Breath?<br /> <br /> And what about an Evolution (regarding re-casting Leviathan abilities to be fire/magma related)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864374#post864374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is right. LotT is gone; with the boosts to size built into Sheol and Transformation there's no longer any place for a Size related Channel.<br /> <br /> And I am going to stick with no powers that reduce a Leviathan's size, in Apotheosis or otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even with space bending distortions or &quot;seeming&quot; smaller?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T11:04:00-07:00","id":864396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864391#post864391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there an Adaptation that let Hunter's Blood do Fire damage? Something related to Tiamat's Breath?</div> </div> </div> </div> It wasn't quite fire; but it was close enough to be a counter argument.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what I'm going to do with that. I might make breathing fire an exception since it's just shooting fire and not being able to control or manifest fire. It's a biology power with high pressure chemical glands and not a psychic power.<br /> <br /> The Hunters Blood itself would probably be reworked to be a generic ranged power - stingers, acids, etc, not just poisonous blood. The Tiamat's Fury adaptation, I have no idea what I'd do with that. The only thing I can think of that's worthy of the name &quot;Tiamat's Fury&quot; would be a power that goes &quot;Tiamat maked all life, and she can unmake all life&quot; - if anything hit by Tiamat's Fury has a Bane; then Tiamat's Fury counts as though it's that bane.<br /> <br /> Though that might be a bit OP <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864391#post864391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what about an Evolution (regarding re-casting Leviathan abilities to be fire/magma related)?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure. As a rule of thumb, an Evolution can break any rule.<br /> <br /> Just don't go to crazy. No I can't take damage or automatic successes on every roll <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864391#post864391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even with space bending distortions or &quot;seeming&quot; smaller?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. Any such powers would more likely make other things larger instead. That said, thinks like making a house grow to enormous sizes so Godzilla can hunt ant-sized humans hiding among the carpet forest seems way more suited to Changeling or Beast than Leviathan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:24:49-07:00","id":864430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864396#post864396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I can think of that's worthy of the name &quot;Tiamat's Fury&quot; would be a power that goes &quot;Tiamat maked all life, and she can unmake all life&quot; - if anything hit by Tiamat's Fury has a Bane; then Tiamat's Fury counts as though it's that bane.<br /> <br /> Though that might be a bit OP <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or not, considering the Exploit Hellfire, or high dot Mage Arcana, or high dot Rage Manifestations, or decent dot Katastrofi...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864396#post864396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. As a rule of thumb, an Evolution can break any rule.<br /> <br /> Just don't go to crazy. No I can't take damage or automatic successes on every roll <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more a Leviathan that took &quot;Primordial Ocean&quot; to mean the seas of molten rock the Earth was formed from before it cooled. Likely School of the Abyss - not too many neighbors in the mantle, and &quot;swimming&quot; up for the occasional virgin volcano sacrifice only goes so far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864396#post864396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not. Any such powers would more likely make other things larger instead. That said, thinks like making a house grow to enormous sizes so Godzilla can hunt ant-sized humans hiding among the carpet forest seems way more suited to Changeling or Beast than Leviathan.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vague idea I had was someone &quot;walking&quot; around, seeming to be in their human form, but trashing everything around them because their &quot;true&quot; form was either covered by an illusion, or lurking in Twilight.<br /> <br /> What about a Swarm form (via Channel or Adaptation), with one of the swarm split off (but the rest lurking nearby, I'd think, for coherency's sake)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:47:23-07:00","id":864448,"title":"","content":"Forgive me if you haven't given this any thought, but what might a Neolithic Leviathan setting be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:00:58-07:00","id":864467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864448#post864448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if you haven't given this any thought, but what might a Neolithic Leviathan setting be like?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Scary, that's what it would be like. I can't see Marduk having a great deal of power back then (although they wouldn't be entirely absent and they'd probably have more of a handle on that thunder-magic). Leviathans could relatively easily set up an indoctrinated kingdom over which they could rule as a god. On the other hand, this is when the New Gods would start turning up, so their servants would have the element of surprise when they do strike. This would also (although I'm not sure about this) be the time in which Boghavti was around and we know what happened with that place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T15:12:46-07:00","id":864561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864430#post864430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking more a Leviathan that took &quot;Primordial Ocean&quot; to mean the seas of molten rock the Earth was formed from before it cooled. Likely School of the Abyss - not too many neighbors in the mantle, and &quot;swimming&quot; up for the occasional virgin volcano sacrifice only goes so far.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, that could be an Evolution. Don't forget to think about why a Abyss School Leviathan would consider this to be the &quot;answer&quot; they've been looking for through the School of the Abyss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864430#post864430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vague idea I had was someone &quot;walking&quot; around, seeming to be in their human form, but trashing everything around them because their &quot;true&quot; form was either covered by an illusion, or lurking in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div> That definately feels more Beast or Changeling than Leviathan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864430#post864430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a Swarm form (via Channel or Adaptation), with one of the swarm split off (but the rest lurking nearby, I'd think, for coherency's sake)?</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Leviathan could do it by stretching out a tentacle then a Swarm Leviathan can do it by splitting of part of themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=864448#post864448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if you haven't given this any thought, but what might a Neolithic Leviathan setting be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I still haven't read the Neolithic setting, but I imagine that Leviathans would be terribly powerful, and probably more Tranquil. The idea of killing or enslaving people (probably) isn't considered abhorent like it is today, and mortals might genuinely believe that going mad through the Wake is a blessing due to different ideas of divinity and madness. All this means that it's easier for a Leviathan to accept what they are.<br /> <br /> The Marduk society would probably resemble the myths of heroes who steal fire from the gods. They still bring progress but they've got no qualms about stealing weapons from the god and giving it to their tribe so they can go out and kill all the other tribes and take their stuff. They have morals, but it's just following their gut for good or ill.<br /> <br /> Also, they're probably not even a society yet. They might still be Marduk's origonal disciples (It's probably easiest to treat them mechanically as Empyerian Thurgists with Virtues that speak of personal ability rather than civilisation; and a bunch of extremely powerful Hunter Endowments that let them fight Leviathans one on one) plus a bunch of completely unEndowed followers (unless a disciple directly casts a buff on them)<br /> <br /> <br /> As always I'm just using my standard metric of how &quot;reasoned&quot; a creature is man in this setting. I'm assuming that it's not very because it's the Neolithic, so Leviathans would be strong and the society would be weak. However since this is the past and not the future, the Society has to exist so that it's future can exist. I mean, sure the Tribe could be completely wrong and the society started in ancient Babylon. But where's the fun in that?<br /> <br /> [edit] On second thought, it's way to early for the society to be sharing anything. So just think of this as the society reimagined for a Neolithic game and not what the present day society were actually like at that point in history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-12-2016, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T11:41:01-07:00","id":865626,"title":"","content":"Another Element Channel - this one is Water, and it's secondary theme is sailor superstitions. Still to go for Descendent elements is earth(quakes) and air so I'll need secondary themes for them.<br /> <br /> The forum sent the formatting a bit off, if it bothers you it's also in the Channels scrapbook.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Echoes of the Deluge (Descendant Channel)</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Progenitors were not mere sea life, they were the Primordial Waters and the Primordial Waters were the Progenitors.</i></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: Intelligence + Science + Sheol</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action Type: Instant</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&lt;TODO&gt; Some nice flavour text goes here.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sidebar: Enslave the Gods</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whenever the Channels Echos of the Deluge, Swallowing the Sun, &lt;TODO, complete list&gt; have an effect with a variable number of Successes a Leviathan must struggle to hold back. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As a Reflexive Action a Leviathan may spend a point of Willpower and roll Eunoia. For the remainder of the scene they may reduce their Successes for the aforementioned Channels by up to their successes on the Eunoia roll; if they are unsatisfied with the result they may spend additional Willpower score automatic successes on the Eunoia roll at a 1:1 ratio. Buying extra successes is an exception to the usual restrictions on spending multiple willpower in a turn.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition any power that creates or enhances Environmental Tilts can be used in reverse to reduce or remove the Tilt. To do this the Leviathan must make the Eunoia roll as above and the Leviathan\u2019s Successes when expressing the Channel are capped at the Successes of the Eunoia roll. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 1: Birthright of Elements</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 2: The Leviathan may spend 1 Ichor to inflict the Flooded Tilt in an area with a diameter of Sheol*10 feet. Water rises out of the ground, even if this is obviously impossible. If the Leviathan is in a contained area such as a room or quarry smaller than the Channel\u2019s maximum radius then the waters will be contained and rise to one foot per success with multiple expressing of the Channel stacking. If the Leviathan is out in the open the floodwaters may rise up to Sheol feet, any additional water washes away like water. Water created remains permanently, but it reverts to natural behaviour at the end of the scene. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively the Leviathan may spend 1 Ichor to ruin any technology with a Size lower than Intelligence + Science + Sheol that contains water, such as a car with a water cooled engine. Roll to express the Channel, on a Success any water immediately escapes its confines doing one point of Damage per Success, bypassing durability. Even a single success removes all the water, and will require it to at least be refilled.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 3: The Leviathan gains an alternative use for the Depth 2 iteration of this Channel. They may animate water and set it upon a foe. The animated water has a Strength equal to the Leviathan\u2019s Successes and a Brawl equal to the Leviathan. It is simple minded and will always try to hold its target underwater until they drown, if they break free the effect ends. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 4: The Leviathan may spend 2 Ichor and roll to create or enhance the Heavy Waves Condition. Each Success is worth a point of severity. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively the Leviathan may target a Wake vulnerable individual and express the Channel contested by Resolve + Supernatural Advantage. If the Leviathan wins the roll the target\u2019s lungs fill with water. Unless the target can survive with water filled lungs they may do nothing but make an Extended Stamina roll with a target number equal to the Leviathan\u2019s successes to spit it all out or use a supernatural power to resolve the problem. If they fail the roll they will require medical intervention. Leviathans can survive with water filled lungs at Depth 3, and treat their Stamina at two dots higher at Depth 2. They may Transform instead of trying to clear their lungs.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 5: The Leviathan\u2019s immunity to Environmental Tilts created through this Channel extends to their Beloved.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 6: The Leviathan is the lord of the sea, and a capricious ruler. Sailors know this truth in the creaking of the decks. Anyone who might be described as a sailor takes the Spooked Condition the first time in a day that they fail a roll related to sailing while within an Environmental Tilt created by this Channe. This usually results in typical maritime superstitions. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 7: The Leviathan may spend four Ichor when using the Depth 2 or 4 iterations of this Channel to affect Tilts. If they do so, and score at least one Success, the Leviathan increases their Successes to five. Alternatively the Leviathan my express this Channel to create or enhance the Perfect Storm Tilt. However if the Leviathan is attempting to create the Tilt the roll is automatically penalised by 5 - severity of the Heavy Waves Tilt. Be warned that a Perfect Storm is large enough to attract unwanted attention, don\u2019t summon them near anywhere you plan on staying long. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Adaptations</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother of all Storms (O): In Depth 7 any natural occurrence of the Heavy Waves or Perfect Storm Tilt within the Leviathan's Wake automatically increases its severity by one to a maximum of 5. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tribute to Tiamat (OOO): In Depth 7 all Wake vulnerable sailors immediately take the Shaken Condition if they enter the Leviathan\u2019s Wake while at sea or set sail within the Leviathan\u2019s Wake. They may resolve the Condition the usual way, or by making a sacrifice that triggers an Integrity breaking point such as slashing your own wrist and offering blood. Gold or wine are offerings for younger gods. If the captain gathers at least half the crew and makes an offering then the entire crew\u2019s Conditions are resolved, otherwise all must make their own offerings. Affected characters instinctively know what is expected of them, and once appropriate sacrifices are made they are immune to this Adaptation for the remainder of the day. </span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To celebrate the progress on Elements here's a Nu. Note it's sunious form, and the way it's tail blends into the elements.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/564x/48/b6/1d/48b61d97ec227c655ff08ad5711f64f1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://foru