really powerful, what with the whole 'salt the fields' thing. Also, I've seen that picture before on Pintrest, so I think that might be it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T13:59:07-07:00","id":865689,"title":"","content":"I was reading up on Primordial Theurgists, and thought: they prize Ophions for the (relatively) easy power. And so, might a PT engage in psy-ops against your Leviathans to try and push them into Ophion-dom? That way, they <i>know</i> an Ophion already (for &quot;use&quot; or trade, as needed).<br /> <br /> Primordial Theurgists: It's not enough that they are trying to steal your powers, some try to drive you crazy for their own gain, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T14:24:53-07:00","id":865699,"title":"","content":"That's a high risk strategy Vent0, but they might.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=865673#post865673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're running a Dark Ages game, this Channel would be really really powerful, what with the whole 'salt the fields' thing. Also, I've seen that picture before on Pintrest, so I think that might be it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it depends on the availability of magical fixes. Perhaps there is a Benediction to unsalt fields?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T14:28:13-07:00","id":865701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=865699#post865699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose it depends on the availability of magical fixes. Perhaps there is a Benediction to unsalt fields?</div> </div> </div> </div>If not, the Leviathan has an excellent way to cripple his enemies' food supply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T15:46:35-07:00","id":865726,"title":"","content":"While I was driven away by the Marduk Society Argument, I've read through the documents and feel it's safe to come back.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, Primordial Theurgists use Cult Ritual rules, once we draft them, yes? For Empyrean Theurgists, they probably need their own Rituals specific to them, since I don't feel The Old Gods' Remembered Rites really fit the invocation of the bringers of wisdom and civilization. A core idea should probably be the idea that Empyrean Theurgists cannot work against their Gods; the lords of order know exactly who's drawing on them, and if they get pissed off, the spigot can be turned off. Also, if it at all fits the overall idea, we should probably stat up a selection of different Empyrean Theurgists; one's a benign rival (they don't like Leviathans but are well-intentioned and act in the benefit of humans-maybe an outside contractor for Marduk), one's a somewhat shadier individual open to negotiating with Leviathans (perhaps a fertility priest, in a less homicidal version of &quot;human blood waters the grain best&quot; sense), and the third's just a selfish git in a shiny vestment, an example of how Virtue can be twisted into something dark and malign (a Domain of Justice has a long history of being twisted to support the actions of moralistic psychopaths, but I'd like it if they had something seemingly completely benign like Hearth, or the Farm, or perhaps Hope-for themself and nobody else. Tzeentch represent, brudda).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I realized-there are, by nature, an assload more Virtuous Domains than there are Channels. This isn't really a problem on the default player character side of things, as it's less bookkeeping, but for the ST, we need a sidebar on guidelines for understanding what Domains can and cannot do when homebrewed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-14-2016, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T02:41:22-07:00","id":865858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=865726#post865726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I was driven away by the Marduk Society Argument, I've read through the documents and feel it's safe to come back.</div> </div> </div> </div> Welcome back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=865726#post865726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly, Primordial Theurgists use Cult Ritual rules, once we draft them, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=865726#post865726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Empyrean Theurgists, they probably need their own Rituals specific to them</div> </div> </div> </div> Obviously they do. Hence why they have Domains.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=865726#post865726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A core idea should probably be the idea that Empyrean Theurgists cannot work against their Gods; the lords of order know exactly who's drawing on them, and if they get pissed off, the spigot can be turned off.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm going to leave as dependent on the individual god &amp; storyteller's interpretation. Plenty of the free will related justifications for theodicy would imply a Christian Thurgist could go against god.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=865726#post865726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, if it at all fits the overall idea, we should probably stat up a selection of different Empyrean Theurgists</div> </div> </div> </div>For sample antagonists I'd want to focus not so much on how they interact with a Leviathan but how they contrast with the Tribe thematically. For example I'd quite like to have a human sacrificing Aztec thurgist to contrast the Aztec's theological justifications with the Tribe's instinctive justifications. Lawful Evil vs Chaotic Evil in D&amp;D parlance. I'd also quite like to do something that shows how religions evolve to contrast the theme of stagnation. Maybe a very young Christian denomination, liberal Jewish, or Wiccian Thurgist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=865726#post865726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we need a sidebar on guidelines for understanding what Domains can and cannot do when homebrewed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. That's in the &quot;waiting for mage&quot; pile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-15-2016, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T10:52:22-07:00","id":866012,"title":"","content":"Good points. Honestly, that thematic difference is kinda what I was going for, though I was honestly more concerned with a good sample selection than anything.<br /> <br /> One thing that occured to me was that the most heroic of the Empyrean Theurgists should come off as someone who evolved past a more savage existence and into one that is based around, essentially, compassionate Cult-busting, freeing Beloved from the Wake as his primary motive, converting them to his faith a close second. Because I like to push the edge of what culture considers the Other to show the Us, I was thinking something like an ex-<i>mujahideen </i>who actually did fight against American invaders of his home (indirectly; he's not a combatant by nature, just running logistics), but as his old comrades began to embrace the, shall we say, not-precisely-humanitarian ways of ideals like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wahhabism\" target=\"_blank\">Wahhabism</a>, he eventually decided that his side was becoming just as monstrous as the imperialists-which was cemented when he realized his cell was now Beloved by a self-proclaimed righteous <i>jinn</i><i>. </i>He developed Empyrean Theurgy to drive off the Leviathan, at which point Marduk approached him about freeing the world from other watery <i>jinn </i>and spreading the revelation that lead to his Domains across the world. Thematically, he's the Theurgist as Noble Reformer, driven by a vision to lead his chosen people to a new age of enlightenment, rather than force them back to the past.<br /> <br /> (And before you ask: Said Leviathan was not, from his perspective, lying-if he's still alive, he's an excellent example of how bad the School of Thunder can get in the right environment).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T11:59:54-07:00","id":866035,"title":"","content":"The Islamic State would make a great setting for Leviathan, that sort of crisis is a magnet for Leviathans hoping to carve out a petty kingdom from the chaos or lay low in a place where people have even bigger trouble than a Leviathan occasionally letting off some steam. And the Leviathan vs Marduk/Emyperian Thurgist conflict might look like Them and Us but they're really metaphors for an internal conflict between the savage and civilised parts of human nature - a conflict that's relevant to the Islamic State.<br /> <br /> But actually writing it would be a ton of research. Just for starters you couldn't write a charachter like that without understanding quite a bit about what exactly a dissadent ex mujahideen can and can't do in the Islamic State without being executed. So sadly I probably won't actually do it.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. Leviathan draws on Middle Eastern mythology. Native middle easterners won't be confusing the Tribe with beings of smokeless fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T13:19:46-07:00","id":866074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=866035#post866035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P.S. Leviathan draws on Middle Eastern mythology. Native middle easterners won't be confusing the Tribe with beings of smokeless fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that can be rectified with an (un-)healthy dose of Wake-induced Mind-F@#!ery.<br /> <br /> I doubt a Beloved is going to tell their (Emissary of) God &quot;No, you don't fit the picture&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T13:41:43-07:00","id":866091,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=The Kings Raven;n866035]<br /> <br /> But actually writing it would be a ton of research. Just for starters you couldn't write a charachter like that without understanding quite a bit about what exactly a dissadent ex mujahideen can and can't do in the Islamic State without being executed. So sadly I probably won't actually do it./QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Is true. I didn't actually have him as still being over there in my vision, more of a guardian to more Western Islamic communities, for that precise reason...but he doesn't really fit in with the West either (even though it's likely Marduk quietly erased his past, he was still a combination of bombarded with propaganda to make him hate the West and being exposed to West-created reasons to hate the West, so he's going to feel more than a tad out of place trying to live in the West, even if he has decided the West's leaders and its civilians are two different things).Truth is, I also thought of him as someone who got out before ISIS actually became infamous, also for that precise reason.<br /> <br /> Probably is for the best we just mine that idea for inspiration with less potentially offensive ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T11:05:33-07:00","id":872519,"title":"","content":"Lets get a little motion in here again.<br /> <br /> Today's update is another Channel. Piercing the Veil of Slumber. This one was hard to write, most of the mental influence possibilities are already covered by Call of the Depth and Besieging the Tower of Will. Especially with Call of the Depth's ability to inflict Conditions.<br /> <br /> I ended up taking it in a different direction. Astral entities. It favours dreams, but it could work quite nicely on a Temenos entity provided it was already on Earth. It's in a bit of an awkward spot in that as written it's mostly useful if you combine it with Changeling for rules for Dreams and dream entities along with Mage for astral entities. Maybe I'll introduce something to the Leviathan corebook, but as a fan-game I think I can get away with a little more dependence on other books than normal.<br /> <br /> The fate manipulation stuff will go into it's own Channel.<br /> <br /> <br /> So without further adu <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Piercing the Veil of Slumber (Descendant Channel)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Tribe transcend the limits of the flesh. They walk the hidden corridors of the mind, inspiring, maddening, as they please.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The innately psychic minds of the Tribe blur the distinction between thought and flesh. Through their divine will dreams may walk the Earth, and mortals may find themselves lost between reality and dreams.</span></span><ul><li><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: Presence + Occult + Sheol</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action Type: Instant</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 0&quot;: Birthright of Sanctity</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 1&quot;: The Leviathan may observe the dreams of others while they sleep. Spend a point of Ichor and for the remainder of the scene the Leviathan may see into the dreams of any sleeping character they can perceive.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 2&quot;: As above, and the Leviathan may manipulate the target\u2019s Dream using this Channel\u2019s Dicepool as though they had Influence 4 (Dreams), Leviathans pay no cost to manipulate a Dream beyond the point needed to open their eyes to dreams. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 3&quot;: The Leviathan gains an additional ability. They may open the gates creatures of dreams and astral planes into the material. Spend two Ichor and roll to express this Channel. A Success places the Open Condition on something or someone for an Astral entity or class of Astral entities of the Leviathan\u2019s choosing. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 4&quot;: The Leviathan may target an astral entity and roll this Channel - Rank to grant it the Materialize Condition for a scene if it did not possess it already. If the Leviathan is looking into a dream and targets an entity within, it also gains the ability to walk between it\u2019s host\u2019s dreams and the material world. Inanimate objects can be affected, and simply appear next to an Open target of the Leviathan\u2019s choosing.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan also gains the ability to grant anyone they wish the ability to see astral entities in Twilight by expressing this Channel vs Resolve + Supernatural Advantage. However unless they\u2019re another Leviathan they take the Madness Condition as they lose the ability to distinguish between dream and reality. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 5&quot;: The Leviathan may spend two Ichor to control any astral entity. Roll this Channel vs Resistance - Rank. If the Leviathan wins the entity falls under it\u2019s control for the remainder of the scene. Otherwise the entity is immune for the remainder of the scene. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 6&quot;: The Leviathan may throw open the doors between flesh and dream. Everything and every Wake Vulnerable person within the Leviathan\u2019s Wake gains the Open condition for all Astral entities and counts as being made of dreamstuff for the purposes of being targeted by Strengthen, Manipulate and Control Influences. If a non-Beloved mortal falls asleep within the perimeter of the Wake then every Astral entity within their minds, be it Goetica or an Incubi gains both the ability to travel between their host and the material world and the Materialize Manifestation.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Adaptations</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Visionary Dreams (OO): In Depth 3 the Leviathan takes no penalty to perceiving world around her while she sleeps. If she has Eye of the Watchful Deity she may use that channel as she dreams. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Recurring Nightmares (OOO): In Depth 4 the Leviathan can spend two Ichor to implant a fragment of themselves with a sleeping person. This fragment remains within the victim's dreams and will use its Influence every night without fail until it completes the task the Leviathan sets for it. This usually creates a madman or a Beloved, albet a Beloved who fulfils their need to interact with the Leviathan in their dreams (it makes a good way to appoint high priests who\u2019ll oppose attempts to summon you). People containing a fragment of a Leviathan have an unusually high chance of developing psychic abilities, usually ones with severe drawbacks. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prophet of Mad Slumber (OOO, Requires Eye of the Watchful Deity): In Depth 3 the Leviathan may spend 2 Ichor and nominate any character, then roll Presence + Occult + Sheol penalised by Knowledge. On a success they may see into or manipulate the target\u2019s Dreams. Physical distance has no meaning in dreams and if the Leviathan is capable of Besieging the Tower of Will he may use that Channel on the target regardless of range. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dreams of a Future that Will Be (OOOOO, Requires Sheol 6, Besieging the Tower of Will) - In Depth 6 the Leviathan may spend four Ichor to create a contagious dream. Define the purpose of this dream, phrased as though it were an Ambition then roll for this Channel as normal. If successful for the next 24 hours everyone Wake vulnerable person who is not Beloved, sleeps within the Leviathans Wake, and has a Dream with a similar subject matter to the contagion must roll Resolve + Composure - the Leviathan\u2019s successes. If they fail they gain a new Ambition of the Leviathans desire, along with an ability to identify who else is affected. However their minds buckle under the long term effects. Mechanically and psychologically they can be treated as the Leviathan\u2019s Beloved and unify as a Cult, however they have no direct obsession with the Leviathan and \u201cworship\u201d their new cause instead. The Leviathan can leave them alone, and while they will get into all sorts of trouble they probably won\u2019t leave the Leviathan\u2019s name and image around for investigators to find. Probably. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=866091#post866091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably is for the best we just mine that idea for inspiration with less potentially offensive ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not worried about it being offensive, we already have the Ascending Ones with cannoical terrorist links. It's just that why create a mujahideen then take him away from the context of the Middle East? He'd be far more interesting in the Middle East but that means research.<br /> <br /> If I get round to writing sample Thurgists; I'll probably focus on the neo-Aztec with the Lawful-Evil / Chaotic Evil contrast to Leviathans. Possibly the monarch of some hidden kingdom in the Amazon - one of the places where Leviathans can go all out without breaking the Masqurade. The second would probably a chaplin who works at a mental hospital so that he might enocounter Leviathan derived madness. He won't be a fighter himself, but good at playing the system if he needs too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=866074#post866074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that can be rectified with an (un-)healthy dose of Wake-induced Mind-F@#!ery.<br /> <br /> I doubt a Beloved is going to tell their (Emissary of) God &quot;No, you don't fit the picture&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why would a Leviathan want to portray itself as a being of fire? They quite like the whole water thing they've got going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T20:19:53-07:00","id":872838,"title":"","content":"I just remembered something I meant to bring up here. I am still trying to work on that crossover comments/opinions/notes thing, but time and mental stability are hard for me to find at the moment.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as we all know, Lovecraft's work makes a big thing about &quot;When the Stars are Right&quot;. But if you look at a lot of his works, they actually describe a cycle; the stars rise, then they fall, then they rise again, only to implictly fall there-after. Beyond the great apocalypses, like how the Elder Things once dominated Earth but eventually fell by the wayside and were replaced by man, the very nature of the seals of the Great Old Ones is described in a cyclical fashion; Cthulhu and R'lyeh once reigned, but then the stars fell out of alignment and they were sealed away. When the stars return to their alignment, they will be free again - but who says that they'll stay that way?<br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is this: is it breaking the theme of the setting to apply a similar motif? The Tribe is currently in its nadir, its stars are no longer in alignment. But, perhaps the stars will rise again, restoring the Tribe to prominence and power... but only for a time; eventually, inevitably, the stars will set and the Tribe's fortunes will falter once more. And so it will go, forever and ever.<br /> <br /> This, to me, seems to be taking the description of the game's mood as described in the GDoc and writing it large; that implicit cycle of attempt, success and failure writ into the cosmos.<br /> <br /> But... I don't know. I like this idea, since it feels like it further reinforces both the horror (the Black Dawn was doomed to end, as will the next, and the next) and the hope (eventually, the Black Dawn will come again, and maybe this time we'll get it right) that this game is tied into. But I'm worried I'm misreading it, and ultimately doing it a disservice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T00:29:18-07:00","id":872945,"title":"","content":"Unlike Lovecraft's creations, Leviathans are metaphors for fundamental human lizard brain instincts. That's important to this question. If you say that Leviathan's setting is cyclical you're metaphorically saying that real world history is a cycle of civilisation/reason rises -&gt; falls -&gt; rises -&gt; falls.<br /> <br /> Now that might be true, it's too early to tell. We know looking at history that, to a certain extent, reason can and has triumphed over those lizard brain instincts. War is down, tolerance is up, yay us, lets hope for even more of that tomorrow. But will those lizard brain instincts eventually triumph, destroying civilisation? Followed by another rise, another fall, repeating itself until the sun burns out. I don't think so, but we can't know for sure because it hasn't happened yet, we're still in the first &quot;rises&quot;.<br /> <br /> So if you think that history will be a cycle of civilisation rising and falling. Or you don't think that but you want to say it's true for the sake of telling a good story then by all means make the Leviathan setting into a great cycle<br /> <br /> <br /> Now what <i>would</i> conflict with the theme and mood of Leviathan: the Tempest is if the Tribe knew there was a great cycle. If Leviathans knew that the Tribe's star would inevitably ascend again they'd swim around looking for a nice secluded spot to go into hibernation until the stars were right; rather than struggling to adapt to the modern world but only achieving stagnation. Cthulhu just slept through the cycles where the Stars Were Wrong but unless you <i>really</i> want to roleplay being asleep for years the Tribe can't copy him.<br /> <br /> An individual Leviathan might try the hibernation plan but the closest the Tribe should get is believing that the great cycle garentees they'll once again triumph but they'll have to actually do the work first. So they can't just wait for the stars tor reach the right spots in the sky. Of course, the Tribe is absolutely full of promised messiahs and prophecies destined to save the Tribe; most of them are lies and the Tribe know most of them are lies. One might be true, but how would you tell which one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-24-2016, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T03:31:15-07:00","id":872994,"title":"","content":"The cycle thing could still work for Leviathans, just not the Lovecraftian version. After all you could say that the Leviathans are just trying to begin a new cycle and as long as those cycles aren't tied to specific points in time or space itshould mesh well with the themes of the game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T03:31:20-07:00","id":872995,"title":"","content":"Alright, I promised I'd do some thoughts on crossing over with Leviathan, and I finally managed to get my thoughts clear enough to do something. As was mentioned...somewhere around here, maybe on the blog, crossovers do often result in a weakening of the &quot;core theme&quot;, or the need to adapt a new one. For these crossovers, I chose to go with the idea of &quot;support it&quot; rather than trying to force it to not happen. So, yeah, this'll be done with an eye towards the positive, as much as I can explain it.<br /> <br /> Firstly, though, I want to advocate that, if it doesn't already, being a Beloved should grant immunity to &quot;passive&quot; mind-rape effects like Lunacy or Sybaris, and significant resistance to active mind-fraggery like the Mind Arcana, Dominate, etc. This reinforces the sheer Insane Faith (with equal emphasis on both &quot;insanity&quot; and &quot;faith&quot;) that being a Beloved induces. Your mind has been broken and remade by the presence of God Most Unholy Herself; lesser auras of mental manipulation pale in comparison to that.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's embarrassing to think your drooling near-zombie cultists could turn against you just because some rookie magician waved her hands and chanted some mumbo-jumbo.<br /> <br /> Secondly, if we do end up doing a &quot;crossing over guidebook&quot; expansion, there should be some thought put into a School that devotes itself to studying the other monsters with which leviathans share the world of darkness, trying to figure out how and why <i>these</i> horrors have managed to successfully grow and change to integrate themselves into the modern era, and how the Tribe might potentially do the same. I mean, Promethean had the Argentum (? Path of Silver) in Magnum Opus for a reason, in that studying other monsters gives prometheans more of a grasp on what humanity is by virtue of what it isn't, and if Leviathan's Schools have similar nature to the Refinements - which is, honestly, how they come across to me - then it makes sense that they'd also consider their fellow denizens of the darkness to be worthy of studying for lessons in what (not) to do to restore the Tribe.<br /> <br /> Anyway, on to the splats... I'm making the assumption that the Wake doesn't affect other supernaturals, simply because such effects are generally &quot;mortals only&quot; - Disquiet is the only exception, was a case of &quot;specific trumps general&quot;, and was generally received poorly to the point we've been told that's getting reworked in 2e. Besides, I don't recall seeing rules for the Wake mind-whammying vampires and the like in the gdocs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Vampire:</b><br /> Lets get the obvious out of the way first; leviathans can potentially scare the hell out of vampires. Between the fanaticism of their cult, the ease with which the Wake insinuates itself into the collective consciousness, and the sheer chaos they can cause even by accident, leviathans are tough enemies and major-league boat rockers. However... vampires are also nothing if not opportunistic, and the two races do have quite a lot of use for each other.<br /> <br /> Vampires are adept at playing the social game, deftly negotiating the landscape that so alienates and confounds leviathans. Furthermore, as supernatural beings, vampires are shielded from the mind-melting auras of the Tribe - never understimate just how powerful that sort of clarity can be, or how welcome it can be; many a leviathan tires of nothing but mindless sycophants, and could be played on out of this desire for someone to simply <i>talk to</i> even by someone less adept at head-games than a vampire.<br /> <br /> And what do leviathans have to offer vampires? Just for starters, the obvious one-two punch is that A: a leviathan's cult is an effortless supply of meals for a hungry vampire to score in trade, and B: if properly motivated, a leviathan makes one hell of a secret weapon for a vampire looking to get ahead in the world. More specifically, the Circle of the Crone and the Ordo Dracul both have reasons to investigate and find common ground with vampires. The Circle from their interest in blood magic and belief in older gods, the Ordo from the fascinating theo-biological possibilities encoded in the Leviathan's nature.<br /> <br /> Leviathans, meanwhile, can find useful allies, or just someone to talk to, in vampires. It's a dysfunctional relationship, but honestly, the Tribe has to take what it can get. There's a strange respectability in a life that refuses to quit even when all of the laws of nature say it should.<br /> <br /> I recall it was mentioned that Ichor can have strange effects on vampires. I'm all for it, but I argue that it should be a double-edged sword; yes, the side-effects can be nasty, but there's equally worthy reasons to drink it. Play up the temptation, and you further strengthen the Tribe as avatars of sin in all its darkly enticing glory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf:</b> <br /> Past all of the initial, instinctive posturing and threat displays, if given the chance to meet each other on relatively equal terms, the Tribe and the Pack can find a strange feeling of kinship with each other. Both are races whom the mortal world has left by, remnants of the bloody age of tooth and claw before civilization. Both are species who are neither flesh nor ephemera but some otherworldly hybrid between the two. Both claim descent from mighty god-monsters who once subjugated humanity, and to have ruled a primordial paradise that was lost and replaced with this all too dissatisfying world.<br /> <br /> It's a relationship fraught with conflict, aggression and arguments... but, at the core of it all, there's an understanding between the two races. Cousins in spirit, if not in flesh.<br /> <br /> A leviathan's cult can easily become shelter and support for a werewolf pack. The Tribe have little complaint about offering their Beloved as breeding stock for werewolves who have proven themselves as allies; more of these strange, land-running, furry kindred can only be a good thing. A leviathan itself can become a monster that can help terrorize and devour those creatures that oppose the pack.<br /> <br /> Even if they do not directly ally with each other, werewolves and leviathans give each other a respectful berth. It's much like the relationship between a pack of wolves and an alpha tiger. Each subtly respects the other's potential as a killer and tries to not provoke a fight that would be bloody, potentially life-threatening, and ultimately useless.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's not all wine and roses. By their very nature, leviathans are spiritual vortices, generating spirits appropriate to their nature and cult - sin spirits, blood spirits, life spirits, death spirits, murder spirits, zealotry spirits, loyalty spirits... great choruses of the more primal and often dangerous spirits tend to flock to the leviathan, suckling from its Wake and its Beloved and feeding on the bounty of Essence. Indeed, as crazy as leviathan cults can get, who's honestly going to notice one or more Spirit-Ridden hanging around?<br /> <br /> That said, whilst an obvious source of problems, it can also be a source of help, if a pack thinks outside of the box. If human meddling is causing problems with the pack's efforts to manage particularly problematic spirits, well, isn't using the Wake to force people stop acting in a different way ultimately better than just murdering hundreds of people? Properly aimed, a leviathan can be used as the mother of all hammers to tend to the spiritual landscape of an area. Blunt as hell, sure. Effective? Unquestionably so.<br /> <br /> Naturally, the easiest &quot;alliances&quot; tend to be between the Pure - especially Predator Kings, who see leviathans as a way to force the restoration of Pangaea - or, more dangerously, Bale Hounds. But, with the right mindset, even the Forsaken can make peace with the Tribe, if not become friends.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you need to add a little more grimdark back in, there's always the jealousy angle; though both species hail from similarly savage origins, werewolves have (arguably) adapted better to the new world than the Tribe has.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mage:</b> <br /> It could be said that interactions between the Awakened and the Tribe if the wizards could just remember the old adage: please do not harass the antediluvian abomination!<br /> <br /> Make no mistake, the Tribe absolutely fascinates many mages. The thing is, mages already make leviathans leery just by virtue of the stories of Marduk; any idealist wizard even looks like he's getting ideas of trying a bit of monster hunting is going to have one very angry monster try a bit of preemptive striking. Of all the groups, they have perhaps the hardest time getting past that initial hostile impression.<br /> <br /> But if they do, well, it's a rather dysfunctional relationship, but both sides have a lot to offer each other, just like leviathans and vampires. There's so very much for mages to obsess over and study when it comes to leviathans, and leviathans... well, mostly what they get out of it is some decent human conversation. The big thing one has to remember is just how <i>hard</i> it is for a leviathan to talk to someone, person to person. A completely normal person who can see past the scales and tentacles and just talk to them? That's an element of normality that many leviathans are happy to trade drops of blood or demonstrations of their power for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Promethean:</b> <br /> Of all the splats, I see these two having the most in common, and tending towards the least-hostile first impressions. Both races are aberrations, things that should not be. Both bear the strain of an unearthly power within that stains the world around them, destroying men's minds and shattering the landscape. Prometheans seek the New Dawn, the transformation from monster to human. Leviathans hope for the Black Dawn, the fall of Man so that Monster may resume its place as the ruler of all things.<br /> <br /> If the Wake stifles Disquiet, at least amongst the Beloved, then I can see a leviathan's cult becoming the closest thing to a home that a promethean may ever know. There's so much potential for a promethean to learn there, about what is - and isn't - human, all while resisting the well-meaning blandishments of the leviathan that, however unwittingly, coaxes the promethean to embrace the path of the Centimanus.<br /> <br /> To say nothing of the scenario of the Marduk Society being confronted by a weeping flesh golem screaming in heartbreak about how they destroyed her entire family for being &quot;different&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Changeling:</b> <br /> At first glance, the Lost and the Tribe seem to go together like oil and water, but look beyond the surface. Sometimes, the best place to hide is in plain sight; when you're surrounded by crazies, who's going to notice you? Plus, that's a lot of hot-running emotions to feed on for glamour.<br /> <br /> Really, this depends a lot on what 2e is going to do with Clarity (which, honestly, I always thought was one of the worst karma meters of 1e) - if changelings are still one stiff breeze away from total madness, then they're never going to mix with the Tribe, and that's a fact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sin-Eater:</b><br /> Generally speaking, these two races won't interact with each other much. Sin-Eaters mostly concern themselves with the dead, and leviathans with the living. Unless leviathans develop powers that let them interfere with the dead, they're not of much concern to each other. Maybe it's kind of like sin-eaters and vampires, where the biggest reason that the Tribe tend to cross sin-eater radars is their tendency to leave a lot of mad ghosts in their wake. That said, the two &quot;cross-pollinating&quot; each other's respective mythologies could be interesting - imagine sin-eaters who were originally Beloved and so still fixate upon their former master to form the centerpiece of their homebrewed religion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mummy:</b> <br /> The fact that the Arisen and the Tribe hail back to similarly ancient times and have a mutually cynical/disapproving attitude towards society's changes provides some common ground. Storyhooks, like what happens when Beloved mistake a Mummy's Relic for an artefact of their master, or when the cult of one kind becomes intermeshed with/subsumed by the cult of another, are obvious. The big thing here is establishing &quot;who's older&quot;; did the Tribe arise sometime after the fall of Irem? Were their waning years before the City of Pillars arose? Or were they equals, and Mummies with sharper memories can dimly recall leviathan war-priests leading armies of gibborim and lahmasu against Iremite slave-legions?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Demon:</b><br /> I made a post on this matter back when Marduk was under fire as too powerful &amp; white-hatted for the setting, but I'll just summarize; though Integrators would be an exception, a match between a Demon and Leviathan is a match made in heaven-hell just waiting to happen. Each has something the other wants, and can offer highly inviting reasons to form an alliance. A demon/leviathan crossover would definitely be one to play up the &quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b><br /> I... honestly, I haven't been able to really sit down and get into Beast at all. I'll have to beg off commenting here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hunter:</b> <br /> This splat's never really interested me that much, mostly because it's kind of set to antagonistic by default against supernaturals, especially the more overt races. I don't really have any ideas here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T06:23:20-07:00","id":873046,"title":"","content":"Lots to reply too here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=872995#post872995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstly, though, I want to advocate that, if it doesn't already, being a Beloved should grant immunity to &quot;passive&quot; mind-rape effects like Lunacy or Sybaris and significant resistance to active mind-fraggery like the Mind Arcana, Dominate, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div> A Fanatacism Merit that protects against mind control makes sense; but I'm ok with other supernaturals being able to influence Beloved.<br /> <br /> Taking over an entire Cult is never easy, the Spell Factors required for a Mastigos to stop an entire cult are crazy. But capturing one Beloved and implanting them with orders is the kind of interesting threat that Leviathans should face. Even if only to track down the culprit and overriding the influence by using Besiging the Tower of Will.<br /> <br /> Sybaris though. Beloved aren't going to be stolen by passive auras, that includes other Leviathans. If you want to poach Beloved you need to capture them and work to break their programming.<br /> <br /> (That said, Call of the Depths is one of the few mass mind control powers out there. Perhaps it should be a little harder to use that one on Beloved)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=872995#post872995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there should be some thought put into a School that devotes itself to studying the other monsters with which leviathans share the world of darkness</div> </div> </div> </div> That was the origonal idea for the School of the Moon. It was changed because it only worked in crossover.<br /> <br /> The biggest barrier to creating a new School based on studying other splat is the rule of 7 (Thunder don't count. The Tribe runs in 7, and Leviathans have decided to kick School of Thunder Leviathans out the Tribe). If you ignore the rule of 7, it's a perfectly reasonable focus for a school <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=872995#post872995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, on to the splats... I'm making the assumption that the Wake doesn't affect other supernaturals</div> </div> </div> </div> You can't turn other supernaturals Beloved but if their Power Trait is 2 less than yours you can still use it for psychic intimidation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=872995#post872995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall seeing rules for the Wake mind-whammying vampires and the like in the gdocs.</div> </div> </div> </div> I still need to write the 2E version of those rules. They'll let you use the Wake to inflict certain Conditions on people, possibly it will just be Leveraged.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=872995#post872995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall it was mentioned that Ichor can have strange effects on vampires. I'm all for it, but I argue that it should be a double-edged sword</div> </div> </div> </div> That's the intention. And someone who isn't me really needs to write a Circle aligned Bloodline that exists because some vampire drank too much Ichor and mutated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=872995#post872995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, it's not all wine and roses. By their very nature, leviathans are spiritual vortices, generating spirits appropriate to their nature and cult - sin spirits, blood spirits, life spirits, death spirits, murder spirits, zealotry spirits, loyalty spirits... great choruses of the more primal and often dangerous spirits tend to flock to the leviathan, suckling from its Wake and its Beloved and feeding on the bounty of Essence. Indeed, as crazy as leviathan cults can get, who's honestly going to notice one or more Spirit-Ridden hanging around?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think you're underestimateing the importance of this. No Werewolf is going to want that anywhere near their territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=872995#post872995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mage:</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> even designed the Knowledge rule with Mage crossover in mind way back in 1E days. Basically, Leviathans use Sympathy in reverse. How much the other guy knows you.<br /> <br /> The idea was to capture the classic Lovecraft trope - don't read the spooky tome you idiots! You read a Leviathan's book, you're a valid target for Rituals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=872995#post872995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Promethean:</b></div> </div> </div> </div> You forget one thing though. Primordial Water and Divine Fire don't mix. Promethians are strongly tied to lightning too.<br /> <br /> I imagine that if Leviathans and Promethians get too close you'd get some really really nasty Firestorms. Also, the Empyerian in Empyerian Thurgist might be related to the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=872995#post872995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At first glance, the Lost and the Tribe seem to go together like oil and water, but look beyond the surface. Sometimes, the best place to hide is in plain sight</div> </div> </div> </div> I think at least one Freehold has somehow dragged an entire Hollow, complete with Doors, into a Leviathan's dream on the basis that it's safer than the Hedge. At least for Changelings who're still wanted by the True Fae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=872995#post872995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beloved mistake a Mummy's Relic for an artefact of their master</div> </div> </div> </div> Mistake? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Heirlooms are what Mummies call Vestiages. They're totally valid tribute for the Judges, though a bit too potent for Mummies to use directly without risk.<br /> <br /> , or when the cult of one kind becomes intermeshed with/subsumed by the cult of another, are obvious. The big thing here is establishing &quot;who's older&quot;; did the Tribe arise sometime after the fall of Irem? Were their waning years before the City of Pillars arose? Or were they equals, and Mummies with sharper memories can dimly recall leviathan war-priests leading armies of gibborim and lahmasu against Iremite slave-legions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=872995#post872995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Beast:</b></div> </div> </div> </div> While the primary themes of Beast and Leviathan are very different (and honestly. I have no idea what Beast's primary themes are meant to be) both include themes of family, and themes of &quot;the primordial part of the human mind&quot;.<br /> <br /> But Beast's idea of family are people you choose, people you like. Leviathan's are people you're stuck with because you've got no one else. Beasts are trying to help people reconnect with the primordial knowledge they've lost. Leviathan's are primordial instincts trying to modernise.<br /> <br /> It seems obvious that rather than trying to focus on Biblical Tragedy and whatever Beast's core theme is one should focus on those shared points and the contrasts between them. I think you could do something interesting with the idea that Beasts run around trying to get monsters to embrace their monsterousness and help them hunt but take one look at Leviathans and go &quot;okay... maybe it's best for everyone if you keep on rejecting your monsterousness&quot;. I'd consider writing rules for &quot;overfeeding&quot;, where a Beast's Saitity goes past 10 and they have to somehow &quot;vomit it up&quot; for their own health. The sort of thing you might get if a Ravager witnesses a Leviathan forcing an entire town to kill each other.<br /> <br /> BTW. I've previously mentioned that Ocean Minds affects Beast's abilitiy to force a good first impression. That was a rule that assumed you're playing a game of Leviathan: the Tempest that includes Beasts. In a true Crossover game.... I've got no clue how you'd handle the conflicting ideas of family.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=872995#post872995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hunter:</b></div> </div> </div> </div> Your mistake is thinking of Hunter as one Splat. Look at each Compact or Conspiracy as a seperate Splat: Network Zero, Null Mysteriis, The Talbot Group, Long Night's Merciful Creed. There's plenty of non-antagonist Hunters to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T09:07:47-07:00","id":873123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=872995#post872995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sin-Eater:</b><br /> Generally speaking, these two races won't interact with each other much. Sin-Eaters mostly concern themselves with the dead, and leviathans with the living. Unless leviathans develop powers that let them interfere with the dead, they're not of much concern to each other. Maybe it's kind of like sin-eaters and vampires, where the biggest reason that the Tribe tend to cross sin-eater radars is their tendency to leave a lot of mad ghosts in their wake. That said, the two &quot;cross-pollinating&quot; each other's respective mythologies could be interesting - imagine sin-eaters who were originally Beloved and so still fixate upon their former master to form the centerpiece of their homebrewed religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if deep in the Underworld you can find Tiamat's ghost. Also, I'm sure some Leviathans could find some sort of use for the Ocean of Fragments.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T10:05:35-07:00","id":873153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, if we do end up doing a &quot;crossing over guidebook&quot; expansion, there should be some thought put into a School that devotes itself to studying the other monsters with which leviathans share the world of darkness, trying to figure out how and why these horrors have managed to successfully grow and change to integrate themselves into the modern era, and how the Tribe might potentially do the same. I mean, Promethean had the Argentum (? Path of Silver) in Magnum Opus for a reason, in that studying other monsters gives prometheans more of a grasp on what humanity is by virtue of what it isn't, and if Leviathan's Schools have similar nature to the Refinements - which is, honestly, how they come across to me - then it makes sense that they'd also consider their fellow denizens of the darkness to be worthy of studying for lessons in what (not) to do to restore the Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe call them something like the School of Silt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T10:40:18-07:00","id":873173,"title":"","content":"Hey Kings? I was vaguely wondering on a certain little something that pretty much dealt with Leviathans. You know how Mages essentially have Goetic Magic? The ability to turn over their vices and make them into spiritual embodiments of the mage's vice? I was wondering, one spell listed underneath goetic magic is one called &quot;Call Eidolon&quot;. Instead of ripping out the Mage's Vice, it instead rips out the Mage's Virtue and makes it into a spirit. Given that one of Leviathan's weaknesses deal with Virtue (more like a ward of Virtue from Marduk from what I read), I was wondering if a Goetic Eidolon is the equivalent of walking spiritual kyptonite on Leviathans. I'm not aware if Goetic Magic is updated to Mage 2E, but just thought it might be something to think about in terms of mages.<br /> <br /> Also, I was hoping if it's fine to comment on how Leviathans controlling fire wouldn't be thematically appropriate. Would it be fine if Leviathans had some work around that had the same (and if not then Similar) effect? For example, Leviathans controlling lava deep within the earth's crust and the like as a Channel for the Elements (Angry Tears of the Earth)? If it's fine to give a small comparison, for Siren, it's just as unfitting for them to control fire, but given how we've (meaning Yads, Reaper and I) have Verses so far, Sirens instead have the opus of &quot;Sear&quot;, which allows them to heat things up or begin the process of heating things up. It's not pyrokinesis, but it still can produce the same effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T11:51:37-07:00","id":873204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873173#post873173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Given that one of Leviathan's weaknesses deal with Virtue (more like a ward of Virtue from Marduk from what I read)</div> </div> </div> </div> Virtue isn't a Leviathan's kryptonite. It's more like gunpowder, so you want to put it behind a kryptonite bullet - that would be Marduk's sigil. <br /> <br /> You could do <i>something</i> with an Endolin and no Marduk Sigil, but it wouldn't be that effective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873173#post873173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, I was hoping if it's fine to comment on how Leviathans controlling fire wouldn't be thematically appropriate. Would it be fine if Leviathans had some work around that had the same (and if not then Similar) effect? For example, Leviathans controlling lava deep within the earth's crust</div> </div> </div> </div>Leviathans can use boiling water, but not lava. The could trigger an Earthquake near a volcano and even shape the Earth to channel the lava where they want, but that's as close as they'll get.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T07:18:17-07:00","id":873735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873046#post873046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots to reply too here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> While the primary themes of Beast and Leviathan are very different (and honestly. I have no idea what Beast's primary themes are meant to be) both include themes of family, and themes of &quot;the primordial part of the human mind&quot;.<br /> <br /> But Beast's idea of family are people you choose, people you like. Leviathan's are people you're stuck with because you've got no one else. Beasts are trying to help people reconnect with the primordial knowledge they've lost. Leviathan's are primordial instincts trying to modernise.<br /> <br /> It seems obvious that rather than trying to focus on Biblical Tragedy and whatever Beast's core theme is one should focus on those shared points and the contrasts between them. I think you could do something interesting with the idea that Beasts run around trying to get monsters to embrace their monsterousness and help them hunt but take one look at Leviathans and go &quot;okay... maybe it's best for everyone if you keep on rejecting your monsterousness&quot;. I'd consider writing rules for &quot;overfeeding&quot;, where a Beast's Saitity goes past 10 and they have to somehow &quot;vomit it up&quot; for their own health. The sort of thing you might get if a Ravager witnesses a Leviathan forcing an entire town to kill each other.<br /> <br /> BTW. I've previously mentioned that Ocean Minds affects Beast's abilitiy to force a good first impression. That was a rule that assumed you're playing a game of Leviathan: the Tempest that includes Beasts. In a true Crossover game.... I've got no clue how you'd handle the conflicting ideas of family.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, one of Beast primary themes is that You Don't Choose Your Family. Even their Kin mechanics works wether the Beast and their Kin are friends or foes, as long as they're important to each other. Also, Beasts are great team players thanks to Mother's Kiss.<br /> <br /> Another theme is about being true to themselves, and not neglect part of their nature wether it is their monstrous or human side, especially since both kinds of neglect are likely to get Heroes on the Beast's trail. Beasts aren't so much about pushing toward monstrosity than about accepting that part of themselves or of their family. Beasts tell their monstrous Kin it's ok to exist the way they are. More, they tell them that they belong to the same great family. It doesn't mean they'll get along, but the Beasts won't judge.<br /> <br /> Many Beasts think of themselves as the children of the Dark Mother which some associate with Tiamat, which could either bring them closer to the Tribe or bring them into conflict. Beasts are also often clannish and territorial which may lead them to either confrontation or alliance. Also, a Leviathan's Wake could generate chambers and affect the Hive dramatically, attracting the attention of the Begotten. Some Beasts, mostly Makaras, may also share the aquatic proclivities of Leviathans and share this aspect of their existences as few can. An aquatic lair might also be a good place for a Leviathan to retreat from the world for a while. The Makara's Vampire Stereotype comes to mind: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;You don't drown. My place, then?&quot; </div> </div> </div>A Begotten's Hunger could also either create links or frictions: A Leviathan would have no troble keeping a Beast well fed thanks to Family Banquet, but a Beast could also decide to feed from an Atoll, a Beloved or even from a Leviathan.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T08:50:41-07:00","id":873791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873735#post873735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, one of Beast primary themes is that You Don't Choose Your Family. Even their Kin mechanics works wether the Beast and their Kin are friends or foes, as long as they're important to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not quite. The Family Ties sidebar says &quot;Associates, rivals, or even genial enemies thus potentially qualify for this condition as well, though it will likely be <u>significantly harder to maintain more hostile connections</u>.&quot;<br /> <br /> This makes Beast's concept of family sound very modern, where the default assumption is that family members like each other but occasionally there's that one uncle. The Steryotypes section also supports this view, where unlike just about everyone else in the WoD, the Steryotypes of other Splats are friendly.<br /> <br /> That's very different from Leviathan, where the Tribe's family relationships resembles pagan gods. A cankerous, fractious, mess riddled with grudges. But they're stuck with each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873735#post873735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another theme is about being true to themselves</div> </div> </div> </div> Which makes Beasts the exact opposite of Leviathans. The Tribe is all about change and transformation. Leviathans don't even know what they are, not truly, but they know they can't stay like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873735#post873735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts tell their monstrous Kin it's ok to exist the way they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much like telling Promethians to abandon the Pilgramage is a bad idea for all involved. Convincing Leviathans to stay the way they are has a high chance of destroying the Leviathan's mind, and chance of causing a small apocalypse.<br /> <br /> I mean. Schools are the way Leviathans try to become something else. Convince a Leviathan it's ok to stay the way they are and you're telling them to leave the Schools. Without a School you loose the primary way to regain Tranquility - and then the question becomes how much damage will the Leviathan do on the way down. The answer could be enough to horrify a Ravager.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873735#post873735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many Beasts think of themselves as the children of the Dark Mother which some associate with Tiamat, which could either bring them closer to the Tribe or bring them into conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div> It depends on the individual Leviathan; but there's a fair amount of Leviathans who'd try to kill a Begotten the instant they &quot;blaspheme&quot; against the Progenitors. And even more agnostic Leviathans might not take kindly to human-linked non-divine astral beings (Leviathans are <b>extremely</b> psychic, they can tell that Beasts are of the Primordial Dream and that the Primordial Dream is part of the Temenos) claiming to be related to Tiamat so a smart Begotten will play it very safe.<br /> <br /> Honestly you should probably tone that down in a crossover game.<br /> <br /> <br /> BTW, there's nothing in the Leviathan setting that says Begotten can't be descended from Tiamat. Leviathans believe that Tiamat is the ancestor of both mankind and the Tribe - even before a few melennia of human/Leviathan cross-breading. Leviathans saying that Begotten have no right to claim to be children of Tiamat because they're from the Temenos are being unfair and prejudiced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873735#post873735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a Leviathan's Wake could generate chambers and affect the Hive dramatically, attracting the attention of the Begotten.</div> </div> </div> </div> Absolutely. It would be hard for any other monster to be the Apex with a Leviathan around.<br /> <br /> In fact, being extremely psychic and constantly projecting a Leviathan's presence is a good justification for the Storyteller to introduce all sorts of freaky goings on in the Primordial Dream. The fact that the Primordial Dream is part of the Temenos and Leviathans have their own completely independent Temenos (the Rift) just adds the icing to the cake.<br /> <br /> And while you're at it. A fragment of the Leviathan's soul exists in everyone who knows about it. God knows what that would do to the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873735#post873735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> An aquatic lair might also be a good place for a Leviathan to retreat from the world for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div> Probably not actually. A Leviathan trying to retreat from the world is trying to get away from humanity. Traveling into humanity's subconscious is the exact opposite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-25-2016, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T10:21:56-07:00","id":873853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873791#post873791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not quite. The Family Ties sidebar says &quot;Associates, rivals, or even genial enemies thus potentially qualify for this condition as well, though it will likely be <u>significantly harder to maintain more hostile connections</u>.&quot;<br /> <br /> This makes Beast's concept of family sound very modern, where the default assumption is that family members like each other but occasionally there's that one uncle. The Steryotypes section also supports this view, where unlike just about everyone else in the WoD, the Steryotypes of other Splats are friendly.<br /> <br /> That's very different from Leviathan, where the Tribe's family relationships resembles pagan gods. A cankerous, fractious, mess riddled with grudges. But they're stuck with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. <u>Family Ties is a Condition</u> that needs a strong relationship. A strong enmity works but of course it's harder to keep things stables with this than with a strong friendship. In the end what really matters is that Family Ties can only be given to Kin, who are all beings descended from the Dark Mother, plus some fundamentally human supernaturals. It doesn't matter if a Beast likes Vampires or not, the blood suckers are family either way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873791#post873791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which makes Beasts the exact opposite of Leviathans. The Tribe is all about change and transformation. Leviathans don't even know what they are, not truly, but they know they can't stay like this.<br /> <br /> Much like telling Promethians to abandon the Pilgramage is a bad idea for all involved. Convincing Leviathans to stay the way they are has a high chance of destroying the Leviathan's mind, and chance of causing a small apocalypse.<br /> <br /> I mean. Schools are the way Leviathans try to become something else. Convince a Leviathan it's ok to stay the way they are and you're telling them to leave the Schools. Without a School you loose the primary way to regain Tranquility - and then the question becomes how much damage will the Leviathan do on the way down. The answer could be enough to horrify a Ravager.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts don't judge family, so there's no reason for conflict except on an individual basis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873791#post873791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on the individual Leviathan; but there's a fair amount of Leviathans who'd try to kill a Begotten the instant they &quot;blaspheme&quot; against the Progenitors. And even more agnostic Leviathans might not take kindly to human-linked non-divine astral beings (Leviathans are <b>extremely</b> psychic, they can tell that Beasts are of the Primordial Dream and that the Primordial Dream is part of the Temenos) claiming to be related to Tiamat so a smart Begotten will play it very safe.<br /> <br /> Honestly you should probably tone that down in a crossover game.<br /> <br /> <br /> BTW, there's nothing in the Leviathan setting that says Begotten can't be descended from Tiamat. Leviathans believe that Tiamat is the ancestor of both mankind and the Tribe - even before a few melennia of human/Leviathan cross-breading. Leviathans saying that Begotten have no right to claim to be children of Tiamat because they're from the Temenos are being unfair and prejudiced.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure I get the issue. Would those Leviathans doubt the Begotten's claim? the nature or existence of the Dark Mother?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873791#post873791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely. It would be hard for any other monster to be the Apex with a Leviathan around.<br /> <br /> In fact, being extremely psychic and constantly projecting a Leviathan's presence is a good justification for the Storyteller to introduce all sorts of freaky goings on in the Primordial Dream. The fact that the Primordial Dream is part of the Temenos and Leviathans have their own completely independent Temenos (the Rift) just adds the icing to the cake.<br /> <br /> And while you're at it. A fragment of the Leviathan's soul exists in everyone who knows about it. God knows what that would do to the Primordial Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div> I must have missed that ability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873791#post873791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not actually. A Leviathan trying to retreat from the world is trying to get away from humanity. Traveling into humanity's subconscious is the exact opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if the Lair isn't part of the Hive?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T11:05:20-07:00","id":873876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873853#post873853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. <u>Family Ties is a Condition</u> that needs a strong relationship. A strong enmity works but of course it's harder to keep things stables with this than with a strong friendship.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which means that over time a Beast will end up with Family Ties mostly applying to people that they like. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873853#post873853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't matter if a Beast likes Vampires or not, the blood suckers are family either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact remains. Beast has core mechanics designed to help family or foster positive social relationships with family. It has none designed to hinder family or cause conflicts with family. This gives Beast a portrayal of family which is incompatible with Leviathan's portrayal of family. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873853#post873853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts don't judge family, so there's no reason for conflict except on an individual basis.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure they do. &quot;it's ok to exist the way they are&quot; is a judgement. And one that creates reasons for interesting dramatic conflicts with Leviathans. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873853#post873853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I get the issue. Would those Leviathans doubt the Begotten's claim? the nature or existence of the Dark Mother?</div> </div> </div> </div> Plenty would doubt the Begotten's claim, but the real issue is that Leviathans have a lot of issues with self identity and would quite likely not take it well if someone outside the Tribe starts talking about what it means to be a Leviathan. Talking about Tiamat qualifies. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873853#post873853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must have missed that ability.</div> </div> </div> </div> Seeing and recognising astral entities is under Transformation, at Depth 3. I'm not putting Beast specific mechanics in the corebook, but that power can tell you more or less what a Beast is. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873853#post873853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if the Lair isn't part of the Hive?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still part of the Primordial Dream isn't it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T13:19:25-07:00","id":873983,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Wake itself, while Sheol lists the maximum area, how does it affect things mechanically? Given the systems and changes in 2E, I'd guess it counts as always having/applying Hard Leverage in social combat? What are the mechanics regarding someone turning Beloved? I think 1E had a sub-system where a target had to fail a number of rolls, right? Given the switch from Morality to Integrity, what about the Wake simply provoking Breaking Points (with a Beloved Condition being a consequence of Failure at Integrity 1, or Dramatic Failure while inside a Wake). The Beloved Condition itself could use Sheol or Wake Strength (?) or the Cult's Zeal as a substitute Integrity (reducing the handicap of most Beloved's tanked Integrity scores, as well as acting as a patch for the Soulless Condition). Other supernaturals wouldn't be subject to the Breaking Point aura effect, but might still be subject to the social combat modifiers.<br /> <hr /><br /> Regarding crossover:<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire</b><br /> 2 Egotistical predators with mind whammy powers - what could go wrong?<br /> <br /> How do Leviathan's handle Vinculum and Vitae addiction now?<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf</b><br /> <br /> Are spirits affected by the Wake? I'd assume not, since they don't seem to be affect by any passive aura, even Disquiet. Largely irrelevant though. Unless you have a particularly asshole-ish Pack, Leviathans are <i>not</i> good for the local real estate. They don't seem like they'd be good Pack mates either.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage</b><br /> <br /> Yes, let's put the person known for obsession in the room with the mind-bending, mad-cultist-making aura - again, what could go wrong?<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean</b><br /> <br /> Tragedy, write large. A reading of both their lots in life looks like they'd be kindred spirits. Pity about that Fire and Water thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling</b><br /> <br /> Oh, boy. I can certainly see the value of a Changeling associating with a Leviathan. Like those people that undergo abuse to harden themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Geist</b><br /> <br /> Considering the casual death Leviathans seem to propagate, combined with the deranged focus they also seem to spread, I can easily see one of the Tribe making the Bounds' lives a lot more busy.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy</b><br /> <br /> Clash of the Titan(ic Ego)s. Both are larger than life powers that lead devoted Cults. <br /> <br /> <b>Demon</b><br /> <br /> Yeah, any alliance here would go bad for everyone else concerned real quick.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast</b><br /> <br /> Like Demon, above, but now expand to everyone. Leviathans <i>really don't</i> need Begotten to enable them.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviant</b><br /> <br /> No ideas, since there is nothing really out yet detail-wise. I think Leviathan Cults might be likely sources of them, though, which wouldn't help any feelings of friendship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-25-2016, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T13:26:27-07:00","id":873986,"title":"","content":"I haven't thought about the Wake yet, but those are some pretty good ideas you've got there and will be my starting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-25-2016, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T14:09:23-07:00","id":874009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873983#post873983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Wake itself, while Sheol lists the maximum area, how does it affect things mechanically? Given the systems and changes in 2E, I'd guess it counts as always having/applying Hard Leverage in social combat? What are the mechanics regarding someone turning Beloved? I think 1E had a sub-system where a target had to fail a number of rolls, right? Given the switch from Morality to Integrity, what about the Wake simply provoking Breaking Points (with a Beloved Condition being a consequence of Failure at Integrity 1, or Dramatic Failure while inside a Wake). The Beloved Condition itself could use Sheol or Wake Strength (?) or the Cult's Zeal as a substitute Integrity (reducing the handicap of most Beloved's tanked Integrity scores, as well as acting as a patch for the Soulless Condition). Other supernaturals wouldn't be subject to the Breaking Point aura effect, but might still be subject to the social combat modifiers.<br /> <hr /><br /> Regarding crossover:<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf</b><br /> <br /> Are spirits affected by the Wake? I'd assume not, since they don't seem to be affect by any passive aura, even Disquiet. Largely irrelevant though. Unless you have a particularly asshole-ish Pack, Leviathans are <i>not</i> good for the local real estate. They don't seem like they'd be good Pack mates either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, actually spirits could be, and are-indirectly. The Resonance of Overwhelming Love, Faith, Need, Addiction, Etcetera gradually leaks Essence of that flavor into the Shadow, drawing and nurturing spirits of those concepts...I'd be surprised if loci <i>don't </i>tend to pop up around Leviathans (making an area where a Cult has lived for a long time even more eerie), and if they become interested, there's entire <i>umia </i>of Shadow beasts glad for their creation and good life. A Leviathan who figures out how to interact with the Hisil has an army of otherworldly creatures to draw on that aren't nearly as bound to the water as beasts from the Primordial Sea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T14:21:58-07:00","id":874019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874009#post874009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, actually spirits could be, and are-indirectly. The Resonance of Overwhelming Love, Faith, Need, Addiction, Etcetera gradually leaks Essence of that flavor into the Shadow, drawing and nurturing spirits of those concepts...I'd be surprised if loci <i>don't </i>tend to pop up around Leviathans (making an area where a Cult has lived for a long time even more eerie), and if they become interested, there's entire <i>umia </i>of Shadow beasts glad for their creation and good life. A Leviathan who figures out how to interact with the Hisil has an army of otherworldly creatures to draw on that aren't nearly as bound to the water as beasts from the Primordial Sea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That gives me an idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a><br /> <br /> How about a Vitality Channel that works by allowing to become like a spirit or spirit like creature in some manner, with the justification that even Spirits are a type of life... unless you already did that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe even doing something along the like having the ability to get spirits into your cult that way...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T14:35:01-07:00","id":874033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874009#post874009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, actually spirits could be, and are-indirectly. The Resonance of Overwhelming Love, Faith, Need, Addiction, Etcetera gradually leaks Essence of that flavor into the Shadow, drawing and nurturing spirits of those concepts...I'd be surprised if loci <i>don't </i>tend to pop up around Leviathans (making an area where a Cult has lived for a long time even more eerie), and if they become interested, there's entire <i>umia </i>of Shadow beasts glad for their creation and good life. A Leviathan who figures out how to interact with the Hisil has an army of otherworldly creatures to draw on that aren't nearly as bound to the water as beasts from the Primordial Sea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Heh. I had a Leviathan whose Evolution was based around interacting with Spirits (to which they'd use to F with Marduk's tech). But I don't think Leviathans innately have any influence on most ephemerals. Goetics, perhaps, are the exception?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T14:37:43-07:00","id":874036,"title":"","content":"Correct. Leviathans innately can interact with Astral/Goetic/etc along with psychics projecting out of their body. Other Ephemeral beings would require Channels, Adaptations, or Evolutions depending on the specific case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874019#post874019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a Vitality Channel that works by allowing to become like a spirit or spirit like creature in some manner, with the justification that even Spirits are a type of life... unless you already did that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible. Spirits are corebook in 2E. I'm not sure how you'd split it into seven powers though, and it might work better as an Evolution where the transformation into Spirit is one way and permanent.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Adaptations that allow a Leviathan to enter the Hisil and survive there - Predation lets the Leviathan feed on spirits. Elements lets the Leviathan treat Hisil water as normal water. Etc. But full on becoming a Spirit requires an Evolution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874009#post874009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Leviathan who figures out how to interact with the Hisil has an army of otherworldly creatures to draw on that aren't nearly as bound to the water as beasts from the Primordial Sea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously doing so must have risks proportional to the rewards.<br /> <br /> That said, the corebook probably won't go beyond a few Spirit related powers. The meat of Leviathan-Spirit interaction will require you to read Werewolf and draw your own conclusions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873983#post873983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Leviathan's handle Vinculum and Vitae addiction now?</div> </div> </div> </div> Ocean Minds applies. So probably a Clash of Wills since Vinculum &amp; Vitae addiction have no roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873983#post873983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are spirits affected by the Wake?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd let the Leviathan use the social effects of the Wake on Spirits.<br /> <br /> Unless someone can point me to precident saying that's now how Spirits work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873983#post873983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clash of the Titan(ic Ego)s. Both are larger than life powers that lead devoted Cults.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's a shame Mummies can't pull of high level sorcery and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ysRK875IRwM\" target=\"_blank\">summon a champion</a> that could go head to head with a Godzilla Leviathan for a final showdown.<br /> <br /> Mummies are much better at playing within the system than Leviathans, and their Cultists are less likely to do something insane self-defeating so giving Leviathans the edge in wonton distruction seems fair. But I wish Mummies were on Leviathan's level so the two could be better rivals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874009#post874009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Deviant</b><br /> <br /> No ideas, since there is nothing really out yet detail-wise. I think Leviathan Cults might be likely sources of them, though, which wouldn't help any feelings of friendship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Leviathans are up there with Geniuses and Mages for creating Deviants.<br /> <br /> I think that a Hybrid and Lahmasu could just be dropped right into a group of Deviants and it would work perfectly. (Obviously not a Lahmasu who comes from a thriving underwater city surounded by their own kind.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-25-2016, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T14:40:07-07:00","id":874039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874019#post874019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That gives me an idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span><br /> <br /> How about a Vitality Channel that works by allowing to become like a spirit or spirit like creature in some manner, with the justification that even Spirits are a type of life... unless you already did that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe even doing something along the like having the ability to get spirits into your cult that way...</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually wrote a homebrew Channel for interacting with spirits back in 1e. I could dig it out and post it tomorrow if anyone's interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T15:21:42-07:00","id":874060,"title":"","content":"Changing topic. Here's The Wake, based on Vent0's ideas. And a picture of a Beloved Priestess I found on DeviantArt because it seems fitting.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/564x/41/21/4b/41214b9774e55fa9c8e61d4e86173bcc.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:26px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Wake</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Wake is the term used by Leviathans for what is, in effect, the sensation that their divine nature produces on normal humans. It is a psychic pressure front that humans feel on an instinctual level - it is the dread majesty of a Leviathan's birthright. Tribal scholars claim that it is the &quot;shadow&quot; cast by the Leviathan's true form, and it affects a region around him, which grows as the Leviathan's Sheol increases.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mortals affected by a Leviathan's Wake are infused with a mixture of awe, terror, and deference. For all that this seems attractive, it is a deeply isolating effect. A Leviathan can't enter a room without people lowering their voices, or go to the grocery store without people self-consciously apologizing for getting in your way (even if they weren't) - the Wake functions as a psychological battering ram, preventing the Tribe from blending in with a crowd. A Leviathan is always, willingly or not, intimidating every mortal in his presence. The Wake is a beacon, a message from the days of the Primordial that impresses itself on human minds - &quot;You're less important than me; everything here is mine if I want it.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The allure of the Wake, especially for Tribe members who might have been socially awkward or bullied before they awoke to their true natures, is obvious. However, the Wake is also extremely dangerous - taking advantage of it means taking advantage of humans, further alienating the Leviathan from the world he has to live in. Many Leviathans have reveled in the Wake until it Eroded their own minds or they created so many enemies that word reached the Marduk Society.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mortals subject to the Wake are aware that they are cowed but will, without training or knowledge, put it down to the Leviathan having unusual charisma or presence. They get the sense that the Leviathan just happens to be the sort of person who the room stops for. The Wake also does not alter a subject's memory, only their current ability to act. Their recollection of events during their exposure will therefore be tinted by their own nature and desires, and how the Leviathan acted towards them. If the Leviathan used intimidation to browbeat them into doing what he wanted, they will recall being intimidated and will attempt to justify their response in a fashion that seems consistent. A timid person, for instance, will assume that they gave way as would be expected, while one that resents being pushed around might formulate reasons why they would permit it. This tendency can be a blessing or a curse - if a person's mental scenario elevates the Leviathan's actions to a criminal offense, they may very well get in touch with the appropriate authorities. A member of the Tribe could breeze into a high-security facility, but the consequences may yet follow them home.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some mortals are more drastically affected by the Wake - these unfortunates are struck with a lingering obsession with the Leviathan, hovering between a dangerous mixture of strong emotions. Unaware of the truth of what they are experiencing, they find ways of explaining it - some outlets more constructive than others. The only unifying element of this obsession is that the mortal is certain that there is something different - something special and unique and equal parts horrible and wondrous - about the Leviathan. If they have not met the Leviathan, they instead become convinced that there is something unique, horrible, and wondrous nearby. In isolation these Beloved end in one of two ways - either the mortal breaks free of the Wake, or the mortal takes ever larger risks as their obsession grows until their complete self-destruction. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is only in a collective that Beloved can find some measure of stability and satisfy their unique needs. While a canny Beloved might attract followers of their own and create an outlet in the sharing of ideas and speculation; perhaps learning genuine occult lore and becoming a danger to themselves and the Leviathan they obsess over. Most long term Beloved either group up with others like themselves or enter the Leviathan's service. However the group forms, the psychology of Beloved ensures that its internal culture will be markable unhealthy. With their obsession over a divine Leviathan, the only appropriate word is a Cult. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Cult serves as extensions of the Leviathan, his agents in the human world, permitting him to avoid the strain of everyday life. It can infuse the Leviathan with Ichor through reverence and the enactment of mystical rites - their subservience reaffirming his divine nature. Beloved are also prime hosts for the generation of Lahmasu, as they are willing, perhaps even eager, to be touched by the bloodline of the Tribe.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With the psychological isolation of the Wake, the lure of staying secluded and meeting only with one's Cult is strong, especially for older, more world-weary Leviathans. This is a potential trap, as interacting with the Beloved is not a substitute for interacting with normal humans, and it is often the ultimate fate of the hidden Cult leader to fall into degeneration, isolated from his own human side.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mechanics of the Wake</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Eye of the Storm</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not everyone is affected by the Wake. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Leviathans, other divine beings, Atolls, and Ahabs are always immune to the Wake. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Characters whose Supernatural Tolerance is two or more lower than the Sheol of the Leviathan are vulnerable to that Leviathan's Wake, but cannot become Beloved. They are otherwise immune.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For resisting the Wake, Marduk agents and Empyrean Theurgists have an effective Supernatural Tolerance equal to twice their highest Virtue.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Characters who have powers that defend against mental effects may use those powers in place of their Supernatural Tolerance. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All others are fully affected. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Storm</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">People within the wake and able to perceive the Leviathan with their natural or psychic senses face a heightened sense of dread, anticipation, but also eager curiosity. Those who spend a significant amount of time within the Storm, or have a conversation more than a quick hello remain within the Storm until they next wake from sleep. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the storm all Integrity Breaking Point rolls take a penalty equal to Leviathan\u2019s Sheol. Mortals, Hybrids and Lahmasu who roll a Dramatic Failure on a Breaking Point roll may become Beloved. If their Integrity is less than (4 + half Sheol) before rolling they may become Beloved on a regular Breaking Point Failure</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sidebar: Mad Oracles</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When a psychic has prophetic dreams, visions, or some other out of body experience they count as though they were physically standing at their viewpoint for the purposes of the Wake. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This means that a lucky, or unlucky, Leviathan could turn someone Beloved without ever going near them. A psychic only has to have a vision of where the Leviathan is, was, or might be (the future in the World of Darkness is never certain). </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Leviathan\u2019s Ripples are as effective at catching the attention of psychics as anything else. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Fringes</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">People within the Leviathan's Wake but unable to perceive the Leviathan through natural or psychic senses are deemed to be within the Fringes. They feel a vague sense of dread, anticipation, and eager curiosity. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the Fringes all Integrity Breaking Point rolls take a penalty equal to half the Leviathan\u2019s Sheol (round up). Mortals, Hybrids and Lahmasu who roll a Dramatic Failure on a Breaking Point roll may become Beloved. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Divine Rights</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When interacting with those affected by the Wake, a Leviathan cannot hold back from intimidating everyone around them anymore than an eagle could avoid intimidating a rabbit. Any social interaction the Leviathan makes automatically counts as Forcing Doors.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the Leviathan spends a point of Ichor to intentionally focus the Wake they gain Hard Leverage and open a number of Doors equal to half Sheol (round up), however barring unusual circumstances this automatically inflicts a Breaking Point roll. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Leviathan may focus the Wake and use other Hard Leverage in combination to open additional doors, or they may focus the Wake to cause a Breaking Point without social interaction or even speaking to the victim. It\u2019s not that rare for Leviathans to simply hammer a person\u2019s Integrity until they become Beloved, are lost to madness, or turn into an Ahab. </span></span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-26-2016, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T18:11:40-07:00","id":874148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874060#post874060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For resisting the Wake, Marduk agents and Empyrean Theurgists have an effective Supernatural Tolerance equal to twice their highest Virtue.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, Virtues are rated now?<br /> <br /> Edit: Ah, they buy a Virtue merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874060#post874060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the storm all Integrity Breaking Point rolls take a penalty equal to Leviathan\u2019s Sheol (round up). Mortals, Hybrids and Lahmasu who roll a Dramatic Failure on a Breaking Point roll may become Beloved. If their Integrity is less than (4 + half Sheol) before rolling they may become Beloved on a regular Breaking Point Failure</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Is this supposed to be half Sheol? Or is the &quot;(round up)&quot; an artifact from copy+paste?<br /> <hr /><br /> Is Beloved going to be a persistent Condition, or a minor/micro template?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-25-2016, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T22:12:46-07:00","id":874268,"title":"","content":"I think Lunacy in Werewolf 2e would be a better model for the Wake - rather than penalizing all breaking point rolls, make perceiving a Leviathan a breaking point that inflicts Beloved status on a dramatic failure. The system you're presenting implies that breaking points that have nothing to do with a Leviathan (or any other supernatural event) can convert one to Beloved, which doesn't make much sense. Why, for instance, would a man who kills someone in a bar fight that escalated promptly decide, on realizing what he's done, to become the loyal servant of a fish demon that's in the neighborhood, but that he may well never have met?<br /> <br /> I also think that the penalties from the Wake should depend not on Sheol, but on Depth. A Leviathan passing for human would inspire dread and obsession for no observable reason, but nothing beyond that; approaching apotheosis would destroy the sanity of all witnesses and swiftly create a cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T23:52:39-07:00","id":874309,"title":"","content":"Can Leviathans make Pacts with Demons?<br /> Can they be bound by deals with the Lost and other Fae?<br /> Can Leviathans be Urged, Claimed, Possessed, etc..?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T02:37:57-07:00","id":874368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874148#post874148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this supposed to be half Sheol? Or is the &quot;(round up)&quot; an artifact from copy+paste?</div> </div> </div> </div>copy+paste artifact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874148#post874148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Beloved going to be a persistent Condition, or a minor/micro template?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874268#post874268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why, for instance, would a man who kills someone in a bar fight that escalated promptly decide, on realizing what he's done, to become the loyal servant of a fish demon that's in the neighborhood, but that he may well never have met?</div> </div> </div> </div> Let me turn that question around at you? Why would a theosophist colony who has never met Cthulhu decide to don white robes en mass and await some glorious fulfillment? That's from Call of Cthulhu. People didn't need to perceive Cthulhu for his Wake to affect them, and neither do Leviathans.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, the answer to your question is because he's standing in a psychic field that's constantly hammering him with &quot;WORSHIP GREG!&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the moment of vulnerability that is a failed Breaking Point, when there are cracks in his self identity, the Leviathan's psychic power seeps into those cracks and &quot;worship Greg&quot; moves from being an outside influence into being part of his core self identity.<br /> <br /> He wouldn't imediately know who Greg is and head over to the temple of Greg and enlist in the cult. Rather when trying to put himself back togeather after the Breaking Point he'd connect his actions to his feelings of dread, <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">anticipation, and eager curiosity; and become obsessed with exploring those feelings. </span></span>If he met actually Greg afterwords then he'd recognize Greg as the source of those feelings and transfer his obsession across. But if he doesn't - see the Wake write up's section on isolated Beloved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874268#post874268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that the penalties from the Wake should depend not on Sheol, but on Depth. A Leviathan passing for human would inspire dread and obsession for no observable reason, but nothing beyond that; approaching apotheosis would destroy the sanity of all witnesses and swiftly create a cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wake is a purely psychic phenomena it has nothing to do with how terrifying a Leviathan looks.<br /> <br /> However if seeing a Leviathan approaching apotheosis is a Breaking Point (a sensible assumption) or provides bonuses to social rolls like Intimidation (another sensible assumption) it will synergies nicely with the Wake mechanics as written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874309#post874309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Leviathans make Pacts with Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div> Same as any other supernatural. However somebody else makes a pact with the Leviathan, say someone selling their grandfather and their grandfather is a Leviathan; that won't affect a Leviathan. Look at the time travel paradox stuff in the Channels scrapbook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874309#post874309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can they be bound by deals with the Lost and other Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div> Same as any other supernatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874309#post874309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Leviathans be Urged, Claimed, Possessed, etc..?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Urged, if the Spirit rolls really well. No to the other two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-26-2016, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T02:46:57-07:00","id":874370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874368#post874368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe Urged, if the Spirit rolls really well. No to the other two.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if a really, really powerful spirit tried though? like, Rank 6 or so? What with the whole 'the leviathan's soul is in everyone who knows about them', could the spirit take advantage of that and possess them 'by proxy' as it were?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T03:06:51-07:00","id":874376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874370#post874370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if a really, really powerful spirit tried though? like, Rank 6 or so?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Imperial Mysteries a Spirit with Influence 7 would be able to change a Leviathan so that it's possible to break the no-mixing templates rule. That would allow Possession or Claiming. (Wait. I think I got mixed up. Possession works on supernaturals doesn't it. It's only Claiming that would be a template mix. If that's the case, any Spirit could Possess a Leviathan if it rolls well enough)<br /> <br /> Anyway. My plan is to say nothing about Imperial Mysteries' interaction with Leviathan. The Storyteller can decide how they fit together. I am happy to say that the Arcana for Leviathans are Life&amp;Mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874370#post874370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What with the whole 'the leviathan's soul is in everyone who knows about them', could the spirit take advantage of that and possess them 'by proxy' as it were?</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of it as like a Mage who has another Mage's soul stone. It makes a great way to target Sympathetic Magic; but if you couldn't do it to the mage standing near you, you can't do it with their soul stone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-26-2016, 06:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T08:51:08-07:00","id":874575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874368#post874368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">copy+paste artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't bonuses and penalties usually cap out at +/-5 from a single source, though?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874368#post874368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, the answer to your question is because he's standing in a psychic field that's constantly hammering him with &quot;WORSHIP GREG!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, is Greg going to be our go to example Leviathan, then? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T08:57:48-07:00","id":874577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874575#post874575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, is Greg going to be our go to example Leviathan, then? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Greg, otherwise known as the Herald of the Lords of the First World, Scion of the Line of the Great Unchained, Descendant of the Seven Divinities and Hierophant of the Sect of the Wanderer of Oceans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T09:04:13-07:00","id":874583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874577#post874577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Greg, otherwise known as the Herald of the Lords of the First World, Scion of the Line of the Great Unchained, Descendant of the Seven Divinities and Hierophant of the Sect of the Wanderer of Oceans.</div> </div> </div> </div>(former assistant sales clerk at Best Buy)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:36:43-07:00","id":874661,"title":"","content":"Sure. Greg, Herald of the Lords of the First World, Scion of the Line of the Great Unchained, Descendant of the Seven Divinities and Hierophant of the Sect of the Wanderer of Oceans (former assistant sales clerk at Best Buy) is now the go to example of a Leviathan.<br /> <br /> (I was just making a reference to <a href=\"https://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/LeviathanTempest:ChapterTwo#Names.2C_Aliases.2C_and_Honorifics\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> sidebar. It will probably arrive in 2E unchanged at some point).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874575#post874575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't bonuses and penalties usually cap out at +/-5 from a single source, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>The key word there is &quot;usually&quot;. Power stats are the most common exception though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:51:35-07:00","id":874673,"title":"","content":"On a more serious note, on the mechanics for becoming Beloved, could there perhaps be a penalty to the roll to resist based on how well you know the Leviathan? As in, a colleague who you only speak with once in a week might get no penalty while a close confidante or best friend (from before the leviathan became so, mind) suffers -5. What with the whole 'there's a piece of the leviathan's soul in you if you know about them' schtick, it might make sense that the more knowledge, and therefore the more soul, the greater purchase the Wake has in the victim's mind.<br /> <br /> Plus it adds another layer of horror to the Wake, making it even more likely that someone you try to confide in will end up just another member of your insane cult. Not to mention the fact that you're more likely to listen to someone who used to be a best friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:55:52-07:00","id":874683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874673#post874673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more serious note, on the mechanics for becoming Beloved, could there perhaps be a penalty to the roll to resist based on how well you know the Leviathan? As in, a colleague who you only speak with once in a week might get no penalty while a close confidante or best friend (from before the leviathan became so, mind) suffers -5. What with the whole 'there's a piece of the leviathan's soul in you if you know about them' schtick, it might make sense that the more knowledge, and therefore the more soul, the greater purchase the Wake has in the victim's mind.<br /> <br /> Plus it adds another layer of horror to the Wake, making it even more likely that someone you try to confide in will end up just another member of your insane cult. Not to mention the fact that you're more likely to listen to someone who used to be a best friend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, to brainwash the foolish investigator that stumbles upon the Leviathan's trail and absorbs more occult Knowledge of the Leviathan than is healthy for the investigator's mind. (Making them prime Primordial Theurgist material)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T13:29:36-07:00","id":874831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874673#post874673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more serious note, on the mechanics for becoming Beloved, could there perhaps be a penalty to the roll to resist based on how well you know the Leviathan? As in, a colleague who you only speak with once in a week might get no penalty while a close confidante or best friend (from before the leviathan became so, mind) suffers -5.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think a temperament penalty to all Breaking Points would be far to nasty a penalty to include as a rule. At most it could be a Condition that affects one Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> So the occult tome trope is downplayed I'm I afraid. You can learn about Leviathans without going mad, but learn enough and one might decide to start visiting your dreams; and that would count as though you were within the Wake and might turn you Beloved.<br /> <br /> (Primordial Thurgists try to look for Leviathans who don't have Piercing the Veil of Slumber for this exact reason. They need to be Beloved, but if the Leviathan can visit their Dream it can order them to do stuff. Then they're no longer a power thief, they're an obedient priest)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-26-2016, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T13:54:33-07:00","id":874850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874831#post874831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the occult tome trope is downplayed I'm I afraid. You can learn about Leviathans without going mad, but learn enough and one might decide to start visiting your dreams; and that would count as though you were within the Wake and might turn you Beloved.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Leviathan would still need to be aware of the investigator's existence to start visiting their dreams though, right? Unless Leviathans have some way to audit &quot;who know about me&quot;?<br /> Is the name of the game then &quot;don't let them know that they you know&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:04:55-07:00","id":874860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874850#post874850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless Leviathans have some way to audit &quot;who know about me&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh. I need to write that power. It will be an Adaptation of Eye of the Watchful Deity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:12:56-07:00","id":874865,"title":"","content":"Here's that spirit Channel I was talking about yesterday. It's a bit mechanic-light and is perhaps a bit weak.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Piercing the Veil of Shadows (Ancestral)</i></b><br /> <i>To the Progenitors, both spirit and flesh were merely two sides of the same coin and each utterly beneath their notice.</i><ul><li>Depth 0: Birthright of Awareness</li> <li>Depth 1: The leviathan gains the ability to roll (Wits + Composure +Sheol) to notice Twilight activity within his Wake. He knows the approximate location of the activity, to within about a meter.</li> <li>Depth 2: The leviathan gains the ability to visually perceive beings in Twilight. He cannot hear or touch them.</li> <li>Depth 3: The leviathan gains the ability to hear and speak to entities in a state of Twilight. He still cannot touch them.</li> <li>Depth 4: The leviathan gains the ability to touch and physically interact with beings in Twilight. This cuts both ways. A leviathan can harm the entity but it can do the same to him.</li> <li>Depth 5: The leviathan becomes able to see across the Gauntlet, as the WtF Gift 'Two World Eyes'.</li> <li>Depth 6: In addition to the Depth 5 effect, the leviathan also becomes able to hear and speak across the Gauntlet.</li> </ul><b><u>Adaptations:</u></b><ul><li>Walking Between the Worlds (OOO) : In Depth 3 and below the leviathan gains the ability to cross the Gauntlet using the medium of water. This should be handled as if the leviathan was entering the Rift, save that Gatewaters provide no benefit and that penalties appropriate to the environment should be applied to the crossing attempt.</li> <li>Show the Path (OO( requires Walking Between the Worlds and Birthright of Fecundity)): The leviathan can bring others into the Shadow with him, provided that they are touching him and he has used the Birthright of Fecundity upon them this scene. This <i>can</i> work on creatures without an Ichor pool, but it still grants no Ichor, costs the leviathan 1 (or more) and acts as a poison of Toxicity 2.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T15:55:54-07:00","id":874964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874831#post874831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the occult tome trope is downplayed I'm I afraid. You can learn about Leviathans without going mad, but learn enough and one might decide to start visiting your dreams; and that would count as though you were within the Wake and might turn you Beloved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see a Merit that makes knowledge more directly harmful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T20:03:01-07:00","id":875170,"title":"","content":"Okay, it took me a long time to get back to this topic, and I'm sorry about that. Trying to reply to the comments that looked like they warranted replies...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873046#post873046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Fanatacism Merit that protects against mind control makes sense; but I'm ok with other supernaturals being able to influence Beloved.<br /> <br /> Taking over an entire Cult is never easy, the Spell Factors required for a Mastigos to stop an entire cult are crazy. But capturing one Beloved and implanting them with orders is the kind of interesting threat that Leviathans should face. Even if only to track down the culprit and overriding the influence by using Besiging the Tower of Will.<br /> <br /> Sybaris though. Beloved aren't going to be stolen by passive auras, that includes other Leviathans. If you want to poach Beloved you need to capture them and work to break their programming.<br /> <br /> (That said, Call of the Depths is one of the few mass mind control powers out there. Perhaps it should be a little harder to use that one on Beloved).</div> </div> </div> </div>All fair and equitable arguments.<br /> <br /> Essentially, what I was going on from was that being a Beloved is supposed to seriously screw up a person's mind. In which case, immunity to Lunacy and Dissonance made sense; when you're the mad cultist of Cthulhu's actual in-universe inspiration, the creature who traumatised Lovecraft into writing his Mythos, then you have ample room in your worldview for magic and are hardly likely to start gibbering at the sight of the wolfman.<br /> <br /> Likewise, a bonus to resisting Mind spells or Domination felt like a good way to emphasize both the insanity and the sheer faith that seem endemic in the Beloved condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873046#post873046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was the original idea for the School of the Moon. It was changed because it only worked in crossover.<br /> <br /> The biggest barrier to creating a new School based on studying other splat is the rule of 7 (Thunder don't count. The Tribe runs in 7, and Leviathans have decided to kick School of Thunder Leviathans out the Tribe). If you ignore the rule of 7, it's a perfectly reasonable focus for a school.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's good to have arc numbers and the like, but when there's such an obvious niche, you really should fill it.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm the first to admit I'm a huge crossover nut. I like to craft a World of Darkness in which everything fits together (one of the ways the New beats out the Old anyday, in my book).<br /> <br /> So, I'm all for there only being seven Schools <b>in the Corebook</b>. When you're tackling the matter of a crossover, which is inherently beyond the scope of the corebook, breaking the arc number feels justified. It's similar to how the Demon Storyteller's Guide added the Analyst Incarnation and the Pentagrammic Cipher, or the inclusion of the Argentum in Magnum Opus.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I think I'm losing my point... basically, if we include the option for crossing over, then I think the &quot;School of Silt&quot; (many hanks to ZealousChristian24 for the name suggestion) is a must to include. It's just too believable to let it be hung up by the theme of 7s.<br /> <br /> Hell, I would easily believe that there are only seven Schools, but there are countless &quot;Sects&quot;; minor philosophies that haven't caught on to the near-universal popularity of the big seven. Studying how various supernaturals have managed to adapt to this modern world would easily be one of those Sects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873046#post873046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems obvious that rather than trying to focus on Biblical Tragedy and whatever [Splat]'s core theme is, one should focus on those shared points and the contrasts between them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I quoted this and tweaked it slightly, because this is basically what I tried to do when I wrote that crossing over post. My goal was to support those who'd want to crossover between Leviathan and the other splats, whether they also seek to build a universally coherent World of Darkness or just specifically crossover.<br /> <br /> I bring this up because it feels a little like you're trying to stifle the option - that you disapprove of crossovers and want to justify a &quot;no, don't crossover&quot; approach. I'm pretty sure that's not what you intend, but that's how it's coming across.<br /> <br /> It's not going to be easy OR all wine and roses. But it is going to be a popular subject, so it's better to try and be supportive about it.<br /> <br /> Let's take this quote for specific example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873046#post873046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're underestimating the importance of this. No Werewolf is going to want that anywhere near their territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>True... to an extent. Many Forsaken will not want that sort of spiritual vortice near them. The Pure, or Bale Hounds, are a whole different story. Even amongst the Forsaken, there are those who can make peace with it; if the Leviathan keeps the vortice in a relatively settled space, then it makes a natural &quot;ghetto&quot; for the spirits that would be running around anyway. So long as they're being fed there, they're not rampaging over the rest of the city. The werewolves don't have to like it... but, if properly channeled, it can be something they can live with.<br /> <br /> <br /> You do have a point in that maybe I was a little too positive, but let's try not to be too negative about it either, or we're falling right back into that &quot;you're making the setting too crapsack&quot; argument, ala Promethean.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=873046#post873046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your mistake is thinking of Hunter as one Splat. Look at each Compact or Conspiracy as a seperate Splat: Network Zero, Null Mysteriis, The Talbot Group, Long Night's Merciful Creed. There's plenty of non-antagonist Hunters to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wanted to say you have a point about there being non-antagonist Hunters. I just generally don't give a flying fig for Hunters, so it's very hard for me to think much about crossing over with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T00:20:10-07:00","id":875393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874865#post874865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's that spirit Channel I was talking about yesterday. It's a bit mechanic-light and is perhaps a bit weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say it is a bit week. No fault to you, you're copying my... god awful mechanics style from 1E (it predates me, but that's no excuse for me continueing onwards).<br /> <br /> If you want to update it Lambant Eyes of Judgement would make a good guideline, think about other 2-4 should be compressed into one Depth, same for 5-6.<br /> <br /> That leaves you room for 3 completely seperate powers. For example, you might be able to tell significant events that happened in the local area by sensing the Resonance of ambient Essence.<br /> <br /> Or compress it all into a couple of Adaptations. That's probably how I'm going to handle Spirits cannonically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=874964#post874964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see a Merit that makes knowledge more directly harmful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still too powerful IMO.<br /> <br /> However the reverse could work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> a Merit that relies on Knowledge of a Leviathan, and gives both a benefit and a Drawback. Omen Sensitivity would work well, you've seen the horrific truths of the world. Benefit: You know truths. Drawback: Go mad from the relevation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=875170#post875170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, what I was going on from was that being a Beloved is supposed to seriously screw up a person's mind. In which case, immunity to Lunacy and Dissonance made sense</div> </div> </div> </div> It would if Lunacy and Dissonance were merely psychological and caused by you not having room in your worldview for magic or wolfmen. However I'm under the impression that Lunacy is, and I know Dissonance is, an active supernatural force that's affecting your mind. Being Beloved won't protect you against that, any more than it would against the Mind Arcana.<br /> <br /> That said, I could see Beloved being Sleepwalkers, since the qualifications needed for Sleepwalking are actually rather low.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=875170#post875170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, a bonus to resisting Mind spells or Domination felt like a good way to emphasize both the insanity and the sheer faith that seem endemic in the Beloved condition.</div> </div> </div> </div> Like I said; a Fanatcism Merit available to Beloved and any other religious fanatics makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> I'm still debating wheather to make a Cult Merit that lets you get it in bulk or not (a Merit for individual PCs seems more appropriate for a book about playing cultists than a book about playing the thing they worship). Pro: It makes sense. Con: Cults are supposed to cause you trouble and create stories, this stops them from doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=875170#post875170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I'm the first to admit I'm a huge crossover nut.</div> </div> </div> </div> That makes one of us <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I don't like the thematic dilution of crossover myself. Though I'm fine with NPCs from other splats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=875170#post875170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">basically, if we include the option for crossing over</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a big if. I haven't even finished the corebook yet, and there's still a ton of work to do.<br /> <br /> I'm unlikely to start a whole second pile of work afterwords, but feel free to write it yourself if you like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=875170#post875170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My goal was to support those who'd want to crossover between Leviathan and the other splats</div> </div> </div> </div> Hence why we have different viewpoints. My goal was to attempt to accurately answer the question of &quot;how would these splats see each other&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=875170#post875170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted to say you have a point about there being non-antagonist Hunters. I just generally don't give a flying fig for Hunters, so it's very hard for me to think much about crossing over with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're really selling Hunters short. Look up The Office of the Lord Stewards for an example of how crossover friendly Hunters can be (Dreamcatchers, see my sig)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T02:46:16-07:00","id":875446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=875393#post875393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say it is a bit week. No fault to you, you're copying my... god awful mechanics style from 1E (it predates me, but that's no excuse for me continueing onwards).<br /> <br /> If you want to update it Lambant Eyes of Judgement would make a good guideline, think about other 2-4 should be compressed into one Depth, same for 5-6.<br /> <br /> That leaves you room for 3 completely seperate powers. For example, you might be able to tell significant events that happened in the local area by sensing the Resonance of ambient Essence.<br /> <br /> Or compress it all into a couple of Adaptations. That's probably how I'm going to handle Spirits cannonically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote it back in 1e very quickly. I don't know if I'll have the time to do it at the moment. I'm a bit busy with exams and such. I'll probably do an adaptation requiring a Vitality Channel which lets the Leviathan change into a spirit shape with all the advantages and drawbacks associated with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T04:07:41-07:00","id":875477,"title":"","content":"By the way, I looked in the chapter quotes folder and I couldn't see anything from The Kraken by Alfred Lord Tennyson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T04:55:39-07:00","id":875494,"title":"","content":"I might actually replace the Antagonists chapter quote (it's a bit long) with the last two or three lines. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In my googling I even found some theory that the Kraken is a metaphor for the subconcious, which makes it work double well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-27-2016, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:35:07-07:00","id":875562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=875393#post875393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said; a Fanatcism Merit available to Beloved and any other religious fanatics makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> I'm still debating wheather to make a Cult Merit that lets you get it in bulk or not (a Merit for individual PCs seems more appropriate for a book about playing cultists than a book about playing the thing they worship). Pro: It makes sense. Con: Cults are supposed to cause you trouble and create stories, this stops them from doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the drawback is: they're <i>Fanatical</i>. I could see an effective (Piety is it, that lets them act normal?) penalty. Less &quot;someone mind controlled me into causing trouble&quot; and more &quot;I can cause insane trouble all on my own. SKULLS AND TVs FOR GREG!&quot;. Not sure how topical it might be, but if the same &quot;resistance to mental influence or subverting them from their goals&quot; also applied even to their Leviathan god...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-27-2016, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T11:28:46-07:00","id":875795,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how to make that mechanically distinct to how Beloved usually are. The more I think about it, the more I think it's best to leave this as a Merit for PC cultists and not something Leviathans can buy for their cult. <hr /><br /> Anyway, I was a little board so in the spirit of Crossover, here Hunter Conspiracies and Wake vulnerability.<ul><li>Ascending Ones: Character's treat Elixir dots as the Virtue Merit while protected by an appropriate Elixir. (There isn't one in the books, but obviously the Ascending Ones would have a potion to protect their minds. Elixir of the Fiery Heart should provide some lesser protection, lets say it reduces the Wake penalty for Breaking Points) (In my WoD Alchemy/Divine Fire is Empyrean)</li> <li>Bastet's Beloved: Character's treat dots in Mantle of Bastet as the Virtue Merit. (In my WoD Bastet is Empyrean - in fact, if I say something counts as the Virtue Merit just assume it's related to the Empyrean in my WoD)</li> <li>Athenic Church: Character's treat dots in Devotion as the Virtue Merit.</li> <li>Hakollel shel Hamerkava: Anyone protected by El Elyon gains a honorary Virtue Merit equal to the speaker's Shemot dots. Elah Yerushelem can block the Wake.</li> <li>Hearth of Hestia: Hearthtending counts as a Virtue merit for all under it's protection.</li> <li>Malleus Maleficarum / Order of St Anthony: Character's treat Benediction dots as the Virtue Merit while protected by Epipodian Safeguard. The Blessed Protection of St. Agrippina can blocks the Wake.</li> <li>Office of the Lord Stewards: A successful use of Pact of Protection confers Wake immunity for the duration. Warding can block the Wake.</li> <li>Staff of Janus: I never wrote them an equivalent of the Blessed Protection of St. Agrippina. Pretend I did.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> Basically: the general rule is that if the Endowment is Empyrean and applies direct mental protection then it probably gets treated as the Virtue Merit. If it's Empyrean and the Endowment Merit can be reasonably described as a virtue, it counts as the Virtue Merit. If it's non-Empyrean and applies direct mental protection then it gets treated as Supernatural Tolerance. Area protection powers like the Blessed Protection of St. Agrippina work as normal, and block the Wake if the defences are strong enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-27-2016, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T08:55:15-07:00","id":876680,"title":"","content":"So, I noticed the Dream Worlds document in the folder. Basically, you are saying that Leviathans have an Oneiros (their Dreamworld) and the Rift is the Tribe's Temenos? But more fleshed out, as it were?<br /> <br /> I'm guessing this is more side-bar, add-on material, since it doesn't seem too relevant to most Leviathan actions?<br /> <br /> Why wouldn't Ahabs be in the Dreamworld, though? Aren't they still a part of the Leviathan's mind (albeit a self-destructive part)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T13:05:57-07:00","id":876902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=876680#post876680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I noticed the Dream Worlds document in the folder. Basically, you are saying that Leviathans have an Oneiros (their Dreamworld) and the Rift is the Tribe's Temenos? But more fleshed out, as it were?</div> </div> </div> </div> Pretty much.<br /> <br /> Unless you go for the theory that the Rift is Tiamat's - dead but dreaming - Oneiros.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=876680#post876680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing this is more side-bar, add-on material, since it doesn't seem too relevant to most Leviathan actions?</div> </div> </div> </div> The origonal was a sidebar, then it grew very long. I'm trying to think of ways to cut it back.<br /> <br /> I want it to be more &quot;Mage/Hunter/PC Primordial Thurgist plot hook here&quot; rather than an entire additonal element of a Leviathan game.<br /> <br /> And I really don't want it to be &quot;an entire additional element of a Leviathan game, which I'm telling you to ignore&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=876680#post876680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't Ahabs be in the Dreamworld, though? Aren't they still a part of the Leviathan's mind (albeit a self-destructive part)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahabs core power is the ability to attack a Leviathans mind. It seemed simpler all round if they didn't spend every night inside the Leviathan's mind.<br /> <br /> Especially if a Hunter/Mage ST comes up with a session where the PCs find and escort an Ahab into a Leviathan's Dream World so she can destroy the Leviathan. No questions about why the Ahab didn't already do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T13:21:23-07:00","id":876911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=876902#post876902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The origonal was a sidebar, then it grew very long. I'm trying to think of ways to cut it back.<br /> <br /> I want it to be more &quot;Mage/Hunter/PC Primordial Thurgist plot hook here&quot; rather than an entire additonal element of a Leviathan game.<br /> <br /> And I really don't want it to be &quot;an entire additional element of a Leviathan game, which I'm telling you to ignore&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think it is interesting enough to warrant further thought and development. I mean, Mage has the Astral, Shadow, and Underworld, which Mages <i>can</i> explore, though it is entirely optional. I could see this similarly - not all Leviathans will deal with this, but there is something there for those that do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=876902#post876902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahabs core power is the ability to attack a Leviathans mind. It seemed simpler all round if they didn't spend every night inside the Leviathan's mind.<br /> <br /> Especially if a Hunter/Mage ST comes up with a session where the PCs find and escort an Ahab into a Leviathan's Dream World so she can destroy the Leviathan. No questions about why the Ahab didn't already do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Ahabs might represent the more destructive forces in a Leviathan's Dream World. As for why they didn't Dream-Kill the Leviathan before? I could see it as a control issue - when the Ahab is in the Leviathan's dreamscape, they have no more control than any other dreamer. A Hunter/Mage/Changeling/Beast mission to get the Ahab into the Leviathan's mind could be more effective because doing it that way allows the Ahab to remain aware (Lucid Dreaming), and thus actually direct their damage.<br /> <br /> This would offer the incidental comparison - a Leviathan that minimizes the damage their Wake induces and has fewer (or no) Ahabs has a comparatively &quot;peaceful&quot; Dream World. One that abuses the Wake and has boat-loads of Ahabs after them has a Mordor-like Hellscape for a Dream World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-28-2016, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T02:28:26-07:00","id":877487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=876911#post876911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think it is interesting enough to warrant further thought and development. I mean, Mage has the Astral, Shadow, and Underworld, which Mages <i>can</i> explore, though it is entirely optional.</div> </div> </div> </div> The difference is that the Rift and dreamlands cover the same niche of investigating a charachter's mind. And the Rift does it better - since it also ties into highly relevent ideas like an ancestral homeland, or the layered Depths.<br /> <br /> Leviathan Dream mechanics are mostly there for non-Leviathan crossover (or Primoridal Thurgist games) where dream exploration is already an aspect and the Rift is not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=876911#post876911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Ahabs might represent the more destructive forces in a Leviathan's Dream World. As for why they didn't Dream-Kill the Leviathan before? I could see it as a control issue - when the Ahab is in the Leviathan's dreamscape, they have no more control than any other dreamer.</div> </div> </div> </div>For such a minor part of the game - keep it nice and simple. Ahabs don't exist in the dreamland, and destructive parts of the Leviathan's mind exist there independent of Ahabs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T08:32:30-07:00","id":879530,"title":"","content":"Today's update is Phronesis and Eunoia, the twin Integrity traits that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> proposed way back in the day.<br /> <br /> I had trouble posting the sample triggers, so you'll have to head over to the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11Cr2Af1VIZfvOOOJtCwAWTbhd4c-gO5R-pVbLn-atQY/edit#heading=h.6bmsfk2qmm25\" target=\"_blank\">Systems and Advantages doc for those</a>. Suggestions for triggers would be welcome.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Phronesis</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Phronesis is the ability to judge right from wrong, to know how to act and speak in a manner that\u2019s moral and socially appropriate. Phronesis is what makes the difference between a civilised thinking being, and an animal that can only act upon it\u2019s instincts. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thoughtless or savage actions risk Eroding Phronesis. With high Phronesis a Leviathan is in control of their actions and emotions, but as Phronesis Erodes they become passionate, instinctive, or \u201chot-headed\u201d. With Erosion they become little ore than a savage animal, a slave to their instincts barely capable of forming a chain of thought long enough to realise what they have become. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Phronesis chains the Leviathan\u2019s divine nature. As it falls the Leviathan becomes increasingly reliant upon their Undertow and inflicting havoc. If Phronesis is ever lost entirely, the Beastal Nature overwhelms the other two creating an Typhon. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Eunoia</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Eunoia is the ability to have another\u2019s interests at heart. In it\u2019s original context Eunoia referred to both the perception and fact of a speaker having the audience\u2019s interests at heart the relevance to a Leviathan speaking to their cult is self evident. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Acts that dominate or use others for one\u2019s own purposes risks Eroding Eunoia. A Leviathan with high Eunoia is able to perceive the desires of others and may choose to put another before themselves. As Eunoia Erodes a Leviathan develops sociopathic tendencies, with further Erosion they all but forget that people are thinking beings with their own interests, and are quite incapable of caring. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Eunoia chains the Leviathan\u2019s divine nature. As it falls the Leviathan becomes increasingly reliant upon their Upwelling and displays of dominance. If Eunoia is ever lost entirely, the Divine Nature overwhelms the other two creating an Opheon. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tranquility</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlike Phronesis and Eunoia which describe specific aspects of the Tribe\u2019s psychology, Tranquility does not actually exist within the world of Leviathan: the Tempest. When a Leviathan speaks of Tranquility, which they frequently do, the word is being used as a rough synonym for \u201chow well I\u2019m coping\u201d. When the game\u2019s rules refer to Tranquility, they simply mean the lower of Phronesis or Eunoia. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sidebar: Keeping it Simple.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Groups who don't want to track two separate traits can merge Phronesis and Eunoia into Tranquillity. Doing so will not create any serious problems with the mechanics, though you are encouraged to &quot;eyeball it&quot; and choose only one Phronesis or Eunoia drawbacks depending on which is more fitting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effects of Tranquility</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When a Leviathan erodes to Phronesis four or less they lose the ability to regain Ichor without indulging their beastal nature. Track any Ichor gained separately from the regular pool. When the Leviathan regains Willpower from their Undertow or regains Ichor from a Havoc check, afterwards they may regain Ichor like normal for the remainder of the scene. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Eunoia four a similar effect happens, and can be resolved by regaining Willpower from an Upwelling or Ichor from a Domination check. If both traits are at four or lower, each resolution provides access to half the Ichor gained in a scene. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Leviathan takes a -1 penalty to Composure rolls at Phronesis 4, which increases by one for each additional dot of Phronesis lost. The Beastal nature is svage and instinctual. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Leviathan takes a -1 penalty to Empathy, Persuasion and Socialise rolls non-divine individuals at Eunoia 4, which increases by one for each additional dot of Eunoia lost. The Leviathan finds begins to forget that mortal beings are more than just an extension of the gods they serve. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-01-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T11:05:57-07:00","id":880294,"title":"","content":"New Channel: The Hydra's Rebirth. I tried to add some alternative abilities in here but apart from the ability to heal others (with risk!) I couldn't think of any. All in all, this one's pretty close to 1E, but with more Adaptations.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Hydra's Rebirth (Descendant Channel)</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>A spark of unnatural life coruscates through the blood of the Tribe, its immense potency granting their very organs the ability to reproduce and evolve.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With this Channel a Leviathan can heal from injury in an instant. Cells divide at an astounding rate, the Leviathan\u2019s body pulls in extra dimensional mass, consumes foreign organisms or transcends time itself to use healed or not yet injured limbs. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Like the Hydra of myth, a Leviathan\u2019s wounds may be cauterised to prevent healing. If an electrically charged weapon is impaled within the Leviathan\u2019s form the wound it inflicted cannot be healed until the weapon is removed or it runs out of power. </span></span><ul><li><ul><li>[*=-1]<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: None</span></span><br /> [*=-1]<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action Type: Reflexive</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 1&quot;: Birthright of Fecundity</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 2&quot;: The Leviathan may expend 1 point of Ichor to heal Depth points of Bashing damage. If this removes the injuries that cause a Tilt, the Tilt is also healed. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 3&quot;: The Leviathan gains the ability to produce an Ichor saturated food or drink from it\u2019s body with miraculous healing powers (it\u2019s also a miracle cure for infertility, even menopause can be reversed). Consuming this, which must be done straight from the Leviathan\u2019s body, heals damage as though the Leviathan spent the same amount of Ichor on this Channel at their current Depth. Mortals and Lahmasu can benefit, Ahabs and Atolls will vomit it up without being affected. Other supernatural creatures are at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Divine Ichor is not safe for mortals, and even Lahmasu find the potency of a full Leviathan\u2019s ichor dangerous. At the end of a scene roll the total Ichor ingested (including wasted points) - Depth. If the roll results in more successes than the character's Genetic Conditions they take a new permanent (and inheritable, sometimes resulting in outright Lahmasu children) Genetic Condition. Hybrids are treated as having two less Genetic Conditions due to their unstable DNA, while the Healthy Genetics Mutation is counted as an extra Genetic Condition. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 4&quot;: You may expend 2 Ichor to heal half Depths (round up) points of Lethal damage.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively the Leviathan may spend 2 Ichor to purge their body of diseases, toxins or parasites (those rare few with enough supernatural power to harm a Leviathan). They spend 1 to 5 Ichor depending upon the severity, and if necessary make a Clash of Wills roll. If the Leviathan is touching someone they may roll Stamina + Intimidation vs Stamina + Supernatural Tolerance to transfer the intrusion into them. Otherwise it is expelled as an ephemeral Spirit and is free to do what it wishes (usually find someone, possibly the Leviathan again, and turn itself back into materium). </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 5&quot;: When attacked by a penetrative weapon, such as a spear or harpoon, the Leviathan may heal so quickly that the weapon is trapped within their body for digestion. This requires healing all the damage the weapon inflicted before it is removed from the Leviathan\u2019s body (usually one turn). Supernatural weapons usually require a Clash of Wills.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 6&quot;: Water is the element of life, and so long as the Leviathan is at least half submerged they can draw life from water, increasing their Safe Ichor per Turn by two points while using this Channel. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 7&quot;: You may expend 4 Ichor to heal 1 Aggravated level of damage. Every time you do so, increase any non-Stamina Attribute by one for the remainder of the scene. No more than (Stamina + Sheol) Dots of extra Attributes may be active at once.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Adaptations</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aggressive Assimilation (OOO): In Depth 4 or below the Leviathan can convert Lethal or Aggravated damage into Ichor at a 2:1 ratio. Any Ichor gained in this fashion vanishes at the end of the turn and can only be spent on The Hydra\u2019s Rebirth, excluding Adaptations. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blessings of the Chirurgeon God (OOO - O): When using the Depth 3 iteration of this channel The Leviathan may produce sustenance that can be preserved for Sheol days and always acts as though the Leviathan was in Depth 7. They must pay one point of Willpower per dose created, but a dose can contain as much Ichor as they wish and cannot be divided. Once the Willpower is spent it takes about an hour before the dose is ready. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With Golden Hair (O): Any person healed by the Depth 3 iteration of this Channel, including by Blessings of the Chirurgeon God, is treated as having Intimate Knowledge of the Leviathan for as long as the Leviathan remains in their system (about 33 hours on average).</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dionysian Relief (O): In Depth 1 or lower the Leviathan can spend a point of Ichor to cure a hangover. This Adaptation is rare, given the enormous quantities of alcohol needed to get a Leviathan drunk most don\u2019t bother or only drink for the taste. However Leviathans that take the edge of their condition with alcohol drink like the gods of old, and consider a point of Ichor to be a bargain for escaping the consequences. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resurgent Corpus (OO): You may expend a point of Willpower to treat your Dexterity as equal to your Stamina for the purposes of Defense. This lasts a scene.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dread Return (OOO, requires Sheol 3): That is not dead which can eternal lie. This Adaptation costs a dot of permanent Willpower to express and may be activated at any point after your health track is filled with Lethal damage, including after death. Doing so causes the Leviathan to fall into a trance-like stasis that appears, to any observer, just like death. During this state the Leviathan is dreaming, will not bleed out and heals damage at the standard human rate, but must spend 1, 2 or 4 Ichor per point of Bashing, Lethal or Aggravated damage. Until you recover you may only regain Ichor through the worship of your cult. If your body is fully annihilated (by incineration or some other means), you are truly dead.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Phylactery (OOO, OOOOO, requires Dread Return, Sheol equal to dots): With Dread Return the Leviathan reforms from the largest part of their body, but with this Adaptation they develop a specific organ, unique for each Leviathan that serves as the focus of their reincarnation. The phylactorial organ is Size 1, and grows to Size Sheol in Apotheosis. If the organ is destroyed without killing the Leviathan then this Adaptation is nullified until the organ is healed. The practical effect of this Adaptation is that the Leviathan can rip out their own Phylactery and throw it to safety. This fills their health track with Aggravated damage, but your still beating heart sinking to the bottom of the ocean is better than leaving your body to regenerate right next to the Marduk agent who killed you and knows to disintegrate the body. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The five dot version increases the time a Leviathan can survive without their phylactorial organ from just long enough to hurl it into the distance to Sheol hours. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan must split Ichor between their body and their phylactery. Their body cannot regain Ichor in any way after the separation. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reap the Whirlwind (OOOOO, requires Sheol 5): Once per week, when you would be slain in combat as a result of filling your rightmost Health box with Aggravated Damage, instead you are restored to maximum Health and Ichor and reflexively shift to Apotheosis Form. The Transformation takes it\u2019s usual time, but during this time you instantly heal all damage. This change is not optional but does not cost Ichor. Distribute (Stamina + Sheol) dots among your Attributes as if you had healed all the aggravated damage with Ichor. Among younger members of the Tribe, this Adaptation is sometimes affectionately referred to as &quot;One-Winged Angel.&quot;</span></span></li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And here's Mortal Devouring Armoury. I'm trying something new for this one, to emphasise the diversity of the Tribe's biology, I think it works - obviously there's lots of room for expansion, once I reread Hurt Locker's weaponry rules. Feel free to suggest stuff.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Leviathan's Primordial form bristles with cruel natural weapons.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In Depth 1 the Leviathan gets 1L Damage natural weapons. In Depth 2-6 they gain one armoury dot to apply various upgrades to their natural weaponry and in Apotheosis they gain 4 armoury dots. A Leviathan may gain no advantage at a particular Depth in order to buy a more expensive upgrade later, The upgrades are chosen when purchasing this Channel, and decisions are permanent. However the Leviathan may redesign their armoury every time they raise Sheol. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Armoury dot may provide: </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Damage (O, stacks to a maximum of 7)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The weapon inflicts Aggravated damage (OOO)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The weapon\u2019s damage is treated as +2 against grappled targets (O)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Armour piercing 2 (O, stacks to a maximum of 14)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+2 to Brawl rolls (O, stacks to a maximum of 14) </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Treat damage as 2 higher for the purposes of inflicting Tilts (O, stacks to a maximum of 14 )</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reduce penalties for called shots by 3 (O)</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Adaptations</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weapons of the Hybrid (OOO): The Leviathan gains an additional armory dot at Depth 3.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weapons of the Monster (OO): The Leviathan gains an additional armory dot at Depth 5.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weapons of the God (O): The Leviathan gains an additional armory dot at Depth 7.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-02-2016, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:25:36-07:00","id":880347,"title":"","content":"I have to say, Dionysian Relief gave me quite a laugh when I read it. The rest looks really good. I'm looking forward to being able to play the final version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:35:40-07:00","id":880358,"title":"","content":"Hehe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I got the idea from John's Scion Resources. I've been mining that to get ideas for appropriately godly powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T07:09:45-07:00","id":880947,"title":"","content":"So... Mage 2E is released tomorrow. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a> when do you think we might see some of the Ritual rules? Obviously you'd need to read through them first, then iron out what they inspire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T07:29:57-07:00","id":880964,"title":"","content":"It seems people are quite excited for Rituals.<br /> <br /> The general framework should be fairly simple and I can probably reuse some of my 1E notes, the hard part would be defining what each Vestige can do at each dot.<br /> <br /> My plan is for 1-5 to be roughly on the level of Mage (ritual not instant casting), even casting a 6 dot ritual would require high Zea and a Long Term Aspiration just to get enough supplies. A 7 dot Ritual is basically impossible without The Stars Being Right (aka, the storyteller allowing it) and mostly exist as plot points for stop the ritual quests.<br /> <br /> Though if you want to play on past the point where a seven dot ritual is enacted then sure. No reason why you can't play after the entire Eastern cost of the USA is underwater and world governments have gone on mission of extermination with Marduk tech or rewind time so the entire Middle East is thrown back to the Neolithic and an impenetrable dome blocks non-Leviathan from travelling between modern Earth and the neolithic middle east, for some nice Sundered World crossover (with airplaines flying overhead).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-03-2016, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T09:03:53-07:00","id":881026,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I remember there was a table/side-bar regarding &quot;Godzilla rules&quot; in 1E. Are those going to be ported over, or redesigned? Are they (or did they) use the &quot;Scale&quot; concept in the Mage Chronicler's Guide?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T09:48:54-07:00","id":881054,"title":"","content":"I think I got MCG just to see if it's scale concept could make a replacement for the godzilla rules and found they just didn't work. They were narrativist where the godzilla rules were supposed to be simulationist.<br /> <br /> The WoD is mostly simulationist with a few asides to narrativism; but the various CG presented ways to break that. You could do it in a Leviathan Chronicler's Guide but not a corebook. <br /> <br /> Godzilla rules are really hard because the WoD size rules are AWFUL; and in all this time I can't really think of any better solution than the 1E godzilla rules, so at some point I'll just copy and paste them over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T10:45:56-07:00","id":881091,"title":"","content":"Where were they, by the way? I was looking through the <a href=\"https://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/LeviathanTempest:CompilationProject\" target=\"_blank\">Compilation</a>, and couldn't find it at a glance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T11:30:02-07:00","id":881115,"title":"","content":"Here you go: <a href=\"https://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/LeviathanTempest:ChapterThree#Exceptional_Size\" target=\"_blank\">https://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/Levia...ceptional_Size</a><br /> <br /> Somebody has been editing the compilation for a while but that bit's unedited I think. I have no idea who's doing it and they're welcome to it but I wish they'd said hi. I could have invited them here to share ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:32:50-07:00","id":881173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=881115#post881115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here you go: <a href=\"https://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/LeviathanTempest:ChapterThree#Exceptional_Size\" target=\"_blank\">https://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/Levia...ceptional_Size</a><br /> <br /> Somebody has been editing the compilation for a while but that bit's unedited I think. I have no idea who's doing it and they're welcome to it but I wish they'd said hi. I could have invited them here to share ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did a bit a while ago. are you talking about adding a couple of descriptions for the pictures? Like the one at the beginning of the Sytems and advantages chapter? Um.. here it is<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">[PICTURE: Full page. A stone wall takes up the majority of the picture and most of that is covered by algae, coral and barnacles. Strands of bladderwrack seaweed wave in front of the sides. Of the wall itself, all is visible is an irregular section in the centre where most of the algae has been cleared, revealing a relief image that depicts a large, staring eye set in the centre of a circular maw replete with jagged triangular teeth. The lines of the relief glimmer faintly with a sickly green light and points of the same light can be seen beneath the barnacles, suggesting that the design continues beneath them. Looking at the wall are three silhouetted figures. One is obviously human and is wearing full scuba gear. To the left of the scuba diver is another figure viewed in profile. It wears no clothing bar a loincloth that appears to be made of seaweed. It has a human shape (two arms, two legs, one head etc) but in place of hair it has a set of quills reminiscent of a porcupine's which continue down its back in a kind of mane. Its mouth extends almost to its ears and is filled with needle-like teeth. A long, thin black tongue darts from between the fangs. On the left of the scuba diver is a figure that is not human at all. It resembles a gigantic eel with black skin and no eyes. Its tail extends beyond the edge of the picture. From behind its head extend four tentacles, two of which are holding what appears to be a crude human-sized idol beneath the thing's body. The other pair are held above its head. All of the tentacles are covered in lidless silver eyes with neither pupil nor iris.]</span></span></span> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sorry for not asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T13:34:43-07:00","id":881225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=881115#post881115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here you go: <a href=\"https://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/LeviathanTempest:ChapterThree#Exceptional_Size\" target=\"_blank\">https://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/Levia...ceptional_Size</a><br /> <br /> Somebody has been editing the compilation for a while but that bit's unedited I think. I have no idea who's doing it and they're welcome to it but I wish they'd said hi. I could have invited them here to share ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. The damage division part is what I was thinking fit from the MCG. Only problem I see with the Exceptional Size rules as they stand is for those cases when the weaponry used doesn't match the size (smaller opponents with weaponry designed for greater damage or larger targets, and larger opponents with weaponry designed for, perhaps multiple, smaller foes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T14:24:02-07:00","id":881264,"title":"","content":"There's text saying you can increase the weaponry's size by one if it's designed for larger targets. In 2E I'll be more flexible, and just say something like &quot;however there is a limit to how much power mundane engineering can pack into a small size. Most weapons designed to take down an exceptionally large creature are sizable themselves&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=881173#post881173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did a bit a while ago. are you talking about adding a couple of descriptions for the pictures?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I was referring to an extra Awareness Channel I noticed when I last looked.<br /> <br /> Awesome picture though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T14:37:31-07:00","id":881270,"title":"","content":"Do you mean Sight Beyond Sight? That was mine, I think (it was quite a while ago and my memory's not the best). You're welcome to use any of the material there if you want to. <br /> <br /> Thanks for what you said about the picture The Kings Raven <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:45:24-07:00","id":881320,"title":"","content":"So it was you who defiled the sacred number 7 ;p","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:18:44-07:00","id":882226,"title":"","content":"So I've been brainstorming Rituals with the awesome <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"148\" data-vbnamecard=\"148\">PenDragon</a> - lots of good ideas and have a solid design now. Sadly, got a bit of a busy period coming up but hopefully I'll have something sooner or later. A little teaser though, we've settled on the idea that Leviathans are very good at giving Blessings. Mechanically this is mostly extra Attribute/Skill dots or Hybrid Mutations - they won't turn you into a Hybird or Deviant (usually) but they'll have other drawbacks.<br /> <br /> This is of course in addition to summoning rain and the other expected godly tricks. Vestiges will double as Arcana. So summoning a rainstorm is Elements, giving a mortal the power to summon rain is also Elements (ok, that's too powerful for a blessing but the general idea is that if you can do something you can also bless mortals to do similar things on a smaller scale)<br /> <br /> The Dots go <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Discover</li> <li>Strengthen</li> <li>Ruin</li> <li>Control</li> <li>Create</li> <li>???</li> <li>Plot points</li> </ol><br /> <br /> If anyone has ideas for the 6th dot or individual Ritual's now is the time for it. Unlike the poor saps who have to print their books, I have no such thing as word count limits <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:28:46-07:00","id":882241,"title":"","content":"Could 6 be the ability to change natural laws within a specific area, literally remaking the world to fit your vision? Like using Sanctity to make it do that (within the area) defiance of the Leviathan's will is, unquestionably, a sin in the same way that killing a baby is a sin. Or Fecundity to make it so that birth within the confines of the Ritual is impossible without the Leviathan's blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:31:46-07:00","id":882243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=882226#post882226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Discover</li> <li>Strengthen</li> <li>Ruin</li> <li>Control</li> <li>Create</li> <li>???</li> <li>Plot points</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>6. 1-5, but <i>more</i>? You already stated that Rituals <i>can</i> invest mortals with power, otherwise I'd put that at 6. Maybe giving out minor/micro templates? Modifying Leviathan (and, optionally, other splat) abilities themselves?<br /> <br /> The <i>easy</i> way to do it would be to map the abilities roughly to what Influences from Spirits/Ghosts/Angels/etc. can do. I mean, isn't that basically what the Ritual is doing anyways, through the medium of ceremony and the Leviathan's Divine power?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-04-2016, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T23:19:25-07:00","id":882598,"title":"","content":"You haven't noticed that it is roughly based on infleunces <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Manipulate and Control were merged. Mass Create and Create were merged. Discover and Ruin were added. And a few things were swapped around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=882241#post882241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could 6 be the ability to change natural laws within a specific area</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Enforce&quot;. I like the sound of that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T04:26:07-07:00","id":882761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=879530#post879530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Phronesis chains the Leviathan\u2019s divine nature. As it falls the Leviathan becomes increasingly reliant upon their Undertow and inflicting havoc. If Phronesis is ever lost entirely, the Beastal Nature overwhelms the other two creating an Typhon. </span></span><br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Eunoia chains the Leviathan\u2019s divine nature. As it falls the Leviathan becomes increasingly reliant upon their Upwelling and displays of dominance. If Eunoia is ever lost entirely, the Divine Nature overwhelms the other two creating an Opheon. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>What happens if both Phronesis and Eunoia are lost at the same time?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T04:37:52-07:00","id":882768,"title":"","content":"The odds of that are pretty much zero, since Phronesis and Eunoia are lost through completely opposite kinds of action. If it happens, just pick whichever one you think is appropriate and say that one happened first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T07:14:17-07:00","id":882839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=882768#post882768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The odds of that are pretty much zero, since Phronesis and Eunoia are lost through completely opposite kinds of action.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't be a beastial, destructive god uncaring for the lives of others?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T07:59:47-07:00","id":882868,"title":"","content":"You can't be a clinical manipulative schemer and a savage unthinking animal at the same time.<br /> <br /> (A Leviathan with low scores in both Phronesis and Eunoia would be constantly swinging from one extreme to the other)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-05-2016, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T09:28:17-07:00","id":882919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=882868#post882868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't be a clinical manipulative schemer and a savage unthinking animal at the same time.<br /> <br /> (A Leviathan with low scores in both Phronesis and Eunoia would be constantly swinging from one extreme to the other)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh? I thought Eunoia merely measured how well you can recognize others as being &quot;people&quot; rather than toys for you to play with. Didn't know it mandated clinical manipulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T11:21:15-07:00","id":883049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=882768#post882768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The odds of that are pretty much zero, since Phronesis and Eunoia are lost through completely opposite kinds of action. If it happens, just pick whichever one you think is appropriate and say that one happened first.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=882868#post882868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't be a clinical manipulative schemer and a savage unthinking animal at the same time.<br /> <br /> (A Leviathan with low scores in both Phronesis and Eunoia would be constantly swinging from one extreme to the other)</div> </div> </div> </div>To my mind, that suggests the double Integrity traits aren't the right model after all. You really want Tranquility to work like Harmony in Werewolf 2e - Typhon is the 0 point, Opheon is the 10 point, and being functional among humans is the 5 point. Leviathans don't shift Tranquility with Experiences; instead those close to becoming Typhons have to control themselves or their environment to push back to balance, and those close to becoming Opheons have to release their passions, or care for something beyond its usefulness for gaining power.<br /> <br /> The names Phronesis and Eunoia can be used for anchors, the Leviathan version of Vampire's Mask/Dirge and Werewolf's Blood/Bone, replacing Virtue and Vice.<br /> <br /> And yes, a psyche in which &quot;rational&quot; equates to &quot;sociopathic&quot; and &quot;loving&quot; equates to &quot;savagely bestial&quot; bears little resemblance to humanity. But that's an advantage here; Leviathans <i>aren't</i> human, physically or mentally - they just learn to pass for human. An Integrity analog that encodes a Blue-and-Orange moral axis emphasizes just how alien this class of being really is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:25:09-07:00","id":883200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=882919#post882919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh? I thought Eunoia merely measured how well you can recognize others as being &quot;people&quot; rather than toys for you to play with. Didn't know it mandated clinical manipulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eunoia doesn't mandate clinical manipulation, but Eunoia chains the divine nature when the divine nature is free and active, it tends towards being a manipulative schemer.<br /> <br /> There's a rule that with low Eunoia you must either use Domination or regain willpower through your Upwelling to regain Ichor. Once Upwellings are written it should be a bit clearer where the whole clinical manipulation thing comes from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=883049#post883049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my mind, that suggests the double Integrity traits aren't the right model after all. You really want Tranquility to work like Harmony in Werewolf 2e - Typhon is the 0 point, Opheon is the 10 point, and being functional among humans is the 5 point. Leviathans don't shift Tranquility with Experiences; instead those close to becoming Typhons have to control themselves or their environment to push back to balance, and those close to becoming Opheons have to release their passions, or care for something beyond its usefulness for gaining power.</div> </div> </div> </div> That would break the mechanic where Schools restore Phronesis and Eunoia, which is probably <i>the single most important mechanic in the game</i>.<br /> <br /> It would also ruin my planned mechanics for making Rituals feel appropraitely lovecraftian and the idea that harmony is halfway between the Beast and Divine nature doesn't even make any sense when you know what. What exactly is halfway between &quot;The Weaver of Fate&quot; and &quot;an ambush preditor&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=883049#post883049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The names Phronesis and Eunoia can be used for anchors, the Leviathan version of Vampire's Mask/Dirge and Werewolf's Blood/Bone, replacing Virtue and Vice.</div> </div> </div> </div> Leviathan's version of Blood/Bone are Upwelling and Undertow.<br /> <br /> What is your Divine Nature and what is your bestal nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-05-2016, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:29:59-07:00","id":883205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=883200#post883200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leviathan's version of Blood/Bone are Upwelling and Undertow.<br /> <br /> What is your Divine Nature and what is your bestal nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mis-quoted, there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:41:25-07:00","id":883216,"title":"","content":"And fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T16:36:58-07:00","id":883288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=883200#post883200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would break the mechanic where Schools restore Phronesis and Eunoia, which is probably <i>the single most important mechanic in the game</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? If each School provides a difficult but reliable way to shift away from either extreme, doesn't that serve the same function as restoring either Phronesis or Eunoia?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=883200#post883200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would also ruin my planned mechanics for making Rituals feel appropraitely lovecraftian and the idea that harmony is halfway between the Beast and Divine nature doesn't even make any sense when you know what. What exactly is halfway between &quot;The Weaver of Fate&quot; and &quot;an ambush preditor&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what exactly is a creature who's both &quot;The Weaver of Fate&quot; and &quot;an ambush predator&quot;?<br /> <br /> See, I can't quite wrap my head around the idea of a Leviathan who's low in both Phronesis and Eunoia. As so far presented that would be someone who constantly acts impulsively, killing people and breaking things for no clear reason, and also controls his Cult with an iron will, directing them like chess pieces to purposes beyond their understanding. And I don't see how you can have both; the two mindsets aren't compatible. If a Leviathan can control his thoughts well enough to give coherent directions to his worshippers, he can also control them enough to suppress violent impulses that don't serve his plans.<br /> <br /> As for Rituals, most of Lovecraft's Elder Gods are Typhons, but Nyarlathotep is an Opheon. Summoning a typical Elder God is basically setting off a nuke or starting a plague. Summoning Nyarlathotep just lets you start bargaining with him. Those are two very different atmospheres - which one do you want to emulate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T20:16:15-07:00","id":883426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=883288#post883288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I can't quite wrap my head around the idea of a Leviathan who's low in both Phronesis and Eunoia. As so far presented that would be someone who constantly acts impulsively, killing people and breaking things for no clear reason, and also controls his Cult with an iron will, directing them like chess pieces to purposes beyond their understanding. And I don't see how you can have both; the two mindsets aren't compatible. If a Leviathan can control his thoughts well enough to give coherent directions to his worshippers, he can also control them enough to suppress violent impulses that don't serve his plans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically not incompatible: The Leviathan might be coldly calculating in the comforts of their own temple, but throw destructive temper tantrums at the slightest personal resistance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T00:07:42-07:00","id":883529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=883288#post883288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? If each School provides a difficult but reliable way to shift away from either extreme, doesn't that serve the same function as restoring either Phronesis or Eunoia?</div> </div> </div> </div> If it's difficult and simply going for a breaking point is easy; no it doesn't serve the same function. Schools are supposed to be the primary way to restore Tranquillity.<br /> <br /> Stagnation is core to the game, Schools are how Leviathans (try to) fight Stagnation. Reducing their importance like this is a no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=883288#post883288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, what exactly is a creature who's both &quot;The Weaver of Fate&quot; and &quot;an ambush predator&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div> Messed up in the head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=883288#post883288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I can't quite wrap my head around the idea of a Leviathan who's low in both Phronesis and Eunoia. As so far presented that would be someone who constantly acts impulsively, killing people and breaking things for no clear reason, and also controls his Cult with an iron will, directing them like chess pieces to purposes beyond their understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div> An extreme case of mood swings, outright split personalities, or what Vent0 said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=883288#post883288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Rituals, most of Lovecraft's Elder Gods are Typhons, but Nyarlathotep is an Opheon. Summoning a typical Elder God is basically setting off a nuke or starting a plague. Summoning Nyarlathotep just lets you start bargaining with him. Those are two very different atmospheres - which one do you want to emulate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would Leviathan rituals summon gods? Leviathans are gods, and the only higher-tier gods Leviathans are likely to worship are the Progenitors who're dead (if they ever existed in the first place) and thus cannot be summoned.<br /> <br /> Leviathan Rituals are dedicated to themselves. You can see an outline a page ago.<br /> <br /> (And no, Progenitors aren't &quot;dead but dreaming&quot;. Leviathans can do that, but whatever killed the Progenitors killed them all the way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T05:02:57-07:00","id":884552,"title":"","content":"So. &quot;Where are the Rituals&quot; is probably the question I got asked the most, and thus I'm pleased to announce: Another Elements Channel<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This is the earth channel. And it's secondary associations are Fertility and Death - since I didn't think I could get enough out of either by themselves. (For those keeping count, there's still &quot;Space/geometry&quot; and Sky to go.<br /> <br /> BTW, if anyone can think of an additional effect for Depth 4 please say.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Unchained Heart of the World (Descendent Channel)</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>A Leviathan can be a being that supports life. Its immense form breaks the unending waters, supporting temples and farms upon its back; but should its monstrous form move in anger the streets quake and spires fall.</i></span></span><ul><li><ul><li>[*=-1]<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: Strength + Brawl + Sheol</span></span><br /> [*=-1]<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action Type: Instant</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 1</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Birthright of Elements</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 2</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Leviathan may spend a point of Ichor and express this Channel vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance to hit someone with a \u201clittle earthquake\u201d. If the Leviathan wins in combat the roll apply the Knocked Down Tilt, outside of combat apply whichever Condition is an appropriate response for the target. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively the Leviathan may express this Channel to shake the ground. This is not enough to cause any serious damage, at most it might knock small items down. But it is loud and applies the Rumbling Tilt. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 3:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Leviathan may command the earth to rise up and imprison his foes, the target must be standing on soil or rock. Roll this Channel vs Strength + Supernatural Tolerance. Success applies the Immobilized Tilt. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 4</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Leviathan may spend two Ichor to express this Channel and apply the Earthquake Tilt in an area with a diameter of Sheol*10 feet. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively the Leviathan may unearth the dead. Target the spot where a corpse is buried and roll this Channel. If there isn\u2019t actually a corpse present the result automatically fails. If the target has no Ghost the corpse rises as a mindless zombie. If the corpse has a ghost somewhere on Earth, including in twilight, the Ghost may spend one Essence to inhabit it\u2019s old body. If the Ghost is in the Upper Reaches of the Underworld then it requires three successes to reach her and applies the Underworld Gate condition as the Leviathan\u2019s power breaks into the Underworld itself. Every River the Ghost has crossed requires an additional two Successes. The Leviathan may roll Eunoia to reduce his successes as per the sidebar: Enslave the Gods. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 5</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The earth is connected to the cycle of death and rebirth, and the Leviathan\u2019s divine presence reminds mankind of these primordial bloody truths. If the Leviathan\u2019s Earthquake opens six or more feet of Earth, whether a large crack tears through the ground or a cellar door simply bursts open, the Underworld Gate Condition is applied. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition any ground plowed by the Leviathan\u2019s Earthquake becomes supernaturally fecund, if appropriately fertilised. Blood from humans, Hybrids or similar sources becomes as potent as strongest artificial fertilisers. If a character sacrifices someone to the Leviathan with the intent of using their blood as fertilizer upon ground plowed by the earthquake then it\u2019s potency is unmatched: A single drop will cause a stalk of corn to grow from a seed to full sized in seconds or produce a piece of fruit when applied to the roots of a mature tree.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Finally the Leviathan\u2019s Beloved now share her immunity to Tilts created by this Channel.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 6 </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">:The Leviathan's ability to shake the earth expands to truly prodigious levels. Tilts created by this Channel expand to cover the Leviathan's Wake. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Depth 7</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Leviathan may create an Earthquake of truly epic proportions, collapsing buildings, tearing apart the earth, and applying the Tartarian Vengeance Tilt. Unless stated otherwise, any of the more unusual effects of a Leviathan\u2019s Earthquake also apply to Tartarian Vengeance. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Adaptations</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Salting the Earth (OOO): The Leviathan may reverse the effects of the Depth 5 iteration of this channel, cursing the land so that nothing will grow. This Adaptation is rare, as the salt water floods created by Echos of the Deluge are equally effective at destroying farmland. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Kin of the Conqueror Worm (OOOOO, Requires Sheol 3): In Depth 7 The Leviathan\u2019s Earthquakes collapse the tunnels of the Underworld, sealing death itself. Any Avernian Gateways in the affected area are destroyed (but may be repaired). Rock falls or similar within the Underworld seal them off and the Strange Aeons Tilt is applied. The Tribe\u2019s grapevine has vague tales of beings attracted by a Leviathan tampering with the natural order, but the Tribe don\u2019t fear these \u201creapers\u201d. As Leviathan\u2019s like to say, in strange aeons, even death may die to a Leviathan\u2019s claws. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unburied Secrets (OO): In Depth 5 or below the Leviathan\u2019s earthquake breaks open deceptions and unearths the past, applying the Unburied Secrets Tilt. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tilt Strange Aeons (Environmental)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For Sheol weeks anyone within the affected area cannot die properly, instead becoming a Ghost trapped within their own decaying (and probably excruciatingly painful body). If their body is burnt or otherwise destroyed they become a Ghost. When the effect ends, or when affected characters leave the affected area, they pass on to their afterlife or remain as a ghost depending on the circumstances of their life, death, and afterlife.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tilt Unburied Secrets (Environmental)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any mundane attempts to investigate something that has been intentionally hidden, from simple adultery and political corruption, all the way up to occult conspiracies, gains a bonus equal to the Leviathan\u2019s Ripple penalty. Physical evidence that has been intentionally destroyed may even be dredged up from the Underworld to be found in some unlikely place. No bonus is applied to searching online, the closest this power will come is returning a laptop that was physically destroyed. And if the data was deleted first it will need to be sent to a data retrieval specialist or someone with supernatural powers more suited for working with modern technology.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Naturally no benefit applies if the secret you\u2019re investigating has no connection to the area affected by the Tilt. </span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Messing with you all. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1f-xnfJTnCPdJAlYX1fdyHdfqCMdR3rQuWjpmKyPKcjU/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the outline for Rituals</a>. It has everything except the actual powers themselves (which will be written up like Mage rotes, complete with extra effects for Reach/Ardour).<br /> <br /> Unlike Mage I'm using Ardour rather than dicepools as the base trait. The general idea for the Ritual economy is that the more trouble a Leviathan brings upon themselves the more power they get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T08:39:37-07:00","id":884648,"title":"","content":"Just a quick note that I've updated Primordial Theurgist with some fluff on how they use Rituals. It turns out the mechanics didn't need any changes (except how to translate Eunioa Erosion into Breaking Points, which is now in the Rituals doc in a sidebar).<br /> <br /> Empyrean Theurgist on the other hand will need alternative sources of Ardour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:14:15-07:00","id":885691,"title":"","content":"The &quot;freedom of religion&quot; bit under Profanities is kind of abstract -- an explanation for why that has any effect would be helpful. (I might also suggest saying something about the <i>de facto</i> state of affairs rather than the <i>de jure </i>-- if the Leviathan enacts a Profanity in a nation with freedom of religion, in a suburb where a specific religion is &quot;more equal than others&quot; and adherents of others are shamed, vilified, etc., I figure that would count as a lack of freedom of religion regardless of the legal technicalities.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:27:57-07:00","id":885707,"title":"","content":"Basically if you put up flyers about your Ritual that's one Ardour. But in some countries flyers will be enough for the police to go after you for following the non-state religion. In other countries you'll only get Flagged.<br /> <br /> So same action = same Ardour everywhere. But depending on where you are, the reaction from the mortals nearby will be different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:42:01-07:00","id":885713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=885707#post885707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically if you put up flyers about your Ritual that's one Ardour. But in some countries flyers will be enough for the police to go after you for following the non-state religion. In other countries you'll only get Flagged.<br /> <br /> So same action = same Ardour everywhere. But depending on where you are, the reaction from the mortals nearby will be different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I understand the reasons why it works, but it might be useful to clarify that in the text, plus the exceptions -- i.e., if you're in a nation where there's no freedom of religion, but the local law barely enforces that and can't be arsed to go after you for leaflets, you'll get the standard Condition, vs. the nation where there's de jure freedom of religion but local law enforcement will invent an offence and go after you for it if you advertise yourself as a member of the Church of Weird Fish. The current phrasing makes it seem more like a metaphysical effect than a social one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T23:58:21-07:00","id":885993,"title":"","content":"It is done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T01:11:59-07:00","id":887974,"title":"","content":"Here's the fluff and a mechanics explaining what Leviathan vs Leviathan conflict look like. (Note, these rules apply to Opheons but not Typhons).<br /> <br /> <br /> The Tribe face conflict with each other all the time. Whether it's secluded waterfront property, Heirlooms, control over isolated towns, or the attention of Atolls, Leviathans share very specific needs, often the supply is limited. There's isn't enough room for two big fish in a small pond. Those who have must defend themselves from the have nots, and the have nots often find the easiest way is to take from the haves.<br /> <br /> When they're not fighting over resources the Tribe fight over theology or morality. A Tranquil Leviathan may object to a tyrannical deposit or horrific occult experimentation upon cultists. Two equally monstrous Leviathans might find themselves disgusted by the form of the other's evil. Theologically, a contradicting view on the Progenitors can be the cause belli for war. It often doesn't matter if both Leviathans made it up a month ago, a Leviathan might let a slight against genuine primordial truth slide but feel compelled to defend a self affirming lie least they can no longer convince themselves.<br /> <br /> Both the Leviathan's Bestial and Divine natures are instinctively opposed to the idea of Transforming and charging in a trashing maelstrom of teeth and claws, while the human nature is usually the least violent of the three. Like an animal the Bestial nature knows how to fight without escalating to any real risk of harm, and it instinctively prefers to loose than to risk injury or death. The divine nature also avoids direct combat, but for different natures. The Tribe's primordial divinity is expressed through power and dominance, the divine nature wants it's foes to remain alive and aware that they have lost, that they are lesser than it. Being so heavily dominated by their instincts conflicts between Leviathans follow predictable patterns and can be decided into three forms, with numerous subdivisions.<br /> <br /> The first and simplest form is simply talking it out. If the Leviathans are on good terms they may meet in person, often mixing conversation with animal like threat displays or pitting their cults against each other in contests. If things are tense they may use telepathy, text messaging, send Beloved back and forth with letters or some other way of keeping things peaceful through distance. The more tense things are the more impersonal the conversation becomes.<ul><li>Use the social manoeuvring rules. Bonus dice may be applied if your cultists win the contest, your messenger is wearing ostentatious displays of wealth, if you've transformed into a more powerful body than your opponent. A more distant method of communication provides fewer or no opportunities for modifiers, but unless things are tense insisting on text messaging is likely to be taken as an insult.</li> <li>The looser may give the winner what they want, offer an alternative, or they may Escalate. Escalation resets both parties Doors, but the winner gains an extra Door for the remainder of the conflict. If a conflict Escalates multiple times, extra Doors stack and both parties retain any extra Doors until the conflict is resolved. Note that Escalation does not have to be to the next stage, nor does it have to wait until the final Door is opened. Any Leviathan can go as far as they wish, whenever they wish.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> The second and most common form of Leviathan conflict is fighting through their Cults and spiteful sabotage. Beloved are sent to steal from the other Leviathan, to interfere with their plans, or sent battles. The aim of these is to say \u201clook, I am stronger, don't let this turn into a real fight, because you'd loose\u201d. Players who wish to get into their character\u2019s headspace could try thinking of it as a particularly vicious divorce where the aim is simply to punish the other party.<ul><li>In this stage Leviathans open their rival's Doors by making a successful Fervour or Piety action to directly challenge their rival. If the two Cults come into direct conflict and the aggressor wins a Door opens. Alternatively if a Leviathan faces a significant setback to an Aspiration and their rival can demonstrate responsibility a Door opens.</li> <li>As before Leviathans have the opportunity to Escalate the conflict instead of admitting defeat. They may either move to the third and final stage, alternatively they can just advance through the subdivisions. Those subdivisions are:<ul><li>Non-violent but hostile conflict. E.G. Destroying that Heirloom your rival is looking for.</li> <li>Involving mortal society. E.G. Telling a Beloved's parent where to find their child.</li> <li>Non-lethal violence between cultists. E.G. Having your Beloved break into their Beloved's home and administer a beating.</li> <li>Non-lethal violence targeted against a Leviathan's sane friends, family, or favourites among non-combatant Beloved.</li> <li>Potentially lethal violence between your cults: E.G. Pitched battles in the streets of Insmouth. Your Beloved look for opportunities to knife their cultists in dark alleyways without the alerting the police.</li> <li>Potentially lethal violence targeted against a Leviathan's sane friends, family, or favourites among non-combatant Beloved.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> The third and final stage is the simplest. The Leviathans want each other dead. A Leviathan may choose to Escalate to this level. However there are many ways Leviathans may find themselves here without wanting to: If a Leviathan inflicts (directly or via pawns) even a single point of Lethal damage during the same scene as a conflict, catches another Leviathan directing the Marduk Society or an Ahab towards them, or harming an Atoll then they instantly escalate to the third stage and take the Ultimate Enmity Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidebar: What\u2019s a Conflict</b><br /> <br /> Unfortunately for the Tribe the term Conflict is broadly defined. If a Leviathan is thrown around during an Earthquake and their spiny body lands on another Leviathan that's fine. But if they were in the middle of an argument or a game of chess before the earthquake struck they take the Ultimate Enmity Condition. If a friendly boxing match results in wrap-around damage they take the Ultimate Enmity Condition.<br /> <br /> The Tribe tend to play it very safe. As a rule, even good friends will remain two bodies length apart at all times unless they have a reason not too. If they are going to have a conflict they try to avoid being in the same building, you can play chess over the internet. Even arch-enemies often collaborate to avoid escalating too far.<br /> <br /> <b>Condition: Ultimate Enmity (Persistant)</b><br /> <br /> Both your Divine and Beastal nature want another Leviathan dead, and nothing will convince them otherwise.<br /> <br /> If you and the other Leviathan are in the same scene you must choose fight or flight or pay one willpower per turn you're doing neither.<br /> <br /> If you choose flight you must run from the scene at your maximum speed, you may not use less instinctive methods of transportation like a car. It's running, swimming, or entering the Rift. You may also change to fight if you're cornered.<br /> <br /> If you choose fight you may take no action except Transforming into a more powerful form or attacking your opponent with your natural weapons. You may use any Channel or Birthright that will help you in combat and you may give your Beloved orders. You may also change to flight if the battle is going against you.<br /> <br /> If your rival is not present in the scene but you have an opportunity to thwart their plans, and you do not make an attempt to do so or an attempt to withdraw your resources further away from your rival, then instead of gaining a point of Willpower after sleeping you loose a point.<br /> <br /> Beat: The conflict causes a serious hardship.<br /> <br /> Resolution: One Leviathan dies. This requires true death. If a Leviathan reincarnates, time travels back to before their rival dies, or anything of that nature occurs, the Condition reappears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-12-2016, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:51:39-07:00","id":888136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=887974#post887974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Leviathan inflicts (directly or via pawns) even a single point of Lethal damage during the same scene as a conflict ...<br /> Resolution: One Leviathan dies. This requires true death. If a Leviathan reincarnates, time travels back to before their rival dies, or anything of that nature occurs, the Condition reappears.</div> </div> </div> </div>WTF? Isn't this a bit too harsh? I can see either perma-hate or easy-bloodfeud, but both together is a little unforgiving, even with the tribe's precautions, isn't it? Especially the <i>per turn</i> Willpower cost to suppress? This just seems like it is actually reducing story potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:32:27-07:00","id":888174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=888136#post888136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WTF? Isn't this a bit too harsh? I can see either perma-hate or easy-bloodfeud, but both together is a little unforgiving, even with the tribe's precautions, isn't it? Especially the <i>per turn</i> Willpower cost to suppress? This just seems like it is actually reducing story potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps a roll to resist? Made harder by circumstances?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:35:21-07:00","id":888178,"title":"","content":"Willpower per turn seems like the standard rate for this sort of Condition - see Beaten Down.<br /> <br /> The idea was based on Hera taking out her rage on Zeus' children, it seemed appropriate for a game based on bronze age gods and themes of family. I could make the bloodfudes a little less easy though. Say make it cost a Willpower point to intentionally attack another Leviathan unless you have the Ultimate Enmity Condition, with it only being automatically applied at Aggravated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T08:19:31-07:00","id":888223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=888178#post888178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower per turn seems like the standard rate for this sort of Condition - see Beaten Down.<br /> <br /> The idea was based on Hera taking out her rage on Zeus' children, it seemed appropriate for a game based on bronze age gods and themes of family. I could make the bloodfudes a little less easy though. Say make it cost a Willpower point to intentionally attack another Leviathan unless you have the Ultimate Enmity Condition, with it only being automatically applied at Aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems fairer.<br /> <br /> I was thinking about 1 Willpower per scene (probably with auto-Hostile social disposition, and a penalty to Outbursts). That enables Scenes/Stories where you have a teeth-clenched meeting with your hated enemy to discuss a matter of mutual import. Without both sides needing to compress the encounter into a few seconds before their Willpower runs out. Of course, if you hate everyone in the room, the costs stack...<br /> <br /> Other idea: You could make resolving the Condition requiring an Exceptional success on a Tranquility (or just Eunoia?) roll, paying Willpower to make said roll, with mere success being suppression. Or they have to pay a Willpower <i>dot</i>. Few enough Leviathans would even bother, so it remains effectively permanent in most cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-11-2016, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T08:28:51-07:00","id":888235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=888223#post888223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without both sides needing to compress the encounter into a few seconds before their Willpower runs out. Of course, if you hate everyone in the room, the costs stack...</div> </div> </div> </div> Isn't using a text-based medium or Beloved mailman sufficent to allow teeth clenched teamwork?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T08:42:35-07:00","id":888244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=888235#post888235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Isn't using a text-based medium or Beloved mailman sufficent to allow teeth clenched teamwork?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess. It just lacks the <i>gravitas</i>.<br /> <br /> And, of course, there is the fact that your Beloved messengers are still subject to the Condition. &quot;If your rival is not present in the scene but you have an opportunity to thwart their plans, and you do not make an attempt to do so or an attempt to withdraw your resources further away from your rival, then instead of gaining a point of Willpower after sleeping you loose a point.&quot; I'm assuming this extends to murdering their Beloved out of spite, if given the opportunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T10:23:58-07:00","id":888334,"title":"","content":"I'd say a single Beloved messenger isn't enough to trigger a response unless they believe that it would specifically hurt you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T10:52:49-07:00","id":888369,"title":"","content":"Question: What <i>is</i> Sheol? We know it is a measure of a Leviathan's power, but what is it aside from a metric? Can it be stored or transferred? Could a Leviathan infuse some of it into a Heirloom/Temple/Ritual for added longevity or power (of the target; obviously the Leviathan is losing power)? Can they steal it from each other (like Kindred with Diablerie)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T11:19:20-07:00","id":888385,"title":"","content":"I have no idea why it's called Sheol, the only definition for the word I can find is the Hebrew afterlife, so I assume there's supposed to be some connection. I can think of links, but the person who first suggested it gave no reason and it was accepted by the first contributes for some reason.<br /> <br /> In practice though. Sheol is a Leviathan's connection to the Tribe. Any Leviathan can say they're a Leviathan and having divine power is neat, but it takes a lifetime of shared experiences, of commiserating over shared history, to truly build a connection. And since a Leviathan's power flows down through untold generations, the stronger a Leviathan's connection to the Tribe and it's history the more power flows. (No, this doesn't mean that the Tribe get weaker over time. This is a sympathetic link like Knowledge. In fact some Leviathans believe Knowledge of Tiamat and the Progenitors is the source of Sheol, but it's debatable at best).<br /> <br /> A Sheol 1 and Sheol 10 Leviathan might both lack any strong sense of what being a Leviathan is. But the Sheol 10 Leviathan would strongly relate and empathise with all the other Levaithans, alive long gone, who faced similar issues to the ones he's facing.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want a real world example to help. Look at the Jewish community. That je ne sais quoi that let the Jewish identity survive both oppression and integration is a good example of Sheol. (Complete with endless questions about what does it mean to be a Jew/Leviathan)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T11:43:28-07:00","id":888414,"title":"","content":"So, it is, to some degree, the amount of confidence behind &quot;I Am A Leviathan&quot;? So while someone newly Transformed still mostly clings to their old human identity, older/stronger Leviathans identify more as <i>Leviathans</i> (even if neither are sure just exactly what that means)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T13:19:27-07:00","id":888498,"title":"","content":"It's not so much that they cling to their old identity or a question of less/more.<br /> <br /> Think of it as the difference between theory and practice. The young Leviathan might leap at the chance to reject humanity and be &quot;special&quot;, but ask him what being a Leviathan means and he'll just say &quot;Oh, you know, we're descended from Tiamat, we have a wake, we do rituals&quot;.<br /> <br /> But to the old Leviathan &quot;descended from Tiamat&quot; means the time he broke into a museum to read ancient Babylonian tablets. &quot;We have a wake&quot; means that time he hid in a basement in a remote town and coming out to find the town a bullet ridden no man's land between fortified compounds. &quot;we do rituals&quot; means the time the local top Leviathan knocked on his door and said he's rounding up an Opheon hunting posse before it does Tiamat-knows-what with all those ancient artefacts he stole; and how just for a little while slaughtering defenceless cultists felt not only good but also heroic.<br /> <br /> <br /> If God poked his head out of heaven and turned every Leviathan into humans, a high Sheol Leviathan may be outright ecstatic. But he'd still seek out with and hang out with (much more frequently now there's no territorial instincts) other Leviathans because of shared experiences. He'd still think of them as &quot;my people&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-12-2016, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T01:09:46-07:00","id":890494,"title":"","content":"A theory on Sheol: A part of a leviathan's soul resides in everyone who knows about them, the more they know, the more of the soul. If Tiamat (or the Progenitors) shared this trait - likely, given the fact that all leviathans do -, it is possible that as a Leviathan's knowledge of Tiamat, the Progenitors and the primordial world grows, more and more of their essence becomes a part of him, becoming what is known as Sheol. All the bloodline of Tiamat does is provide the physiology necessary to harness this shard of hideous divinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T06:24:49-07:00","id":890553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=888498#post888498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not so much that they cling to their old identity or a question of less/more.<br /> <br /> Think of it as the difference between theory and practice. The young Leviathan might leap at the chance to reject humanity and be &quot;special&quot;, but ask him what being a Leviathan means and he'll just say &quot;Oh, you know, we're descended from Tiamat, we have a wake, we do rituals&quot;.<br /> <br /> But to the old Leviathan &quot;descended from Tiamat&quot; means the time he broke into a museum to read ancient Babylonian tablets. &quot;We have a wake&quot; means that time he hid in a basement in a remote town and coming out to find the town a bullet ridden no man's land between fortified compounds. &quot;we do rituals&quot; means the time the local top Leviathan knocked on his door and said he's rounding up an Opheon hunting posse before it does Tiamat-knows-what with all those ancient artefacts he stole; and how just for a little while slaughtering defenceless cultists felt not only good but also heroic.<br /> <br /> <br /> If God poked his head out of heaven and turned every Leviathan into humans, a high Sheol Leviathan may be outright ecstatic. But he'd still seek out with and hang out with (much more frequently now there's no territorial instincts) other Leviathans because of shared experiences. He'd still think of them as &quot;my people&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The side scale between &quot;Cursed with Awesome&quot; and &quot;Blessed with Suck&quot; is about maturity ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T09:51:50-07:00","id":891208,"title":"","content":"A question, after you think you have revised and reworked everything, are you going to put it all in a pdf format or just put it in website like the old one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T07:05:27-07:00","id":892471,"title":"","content":"I'll probably keep this one as a google doc, so just click the save-to-pdf button. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=890494#post890494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A theory on Sheol: A part of a leviathan's soul resides in everyone who knows about them, the more they know, the more of the soul. If Tiamat (or the Progenitors) shared this trait - likely, given the fact that all leviathans do -, it is possible that as a Leviathan's knowledge of Tiamat, the Progenitors and the primordial world grows, more and more of their essence becomes a part of him, becoming what is known as Sheol. All the bloodline of Tiamat does is provide the physiology necessary to harness this shard of hideous divinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about that too. Sheol requires it to be personal, which makes it more like Mage's Sympathy or Princess' Intimacy than Leviathan's Knowledge which was specifically designed to mimic the &quot;don't read the occult tome&quot; trope and so works just fine with impersonal book knowledge.<br /> <br /> But don't let that get in the way of a good theory. Also, there's no reason why Leviathans can't use Sympathy for Sheol and Knowledge for Rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T10:52:31-07:00","id":892627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=892471#post892471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll probably keep this one as a google doc, so just click the save-to-pdf button. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>One Google Doc, or several?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=892471#post892471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought about that too. Sheol requires it to be personal, which makes it more like Mage's Sympathy or Princess' Intimacy than Leviathan's Knowledge which was specifically designed to mimic the &quot;don't read the occult tome&quot; trope and so works just fine with impersonal book knowledge.<br /> <br /> But don't let that get in the way of a good theory. Also, there's no reason why Leviathans can't use Sympathy for Sheol and Knowledge for Rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what if the Knowledge here is a bit more abstract? It isn't just &quot;yeah I heard those names&quot;, the Knowledge of Tiamat here goes beyond mere sound and letter. You <i>Know</i> of Tiamat when you see what glories and follies your cult has wrought in your name. You <i>Know</i> Tiamat when you feel blood and Ichor pumping as you engage in mortal combat. The Knowledge here is shared in experiences, not in words as for lesser Leviathans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T09:40:39-07:00","id":897899,"title":"","content":"Lets get some movement here again. Here's one of the sample Emperian Thurgists. The heart ripping Aztec.<br /> <br /> The second Thurgist will probably be the exact opposite in every way except for also being hispanic. A modern, progressive, priestess of Santa Muerte with a congregation of working class and outcasts.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enrique Puente</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>This is a different kind of company. We offer you flexible working, mentorship, benefits, and most importantly a chance to make our world a better place. </i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>In return, we only ask that you give us your heart.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Aztecs believed that the world was a fragile delicate thing. Only the constant labour of the gods kept the world from collapse, and only the sacrifice of man gave the gods the strength they need. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An discriminating observer may notice that it has been a long time since the Spanish ended the Aztec practices of human sacrifice, and the world hasn\u2019t ended. Enrique sees it differently: Global warming, environmental collapse, without the Teotl at the helm the world is very much dying. The enormous lump of rock and water we live on will survive, just as it survived the previous four worlds ending in Aztec mythology, but if humans want to survive we\u2019d better start taking care of the planet and offering up blood. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In his quest to save the Earth Enrique blends mundane and occult methods. He is the founder, chief scientist, and sole owner of Huitzilopochtli Photovoltaics, as well as a philanthropist and leading sponsor of archeology and Aztec heritage events. Few outside the upper echelons of Huitzilopochtli Photovoltaics realise know his interests go beyond the academic curiosity and establishing a sense of national pride; or know about the secret attic in his corporate tower where the sacrifices take place. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Appearance</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enrique looks far more South American than his mixed indigenous and Spanish heritage would suggest. In person he cuts an imposing figure, standing six foot two with a regal continence and flowing jet black locks. One might say he was made for the roll, especially if they see how different he looks in his childhood photographs. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Storytelling Hints</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlike most Empyrean Theurgists who merely react to the Tribe\u2019s presence, Enrique seeks out Leviathans to sacrifice their enormous blood filled hearts. His focus is on his photovoltaic research and attempting to subtly restore the worship of the Teotl but he has enough resources to pursue secondary goals. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As a corporate man and a philanthropist Enrique\u2019s resources don\u2019t provide him with much in the way of firepower, especially not the specialist forces one needs to take on a Leviathan, so unless his interests are directly threatened Enrique is unlikely to take the risks necessary to acquire mercenaries. Instead he will discreetly use his considerable resources to support any Hunters or Ahabs who looks competent. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most of Enrique\u2019s worship is just that, worship and sacrifice to honour the gods rather than a practical use of occult power. When he practices theurgy Enrique focuses on enhancing his company, providing Blessings that help him outcompete his rivals and create life-saving green energy to an increasingly polluted planet. Often without the knowledge of the recipient. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To fuel his miracles Enrique\u2019s mostly uses small measures of blood donated by the congregation, and occasionally abducts somebody who won\u2019t be missed when a more potent sacrifice is required. He\u2019s no hypocrite, and if he believed would sacrifice his friends or himself in a heartbeat if he believed the gods wished it. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sidebar: Seems Sacrilegious</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Empyrean Theurgists cannot use Sacrilegious, but human sacrifice is a horrific crime. Does that not qualify? </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In Enrique\u2019s style of Theurgy the quality of the sacrifice is important. An exceptional individual provides a better sacrifice than an average joe, and a Leviathan is a uniquely potent sacrifice. Enrique gains Ardour for tracking down and acquiring the right victim, not for making his ritual especially heinous. This shows that his sacrifices fall under Portents, not Sacrileges. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mental Attributes: Intelligence 5, Wits 2, Resolve 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Physical Attributes: Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Social Attributes: Presence 5, Manipulation 3, Composure 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mental Skills: Academics 3 (Aztec Theology), Computer 2, Investigation* 2, Occult 4 (Theurgy), Politics* 2, Science* 4 (Photovoltaics)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Physical Skills: Athletics 1, Drive 1, Firearms 1, Stealth 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Social Skills: Empathy 2, Expression 3 (preaching), Intimidation 1, Persuasion* 4, Socialise 2 (fundraising), Subterfuge* 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits: Good Time Management O, Indomitable OO, Library OOO (Photovoltaics), Library OO (Aztec Theology), Professional Training (Scientist) OOOO, Professional Training (Executive) OOO, Tolerance for Biology O, Giant OOO, Allies OO (Political), Allies OOOO (Scientific), Allies OOO (Archeology), Contacts OOOO (Politics, Corporate, Scientific, Archeology), Fame O, Inspiring OOO, Resources OOOO, Safe-Place OOOOO (a temple hidden in the penthouse of his corporate HQ), Striking Looks OO (Regal)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Virtues: Leadership 5, Piety 4, Dutiful 2<br /> Domains: The Sun, Sacrifice, Death<br /> Willpower: 7</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Integrity: 6 </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Humble: Hopeful. Enrique\u2019s methods might be suspect, but his motives are not. He his genuine in his faith, humble before the gods, and humble before the common good. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vice: Deceitful. While Enrique is not untrustworthy by nature, as a devout practitioner of human sacrifice he is always hiding both his crimes, and his true beliefs. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Health: 7</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiative: 5 </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Defense: 2 </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed: 9</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cult: Huitzilopochtli Photovoltaics. Fervour 1, Piety 4, Zeal 3. Legitimate Organization. Compartmentalized OOO, Home Turf OO (the corporate headquarters), Old Hands OO (Kidnapping). </span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=892627#post892627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One Google Doc, or several?</div> </div> </div> </div> One<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=892627#post892627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, what if the Knowledge here is a bit more abstract?</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely up to you, this is the sort of theory Leviathans come up with all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-24-2016, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T11:05:43-07:00","id":898006,"title":"","content":"That said, I'd quite like to see this become a full PDF with art etc.<br /> <br /> I don't know what all would be needed to make that happen, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:12:23-07:00","id":898065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=898006#post898006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I'd quite like to see this become a full PDF with art etc.<br /> <br /> I don't know what all would be needed to make that happen, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Artists, for one. I remember a lot of notes, but a shortage of actual images in 1E. After that, layout and other PDF-fu could be done. Maybe some more fiction for the chapters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:36:15-07:00","id":898226,"title":"","content":"Yep, it would need artists first of all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T22:45:39-07:00","id":902496,"title":"","content":"Upwellings and Undertows are done - the Tribe's virtues and vices.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Upwellings and Undertows are the two paths that lead from the transitional state that is a Leviathan\u2019s existence; Upwellings raise Leviathan up to the heights of godhood while Undertows drag them down into the thoughtless depths of beasthood. Together they threaten to pull a Leviathan in two.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An Upwelling describes the fundamental identity of an individual Leviathan\u2019s divine nature, while an Undertow does the same for her beastal nature. When she acts in coordination with her other natures the two facets of her mind ally, giving her a much needed respite from the Tempest. For a few moments she breaks the surface and may draw a much needed breath of air before the Tempest once again threatens to drown her. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A simple act in accordance with a Leviathans Upwelling or Undertow restores a point of Willpower, while one which causes the Leviathan significant trouble and creates dramatic possibilities restores all Willpower. Phronesis &amp; Eunoia chain the beastal and divine natures; and loosed from their chains the other natures can also hold a Leviathan\u2019s Ichor hostage, demanding that a Leviathan fall or rise further.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The beastal nature is primal and direct, so regaining Willpower from Undertows requires the Leviathan act personally. Always it\u2019s opposite, the divine nature is calculating and works in mysterious ways and so the divine nature provides Willpower when a Leviathan works through proxies, usually but not always their Cult. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sample Undertows</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Man-Eater</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Man-Eater hungers for human flesh. He is the nightmare of civilised man, that the walls between us are thin stand only because the monsters outside fear the strength of a long gone generation when man remembered how to hunt and survive. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Man-Eater regains a point of Willpower when he solves a problem by eating a person (or uses some other suitably dramatic and personal method). He regains all Willpower when the act is witnessed by a significant number of mortals.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Hoarder </span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The dragon atop his mountain of gold. The serpent with lidless eyes, forever watchful for thieves and intruders. The Hoarder lives to expand his collection and to guard it against all comers. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Horder regains a point of Willpower when he prevents a loss to his collection (this can include preventing escapees from his collection of princesses) and regains all his Willpower when he causes a significant problem in order to add add to his collection. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Fury</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Fury is the sea and the storm made flesh. She has no desire to destroy, and she has no understanding of any way but destruction. Cliffs are shattered and cities sink in her wake. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Fury regains a point of Willpower when she causes a significant amount of destruction. If the Fury chooses the path of destruction when there are clear alternatives she regains all spent Willpower. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Nest-Maker</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A shark on dry land is pitiful, not threatening. The Nest Maker knows well that a beast is only fearsome in its own lair. He stakes his claim, and permits no trespass. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Nest-Maker regains a point of Willpower when it drives intruders from it\u2019s lair. When he claims a new lair by driving out its current inhabitants he regains all his spent Willpower. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Terror</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">She lurks beyond the village, a story mothers use to make their children behave. When she emerges from the depths she need not fight, she need not ask, she gives one look and the tribute flows freely. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Terror regains a point of Willpower whenever she uses fear and intimidation to get her way, she may not regain Willpower by intimidating her own Beloved. If she successfully uses fear and intimidation against a superior foe she regains all spent Willpower. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sample Upwellings</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Conqueror</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Conqueror sets forth with a sword and an army to bring foreign nations under his divine rule. Victory is everything, and he weeps when there are no more lands left to conqueror. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Conqueror gains a point of Willpower when his followers win a marital conflict in which they are the aggressor. If they take ownership of land through force of arms the Conqueror regains all his spent Willpower. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Devil</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Even the gods must acknowledge others, even if only other gods. The Devil defines herself by opposition, another church, another nation is her enemy. But she has no wish to destroy it for where would that leave her? The Devil instead spreads her corruption, turning her enemy against it's sacred values. Leaving it alive in name only as a testament to her victory.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Devil regains a point of Willpower whenever she makes one of her enemies betray their principles or ideals. If she corrupts her own allies or some other group whose moral behavior is of benefit to herself then she regains all Willpower. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Judge</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Judge does not wish to create a world without sin, no his motive is far more brutal. The Judge wishes to create a world where all sin is punished and all sinners face their judgement. The Judge would be satisfied if the whole world turned against the gods, so long as the whole world was thus drowned for their sins. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Judge gains a point of Willpower when her followers exact a harsh punishment on a Sinner. If she sacrifices an asset or an opportunity on the altar of judgement she regains all spent Willpower. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Lawgiver</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In many ways the Judge's twin, the Lawgiver emerges from the depths with bronze tablets to create a world where all follow the laws within. He punishes harshly and rewards sparingly but when faced with the choice the Lawgiver would ignore one sinner to instil his commandments within two.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Lawgiver regains a point of Willpower when he witnesses his followers obey one of his laws despite a personal cost. He regains all his Willpower when his followers act against his own best interests because his laws demand they do so. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Mother</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Mother exists for her children, she has given birth to heroes and monsters and will give birth to many more until the day she is dragged up from the depths. Her only wish is to see her children triumph. Her children\u2019s own wishes are meaningless to her. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Mother regains a point of Willpower when his children use his gifts or advice to overcome a challenge. If his children overcome a significant challenge (as a rule of thumb, if you could imagine a Greek myth about it, it qualifies) then the Mother regains all his spent Willpower. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Patriarch</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parisian without limits, The Patriarch will see his people thrive. He bestows his favor freely but never spares the teacher's rod when his people stray from their own best interests. To those who threaten the chosen people or just stand in their way The Patriarch sends his storms and his plagues.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Patriarch gains a point of Willpower when her followers expand their numbers or influence. She regains all her Willpower if they are able to assimilate another group into themselves.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Weaver</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is said Fate binds even the gods, but the Weaver believes she can play Fate at it's own games and master the future. But no Weaver plays for the love of the game, they have goals and plans which they enact through mortal pawns.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Weaver gains a point of Willpower when she fulfils an Ambition or makes significant progress on a long term Ambition without anyone other than her Cohort being aware of her involvement - that usually means they mustn\u2019t notice her Cult\u2019s involvement either. If the Weavers enemies contribute to her success of their own free will and without coercion then she regains all her spent Willpower. </span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I still need a couple more sample Undertowes to make 7.<br /> <br /> In other news, after wavering back and forth for a while - Judges are going to be officially included in Leviathan. For those who don't know Judges were originally written a blue-book minor template that I wrote in collaboration with LostLight. Based heavily on the Biblical book of judges, they're basically God's (or Zeus' etc) personal Jack Bauer. I made a few small tweeks to the mechanics to fit better in Leviathan, most notably they now get Supernatural Tolerance so that they're immune to becoming Beloved without needing to be a special case. The updated version is in the Leviathan folder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T11:28:49-07:00","id":902836,"title":"","content":"So the Nest Maker needs to put his secret lair in areas with potential intruders, to make sure his WP are restored? Kinda ironic, if you ask me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 05-29-2016, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T11:45:03-07:00","id":902852,"title":"","content":"Well no one ever said that a Leviathan was mentally healthy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but this is more of an OOC thing really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T08:22:34-07:00","id":903548,"title":"","content":"And now I've ported the 1E Merits. Not much to do, but a few of them have become obsolete in 2E. Suggestions for replacements will be welcome (note that I'm quite strict about Merits that just modify dicepools. I'd allow some, but they'd have to really impress me)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dehumanising Ethos (OO)</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan subscribes to an code of ethics accepted by mortal culture that dehumanizes some rival group, allowing them to focus their wickedness upon them with less guilt and gaining a +2 bonus to Erosion dicepools when the victims are in the target group. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The drawbacks of this strategy should be extremely obvious. When regular humans come up with a dehumanising ethos it tends to have horrible results. When Leviathans do so it tends to be even worse. In addition, a Leviathan who subscribes to a Dehumanizing Ethos act in ways that cause more frequent and worse Erosion. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Divine Prerogative (OO)</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The divine bloodline inside your character is eager to express itself in the defeat of mortals. You may select a Skill. When engaging in a contested roll using that Skill against a human (one not subject to a major supernatural template), you may chose to risk Willpower instead of spending it. You receive the normal bonus dice as though Willpower were spent, but, if you are successful in overcoming the victim's resistance, you do not lose the Willpower risked, instead retaining that point and in fact regaining an additional point beyond that. You cannot risk Willpower to boost your resistance - you must be acting aggressively to benefit from this Merit.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Should you fail, the risked Willpower is spent as usual </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>and</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> your failure is upgraded to a Dramatic failure. This often triggers an Outburst check.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gatewater (O)</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your character has control of their own Gatewater. See page xx for rules on Gatewaters. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Giant (O)</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Leviathans may buy the Giant Merit at a discount. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Heirloom (O - OOOOO)</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your character has some physical artifact that was once a possession of a long dead Leviathan and has soaked in some of their essence. It might be an art object or everyday tool, but it is generally unsuitable for its original task - too brittle or too precious to make use of. Its primary role, instead, is to be a vessel for the Tribe\u2019s cultural memories. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Should a Leviathan take a Heirloom into the Rift it will manifest as a Rift Creature, as an inanimate possession it is infallibly loyal to it\u2019s owner and it can unerringly seek out its own presence in other memories. A pen that sat on a Leviathan\u2019s desk could take it\u2019s owner to every memory of events within that room. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Searching through the Rift takes time, but there is no need to wait until information is vitally important before taking a study session. A Leviathan who spends a significant amount of time investigating a Heirloom stores it\u2019s dots in points that may be redeemed for: </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An answer to a short question about a Leviathan who owned the heirloom. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A yes/no answer about something a Leviathan who owned the heirloom encountered.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Clue for an ongoing investigation related to one of the Heirloom\u2019s previous owners. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively if the Leviathan is able to personally relate to Heirloom\u2019s original owner they may trade in dots in a Heirloom to acquire and experience point to be put towards Sheol. Dots spent this way do not diminish the Heirloom\u2019s potency. Rather, like a book that\u2019s been read again and again, a there is nothing more to be learned. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nothing says the former owners of a Heirloom have to be dead. Any of of them might object to another Leviathan having a map to their memories, and Heirloom\u2019s make great foci for rituals. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sidebar: That Belongs in a Museum</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Leviathans aren\u2019t the only ones with interest in Heirlooms. All Heirlooms are receptacles of mystical energies and while most simply contain those energies some develop other, rarer, properties. Mystical orders such as the Aegis Kai Doru are frequently tempted either by what they could learn about the past or in using their secret knowledge to unlock an Heirloom\u2019s practical applications as a mystical talisman. Private collectors, archaeologists and museums also have a stake in owning an Heirloom. Iremite Mummies will go to great length to acquire Heirlooms, or as they call them: Vestiges.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Despite this Heirlooms tend to cause little stir among those not in the know: vanishingly few Heirlooms predate known civilisation, most come much more recent exploits of the Tribe and aren\u2019t markedly distinct from entirely human artefacts of the period. It\u2019s unsure what exactly would happen if regular academics did get hold of a Heirloom that predated Tiamat\u2019s death, such a discovery could rewrite known history but only if it wasn\u2019t snatched by Leviathans or some other party. It would certainly make an interesting story. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mandate of Babel (O)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When your character expends Ichor to focus his Wake on a subject whose primary language is foreign to the Leviathan, they gain the supernatural ability to speak the Leviathan\u2019s mother tongue for the remainder of the scene. However if they roll a Failure or Dramatic Failure on the Breaking Point, they also lose the ability to speak their mother tongue for the scene. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Narrow Wake (OO)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your Leviathan has an unusually subtle and mild Wake - for the purposes of its diameter your Sheol is treated as though it were one point lower. If your Sheol is at 1, your Wake's maximum diameter is 50 feet. Your Ripple penalty is measured by your decreased Sheol, and is at -0 if your Sheol is 0. This Merit has no effect on your Sheol for focusing the Wake on a single subject.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Well, the thing the Merit does, sort of.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wide Wake (OO)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your Leviathan has an unusually potent Wake - for the purposes of its diameter, your Sheol is treated as though it were one point higher. If your Sheol is at 10 (Way to go, Cthulhu), your Wake's maximum diameter is 10 miles. This Merit has no effect on your Sheol for focusing the Wake on a single subject.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Your Ripple Penalty is measured by your increased Sheol. If your Sheol is at 10, it increases to -4.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T12:59:18-07:00","id":903724,"title":"","content":"TKR since the Rift as far as I can tell is the Leviathan version of the Astral but way more personal. What of rift creatures? Are they just parasites, etc. of the collective madness of the Tribe? I'd love more info on the Rift.<br /> <br /> Also I wanna say I cant wait for Leviathan to get more meat on its primeval bones!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T16:15:54-07:00","id":903834,"title":"","content":"I'm curious TKR are evolutions going to remain much the same or are there going to be any major changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11554-fate-inker","name":"Fate Inker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T18:32:12-07:00","id":903887,"title":"","content":"Hi all,<br /> As keen as I was to get into this, life just threw work at me constantly.<br /> Just using this to subscribe. I'll be taking a quick catch up from where I was, and then getting into it now that work is letting up. What are we looking at currently that needs work? Still Rituals and the such?<br /> (RTFM is fine, I'll read it over)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11740-diserasta","name":"Diserasta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T00:54:38-07:00","id":904023,"title":"","content":"The two largest blocks of unfinished work are Channels and Rituals - there's still lots of Channels to update and new ones are needed to replace attribute boosters. For rituals the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1f-xnfJTnCPdJAlYX1fdyHdfqCMdR3rQuWjpmKyPKcjU\" target=\"_blank\">framework is done</a> but no sample rituals are written yet - they should be done in the style of Mage 2E spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freederp92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=903724#post903724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What of rift creatures? Are they just parasites, etc. of the collective madness of the Tribe? I'd love more info on the Rift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rift creatures are roughly equivilant to the inhabitants of the Oneiros, and as you swim lower, the Temenous. Some represent madness, but they also represent the saner parts of the Tribe's psychology.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;meat on its primeval bones&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fate Inker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=903834#post903834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious TKR are evolutions going to remain much the same or are there going to be any major changes?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're going to be more simmilar than different to 1E. The sample Evolutions are probably going to be changed more to make sure they present a clear picture of what that Leviathan believes is their true purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-31-2016, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T07:55:57-07:00","id":904151,"title":"","content":"It was a pun TKR. Thanks for fleshing out the rift dwellers. I take it just like astral entities they can at times find themselves in the waking world with strong enough magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T08:06:36-07:00","id":904160,"title":"","content":"Yes, though Leviathans usually do that with dreams rather than Rift creatures. Look at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ibcuayqS6LdyhuGAyfdj6-MMyrpon_f6qd4gBvcy08w/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Piercing the Veil of Slumber</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T10:12:09-07:00","id":904239,"title":"","content":"Great stuff so far! <br /> <br /> Just wondering though, would things like the Hedge, the spirit realm, the Underworld, etc...still be something of a blind spot to Leviathans? <br /> <br /> Also, I remember early drafts of where leviathans would have violent reactions to the presence of prometheans (and vice versa) due to the opposing forces of the primordial waters and the divine fire...will that be in this game as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T10:18:43-07:00","id":904246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=904239#post904239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wondering though, would things like the Hedge, the spirit realm, the Underworld, etc...still be something of a blind spot to Leviathans?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. The Hedge is a total blind spot (I play the Hedge as a huge blind spot to all except specalists). The Spirit world is something Leviathans can learn to interact with, but few do. Leviathans can summon ghosts and it tends to happen acidently when they create Earthquakes, but their actual ability to interact with Ghosts isn't much better than Spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=904239#post904239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I remember early drafts of where leviathans would have violent reactions to the presence of prometheans (and vice versa) due to the opposing forces of the primordial waters and the divine fire...will that be in this game as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Crossover specific mechanics are unlikely to be in the game, but if they do that will be there.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T12:57:05-07:00","id":904371,"title":"","content":"A couple of new Predation powers (and the older one: Mortal Devouring Amroury got some new Adaptations)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Tyrant\u2019s Privilege (Birthright of Predation) </span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan\u2019s ability to focus his Wake is improved. As before she spends a point of Ichor to focus the Wake and triggers a Breaking Point roll, however if this results in a Failure or Dramatic Failure they may choose to inflict the Beaten Down Tilt in addition to any other effects. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">King Atop A Bloody Throne (Ancestral Channel) </span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Leviathan is too terrible to contemplate opposing. All must surrender and appease his wrath. </i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fluff goes here. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And remember that as always the Beaten Down Tilt doesn\u2019t apply if the Leviathan\u2019s actual goal is to inflict violence.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 1&quot;: Birthright of Predation</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 2&quot;: Wake vulnerable Mortals who get into a fight with the Leviathan automatically take the Secret Condition. They are convinced that standing up to the Leviathan was shameful and wrong, and if word gets out their community will turn upon them for attracting the Leviathan\u2019s Ire. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 3&quot;: If the Leviathan successfully inflicts Lethal or Aggravated damage to a Wake Vulnerable target they also lose a point of Willpower. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 4&quot;: Wake vulnerable Mortals who takes the Beaten Down Tilt from combat with a Leviathan also take the Subservient Condition. When a god beats you down, you stay down. If someone is Beaten Down from another source, like the Birthright of Predation, the Leviathan may rough them up until they\u2019re Subservient. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 5&quot;: The Leviathan may inflict the Beaten Down Tilt on Wake Vulnerable supernatural beings whose psychology is normally immune to such routs. This is explicitly a supernatural effect. The Wake pushes seeds of doubts in to the mind, which sprout when watered with defeat. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 6&quot;: The Depth two effect expands, vulnerable mortals within the Storm of the Leviathan\u2019s Wake will now take the Subservient Condition if the Leviathan\u2019s Beloved inflict the Beaten Down Tilt. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Depth 7&quot;: The Leviathan\u2019s true form is so terrible that even even the thought of opposing it is anathema. Wake vulnerable mortals must roll Resolve + Firearms or Weaponry - Sheol. On a Failure they take the Beaten Down Tilt. This does not inflict the Subservient Condition unless the Leviathan takes the time to \u201cfight\u201d someone who\u2019s already Beaten Down. </span></span></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:13:41-07:00","id":904378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=904371#post904371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of new Predation powers (and the older one: Mortal Devouring Amroury got some new Adaptations)</div> </div> </div> </div>Is King Atop a Bloody Throne going to get an Adaptation called Kneel Before Zod?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:38:32-07:00","id":904397,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think the only way I could make it work would be is if defeating a Leviathan inflicts the Tilt on all their Beloved. Forcing other Leviathans to kneel to you doesn't fit the all or nothing feeling I want from Leviathan vs Leviathan combat.<br /> <br /> P.S. Don't make a habit of controlling me through my love of shout outs and references.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-31-2016, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T11:42:18-07:00","id":905077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=904397#post904397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the only way I could make it work would be is if defeating a Leviathan inflicts the Tilt on all their Beloved. Forcing other Leviathans to kneel to you doesn't fit the all or nothing feeling I want from Leviathan vs Leviathan combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about expanding it to whenever the Leviathan defeats someone the group considers their &quot;superior&quot;? Such as if Greg defeats the Prince, the local vampires there are Beaten Down, as per KAaBT?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=904397#post904397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P.S. Don't make a habit of controlling me through my love of shout outs and references.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure I have no idea what you mean.<br /> <br /> Would King Atop a Bloody Throne support Adaptations the impose a different sequence of emotional Conditions/Tilts? Tilts like Stunned, Insensate, or Insane (heh)? Or Conditions like Atavism, Captivated, Awestruck, Swooning, Paranoid or Resigned? Basically, King Atop a Bloody Throne provides the mechanics to apply the Tilts/Conditions, but the Adaptation changes which are applied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-01-2016, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T14:11:58-07:00","id":905165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=905077#post905077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about expanding it to whenever the Leviathan defeats someone the group considers their &quot;superior&quot;? Such as if Greg defeats the Prince, the local vampires there are Beaten Down, as per KAaBT?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd be worried that it leads to odd edge cases with how different groups define superiors.<br /> <br /> Taking your vampire example. How many vampires would see the Prince getting beaten as an oppotunity for promotion rather than terrifying? Obviously you can just justify it with &quot;mind control&quot; but still, I think it works better when it basically works without mind control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=905077#post905077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would King Atop a Bloody Throne support Adaptations the impose a different sequence of emotional Conditions/Tilts? Tilts like Stunned, Insensate, or Insane (heh)? Or Conditions like Atavism, Captivated, Awestruck, Swooning, Paranoid or Resigned? Basically, King Atop a Bloody Throne provides the mechanics to apply the Tilts/Conditions, but the Adaptation changes which are applied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I'm limiting it to things that feel appropriate. So no Atavism. Swooning I'd be more likely to say affects any witnesses to the fight who're in a relationship with the looser - I'm not zoologist, but I know that's how &quot;romance&quot; works for some animals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T14:15:16-07:00","id":905168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=905165#post905165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd be worried that it leads to odd edge cases with how different groups define superiors.<br /> <br /> Taking your vampire example. How many vampires would see the Prince getting beaten as an oppotunity for promotion rather than terrifying? Obviously you can just justify it with &quot;mind control&quot; but still, I think it works better when it basically works without mind control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. I was supposing it would work in the same way higher Status nets your social bonuses - it requires ST arbitration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=905165#post905165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but I'm limiting it to things that feel appropriate. So no Atavism. Swooning I'd be more likely to say affects any witnesses to the fight who're in a relationship with the looser - I'm not zoologist, but I know that's how &quot;romance&quot; works for some animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the victors go the spoils?<br /> <br /> I mostly was thinking of what Adaptations it could possess to expand utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:34:32-07:00","id":907837,"title":"","content":"So, way back on page 33, I brought up the topic of a Leviathan X-splat (? The philosophical/social splat) that basically studies the other supernatural races to try and figure out if they have any tricks worth pursuing in their desperate need to find some way to evolve the Most Wicked Tribe. Corvus Rex's response was, basically, &quot;I don't like crossovers, but more importantly I have too much work to do; you can try and write it yourself, if you want&quot;.<br /> <br /> Things have been kind of haywire on my end, but I want to take him up on that. I can't do crunch if my life depends on it, but working fluff, I have few problems with.<br /> <br /> To start with, I'm going to make this into a &quot;Sect&quot;; a smaller philosophy that doesn't have the numbers or the backing to call itself a full-fledged School, which in this particular case probably splintered off from the School of Clay. This will hopefully respect Corvus Rex's drive to preserve the Rule of Seven, maintaining the arc number whilst still acknowledging that this is something Leviathans would be interested in.<br /> <br /> But, before I begin... can I ask someone to post one of the Schools from the Gdocs here? My internet has been utterly abysmal - I haven't been able to open a Gdoc for over nine days now - and Telstra shows no signs of pulling their thumbs out of their overpaid asses and fixing the problem anytime soon. I wouldn't ask this, but I need to look at the layout for the existing schools so I know how to properly approach writing this sect up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T04:57:10-07:00","id":908264,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">School of the Abyss</span></span></b><br /><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Explorers of the Depths</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sunken School</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tehom\u2019s Devotion</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ehus</span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Picture: The Symbol of Tehom\u2019s Devotion: An Anglerfish underwater. The light from the anglerfish illuminates hazy shapes of ziggurats and spiraling towers, just at the edge of vision. This serves as a watermark]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Picture: Central. A young and pale woman, black haired and anorexically thin, sits cross-legged in shallow water wearing a simple white shift. Her eyes are closed and cosmetically blackened, and her hands are in a meditative position in her lap. Eight tentacles extend from her back and shoulders, each holding an old-style oil lantern, but deliberately coiled around it to cut off most of the light.]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>We talk about their world and our world, but what do those simple words really mean? I say they are literal. The surface world is theirs, and the depths are ours. We bemoan the lack of our world, never noticing that it is right outside our door. Cast off what shackles you to the surface. </i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Come Home. </i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The School of the Abyss solve problems by retreating from humanity. Taken to it\u2019s bare essentials the School can be boiled down to a single question: How much contact with humanity does a Leviathan require to stay sane? Certainly a Leviathan that speaks to nobody, or nobody save other Leviathans and Beloved, will inevitably become a Typhon. But that doesn\u2019t mean they need the stress of mortgages and home maintenance, or the risk of paper trails, not when their bodies are so well adapted to life outdoors and a diet of live seafood. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However the Sunken School is the first to admit that sitting at the bottom of a lake might be a good way to avoid stress, but it gets boring very fast. An Ehus is an explorer: many swim through the seas seeking lost temples and underwater cities, others dive into the Rift, watch past eras through the eyes of their ancestors, or explore strange philosophies within the caverns of their own mind. Any problems they encounter can be put aside with a swish of their tail. No nets will catch them. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Oceans comprise over seventy percent of the Earth\u2019s surface, and the waters cast dark shadows upon the depths. For all the occult mysteries upon the surface of the World of Darkness there is even more in the depths, and most have no relation to the Tribe. For an explorer, the seas are vast and delightfully unmapped. Secure in the power of their divine bloodline and their ability to escape into the Rift, the Sunken School is as eager to investigate foreign mysteries as their own heritage. Their discoveries give unique insights into the World of Darkness and experience in dealing with the strange and unknown.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Direction</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The School of the Abyss may roll to regain Phronesis or Eunoia every time they solve a problem by abandoning a connection to humanity, including independent Lahmasu or Hybrids. Tehom\u2019s Devotion believe the Tempest is created by friction between the Tribe and man, with distance the Tempest will still and they may find Tranquility in the depths. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They take a -3 penalty to Erosion rolls encountered while trying to retain a connection to mundane humanity.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Traditions</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Even the most sessile Ehus who spends their time exploring the past through their Channels is likely to live outdoors and eat live fish whole. They\u2019ve all picked up the basics of living in the natural world, and most know far more than the basics about navigating the Oceans or the Rift. Since every Leviathan is likely to go on the run at least once in their life offering an Ehus safe harbour when they surface can be a small price to pay for the insurance they provide. When a Cohort\u2019s goals require a visit to the Rift or some sunken temple Tehom\u2019s Devotion naturally take the lead. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the rest of the Cohort remain firmly planted on land there is still room for the School of the Abyss to contribute. Their experience exploring beyond the boundaries of the Tribe require the same skills above or below the waterline, if the Cohort has issues with some strange foreign creature like a Vampire or Werewolf Tehom\u2019s Devotion are old hands at first contacts. Their long voyages mean that the Sunken School often has connections in all sorts of odd places, whether the Cohort needs untraceable guns, sacrifices who nobody will look for, or something stranger like occult technology that\u2019s only made in some underwater city, Tehom\u2019s Devotion often know where to find it. If they don\u2019t an Ehus is usually happy enough to swim to whichever humanitarian crisis is in the news and ask where to find the nearest warlord or grab whoever is closest to the waterline. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In turn the Cohort offer an Ehus an anchor. It is always a risk for a Leviathan to cut connections with humanity for there\u2019s no easy way to know when you\u2019re about to go too far and are at risk of Erosion. A Cohort can keep an eye out and warn an Ehus not to begin another voyage if they haven\u2019t fully returned from the previous one. Since they won\u2019t freak out if an Ehus stays in touch through telepathy a Cohort can make long ocean voyages a little less lonely. When the Sunken School need to surface a Cohort is usually superior to a Cult at making introductions and easing an Ehus\u2019 way back into human society. Naturally a Cohort can also take care of any Beloved left on the shore, saving Tehom\u2019s Devotion the significant effort required to train a competent high priest. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Maturation</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The School of the Abyss is a school of solitude, patience, and receptivity. This manifests as dark forms and soft lines, as well as large, aware eyes. As scholars of the Depths and seekers in quiet places, they tend towards forms that suggest the life that exists in the ocean\u2019s farthest reaches \u2013 markers of the squid, the octopus, and startling deep-sea fish are common. However, their final goal is the illumination of these depths \u2013 like most deep-sea life, patches of bioluminescence are also common, or pools of light shining out from great, staring eyes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Membership in Tehom\u2019s Devotion grants an experience Discount to Adaptations of Awareness and Elements. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stereotypes</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">School of Clay: Did you know that some whales beach themselves repeatedly. I don\u2019t know why I just thought of that. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">School of Fog: You wait here. I can swim farther by myself.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">School of the Moon:</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">School of the Reef: I think your body is trying to tell you something.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">School of Sand: </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">School of the Sun:</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Typhons and Orpheons: The tragic result of people who couldn\u2019t let a fight go.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hybrids: I\u2019ve seen their cities, they bring the surface with them but the sea is still large enough for us.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mages: I\u2019ve visited dozens of so-called Atlantises, most are six Hybrids huddled in a cave. Be careful near them, they attract these annoying little remora. Don\u2019t let them see you or kill them quickly, otherwise they\u2019ll never leave you be. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mortals: Let them have their world, as long as they stay out of mine.</span></span></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> <br /> As requested here's a school.</span></span></li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T13:54:18-07:00","id":908577,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Corvus Rex. By the way, is the list of Schools and Tribes on the TVtropes article for Leviathan accurate to 2e, or is it still based in the 1e model? If the latter, you may want to consider tweaking that if you find the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T19:13:38-07:00","id":925169,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hi guys,<br /> <br /> We over at the Dragon project are interested in working on some crossover material with you guys. Would anyone be interes