2186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T19:38:15-07:00","id":994351,"title":"","content":"I've also got notes on a Dishonored/Cinder Spires inspired Shard for Leviathan (if having an alternate world before the 2E material is even done isn't jumping the gun).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T04:49:48-07:00","id":994494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=994329#post994329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is it okay if their leader used to be a sorcerer from The Society of Marduk that managed to escape the revolution?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it's ok. I'm not going to close off a cool story hook like escaped Marduk Sorcerers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I don't have any plans to give them mechanics though. If they're the same people who helped Marduk kill Tiamat their power level would be &quot;plot device&quot;, and if they're not then you could make them Theurgists or borrow mechanics from Awakening. If you want to be really mean you could also make them Atolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=994351#post994351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've also got notes on a Dishonored/Cinder Spires inspired Shard for Leviathan (if having an alternate world before the 2E material is even done isn't jumping the gun).</div> </div> </div> </div>No such thing as jumping the gun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T05:08:30-07:00","id":994499,"title":"","content":"Is the evil carnival an okay idea for a cult? Also, the Marduk sorcerer is gonna be the ringmaster of the carnival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T07:24:28-07:00","id":994560,"title":"","content":"Sure (and you don't need my permission <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:58:56-07:00","id":994684,"title":"","content":"Very rough draft:<br /> <br /> Basic setting is a world long after some calamity. Scholars know humanity and civilization was more developed at some point, but few have little details about that time before. The world is heavily populated by the Tribe, and various groups of humanity that have varying degrees of response to the lords of the deep.<ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sky-People: Civilized folk, controlled by a very visible Marduk Society. They dwell in places far away from the sea (elevated towers or outright flying cities, if desired). They\u2019d never set foot upon land or especially sea if they could help it, but air travel is costly, and maintaining such infrastructure requires resources. [You want anachronistic, socio-political heavy adventure?]</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Technology: Anachronistic. </span></span>Da Vinci like<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> with a bit of electrical focus, thematically. The Marduk society tries their best to understand old technologies and develop new ones, but frankly some works are better described as Occult Tech than Super Science.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Culture: Renaissance like, Republic with heavy guild influence. The church of Marduk varies it's presentation from Marduk as a still extant monotheistic god, a vanished divinity who handed out commandments/and ethos, or a mortal visionary that others should aspire too. (Members may be anything from a corrupt despair/desperation magic using occultist seeking temporal power, to an enlightened visionary seeking to uplift the rest of humanity)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Supernatural abilities: Generally, it marks you as an outsider, casts questions on your bloodline (those descended from the Tribe are shamed), or might be indicative of being an Atoll (see below). Higher social position is bared from those of &quot;corrupted blood&quot;, ostensibly for the risk they pose if one of the Deep Ones awakens to their power in control of key posts in society. Having a Hybrid develop in your family (or worse, a Leviathan) is something most would try to cover up for fear of the shame and social stigma.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Atolls: Subject to mixed regard - they are a vast asset against the Beasts Below, but their potential for power, and the abuse of said power, marks them as a risk (see Green Witches). Of course, few have an opportunity to realize if they are or not, as most avoid getting anywhere </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>near</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Leviathans, if possible.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Mudborn&quot;: Barbaric people, dwelling on the land, especially near water, and often worshipping the various Deep Ones in the area as living gods.The Tribe\u2019s bloodline runs through them so thickly that minor mutations (not exceeding 5 dots) are not uncommon (said individuals would not be considered Hybrids, or Depth 0 if they are). [Want a nice Conan-esque romp through superstitious tribes and dread cults?]</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Technology: Neolithic to early Iron Age, with most being Bronze Age.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Culture: Varies wildly. Tribal, hereditary monarchy, Theocracy, etc.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Supernatural abilities: Varies wildly. Some revere those who possess the blood of the Gods, some vocally praise it while secretly fearing it, some despise it outright. Mostly depends on the reaction to their gods.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Atolls: Varies. Some are favored as a new high priest/ess or messenger to the Gods, others feared as potential liabilities (or tyrants), and others as used as chosen sacrifices to appease the gods.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">High Folk: Deeper inland than the Mudborn, usually dwelling in hills or mountainous terrain, but not quite at the remove of the Sky-People. Mutations and Hybrids are uncommon, but not unheard of. [Want a quasi-medieval fantasy, with terrible monsters lurking just outside the borders?]</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Technology: Mostly Iron Age, with some deviation up and down depending on region.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Culture: Feudalism and Monarchy, mostly. Some early manifestations of guild structures, but it isn\u2019t common. Hierarchical.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Supernatural Abilities: Varies, though usually shunned or at least treated as different/outsider.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Atolls: High Folk have less interaction with Leviathans, and thus less chances for being an Atoll to even be discovered. They inevitably are either driven out for causing the monsters/old gods to approach, or treasured as being able to influence them away from destruction.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Deep Ones: The Leviathans. Born of the descendants of the monsters of old and mortal-kind, they rule over the seas, and any humans they can ensnare. [Want a mind-warping adventure in the alien depths - madness optional, but recommended?]</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Technologies: Hardly necessary. Maybe some use of Heirlooms, but that\u2019s it.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Culture: A culture of solitary, or close groupings of monsters, ruling over their minions.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Supernatural Abilities: Rampant, since they are comprised of either Leviathans or their Hybrids.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Atolls: Almost unheard of. Atolls don\u2019t come from the Tribe\u2019s bloodlines, and Leviathan blood runs thick throughout the populace. One </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>might</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> arise amongst the human Beloved families that form the cultists of certain Leviathans, but that is about it.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Green Witches: A cadre of Atolls outside the borders of the known lands. They\u2019ve figured out how to augment their influence, and have enslaved the Leviathans in their area to use them to their purposes. Other Leviathans face the perilous choice of Tranquility for Enslavement, or remaining free, but in torment by their natures. [Want an internal exploration as to the nature of power and exploitation?]</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stance towards other Atolls: Join us and tow the line, or die.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stance towards others: Bow down to us, or be destroyed by our pet monsters.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> I need to flesh things out a bit more and develop some concrete examples. This should give an idea, though. The entire setting concept supports either being a human (or close enough) in one of the above societies, or a Leviathan from them (and how their host/birth society might react to them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Changed the Sky-People's technological aesthetic based on the recommendation here: http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chron 10-28-2016, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:02:42-07:00","id":994730,"title":"","content":"It looks like a good start. I'd suggest going more Leonardo da Vinci than Steampunk for Marduk. It's a bit more unique and what you've written does sound quite culturally Renaissance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:12:51-07:00","id":994736,"title":"","content":"What strain of Leviathan would use a wandering carnival as a cult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-28-2016, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:25:22-07:00","id":994838,"title":"","content":"What do you think of this appearance for the cult leader? <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/originals/80/ba/a7/80baa7b5b50da822eb2f9be99a1929c8.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com...e99a1929c8.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T05:21:55-07:00","id":995159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=994736#post994736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What strain of Leviathan would use a wandering carnival as a cult?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thalassan if it looks like a normal carnaval from the outside. Dagonite if it's obviously weird and you have to ask yourself why on earth anyone would actually visit.<br /> <br /> (Either way, the Leviathan should stay far away when they set up or the Wake would drive away visitors)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=994838#post994838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of this appearance for the cult leader? <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/originals/80/ba/a7/80baa7b5b50da822eb2f9be99a1929c8.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com...e99a1929c8.jpg</a></div> </div> </div> </div>It's more Sin-Eater than Leviathan / Leviathan's Beloved. You've got fire and death motifs there. Leviathans are drawn towards water and life symbology. They're gods of the sea and fertility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-29-2016, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T05:38:47-07:00","id":995163,"title":"","content":"About the leader's appearance, I thought it looked cool . Also, the carnival is a horror-themed one that is infamous for it's death defying acrobatics and sideshow. When they arrive in a town they immediately start advertising to attract as many people possible to the carnival. On the night of the carnival, they enthrall the people with acrobatics, their world-famous sideshow, the bigtop and the occasional haunted corn maze if a local farmer is feeling generous. What no one knows is that during the carnival the ringmaster,( The guy with the skull face-paint) sends out cultists to scout out among the crowds of people to find someone worthy of being sacrificed. Once the cultists find someone find someone worthy, they immediately kidnap him from the crowd, with the other people in the crowd thinking he was planted their by the carnival to scare people. The unlucky person is then taken to The House of Illusion, the carnival's funhouse, and is sacrificed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T07:23:31-07:00","id":995184,"title":"","content":"Sorry for double posting but i got another question. Is it okay if a couple of Lahmashu are part of the carnival's sideshow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T09:18:37-07:00","id":995233,"title":"","content":"Of course. They'd have to be low depth otherwise you'd just end up with a Gravity Falls &quot;Real magic just freaks people out.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T09:48:18-07:00","id":995242,"title":"","content":"Ok. Also, For the sideshow, they would probably give the Lahmashu titles based on their disfigurements. For example, if they have a hegen in their freak show they would label him &quot; The Amazing Frog Man.&quot; Also, how much trouble could a carnival-based cult cause? Finally, how hard would it be for their Leviathan to keep an eye on them when they constantly move from town to town, sometimes ending up in a different state?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-29-2016, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T15:50:31-07:00","id":995387,"title":"","content":"If it is okay with you Raven, i will post some fiction about the carnival before posting the stats. Also, i have an idea for a second idea for a cult that has a Masonic feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T09:38:52-07:00","id":998801,"title":"","content":"Chapter Four is done: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XTwtl5WQoYpi2LTpkbNuMcX-wjW8l6C4bK8vz3TSAFo/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...vz3TSAFo/edit#</a><br /> <br /> Next up is the Chapter on Cults. Which will probably be quick since I think the draft can be used as is.<br /> <br /> [edit] I've also updated chapter two, replacing the quote opening each Strain with a quote from the Bible showing the ancient Israelites acting like that Strain's Beloved (still looking for one for the Lahamin). I'm actually very pleased how quickly I could find good bible quotes for each, it suggests the Beloved's behavioural patterns were chosen well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-05-2016, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T23:54:36-07:00","id":999092,"title":"","content":"Need any sample characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T00:39:12-07:00","id":999104,"title":"","content":"I would like some <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T01:56:24-08:00","id":999126,"title":"","content":"Chapter five is now up: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FclymCyf4TB9JiG7lat3bbPGYKZGbkVYq3f7G7Wl32U/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...7G7Wl32U/edit#</a><br /> <br /> As I thought the cults document was pretty much used as is so this didn't take long. Chapter six is Merits, Channels, and Rituals. I'm going to put what I have up then move on to formatting Chapter seven (Antagonists) for now. There's still a lot of rituals and channels work to be written.<br /> <br /> My plan is to work towards a complete alpha document - that is to have everything except individual powers like channels and mutations fully written up in a single file. After that I'll worry about the missing powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T22:44:15-08:00","id":1000157,"title":"","content":"Proofreading proceeding apace; sample character somewhat less so, but it's going. Have you considered coming up with Strain epithets beyond Bahamutan, Lahamin et al. -- like, I don't know, Behemoths for Bahamutans, or the Thousand Young for Dagonites... etc., etc.? It could break up the text a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T01:47:15-08:00","id":1000187,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the proof reading, it's really appreciated.<br /> <br /> As for epithets, I have not thought about it until now.<br /> <br /> Behemoths were an antagonist splat in Leviathan 1E, I'm not sure if I'll keep them in 2E but I'm leaning against that epithet to keep the option open. Which is a shame since it works really well. Titans might be a second best.<br /> <br /> Judges works well for Tanninim. It's already used to describe them here and there. I'm not really coming up with any ideas for the others...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T13:55:34-08:00","id":1003046,"title":"","content":"Chapter seven is almost done. Just Typhons and Ophions to go. Meanwhile Richard T Powell had a neat idea for reworking Tranquillity. I've written up his concept here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jVlHheLw0478DJAdQvBALIQLYQxh9N8DSnDmva1t-7s/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...mva1t-7s/edit#</a><br /> <br /> What does everyone think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:39:58-08:00","id":1003132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1003046#post1003046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapter seven is almost done. Just Typhons and Ophions to go. Meanwhile Richard T Powell had a neat idea for reworking Tranquillity. I've written up his concept here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jVlHheLw0478DJAdQvBALIQLYQxh9N8DSnDmva1t-7s/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...mva1t-7s/edit#</a><br /> <br /> What does everyone think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Looks interesting. Since Tranquility is rated from 1-12 now, and the natures can grow, what does it meant to occupy one side? The effects of having one's nature grow is outlined, but not the current rating.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, instead of the natures inflicting penalties when their total expansion hits a certain level, they just have scaling penalties/effect when you are &quot;in&quot; them? As they grow, you can fall further into them anyways, and as both grow, a Leviathan has smaller &quot;wiggle room&quot; to move around on the Tranquility scale before hitting some kind of penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T18:06:46-08:00","id":1003174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1003046#post1003046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapter seven is almost done. Just Typhons and Ophions to go. Meanwhile Richard T Powell had a neat idea for reworking Tranquillity. I've written up his concept here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jVlHheLw0478DJAdQvBALIQLYQxh9N8DSnDmva1t-7s/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...mva1t-7s/edit#</a><br /> <br /> What does everyone think?</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds cool, but the way erosion triggers seems to be more Morality based instead of pulling from Integrity as inspiration. Maybe instead of just rolling a flat amount of set dice they could instead be rolling to resist their breaking point with a penalty based on their own stats to reflect their own nature's rebelling against them. Like for example:<br /> <br /> Bestial side is offended: Resolve+Composure - Strength to see if the monster gets fed a part of their mind.<br /> Divine side is triggered: Stamina+Composure - Intelligence to keep the little god that lives in their head little.<br /> <br /> If it being based on Morality was intentional please forget I posted anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11554-fate-inker","name":"Fate Inker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T01:28:19-08:00","id":1003289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1003132#post1003132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps, instead of the natures inflicting penalties when their total expansion hits a certain level, they just have scaling penalties/effect when you are &quot;in&quot; them?</div> </div> </div> </div> I cannot comment without some idea of what &quot;in them&quot; means and how it might happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fate Inker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1003174#post1003174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it being based on Morality was intentional please forget I posted anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was indeed intentional. It's based on the 2E Humanity rules from Vampire.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T03:42:13-08:00","id":1003306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1003289#post1003289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I cannot comment without some idea of what &amp;quot;in them&amp;quot; means and how it might happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Starting Leviathan has Tranquility 7, Bestial 1, Divine 12. Their Tranquility can range from 2 to 11 without hit either extreme. Say Bestial grows to 3 dots - then the range is 4 to 11. If the Leviathan hits Tranquility 3, they are &quot;in&quot; the Bestial range now, whereas before they wouldn't have been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T04:02:50-08:00","id":1003310,"title":"","content":"And how would Tranquility &quot;move&quot; in this system? Currently Tranquility is just 12 - beastal dots - divine dots.<br /> <br /> That said. Currently the system has two moving parts: beastal dots and divine dots. I'm hesitant to add a third.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T06:38:11-08:00","id":1003360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1003310#post1003310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how would Tranquility &quot;move&quot; in this system? Currently Tranquility is just 12 - beastal dots - divine dots.<br /> <br /> That said. Currently the system has two moving parts: beastal dots and divine dots. I'm hesitant to add a third.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then is ceases to make sense as one bar. It's really just two tracks. When I first read it, I was thinking [B][ ][ ][ ][ ][ ][\u2022][ ][ ][ ][ ][D], where the \u2022 would fluctuate, but hitting the B or the D zones would mean you are under the sway of your Bestial or Divine natures. As either track grew, it would become easier and easier to enter those danger zones, but otherwise it is an Integrity track like normal (though closer to Harmony). If there isn't any movement in the center, it makes no sense putting them both on the same track.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T07:23:48-08:00","id":1003377,"title":"","content":"Well yes. It is pretty much the old two track system but with a different presentation. I thought that was clear.<br /> <br /> Anyway; what did you imagine would move the \u2022 and how would it be different from the things that make the B/D zones grow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-15-2016, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T07:30:42-08:00","id":1003380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1003377#post1003377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yes. It is pretty much the old two track system but with a different presentation. I thought that was clear.<br /> <br /> Anyway; what did you imagine would move the \u2022? The only things I can think of are the things that would make the Divine/Beastal nature grow - and using the same thing twice isn't the best idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you could basically treat most instances like Harmony (break towards Bestial or Divine) which moves Tranquility. Have Dramatic Failure or certain other extreme actions actually have Bestial or Divine colonize more dots on the chart. Maybe, Penalties are how close to the edge you are (moving Tranquility will do it, as will that nature growing) like with Health and Wound Penalties. If you ever enter one of those dots, you become a Typhon (if you fall into the Bestial range), or an Ophion (if you hit the Divine range). As you badly mess up more, you have less room for Tranquility to move (and the Penalties start hitting no matter how balanced you are). Screw up enough, and there simply isn't any room left and you fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T07:55:25-08:00","id":1003391,"title":"","content":"A Harmony like system is actually something I'm keen to avoid. A Leviathan who commits both kinds of wicked behaviour equally should be in a worse spot than a Leviathan that only does bad things in line with the besteal nature. It's not about finding a balance bewteen the divine and the god; it's two different sets of wicked instincts both of which must be resisted.<br /> <br /> Thinking a bit more about this. The only way such a system could work is if the \u2022 could move from any point on the track to any point on the track in a single jump. If it just moves one place at a time then you might as well give an extra box to the beastal or divine nature. If it enters a box occupied by the beast or divine nature something bad happens (but not turning into an Ophion/Typhon).<br /> <br /> That still leaves the question of what could cause the \u2022 to jump; and if it's better to make the drawbacks of either nature growing too much random or persistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T13:26:11-08:00","id":1006365,"title":"","content":"I've merged in the new Tranquility system - as discussed above it's not <i>that</i> different from the old one but it's a cool visual. I've also finished chapter seven; actually chapter seven was finished a few days ago. It just got held back by my search for a good quote for Ophions. I found a nice one from Person of Interest after wracking my brain for artificial intelligence related quotes. (I really wanted a sci-fi quote to show how the Tribe represent things about humanity that are timeless, &quot;we come in many, many guises&quot;).<br /> <br /> This means the only things left to do are Hybrids/Lahmasu (done), Evolutions, and the Rift. Then the Alpha release will be complete. Evolutions and the Rift will probably be very much like 1E, because I don't have any better ideas. I'm not sure if the individual examples of evolutions will survive the transition. I have doubts about their quality.<br /> <br /> Looking at you, 6 years ago The Kings Raven <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-21-2016, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T11:38:41-08:00","id":1007351,"title":"","content":"First of all, just wanna say how much I love this project. It's honestly just so amazing.<br /> <br /> That being said, is there a chance of us getting a character sheet? I have no idea how to make it, especially with a system as different as Leviathan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11767-newsiedoosie","name":"Newsiedoosie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T00:05:25-08:00","id":1007601,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid I don't have the skills to make a charachter sheet. The only person I know who has the talent is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24\" data-vbnamecard=\"24\">Mr Gone</a> so I guess I'll direct the question to you Mr Gone. How plausible would it be to make a charachter sheet for Leviathan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T05:29:40-08:00","id":1007669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1007601#post1007601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid I don't have the skills to make a charachter sheet. The only person I know who has the talent is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24\" data-vbnamecard=\"24\">Mr Gone</a> so I guess I'll direct the question to you Mr Gone. How plausible would it be to make a charachter sheet for Leviathan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey! Umm...I guess if you can compile a list of all the things you'd need on a sheet, and how you think it might need to look, I can add it to my list. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You can post it here, message me or email me...whatever is easier...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T08:24:57-08:00","id":1007712,"title":"","content":"Awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For Attributes I'd go for 10 dots. In theory a Leviathan can go beyond that, but regular character sheets don't go beyond 5 dots when the maximum is ten. For Leviathan 10 dots for a maximum of 17 should have a similar balance. (Leviathans can't boost Skills past 10).<br /> <br /> The following traits are just renames:<br /> <br /> Power stat: Sheol<br /> Energy Stat: Ichor<br /> X-Splat: Strain<br /> Y-Splat: School<br /> Z-Splat: Evolution<br /> Virtue: Upwelling<br /> Vice: Undertow<br /> <br /> Integrity Trait: Leviathans have an unusual integrity trait called Tranquility. It has 12 boxes not 10 dots (ideally they'd be vertical), and each box can be empty, occupied by the divine nature, or occupied by the bestial nature. The divine nature always occupies the top box and grows downwards. The bestial nature always occupies the bottom box and grows upwards. Both the divine and bestial nature cannot grow beyond seven boxes total so the middle two boxes can potentially belong to either.<br /> <br /> Willpower: This would need a second set of dots in brackets (like Princess has)<br /> <br /> Size could be split into 6 different numbers; but that might not be worth the effort.<br /> The Ripple Effect should be included with Size, it's just a space to write a number.<br /> For Health I'd suggest having space to write numbers rather than boxes. Since Size is health Leviathans can get enormous health quite easily.<br /> <br /> <br /> For supernatural powers Leviathans have 4:<br /> <br /> Atavisms: Which can be lesser, greater, or ancient. The theoretical maximum is to have 2/3/2 atavisms and each Atavism is linked to an Attribute. You can have multiple Atavisms for a single attribute.<br /> <br /> Channels/Birthright. These are simply a you have them or you don't.<br /> <br /> Adaptations: These have a dot rating and are always associated with a Channel.<br /> <br /> Codified Rituals: In a word, Mage Rotes.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Leviathan sheet will definitely need space for a Cult. The Cult should have the following traits:<br /> <br /> Name<br /> Structure (one of eight options)<br /> Fervour rated 1 - 7<br /> Piety rated 1 - 7<br /> Zeal rated 1 - 5<br /> Space for the Cult's Merits<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For the general look, well I'm not sure if this is practical, but I imagined a sort of dishevelled academia look. As though this were one of H.P. Lovecraft's half mad investigator's research notes. The colour scheme is a watery blue/green - like the opening picture in <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ISiYxINVYvbHsFDcXKopDS8Lxwa0RzNIVgIWQcjg5Qw/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...WQcjg5Qw/edit#</a><br /> <br /> Let me know if you have any more questions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/membe