rld-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:29:59-08:00","id":1034781,"title":"","content":"Question about the Erosion Triggers in Chapter Four. There are multiple instances of &quot;human contact&quot; and &quot;losing touch with blood relatives&quot;.<br /> <br /> If I were a member of the School of Sand and believed that I could stave off Erosion through Skype alone, would Skype chats stave off Erosion, would I gain a bonus on the Erosion roll for following the Direction of the School, or would Skype have no effect on the Erosion roll, i.e. would 'contact' require you to be physically present?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":867,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","user":"Jimborg","date":". 01-19-2017, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T15:04:14-08:00","id":1034889,"title":"","content":"Skype would provide some protection, either bonus dice or longer durations between rolls, but not full immunity.<br /> <br /> The first time you used Skype you'd get a chance to regain Tranquility. If you wanted you could build an Evolution around using Skype which would replace the first time restriction with a far lesser restriction that you can attempt to regain Tranquility every time you solve significant problem by using Skype.<br /> <br /> This Evolution sounds really powerful, and it is, but if Skype is made obsolete it can leave a Leviathan in a serious bind. There's probably an Ophion or two out there that thought the telegram is the final solution to the wake cutting leviathans off from mortals they cared about. With a bit more effort (it will probably be a pure roleplaying restriction) you could make the evolution work on anything similar to Skype, but it would be extreemly hard to make an Evolution that could still function after a fundamental technology shift such as replacing Skype with virtual reality or holographic projectors.<br /> <br /> A School of Sand Leviathan who managed to make a future proof Evolution that functions with any instant communication technology can essentially be said to have won the game. Even if admittedly the difference between future proof and only working with Skype is zero in most games since most games don't have 100 year timeskips.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T01:26:32-08:00","id":1035127,"title":"","content":"Sample character.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Anneke \u201cAnswer\u201d Herbert</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Strain</b>: Lahamin</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>School</b>: Abyss</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Concept</b>: Waterpark Horror</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Undertow</b>: The Nest-Maker</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Upwelling</b>: The Mother</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">STR: 2 DEX: 3 STA: 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">INT: 2 WIT: 3 RES: 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">PRE: 2 MAN: 2 COM: 3</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sheol</b>: 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Ichor</b>: 8/12</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Willpower</b>: 5/5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Tranquility</b>: 7 [3 bestial, 2 divine]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Skills</b>:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Stealth 4 (Underwater Environments), Larceny 3, Athletics 3 (Small Spaces) (Deep Pools), Weaponry 2, Survival 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Occult 2, Science 2, Medicine 1 (First Aid), Crafts 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Animal Ken 2 (Aquatic Life), Intimidation 2 (Get The Fuck Back!), Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 1</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Atavisms</b>:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Lesser</i>: Presence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Greater</i>: Wits</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Ancient</i>: Dexterity</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Vestiges</b>:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Awareness, Predation, Elements</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Cult</b>: Fervor 2, Piety 1, Zeal 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cWaterpark patrons, including the vagrants who squat in park facilities after dark.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Merits</b>:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Fame (\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Gatewater (\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Home Turf (\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Double-Jointed (\u2022)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Anneke was born in a compound in Maine \u2014 an old seaside resort converted to a group home years ago, by some long-dead leviathan. There, she was raised on a doctrine in which Gnostic Christianity and Progenitor worship intertwined: children were taught to fear and adore the serpent-goddess Sophia, mother of the Earth, and to fear her son, who had imprisoned her in the physical world. Back then, Anneke was <i>Answers-Contained-Within-The-Flesh Herbert</i>, called Answer by her fellows, since the community had taken on the Puritan tradition of naming children after lines from its holy texts. Answer was never entirely satisfied with her life in the compound, and after learning that the world outside wasn\u2019t a wasteland, she staged an escape through an old quarry beneath the hotel.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">As a photogenic late-teenaged escapee, Answer \u2014 who took the name <i>Anneke</i> from a phone book to commemorate her new life \u2014 got her fifteen minutes of fame across the U.S., inspiring negligent local authorities to crack down on the Maine compound. Once they were over, Anneke decided to put the past behind her. She moved to Arizona, embracing an atheistic worldview and a career as a waitress (to put herself through <i>real</i> high school), and that would have been the end of her story, if she hadn\u2019t woken up one morning with the eyelid of her left eye gone.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Her Metamorphosis started slow. Anneke thought it was a medical emergency \u2014 the doctors gave her eyedrops and scheduled a battery of tests. When she developed the power to see guilt, she was convinced she was delusional \u2014 her doctors prescribed therapy and antipsychotics. Then, the situation escalated: she ended up driving another waitress to a psychotic episode, and fled, realizing that the old preacher\u2019s stories about serpent-spawn and dragons and the will of Eve had been true all along. About that time, she began to need water, to crave immersion. Sun City is landlocked; only after sequestering herself in a water park for a few weeks (and finding an underground reservoir to squat in), stealing Popsicles and raiding the snack stand, did she complete her Metamorphosis, and gain a measure of control over her form.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Nowadays, Anneke\u2019s Wake has begun to call to the patrons, some of whom discover her and begin to worship, and the waitress has been hunting for information about her, about the old Maine compound and her escape, though whether it\u2019s as a supplicant or an Ahab isn\u2019t clear. Some of the park's underground pipe systems have produced a natural Gatewater, and Rift exploration has provided insight to a girl with very little understanding of her situation and endless time on her hands; confronted with any kind of lead, be it Lahmasu, Hybrids or other Leviathans, she would commit all her resources to figuring out what, exactly, has happened to her. Left alone too long, on the other hand, she could easily lose the measure of stability that she found in escaping her childhood\u2026 and with the powers of the Tribe and an eschatology to grant unto her followers, Answer Herbert could rebuild her old faith in the depths of Sun City's artificial sea.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:22:37-08:00","id":1036114,"title":"","content":"Nice charachter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I've uploaded the Lahmasu and wrote the 2E Evolutions appendix. Which means that the initial Alpha draft is officially complete <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The next stage is to fill out the individual channels, mutations, etc. That will probably take a while. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T10:06:10-08:00","id":1040738,"title":"","content":"Hey there -- I just found this.<br /> <br /> I was inspired by the old Leviathan: the Tempest, and worked on updating and streamlining it for a while -- my plan had been to create a more pulpish World of Darkness, with Leviathans, Geniuses, and Princesses replacing the old vampire-mage-werewolf bit, and strong roles for promethians and changeling.<br /> <br /> Here's two documents I used for leviathan, uploaded to Google Docs. Feel free to use any ideas, and I'd be interested to hear any criticism. They're nothing like the polished finished project you're putting together! Just mechanic changes for play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B4Sp-qmJ_qXwa3d4UnpZSXpGU0k/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B4Sp-qmJ_qXwa3d4UnpZSXpGU0k/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B4Sp-qmJ_qXwa3d4UnpZSXpGU0k/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B4Sp-qmJ_qXwa3d4UnpZSXpGU0k/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B4Sp-qmJ_qXwNThQaEtaeUdkRVk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B4Sp-qmJ_qXwNThQaEtaeUdkRVk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B4Sp-qmJ_qXwNThQaEtaeUdkRVk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B4Sp-qmJ_qXwNThQaEtaeUdkRVk/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12922-zebediah","name":"Zebediah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T10:36:14-08:00","id":1047769,"title":"","content":"I think a good place to start for replacing the attribute boosting channels is looking at the unique powers they grant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew thought process.<br /> &quot;I have this great idea for a power/splat/merit/etc/&quot;<br /> &quot;I have no idea if this is balanced, useless, or gamebreaking.&quot;<br /> &quot;I'll ask the internet&quot;<br /> &quot;The thread has died.&quot; <img src=\"images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4226-spiderlord","name":"Spiderlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T10:39:55-08:00","id":1048819,"title":"","content":"Seeking clarification regarding the interaction of the Ocean Minds and the Leviathan's cult. It's stated that a cult is metaphysically a part of itself, and effects that alter the Leviathian's emotions, mind, or soul perpetrated by the cult bypass this protection. But does the protection work the other way? Do a leviathan's cultist get some lesser version of Ocean Minds to protect against such direct manipulation? The only explicit defensive bonus they have so far is when rival Leviathans try to poach them for their own cults.<br /> <br /> For that matter, how deep is the metaphysical connection between a Leviathan and their Cult/Ahab?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":867,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","user":"Jimborg","date":". 02-16-2017, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T11:47:51-08:00","id":1050625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1048819#post1048819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeking clarification regarding the interaction of the Ocean Minds and the Leviathan's cult. It's stated that a cult is metaphysically a part of itself, and effects that alter the Leviathian's emotions, mind, or soul perpetrated by the cult bypass this protection. But does the protection work the other way? Do a leviathan's cultist get some lesser version of Ocean Minds to protect against such direct manipulation?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not beyond the purely mundane protection granted by being a fanatical cultist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1048819#post1048819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter, how deep is the metaphysical connection between a Leviathan and their Cult/Ahab?</div> </div> </div> </div>On a metaphysical level a Leviathan and her Beloved/Ahabs are kinda the same entity. But aside from things like Ritual's Knowledge or a Mage's Sympathetic magic it's fairly hard to exploit that sameness - a bit like Archmage's and their subsouls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:11:20-08:00","id":1050955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1050625#post1050625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a metaphysical level a Leviathan and her Beloved/Ahabs are kinda the same entity. But aside from things like Ritual's Knowledge or a Mage's Sympathetic magic it's fairly hard to exploit that sameness - a bit like Archmage's and their subsouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, they're only &quot;the same&quot; to certain metaphysical checks that ask &quot;are A (cultist) and B (Leviathan) the same?&quot;, but they obviously aren't the same in spatial location, mental identity, etc.<br /> <br /> ...Though that does provide some inspiration for a few powers (Ritual, Vestige, Adaptation) - turning your &quot;yous&quot; into a Hive-Mind, or acting through them spatially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T09:34:55-08:00","id":1051023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1050955#post1050955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, they're only &quot;the same&quot; to certain metaphysical checks that ask &quot;are A (cultist) and B (Leviathan) the same?&quot;, but they obviously aren't the same in spatial location, mental identity, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div> Correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1050955#post1050955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Though that does provide some inspiration for a few powers (Ritual, Vestige, Adaptation) - turning your &quot;yous&quot; into a Hive-Mind, or acting through them spatially.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. There's already a few like that - Eye of the Watchful Deity for example. I don't think I've written it yet, but there's definately going to be an Adaptation that means a Leviathan can ignore the fact they're dead so long as a single person (or object) with Knowledge of them left in existance.<br /> <br /> (You really want Eye of the Watchful Deity + Prophets or some other way of interacting with the world without distance limiters because you'll still erode without human contact; but there's probably a bunch of &quot;dead but dreaming&quot; Ophions around)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T19:33:58-08:00","id":1051313,"title":"","content":"Oh! Speaking of rituals, I had an idea for a ritual that gave a selected sub-group of people &quot;The Black Spot&quot; or something similar that left them by tracked by the Leviathan, no matter where they go. I'm not sure of the exact mechanical implementation, but since this the only WoD game centered on themes of an aquatic nature, I thought you guys might be able to do something with the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T00:22:00-08:00","id":1051399,"title":"","content":"That sounds like it would be a Create Predation ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T18:56:24-08:00","id":1052966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1051399#post1051399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like it would be a Create Predation ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh neat! I wasn't sure what a &quot;Predation&quot; Ritual would invoke.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I had some time earlier this month, and I wrote up some crossover notes:<br /> <br /> <b>Demon</b><br /> <br /> Demons can drive the hardest bargains when people are at their most desperate, and few situations are more desperate than when a leviathan is involved. An unscrupulous demon can turn any conflict spurred by the presence of a leviathan into a pacting <i>bonanza</i>. An enterprising unchained could offer information, resources and/or weapons to an Ahab in exchange for their signature, then shift into a different Cover and do the same thing for the leviathan(\u2018s cult). And this all before you include family members seeking to free cultists of the leviathan\u2019s influence, free hybrids seeking to be rid of the Tribe\u2019s genetic influence, or cultists seeking to become <i>more</i> divine. All available with the stroke of a pen.<br /> <br /> A leviathan can easily convince a cultist to sign a pact on their behalf, though doing so almost always provokes an Enuoia roll. And while hybrids can be rid of the tribe\u2019s influence through demonic pacts, leviathans themselves have no such easy out: whatever mechanism that permits the unchained to interface with reality\u2019s source code cannot alter the leviathan\u2019s divine nature. Any pact that attempts to do so has no effect, with any resources committed to the pact wasted in the attempt.<br /> <br /> Leviathans and demons both retain the full effectiveness of their unique defenses against each other: the leviathan\u2019s supernatural senses have just much trouble picking through the lies of the unchained as much as the demon struggles against the leviathan's resistance against direct manipulation.<br /> <br /> <b>Is the God Machine a god?</b><br /> <br /> Short answer: No.<br /> <br /> Rather than a singular natural force, the God Machine is better comprehended as a series of networked intelligences, whose presence is represented in the World of Darkness by angels and infrastructure. It does not directly interact with or give blessings to humanity. What influence it does exert is done through intermediaries: for example, the Ink Endowments of the Knights of St. Adrian are the result of angelic blessings, and technically not the work of the greater God Machine.<br /> <br /> Anyone who worships the God Machine directly will either be ignored outright, or incorporated into the God Machine\u2019s inscrutable plans, either as an asset or as spare parts.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean</b><br /> <br /> At first glance, Leviathans and the Created appear to be long lost cousins. Both are creatures whose supernatural nature have forced them to isolate themselves from humanity. Both wear a human guise that conceals their true, inhuman self. Both of them even share the ability to drag themselves back from Death\u2019s doorway. Add to the fact that Leviathans are largely immune to a Promethean\u2019s Disquiet, and you end up with the <i>bizarre</i> situation of a Leviathan\u2019s cult being one of the safer places for a Promethean to be.<br /> <br /> Appearances can be deceiving however, and like most of the relationships the two groups have, it almost always ends in tragedy.<br /> <br /> The ultimate sticking point between the two is their relationship to humanity. While the Created attempt to move closer to humanity, the Leviathan finds their power pushing them <i>away</i> from humanity, both externally with the growth of the Wake, and internally, with their Channels making their true forms ever more monstrous.<br /> <br /> Even the <i>suggestion</i> that it\u2019s possible become human again is often enough for desperate Leviathans to become dangerously possessive of the Created, and what the Prometheans thought was a sanctuary among the Tribes\u2019 cultists can quickly become a prison. Adding to the friction is that while the Leviathan\u2019s power gives them protection against the mental effects of Disquiet, it does <i>not</i> prevent a Wasteland from forming around a Promethean.<br /> <br /> Whatever measures a leviathan put in place to counter the Ripples of the Wake must now also contend with supernatural blights on their land. This is especially worrying if the Promethean happens to be a Frankenstein who creates Wastelands of fire and lightning, the Tribe\u2019s ancestral bane; or an Osiran whose Wasteland introduces droughts and steals the moisture from the air, potentially threatening the Leviathan\u2019s ability to utilize their two most powerful stages of transformation and their supply of divine Ichor.<br /> <br /> At this point, it\u2019s up to the Leviathan whether to slay the Created and see if the secrets of the Divine Fire can be dissected from their corpse, join the countless others who have expelled the Created from their lands, or attempt to find some way to mitigate the Wasteland before Hunters come knocking.<br /> <br /> <b>If you gaze into the Abyss\u2026</b><br /> <br /> A possible exception to the above scenario are those Leviathans who belong to the School of the Abyss. The School is oriented around severing their connections to humanity and would therefore be the most likely to avoid falling into the behavior patterns described above. This does not mean that the followers of the Sunken School are in <i>any</i> way \u201csafer\u201d than those of other philosophies, rather that the nature of the threat they present to the Created is radically different.<br /> <br /> To those of the Sunken School, the goal of the Pilgrimage seems completely baffling: why in the world would you want to become more human? Isn\u2019t humanity your greatest source of grief? Look at the nutbar cultists that dog my steps; why in the world would you want to be more like <i>that</i>?<br /> <br /> To a Promethean who has been frustrated and stymied by humanity's continued rejection of them, these arguments are seductive. Add to the fact that leviathans are almost completely immune to Disquiet and that members of the School of the Abyss are likely in the best position to handle the Wastelands that follow the Prometheans (the examples above notwithstanding), and the resolve of the most determined of the Created might start to waver.<br /> <br /> Of course, tragedy dogs the steps of such a relationship, even if it\u2019s longer in coming. Despite being created in humanity\u2019s image, a Promethean is not mortal and does not count as such for the purposes of preventing Erosion. Even though the Direction of the School of the Abyss significantly slows the process, any leviathan who stubbornly remains in isolation from humanity is doomed to eventually be devoured by either their bestial or divine nature, whereupon the Promethean will get a first hand example of what a lack of humanity <i>really</i> looks like.<br /> <br /> The development of the Created are similarly stymied. Attempting to analyze the behavior of a levithan\u2019s cult as an example of humanity produces contradictory and confusing answers. Through the funhouse mirror-like distorting and twisting brought about by the Wake, no clear or consistent examples of the human mind can be distinguished.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage</b><br /> <br /> Leviathans who have heard the stories of the Sky Wizards of Marduk would be very wary when dealing with the Awakened. Their worries are only reinforced when they discover that the Obrimos claim to be the agents of the divine and are able to produce the Tribe\u2019s electric bane at will.<br /> <br /> This wariness is replicated on the Awakend\u2019s side, as Mages who discover the effects of the Leviathan\u2019s Wake can easily mistake the them for some kind of Abyssal creature. Those attempting to attack the Leviathan through Sympathetic connections would be shocked and horrified to learn that doing so made them equally as vulnerable to the Leviathan\u2019s Knowledge based powers, cranking their natural paranoia up to 11.<br /> <br /> An experienced Leviathan can be one of the most tenacious foes a Cabal can face. Leviathans are all but immune to mind control and other forms of direct manipulation, their thoughts can\u2019t be read without risking madness, attempting to kill them at a distance opens the Awakened up to Knowledge based powers, and attempting to slay a Leviathan in the past or future has no effect on the Leviathan in the prime time line, not to mention that said Leviathan is capable of the paradoxical feat of remembering what the Cabal hasn\u2019t done yet. Add in the Leviathan\u2019s aquatic nature, and speculating Mages can\u2019t help but wonder if the Tribe played a role in the downfall of Atlantis.<br /> <br /> <b>A Deal with The Devil</b><br /> <br /> Leviathans are objects of fascination and fear for the Awakened, and nowhere is this clearer than with the Mastigos. Attempting to read the thoughts of the Tribe brings them in direct contact with one of the most potent psychic forces they\u2019ve ever encountered, not to mention that their hyper dimensional nature duplicates the more subtle effects of Space. In addition, any Mastigos who learns of the existence of the Rift will immediately make parallels to Pandemonium, fueling speculation over exactly who and what those Sky Wizards were, and what their relationship was to Tiamat and Marduk, and what relationship, if any, they have with the Awakened.<br /> <br /> If the two groups are able to overcome their <i>incredible</i> mutual paranoia, they would find that each has resources to offer to the other. The Key and The Gate is a simpler way to gather information about the past and future of the World of Darkness, so long as they don\u2019t mind being restricted to the perspective of the Tribe\u2019s descendants. The leviathan\u2019s psychic might even grants the Awakened new avenues of attack against enemies who would otherwise provoke Paradox. Not to mention that their Cult can act on the Awakend\u2019s behalf.<br /> <br /> In return, the Awakened can act as a bridge to humanity for the Tribe. By casting Mind Shield, a Mastigos can steel a mortal against the effects of the Wake: used in this way, every dot of Mind negates a -1 penalty on Breaking Points caused by the Wake, with complete negation meaning they are no longer influenced by the Wake (If a Leviathan chooses to Focus the Wake, roll Clash of Wills). The simple act of having a conversation with a normal person without the Wake battering them into submission is incredibly life affirming, and makes a remarkably potent bargaining chip in the hands of the Awakened, a fact the Seers of the Throne are all too eager to exploit...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:16:51-08:00","id":1053415,"title":"","content":"One thing to bear in mind with Prometheans. The Divine Fire is in fact divine. If you want to outright say that the Gods powering Empyrean Theurgists and Judges are a form of the Divine Fire, or have a Qashmallim turn up in person to give a new Judge their commandment I can't see it contradicting anything in either gameline.<br /> <br /> Then there's the fact that both Azoth and Ichor contain the divine power of <i>creation</i> in a highly unstable form. One alone is trouble, but putting them together is like trying to mix... well, fire and water. The Tribe and the Created both have a fair amount they could offer each other, sadly their own fundamental natures are opposed.<br /> <br /> <br /> For Mage. The Symmetry between Sympathy and Knowledge is completely intentional. Thank PenDragon, it was his idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> some of the powers (Read Not the Tomes in particular) are actually designed specifically for Storytellers using Leviathans as antagonists in a Mage game.<br /> <br /> The Rift wouldn't be compared to Pandemonium though. The Rift is quite explicitly the Temenos, however it's the Tribe's Temenos not humanity's Temenos, there's no direct connection between the two Temenoi. Of course, that would be just as interesting to the inquiring Mage. Do bring a Thyrus or Moros though, you'll need gills or a supply of oxygen.<br /> <br /> The Tribe can also be the patron in Patron Yantras and probably other stuff as well. Someone (who knows Mage mechanics better than me) would have to figure out the details, but it would be quire appropriate to go through Summoners and add Leviathans as another potential thing to be summoned (or at least astral projections of said Leviathan).<br /> <br /> There also are ways to get around the Tribe's potent defences (especially if the Mages are PCs and the Leviathan is not). Turn a Heirloom into an Imbued Item for example (can you make an Imbued Item with a mind of it's own? If so you could just make it Beloved). So long as the Leviathan doesn't figure out what you're doing and start using the Item to target Rituals that could work. Plus, Mages have numbers on their side.<br /> <br /> Finally. I'd say it's the Pentacle not the Seer's who're busy exploiting the Tribe's desire to mind shield their friends and family. Part of the Seer's core manifesto is &quot;Enslave the Gods&quot;. IMO that includes Leviathans.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. My favourite crossover titbit. Vampires who drink Leviathan blood turn from undead to alive for as long as the blood is in their system. Mechanically this just means they get the Blush of Life for free and fall under Life Arcana rather than Death, they're still vampires with all that implies. They age normally though, their hair grows, they find it easier to change as a person, and when it wears of their current state becomes their new baseline state. <br /> <br /> They also have a risk of mutating, growing huge cancerous tumours, or spontaneously developing a Bloodline. There's probably a few Circle and Dragon aligned Bloodlines who's origins involved reckless use of Ichor. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 02-22-2017, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T11:12:16-08:00","id":1054378,"title":"","content":"Gasp! Senpai noticed me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"