gh. The Rift is quite explicitly the Temenos, however it's the Tribe's Temenos not humanity's Temenos, there's no direct connection between the two Temenoi. Of course, that would be just as interesting to the inquiring Mage. Do bring a Thyrus or Moros though, you'll need gills or a supply of oxygen. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Nuts! I thought for sure I found a Mind/Space correspondence. Oh well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1053415#post1053415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Tribe can also be the patron in Patron Yantras and probably other stuff as well. Someone (who knows Mage mechanics better than me) would have to figure out the details, but it would be quire appropriate to go through Summoners and add Leviathans as another potential thing to be summoned (or at least astral projections of said Leviathan). <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaaand add 2e Mage and Summoners to my Wishlist <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1053415#post1053415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There also are ways to get around the Tribe's potent defences (especially if the Mages are PCs and the Leviathan is not). Turn a Heirloom into an Imbued Item for example (can you make an Imbued Item with a mind of it's own? If so you could just make it Beloved). So long as the Leviathan doesn't figure out what you're doing and start using the Item to target Rituals that could work. Plus, Mages have numbers on their side.<br /> <br /> Finally. I'd say it's the Pentacle not the Seer's who're busy exploiting the Tribe's desire to mind shield their friends and family. Part of the Seer's core manifesto is &quot;Enslave the Gods&quot;. IMO that includes Leviathans. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>I... did not know this! Another reason to pick up 2e Mage!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1053415#post1053415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> P.S. My favourite crossover titbit. Vampires who drink Leviathan blood turn from undead to alive for as long as the blood is in their system. Mechanically this just means they get the Blush of Life for free and fall under Life Arcana rather than Death, they're still vampires with all that implies. They age normally though, their hair grows, they find it easier to change as a person, and when it wears of their current state becomes their new baseline state.<br /> <br /> They also have a risk of mutating, growing huge cancerous tumours, or spontaneously developing a Bloodline. There's probably a few Circle and Dragon aligned Bloodlines who's origins involved reckless use of Ichor. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Gosh darnit! I only have so much time for books &gt;.&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T13:17:31-08:00","id":1054440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1054378#post1054378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nuts! I thought for sure I found a Mind/Space correspondence. Oh well.</div> </div> </div> </div> At their core the Tribe are Mind/Life. Plus Divine, which doesn't really fit into any Arcana. Though like most splats they've got things from all over the 10 arcana spectrum.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T19:20:04-08:00","id":1054589,"title":"","content":"This is one of my sample cults.<br /> <br /> The Lorekeeper Society<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you were to compare Leviathan cults by sanity, The Lorekeeper would probably rank high on the sanity scale. Even though their god's wake does it's job on deteriorating their sanity, the members of this book collecting society has somehow managed to retain most of their sanity. Based in Washington D.C., The Lorekeepers have close ties to The Library of Congress, due to the fact that their founder was a employee of The Library. Their outside fa\u00e7ade is just a bunch of men toiling over dusty tomes and locating more books to place in their already crowded library. However, there is a feeling of something sinister deep within the clubhouse. But, no visitor can pinpoint where exactly.<br /> <br /> \u200bWithin the clubhouse there is a secret door that leads to a subterranean tunnel. This tunnel leads to what a bookworm would call, something out of Lovecraft. The tunnel leads to a alter room where the alter is covered in blood and where there is a idol of a terrible sea serpent. The serpent is their god. whether the god is male or female is a secret only the highest ranked members of the Society know. The leader of the cult is a man named Roderick Croswell, a tall, pale skinned man with black hair and gaunt features. Roderick used to be the leader of a other cult which was wiped out by the Mardukian's, along with their Leviathan. Roderick joined The Society in order to possibly find a book that could resurrect his goddess. During that time, he took over leadership of The Society and started to restructure it to make it fitting for his goddess when she inevitably returns. Since the goddess was a Oceanead he structured it in a way where it is assured that she would be entertained by the cultist's squabbling over promotions.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt is unknow how The Society discovered their god. But, in under five minutes of the god's first arrival, the wake took it's toll and completely made all of The Society's members devoted servants to the god. Today, the Society has a strict rank system. On the bottom are potential initiates while the top consists of the high priest and the Board of Directors of the club. Between therse are a bunch of squabbles, fights and competitions for promotions and every cultist hope that one day they will get to be a Board Member. Their god surprisingly has allowed them to continue collecting books and tomes. While they manage to keep a thin fa\u00e7ade of sanity, sometimes the insanity boils over and they do something stupid. For example, one of their larger members once beat the shit of a guy for no reason. This caused a manhunt which nearly exposed the cult. This has caused The Board to realize that the low-level cultists needed to be placed under a tighter reign. So, with approval from their god, they made it a rule that if anyone breaks a rule of the cult, they get beheaded and their body burnt on the altar. This new rule has managed to keep the cultists under control, but for how long?<br /> <br /> Fervor: 3<br /> Piety: 4<br /> Zeal:1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T21:14:15-08:00","id":1054631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1054440#post1054440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> At their core the Tribe are Mind/Life. Plus Divine, which doesn't really fit into any Arcana. Though like most splats they've got things from all over the 10 arcana spectrum.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><s>Divinity is actually under Prime's purview now.</s> Okay, that's not entirely accurate upon rereading. Divinity is part of Obrimos symbolism, but it isn't strictly part of Prime's purview. Though, I'd probably put it there as &quot;magic.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 02-25-2017, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T18:42:37-08:00","id":1055494,"title":"","content":"<b>Princess</b><br /> <br /> The nobility draw their power by painstakingly defending and uplifting humanity. By contrast, all the Tribe has to do is stand in a populated area, and the Wake will brutalize and twist the minds of everyone nearby, stripping away the veneer of civilization and leaving behind lesser creatures who eagerly submit themselves to the whims of a monstrous god.<br /> <br /> Such as it was in the time of the Old Kingdoms, and the intervening centuries haven\u2019t done much to change the situation. This alone make leviathans priority targets for the Nobility, especially if they're sitting in or near an area they\u2019ve chosen for their proto-kingdom. It\u2019s up to each individual Tribe member whether they seek to avoid the notice of the Nobility, strike them pre-emptively, or flee.<br /> <br /> <b>Mind Breaking Horrors</b><br /> <br /> It should be noted that the Nobles\u2019 closest allies, the Shikigami and the Sworn, lack the full protection of the Light the Nobles do and have Integrity instead of Belief. Although they can\u2019t become Beloved, this state does makes them vulnerable to the Leviathan's Wake, facing members of the Tribe in full Apotheosis, and any other power that has a greater effect against those with Integrity.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that while most supernatural effects treat Nobles in their Mundane and Transformed states as two different people, the two forms share the same mind and are thus equally vulnerable to effects that use the Knowledge modifier. This makes <i>Somebody Else\u2019s Problem</i>, a Charm that deletes the memories of the user, one of the most effective ways of defending against the Leviathan\u2019s rituals. Could the Queen of Mirrors have intentionally devised the Charm as a defense against a Leviathan's more insidious powers? Theories abound and The Queen certainly isn\u2019t talking.<br /> <br /> <b>Leviathan cults of Darkness?</b><br /> <br /> Given the unholy acts committed during a leviathan's rituals, and their precarious Integrity, a Leviathan\u2019s cult appears to be prime candidates to be tainted and corrupted by the Outer Darkness. In practice, this almost never happens.<br /> <br /> As horrific as the effects of the Wake are, it does grant the Leviathan\u2019s cult protection against competing influences, including the effects of the darkness (Treat the Outer Darkness as a Poaching Leviathan, using the dice pool of the local Taint or relevant power). Only an especially powerful taint could gain a foothold on those so claimed, and any area so <i>thoroughly</i> tainted often bears obvious scars of whatever sins were committed there, leaving such areas as the refuge of the truly desperate or arrogant.<br /> <br /> Even if a leviathan were aware of the existence of the darkness, most wouldn\u2019t use it. Their divine might trumps most powers offered by the darkness, not to mention that leviathans feel a certain instinctual revulsion at the mutations inflicted by the darkness. The divine Ichor is a catalyst of life and growth, however hideous and unstable it may be. The influence of the Outer Darkness, by contrast, can only degrade and decay.<br /> <br /> Of course, there\u2019s nothing stopping an enterprising cultist of the darkness from taking advantage of any taint left behind in a leviathan's temple after they have to skip town.<br /> <br /> <b>Are the Queens gods?</b><br /> <br /> Not quite.<br /> <br /> While the Queens do promote (what they see as) virtuous behaviour and grant power to their followers, their purview does not extend to humanity as a whole, nor do they possess the mystical potency or inclination to fuel miraculous rituals. Their <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i> is for humanity to lift <i>themselves</i> up out of the darkness, not for them to rely on divine assistance, however well intentioned.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that Queens lack the power to produce wide ranging supernatural effects as can be produced by rituals, so long as it's keeping with the themes of their Invocations. It\u2019s just they have to produce such magic <i>personally</i>, and can\u2019t grant those powers to another person on their behalf.<br /> <br /> While the Queen of Storms <i>theoretically</i> has the power to fuel miraculous rituals, in practice, the collection of souls that make up her gestalt Empress body denies her the focus that would be available to a singular divine soul. Which is just as well, as her power would almost certainly be just as dangerous to those invoking her power as to their intended targets.<br /> <br /> <b>Genius</b><br /> <br /> Where one threatens to drag humanity back to the bronze age, the other is the herald of an uncertain future. One is the scion of divine blood, the other graced with mad Inspiration. One expresses their power through monstrous transformation, the other through miraculous invention. It\u2019d be difficult to imagine two creatures that are more different than the Inspired and Earth\u2019s Most Wicked Tribe.<br /> <br /> Of those Inspired belonging to the Peerage, the Progenitors are the most interested in the Tribe. The biology of a hyperdimensional aquatic demigod is fascinating to them, and are attracted, perhaps to an unhealthy degree, of the mutagenic possibilities of the Divine Ichor. Their attempts to capture a Leviathan as experimental specimens tend to go badly for everyone involved.<br /> <br /> Due to their natural inclination for exploring into and beyond the dark corners of the world, the Navigators tend to encounter Leviathans the most often, especially those who have or are in the process of succumbing their inhuman natures. Seeing Leviathans at the height of their wickedness has left the Navigators with a \u201cshoot first, ask questions later\u201d mentality when dealing with the Tribe. <br /> <br /> The other members of the Peerage often ignore the Tribe unless their activities directly affect whatever plans or experiments they have. Though it is advised that the Tribe keep a healthy distance from the Inspired regardless, as most take it personally when their lab assistants are swept up in the Wake.<br /> <br /> <b>\u201cWe won\u2019t have these problems when <i>I</i> rule the world!\u201d</b><br /> <br /> If one were to look beneath surface comparisons of the Inspired and Earth\u2019s Most Wicked, similarities begin to emerge. Both have existed since time immemorial. Both have powers that isolate them from humanity, leaving them to struggle against an encroaching madness. And neither is entirely certain where their powers originate. Nowhere, however, are these similarities with the Tribe more pronounced than with the Bahraims of Lemuria. <br /> <br /> Like Lemuria, the Tribe believes that humanity has gone down the wrong path, i.e. any path not under the Tribe\u2019s rule. Like the Unmada of Lemuria, the members of the Tribe project a supernatural field that bends others towards their will and deepens their isolation them from the rational world.<br /> <br /> Despite all of this, an alliance between the Tribe and Lemuria is likely to only be one of convenience. Lemurians are all, to one degree or another, insane egomaniacs, and do not take kindly towards anything they perceive as attempting to usurp their vision.<br /> <br /> <b>Resetting the Clock</b><br /> <br /> For Leviathans seeking to reclaim the glory the Tribe had at it\u2019s apex of their rule, they could ask for no better weapon than the Clockstoppers. The Voids of Clockstoppers dampens the powers of thought and technology, and at higher levels of Acea, is able to return the purity of an age the Tribe thought has long since passed, when the powers of Earth\u2019s Most Wicked ruled humanity unopposed, the toys of the Marduk Society rendered all but impotent.<br /> <br /> By the same token however, a Leviathan can also be a Clockstopper\u2019s greatest enemy. Given that a Levithan\u2019s powers are not affected in the slightest by even the greatest of a Clockstopper\u2019s Voids, a truly bizarre twist of fate may bring it to pass that Earth\u2019s Most Wicked will be the only thing standing between them and a new Dark Age.<br /> <br /> <b>\u201cHow does it work? HOW DOES IT WORK?!?!\u201d</b><br /> <br /> While the Inspired an overall negative impression of the Tribe, either due to viewing at it them a primitive throwback, a dangerous abomination, or an uncooperative test specimen, that has NOTHING on enmity they reserve for the Marduk society.<br /> <br /> {I must defer to Void Drifter here, because he did this write up better than I could (http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles/page19)}","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T20:30:45-08:00","id":1055524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1055494#post1055494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Genius</b><br /> <br /> Of those Inspired belonging to the Peerage, the Progenitors are the most interested in the Tribe. The biology of a hyperdimensional aquatic demigod is fascinating to them, and are attracted, perhaps to an unhealthy degree, of the mutagenic possibilities of the Divine Ichor. Their attempts to capture a Leviathan as experimental specimens tend to go badly for everyone involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the Progenitors are most interested in their <i>bodies</i>. The Directors take the most interest in their Wake, the Mad Sociologists and Political Scientists that they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T01:46:18-08:00","id":1055566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1055494#post1055494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Princess</b></div> </div> </div> </div> One thing to bear in mind. Princesses just don't have the fire power to take down a combat focused leviathan with a few points of Sheol in it's Apotheosis. Unless they can catch it on land the most effective strategy for Princesses to fight a leviathan is to find someone with bigger guns (typically the local army, they're easy to find) and start throwing around Bless and Inspire Charms.<br /> <br /> Incidently Acqua Charms just look and feel really weird to leviathans. Acqua is built on the concept that water connects; that it's easier to travel, trade, and share ideas, by sailing than by travelling over land. A bit obsolete now, but it was true for most of history: Ancient Greece, Renaissance Italy, Victorian England, all major maritime powers. (I'm not sure about golden age Arabia, it may be an exception). Leviathans are connected to water as the a source and requirement of life: The primordial ooze, drink regularly or dehydrate and die, our bodies are 70% water, etc.<br /> <br /> There's no mechanical effect for this though. It won't let a Princess of Diamonds hurt a leviathan with Uncrowned Fisher King by firing jets of water. The leviathan will simply assert that it's interpretation of water takes precedence and continue along it's way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1055494#post1055494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted that while most supernatural effects treat Nobles in their Mundane and Transformed states as two different people</div> </div> </div> </div> A leviathan still needs to name or otherwise identify the target he wants to focus a ritual on. If he nominates Princess Gwendolyn as the the target and she's unTransformed then the Ritual cannot find her.<br /> <br /> The Adaptation Read Not the Tomes also treats Princesses as two people. So if he looks for &quot;whoever attacked me yesterday&quot; and she's unTransformed at the time it can't find her.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if he looks for &quot;any spies within ten miles of the temple&quot; after the guards spotted a Noble sneaking around; that would likely catch whichever form she's in right now. Transformed or not she's still a spy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1055494#post1055494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Are the Queens gods?</b></div> </div> </div> </div> Remember that the difference between god and not-god is in many ways like the difference between psychic powers and mind arcana. A Mind spell and a telepathic power might have identical mechanics, but even if the only difference is the fluff, they're clearly distinct entities.<br /> <br /> Most of the difference between Queens and gods comes down to that. The way a Queen's existence creates an Invocation even resembles the way a god's existence creates a power source that can empower people into Thurgists can tap into.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you step behind the curtain. Queens and Leviathan style gods serve the exact same story role: Extraordinary powerful entities that teach virtues and empower those who live up to their virtues (playable Queens are possible, but not really part of the core Princess game). And the fluff for both were written by the same person; so unsurprisingly they ended up very similar. The difference between the two mostly comes down to Mind Arcana vs telepathy like technicalities, and the fact gods are significantly stronger than Queens.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. The gestalt Queen of Storms has a focus that surpasses most singular souls. The reason she doesn't fuel rituals is that she's <i>too</i> focused on fighting Darkness to listen. Even if you try to direct her attention to the Darkness, she won't actually hear your message, listening to you takes up attention that could be spent fighting the Darkness. However when she notices the Darkness she can grant Ritual-like Miracles. There's rules for it in Princess, they're significantly less powerful than rituals; but chalk that up to gameplay and story segregation. Princess games are supposed to be lower power than leviathan games.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1055494#post1055494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Genius</b></div> </div> </div> </div> One important addition: Geniuses are one of the few splats that Leviathans fear. Most Geniuses wouldn't stand a chance in a fight against a Reef Leviathan. But the minority of Geniuses who have the Inspiration and resources, they can single handedly take down the largest Leviathans. The Steyotype section for Geniuses makes this clear.<br /> <br /> The reason is two fold: Firstly a quick look at Genius mechanics shows that Wonders can be more powerful than Marduk's super science. Secondly a Genius who builds an orbital death ray is unlikely to share Marduk's sane and rational viewpoint about collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Fortunately for players who want to have fun, a Genius might also lack Marduk's sane and rational view that blasting leviathans from high orbit is safer and more practical than building a giant robot with a lightning sword. (Not that Marduk could, unlike mad science, super science respects the square cube law).<br /> <br /> <br /> One last point. The most proactive group at stopping Leviathans from doing evil would be Lemuria, with the Navigators coming in second. After all the core difference between the two groups is that Lemuria thinks that Geniuses should help mortals, and the Peerage thinks that they're too insane and will only make things worse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 02-27-2017, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T16:52:26-08:00","id":1056376,"title":"","content":":O Thank you so much for the feedback! I know that crossovers aren't your favorite thing, so I <i>really</i> appreciate the notes!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1055566#post1055566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One thing to bear in mind. Princesses just don't have the fire power to take down a combat focused leviathan with a few points of Sheol in it's Apotheosis. Unless they can catch it on land the most effective strategy for Princesses to fight a leviathan is to find someone with bigger guns (typically the local army, they're easy to find) and start throwing around Bless and Inspire Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm suddenly getting an image of Homura unloading All Of The Guns at Walpurgisnacht.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1055566#post1055566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Incidently Acqua Charms just look and feel really weird to leviathans. Acqua is built on the concept that water connects; that it's easier to travel, trade, and share ideas, by sailing than by travelling over land. A bit obsolete now, but it was true for most of history: Ancient Greece, Renaissance Italy, Victorian England, all major maritime powers. (I'm not sure about golden age Arabia, it may be an exception). Leviathans are connected to water as the a source and requirement of life: The primordial ooze, drink regularly or dehydrate and die, our bodies are 70% water, etc.<br /> <br /> There's no mechanical effect for this though. It won't let a Princess of Diamonds hurt a leviathan with Uncrowned Fisher King by firing jets of water. The leviathan will simply assert that it's interpretation of water takes precedence and continue along it's way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that makes sense, since Leviathans rely on water much more than Princesses do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1055566#post1055566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A leviathan still needs to name or otherwise identify the target he wants to focus a ritual on. If he nominates Princess Gwendolyn as the the target and she's unTransformed then the Ritual cannot find her.<br /> <br /> The Adaptation Read Not the Tomes also treats Princesses as two people. So if he looks for &quot;whoever attacked me yesterday&quot; and she's unTransformed at the time it can't find her.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if he looks for &quot;any spies within ten miles of the temple&quot; after the guards spotted a Noble sneaking around; that would likely catch whichever form she's in right now. Transformed or not she's still a spy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops! That's on me for not paying close enough attention to the ritual rules &gt;.&lt;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1055566#post1055566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Remember that the difference between god and not-god is in many ways like the difference between psychic powers and mind arcana. A Mind spell and a telepathic power might have identical mechanics, but even if the only difference is the fluff, they're clearly distinct entities.<br /> <br /> Most of the difference between Queens and gods comes down to that. The way a Queen's existence creates an Invocation even resembles the way a god's existence creates a power source that can empower people into Thurgists can tap into.<br /> <br /> If you step behind the curtain. Queens and Leviathan style gods serve the exact same story role: Extraordinary powerful entities that teach virtues and empower those who live up to their virtues (playable Queens are possible, but not really part of the core Princess game). And the fluff for both were written by the same person; so unsurprisingly they ended up very similar. The difference between the two mostly comes down to Mind Arcana vs telepathy like technicalities, and the fact gods are significantly stronger than Queens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I had never gotten that similarity between drawing power from an invocation and drawing power from a ritual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1055566#post1055566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> P.S. The gestalt Queen of Storms has a focus that surpasses most singular souls. The reason she doesn't fuel rituals is that she's <i>too</i> focused on fighting Darkness to listen. Even if you try to direct her attention to the Darkness, she won't actually hear your message, listening to you takes up attention that could be spent fighting the Darkness. However when she notices the Darkness she can grant Ritual-like Miracles. There's rules for it in Princess, they're significantly less powerful than rituals; but chalk that up to gameplay and story segregation. Princess games are supposed to be lower power than leviathan games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was me fumbling around in the dark for a fluff justification. I was looking at all of the gods presented so far and I asked myself &quot;Hmmm, what do all these things have in common?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1055566#post1055566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One important addition: Geniuses are one of the few splats that Leviathans fear. Most Geniuses wouldn't stand a chance in a fight against a Reef Leviathan. But the minority of Geniuses who have the Inspiration and resources, they can single handedly take down the largest Leviathans. The Steyotype section for Geniuses makes this clear.<br /> <br /> The reason is two fold: Firstly a quick look at Genius mechanics shows that Wonders can be more powerful than Marduk's super science. Secondly a Genius who builds an orbital death ray is unlikely to share Marduk's sane and rational viewpoint about collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Fortunately for players who want to have fun, a Genius might also lack Marduk's sane and rational view that blasting leviathans from high orbit is safer and more practical than building a giant robot with a lightning sword. (Not that Marduk could, unlike mad science, super science respects the square cube law).</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't have that much experience with WoD games or Genius in particular, so I don't really have that great a grasp about how the mechanics of different splats interact with each other. Though given Genius' similarities with Mage, your explanation does make sense here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1055566#post1055566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One last point. The most proactive group at stopping Leviathans from doing evil would be Lemuria, with the Navigators coming in second. After all the core difference between the two groups is that Lemuria thinks that Geniuses should help mortals, and the Peerage thinks that they're too insane and will only make things worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I had sort of forgotten that Lemuria sees <i>itself </i>as the hero, rescuing humanity from The Darkest Timeline. The fact that everyone sees themselves as the hero of their own story could probably be used to explain a great deal about the state of the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":867,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","user":"Jimborg","date":". 03-01-2017, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T15:30:32-08:00","id":1057291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1054589#post1054589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of my sample cults.<br /> <br /> The Lorekeeper Society</div> </div> </div> </div>Killerclown brings up a good point: what are the extent of the activities you can perform while your Leviathan is Dead But Dreaming? Are they still subject to the same Tranquility requirements for human contact as before? Does psychic interaction count as human contact? Can you use Ichor to go to a lower Depth, so as to gain access to your powers and gain better control of your Cult?<br /> <br /> Heck, you could probably do most of a campaign around just bringing yourself back from death, though it'd be more &quot;Sim Cult&quot; than your standard WoD game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":867,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","user":"Jimborg","date":". 03-02-2017, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T20:02:11-08:00","id":1057415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1057291#post1057291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Killerclown brings up a good point: what are the extent of the activities you can perform while your Leviathan is Dead But Dreaming? Are they still subject to the same Tranquility requirements for human contact as before? Does psychic interaction count as human contact? Can you use Ichor to go to a lower Depth, so as to gain access to your powers and gain better control of your Cult?<br /> <br /> Heck, you could probably do most of a campaign around just bringing yourself back from death, though it'd be more &quot;Sim Cult&quot; than your standard WoD game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like that's the moment where you put down ChroD and switch to Unknown Armies temporarily","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T03:54:30-08:00","id":1057523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1057291#post1057291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Killerclown brings up a good point: what are the extent of the activities you can perform while your Leviathan is Dead But Dreaming?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not that much. You're limited to channels/adaptations that explicitly state they work when you're dead and channels/adaptations that explicitly state they work while you're dreaming. Your cult can use Rituals like normal.<br /> <br /> Though on the other hand, that list does let you possess a Beloved to use as an avatar. So a dead leviathan could make a very atypical charachter for a mortals+ level game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1057291#post1057291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are they still subject to the same Tranquility requirements for human contact as before? Does psychic interaction count as human contact? Can you use Ichor to go to a lower Depth, so as to gain access to your powers and gain better control of your Cult?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes to all three. However psychic interaction that works on targets within a certain distance of you won't work, because your mind is somewhere beyond this mortal plain and thus out of range (unless you're currently possessing an avatar). You have to use things like Contact List.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1057291#post1057291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, you could probably do most of a campaign around just bringing yourself back from death, though it'd be more &quot;Sim Cult&quot; than your standard WoD game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sim Cult is pretty much the intent. The ability to survive death is mostly there to be a last chance to claw your way back to life. You could play an entire story of &quot;Sim Cult&quot; if you like, and there's potential with using a dead Ophion as a nearly unkillable reoccurring antagonist who appears as the puppetmaster behind a new cult every a few sessions after you exterminated the last cult.<br /> <br /> However the intent is that you use this state to plan your cult's heist on the Cheiron Group laboratory storing your body and then order them to supply you with Ichor so you can regenerate. My hope is that the many limitations of being dead will add to the fun of organising your own rescue; but I'm not really worried if the novelty wears off after a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-03-2017, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T11:21:14-07:00","id":1068352,"title":"","content":"<b>Beast</b><br /> <br /> Of all the creatures of the World of Darkness, only the Begotten claim a shared descent of Tiamat with Earth\u2019s Most Wicked. Many of the Children would be thrilled upon discovering the Tribe, viewing them as something akin to a long lost sibling: both feed on the minds of men. Both of their predations inevitably create Heroes (or Ahabs, in the case of Leviathans). The Makara even share the Leviathan's aquatic inclinations, leading to speculation that the former were the predecessors of the later (or vice-versa, in the view of the Leviathans concerned).<br /> <br /> Upon closer inspection however, The actions of Leviathans tend to confuse and mystify The Children: while they can appreciate the value of cultists as a convenient food supply, they are unsure what role Beloved are supposed to play in the Primordial Dream. What\u2019s more, Beloved cannot be used as pathways to the Primordial Dream: trapped in the Leviathan\u2019s psychic orbit, Beloved are cut off from the Astral plane, and are thus unable to be used as a gateway to the Primordial Dream with the Under The Bed ability.<br /> <br /> This first impression is <i>not</i> reciprocated by the Tribe. They view the Begotten as, for lack of a better word, posers.<br /> <br /> Beasts seem wholly unconcerned with seeking evidence of their much vaunted lineage lineage. For all they complain about Heroes not understanding their place in the Primordial Dream, Beasts themselves seem to have relatively little interest in the quest for self identity that consumes the Tribe.<br /> <br /> While there\u2019s no way for Leviathans to conclusively disprove claims of shared lineage (especially given the similarities above), Beasts claim that <i>every</i> supernatural is descended from Tiamat. As followers of the School of the Sand point out, any theory you can\u2019t disprove is no theory at all. Not to mention that the souls of Beasts <i>reek</i> of humanity, regardless of whatever twisted forms their Souls take. Just because you look like a squid and act like an asshole doesn't make you a proper monster.<br /> <br /> It would be remiss to mention that the Tribe\u2019s animosity towards the Begotten at least partially stems from jealousy. Lacking the Wake, a well fed Beast can live among humanity in ways that the Tribe can only dream of.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidebar: Nightmares in the Deep</b><br /> <br /> Though it seems like a Beast\u2019s Nightmares are exactly the sort of thing a Leviathan\u2019s Ocean Minds defense would apply to, Leviathans are just as vulnerable to a Beast\u2019s Nightmares as any other creature in the World of Darkness. It is only when the <i>effects</i> of a Beast\u2019s Nightmares attempt to directly influence their mind, soul, or emotions that Ocean Minds is tripped. For example \u201cBehold my True Form\u201d inflicts lethal damage, and affects the Leviathan\u2019s body, not their mind. By contrast \u201cRun Away\u201d or \u201cYou Must Obey\u201d directly attempt to directly influence the Leviathan\u2019s behavior and therefore trigger Ocean Minds.<br /> <br /> Similarly, while most of a Beast\u2019s kinship powers treat a Leviathan as a fellow Child of the Dark Mother, using Thicker than Water provokes a Leviathan\u2019s Ocean Minds defense and a clash of wills, as the power attempts to influence how the Leviathan feels towards the Begotten.<br /> <br /> <b>Non-Euclidean Labyrinths</b><br /> <br /> To an aspiring Lovecraftian demigod, a Beast\u2019s lair may seem to be the perfect spot to hide and plot your next move.<br /> <br /> The unfortunate truth is a Begotten\u2019s lair is among the <i>last</i> places a Leviathan wants to be, especially if they are trying to keep a low profile.<br /> <br /> Remember: a Beast\u2019s lair is located within the Primordial Dream, part of the collective human consciousness. The same mechanism that lets the Beast\u2019s soul hunt in the local mindscape can also carry echoes of the Leviathan\u2019s Wake, creating Beloved and Ahabs in unexpected places, who are sure to cause the Leviathan trouble later.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Beasts create new chambers in the Lair through breaking points, and few tools are as useful in that regard as a Leviathan\u2019s Wake. In a pinch, the extra defense a new Chamber provides <i>may</i> be worth the risk to a Beast and/or Leviathan under siege.<br /> <br /> <b>Feeding Frenzy</b><br /> <br /> Beasts are able to use Family Dinner to sympathetically feed from Leviathans as they regain Ichor. Specifically, Beasts can regain Satiety through observing a Levithan making a Havoc or Dominance check, most instances of a successful Fervor check, and certain Channels that grant Ichor through the use of predatory means. As a rule of thumb, if it restores Ichor and requires the Leviathan to act in a physically predatory fashion, it restores Satiety.<br /> <br /> Some Beasts have also reported feeling especially full after a given \u2018hunting session\u2019 with a Leviathan, receiving unexplained additional Satiety. Only those with intimate familiarity of the Leviathan psyche realize this Satiety comes from a Leviathan\u2019s mind <i>feeding on itself</i>. For whenever the chains of Eunoia or Phronesis slip, the sociopathic deity and the savage beast feast on an increasingly unstable human psyche, restoring both Ichor and Satiety in the process.<br /> <br /> This can result in rapid Satiety gains that can force a Beast\u2019s Soul into dormancy if they aren\u2019t careful. For example, say that a Beast is observing a Reef Leviathan who is set on destroying a rival. During the battle, the Leviathan get\u2019s <i>particularly</i> cross and decides to consume their rival, body and soul. This would potentially provoke two instances of regaining Ichor from degeneration (a Phronesis check for eating it\u2019s body, and a Enuoia check for eating its soul.) and regaining Ichor from eating it\u2019s soul, providing an opportunity to gain three Satiety from the same act.<br /> <br /> The Beast, however, will only be aware that a potential to regain Satiety exists, and not the exact amount. If, this would force a Beast above 10 Satiety, their Soul is forced to disgorge the excess horror, forcing them to spend one Willpower per Satiety they wish to disgorge (the Hunger Management merit can reduce the amount of Satiety you have to deal with). This excess horror spreads nightmares, similar to when a Beast\u2019s Soul is Ravenous. Such nightmares often serve as a clue or omen to all nearby that something great and terrible has happened.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidebar: \u201cYou tricked me!\u201d</b><br /> <br /> Invoking the \u201cFeeding Frenzy\u201d rules above uses the themes of Leviathan: The Tempest to subvert the themes of Beast: The Primordial. To a Beast, the other inhabitants of the World of Darkness are one big extended family, and the use of the Family Dinner ability emphasizes that connection, and makes it easier to establish Kinship.<br /> <br /> To an unprepared Beast, trying to draw Satiety off of a Feeding Frenzy may subvert this perspective: Beast do indeed gain the bonus to establish Kinship with a Leviathan, but only after getting a first hand introduction to the amount of physical and psychic trauma they inflict on themselves and others, to the point of possibly causing them to become sick with Satiety. As such, a ST should consult with Beast PCs before implementing this rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":867,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","user":"Jimborg","date":". 03-26-2017, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T08:09:57-07:00","id":1075484,"title":"","content":"Looks good. A couple of things I'd point out:<br /> <br /> For some Leviathans the idea that beasts are descended from Tiamat is not only wrong but out right blasphemous and a good way for a Beast to screw up a &quot;first contact&quot;. The School of the Moon would be particularly likely to react negatively but it's not unique to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> One of the core thematic contrasts between Leviathan and Beast is the idea of family. Beast, at least to some extent, treats family as people who you like and who you support; a view that's hard coded in mechanics that let Beasts give other supernatural a power boost or have higher first impressions.<br /> <br /> For Leviathan family resembles classical deities like the twelve Olympians. A cesspool of bitter feuds, self-destructive envy, petty bickering, one-upmanship, and other assorted behaviours that makes you wonder if this is the realm of the gods or a badly behaved high school.<br /> <br /> <br /> Due to the way apexes work; a Leviathan's wake is practically an automatic apex button. There's probably some story potential in that.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've heard it said that the Dark Mother existed for as long as living creatures were able to feel fear or hunger. If that theory is true, and if the theory that Tiamat was literally the first living being in existence is true, then that would make the Dark Mother Tiamat's hunger &amp; fear. Obviously this isn't intentional. I didn't set out to write about another game's mythos, it's just the logical conclusion of combining two theories written in isolation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Transformed Leviathans can physically touch astral entities. That includes the Horror. If a Beast uses Monster from the Deep to grapple a Leviathan, then the Leviathan can see and strike at the kraken's tentacles. There's no mechanical advantage for this, but there's some neat role play potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T05:30:53-07:00","id":1097082,"title":"","content":"I have an idea for an Evolution, but I couldn't find any rules for writing one. Would it be possible to be furnished with one, or do I just write a set of Adaptations?<br /> <br /> For the idea of the Evolution itself, it was intended to be very closely connected to the School of Sand, whereby the Leviathan can transform into a sort of machine-form, inhabiting and becoming technology, at the price of slowly degrading all the technology that they inhabit. I have a very strong image of a cult of technicians, maintaining the body of their machine-god, as well as the heart of the Leviathan's form being a 'core' of eldritch code which functions as if it's Apotheosis form for the purpose of Breaking Points and becoming Beloved. <br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm not sure what would happen with the Wake, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 05-26-2017, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T06:25:25-07:00","id":1097099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1097082#post1097082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea for an Evolution, but I couldn't find any rules for writing one. Would it be possible to be furnished with one, or do I just write a set of Adaptations?<br /> <br /> For the idea of the Evolution itself, it was intended to be very closely connected to the School of Sand, whereby the Leviathan can transform into a sort of machine-form, inhabiting and becoming technology, at the price of slowly degrading all the technology that they inhabit. I have a very strong image of a cult of technicians, maintaining the body of their machine-god, as well as the heart of the Leviathan's form being a 'core' of eldritch code which functions as if it's Apotheosis form for the purpose of Breaking Points and becoming Beloved. <br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm not sure what would happen with the Wake, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds similar to some I've made (though I'm not sure how compliant they are).<br /> <br /> As for the Wake, I'm reminded of Reaper Indoctrination in Mass Effect. Even dead gods can dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T15:29:14-07:00","id":1097323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1097099#post1097099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds similar to some I've made (though I'm not sure how compliant they are).<br /> <br /> As for the Wake, I'm reminded of Reaper Indoctrination in Mass Effect. Even dead gods can dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will neither confirm nor deny that the Reapers were an inspiration for the Evolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T02:18:52-07:00","id":1097717,"title":"","content":"The way I'd write the evolutions mechanics would just be:<br /> <br /> You're an Ephemerial Being, and you loose Ichor if you're more than a few feet away from a working computer which you have legitimate or hacked control over. Computers in a few feet from yourself loose one point of equipment bonus every &lt;time increment&gt; and are utterly destroyed when they reach -6. Supernatural computers, if they have an equipment bonus greater than Sheol and a durability greater than Sheol will not degrade (I.E. A powerful Genius could build you a reaper style body)<br /> <br /> Supernatural powers that can control technology (E.G. a Genius with Epikrato) can either be used to mind control you (Ocean Minds applies) or treated as a weapon, Storyteller judgement will need to be applied to work out it's damage rating. Psychic powers also work on you as though you were a Leviathan projecting your mind with Eye of the Watchful Deity&quot;.<br /> <br /> After that just design any Adapatations that give you computer related powers. You'd definately need one that lets you &quot;teleport&quot; to annother computer if you have an internet connection<br /> <br /> The Wake would work as normal, projecting from the computer you're inhabiting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T03:29:07-07:00","id":1098047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1097323#post1097323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will neither confirm nor deny that the Reapers were an inspiration for the Evolution.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not even when the first Reaver, Harbringer, was originally a Leviathan aka ancient goldlike squids with mind controlling powers and a knack for entralling civilizations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T03:31:28-07:00","id":1098048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1098047#post1098047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not even when the first Reaver, Harbringer, was originally a Leviathan aka ancient goldlike squids with mind controlling powers and a knack for entralling civilizations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Make of it what you will. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T18:52:54-07:00","id":1107480,"title":"","content":"Greetings friends! I bring new musings on our sea monster overlords!<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy</b><br /> <br /> Origins in an unfathomably ancient past. Loyaly served by cultists. Unnatural auras that bring madness to mortals. But more than that, both Leviathans and the Arisen are driven by self discovery: the leviathans seek the true nature of their monstrous legacy, while the arisen seek to re-discover the person they were before they were bound to the judges of Duat. They could almost be said to be opposite sides of the same coin: life on one face, death on the other.<br /> <br /> Given their respective ages and the connections each hold to ancient Babylon, it is not inconceivable to speculate that Irem was one of the first major societies to be established after the overthrow of the progenitors.<br /> <br /> <b>Don\u2019t touch my stuff!</b><br /> <br /> Unfortunately, these similarities predispose the two to conflict, as the vestiges (or as the leviathan would call it, heirlooms) that offer the best chance of proving of such a connection are likely stashed inside a mummy\u2019s tomb. Knowingly stealing such a vestige is arguably one of the <i>dumbest</i> things you can do in the World of Darkness, but there are no shortage of those desperate for answers among Earth\u2019s Most Wicked.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the arisen have their own set of avaricious urges with which they must contend. Absent any other priorities, a Levithan would attempt to acquire any such artifact and add it to their panoply. <br /> <br /> <b>Sidebar: \u201cWhy won\u2019t you die?!\u201d</b><br /> <br /> A clever Leviathan player who has read the core books of both game lines might look at the <i>Kin of the Conqueror Worm</i> adaptation and think \u201cAh ha! I can use this power to prevent the Arisen from returning to the Underworld, and therefore prevent their resurrection.\u201d You\u2019d be right\u2026 mostly.<br /> <br /> By preventing them from dying, the leviathan has also given the arisen a chance to physically re-assemble themselves (pg. 145 of Mummy: The Curse). In order to properly take advantage of the adaptation, the leviathan needs to ensure there is <b>nothing</b> for the arisen\u2019s spirit to possess, requiring that the mummy\u2019s form to be <i>obliterated</i>, no mean feat, even for a leviathan.<br /> <br /> And even then, this is a temporary measure, as the Underworld <b>will</b> notice the damage done to the Avernian gateway and investigate. And when the gateway is repaired, the mummy\u2019s cult can simply provide it another vessel to inhabit. Meaning that that anyone who wants to put a mummy out of commission <i>permanently</i> needs to <b>utterly</b> destroy both its body (including any auxiliary vessels it may still have) and its cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T20:16:17-07:00","id":1107498,"title":"","content":"I could see an Arisen and a Leviathan with Dead But Dreaming (and related Adaptations) having a hate-feud, each killing off the other down the years, only for their opponent to return and plague them again. Might even evolve into <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AntagonistInMourning\" target=\"_blank\">Antagonist in Mourning</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T08:33:54-07:00","id":1107642,"title":"","content":"hey, just wanted to note that the new Thousand Years of Night has detailed an official Judge (Deborah), and as the Judges take the place of the thematic antagonists in the new edition you may find it interesting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T00:49:46-07:00","id":1108316,"title":"","content":"What sort of mechanics do they use to represent Deborah?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1107480#post1107480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By preventing them from dying, the leviathan has also given the arisen a chance to physically re-assemble themselves (pg. 145 of Mummy: The Curse). In order to properly take advantage of the adaptation, the leviathan needs to ensure there is <b>nothing</b> for the arisen\u2019s spirit to possess, requiring that the mummy\u2019s form to be <i>obliterated</i>, no mean feat, even for a leviathan.<br /> <br /> And even then, this is a temporary measure, as the Underworld <b>will</b> notice the damage done to the Avernian gateway and investigate. And when the gateway is repaired, the mummy\u2019s cult can simply provide it another vessel to inhabit. Meaning that that anyone who wants to put a mummy out of commission <i>permanently</i> needs to <b>utterly</b> destroy both its body (including any auxiliary vessels it may still have) and its cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Arisan is out of magic, or squashed into a fine paste (given the size of Leviathans this is a real possibility) than sealing the underworld won't give them any additional advantages. They might get the usual effects of sealing the flesh, but it's not exactly hard to physically mangle a human body beyond repair.<br /> <br /> I'd say the real effect of <i>Kin of the Conqueror Worm </i>is that it makes it hard to summon the Mummy. The cult would have to move enough paraphernalia, and probably the Mummy's body, outside of the affected area. Of course, if a Mummy's cult lets a Leviathan enter it's apotheosis close enough to the temple to hit it with an earthquake they deserve what they get.<br /> <br /> The real problem is that mecanically mummies just aren't powerful enough to play with Leviathans, which is a shame because thematically the two make great antagonists for each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-27-2017, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T03:08:31-07:00","id":1108330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1108316#post1108316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real problem is that mecanically mummies just aren't powerful enough to play with Leviathans, which is a shame because thematically the two make great antagonists for each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Blinks*<br /> <br /> Well that's a terrifying thought. Mummies <i>not</i> being strong enough to throw down in a weight category.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T05:20:20-07:00","id":1108356,"title":"","content":"*blinks together with ajf115*<br /> <br /> That <i>is</i> terrifying. Then again, Mummy mechanics are largely 1E right now, and thus of lower power level in general. (Like how Vampire and Werewolf were)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T11:46:39-07:00","id":1108462,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind I haven't really looked at Mummy in ages, but my impression is that they've got a few very powerful tricks like triggering an Earthquake, and an automatic loyal cult, but apart from those they're squarely mid tier when compared to others with the same power stat rating.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind though, that Leviathans are intentionally really really powerful. You are playing Cthulhu after all, that's way more powerful than Count Dracula. Something like Heart of the Swarm or the exceptional size rules is beyond any other splat. I'd say even a Mummy shouldn't be able to take on a Leviathan in a fist fight, but they should be able to pull of rituals that affect as many people as Leviathans, and could probably outdo them in creative effects and have an easier time of organising everything because their Cults are more competent.<br /> <br /> So while a powerful Leviathan doesn't need outside help to create an entire swarm of minions, I'd like to see a Mummy with prep time being able to match him by using a ritual to summon an army of it's own; or convert it's entire tomb into a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hdG_MYPq2lc\" target=\"_blank\">giant battle relic</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T13:25:09-07:00","id":1108485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1108316#post1108316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sort of mechanics do they use to represent Deborah?</div> </div> </div> </div>ammm her power set is called Gifts, which are powered by her faith- she must have a belief in her mission and justice, else her powers simply fail. They cost either a Willpower or a meditation in order to activate them. It includes rising her Attributes through prayer, regeneration, and the ability to enhance the elemental qualities of an object through song. She also have a number of Supernatural Merits to represent her powers (like Laying on Hands). She may also be immune to Blood Bonds, Domination, the Embrace and other vampiric mind manipulation. Some of her powers flow through her blood, and so her descendants may carry them in them (if I'm reading it right, she may choose what Gifts her descendants may have). The principle around her mechanics seems to be more or less what we have worked about- a primal power of divinity, channeled directly through her faith and body instead of delicate rituals and invocations. As she isn't meant to be a PC, there aren't many details about how to make Judges in the game- but maybe it is a sign we'll get Book of Judges in the next Dark Eras book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T13:48:40-07:00","id":1108495,"title":"","content":"Wait. No leadership themed powers. For Deborah?! That's crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T15:08:48-07:00","id":1108521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1108495#post1108495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait. No leadership themed powers. For Deborah?! That's crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, fluff wise, the Torah (her singing power) is meant to be such a leadership power, although that is represented through buffing by elemental enhancement (ice strength a structure, fire rise damage and earth enhance armor).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T01:06:59-07:00","id":1108655,"title":"","content":"Which as I said, is crazy. Deborah's singing shouldn't be an elemental power. It should be a buff to her soldiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T01:20:06-07:00","id":1108658,"title":"","content":"well, it does- it does buff her soldiers by enhancing the items they use (weapons, armor, etc). The way I understand it, the Torah enhance an elemental &quot;quality&quot;- it increase the &quot;fire quality&quot; of a weapon to deal more damage, or the &quot;earth quality&quot; of an armor to protect her soldiers better. It is not really an elemental power- although I agree that the power may have felt a bit more thematic without that flavor text, and simply state that by singing she can grant her allies a bonus to damage/armor/structure/etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T03:17:50-07:00","id":1108679,"title":"","content":"A &quot;bit more thematic&quot; is an understatement, and thematics are king. What kind of bonus are we talking? This is supposed to be an antagonist for a Vampire elder right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T08:46:30-07:00","id":1110868,"title":"","content":"So, a question:<br /> <br /> What kind of stuff would need to be on a Leviathan character sheet, beyond the standard CofD stuff? I figure that the following would probably be required, but if there's anything else, please tell me so I can have a go at making the thing.<ul><li>Tranquility meter (12 dots, top and bottom already shaded)</li> <li>Sheol (as normal for Supernatural Potency)</li> <li>Ichor (as normal for 'fuel')</li> <li>'Transformation' stat entries Ala Werewolf's thing (places where you can write down attribute modifications, armour etc for different Depths</li> <li>Atavism record area</li> <li>Channel record area (would it be better to separate Ancestral and Descendant channels?)</li> <li>Cult section (likely similar to Mage's Familiar section)</li> <li>Codified rituals</li> </ul>That's all I can think of off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Also, I've come across a large number of images which I thought would be cool for leviathans, and I thought I'd link to them here, if that's alright.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0p