mage\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> A shark-giant.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/bloodborne/images/8/81/Bloodborne%E2%84%A2_20151127095819_-_2.png/revision/latest?cb=20151229151135\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T06:31:28-08:00","id":1184362,"title":"","content":"<u>Draft 4</u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u><b>Self-Serving Idol of Glory (Ancestral Channel)</b></u><br /> <i>The Leviathan is no mere creature of flesh and bone, but a living god capable of empowering icons made in their honor.</i><br /> <br /> The Leviathan's Divine nature empowers and curses objects in their vicinity.<br /> <b>Depth 1:</b> Birthright of Sanctity<br /> <br /> <b>Depth 2:</b> Items that the Leviathan has made partake of their divine nature. They gain 7 Dedication points to assign to the item, but only can access their current Depth in benefits, and only while they hold the item. The Leviathan can have up to Sheol in personally crafted items dedicated in this way, though they can destroy previous creations to make way for new ones.<br /> <br /> <b>Depth 3:</b> The Leviathan can now blight a type of object with curses, reducing its effectiveness in their presence. They declare a category of item (such as medical tools, chain armor, swords, pistols, etc.) for each dot of Sheol anathema to them, and assign a pool of 7 Blight points to effects, though they can only utilize up to their current Depth in effects. The Leviathan can suppress this effect for the Scene for 1 Willpower. They can rededicate target items and blight effects after successfully meditating after 24 hours.<br /> <br /> <b>Depth 4:</b> Blessings now flow through onto the Leviathan's followers. Objects in the current Scene that have been crafted by their Cult and dedicated to Leviathan (such as by having one of their names or depictions inscribed upon it or being used in a Ritual) can gain Dedications as well, though they all possess the same bonuses, as applicable. The Leviathan can change which Dedications are in effect in the same Scene by spending 1 Willpower point.<br /> <br /> <b>Depth 5: </b>Wrath falls upon whatever mortal artifice would dare impede a living god. Blighted items that strike or impede the Leviathan automatically take Sheol points of Structure damage (bypassing Durability). Supernatural objects can still be dealt damage, but do not have their Durability ignored.<br /> <br /> <b>Depth 6:</b> [Placeholder: The Leviathan's power can reach across their Wake, enabling dedicated items to act as if they were the Leviathans own hands. Powers that rely upon the Leviathan touching a target can apply if they are touching the chosen item. This does not give a Leviathan any ablility to see the item in question, or know the conditions around it - they require other means of communication or Awareness Vestiges for that.]<br /> <br /> <b>Depth 7:</b> A Leviathan in Apotheosis can expunge the presence of blasphemous object from their very presence. All Blighted objects within the Leviathan's Wake are treated as if they were a character in an Extreme Environment with a rating equal the the Leviathan's Presence, and their Durability treated as Stamina. The effect lasts until the item leaves the Leviathan's Wake, or the Leviathan changes Depth. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Dedication Cost</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Effect</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+1 Equipment Bonus (max. +5 total)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+1 Weapon Damage (max. 5 total)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+1 Durability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+1 General or Ballistic Armor</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">9-Again on Skill rolls (or upgrade to 8-Again)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Exceptional Success on 3 Successes</td> </tr> </table></div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Blight Cost</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Effect</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">-1 Equipment Bonus (min. 0 total)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">-1 Weapon Damage (min. 0 total)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">-1 Durability (min. 0)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">-1 General or Ballistic Armor</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Lose 10-Again (or downgrade 9-Again)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Failures become Dramatic Failures</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>Adaptations</b>:<br /> Divine Receptacle (\u2022\u2022): The Leviathan has access to an additional 1-dot Dedication - the ability to store Ichor inside the item. Items can only store Ichor up to their Durability safely.<br /> Channel the Divine (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Requires Divine Receptacle): The Leviathan has access to an additional variable cost Dedication - the item can replicate the ability of a Channel the Leviathan knows. The cost in Dedication points is equal to the Depth of the Channel ability. Any Ichor costs must be paid for from either the bearer, or the item's own reserve (through Divine Receptacle). Sheol is treated as 1 in the case where the bearer does not possess a Sheol Attribute (such as a favored cultist being given such an item).<br /> Primordial Creator (\u2022\u2022\u2022): The Leviathan gains 3 additional Dedication points and can access their Depth+1 at Depth 2, Depth+2 at Depth 4, and Depth+3 at Depth 6.<br /> Accursed Idol (\u2022\u2022\u2022): The Leviathan gains 3 additional Blight points and can access their Depth+1 at Depth 3, Depth+2 at Depth 5, and Depth+3 at Depth 7.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm also thinking about a &quot;The Leviathan knows the location of all dedicated item inside their Wake&quot; effect, but that seems lackluster alone. Also a &quot;restore/reinforce dedicated items&quot; power. Not sure that is thematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T05:18:41-08:00","id":1191597,"title":"","content":"Just an image I came across. What Strain do you think it would be? <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://pre00.deviantart.net/fe78/th/pre/i/2014/336/0/8/the_dragon_god_by_alexkonstad-d88i7ua.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T07:18:25-08:00","id":1191614,"title":"","content":"Tanninim? Thalassan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T16:59:41-07:00","id":1209819,"title":"","content":"I'd say Tanninim or Bahamut, it doesn't have the arms most Thalassans have.<br /> <br /> I have a question related to what strains would several characters be:<br /> <br /> Morgana Pendragon from Merlin<br /> She starts nice, opposing her foster father who burns all who are accused of magic. But as the serie continue, she opposes him more and more until she finally rebel openly. After that most of her allies are traitors, mercenaries and barbarians.<br /> I'd say Tannanim<br /> <br /> Light Yagami from Death Note<br /> He considers himself a god, beside L most of the peoples surrounding him seems like idiots and incompetents, while they were succesful policemen before that (they represented the police of Tokyo at a meeting of most agencies of the world). He is good looking and intelligent, his true allies all consider him to be superior to them in all ways possible.<br /> I'd say Oceanid.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lelouch Vi Britannia from Code Geass<br /> All he wishes is to protect his little sister, then his friends. The Black Knights without him are mostly incompetents and their only victory without him was when they freed him at the start of R2<br /> That would makes him a Bahamut<br /> <br /> But he revels in the power of his geass give him. The Black Knights are, during the first season, his puppets. He loves announcing his superiority to his enemies. Diethard says that without him, the Black Knights would fall apart. <br /> So maybe Oceanid<br /> <br /> Yet, he is also very secretive, he hides behind masks. His geass slaves do most of the work to make his miracles possible, most never meet each others and the Black Knights know nothing of them. Black Knights which know only what he tells them (not that much).<br /> He could be a Lahamin<br /> <br /> Finally, he could be a Thalassan<br /> The Black Knights follow him because he produces results and when he appears weak, when he seems to not be in control of the situation, the inner circle betray him, and chose their own interest over the other Black Knights'. And he is always at the edge of being as bad as his father <br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24160-n\u00e9ocorvinus","name":"n\u00e9ocorvinus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T10:41:43-07:00","id":1224757,"title":"","content":"So, how's the development going? Is this dead in the water? The calm before the tempest?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/co