:"","content":"So, for the hypothetical Dark Ages: Bronze Age collapse section--would there be strains that went extinct in the modern era? (sorry if this was broached before, I can't really keep up with a 60 page thread).<br /> <br /> (Full disclosure: I'm always fascinated by extinct groups of supernaturals. Always)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T10:01:52-08:00","id":1270133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1270083#post1270083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for the hypothetical Dark Ages: Bronze Age collapse section--would there be strains that went extinct in the modern era? (sorry if this was broached before, I can't really keep up with a 60 page thread).<br /> <br /> (Full disclosure: I'm always fascinated by extinct groups of supernaturals. Always)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not That I Have done any writing for this, but I hope so, I am also a big fan of extinct groups... they make a lot of fun in modern games when one turns up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T10:24:20-08:00","id":1270139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1270133#post1270133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not That I Have done any writing for this, but I hope so, I am also a big fan of extinct groups... they make a lot of fun in modern games when one turns up!</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember 1e mentioning a number of other Progenitors (Sanna the Glacierhide is one I recall) doing the mythological rounds, so it's not impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T08:52:26-08:00","id":1276463,"title":"","content":"Is this still monitored, TKR? I had some ideas on Vestiges and Channels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T17:00:09-08:00","id":1278196,"title":"","content":"Next submission, Descendant Awareness:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Weaving the Loom of Fate (Descendant Channel)</b></u><br /> <i>Description pending</i><br /> <br /> <b>Depth 1:</b> Birthright of Awareness<br /> <b>Depth 2:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By spending 1 Ichor, the Leviathan can glimpse the threads of Fate. They state a desired goal, qualities of a person they seek, or generalities for an item. They know which direction and rough distance to a person or source that either fits their criteria, or could lead them to it (though they don't quite know how, yet). Upon finding the subject, they also get a sense that it is who or what they seek.<br /> <b>Depth 3:</b> </span> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan's sense are now open to the omens of strange fates around them. They can see supernaturally altered destinies, or even just particularly potent ones. The Leviathan also effectively has access to the Omen Sensitivity merit, except without the drawback.</span><br /> <b>Depth 4:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No longer merely restricted to merely seeing Fate's threads, the Leviathan can now pull them to bend events to their will. As an Instant action spending 2 Ichor and rolling Wits + Occult + Sheol - Resolve + Sheol, the Leviathan can give modify their own or another's dice pool. Each success adds or subtracts 2 dice from the pool, or adjusts the threshold for Exceptional Success by 1 in either direction.</span><br /> <b>Depth 5:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Upon using the Depth 2 ability on a subject, they can intuit their weaknesses, figuring out the target's Ban, Bane, who or where they can hurt they target the most, or what they fear (The Leviathan might not be able to grasp <i>why</i> the target fears the action, but they know just what to do or say).</span><br /> <b>Depth 6:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When using the Depth 4 ability, you can also force the target to re-roll once per usage, as events conspire to steal or grant victory as you choose.</span><br /> <b>Depth 7:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By spending 4 Ichor, the Leviathan can gaze into the weaving of Fate and spin their own destiny. The Leviathan creates a Prophecy Condition, tied to a goal or fate they set. Unlike most Conditions, this isn't tied to a character or object, but is rather available to any it concerns.</span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Sidebar: You Can't Fight Fate (Unless You Do)</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">If the Storyteller and Players want a bit more activity and urgency, they can give the Prophecy a bit more mechanical weight. Treat the stated goal as an Extended Action with a target number of (chart). Each Session, the Prophecy itself rolls the Leviathan's Sheol as a Dice Pool, as Fate itself works to ensure its designs come to pass. Significant actions toward fulfilling the Prophecy act as supporting actions in a Teamwork roll. Actions that impede the Prophecy can generate a Dice Pool to make it a contested roll.</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <b>Adaptations:</b><br /> <i>Just As Planned (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i>: <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Once per Chapter, by spending 2 Ichor, you can decree that an action actually forwarded one of your ongoing Prophecy Conditions. The owner of the action still gets a Beat for advancing the Prophecy.</span></span><br /> <i>Reading the Omens (\u2022\u2022)</i>: At Depth 3 and below, the Leviathan can spend another point of Ichor to active their effective Omen Sensitivity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T02:36:18-08:00","id":1278273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1278196#post1278196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the mechanics, but the fluff doesn't feel quite right - 'strings of fate' sounds too god-like, too <i>human</i> god-like, for the Leviathans. I feel like they'd be more like reading the flow and eddies of the great current that is time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T09:29:26-08:00","id":1278338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1278273#post1278273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the mechanics, but the fluff doesn't feel quite right - 'strings of fate' sounds too god-like, too <i>human</i> god-like, for the Leviathans. I feel like they'd be more like reading the flow and eddies of the great current that is time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free to suggest flavor and rewordings. My main goal was something that communicates <i>why</i> the power is working.<br /> <br /> Oh, and what were you thinking of for Irresistible Hex-Rending Talons?<br /> <br /> Current progression is:<br /> <b>Depth 1:</b> Birthright of Might<br /> <b>Depth 2:</b> 1 Ichor - Can trigger a Clash of Wills to undo supernatural effect on themselves /OR/ Can trigger a Clash of Wills to negate a power currently being employed<br /> <b>Depth 3:</b> <br /> <b>Depth 4:</b> 2 Ichor - Can trigger a Clash of Wills to undo a supernatural effect upon a target they touch<br /> <b>Depth 5:</b> <br /> <b>Depth 6:</b> <br /> <b>Depth 7:</b> 4 Ichor - Can shred all supernatural power in the area, triggering a Clash of Wills against all supernatural powers on Scene<br /> <br /> Power may need to be adjusted. The Depth 7 one might require additional Ichor beyond the first effect (per target) to prevent it from being OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-03-2019, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T09:57:44-08:00","id":1278344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1278338#post1278338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and what were you thinking of for Irresistible Hex-Rending Talons?<br /> <br /> Current progression is:<br /> <b>Depth 1:</b> Birthright of Might<br /> <b>Depth 2:</b> 1 Ichor - Can trigger a Clash of Wills to undo supernatural effect on themselves /OR/ Can trigger a Clash of Wills to negate a power currently being employed<br /> <b>Depth 3:</b><br /> <b>Depth 4:</b> 2 Ichor - Can trigger a Clash of Wills to undo a supernatural effect upon a target they touch<br /> <b>Depth 5:</b><br /> <b>Depth 6:</b><br /> <b>Depth 7:</b> 4 Ichor - Can shred all supernatural power in the area, triggering a Clash of Wills against all supernatural powers on Scene<br /> <br /> Power may need to be adjusted. The Depth 7 one might require additional Ichor beyond the first effect (per target) to prevent it from being OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Works alright, I think. I could see the Depth 3 effect letting you do something to gain bonuses on the Clash of Wills, or perhaps inflict some kind of nasty Condition on the one who used the power. I feel like the Depth 4 effect would probably require you to deal 1L to the person you're 'freeing' - the aid of the Leviathans isn't gentle, after all. The natural progression would seem to be some ranged method of doing it at Depth 5 or 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T15:32:18-08:00","id":1278435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1278344#post1278344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Works alright, I think. I could see the Depth 3 effect letting you do something to gain bonuses on the Clash of Wills, or perhaps inflict some kind of nasty Condition on the one who used the power. I feel like the Depth 4 effect would probably require you to deal 1L to the person you're 'freeing' - the aid of the Leviathans isn't gentle, after all. The natural progression would seem to be some ranged method of doing it at Depth 5 or 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, who says you are &quot;freeing&quot; a target as opposed to ripping apart magical defenses protecting your foe?<br /> <br /> Extending the targeted effect to Ranged makes sense, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T15:41:59-08:00","id":1278438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1278435#post1278435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, who says you are &quot;freeing&quot; a target as opposed to ripping apart magical defenses protecting your foe?<br /> <br /> Extending the targeted effect to Ranged makes sense, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but then it's even more thematic. You're not gentle with your enemies, are you? And it's a theme with leviathans that they're better at being nasty than nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T16:00:05-08:00","id":1278445,"title":"","content":"And now for a &quot;heretical&quot; Channel<br /> <br /> <u><b>Reflections Upon the Deep (Ancestral Sanctity)</b></u><br /> <i>The thoughts of one of Tiamat's Brood are not restricted to inside of their mere skulls. Their daydreams drift freely, swaying the perceptions of lesser minds easily.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Depth 1:</b> Birthright of Sanctity<br /> <b>Depth 2:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan can weave a simple psychic impression upon the mind of another - a trick of the light, an unidentifiable sound, a smell they can't quite place, etc. The Leviathan can change the stimulus as desired from turn to turn. The affects one target within view and lasts only as long as the Leviathan concentrates. The Leviathan may choose to spend 1 Willpower point at any time while concentrating - this persists the psychic illusion for the rest of the Scene without needing concentration.</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 3:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan can now project multiple figments at once - either separate instances, or different senses - equal to their Intelligence.</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 4:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Illusions become more detailed, resembling real things. Targets who do suspect their false nature must succeed at a contested Wits + Composure vs the Leviathan's Manipulation + Subterfuge to pierce the deception.</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 5:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan can also remove things from sensory perception as well as add them. They could replace the sight of a door with empty wall, or a lurking Cultist with a rustle of leaves.</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 6:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The daydreams can now replace entire landscapes, shaping impressions of a Scene's location to what the Leviathan desires. Particularly detailed changes might require an Extended Action (target number set by the Storyteller) to fully envision.</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 7:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan's thoughts become manifest throughout its Wake. Given time and imagination, it could conceal it's entire cult compound, create a maddening labyrinth, or surround a town in a tableau of horrors.</span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Sidebar: The Art of Deception</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Illusions are just tricks of the senses, right? You might <i>think</i> something is crawling up your leg, but it can't actually hurt you, surely. Yes, the illusion itself cannot - but if you walk into a pit expecting solid ground, <i>that</i> can hurt you. Phantom sounds can distract (and bestow the Distracted Condition), and a panorama of frightful things can drive one mad - especially if the Leviathan takes care that only you seem to see it.</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-03-2019, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T16:19:04-08:00","id":1278450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1278445#post1278445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now for a &quot;heretical&quot; Channel<br /> <br /> <u><b>Reflections Upon the Deep (Ancestral Sanctity)</b></u><br /> <i>The thoughts of one of Tiamat's Brood are not restricted to inside of their mere skulls. Their daydreams drift freely, swaying the perceptions of lesser minds easily.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Depth 1:</b> Birthright of Sanctity<br /> <b>Depth 2:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan can weave a simple psychic impression upon the mind of another - a trick of the light, an unidentifiable sound, a smell they can't quite place, etc. The Leviathan can change the stimulus as desired from turn to turn. The affects one target within view and lasts only as long as the Leviathan concentrates. The Leviathan may choose to spend 1 Willpower point at any time while concentrating - this persists the psychic illusion for the rest of the Scene without needing concentration.</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 3:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan can now project multiple figments at once - either separate instances, or different senses - equal to their Intelligence.</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 4:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Illusions become more detailed, resembling real things. Targets who do suspect their false nature must succeed at a contested Wits + Composure vs the Leviathan's Manipulation + Subterfuge to pierce the deception.</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 5:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan can also remove things from sensory perception as well as add them. They could replace the sight of a door with empty wall, or a lurking Cultist with a rustle of leaves.</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 6:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The daydreams can now replace entire landscapes, shaping impressions of a Scene's location to what the Leviathan desires. Particularly detailed changes might require an Extended Action (target number set by the Storyteller) to fully envision.</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 7:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Leviathan's thoughts become manifest throughout its Wake. Given time and imagination, it could conceal it's entire cult compound, create a maddening labyrinth, or surround a town in a tableau of horrors.</span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Sidebar: The Art of Deception</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Illusions are just tricks of the senses, right? You might <i>think</i> something is crawling up your leg, but it can't actually hurt you, surely. Yes, the illusion itself cannot - but if you walk into a pit expecting solid ground, <i>that</i> can hurt you. Phantom sounds can distract (and bestow the Distracted Condition), and a panorama of frightful things can drive one mad - especially if the Leviathan takes care that only you seem to see it.</td> </tr> </table></div></div> </div> </div> </div>I love it, but why 'heretical'? One element that might be interesting to add is that these illusions really are self-directed delusions manifested outwardly - that is, perhaps there's an Adaptation that allows a leviathan to make an illusion last for a long time or indefinitely, so long as the Leviathan takes on a Condition which basically describes them seeing their own illusions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T17:16:02-08:00","id":1278461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1278450#post1278450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love it, but why 'heretical'? One element that might be interesting to add is that these illusions really are self-directed delusions manifested outwardly - that is, perhaps there's an Adaptation that allows a leviathan to make an illusion last for a long time or indefinitely, so long as the Leviathan takes on a Condition which basically describes them seeing their own illusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heretical, because it breaks some of the assumptions regarding Ancestral and Descendant Channels, and is unlikely to be cannonized.<br /> <br /> Taking a Persistent Condition and tying that to an Illusion does sound neat.<br /> <br /> I've got more to post, but I'll do that over time. Still have an Ancestral Channel for Might to fill. And probably Descendant Vitality and Ancestral Elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T06:59:29-08:00","id":1278571,"title":"","content":"<u><b>That Hideous Strength (Descendant Might)</b></u> <i>OR</i> <u><b>Overpowering Strength of Titans (Descendant Might)</b></u><br /> <i>Empowered by divine Ichor, the Tribe can shred mere artifice and land frightfully potent blows.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Depth 1:</b> Birthright of Might<br /> <b>Depth 2:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By Reflexively spending 1 Ichor, the Leviathan can ignore up to their Sheol in Durability from objects for their turn.</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 3:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You no longer need to spend Ichor to use the Depth 2 ability against objects with a Size less than half your own (round down).</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 4:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By Reflexively spending 2 Ichor, prior to making a melee attack, the Leviathan can smite a foe off their feet and out of their senses. If the final damage exceeds the target's Stamina, they take the Knocked Down and Stunned Tilts.</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 5:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each use of the Depth 2 ability against an object reduces its Durability by 1, as it cracks and weakens. When using the Depth 4 ability, rather than inflicting Knocked Down and Stunned, the Leviathan can lower the target's effective Stamina against physical Tilts being applied by 1 for the rest of the Scene.</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 6:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When moving, the Leviathan can make a Reflexive Brawl attack against each object or foe that impedes their movement.</span></span><br /> <b>Depth 7:</b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Leviathan, by charging its muscles with divine Ichor, can strike with the force of artillary. By Spending 4 Ichor, the Leviathan can make a brawl attack that is treated as an Explosive, with the Leviathan's current Damage rating, a Blast Area of Size/2, and a Force of 0. Even if the attack misses, the target is still in the primary blast area. The Leviathan never suffers damage from their own explosion, but any allies caught in it are not so lucky.<br /> <br /> <b>Adaptations</b>:<br /> <i>Shockwave (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i>: When using the Depth 7 ability, add the Leviathan's unmodified Strength (before adjustments for Depth and Atavisms) to Force.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-04-2019, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T11:24:17-08:00","id":1278646,"title":"","content":"I think I prefer That Hideous Strength as a name, and I want to suggest either a change to the Depth 4 effect or an Adaptation which lets you throw someone like a rag doll when you hit them - like 'name a monster' in film or TV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 01-04-2019, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T16:41:19-08:00","id":1278728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1278646#post1278646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I prefer That Hideous Strength as a name, and I want to suggest either a change to the Depth 4 effect or an Adaptation which lets you throw someone like a rag doll when you hit them - like 'name a monster' in film or TV.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either a general Adaptation or a replacement of Depth 6?<br /> (As Adaptation)<br /> <i>Tidal Surge (\u2022\u2022):</i> When using any of the abilities of this Channel, if the Leviathan deals damge equal to or greater than the target's Size, it is thrown 5 + additional Successes in meters away from the Leviathan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T19:08:42-08:00","id":1279097,"title":"","content":"Proposed Birthrights:<br /> <br /> Making is so that each grant an Active (for 1 Ichor) and Passive effect, scaling according to the number of Channels inside that Vestige known. Active is 1/2 round up (so every odd Channel) and Passive is 1/2 round down (so every even Channel).<br /> <br /> <b>Awareness</b>:<br /> Active - 1-3 bonus Elements found when searching for Clues.<br /> Passive - Reduce sensory penalties by 0-3.<br /> <b>Elements</b>:<br /> Active - Create a fog cloud Size*2 in diameter that inflicts a visibility penalty of 1-3.<br /> Passive - Reduce the rating of Extreme Environments by 0-3 so long as there is moisture.<br /> <b>Fecundity</b>:<br /> Active - Create the Undergrowth Tilt with a Durability of 1-3.<br /> Passive - Increase healing rate by x1/x2/x3/x4 (round up).<br /> <b>Might</b>:<br /> Active - Gain a +1-3 bonus to Athletics for Stamina in Turns.<br /> Passive - Increase Strength for throwing capacity by 0/100/200/300%.<br /> <b>Predation</b>:<br /> Active - Gain a +1-3 bonus for calculating Chase threshold or on rolls to gain the Edge.<br /> Passive - Track via Scent up to 0/500/1000/1500 yards.<br /> <b>Sanctity</b>:<br /> Active - Reduce a target's effective Composure by 1-3 for the Scene.<br /> Passive - Social Maneuvering against the Leviathan has +0-3 Doors.<br /> <b>Vitality</b>:<br /> Active - Reflexive; Downgrade 1-3 damage from an attack.<br /> Passive - Gain 0-3 Health.<br /> <br /> Feel free to comment, suggest replacements, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T21:37:11-08:00","id":1294593,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Not sure if the right place for this, or even if King Raven is still working on it (or will notice) but here are my Birthrights styled by the two current ones.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Unseen Giant (Birthright of Might)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The power of Leviathan is an often overt and obvious thing, bulging muscles and titanic claws, but the might of semi-divine is not without subtlety. Even the flimsiest of Earth\u2019s Most Terrible Tribe possess a might that cannot be seen, but is no less real. By spending a point of Ichor the Leviathan may increase his Strength by +1 until the end of the Scene, this may increase the Attribute beyond it normal limits.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the Leviathan has mastered three Channels of Might then the Strength bonus increases to +2, at five mastered Channels of Might then the Strength bonus increases to +3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Blind and All-Seeing King (Birthplace of Awareness)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You can run from the King, but you cannot escape his gaze, and for the Leviathan this is a truth beyond doubt. By spending a point of Ichor until the end of the Scene the Leviathan suffers no penalties to Perception from ANY source up to the range of its Wake (except for Total Cover, you don't get to see </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>through</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> objects), even if the Leviathan is Totally Blind (from birth or injury) they can temporarily see perfectly up to the edge of its Wake. If this would run counter to a Supernatural ability, roll Clash of Wills as normal for that effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While this Birthright is activated you do not suffer penalties to Combat or Defense rolls due to poor visibility (such as Darkness) or distance (such as Long Range).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Abyssal Minds, Eternal Thoughts (Birthright of Fecundity)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It\u2019s often said that Leviathans are mere beasts that are bereft of Inspiration and Intelligent, this could not be farther from the truth. It is ultimately from the \u2018abyss\u2019 of the human mind that all ideas spring from, and for those who are blessed with great Fecundity it is a very deep abyss indeed. By spending a point of Ichor the Leviathan may increase his Intelligence or Wits by 1 until the end of the Scene, this may increase those Attributes beyond it normal limits.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the Leviathan has mastered three Channels of Fecundity then the bonus increases to +2, at five mastered Channels of Fecundity then the bonus increases to +3. Alternatively you may split the Bonus between your Intelligence and Wits.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Yellow King\u2019s Command (Birthright of Sanctity)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Leviathan\u2019s divine nature means that authority is a natural part of their existence, and one that is inherited in their very blood. A God commands, the Mortal follows...or least that\u2019s what the God expects to happen. By spending a point of Ichor the Leviathan may roll Presence + Expression vs Resolve + Potency on a Wake Vulnerable individual. On a success the Leviathan can give that individual a One-Word command that it must follow to the best of it\u2019s abilities, if this would require an Extended Action the effects of this command last until the end of the Scene.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Commanding someone to \u201cDie\u201d only causes them to play dead... before or after a theatrical \u2018death scene\u2019.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Domain of </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Azathoth (Birthright of Elements)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Primordial World was one of crashing waves against rampant storms, and pillars of flame that warred with thundering slabs of stone. In these early days of chaotic maelstroms the ancient </span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Progenitor ruled over the very fabric of the world with impunity, but in the modern days the world is almost </span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>still</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> in comparison. Despite this more orderly world the descendants of those ancient being still hold some meager command over the basic building blocks of creation. By spending a point of Ichor a Leviathan can select one of the four Primary Element (Fire, Air, Earth, or Water) and create, alter, or manipulate up to 1 cubic-foot of that element within the range of their Wake.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most Leviathans use this Birthright for small quality-of-life benefits, though a few ingenious and malicious ones find some disturbing (and deadly) uses for it. If used as an \u2018attack\u2019 the Leviathan only rolls their Sheol vs the targets Defense and only deals 1 point of damage Bashing (Water and Air) or Lethal (Fire and Earth) damage that can be further reduced by armor, unless Bans and Banes apply (unless your nemesis is the Wicked Witch from the West you probably shouldn't waste the Ichor this way).</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24424-magus-black","name":"Magus Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T21:59:06-07:00","id":1309862,"title":"","content":"Going to be honest here I found out about this fan project from random web-surfing on tvtropes once I read it feel in love with it. I have also read this monster of a form from beginning to end before posting. Alright with that out of the way I have some questions about Atolls and leviathans created by Mother of A thousand among among other things. When I speak about Aspects I am talking about leviathans created by Embody Aspect.<br /> <br /> 1. Can Leviathan be imprinted to more than one Atoll? I can understand how one Atoll by be imprinted upon by more than one Leviathan by can a Leviathan imprint on more than one Atoll? Also does the Wake Muter merit effect the wake produced by Aspects?<br /> <br /> 2. Are Aspects imprinted upon the same Atoll as their parent(progenitor?). From what I am reading mechanically speaking they are the same person as said<br /> Leviathan and if that Leviathan is imprinted on a Atoll then they would be too which brings up another question. Can Aspects imprint on Atolls?<br /> <br /> 3. How independent/loyal is a Aspect ? seeing that they can actually refuse to help bring their parent back to life even though their parent can easily bring them back. I can see them having their own agenda's but seeing as their parent can read their entire memories without their knowledge I can see it being hard to do.<br /> <br /> 4. Can a Leviathan give orders to its embody Aspects via their mental link? Seeing as a Leviathan can read the minds of their Aspects could it also not send messages/orders along this link?<br /> <br /> 5. With the incubation of the Seconded self can a Leviathan raise the changes of their clone becoming a Leviathan? because reading the end with them being a Leviathan looks to me more of a story thing. Also for Embody Aspect Leviathans who have the 5 point version of this merit is there any chance at all for them to create Leviathans because I don't see it. Also if they implant their essence into their child and die will they be resurrected by the ability as normal or will their parent have to spend a willpower dot to bring them back?<br /> <br /> 6. Can Aspects Embody their own Aspects? the answer in this case I believe is going to be no even if they do become independent of their parent.<br /> <br /> 7. Is it possible for a leviathan to gain though rituals armor or some other clothing that reshapes itself to match their current depth or is it something I will need to rely on some wizard to do? because yes I know armor is out of place for what is basically a Kauji to wear but whats more frightening? a Kauji barreling down on you or a Kauji wearing armor that gives resistance to lighting (courtesy of some jackass wizard it somehow manage to get to make them the dawn item seeing as any armor originating from the tribe's rituals will not protect them from the lighting) which survives multiple shots from Marduk's kill-sats (with little to no visible effects depending on the quality of said armor). Though knowing Earth's most wicked I doubt many would actually think about this.<br /> <br /> Going to be honest I ask because when I finally play I plan on abusing the hell out of the Embody Aspect ability such as setting up one of my Aspects as a prison warden to get a steady stream of &quot;Converts&quot; from the system as well as a place for rituals.To when I finally evolve the means to not only survive in the vacuum of space but also if possible be able to open gatewaters in the void in order to assault Space Station Babylon with a School of it's children attacking the station themselves and sending boarding swarms of offshoots and hybrids (maybe even beloved in space suits if possible) to attack and if they don't self-destruct the station commandeer it and their orbital kill-sats. At that point I can see my Leviathan either looking at earth from the station's observation deck or the outside of the destroyed station looking at earth and wondering either &quot;What now?&quot; or &quot;What dragon have I awakened?&quot; (because its one thing for a secret because it's one thing for a secret society and some select individuals who know about your kind its another when the entirety of humanity learns about you).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25293-his-dread-monarch","user":"His Dread Monarch","date":". 05-05-2019, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25293-his-dread-monarch","name":"His Dread Monarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T15:18:59-07:00","id":1310115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>His Dread Monarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1309862#post1309862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7. Is it possible for a leviathan to gain though rituals armor or some other clothing that reshapes itself to match their current depth or is it something I will need to rely on some wizard to do? because yes I know armor is out of place for what is basically a Kauji to wear but whats more frightening? a Kauji barreling down on you or a Kauji wearing armor that gives resistance to lighting (courtesy of some jackass wizard it somehow manage to get to make them the dawn item seeing as any armor originating from the tribe's rituals will not protect them from the lighting) which survives multiple shots from Marduk's kill-sats (with little to no visible effects depending on the quality of said armor). Though knowing Earth's most wicked I doubt many would actually think about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on Crossover, Demons. Pay/Have one create a Form Gadget of Electrical Resistance. Anyone can use Gadgets. Leviathans probably aren't going to get their soul burnt out from using a Form Gadget. Hence, immunity to all electrical damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T19:08:21-07:00","id":1310447,"title":"","content":"This fansplat is shaping up rather well is all I can say. It was a true pleasure to come across alongside Moochava's Genius: the Transgression. I would dare say that the two splats would go well together in a common setting if you replace the Marduk Society with the Inspired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T22:48:04-07:00","id":1310482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1310447#post1310447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This fansplat is shaping up rather well is all I can say. It was a true pleasure to come across alongside Moochava's Genius: the Transgression. I would dare say that the two splats would go well together in a common setting if you replace the Marduk Society with the Inspired.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> You know, asides from some light reading of Leviathan back in 2010-2011 to get the broad picture, I've never read Leviathan?<br /> <br /> I think I'm going to keep it that way now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T03:14:30-07:00","id":1310506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1310482#post1310482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> You know, asides from some light reading of Leviathan back in 2010-2011 to get the broad picture, I've never read Leviathan?<br /> <br /> I think I'm going to keep it that way now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haters gonna hate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T09:16:53-07:00","id":1310550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1310506#post1310506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haters gonna hate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's not a great comparison. I liked what I read back in the day and have general positive feelings towards it, but between that comparison and other things that have come up, I've increasingly been getting the impression that wouldn't last with deeper contact. Honestly, I'd rather not read it and stay positive towards it then read it and end up hating it.<br /> <br /> If you've seen my attitude towards Genius since that review, you've probably seen that, while I've not lied about the fact I take issue with it, I've worked to try and keep positivity for the game going, because regardless of flaws, Genius speaks to people and I don't want to shit on people just enjoying things even if I want them to think more critically about it. With that in mind, you can see how the attitude towards Leviathan with the creeping impressions I have play out the way they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-07-2019, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T14:52:43-07:00","id":1310620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1310482#post1310482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> You know, asides from some light reading of Leviathan back in 2010-2011 to get the broad picture, I've never read Leviathan?<br /> <br /> I think I'm going to keep it that way now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some light reading all the way back in the beginning of this current decade that is about to end? I can assure you, Sean d'Arc, that much has indeed improved and I recommend that you go from Depth 1 to Depth 7 in your exposure to Leviathan. When I first read it, it was appallingly short and helter-skelter, but now it is more fully fleshed out and readable with an interesting tone that reminds me of a hot summer day on Florida's Forgotten Coast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7106,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","user":"Extant Reality","date":". 05-15-2019, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T18:10:36-07:00","id":1313046,"title":"","content":"Here is a splat for ritual blessings dots depend on the mutation.<br /> <br /> Wakening of the mind (OO-OOOOOO) (See mutations)<br /> This useful ritual blesses the target with grant psychic powers. Many leviathans find this useful for granting their worshipers powers they would not otherwise have and wish to use more human actors instead of relying on Lahmasu or other hybrids. The ritual itself is very popular with Leviathans who wish to create their own psychic network working in tandem with the Besieging the Tower of will channel and other similar channels. Often though this ritual is used to waken the mind of individuals rather than large groups considering it requires more Ardour for large groups.<br /> <br /> Mutations Taken from Appendix Lahmasu and Hybrids<br /> Awareness Mutations: Aura Reading (OOO), Clairvoyance (OOOO), Omen Sensitivity (OOOO), Psychometry (OOOO)<br /> Elements Mutations: Psychokinesis (OOOO-OOOOOO) (Cannot Apply Electricity or Fire) (Can apply Fire if Burning Lamps channel is fire in nature or has a Fire element Channel from Elements)<br /> Sanctity Mutations: Medium (OOOO), Telepathy (OOOO-OOOOOO)<br /> Vitality Mutations: Biokinesis (OO-OOOOOO)<br /> <br /> Though what I am confused on is does a ritual that grants a blessing have to be one dot more than the merit itself? otherwise these rituals are a dot less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25293-his-dread-monarch","user":"His Dread Monarch","date":". 05-18-2019, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25293-his-dread-monarch","name":"His Dread Monarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-19T09:26:29-07:00","id":1313133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/4crBjS\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/4crBjS\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/4crBjS\" target=\"_blank\"> https://discord.gg/4crBjS </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T07:58:54-07:00","id":1316632,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone! I'm so glad to see this project is still alive. I'm one of the ones who helped shape it back on the rpg.net forums the first time around. <br /> <br /> Among others, I did the start to the San Diego/Tijuana chapter. I couldn't see that on the drive this time around. Are you planning on updating that as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25385,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25385-llenlleawch","user":"Llenlleawch","date":". 06-05-2019, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25385-llenlleawch","name":"Llenlleawch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T04:56:22-07:00","id":1410498,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone, I've been looking over the Leviathan documents, and there are some things that seem to be missing. In particular, there seem to be a lot of references to the Rift, but no explanation of exactly what it is, how to enter or navigate it, or what might be found in it. Also, the book says that if a Leviathan falls to Ophion status, then unless its Cult is strong enough to anchor it to this world it will flee into the Rift. But if it does that, then unless it has the Channels to communicate at range it can no longer affect the real world, so how are Ophions at the bottom of the Rift supposed to be a threat? Or am I misunderstanding the purpose they serve?<br /> <br /> Also, I had a Merit idea I wanted to share:<br /> <br /> Focused Tranquility (O)<br /> <br /> Whether through training and practice or a quirk of your particular psychology, your restraint of one of your two natures is unusually secure. Choose your divine or your bestial nature and gain a bonus die on all Erosion rolls for that nature.<br /> <br /> Drawback: The twin natures of the Tribe are Scylla and Charybdis, to stay clear of one is to draw near to the other. You lose one die on all Erosion rolls related to the nature you did not choose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26379-aeshdan","name":"Aeshdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26379_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T11:14:28-07:00","id":1410532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeshdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1410498#post1410498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone, I've been looking over the Leviathan documents, and there are some things that seem to be missing. In particular, there seem to be a lot of references to the Rift, but no explanation of exactly what it is, how to enter or navigate it, or what might be found in it. Also, the book says that if a Leviathan falls to Ophion status, then unless its Cult is strong enough to anchor it to this world it will flee into the Rift. But if it does that, then unless it has the Channels to communicate at range it can no longer affect the real world, so how are Ophions at the bottom of the Rift supposed to be a threat? Or am I misunderstanding the purpose they serve?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably just being copied semi-wholesale from <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/LeviathanTheTempest\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: The Tempest</a>. But if you want to redo it for this version, then go for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeshdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1410498#post1410498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I had a Merit idea I wanted to share:<br /> <br /> Focused Tranquility (O)<br /> <br /> Whether through training and practice or a quirk of your particular psychology, your restraint of one of your two natures is unusually secure. Choose your divine or your bestial nature and gain a bonus die on all Erosion rolls for that nature.<br /> <br /> Drawback: The twin natures of the Tribe are Scylla and Charybdis, to stay clear of one is to draw near to the other. You lose one die on all Erosion rolls related to the nature you did not choose</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! But I'd word the Drawback like this;<br /> <br /> Drawback: The dual nature of the Tribe is akin to the paradigm between Scylla and Charybdis, for to stay clear of one is to draw near the other. You lose one die on <i>all</i> Erosion rolls related to the nature you did not choose, to represent the greater ease you have of being subsumed by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 08-26-2020, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T07:36:55-07:00","id":1410995,"title":"","content":"This is great! I love the idea of a 2nd ed update for Leviathan. Leviathan is my favorite Chronicles of Darkness Homebrew! It is so damn well done!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T06:28:49-07:00","id":1412425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeshdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles?p=1410498#post1410498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if it does that, then unless it has the Channels to communicate at range it can no longer affect the real world, so how are Ophions at the bottom of the Rift supposed to be a threat? Or am I misunderstanding the purpose they serve?</div> </div> </div> </div> You understand it perfectly. Ophions in the Rift work by using channels to direct their cults and pawns from a long distance. Those who lack pawns or appropriate channels generally aren't relevent to the story.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you c